{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:46:00.377642+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5eda6175d629e8bddd4058a5714ae59db05afc033de9257b14e741d553178080","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition pr:second-moment of arXiv:2607.21443, 'The critical KPZ scale for the averaging process'] Fix $\lambda =7/8$, and recall from (equation eq:beta-lambda-N of the paper) that $\beta_{\lambda,N}\sim N^{-1/8}$. Then, for every $t\ge 0$ and sequence $\mathbf x^N\in \mathbb{Z}^2$ such that $N^{-1/2}\mathbf x^N\to \mathbf z\in \mathbb{R}^2$, 
