{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:42:08.474803+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5edbb03067da0018cf9fc7e759f884b70c2dbd98f0c77e33bffc378582c6b59b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition Proposition1 of arXiv:2511.19391, 'Central limit theorem for supercritical Crump-Mode-Jagers processes counted with non-indiv'] Suppose that assumptions (A1 of the paper)-(A7 of the paper) hold and  let $\varphi$ be an $h$-dependent descendant characteristic, for some $h \in \mathbb{N}_{0}$, satisfying (C1 of the paper)-(C5 of the paper). Then, for any $\varepsilon>0$, as $n \rightarrow \infty$,
