{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:30:50.727148+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5ef6b169702b8e141554147f5cf8c6e419a2e902d9043e99cd89b6b212bb682d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:Dj of arXiv:2609.03855, 'A Fejér--Riesz inequality for Dirichlet series'] For $0 \leq j \leq J$, let $D_j\subset\mathbb T^d$ be the set of $w$ such that
\begin{equation*}
 \left|\sum_{p\le P}a_p^{jk}w_p\right|\le\varepsilon \mathcal{E}_{jk} \; \textrm{ and } \;
