        	we call $\delta_{i}:H^{i}(E) \longrightarrow H^{i-k}(B)$ \textbf{the connecting homomorphism in degree $i$}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:07.252226+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5f1614ed0ed97bceb5517ceeba16d887c67da6add1c834b39823f355f572595b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 of arXiv:2604.19220, 'Split merge dynamics for expanding intervals and point processes on the real line.'] Define a random process $(\tau_n)_{n\geq1}$ as
