{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:05:28.288159+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5f18fc9029cd0e94fc7f47bdf2f5cd377b53694959a8f1c942e67f60e86660a7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop PropNonInteger of arXiv:2602.08739, '\large \bf MOMENTS OF C$\beta$E FIELD PARTITION FUNCTION, $\mathsf{Sine}_{\beta}$ CORRELAT'] Let $\beta,s>0$ and $k \in \mathbb{R}_{\ge 1}$ such that $2s^2(2k-\lceil k \rceil)>\beta$ and moreover for $k>1$, $4\lceil k-1\rceil(k-\lceil k-1\rceil)s^2>\beta$. Then, as $N \to \infty$,
