{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.538378+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5f1d614dd03c72cc1e33c072daf67a903166a6e1b642c56c77dc4d05fe18b875","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor one:step:error of arXiv:2411.11759, 'Milstein-type schemes for McKean--Vlasov SDEs driven by Brownian motion and Poisson random'] If Assumptions \mbox{\normalfont  (asum:ic of the paper)}, \mbox{\normalfont  (asum:lip of the paper)} and \mbox{\normalfont  (asump:super of the paper)} to \mbox{\normalfont  (asum:derv:liningam of the paper)} hold, then  for $ 2\leq p_0\leq \min\{{\bar p}/((\eta+1)(\eta/8+1))\color{black},\bar p/2\}$
