{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.740789+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5f49081ef463f6b4dbfa7eb38a7542ee7f03e13f29b7335592d21f26b46b10f6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem label_multiple_vertices_conditional_degrees of arXiv:2606.09386, 'High-degree vertices in uniform recursive directed acyclic graphs with freezing'] Fix $m,k\in\mathbb{N}$ and $(b_v)_{v\in [k]}\in[0,m+1)^k$. Let $V_1,\ldots,V_k\in\mathbb{A}_n$ be distinct active vertices selected uniformly at random. Let $(d_v(n))_{v\in[k]}$ be $k$ integer-valued sequences diverging to infinity such that, for all $v\in[k]$, $\lim_{n\to\infty}d_v(n)/h_n^+ = b_v$. Fix a choice sequence $\mathbf x$ such that Assumption~$\hyperref[ass:A]{\mathbf{x}}$(item:geq1 of the paper) and~$\hyperref[ass:A]{\mathbf{x}}$(item:lb of the paper) are satisfied  with $I_{\hyperref[ass:A]{\mathbf{x}}}=\mathcal{O}((h_n^+)^{\gamma_0(1/2-\delta)})$, where $\gamma_0\in(1,\min\{(1/2+\delta)^{-1},(1-2\delta)^{-1}\})$ and $\delta$ is as in Part~(item:lb of the paper).
Let $(M_i)_{i\in[k]}$ and $(N_i)_{i\in[k]}$ be i.i.d.\ standard normal random variables. Then, conditionally on the event $\{\deg_n(V_v)\geq d_v\text{ for all }v\in[k]\}$,
\begin{equation} \begin{aligned} 
\bigg({}&\frac{u_n(V_v)-(mh_n^+-\frac{m}{m+1}d_v)}{\sqrt{mh_n^+-\frac{m}{(m+1)^2}d_v}}, \frac{h_{V_v}^+-(h_n^+-\frac{1}{m+1}d_v)}{\sqrt{\frac{1}{(m+1)^2}d_v}}\bigg)_{v\in [k]}\\
&\buildrel {\mathrm{d}}\over{\longrightarrow} \bigg(M_i\sqrt{\frac{mb_v}{(m+1)^2-b_v}}+N_i\sqrt{1-\frac{mb_v}{(m+1)^2-b_v}},M_i\bigg)_{i\in[k]}.
\end{aligned} \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:31.971248+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5f4c1f4a7af0dbefbe35475ddb311f019b04167a8d5e446933701e420f165ec4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 8 of arXiv:2606.10074, ''] For $j\ge1$,
  \begin{align} 
    C_{\theta_j}(a) - C_{\theta_j}(b) = \omega_j
    &= Y_{\tau_{j-1}+1}
    =
    \begin{cases}
      1 & \text{if~} (X)^L_{\theta_j}=a \\
      -1 & \text{if~} (X)^L_{\theta_j} = b
    \end{cases}
    \\
    &=-Y_{\tau_j}
    =
    \begin{cases}
      -1 & \text{if~} (X)^L_{\sigma_j}=a \\
      1 & \text{if~} (X)^L_{\sigma_j} = b.
    \end{cases}
  \end{align}
  Furthermore,
  \begin{gather} 
    \theta_j =
    \min\{t>\sigma_{j-1}: C_t(a) \ne C_t(b)\},
    \quad
    \sigma_j = \min\{t>\theta_j: C_t(a) = C_t(b)\},
  \end{gather}
  i.e., $\{\sigma_{j-1}, \ldots, \theta_j-1\}$ is a neutral period and
  $\{\theta_j, \ldots, \sigma_j-1\}$ is a $\kappa(\omega_j)$-period.","status":"unverified"}

