{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:15:08.889708+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5f67b1ab27ed9b466a58f8816a0adef17441d8779718e0a3d63aa18e73e278d8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm cor:boundtype2constant_TCS of arXiv:2411.10633, 'A Geometric Perspective on the Injective Norm of Sums of Random Tensors'] Let $r\geq 2$ an integer, $2 \leq p < \infty$, and $\mathcal{C}_{r,p}(d)$ the type-2 constant of the $\ell_p$ injective norm of order $r$ tensors as in (def:type2constant_TCS of the paper). Then\footnote{The notation $f \lesssim_{r,p} g$ means that the inequality $ f \leq C_{r,p} g$ holds for some constant $C_{r,p}$ that only depends on $r$ and $p$ (see (subsec:notation_TCS of the paper)).}
