{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:48:25.215525+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5f76d836c4c8659830c0557c289ab321a965b68fc569dbedfc54bd7e0c25dae8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:SBPformula of arXiv:2607.05671, 'Bi-infinite systems of singularly interacting Brownian particles and the KPZ equation'] Fix $m >0, \varepsilon>0$. For some $T > 0$, suppose $F$ is an element of $C^{0,1}([0,T] \times \mathbb{R})$ such that for all $c \in (0,\infty)$ and $T' \in (0,T)$, 
$$
\sup_{(s,y) \in [0,T'] \times \mathbb{R}} e^{cy^+} |e^{-m\sigma\varepsilon^{-1/4}y}F(s,y)| < \infty.
$$ 
For $i \in \mathbb{Z}$ and $s \in [0,\infty)$, let $Y_i^\varepsilon(s) = X_i^\varepsilon(s) + \sigma\varepsilon^{-1/4}s$. The following equality holds, for all $s \in [0,T)$,
\begin{equation} 
\begin{split}
& (1 - e^{-m\sigma\varepsilon^{1/4}}) \sum_{i \in \mathbb{Z}} e^{m\sigma\varepsilon^{1/4}i - m\sigma\varepsilon^{-1/4}Y_i^\varepsilon(s) + \frac{1}{2}m\sigma^2\varepsilon^{-1/2}s} F(s,Y_i^\varepsilon(s)) \\
& \hspace{1.5in} = \int_{\mathbb{R}} \mathcal{G}^\varepsilon(s,z)^m \left[ m\sigma\varepsilon^{-1/4} F(s,z) - \partial_z F(s,z) \right]dz,
\end{split}
\end{equation}
where the sums and integrals appearing above converge uniformly on compact subsets of $[0,T)$ in $L^r(\mathbb{P})$ for all $r \in [1,\infty)$.","status":"unverified"}

