    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:11:02.375528+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5fba2c31b03233ac5415c932c042c3cc70a7ee54c13670463d7cc867ca4ef316","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition multishelfcorrespondence of arXiv:2507.10294, 'Guessing Strategies for Shelf-Shuffling Machines'] Let $m\geq 1$ and let $S_{2^{m-1}}$ be the transition matrix for a $2^{m-1}$-shelf shuffle. Let $M$ be the transition matrix for a single-shelf shuffle. Then, we have $S_{2^{m-1}}=M^m$.
