{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:31:14.334213+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5fc34be9ab7f5228d7489dbc32960b7322f5454863f9b90fd9f29ba57045f8d5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition sum_condition of arXiv:2606.17425, 'Order statistics for edge eigenvectors of Wigner matrices'] We call an $N \times N$ symmetric random matrix generalized Wigner if it satisfies \begin{enumerate}
		\item The elements $(h_{ij})_{i \geq j}$ are independent random variables with $\EX[h_{ij}] = 0$. 
		\item The variances of $h_{ij}$ are given by the variance profile matrix $V = (V_{ij})_{1 \leq i, j \leq N}$, where $V_{ij} = \EX[h_{ij}^2]$. We require $V$ to satisfy the normalization condition \begin{equation}
			\sum_{i = 1}^N V_{ij} = 1, \quad 1 \leq j \leq N. 

		\end{equation} Further, we assume there exist two constants $C_{\mathrm{inf}}, C_{\mathrm{sup}} > 0$ independent of $N$ such that \begin{equation}
			C_{\mathrm{inf}} \leq \inf_{i,j} \{N V_{ij}\} \leq \sup_{i,j} \{N V_{ij}\} \leq C_{\mathrm{sup}}.

		\end{equation} 
		\item All moments of $\sqrt{N} h_{ij}$ are uniformly bounded, \emph{i.e., } for any $k \geq 3$ there exists $C_k$ independent of $N$ such that for all $1 \leq i, j \leq N$, \begin{equation}
			\EX[(\sqrt{N} h_{ij})^k] \leq C_k.

		\end{equation}
	\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

