    \gamma^{*}(\nu,z):=e^{-z}\sum_{m=0}^\infty \frac{z^m}{\Gamma(\nu+m+1)},
\end{align}
for all $z\in \mathbb{R}$ and $\nu>0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:41:33.824108+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6017e239de3975f95bce84bc3eee82e5a9575611513cd644324e08d8ef663654","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 18 of arXiv:2604.10244, 'Ergodicity for regime-switching neutral stochastic functional differential equations with '] Suppose that assumptions of Proposition  \ref{Pro:0929}  hold. Then there exist constants $C,\lambda>0$  such that for any   $\xi$, $\eta \in  C_r$,  $i \in \mbb S $, and  $t\geq 0 $,
