{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:52:23.586540+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_602b2bff51682e277c78bfd512e8d9677d3a72c4d16872282a27fc9378e76da3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:degree_hyperuniformity_palm_perturbed_lattice of arXiv:2602.19773, 'Regularization of a stationary point process by a stationary increments perturbation'] Let $\hat{\xi}=\mathbb{Z}$ and $B$ a fBm with index $0<h<1$, \textit{i.e.} $\@ifnextchar[{\@withv}{\@withoutv}{B_t}=|t|^{2h}$. Then, 
		\begin{equation}
