\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:31:49.845125+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_607c70cf3148ab451771d6e4ebf6f6973e8dea5a864f6cb297d4272be562498d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem the: long-term behavior of solutions of arXiv:2608.23756, 'Measure-valued fluid limits for partial service queues\\with correlated patience and servi'] Suppose that $\boldsymbol{\mu} \in \mathcal{S}^+$ and define $\boldsymbol{\nu}$ and $\boldsymbol{\xi}$ as in Theorem (the: structure of solutions of the paper). Then the measure $\boldsymbol{\xi}_t$ converges vaguely to the null measure as $t \to \infty$ and the measures $\boldsymbol{\mu}_t$ and $\boldsymbol{\nu}_t$ converge vaguely to the measure $\mu_\infty$ defined in (equation eq: global attractor of the paper). Further, $\boldsymbol{\xi}_t$ in fact converges weakly to the null measure if $y_* < \infty$. If in addition the survival function is such that
	\begin{equation}

		\int_0^\infty S_g(u \wedge y_*, u)du < \infty,
	\end{equation}
	then $\mu_\infty \in \mathcal{M}_F^+(\mathbbm{R}_+^2)$ and the measures $\boldsymbol{\mu}_t$ and $\boldsymbol{\nu}_t$ converge weakly to $\mu_\infty$ as $t \to \infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.718446+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_607da47b4aea1576b10a83260c3865c6b35507c95bf4a23ca1bfd3dd2c8ac8e8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem intersection.twodifferent of arXiv:2411.19145, 'On the intersection of critical percolation clusters and other tree-like random graphs'] Let $\mathcal G$ and $\widetilde{\mathcal G}$ two random graphs on the same metric space $(V,d_V)$, satisfying both the BK inequality, and respectively~(equation Halpha of the paper) and $(\mathcal H_\beta)$, for some $\alpha,\beta \in(\frac{d}{2},d)$, with $\alpha\le \beta$, and $2\alpha + 2\beta > 3d$. Let $\mathcal C_0$ and $\widetilde{\mathcal C}_0$ the clusters of the origin in $\mathcal G$ and $\widetilde{\mathcal G}$ respectively. There exsits a constant $\kappa>0$, such that 
\begin{equation}
\mathbb E\Big[\exp\big(\kappa\cdot  |\mathcal C_0\cap \widetilde{\mathcal C}_0|^\gamma\big)\Big]<\infty, \quad \textrm{with}\  
\gamma = \frac{2\alpha - d}{d+ 2\alpha - 2\beta}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:22:08.539989+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_60803ee30d75e577e99b01295e3265f5bf4923e6f6e028468df2b1bb16c66e6c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:CT-TASEP-scalar of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] The one-point Fredholm determinant
$F_{t, a, n} \vcentcolon= \det(I - K_{t, a, n})$ satisfies
\begin{equation}
F_{t,a,n}\partial_t F_{t,a,n+1}
- F_{t,a,n+1}\partial_t F_{t,a,n}
+ F_{t,a,n}F_{t,a,n+1}
- F_{t,a+1,n}F_{t,a-1,n+1} = 0.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:13:18.517016+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6081b89539e85c848c09f9b355d4231a94c8285c4ac44ded5d6e354b4e61ba6c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 27 of arXiv:2608.30602, '2608.30602'] Let $|V(x)|\lesssim \langle x\rangle^{-6-}$. If $f_0 \in C^{2}(\mathbb{R})$ satisfies
