{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.118485+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_609c8033cb7eb8201eb967af10d316156021938fd043f09f53c37644c58d1f01","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:Intro:DirectionalBounds of arXiv:2608.17031, 'A shape theorem for periodic branching diffusion'] Assume the hypotheses of Theorem (thm:Intro:ShapeHauss of the paper). Let $\Tilde{c}:S^{d-1}\to (0,+\infty)$ be defined by (equation eq:Intro:SpeedRelativeTo of the paper). There exists a positive constant $C>0$ depending on $b$, $\sigma$, $g$ and $\mathcal{M}$,  such that, for every $\epsilon\in (0,1)$, there exists $\Gamma>0$ with
