{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:38:23.528311+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_60acfa3574857b75429d6d09380f2fca944ed3647f813d1f91f02abbbc7b62b2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem TCg of arXiv:2510.22701, 'Gaussian fluctuations in Mean Field Stable matchings'] Suppose that $\rho$ satisfies (equation pd of the paper) for some $d>1$ and has finite $r$-th moment for some $r> 2d/(d-1)$. As $n\to\infty$, we then have that
