{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.857815+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_60b1778ee3139027d64540dd48e8de23a4209ccf54271d8c03dc8bd4eb11623c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary thm|Consequence2 of arXiv:2504.08935, 'Higher-Order Derivatives of First-Passage Percolation with Respect to the Environment'] The pair of edges $(i,j)$ is called {\em convoluted} on the outcome $\omega\in \Omega$, if $\partial_i\partial_jf(\omega)\neq 0$.   
