\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.670246+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_60c2ead427813127e3a5c125f646fb7bbf8d4bb0900ab1afa61df9ab9ca8be56","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:a_ell-bounds of arXiv:2602.14998, 'Random geometric graphs with smooth kernels: sharp detection threshold and a spectral conj'] Assume \prettyref{eq:coeffs-assumption} and $d \ge 4 r^2$. The quantities $a_{\boldsymbol \ell}$ defined in \prettyref{eq:def-a-ell} satisfy 
