{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:55:27.257636+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_60cc4e29d62cbd322716aa95512798e72270871f66ff0d2ca1e62b7e04fb6ffb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:1 of arXiv:2410.23250, 'Strict inequalities for arm exponents in planar percolation'] Let $f, g:\{0,1\}^n\to \mathbb R_+$ be two non-negative functions with \mbox{$\mathrm E[f],\mathrm E[g]>0$}. Then we have

