{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.897028+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6103aa8721c327513b7187c24c44e7bfa10b1edc6c8d6cb2b169ca67523c0545","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 56 of arXiv:2508.04938, 'Perfect t-embeddings of doubly periodic Aztec diamonds'] For~$q'\in \{q_0,q_\infty\}$ and~$p'\in \{p_0,p_\infty\}$, the~$1$-forms~$\omega_{q',p'}^{\mathcal Z}$ and~$\omega_{q',p'}^{\vartheta}$ are meromorphic~$1$-forms with simple poles at~$q'$ and~$p'$ and no other poles. Moreover, their residues are given by
\begin{equation*}
\int_{\mathcal C_{q'}}\omega_{q',p'}^{\mathcal Z}=-\int_{\mathcal C_{p'}}\omega_{q',p'}^{\mathcal Z}=c_{q',p'}^{\mathcal Z}
\end{equation*}
and
\begin{equation*}
\int_{\mathcal C_{q'}}\omega_{q',p'}^{\vartheta}=-\int_{\mathcal C_{p'}}\omega_{q',p'}^{\vartheta}=c_{q',p'}^{\vartheta}
\end{equation*}
where
\begin{equation*}
c_{q',p'}^{\mathcal Z}=
\begin{footnotesize}
\begin{cases}
a\sqrt{a^2+1}, & q'=q_0, p'=p_0, \\
\i\sqrt{a^2+1}, & q'=q_0, p'=p_\infty, \\
-\i\sqrt{a^2+1}, & q'=q_\infty, p'=p_0, \\
-a\sqrt{a^2+1}, & q'=q_\infty, p'=p_\infty, \\
\end{cases}
\end{footnotesize}
\quad 
c_{q',p'}^{\vartheta}=
\begin{footnotesize}
\begin{cases}
-a(a+\i), & q'=q_0, p'=p_0, \\
\i(a+\i), & q'=q_0, p'=p_\infty, \\
\i(a+\i), & q'=q_\infty, p'=p_0, \\
-a(a+\i), & q'=q_\infty, p'=p_\infty, \\
\end{cases}
\end{footnotesize}
\end{equation*}
and~$\mathcal C_{q'}$ and~$\mathcal C_{p'}$ are positively oriented small circles in~$\mathcal R$ around~$q'$ and~$p'$, respectively.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.525594+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_61045095b33a0a8221317dace4426186ea787ffc649117724c06858aa7b0a944","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop e:accessible of arXiv:2411.03482, 'Ergodicity of 2D singular stochastic Navier--Stokes equations'] For every $u_0, u_1\in \mathcal{C}^{-\kappa}_{\div}$ and $\delta > 0$, we have 
