{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.040277+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_610b3a3cda49b04e873bd0a4d6d24207b17001c955bb00b3dac295fc343b9ed1","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 8 of arXiv:2606.31596, 'The Invariant Measure of Multiscale Markov Chains via Fast Arborescence Factorization'] For every $M_1,M_2\in \mathcal M$ with $M_1\neq M_2$ the \textit{effective rate} is
