{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:12:46.884599+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6128f48f24d940f42636d6eb90d951d48330b8b15f12225d6dfd11aeaba45428","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma fchangemetric of arXiv:2608.09856, '\bf Mass erasure on measured $\bbR$-trees,\\ applications to L\'evy forests'] Let $a,b\! \in \!  (0, \infty]$ and let $g\colon[0, a) \! \to \! [0, b)$ be an increasing homeomorphism. We fix a rooted $\mathbb{R}$-tree $(T,d,\rho)$ such that $\mathtt{Ht}_{d, \rho} (T) \! \leq \!  a$.  We set $T^o\! \! :=\! B^o_{T,d} (\rho, a)\! = \!  \{ \sigma \! \in \!  T: d(\rho, \sigma) \! < \!  a \}$ and  
\begin{equation}

\forall \sigma, \sigma' \! \in \!  T^o, \quad d_g(\sigma, \sigma')\! = \!  g \big( d(\rho, \sigma) \big)+ g \big( d(\rho, \sigma') \big) \! - \! 2g \big(d(\rho, \sigma \! \wedge \! \sigma') \big).
\end{equation}
Then $(T^o\! , d_g)$ is an $\mathbb{R}$-tree and the identity function on $T^o$ is a $(d,d_g)$-homeomorphism. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:11.645263+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_612c4ac9ff8e93b8a85d0f3bc16b6a967aecd1595e09c59031f3af9e64b84fc5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 2 (Theorem 4.1, \cite{LP17}) of arXiv:2605.31568, 'Lipschitz continuity of the time constant for continuum percolation'] \emph{[Palm theory for Poisson processes.]}
For all non-negative bounded and measurable functions $f$ we have \begin{align*}
\E\left[\sum_{x_1,x_2,...,x_k \in X_\lam} f(x_1,x_2,...,x_k,X_\lam) \right] &= \lam^k \int_{\R^d} \E\left[f(x_1,...,x_k,X_\lam \cup \{x_1,...,x_k\}) \right]\,dx \ \\
&= \lam^k \int_{\R^d} \E^{\lam}_{x_1,...,x_k}\left[f(x_1,...,x_k,X_\lam) \right]\,dx. 
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:45:01.978261+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_612d9a06c1cf675d95e7a6d8d9586a867b3b34b36e2862a3f567a3fd7bf48df6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma LEM:BD of arXiv:2512.23957, 'Concentration and fluctuations of sine-Gordon measure around topological multi-soliton man'] Let $Q\in \mathbb{Z}$ and let $\varepsilon>0$. Suppose that  $F$ is a measurable real-valued functional such that
$\mathbb{E}\big[|F(Y(1))|^p\big] < \infty$ and $\mathbb{E}\big[|e^{-F(Y(1))}|^q \big] < \infty$ for some $1 < p, q < \infty$ with $\frac 1p + \frac 1q = 1$.
Then, we have
\begin{align*}
-\log \mathbb{E}_{\mu^Q_\varepsilon}\Big[ e^{-F(\phi)}   \Big]=\inf_{\theta \in \mathbb{H}_a}  \mathbb{E}\bigg[ F\big(
\ell^Q +  \sqrt{\varepsilon}Y(1)
+\sqrt{\varepsilon}\Theta(1) \big)  +\frac 12 \int_0^1 \| \theta(t) \|_{L^2_x}^2 dt  \bigg], 
