{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:22:39.566529+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_61312799d19727784c3dcbfab3c2d446d0c91a96dce9b9374229024743f1e3bd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop up-to-constants_volume-tail of arXiv:2508.18807, '{\bf Critical long-range percolation I: High effective dimension}'] Suppose that $\mathbb E_{\beta_c,r}|K| \asymp r^\alpha$ as $r\to \infty$ and let $f:(0,\infty)\to(0,\infty)$ be an increasing function whose inverse $f^{-1}$ is doubling.
