{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:44:17.353842+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_613706f7146c09577ec8b4773bc31b0ad0577b0536e073917502a66a69b7d85a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition lem:approx-exact of arXiv:2608.23554, 'Provably adaptive sampling with uniform and remasking \\ discrete diffusion models'] Fix \(k \in \{0, \ldots, N - 1\}\) in the time discretization \(0 = t_0 < t_1 < \ldots < t_N < T\). Consider the uniform or remasking process and recall~\(\cF(t, b)\) from~(eq:def-ftb of the paper). Letting \(u = T - t_{k+1}\) and \(\ell = T - t_k\), we have

