{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:50:48.852843+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_61371650710013c95a3763d265b9ef3754045a04278a5f76838f595b7946f264","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:stat.dist.alpha>0.beta=lambda0 of arXiv:2607.10708, 'A class of Markov processes with resetting and applications to cybersecurity'] \addcontentsline{toc}{subsection}{Theorem \thetheorem\ {case \texorpdfstring{$\beta=\lambda_o$}{Theorem β=λₒ}} and \texorpdfstring{$\alpha>0$}{α>0}}
    Let $X=(N,\Lambda,C)$  be a self-exciting PDMP with resetting and $Y=(N,\Lambda)$.  Under Assumption (a:finitereset of the paper) and with $\alpha>0\ \&\ \beta={\lambda^o}$,


    the invariant measure $\Pi$ for $Y$ is given by the following:


\begin{equation} 
    \begin{split}
      \Pi(0,\{{\lambda^o}\}) &= K_0/{\lambda^o}\\
      \Pi(n, d\lambda)&=\pi(n,\lambda)d\lambda, \quad n\geq 1, \lambda \in ({\lambda^o}, A),
                \end{split}

\end{equation}
    where the density is given by 

\begin{equation} 
    \begin{split}
      \pi(1,\lambda)&= {\frac{K_0}{\alpha}\int\mathds{1}_{\{\lambda<y+{\lambda^o}<A\}} \frac{F({\lambda^o} + y)}{yF(\lambda)} \,dG_{\ell}(1, y)}, \mbox{ and} \\
      \pi(n,\lambda)&=
      \frac{1}{\alpha}\int_{\lambda-{\lambda^o}}^{A-{\lambda^o}} \frac{F({\lambda^o} + y)}{yF(\lambda)} p(n-1,{\lambda^o} + y) \, dy, \; \mbox{ for } n\geq 2
          \end{split}

