{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:53:39.211768+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6137decc7585160c698e12001b265740fcd677d034cc21afb538c22cc28c08a3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 4 of arXiv:2608.27022, 'On LCK Geometry of Gauduchon Connections'] Let $(M,J,\omega)$ be a compact lcK manifold. If for two distinct parameters $t,s\in\mathbb R$,
