{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.812203+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_615c1cdea6d0453e302b56e80c360c55911ab053e34a8f6eb0e2dab18ee5a62a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma nu-K-lower-bound-sub-HW of arXiv:2504.02207, 'Finite-Time behaviors of M/M/$n$ Queue: Mixing Time, Mean Queue Length and Tail Bounds'] Consider the continuous-time $M/M/n$ system with the arrival rate $\lambda_n = n - n^{1-\alpha}$, the service rate $1$ and the stationary distribution be $\nu_n$. For $\alpha \in (0,1/2)$ and $n$ sufficiently large such that $\lambda_n \geq 3$ and $n - \lambda_n \geq 1$, we have that:
