{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:02:11.325778+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_615dc37fb75c8a70111670c76944e3014955e078e5cf04479afa14eef6c95c44","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn planar-map-with-missing-edges of arXiv:2510.26123, 'Directed distances in bipolar-oriented triangulations:\\ exact exponents and scaling limit'] A \textbf{planar map with missing edges} is a planar map $\mathfrak m$ with two types of edges: \textbf{missing} and \textbf{non-missing} edges (we often refer to non-missing edges simply as edges). The missing edges are always on the boundary of the external face of $\mathfrak m$ and are \emph{not} considered to be part of $\mathcal E(\mathfrak m)$. 

    A \textbf{directed planar map with missing edges}  is a planar map $\mathfrak m$ with missing edges equipped with an orientation of the edges in $\mathcal E(\mathfrak m)$ that is acyclic. In particular, missing-edges are \emph{not} oriented.
    See the left-hand side of Figure~(fig-bipolar-boundaries of the paper) for an example.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:00.770974+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_616298965397edbb7f8c6208afed0aaf79318769edcdab7f182ae4cc9e37376a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2512.05340, 'The rate of convergence of the critical mean-field $O(N)$ magnetization via multivariate n'] Let $V$ satisfy Assumption~\ref{assumption: assumptions on V} and let $P_t$ denote the semigroup corresponding to~\eqref{eq: overdamped langevin}.  
