{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:06:55.255995+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6163ffe745672c5c23f3393c8d847150bff70f8261c62bff9c4372cdf5690a73","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:consistency of arXiv:2512.21026, 'Minimax Duality in Game-Theoretic Probability\thanks{Work in progress: mistakes are likely'] We say $P\in\Delta(\Omega)$ and measurable $Z:\Omega\to\overline{\mathbb{R}}$ are \emph{consistent} if $\mathbb{E}_P Z \leq 0$.
  Similarly, a set $\mathcal{P} \subseteq \Delta(\Omega)$ is \emph{consistent with} $\mathcal{Z}$ if $\mathbb{E}_P Z \leq 0$ for all $P\in\mathcal{P}, Z\in\mathcal{Z}$.
  For gamble space $(\Omega,\mathcal{Z})$, we define
  \begin{align}

