{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.576940+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_616599ac7a9936ca774964aca76552038bc153bb3f0c54527c5f490b268a3fd9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: grid lemma for circulant of arXiv:2509.04349, 'Precise asymptotics for the norm of large random rectangular Toeplitz matrices'] For any $\tau \in (0, 3/4)$, there exist positive integers $T = T(\tau)$, $k = k(\tau)$, and vectors $\mathbf{u}^{(1)}, \dots, \mathbf{u}^{(T)}$ from the interior of the unit ball in $\mathbb{C}^k$ such that, for any $t \in \{1, \dots, T\}$ and all $p/n \in (\tau_{t-1}, \tau_t]$,
\begin{equation}
    \frac{\|\Pi_{p/n}^{[k]}\operatorname{diag}\{\mathbf{u}^{(t)}\}\|}{\sqrt{p/n}} > 1 - \tau/2.
\end{equation}
