{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:57:16.060996+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_61b19a8a26473d0e54f0280fe70fc7ac8cb6f7f1b58817467b00f8c2249e460f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop bound_on_integrated_G_tilde of arXiv:2506.10623, 'Polynomial slowdown in an angle-dependent 2d branching Brownian motion'] Let $\alpha \in (0,2)$ and $\beta>0$.
    Let $\vartheta_1 >0$ be defined as in Proposition (prop:estimate_G of the paper).
	Let $L>0$, $a> (1-\kappa)/(1-\frac{\kappa}{2})$ and $b>1-\kappa$.
    Let $\eta > 0$.
	There exist $K,C,c > 0$ such that the following holds for any $s \geq K$ and $t \geq s + Ks^\kappa$.
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item For any $x \in \mathbb{R}$ and any function $f$ satisfying $f \geq f^-_{L,a,b}$,
		\begin{equation}
		\int_\mathbb{R} \widetilde{G}(s,x;t,y) \mathop{}\mathopen{}\mathrm{d} y
		\leq C (t/s)^{\kappa/4} \exp\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft(\vartheta_1 (s^{1-\kappa}-t^{1-\kappa})\aftergroup\egroup\originalright).
		\end{equation}

		\item For any $\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft\lvertx\aftergroup\egroup\originalright\rvert \leq s^{\kappa/2}$ and any function $f$ satisfying $f \leq f^+_{L,a,b}$,
		\begin{align}
		& \mathbb{E}_{(s,x)} \mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft[ \exp \mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft( - \beta \int_{s}^t \abs{\frac{B_r}{\sqrt{2} r}}^\alpha \mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft( 1+f(B_r,r) \aftergroup\egroup\originalright) \mathop{}\mathopen{}\mathrm{d} r \aftergroup\egroup\originalright) 
        \ind{\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft\lvertB_t\aftergroup\egroup\originalright\rvert \leq t^{\kappa/2}}
        \ind{\forall r \in [s,t], \mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft\lvertB_r\aftergroup\egroup\originalright\rvert \leq r^{(\kappa+\eta)/2}} 
        \aftergroup\egroup\originalright] \nonumber  \\
		& \geq c (t/s)^{\kappa/4} \exp\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft(\vartheta_1 (s^{1-\kappa}-t^{1-\kappa})\aftergroup\egroup\originalright). 

		\end{align}
	\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.686367+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_61b33d1bb9c3f934c5724066c5ad9960ed724a80881480e4dd4551b40615b9f4","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Cumu of arXiv:2604.20215, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices II: Markov Chain Comparison and Cr'] The joint cumulants of mixed Chebyshev  moments are defined recursively by
    \begin{equation}
        \begin{gathered}
            \kappa_X(n_1)=\mathbb{E}\!\Big[\mathrm{Tr}\big(U_{n_1}(\tfrac{X}{2})\big)\Big],\\
            \kappa_X(n_1,n_2)=\mathbb{E}\!\Big[\mathrm{Tr}\big(U_{n_1}(\tfrac{X}{2})\big)\mathrm{Tr}\big(U_{n_2}(\tfrac{X}{2})\big)\Big]-\kappa_X(n_1)\kappa_X(n_2),\\
            \cdots\\
            \kappa_X(n_1,\dots,n_s)=\mathbb{E}\!\Big[\mathrm{Tr}\big(U_{n_1}(\tfrac{X}{2})\big)\mathrm{Tr}\big(U_{n_2}(\tfrac{X}{2})\big)\cdots\mathrm{Tr}\big(U_{n_s}(\tfrac{X}{2})\big)\Big]-\sum_{\Pi}\prod_{P\in\Pi}\kappa_X\big(\{n_j\}_{j\in P}\big),
        \end{gathered}
    \end{equation}
    where the sum runs over all nontrivial partitions $\Pi$ of $[s]$, i.e., excluding the partition $[s]$ itself.","status":"unverified"}

