{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:10:43.990281+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_61cfe20bb7168da3e2cd258d00923c524737c544f5eb0c4fe6a1ebae6999badf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:block_basic_1 of arXiv:2412.04579, 'Solvable Families of Random Block Tridiagonal Matrices'] Suppose that $\mathbf{M}$ is an ${\mathbb{F}}$-Hermitian $rn\times rn$ matrix for which the matrix
 \begin{align}
