 Then there is an ${\mathbb{F}}$-unitary matrix $\mathbf{O}$ of the form $\mathbf{I}_r\oplus \widetilde{\mathbf{O}}$ and a unique $\mathbf{T}\in \mathfrak{M}_{n,\beta, r}$, so that $\mathbf{T}=\mathbf{O}^{\dag} \mathbf{M} \mathbf{O}$. The matrix $\mathbf{O}$ can be chosen as the $\mathbf{Q}$ in
