{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:04:30.568042+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_620e0894a47725b7f0acf0934ca1651b01f1a75432624c893a5b2b55b5256e15","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2411.10296, 'Parking on a random rooted binary tree'] If $\alpha > 2 - \sqrt{2}$, then $\frac{e^{-\alpha}}{4} \lor (1 - \alpha) < p < c(\alpha)$ where
