{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.576585+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6212a7e46b3d75a224af1e613546337eb68ad380b0b325dac5a8e693cf537720","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma FNB-inequality of arXiv:2412.08932, 'Gaussian heat kernel asymptotics for conditioned random walks'] Assume that $\bb EX_i =0$ and $\bb E (X_i^2) = \sigma^2 >0$.  
