{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:37.642728+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6220294c5dac73bf9568dc49a2d2e4c1b93cb3866ca7a47af0f3dc95b18430f3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Def spin models of arXiv:2608.18045, 'Supercritical sharpness for the random cluster representation of real-valued spin models'] Let $\rho$ be an admissible measure on $\mathbb{R}$. The corresponding real-valued spin model on a finite subset $\Lambda\subset \mathbb Z^d$, with coupling constants $J=\{J_{xy}\}_{xy\in \overline E(\Lambda)}\in (\mathbb{R}^+)^{\overline E(\Lambda)}$, external magnetic field $\mathsf h=\{\mathsf h_x\}_{x\in \Lambda}\in \mathbb{R}^\Lambda$, boundary condition $\eta\in \mathbb{R}^{\partial^{\textup{ext}}\Lambda}$, and inverse temperature $\beta \geq 0$, is defined as the probability measure $\nu^\eta_{\Lambda,\beta,J,\mathsf h}$ on $\mathbb{R}^{\overline{\Lambda}}$ given by
\begin{multline}
\mathrm{d}\nu^\eta_{\Lambda,\beta,J,\mathsf h}(\tau) = \frac{1}{\mathbf{Z}^\eta_{\Lambda,\beta,J,\mathsf h}} \exp\Big(\beta \sum_{xy\in \overline{E}(\Lambda)} J_{xy} \tau_x \tau_y + \beta \sum_{x\in \Lambda} \mathsf h_x\tau_x  
\Big)\prod_{x\in \Lambda}\mathrm{d}\rho(\tau_x) \prod_{x \in \partial^{\textup{ext}} \Lambda} \delta_{\eta_x}(\tau_x),
\end{multline}
where $\mathbf{Z}^\eta_{\Lambda,\beta,J,\mathsf h}$ is a normalisation constant, and where $\delta_t$ is the Dirac measure at $t\in \mathbb R$. We will denote by $\langle f \rangle^\eta_{\Lambda,\beta,J,\mathsf h}$ the expectation of a function $f:\mathbb{R}^{\overline{\Lambda}}\rightarrow \mathbb R$ with respect to $\nu^\eta_{\Lambda,\beta,J,\mathsf h}$. When $J\equiv 1$, $\eta\equiv 0$ or $\mathsf{h}\equiv 0$, we may drop them from the notation.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:00:30.489825+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6222385bd215bd2025b5973f93a042590f97889ef2f36a6e7ad8e45af2e0712b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 20 of arXiv:2607.03924, 'Tree Coordinates and Range Martingales for Positive Operator-Valued Measures'] There is a one-to-one correspondence 
