{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:47:32.876383+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_625d2ec314eae5f51aca12e9c0e444c402bbb76ea518b5447cb21cc39c1bcaeb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 23 (Formal logarithmic realization) of arXiv:2609.02449, 'Finite Directional Coefficient Modules over Euler Fibers of $A$-Hypergeometric Systems'] For every $\Lambda\in\mathfrak{L}_{\bm{\beta},\bm{w}}^{\mathrm{adm}}$, the map $\Ser_{\Lambda,\bm{w}}^{\bm{\lambda}_{\Lambda}}$ is a linear isomorphism.
Their finite direct sum of isomorphisms
\begin{equation}

