{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:49:06.316427+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6293c234ace58b638ef38fcde9939c69d6e93ccca0129a198bc14077aee139f0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:bracket of arXiv:2601.10359, 'An Operator It\^o Formula for Volterra Gaussian Processes:\\ The Intrinsic Bracket via Cau'] Let $Y = (Y_t)_{t\in[0,T]}$ be such that $Y_t\in\Dom(D)$ for a.e.\ $t$ and $t\mapsto \Pi DY_t$ lies in $L^2([0,T]\times\Omega;\mathcal{H})$. Define the \emph{energy function}
