{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:36.745127+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6297a2b49354a0e3221f15fde70212d4be9ac63e2c37cd0a4e0f9abe95c96f0b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 6 of arXiv:2511.14757, 'A weak convergence approach to the large deviations of the dynamic Schr\"odinger problem'] Take a bounded, continuous function $F: \calC_1 \to \bR$ and let $\delta>0$. Then there exists an $M < \infty$, depending on $\norm{F} _\infty$ and $\delta$, such that for all $\eta \in (0,1)$,
