{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:20.889763+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_62a639119ecf68936244a098fced8273500daadfc54fb10e0ebc9f761347273c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Teorema 24 of arXiv:2506.11937, 'Random rotational invariance of integration by parts formulas within a Bismut-type approac'] Let $\ V=(Y,C,\tau, H)$ be a stochastic infinitesimal transformation. Then $\ V$ is an infinitesimal $\mathcal{G}-$ weak symmetry of $\ SDE_{\mu,\sigma}$ if and only if $\ V$ generates a one-parameter group on $\ M$ and the following determining equations hold:
