{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:38:57.120164+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_62a71273aedd1de2ecc7dfb0ffd91a8ec7e984b7542eb7954833aa64b94ab566","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 12 of arXiv:2604.04840, 'Bounding the Gap Between Zeros of the Variable-\\Parameter Confluent Hypergeometric Functi'] Let $G(\nu)$ be as defined in (\ref{eq:ratio of hypergeometrics}) and let $\nu$ be any point on $C$ in Fig. \ref{fig:closed contour} such that $R>>1$ and $\Phi(-R, b, z) \neq 0$. Then with $(x)_i = x (x+1) \cdots (x + i - 1)$, there exist finite $M_1$ and $M_2$ such that

