{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:38.633455+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_62a74bf186fb90eea1396df0674406e7e25c8093fc85cb7ebde18b45c1357c6c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 10 of arXiv:2506.17061, 'Non-uniform bounds for non-normal approximation via Stein's method with applications to th'] Let $p\ge 3$. Under the above setting, if $(J, h)=\left(J_c, h_c\right)$, then for all $z\in\R$, we have
