{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:02.094365+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_62a9a9f9ded3b22de5e6ad777bca5917aa29f07f9e2d996d424d6633f07016d9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 10 of arXiv:2604.26026, 'Stochastic Ordering of Dependent Systems under Transformation Models and Archimedean Copul'] Let $1\le k\le n-1$ and let $X_1,\dots,X_n$ whose joint distribution is described by an Archimedean copula with generator $\psi$. For $x\in\mathbb{R}$ such that $0<T(\alpha_i,F)(x)<1$ for all $i$, define
\begin{equation}

u_i(x):=T(\alpha_i,F)(x), \qquad t_i(x):=\phi\bigl(u_i(x)\bigr),\qquad i=1,\dots,n,
\end{equation}

Then, with $\balpha=(\alpha_1,\ldots,\alpha_n)$,
\begin{equation}

F_{n-k:n}^{(\balpha)}(x) =
\sum_{j=n-k}^{n} (-1)^{j-(n-k)}\binom{j-1}{n-k-1} \sum_{\substack{I\subseteq\{1,\dots,n\}\\ |I|=j}}	\psi\left(\sum_{i\in I} t_i(x)\right).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:36:31.221679+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_62aa7dc56d382d6a68b9d4e57deafe1c76048d002ea7a7acad6447f51870132c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2609.00483, 'On Embedding Hamming Spheres with Applications to Positive Curvature'] \cite{AS} Let $M^n$ be a closed,  positively curved Riemannian $n$-manifold, $n\geq 5$. Suppose that $N_1^{n-k_1}$ and $N_2^{n-k_2}$ are two closed, totally geodesic submanifolds of $M$ with $ k_1\leq k_2$, $4k_1\leq n+3$, and $k_1+2k_2\leq n+1$. Then 
\begin{enumerate}
\item If $\widetilde{N_2}$ is a cohomology sphere and $N_2$ has cyclic fundamental group, then  
 $M$ is homotopy equivalent to $S^n$, $\RP^n$, or a lens space; and
 \item If  $\widetilde{N_2}$ is cohomology complex projective space,  $2|k_1$ and $\pi_1(N_2)$ is trivial, then $M$ is homotopy equivalent to $\CP^{n/2}$.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.350592+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_62ab8fcc7349600f834316f1782394a2a87b08447958f5001b326bb15b69830f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma L:one-point-TASEP of arXiv:2604.10020, 'The directed landscape in half-space'] Fix $\alpha_0 \in \mathbb{R}$. 
Then there exists a constant $c > 0$ depending only on $\alpha_0$ such that for all $t > 0$, $\alpha \ge 1/2 - \alpha_0 t^{-1/3}$, $x, y \in \II{0, \alpha_0 t^{2/3}}$ we have
