{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:28:33.794577+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_62ad6e279882ee6b20abcce344d4a6081fc78dca4308336f71452114a46392b9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:41 of arXiv:2504.12293, 'Near-existence of bigeodesics in dynamical exponential last passage percolation'] {LR10}}]

  Fix $K>0$. There exist constants $C_1,c_1,C_2,c_2>0$ such that for all $m,n$ sufficiently large which additionally satisfy $\mathrm{slope}(\0,(m,n))\in (K^{-1},K)$ and all $\alpha>0$, we have
