{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.319555+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_62b37e6639797a907260bf0f25fb3b81c6d13cf047b98b10b8dd10f975324d84","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:superheavy of arXiv:2411.14926, 'Convex combinations of random variables stochastically dominate the parent for a new class'] We say that a random variable $X$ such that $F_X(0)=0$ is
