{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:00:46.839783+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_62cbd423d09ef50588efe905705fa0db3bf8a0ecab80db0afadbb9381d19206b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 7 (Local entropy bounds for $(\mathbb{RP}^{d-1},\delta)$) of arXiv:2608.13374, 'Nearly Sharp Comparison Results for sliced and max-sliced Wasserstein distances'] For $0 < \epsilon < 1$, there exists an $\epsilon$-packing of $\R\prob^{d-1}$ of size $m$ with respect to the metric $\delta$
