{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:03.902145+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_62dab6e8caa38a49c89227fe2acfdbefba0f31076d3428a9dbeaedf1ef1e9baa","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2606.20908, 'On It\^o-Stratonovich formula for rough sheets'] Let $x\in \mathcal{P}_{1,1}^{\ga_1,\ga_2}$ with $\ga_1>1/3$, $\ga_2>1/2$ and $\varphi\in C_b^{5}(\mathbb R)$. For $i=1,2$, recall that we have set  $y^{(i)}:=\varphi^{(i)}(x)$ and in~\eqref{E:delta-y-expansion} we have defined $\mathbf{R}^{(i)}$ by:
\begin{equation}
\mathbf{R}^{(i)}:= \delta y^{(i)}-  y^{(i+1)}\delta x \, -\,\delta_2 y^{(i+1)} \delta_1 x,
