\end{multline}
In particular, the conclusion of Lemma \ref{L:2D-Taylor-expansion1} still hold when one replaces Hypothesis \ref{hyp:bounds-higher-derivatives} by $\vp \in \cac_b^{5}(\RR)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:27:25.802592+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_62dc852d51cbd90ed5f2eb51eb40039165edae1d5fbbe6b3c3143f648171c41c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:G of arXiv:2605.17082, 'Spectral Purification in Reversible Markov Chains: Hidden Parameters, Observable Equivalen'] The \emph{spectral entropy-energy} is
