{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:52:47.261027+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_62ddb2d7ba0daa54892e6b3702f5c11d08bd43b88a65d7259732df2a060ba2fe","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 9 (see \cite{paper1}) of arXiv:2609.01114, 'Unbalanced spectral Tur\'an problem for color-critical graphs with prescribed large maximu'] Let $F$ be a graph with $\chi(F)=r+1\ge3$.  Define
	\begin{equation*}
		t_F:=\inf\left\{t\in[-1,1):\,\limsup_{n\to\infty}\frac{\ex(n,\mathcal M(\partial_c F))}{n^{1+t}}<+\infty\right\}.
	\end{equation*}
	Then $t_F\in\{-1\}\cup[0,1)$, where the gap $(-1,0)$ is excluded by \cite[Theorem 2.36]{Furedi-Simonovits}.  For each fixed boundary family used below, we choose an exponent $s_F\in[0,1)$ large enough so that
	\begin{equation*}
		\max\{0,t_F\}\le s_F
		\quad\text{and}\quad
		\ex(n,\mathcal M(\partial_c F))=O_{F}(n^{1+s_F}).
	\end{equation*}
	The value of $s_F$ is not assumed to be optimal.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:12:13.442323+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_62dde850d865a12992e53c505f7023aa838f7b7e8dba614a0f9b5332e4732d82","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 5 ({\cite[Lemma 2.1) of arXiv:2608.28234, 'A note on the positivity of $Q$-curvature via the continuity method'] {GurHangLin2016}}]

Let $(M, g)$ be a smooth compact Riemannian manifold with dimension $n \geq 6$. If $0\leq \lambda \leq 4$, and
\begin{equation}
Q - \lambda \sigma_{2}(A) > 0, ~~~ J>0,
\end{equation}
then the operator
\begin{align}
H(\varphi) := P\varphi - \frac{n+4}{2}Q\varphi + \lambda\left(J\Delta\varphi - g(A, \nabla^{2}\varphi) + 4\sigma_{2}(A)\varphi\right) + \frac{n+4}{2}(Q - \lambda\sigma_{2}(A))\varphi
\end{align}
is positive definite. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.388155+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_62de1b0b69faafbb6acc31f8d4dfb73e9d5828a4697697e08281e2c4dc8041c3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:Wg-bdd of arXiv:2509.23086, 'On Optimal Markovian Couplings of L\'evy Processes'] Let $\mathcal{A},\mathcal{B}\in \mathcal{G}_2^\Lambda(\mathbb R^d)$. Then it holds for all $x,y\in\mathbb R^d$ and $t\ge 0$:
	\begin{align*}
