{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:06:07.084127+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_62eafdd2177108f13ac0d78595822e75c7ed2b91bdd40eb8b0b703eff1e21a51","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 14 of arXiv:2608.27934, 'An example of biquandle and an invariant of long virtual knots defined through it'] Let $K$ be a long virtual knot. Take a long virtual knot diagram $D$ representing $K$. 
