{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:25:35.609319+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_62eb8b741b3769e9ccb18cf2a84ffe4620275e3f19f03164f4874daf36f782c4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma annealing of arXiv:2603.00705, '$L^2$-cutoff for the averaging process \\ on random regular graphs'] Fix $d\ge 3$. Then, for all $n$ large enough and $t\le \frac{1}{2d}\log^2 n$, we have
