{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:24:45.962572+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_62f296c034922efb25c0c2c38bec46ff37189e195023b81ace569b00269348a7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:block of arXiv:2509.11384, 'The Horton-Strahler number of butterfly trees'] Let $\mathcal T_1,\mathcal T_2$ be independent and identically distributed (iid) Catalan trees with $m$ nodes. Then
