{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.504092+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_63166538409b1659868149aeb0033b69c1eb0a4035fd9b9593981d4a4691c66d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 74 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] Suppose that $f_0 \in \Lip([0,T] \times \bbr^m,\bbr^m)$ and $f \in C_b^{2\beta,3}([0,T] \times \bbr^m, \bbr^{m \times d})$. Then for every $\xi \in \bbr^m$ the following statements are true:
