{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:33:17.722628+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_633ee3516f71f507511fbb573ff53bd1a9a12d9539ac0eaa77a7b4a6558e4739","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 64 (Quantitative dyadic Hardy bounds) of arXiv:2607.10813, '2607.10813'] Let $(x_Q)_{Q\in\Dyd}$ be a nonnegative square-summable sequence.
For every $\alpha>0$,
\begin{equation}
 \left(\sum_M\left[M^{-\alpha}\sum_{Q\le M}x_Q\right]^2\right)^{1/2}
