{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:21:56.733183+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_639c405df55c5e404853be6db0b868b0477b1f433dc22a3a80159013ae6c56e3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition pr:hf_compactness of arXiv:2507.15589, 'Tightness of approximations to metrics on non-simple conformal loop ensemble gaskets'] Let $(W,d_W)$ be a compact metric space. Suppose that $\mathcal {K}^W$ is a collection of non-empty compact subsets $K \subseteq W$ each equipped with a continuous function $f\colon K \to Y$. Suppose that
 \begin{enumerate}[(i)]
  \item There exist $0_Y \in Y$ and $M \in (0,\infty)$ such that $\sup_{x \in K} d_Y(f(x),0_Y) \leq M$ for all $(K,f) \in \mathcal {K}^W$.
  \item For every $\varepsilon > 0$ there exists $\delta > 0$ so that $d(x,y) < \delta$ implies $d_Y(f(x),f(y)) < \varepsilon$ for all $(K,f) \in \mathcal {K}^W$.
 \end{enumerate}
 Then $\mathcal {K}^W$ is relatively compact with respect to the metric $d_\infty$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.268417+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_63a16b85de28d52147b916bc5747ce7e9718a96bb006f2785e82d43d7f0291ae","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma cor:cheeky_zeta_K_min_T_K of arXiv:2507.12601, 'Multi-type logistic branching processes with selection: frequency process and genealogy fo'] There exists a coupling and a deterministic sequence of times $\zeta_K\to +\infty$ such that for any $\beta\in (0,1)$ $u\in \mathfrak{T}$,
\begin{equation*}
\lim_{K\to \infty} F^u_K(\zeta_K\wedge T^{\beta}_K)=F^u_\infty(\infty),
\end{equation*}
in probability, where $T_K^\beta := \inf\{t\geq 0\;:\; N_K(t)\geq K - K^\beta\}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:12:08.987875+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_63a5e41c50c4df88d9362235c40dc3e5733d26e285daa2c5d0fa1297c6219e99","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor cor_SlepianPosCorr of arXiv:2608.17463, 'Persistence probabilities of fractional L\'evy fields indexed by hyperbolic space and othe'] Let $(E,d)$ be a metric space and let $(Y_t)_{t\in E}$ denote a real-valued, separable, centred Gaussian process such that $\mathbb{E}\left[Y_s Y_t\right] \geq 0$, $\forall s,t\in E$.
    Let $f: E\to \mathbb{R}$ be a measurable function that is continuous except for possibly countably many points. Let $E = A \cup B$. Then
    \begin{align*}
        \mathbb{P}\left(Y_t \leq f(t) ~ \forall t\in E\right) \quad \geq \quad \mathbb{P}\left(Y_t \leq f(t) ~ \forall t\in A\right) \cdot \mathbb{P}\left(Y_t \leq f(t) ~ \forall t\in B\right).
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:57:20.675894+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_63a8ead481b3abda7a0ce369e184b8b6866c43e6eea1d8b5d227c388d75af687","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:firstboundongradsth1 of arXiv:2411.10235, '\textbf{Smooth transport map via diffusion process}'] For all $f\in L^2(\mathbb{R}^d)$, $i\in \{1,2\}$, $t\in[ 0,1)$ and $x,\xi\in \mathbb{R}^d$, we have
    \begin{align*}
    \|\int f(y) \nabla_x^i p^{t,x}(y)d\lambda^d(y)\| 
    &\leq \frac{Ct^i}{(1-t^2)^{i/2}}\left(\int \|f(y)-\xi\|^2dp^{t,x}(y)\right)^{1/2}.
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:38:23.595929+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_63a92993a4e4571d883b7265d785f30fec2e7b83aa3471bfd65062bb7afad965","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Harmonicity of arXiv:2511.08956, '\textbf{Towards a characterization of elliptic Harnack inequality for jump processes}'] For all open $D \subseteq \mathbb{R}^d$, we say that a function $h:\mathbb{R}^d \to \mathbb{R}$ is \emph{harmonic} on $D$ (with respect to $X$) if for all open $U \Subset D$ and for all $x$, we have
    \begin{equation*}
        h(x) = \mathbb{E}_x \left[ h(X_{\tau_U}) \right].
    \end{equation*}
    (Note that when $X$ is a jump process, the harmonicity of $h$ on $D$ depends on the values $h$ takes on $D^c$, because for $U \Subset D$, $\tau_U$ need not be in $D$.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.286534+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_63b138449915033a1bfc73b44fdd8c91cf24e19d6bcae12c5be3e8caca5a2cb7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 12 of arXiv:2606.22964, 'Signature McKean--Vlasov stochastic differential equations'] Let $p\in (2,3)$ and $X:[0,T]\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^d$ be a semimartingale defined on the probability space $(\Omega,\mathcal{F},\mathbb{F},\mathbb{P})$ with geometric $p$-rough path lift
    \begin{equation*}
        \mathbb{X}_t = \left(1,\mathbb{X}^1_t,\mathbb{X}^2_t\right) = \left(1,\int_0^t\circ dX,\int_0^t\circ dX^{\otimes 2}\right)\quad \forall t\in[0,T].
    \end{equation*}
    Then,
    \begin{equation}
        S(\mathbb{X})_T=\left(1,\int_0^T\circ dX,\int_0^T\circ dX^{\otimes 2},\int_0^T\circ dX^{\otimes 3},\dots\right) \in (T(\mathbb{R}^d)),
    \end{equation}
    where all the stochastic integrals are taken in the Stratonovich sense.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:54:15.662529+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_63b2ff06f9634bb52975b9748dc2d31de3a9b1fdb49d61a630ceef82f76971c8","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 27 of arXiv:2608.09700, 'A general paracontrolled ansatz for singular SPDEs'] An uplet $(Z_\tau)_{\tau\in\mcT}$ is said to be admissible if it satisfies \eqref{eq_defZtau_T+} and 
