{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:40:26.989466+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_63b9aca075f52f5f824841a139b9e0afce44cc95a617ecdc8f47eae4f0f5049e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm-freeenergy of arXiv:2604.14318, '\large The free energy of the interacting Bose gas:\\\medskip a variational description \\'] Assume $\beta, \rho\in(0,\infty)$ to be fixed and suppose that $v$ satisfies Assumption (V). Fix a sequence of centred boxes $\Lambda_N\subset\mathbb{R}^d$ such that $\lim_{N\to\infty}|\Lambda_N|/N=1/\rho$. We partition (up to boundary elements) $\Lambda_N=\bigcup_{z\in Z_{N,R}}W_z $ into the subboxes $W_z=z+W=z+[-R,R]^d$ with  $Z_{N,R}\subset 2R\mathbb{Z}^d$. Then, in the limit as $N\to\infty$, followed by $R\to\infty$, the pair $\frac 1{|\Lambda_N|}(\mathfrak N_{\Lambda_N}^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({\ell, R}})}}},\mathfrak N_{\Lambda_N}^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({\ell, \neg R}})}}})$ satisfies under the transformed measure $\widehat{\tt Q }^{\ssup{\Lambda_N,{\rm bc}}}$ defined in (equation transformedmeasure of the paper) a large-deviations principle on the set $\{(\rho_1,\rho_2)\in[0,\infty)^2\colon \rho_1+\rho_2=\rho\}$ with continuous and convex rate function $(\rho_1,\rho_2)\mapsto \chi(\rho_1,\rho_2)-\overline \chi(\rho)$, where $\overline \chi(\rho)=\inf_{\rho_1+\rho_2=\rho}\chi(\rho_1,\rho_2)$ and
\begin{equation}
	\chi(\rho_1,\rho_2)\vcentcolon= \inf\Big\{{\rm h}^{\ssup{{\mathcal L },{\mathcal S }}}(P)+\langle F_U,P\rangle\colon 
	P\in {\mathcal M }_1^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({\rm s}})}}}({\mathcal L }\times {\mathcal S }), \langle {\mathfrak N}_U^{\ssup {\ell,{\mathcal L }}},P\rangle=\rho_1 , \langle {\mathfrak N}_U^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({\ell,{\mathcal S }}})}}},P\rangle=\rho_2\Big\}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:00:30.496706+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_63ba75d34ac0440e3cea1407019fd410d827a816214f8c248d1c78f41c6a8ce8","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 11 of arXiv:2607.04193, 'Onsager--Machlup Functionals for Generalized Newtonian Equations of Motion with Time-Varyi'] Let $f$ be a non-negative, convex, symmetric, and measurable function on the Wiener space $(\Omega, \mathcal{F}, \mathbb{P})$. Let $A \in \mathcal{F}$ be a symmetric convex set with $\mathbb{P}(A) > 0$. Then the following inequality holds:
