    \mathbb{E}\bigl[f \mid A\bigr] \le \mathbb{E}\bigl[f\bigr].
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:59:45.430305+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_63bace0d006b11f03668ff00d1ae3da5fcfc8155fe84c87325cc41675135ab9b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi app_def_IOP of arXiv:2411.16464, 'Generating social networks with static and dynamic utility-maximization approaches'] For a given individuals graph $\mathcal{G}_N(\mathscr{I} , \alpha, C)$, we define for all individual $i \in \Iintv*{1, N }$ the Individual Optimization Problem (IOP) as:
