{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:25:35.633197+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_63c63119325933ac53c675deae1021f95ce9e41bfa2534ec7b6e777528c6f16b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition1 of arXiv:2603.05491, '\textbf{Local limits of uniform triangulations with boundaries in high genus}'] Let $T$ be a random infinite planar triangulation. We say that $T$ is weakly Markovian if there exist numbers $a_v^{p_1,\dots,p_k}$ for $k \ge 1$ and $p_1,\dots,p_k \ge 1$, $v \ge 0$, such that for any triangulation $t$ with $k$ holes of perimeters $p_1,\dots,p_k$ and $v$ internal vertices,
