{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:23.370299+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_63e87893dfaa6eedf254013d6e6d15ebed573acfb8fc2ce9c8b7ad0208c1dd43","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 52 of arXiv:2512.07202, 'Hitting Probabilities for Hypoelliptic Differential Equations Driven by Fractional Brownia'] For any $p\geqslant 1$, there exists a smooth random $\Psi_{l,p}$ such that
