{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:48:49.899193+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_63fa5a8b5f1e3a926936851b5afc93f7d5ce424e5ab933e346f0a98bf65270cb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:SSK_crit of arXiv:2510.26960, 'Free energy fluctuations in SK and related spin glass models: \\ A literature survey'] When no external field is present, and the inverse temperature is $\beta=1+bN^{-1/3}\sqrt{\log N}$ for some fixed $b\in\mathbb{R}$, the free energy of SSK exhibits the following convergence in distribution as $N\to\infty$.
