where the implicit constant depends only on $\mu,p,r,\varrho$ and $d$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:38:13.626579+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_63ff0ef5fa4f4ba5d2185e14b190efbbeb301e915299e0f598d68b709d9a3da0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 1 of arXiv:2609.00598, 'Supercritical mean--field limit for magnetized Hamiltonian dynamics'] Suppose that 
\begin{itemize}
\item[{\rm(i)}] $B\in W^{1,\infty}(\mathbb{R}_{+};W^{2,\infty}(\mathbb{T}^{2}))${\rm;}
\item[{\rm(ii)}]
$f_{\varepsilon}\in W^{1,\infty}([0,T]\times \mathbb{T}
    ^{2}\times \mathbb{R}^{2})$ is a solution to \eqref{magnetized vp with quasineutral scaling} with $f^{\mathrm{in}}_{\varepsilon}\in \mathcal{P}(\mathbb{T}^{2}\times \mathbb
    {R}
    ^{2}),$ finite second velocity moment and sufficient velocity decay{\rm;}
