{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:55.639421+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_641a4936d5005fd9cd5e25b09413ef68d0027352aff4cdf23fbc010005f6e30e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 21 (Ibragimov \cite{Ibragimov62}) of arXiv:2605.23461, 'An almost sure invariance principle for the Takagi--van der Waerden class functions'] Let $U$ be $\sigma\{X_i\colon 1\le i\le n\}$-measurable and $V$ be $\sigma\{X_i\colon n+m\le i\}$-measurable for some integers $n,m\ge 1$. Suppose that $|U|\le 1$ a.s. and $|V|\le 1$ a.s. Then,
