{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:27.008761+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_642f5bbb156c799444a4b05b9b322463551c0ad1679cb4728490606696f621d8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma otptilem of arXiv:2505.13382, 'The localization transition for the directed polymer in a random environment is smooth'] Let $p\in(1,2)$ and $X$ and $Y$ be two $L^p$ random variables such that ${\ensuremath{\mathbb E}} [Y | X]=0$ then if ${\ensuremath{\mathbb E}} \left[ |Y+X|^p-|X|^p \right]\le {\ensuremath{\mathbb E}} [|X|^p]$ have

