{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:48:27.276894+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_643094e6fa1d01383a7be3ebdedb9b72c0d9e29bb845125cfa9fb1f151ec1e4a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 of arXiv:2604.24664, 'Absolute continuity of Rosenblatt measures'] Let $\alpha > 0$ and $f \in L^1([0, T])$. The \emph{left} and \emph{right  Riemann--Liouville fractional integrals of $f$ of order $\alpha$} are defined by
	\begin{align*}
		(I^\alpha_{0+} f)(x) &= \frac{1}{\Gamma(\alpha)} \int_0^x (x-y)^{\alpha-1} f(y) \d{y},
		\\
		(I^\alpha_{T-} f)(x') &= \frac{1}{\Gamma(\alpha)} \int_{x'}^{T} (y-x')^{\alpha-1} f(y) \d{y},
	\end{align*}
	respectively, for almost all $x,x' \in [0, T]$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:53:10.161728+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6432659dd22e427c44b40c781f72754c5cd78d0e562523aef653a7fc351c4046","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem ThmKL of arXiv:2608.28949, 'The information geometry of product-reference discrete diffusion: Interaction growth compl'] Assume that the mixed partial derivatives appearing
in~(LemExactKL of the paper) are continuous on the compact log-odds region
