 \pi_1(N) = N^{-1/8 + o(1)},\\
 \pi_2(N) = N^{-1/2 + o(1)},\\
 \Delta(N) = N^{-1/2 + o(1)}.

\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:16:53.574658+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_643887f3341683a4bcfd70040662efc7cfc3249f000ab2c4d69e5462d0c422c2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:redtilingpoly of arXiv:2412.04607, 'Asymptotics of the partial \(n\)-fold dimer model'] The reduced tiling polynomial for a cycle graph of length \(L \geq 1\) is
