{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:50:30.566604+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_643a758094a10c032d092bebb932d5eec5539afacda9d318bdd317a2a8ee9575","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 28 of arXiv:2605.30616, 'Brownian motion: the hyperbolic number setting'] (see \cite{MR3029153,MR3404695}) With the convolution of coefficients as product, if $f\in\mathcal{H}_{p}$ and $g\in\mathcal{H}_{q}$
with $p-q\ge2$, then $f\star g\in\mathcal{H}_{-p}$ and there exists
a positive $A(p-q)$, depending only on $p$ and $q$, such that 
\begin{equation}

