{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:56:14.342035+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_644657407562fd005d2aad986cfa2ab9ebb8faa5c4205ae2a2a274f509fc5a49","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Pro of arXiv:2412.10001, 'On the Markov transformation of Gaussian processes'] Consider $H \in ]0,1[$ and denote by $\mathcal{B}_H$ the fractional Brownian motion with Hurst parameter $H$, \textnormal{i.e.} ,\ the centered Gaussian measure with covariance function $K_H : (s,t) \in \mathbb{R}_+^* \times \mathbb{R}_+^* \mapsto \frac{1}{2}(|t|^{2H} + |s|^{2H} - |t-s|^{2H})$. The centered Gaussian measure $\mathcal{B}_H'$ with covariance matrix \[K_{H}' : (s,t) \in \mathbb{R}_+^* \times \mathbb{R}_+^*  \mapsto 
		\begin{cases}
			s^{H}t^H\mathds{1}_{s = t} + 0\mathds{1}_{s \neq t} & \text{if } H < 1/2  \\ \min(s,t) &\text{if } H=1/2 \\   s^{H}t^{H}& \text{if } H > 1/2 
		\end{cases} \] is the strong local Markov transform of $\mathcal{B}_H.$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:06.332712+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_64468f7b3aa8169db6ad247f2b753a217c5507cf07f88c68013157e191ac698e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 24 of arXiv:2607.06745, 'Regularization and asymptotic behaviour of Ornstein-Uhlenbeck evolution operators in infin'] For every $c_{1}>0$ and $c_{2}>1$ such
