{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:31:20.610143+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6456cedc498ea8e23cd5438569d8b214eb7fabee09f35d3f23548f572a753452","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 18 of arXiv:2608.25772, 'Propagation of Chaos and Gaussian Fluctuations for Mean-field Coupled Maps'] Let $E$ be a Polish space and $\mu,\nu\in\mathcal{P}(E)$ be two probability measures on $E$. Suppose that $\Phi:E\to\R$ is a measurable function. Then $\forall\lambda>0$,
