{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:44:17.354605+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6460b8255bddfa9a4c3546327c6a944409bbb8927619d1dc9853097f2e381182","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition lem:approx-to-se of arXiv:2608.23554, 'Provably adaptive sampling with uniform and remasking \\ discrete diffusion models'] Consider the \(k\)-th interval of the time discretization \(0 = t_0 < t_1 < \ldots < t_N < T\) and let \(u = T - t_{k+1}\), \(\ell = T - t_k\). Recall the true score \(s_t\) from~(eq:score of the paper) and our score estimator \(\widehat s_t\) from~(eq:our-shat of the paper). If \(\ell - u \leq \kappa \min(1, u)\) with \(0 < \kappa < 1\), then
