{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:37.647481+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_64676090869772f46bd3ce010b58db6265c40ffeb40f6af9f8a951707a16e0ef","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem abs value approx of arXiv:2608.18045, 'Supercritical sharpness for the random cluster representation of real-valued spin models'] Let $\beta >0$ such that $\beta \not\in \Xi$. For every $\varepsilon,\delta > 0$, there exists $\ell$ large enough such that
