{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:43:19.154757+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_647b8f9421a6a24b64e05a9a725df08987f1d7e7663338dbedee3d2ecdb9198a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma3.8 of arXiv:2609.02607, 'Spatial inhomogeneity for a three-dimensional doubly degenerate nutrient system with indir'] Let $\Omega\subset\mathbb{R}^3$ be a smoothly bounded domain. Then there exist $\gamma>0$ and $C>0$ such that for any $p>4$ and $\eta\in(0,1]$, and for all $\varphi\in C(\overline{\Omega})$ and $\psi\in C(\overline{\Omega})$ fulfilling $\varphi>0$ and $\psi>0$ in $\overline{\Omega}$, we have
