{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:11:02.389128+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_647cfe02bcd6b86bce2a47019ccfc1c4ebeac3461022a43948883b50c2d683e0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:LDP_general of arXiv:2507.10531, 'Quantitative central limit theorems for exponential random graphs'] For any $\eta > 0$, there are constants $c(\eta), C(\eta) > 0$ such that
\begin{equation}
