{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:29:08.708005+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_64a62c825da271d36f3f8bf371cdef7980d51d9a86a0a525c0468178e5a94b45","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:miss_rate_fixed_N of arXiv:2412.00279, 'Optimal local storage policy based on stochastic intensities and its large scale behavior'] Let $p_N^{\pm}=p_N\pm\frac{1}{N}$ where $p_N=1-\frac{C}{N-1}$. Let $\varphi_N^{\pm}$ be the probability distribution function of the random variable $\widehat{\theta}_N^{\pm}:=\widehat{Q}_N\left(p_N^{\pm}\right)$ under the probability ${\rm P}$. Then the miss rate is bounded from above and below by
