{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:23.367852+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_64c3f4f2ed6316943d966dfd3447bddc5b2ea228ca47e66afb47cfad3efe654f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 22 of arXiv:2512.07202, 'Hitting Probabilities for Hypoelliptic Differential Equations Driven by Fractional Brownia'] \begin{comment}
Let $(X_t)_{0\leqslant t\leqslant T}=(X^1_t,\cdots,X^d_t)_{0\leqslant t\leqslant T}$ be a continuous Gaussian process with i.i.d. components. Assume that every component of $X$ satisfies:
\begin{itemize}
\item Condition $\ref{con1}$, for some $\rho\in[1,2)$
\item Condition $\ref{coninf}$, with index $\alpha<2/\rho$
\item Condition $\ref{concov}$, namely $X$ has nonnegative conditional covariance.
\end{itemize}
\end{comment}
For any $q>1$, there exists  $C_q>0$ such that 
$$
