{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:25:44.953371+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_64c9ab7a79e2826ca060380fb45bb37736ca5b2d858a6337b1bf0ca7d1a9cd9a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 of arXiv:2605.10609, '\Large \bf Stochastic curve shortening flow driven by a transport-type pure jump L\'evy no'] Let $u_0\in V$. An $H$-valued c$\grave{a}$dl$\grave{a}$g $\mathcal{F}_t$-adapted process $u:=\{u_t\}_{t\geq0}$ is called a strong solution to \eqref{c2eq6}, if \\
