{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.724169+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_64cb3ec98986b260dd903c3f7de82350baaab37f3ee13a7a957cda14e2d31efd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:key-area-p of arXiv:2606.06612, 'The limit shape and emergence of the \\ Discrete Gaussian level lines'] Fix $g\geq 0$, $n \geq 0$, and set $h = H+1-n$. The following hold for every subsets $F\subseteq V \subset\mathbb Z^2$ where $F$ is connected with $g$ holes. There exists constants $\delta_p, c > 0$ such that
        \begin{enumerate}
            \item[\emph{Mesoscopic range}] If $1 < p < 2$ and $|\partial F|\vee |\partial V| \leq O(L^{\frac23+\frac{\delta_p}5})$, or if $p > 2$ and $|\partial F|\vee |\partial V| \leq O(L^{2/3}e^{c\sqrt{\beta\log L}})$, then 
    \begin{align}{\widehat\pi}^{(p), 0}_V(\phi_x \geq -h,\, \forall x \in F) = (1+o(1))\exp\left(-\upxi^{(p)}_n|F|\right)\,.
