{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:38:57.144869+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_64df9944589e5f53aae6e50c48b9a282d911a18a6881a737fa2f91ce4e744bce","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 17 of arXiv:2604.06122, 'REM universality for linear random energy'] Let $(F_n)_{n\in\mathbb{N}}$ be a sequence of extended real-valued random fields
\been{
F_n : \R^{\N} \to \mathcal{M}(\R_{> 0},\overline{\R}),}
and let 
\been{
f\in \mathcal{M}(\R_{> 0},\overline{\R})
}
