{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:11:11.719502+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_64e3afe06e7cc77f73586ee48fc4d4ac86ee696738470fe299b5ae7cabc0d20a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:localized-wedge-data of arXiv:2609.00698, 'Kinetic Wedge Layers and Diffusive Limit of Neutron Transport in Polygonal Domains'] For each matching coefficient whose recurrence chain is retained through order $N$, with $s_\ast=\beta+3$ as in (equation eq:basic-parameters-comp of the paper), the fixed vertex-scale regularizations and one-sided ray extensions make the data (equation eq:generated-wedge-data of the paper) well defined and measurable in the mild/distributional sense, and
\begin{align}
 \abs{F_{m,\alpha,b}(Y,v)}
 \le C\left\langleR\right\rangle^{-s_\ast},
 \qquad
 \abs{h_{m,i,\alpha,b}(\sigma,v)}
