{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:01:54.381796+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_65269afe8dc17eae129634b52540c19413b0d5172602328ffe49f4bced51fed0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 1 of arXiv:2411.02030, 'Finite ergodic components for upper probabilities'] Let $(\Omega,\mathcal{F},P)$ be a probability space and $T:\Omega\to \Omega$ be a measurable invertible transformation. Suppose that $(\Omega,\mathcal{F},P,T)$ satisfies the finite irreducible invariant set partition assumption. Assume that for each $j=1,2,\ldots,n$, the limit
