{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.327040+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_653f3008dfd1ffc1e549395813898f594bc552ad7aa3d55c53bcd79850f3aaca","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition d:ShadowMP of arXiv:2411.14936, 'Massive Particle Systems,\\Wasserstein Brownian Motions,\\ and the Dean--Kawasaki Equation'] A $\msP$-valued process~$(\rho_\bullet,\mbbP)$ with $\mbbP$-a.s.\ $\tau_\mrmn$-continuous trajectories is a \emph{distributional solution} to the \emph{shadow martingale problem~$\hmartp{}{\mssL}$} if
\begin{equation}
\widehat M^{\class{\varphi\otimes f}}_t\eqdef\ (\varphi\otimes f)^\star(\rho_t) - (\varphi\otimes f)^\star(\rho_0) -\int_0^t (\mcL'\rho_s)(\varphi\otimes f)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d} s
\end{equation}
is an $\msF_\bullet$-adapted $\mbbP$-martingale for each $\varphi\in\msR_0$ and each~$f\in\msA$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:09:49.860728+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6540167d53f12186a4957272d60a6eb42b025d2ae01205adec7a5cb006c71892","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 of arXiv:2609.03084, 'Convergence rates to traveling waves for an FKPP model with nonlinear advection'] Let $\beta \geq 0$. There exists a constant $C > 0$, depending only on $\beta$, such that, for all $\varphi \in H^1(\R_+)\cap L^1(\R_+, x^\beta dx)$ and all $L > 0$,
