        \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:32:11.131819+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_65413a87af760804dbd62846ac4f1e24646e5747f33fc8bd38be08f520c9691a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem eq:LiGol-bound-example of arXiv:2510.11015, 'An interpretable universal bound for multiserver queues via a leave-one-out technique'] Consider the $GI/GI/n$\xspace queue with homogeneous servers under the FCFS policy. Assume that (1) $\mathbb{E}\left[A^2\right] < \infty$; (2) there exists $\epsilon\in(0, 0.5)$ s.t. $\E{S^{2+\epsilon}}<\infty$; (3) $\rho < 1$; (4) the system has a unique limiting distribution $\pi$. Then 
\begin{equation}

    \Ep{\pi}{Q} \leq \left(2.1 \times 10^{21}  \mathbb{E}\left[(\mu S)^2\right]  \Big(\mathbb{E}\left[(\mu S)^2\right]^{1+\epsilon} + \E{(\mu S)^{2+\epsilon}}\Big) \big(\frac{1}{\epsilon}\big)^4 + 49 \mathbb{E}\left[(\Lambda A)^2\right]\right) \frac{1}{1-\rho},
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.212887+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_65436584bf75764002668069e045742e5abe3480d6fd8ebbc4e08ab24456c1f6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop: poly_neighboring of arXiv:2512.06640, 'Existence and sharpness of the phase transition for the frog model on transitive graphs'] Let $G$ be a quasi-transitive graph of superlinear polynomial growth. 
    Let $V_0$ be an $(a, \beta a)$-group net on $G$. 
