    \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:37:28.989521+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_65444e09325aa9c235db4eea342eccfaa65eb7b321aae0f9ef4f5af121ef5609","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem POC of arXiv:2412.01070, 'A note on Lévy-driven McKean-Vlasov SDEs under monotonicity'] Assume that Assumptions $({\bf A}_1')$, $({\bf A}_{2})$ and $({\bf A}_{3})$ hold, and suppose further  $X^i_0\in L^\beta(\Omega\to\mathbb R^d,\mathscr F_0,\mathbb{P})$ for any $1\le i\le n$.
Let $(\mu_t)_{t\ge0}$ be the common distribution of $(X_t^i)_{t\ge0}$ for all $1\le i\le n$, and $\bar{\mu}^n_t=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^n\delta_{X^{i,n}_t}$, where $\{(X_t^{i,n})_{t\ge0}\}_{1\le i\le n}$ is the solution to the mean-filed interacting particle system
(equation MF of the paper)  with   $f(x,z)=f(x,\mu,z)$.
Then, for any fixed $T>0$, there is a constant $ C_T>0$ such that
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
 \mathbb{E}{\mathbb W}_p^p(\bar{\mu}^n_t,\mu_t)
\le C_T\phi_{p,\beta,d}(n),\quad t\in[0,T],
\end{split}
\end{equation}
where the quantity $  \phi_{p,\beta,d}(n)$
is defined as below:
\begin{equation}
\phi_{p,\beta,d}(n):=
\begin{cases}
n^{-(1-\frac{p}{{\beta}})}, & d=1,2;  d=3 {\rm ~and~} \frac{3}{2}\le p<{\beta}; \\
                            &d=3, 1\le p<\frac{3}{2} {\rm ~and~} {\beta}<\frac{3p}{3-p}; d\ge4 {\rm ~and~} {\beta}<\frac{dp}{d-p}; \\
    n^{-\frac{p}{d}}, & d=3, 1\le p<\frac{3}{2} {\rm ~and~} {\beta}\ge\frac{3p}{3-p}; d\ge4 {\rm ~and~} {\beta}\ge\frac{dp}{d-p}.
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
Furthermore, for  any $0\le q_1<q_2<1,$
there exists a constant $\hat C_T>0$ such that
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
\mathbb{E}\Big(\sup_{0\le t\le T}|X^{i,n}_t-X_t^i|^{pq_1}\Big)\le \frac{q_2}{q_2-q_1}\big(\hat C_T
\phi_{p,\beta,n}(n)\big)^{q_1}.
\end{split}
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:33:11.988147+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_65448603f5a105626f1cd196f36c8f626ea2df721cf6f0e7ab69f6a0d07a4cf3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:4.5 of arXiv:2608.27474, 'Nonlocality of Cover-Time Changes Under Edge Addition'] For the graph (equation eq:4.15 of the paper), with path length measured in edges and the walk
