{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:27.032985+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_654f00f3bf1a4523e95cc5171d8cf87e261c5c88f590d210aacf216e1ff540d7","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:radially of arXiv:2505.14012, 'Ergodicity for stochastic neural field equations'] If for $J\in L^1(\mathbb{R}^d)$ there exists a non-negative decreasing function $j_0:\mathbb{R}\to [0,\infty)$ that is continuous except at a finite number of points such that
\begin{align*}
