where $D_{\omega_{\mathbf{X}}, \omega_{\mathbf{Y}}} := \omega_{\mathbf{X}}(a,b)^{1/p} \omega_{\mathbf{Y}}(c,d)^{1/q}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:51:15.030458+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_657980863e556237d8bde2f99bbe82e4c7e5b2ca85e4cb2554570e706c9fb6a9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:transposition-additive of arXiv:2609.03904, 'Extremal Families for Matchings in Permutations'] Let $n\geq4$, and let $f:S_n\to\mathbb R$ have local transposition differences.
