{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:40:22.390162+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_65870f70f322fd57783b0ad0d6fc20b6456b005fd7fbbeb8f71b87a24586212f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lem-ptwise-conv of arXiv:2506.18827, 'Random walk reflected off of infinity, with applications to uniform spanning forests and s'] Almost surely, the following is true. Let $\eta\in\Xi$, let $\widehat\eta$ be its successor, and let $K$ be a compact subset of $[ \tau_\eta, \tau_{\widehat\eta})$. 
