{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:34:45.765263+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6593f01f2ba195759389710d6d8515523f4444b9d7c12289ec0da81ed1d05298","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition H1sn of arXiv:2609.01990, 'Jacquet-Zagier treatment of the beyond endoscopy trace formula for \(\GL_2\)'] The term given by \(H_s^1(n)\) is equal to
    \[
    \frac{(4n)^{1-s} \pi^{s-\frac{1}{2}}}{4\Gamma(\frac{s+1}{2})} \sum_{f=1}^{\infty} \frac{1}{f^{3-2s}} \sum_{l=1}^{\infty} \frac{1}{l^{2-s}} \sum_{\xi \in \mathbb{Z}} \text{Kl}_{l,f}(\xi,n) I_{l,f}(\xi,n)
    \]
    where
    \begin{equation}
        I_{l,f}(\xi,n) = \int_{-1}^{1} (1-y^2)^{\frac{1}{2}-s} F_s(y) \Phi_1\left(\frac{\sqrt{\pi} lf^2}{2 \sqrt{n(1-y^2)}} \right) e\left(\frac{-\xi \sqrt{n} y}{2lf^2}\right) dy 
