{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:31.959107+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_65a7fa101280b4061925ee91c8cd246a669648126896ef9f49a1cd03323e5689","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lm 22 of arXiv:2512.02286, 'Pfaffian Transition Probability and Correlation Kernel of TASEP in Half-space'] Let $f$ be an anti-symmetric function in $N$ variables and let $x=(x_1,\dots,x_N)$ where $x_1> \cdots > x_N$ are integers. We have the following identity of sums over triangular arrays:
