{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:25:45.017779+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_65d0c294dfd188b25343be4bbcf7da9f9283b02648a6676a81b3ee7047836020","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2605.11877, 'Fluctuation analysis for a randomly perturbed dynamical system with state-dependent impuls'] Let $B_t$ be a standard one-dimensional Brownian motion. Then, for any fixed $\sfT>0$, $\alpha \in (0,\tfrac{1}{2})$, we have
