{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.575274+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_65d2b8aa819adedd42c7d13b350d265c2cbd44012c71e29c3b03da034e7d8307","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition equivalent prop 8 of arXiv:2509.04349, 'Precise asymptotics for the norm of large random rectangular Toeplitz matrices'] For each division of the interval $\{0,1,\dots,N-1\}$ into bricks, the following holds with high probability (that is, with probability approaching one as $n\rightarrow \infty$): 
