{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:31.958793+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_65d76ef5c5a80643b6d4930402e86d7fa46b9b78ddd554109e530383efc010bb","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 18 (Pfaffian $L$-ensemble) of arXiv:2512.02286, 'Pfaffian Transition Probability and Correlation Kernel of TASEP in Half-space'] Let $\mathcal{Z}$ be a set of points, and let $L:\mathcal{Z}\times\mathcal{Z}\to \mathbb{C}^{2\times2}$ be a skew-symmetric $2\times2$-matrix valued function. A measure $\mu$ on $2^\mathcal{Z}$ is a \emph{Pfaffian $L$-ensemble} on $\mathbb{Z}$ if its correlation function $\rho$ is given by
	\begin{equation}

		\rho(X) = \frac{\Pf L_X}{\Pf(J + L)},\quad X \subset \mathcal{Z}.
	\end{equation}
	Here $L_X$ denotes the $(2|X|)\times(2|X|)$ matrix $[L(x,x')]_{x,x'\in X}$, while $\Pf(J + L)$ denotes the Fredholm Pfaffian of $L$ on $\ell^2(\mathcal{Z})$ (which coincides with the Pfaffian of the matrix $J + L$ when $\mathcal{Z}$ is finite).","status":"unverified"}

