{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:03:39.775491+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_65e68d1b049951649d3704d1c33cab56f029b9947f2846aa62a22ba07b27045c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop checking-the-inequalities of arXiv:2411.03065, 'Growing conditioned BGW trees with\\ log-concave offspring distributions'] Assume that ${\mathbf{w}}$ is log-concave and that $r=r({\mathbf{w}})$ is finite.
