{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.360292+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6642607a88cd649273301e755532df1e9436396d449ba1faf9df3d01306276a5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition diff-dual-def of arXiv:2509.23086, 'On Optimal Markovian Couplings of L\'evy Processes'] Given \( \mathcal{A}, \mathcal{B} \in \mathcal{G}(\Pi) \) and points \( x_0, y_0 \in \Pi \), define the \emph{dual value} of (equation om-def of the paper) by
	\begin{align}
		\omega_c^*(x_0, y_0; \mathcal{A}, \mathcal{B}) := \sup_{(\varphi, \psi)\in \mathcal{D}(x_0,y_0)} \left[ \mathcal{A} \varphi(x_0) + \mathcal{B} \psi(y_0) \right],
	\end{align}
	where $\mathcal{D}(x_0,y_0)$ is the set of all pairs of functions $\varphi,\psi:\Pi\to\mathbb R$ such that:
	\begin{itemize}
		\item \( \varphi \in \bar D(\mathcal{A}) \), \( \psi \in \bar D(\mathcal{B}) \);
		\item $(x,y)\mapsto c(x,y)-\varphi(x)-\psi(y)$ achieves a global minimum at $(x_0,y_0)$. 
	\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

