{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:32:23.896757+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_664564f57a1816ed3dfa4ba5364113e91bb83756ea11744c9d47009fa76e23a5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop thm:shearer_gen of arXiv:2603.27144, 'On the critical fugacity of the hard-core model on regular bipartite graphs'] [generalized Shearer inequality]
\begin{comment}
Older formulation of Shearer's inequality:
\begin{thm}
Let $\mathcal{X}$ be a finite set of RVs. Let $\gamma$ be a measure
on the set of subsets of $\mathcal{X}$. Assume for a fixed $p>0$
that $\int\indic{X\in\mathcal{A}}d\gamma(\mathcal{A})\ge p$ for every
$X\in\mathcal{X}$. Then
\[
\ent(X:X\in\mathcal{X})\le p^{-1}\int\ent(X:X\in\mathcal{A})d\gamma(\mathcal{A})
\]
\end{thm}

\end{comment}
Let $J$ be a finite index set. Let $(\boldsymbol{X}_{j})_{j\in J}$
be random variables. Suppose that $\boldsymbol{K}$ is a random subset
of $J$, independent of $\boldsymbol{X}$, with $\mathbb{P}(j\in\boldsymbol{K})\ge p$
for each $j\in J$. Then
\begin{equation}
S(\boldsymbol{X})\le\frac{1}{p}S((\boldsymbol{X}_{j})_{j\in\boldsymbol{K}}\,|\,\boldsymbol{K}).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

