{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:09.863955+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_66877600c35dead3a8fbc16480710b00b3db94c8dd563d122a9132b03bfc920e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 16 (Limit of $D(t)$) of arXiv:2605.21459, 'Network evolution with self-reinforcement'] For any $\delta >-1$, there exists a non-negative random variable $X_\delta$ with $\E[X_\delta] >0$ such that, almost surely and in $L^1$, as $t \to \infty$,
