{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:59:45.007424+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6688fa0c55951eaa38b91b24085ab493183b4bceaf3828a5079df608c3415700","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition B4re of arXiv:2605.12777, 'Mesoscopic Rates of Convergence for Complex Wishart Matrices at the Leftmost Spectrum Edge'] Let $R_{n-1,N}(s)$ and $R_{n,N-1}(s)$ be the integral remainders defined in (equation B4D of the paper). For $s\in\left[s_0,N^{\frac{1}{6}}\right]$, we have
