{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.598194+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_668942401450efc3f70a6f9ab33272e71e759276db0c2e901ea65787e49fa678","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lem3.3 of arXiv:2411.15724, 'Wasserstein Convergence Rates for Empirical Measures of Random Subsequence of $\{nα\}$'] Given $\eta \in \mathbb R$, define a function
$$
g_\eta(\varepsilon) = \sum_{l = 1}^{\infty} \text{\rm{e}}^{ - 4^l \varepsilon} 2^{\eta l}, \quad \varepsilon \in (0, 1].
$$
Then
