{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:34:33.548255+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_668e055387cadd504de0eeb089933fc1c52bc5be0bcb95d2066620baa929ee5e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 (Mixing times asymptotics for $\frac{1}{3}<\gamma<1$) of arXiv:2603.29473, '$\chi^2$--cut-off phenomenon for Galerkin projections of Fokker--Planck equations with mon'] \hfill

	\noindent
	Let $\frac{1}{3}  < \gamma < 1$, $x_0 \neq 0$ and let $t_\varepsilon$ be the time defined by \cref{eq:mixing_0}. Given $1 \leq n < \infty$, then for small enough $\varepsilon$ it holds
	\begin{equation*}
		d_{n,\varepsilon}(t_\varepsilon,x_0) \approx 1
	\end{equation*}
	with implied constant independent of $\varepsilon$.
	Furthermore, for small enough $\varepsilon$ it holds for a constant $C:=C(\gamma)\geq 1$
	\begin{equation} 
		\frac{\log(1/C)}{\lambda_{1}} \varepsilon^{\frac{1-\gamma}{1+\gamma}}+ \frac{|x_0|^{1-\gamma}}{1-\gamma}
		\leq
		t_\varepsilon
		\leq
		\frac{\log(C)}{\lambda_{1} } \varepsilon^{\frac{1-\gamma}{1+\gamma}} + \frac{|x_0|^{1-\gamma}}{1-\gamma}.
	\end{equation}

	If, on the other hand, $x_0 = 0$, define
	\begin{equation*}
		E_n:=\{1\leq j\leq n:\ \psi_j(0)\neq 0\}.
	\end{equation*}
	If $E_n=\emptyset$, then $d_{n,\varepsilon}(t,0)=0$ for all $t\geq 0$. Otherwise, let $m:=\max E_n$ and define $t_\varepsilon$ by the condition
	\begin{equation*}
		e^{-2\lambda_m \varepsilon^{\frac{\gamma-1}{1+\gamma}} t_\varepsilon}
		\left(\int \varrho_{\varepsilon,0}(x)\psi_{m,\varepsilon}(x)\,\dx\right)^2 = 1.
	\end{equation*}
	Then, for $\varepsilon$ sufficiently small, we have
	\begin{equation*}
		d_{n,\varepsilon}(t_\varepsilon,0) \approx 1.
	\end{equation*}
	In addition, for small enough $\varepsilon$ it holds
	\begin{multline} 
		\frac{\varepsilon^{\frac{1-\gamma}{1+\gamma}}}{\lambda_m}
		\left (\frac{\gamma(1-\gamma)}{1+\gamma} \log(\varepsilon)-\log(C) \right ) + \frac{1}{1-\gamma}\varepsilon^{\frac{(\gamma-1)^2}{\gamma+1}}
		\leq
		t_\varepsilon
		\\
		\leq
		\frac{\varepsilon^{\frac{1-\gamma}{1+\gamma}}}{\lambda_m}
		\left (\frac{\gamma(1-\gamma)}{1+\gamma} \log(\varepsilon)+\log(C) \right )
		+ \frac{1}{1-\gamma}\varepsilon^{\frac{(\gamma-1)^2}{\gamma+1}}.
	\end{multline} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:03.892994+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_668eb2447a2bb517e3b0bbdf41ab9704df4ab9dc41a9b019bd62004a04ce5d31","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2606.18866, 'Cram\'er-Type Moderate Deviations for Engel's Series via a Martingale Approach'] Under \eqref{eq:FS-A1}--\eqref{eq:FS-A2}, there is a constant $C>0$, depending only on $C_0$, such that
