	as $N\to\infty$. Then $(X_\epsilon)_{\epsilon\in (0,1)}$ is also tight in $Y_\alpha$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.237474+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_66910fcb87c44c427edd76fd3317c849932378fe5ae58599769063e63db0ba0c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:proj-est2 of arXiv:2606.00325, 'Ergodicity for a class of stochastic Hasegawa-Mima equations with dissipation'] There exists $C>0$ such that for all $x\in D(A^{1/2})$ we have 
