{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:04:30.600792+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_66a1cf6fb1633b93ac03ff7e52443dd6a2aee1b78645d16c7c945b5c2e053fb5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem parti-clo of arXiv:2411.10586, 'A convergence framework for Airy$_\beta$ line ensemble\\ via pole evolution'] Take any parameters $K>100$ and $0\le \delta<1$. Suppose that a particle-generated Nevanlinna function $Y$ satisfies the following conditions:
\begin{itemize}
    \item there is no pole of $Y$ in $(K,\infty)$;
    \item for any $w=x+\mathrm{i} y$ with $x\le K^2$ and $y\ge 4K^2/(1+|x|^{\delta/2})$, we have
    \[
            \left|Y(w)-\sqrt{w}\right|\leq \frac{{\rm Im}[\sqrt w]^{1-\delta}}{{\rm Im}[w]}.
    \]
\end{itemize}
Then $Y$ has infinitely many poles $x_1\ge x_2\ge \cdots$, and $|x_i-{\mathfrak a}_i|<CK^4i^{-\delta/6}$ for any $i\in \mathbb{N}$, where $C>0$ is a universal constant. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

