{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:48:17.123654+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_66b0c681ca9d2ebc77d80542740d019aca44a7cdc413ebc85210502b5f6493f7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 11 of arXiv:2605.27713, 'Lower path regularity in all dimensions'] Suppose that $X=(X_t)_{t\in[0,T]}$ satisfies Assumption \ref{a1} (i). Let $0\leq \alpha < d$ and let $0\leq \beta \leq 1$ be such that 
