{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:25:49.869832+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_66e96a78e8cf2fcbb513f67bc13f6a1929062f959f39f65ce49f0f3c7940f39c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 7 of arXiv:2609.02050, '2609.02050'] Given two diagrams $D=(D_1,D_2,\ldots,D_n)$ and $C=(C_1,C_2,\ldots,C_n)$ of $[n]^2$ with $|C_j|=|D_j|$ for each $j\in[n]$, we have
