{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:02.094003+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_66ec5c888f91cf96c730028d8d41e4d84fe2da61a4c0b60ef96ee0453361e2d3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 of arXiv:2604.26026, 'Stochastic Ordering of Dependent Systems under Transformation Models and Archimedean Copul'] {Assume $T$ is differentiable with respect to its first argument, the generators are such that $\phi_2\circ\psi_1$ is super-additive, $\psi_1$ is $d$-monotone with $d\geq 3$, $\boldsymbol{\beta}\overset{m}\succeq\boldsymbol{\alpha}$} and 
