{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.777354+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6709a6d3e2b25efe4d91c21550161bab603b4e0a222d0a3ef759ba5a174bcb65","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 10 of arXiv:2603.25459, 'Cram\'{e}r-type moderate deviation for double index permutation statistics'] Let $(W,W^{\prime})$, $\Delta$, $D$ and $D^{*}$ be defined as in Theorem \ref{thm-general-MD}. Assume that there exits a constant $\tau_0>0$ such that for all $0\leq t\leq \tau_0$,
