{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:45:17.697055+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_671934d2cd63db7081a90378302ee64eb3178bb67dd93849df6f5ab7aa9c42a5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:apriori of arXiv:2604.08462, 'Convergence of $k$-point functions in\\ high dimensional percolation'] For each $\epsilon > 0$, there is a $C_k=C_k(\epsilon)$ such that if $(x_1, \dots, x_k) \in G(\epsilon, n)$ then 
\[\tau_{k+1}(x_0, x_1, \dots, x_k) \leq C_k(\epsilon) \mathrm{dist}(x_0, \{x_1, \dots, x_k\})^{4-d} n^{(4-d) (k-1) - 2}. \]
Dependence of $C(\epsilon)$ on $\epsilon$ is polynomial:
\begin{equation}
C_k(\epsilon)\le c\epsilon^{-10dk},
\end{equation}
where $c$ does not depend on $\epsilon$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:46:36.093558+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_671efc2fb8ee87da4a9b2e1e37bc43fb7d1a7c00dba4d2062ca0127c26fc5ccb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:Lie-formula of arXiv:2609.02710, 'Asymptotic Mean Value Laplacian\\ on equiregular sub-Riemannian manifolds'] For every $f\in C_c^\infty(G)$, locally uniformly in $x$,
\begin{equation}
  A_hf(x)\longrightarrow\mathcal A_Gf(x),
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}
  \mathcal A_Gf(x)
  =\frac1{\widehat V}\left(
    \frac12\sum_{i,j=1}^kM_{ij}X_iX_jf(x)
    -\frac12\sum_{i,j=1}^k
      M_{ij}\Tr(\ad_{X_j})X_if(x)
  \right).
\end{equation}
In particular, the drift vanishes when $G$ is unimodular.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:41:29.042352+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_67200b0789d1439588a40c48aa46be2217e8da8813be6759bac83e5fa7349dfb","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 (Lemma 3.6 of \cite{Chen2024} at $n=8$) of arXiv:2608.26598, 'Pinching cones for positive isotropic curvature in dimensions seven and eight'] Let $n=8$ and $0<b\le b_{max}$. Then, with $a,\gamma,\omega,A,P,Q$ as in \eqref{data},
