{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:02:18.047729+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6728447f60ab1d55c0a9986780b6cdaaebacfad83a310befce83254711348f4b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:h-collected-chernoff of arXiv:2602.21315, 'The Instability of all Backoff Protocols\thanks{For the purpose of Open Access, the author'] Let $\alpha > 0$, and let $j\ge1$ be a sufficiently large integer. Let $Y$ be a sum of independent Bernoulli random variables with mean $\mu$. If $\mu \leq \alpha^2 j(\log j)^2/6$, then with probability at least $1-j^{-3j}$, 
