{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:38:23.623592+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6733a8d46800fd0c4d7469b09bfbbc7f257cca5fa6da0ee3bf126aacbfb1ee1d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma EHI:l:LeaveBallExponential of arXiv:2511.08956, '\textbf{Towards a characterization of elliptic Harnack inequality for jump processes}'] There exists a universal constant $c_{(EHI:l:LeaveBallExponential of the paper)}=c_{(EHI:l:LeaveBallExponential of the paper)}(d)>0$ such that if $X \in \mathcal{I}(d, r_0)$, then for all $r>0$, $x \in \mathbb{R}^d$, and $t>0$,
