{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:44:39.727332+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_673582c481daaf6b1fdc34ecb1cb0257699873f3ea2b5a57b04b9c2e532ea233","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2608.29761, '2608.29761'] Let $\epsilon>0$, and $0<q<1$. There exists a constant $C>0$ so that for every  $w \in B_r(v, \epsilon)$  there exists $c\in (-\epsilon,\epsilon)$ with 
