{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:00.614924+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6747da59e6861c7b1f281bf108e4d5c8b344edcfb0a7ed467e05c4b2b0342836","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 27 of arXiv:2510.27589, 'Geodesic switches and exceptional times in dynamical Brownian last passage percolation'] Fix $\beta\in (0,1/2)$, $\mu\in(0,1)$ and $\varepsilon>0$. For any $p\in \{0\}_{\RR}$ and $q\in \{n\}_{\RR}$ with $\slope(p,q)\in (\mu,\mu^{-1})$, and for all $n$ large enough and all $[s,t]\subseteq \RR$, we have
