	with the boundary data $h^2 = 0$, $( h^2 )' = \pm 2$ at $f_1^2 = 0$, $f_1^2 = L (t)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:43:18.951716+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_677b6ae31d620b24418c345c9d8d3ed64501e39af14685d66396b77e64750642","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem VEV of arXiv:2609.02409, 'Membranes and Maps'] [OP06:GW-H]
    The connected vacuum expectation value $\langle \mathcal{E}_{k_1}(z_1) \cdots \mathcal{E}_{k_n}(z_n) \rangle^{\circ}$ vanishes for $n>1$ whenever $k_1\leq 0$, $k_n\geq 0$, or $\sum_j k_j\neq 0$. If $k_1 > 0$, it satisfies the recursion
    \begin{equation}
        \left\langle \mathcal{E}_{k_1}(z_1) \cdots \mathcal{E}_{k_n}(z_n) \right\rangle^{\circ}
        =
        \sum_{i=2}^n
        \varsigma\Bigl(
            \det\begin{psmallmatrix} k_1 & k_i \\ z_1 & z_i \end{psmallmatrix}
        \Bigr)
        \left\langle
            \mathcal{E}_{k_2}(z_2) \cdots
            \mathcal{E}_{k_i+k_1}(z_i+z_1) \cdots
            \mathcal{E}_{k_n}(z_n)
        \right\rangle^{\circ} \,,
    \end{equation}
    with initial condition $\langle \mathcal{E}_{k}(z) \rangle^{\circ} = \frac{\delta_{k,0}}{\varsigma(z)}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:23:58.626933+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_677e3084d0464f74a01def323a9c165877efd9dad59b8a62d3f3c19d19818408","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 209 (The main below-top-order a priori estimates for the transport variables and the modified fluid variables) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] Let $N = \Ntop$ and let $\fluxcontrolVort_N(\ubar,u),  \dots, \bulkcontrolDivGradEnt_N(\ubar,u)$ be the $L^2$-transport-controlling quantities as defined in Def.\,\ref{D:FUNDAMENTALTRANSPORTL2CONTROLLINGQUANTITIES}. 
