{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:23:27.787642+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_67a3bba6cb7ae61d22b583a060cc6697d339688fb2db56d58326117e6ab17ce5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Dfn indices of arXiv:2606.09228, 'On topological indices of random caterpillar graphs'] Let $H=(V,E)$ be a graph with node set $V$ and edge set $E$.\\
    The Zagreb index is defined as
    \begin{align}
        Z_H:=\sum_{v \in V} (d(v))^2.
    \end{align}
For $\alpha \in \mathbb{R}$, the  $\alpha$-Randić index of $H$ is given by
    \begin{align}
        R_H^{[\alpha]}:=\sum_{\{u,v\} \in E} (d(u)d(v))^\alpha.
    \end{align}
If $H$ is connected, the Wiener index is defined as  
    \begin{align}
        W_H:=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{u,v\in V} \dist(u,v).
    \end{align}
If $H$ is connected and rooted, the level index is defined as 
    \begin{align}
        L_{H}:=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{u,v \in V} \vert D(u)-D(v)\vert.
    \end{align}
For a random graph $H$ of a class of rooted, connected graphs $\mathcal{H}$, the Gini index is given by
\begin{align}
G_H:=\frac{L_{H}}{\,{\mathbb{E}}[V]^2\,{\mathbb{E}}[D_\mathcal{H}^\star]},
\end{align}
where $D_\mathcal{H}^\star$ is the depth of a randomly chosen node in a random tree of class $\mathcal{H}$ (see [ma17] for more information).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:31.959035+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_67a3ea9616f66c172ddd223100695db1f17e016eedb46de31c97cd84dd52cb9a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 21 (Triangular array marginal for empty initial conditions) of arXiv:2512.02286, 'Pfaffian Transition Probability and Correlation Kernel of TASEP in Half-space'] Let $N$ be an even integer and let $x=(x_1,\dots,x_N)$ be the ordered coordinates of TASEP particles. Then the half-line open TASEP transition probability from an empty state to $x$ can be written as a sum over Pfaffian kernels indexed by Gelfand--Tsetlin patterns with endpoints fixed by $x=(x_1,\dots,x_N)$:
	\begin{equation}

		\mathbb{P}_t(\emptyset\to x) = (-1)^{\binom{N}{2}}\mathrm{e}^{-\alpha t} \sum_{z\in\mathsf{GT}_N(x)} \Pf\left[\Psi(z_i^N,z_j^N)\right]_{1\leq i,j\leq N},
	\end{equation}
	where we have defined
	\begin{equation}
		\Psi(x,y) := Q_{1,1}(x,y)
		= \alpha^2\oint_\contour \frac{\dd u}{2\pi\ii} \oint_\contour \frac{\dd w}{2\pi\ii} \frac{u-w}{1-u-w} \frac{w^{1-x}\mathrm{e}^{t(w-1)}}{(w-\alpha)(w-1)} \frac{u^{1-y}\mathrm{e}^{t(u-1)}}{(u-\alpha)(u-1)},
	\end{equation}
    where contour $\beta$, as in Definition \ref{defn:TASEP countours}, surrounds poles at $u,w=1,0,\alpha,1-\alpha$ and omits all other singularities of the integrand. The kernel $\Psi(x,y)$ is skew-symmetric under the interchange of $x$ and $y$ when $x,y\geq1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:26.945046+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_67a769ba0286720e9a90dce940ba5e535cc945fbb2681c2fabd386868e1e6f12","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition p:fin_bubble of arXiv:2505.09604, 'Exceptional force, uncountably many solutions in the KPZ fixed point'] The following holds on the event $\Omega_1$. Let $\xi \in \Xi$ and $(x_0,s) \in \mathbb{R}^2$ be such that 
