{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:43:55.610776+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_67a79fa4778308a78febc1a506a9ee8b8df14c35a9c68dbbb41aefaca240c10f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop: translation of arXiv:2604.05941, 'Banach spaces of continuous paths with finite $p$-th variation'] For any $p>1$ suppose that $x\in V^p_{\mathbb{T}}$ and $g\in V^p_{\mathbb{T}}$ with $[g]^{(p)}_{\mathbb{T}} \equiv 0$ are given. Then, the continuous function $y := g x \in C([0, 1])$ also belongs to $V^p_{\mathbb{T}}$, and admits finite dyadic $p$-th variation
