{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:13:18.528910+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_67ca218ac81b9217f92c2d9bc69708297683b39dfcb0ff023df145e17901936a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 5 of arXiv:2608.30658, 'Higher Regularity of Time-Periodic Solutions to Nonautonomous Hyperbolic Problems: Away fr'] Let $V$ be a vector space, $U\subseteq V$ be a subspace of $V$, and $\CC,\E: V\to V$ be linear operators. 
Assume that integers $m\ge 1$ and $k\ge 2$ are such that:
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item 
	If $(I-\CC^m)v\in U$  for $v\in V$, 
		then  $v\in U$;
\item 
$\CC u\in U$ and $\E u\in U$ for all $u\in U$;
