{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:07:48.568216+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_67fda46cbe737cf942456a45359ee3fd2c9b285acba0ba8eb9335f93d3b1f29a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 41 of arXiv:2609.01460, 'On cost-induced Santal\'o-type inequalities \\ in Polish measure spaces'] Let $\mu$ be an even, log-concave probability measure on $\R$ with density. 

For any pair of measurable functions $f, g:\R \to [0,\infty)$ and any non-decreasing measurable function $W: \R_+ \to (0, \infty)$ satisfying the pointwise relation
\begin{equation}

f(x)^{\frac{1}{2}} g(y)^{\frac{1}{2}} \leq W\left(\frac{|x-y|}{2}\right) \quad \text{for all } x, y \in \R,
\end{equation}
one has the functional inequality
\begin{equation}

\left( \int_{\R} f(x) \, d\mu(x) \right)^{\frac{1}{2}} \left( \int_{\R} g(y) \, d\mu(y) \right)^{\frac{1}{2}} \leq  \int_{\R} W(|r|) \,d\mu(r).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.931742+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_67ff12574206ab2f948102915138a235bd3a17f29d8a1919e936d67905fd4c61","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 21 (Relation between $q$, $Q$ and the stopping times $\sttm_k$) of arXiv:2506.19123, 'The longest increasing subsequence of Brownian separable permutons'] We have
