{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:41:29.025168+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_68024758d82a87d40ccda6a253603ef340f573b2f02fc40605bd2b9d79c7e20b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 3 (Janson, \cite{janson2013}) of arXiv:2608.26501, 'Explicit Bounds on the Entropy of Piecewise H\"{o}lder Graphon Models'] Let $W$ be a graphon defined on a set $\Omega$ with probability measure $\mu$. Then 
\begin{equation}
H\big(G(n,W)\big)\geq\binom{n}{2} \iint_{\Omega^2}h\big(W(x,y)\big)\dd\mu(x)\dd\mu(y),
\end{equation}
where $H\big(G(n,W)\big)$ is the entropy of $G(n,W)$. Further,
\begin{equation}
