{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:33:12.363362+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_68263775e3c566ce4e5625ea1a2a268e9dd4b15320b16d1088411a263f28fee9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 (Consistency and rate for \textup{($ii$)}) of arXiv:2608.29465, 'Deciding When to Decide:\\Testing Operational Suboptimality Under Distributional Shift'] Suppose the assumptions of Lemma~\ref{lem:termI_consistency} hold, specifically that the envelope $F(X)$ and the Lipschitz modulus $L(X)$ are square-integrable under the target distribution $\mathbb{P}_1$.
