{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.224410+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_686391690be0c0b7f0f2c792f1626779481c0caa30d465dfeec8a6e172c60641","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 (Orbit average of quadratic form on $\su(N)$) of arXiv:2607.17943, 'Coadjoint averaging and cross-scale fluxes in a fast-slow stochastic Euler-Arnold system o'] Let $\mathcal{O}^*(\Lambda)$ be the $\su(N)$ coadjoint orbit passing through $\Lambda=\text{diag}(i\lambda_1,...,i\lambda_N)$ for $\Lambda\in \su(N)$, as defined in \emph{(\ref{Eq:CoAdjointOrbitsuNIsospectral})}. For any $\Omega\in \mathcal{O}^*(\Lambda)$, consider the decomposition \emph{(\ref{Eq:ZeitlinExpansionVorticityAndStreamMatrices})}. Then we have
