up to null events. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:27:25.787033+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_686d1232f7b723ccf1a2149c098e1ba314dfabea74949f734f2359e08b38f6fc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor short-rectangle-vertical-oscillation of arXiv:2605.08052, 'Rapid phase ordering of Ising dynamics on $\mathbb Z^2$'] In the context of Proposition~(prop:vertical-maximum-bound-replacement of the paper), suppose $\ell \le \beta^2 e^{2\beta}$. For large $\bar \kappa$ (independent of $\beta$) and all $\beta>\beta_0$, we have 
