{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:06:07.078343+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_688908a3eafb50632fcd24845d67a8b74360bbb3ca6d80fa923f8e12e21cec86","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 11 (Log-concave bilinear forms) of arXiv:2608.27657, '\bfseries Stein Kernels and Normal Approximation\\ for Log-Concave Bilinear Forms'] Assume the estimates in \cref{thm:letwin}.  Let
\(X\in\R^m\) and \(Y\in\R^n\) be independent isotropic log-concave random
vectors, let \(0\neq B\in\R^{m\times n}\), and set
\[
