{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:43:43.239407+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_68bcec584d6c45f8db38e6b1e81090e6c3aee455c60e47237d5b06443168119c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop: bulk enhancement of arXiv:2506.21466, 'The Markov property for $\varphi^4_3$ on the cylinder'] For every $p \in [1,\infty)$, there exists $C>0$ such that for every $T>0$,
