{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.831423+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_68fd5b945218c1b04ebb6543a6685ff807ca15e54580a1fb286aa7e94df73104","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 14371 of arXiv:2606.29143, 'Comonotonic and moment matching approximations for sums of lognormal random variables'] Let $A = (a_1, ..., a_m)^{'}$ and $Q = (q_1, ..., q_m)^{'}$ be two numerical vectors with $\min(a_1, ..., a_m) \geq 0, \max(a_1, ..., a_m) > 0$ and $0 =q_0 < q_1 < q_2 < ... < q_m = 1$. Let $X$ be a continuous random variable and $X_{A, Q}$ be the step-weighted version of $X$. Then for any $p \in (0, 1)$ it holds that 
\begin{align*} 
\text{TVaR}_p[X_{A, Q}] = 
\frac{a_{l}(1 - p^{*})}{a(1 - p)}\text{TVaR}_{p^{*}}[X] + \sum^{m - 1}_{k = l}\frac{(a_{k + 1} - a_{k})(1 - q_k)}{a(1 - p)}\text{TVaR}_{q_k}[X]
\end{align*}
with $p^{*} = G^{-1}_{A, Q}(p) \in [q_{l - 1}, q_{l}]$ for some $l \in \{1, ..., m\}$ and $\sum_{k = m}^{m - 1} = 0$ by convention.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:53:30.538791+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_69020b0179fe40a9c4f1985ad5d00817eb4e56a95bcc2a3ff1b2200e6984e3dd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma-M_N martingale of arXiv:2505.24043, 'Weak solutions of Navier-Stokes Equation with purely discontinuous L\'evy Noise'] For every $n \in \mathbb{N}$, the process ${{M}}_{n}$ is a square integrable $\mathbb{F}$-martingale and 
\begin{align}

\sup_{n \in \mathbb{N}}\mathbb{E} \left[ \sup_{t\in [0,T]}\bigl\vert  {{M}}_{n} (t) \bigr\vert_{H}^2 \right]
&\leq C_2 \sup_{n \in \mathbb{N}}
\mathbb{E} \Bigl[   \int_0^{T} \int_{Y} \rvert P_n F(s, u_n(s),y)\vert_{H}^2 \, \nu(\mathrm{d} y) \, \mathrm{d}s
\Bigr]
\\
&\leq C_2 \sup_{n \in \mathbb{N}} \left( 1+ \mathbb{E} \left[ \int_0^T  \lvert u_n (t) \rvert^2_H \, \mathrm{d}t \right] \right) < \infty. 

\end{align}
Moreover, if Assumption F.(assum-F5 of the paper)  is satisfied,  then for every $p\in [2, 4+\gamma] $ and for every $n \in \mathbb{N}$, the process ${{M}}_{n}$ is a $p$-integrable $\mathbb{F}$-martingale
\begin{align}
\sup_{n \in \mathbb{N}}\mathbb{E} \left[ \sup_{t\in [0,T]}\bigl\vert  {{M}}_{n} (t) \bigr\vert_{H}^p \right]
&\leq C_p \; \sup_{n \in \mathbb{N}}
\mathbb{E} \Bigl[   \Bigl( \int_0^{T} \int_{Y} \rvert P_n F(s, u_n(s),y)\vert_H^2 \, \nu(\mathrm{d} y) \, \mathrm{d}s \Bigr)^\frac{p}2
\\
\nonumber
&\hspace{2truecm}+\int_0^{T} \int_{Y} \rvert P_n F(s, u_n(s),y)\vert_H^p \, \nu(\mathrm{d} y) \, \mathrm{d}s
\Bigr]
\\

&\leq C_p \sup_{n \in \mathbb{N}} \left( 1+ \mathbb{E} \left[ \int_0^T  \lvert u_n (t) \rvert^p_H \, \mathrm{d}t \right] \right) < \infty .
\end{align}
The constants $C_2$, $C_p$ are generic positive constants which can change from line to line but which do not depend on $n$.","status":"unverified"}

