{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.329354+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_694cd4bebb5f11d6b700c9f7e15fabaf5fe86057c39b11dc3ce712e170b071ec","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:spectral0 of arXiv:2606.01937, 'Stationary fluctuations for an exclusion process with mass and energy conservation'] Let $(f_i)_{i\ge 1}$ be a sequence of local functions from $\Omega$ to $\mathbb{R}$ that have disjoint supports, and assume that the support of the function $f_i$ has cardinality $\ell_i$ for any $i\ge 1$. Assume that $\psi_{f_i}(\rho ,\mathcal{E})=0$ for any $\rho\in [0,1]$, any $\mathcal{E}\in [\rho ,\kappa\rho ]$ and any $i\ge 1$. Finally, assume that the series $\sum_{i=1}^\infty \mathrm{Var}_{\rho ,\mathcal{E}}(f_i)$ converges. Then, we have
    \begin{equation}
        \left\|\sum_{i=1}^\infty f_i\right\|_{-1}^2 \le C_6\sum_{i=1}^\infty \ell_i^2 \mathrm{Var}_{\rho ,\mathcal{E}}(f_i).
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

