{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:03:35.744047+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_694f89fee3c28c2a3f26340479703b543eca19e11b4d7b11a47915b2d8d91695","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop rieszLaplaceLogFallback of arXiv:2609.02743, 'Sharp mean-field estimates for diffusive log/Riesz gases in the Hilbert--Schmidt regime'] Assume $0\le\mathsf{s}<\mathsf{d}/2$, $\mu\in L^\infty\cap\mathcal{P}({\mathbb{R}}^\mathsf{d})$, and $\beta>0$ is fixed.  If $\mathsf{s}=0$, assume in addition (equation eq:logEnergyAssumption of the paper) and (equation eq:logRateExtraAssumptions of the paper).  Then there are constants $C_{\beta,\mu}<\infty$ and, in the case $\mathsf{s}=0$, $c_{\beta,\mu}>0$ such that, for all $N\ge1$,
\begin{align}
