{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:23:27.793181+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6978d4f2937b051860c4827ef1b070115c4942b7a6f344572d163daef71a914f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop p.modcontGFF of arXiv:2606.11043, 'Thick points under Gaussian free field dynamics'] The process $(\Gamma_{\varepsilon}(x))_{\varepsilon, x}$ possesses a modification (that we also denote by $\Gamma_{\varepsilon}(x)$) such that for every $\alpha \in (0,1/2)$ and $\zeta, \delta>0$ almost surely there exists a constant $C=C(\alpha,\zeta,\delta)$ such that 
