{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:35:10.785556+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6978fd14fe8bc660dc72a7871ced62a5367dcccd0734bc9c59f83a52a52cddb1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 1 of arXiv:2604.00598, 'Allowing for Imprecision in the Game-theoretic Characterisation of the Poisson Process'] Suppose \(\gencapprocs\) contains all constant processes and is a cone---that is, closed under pointwise addition and multiplication with positive scalars.
