{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:53:39.112561+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_697dfc4750a6a94329964f9ccbdf95b33e4f8942c9454638a4580311401fa323","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 3 (Linear response-aware covariance envelope) of arXiv:2608.26877, 'When Is the Sharp Covariance Envelope Tight? Feature-Only Geometry for Volume-Sampled Leas'] Assume $m>d$, $L^*>0$, and $d<s<m$.  Define
\begin{equation}
 A=XG^{-1/2},
 \qquad z=\frac{e}{\sqrt{L^*}},
 \qquad B=[A\ z],
 \qquad b_i^\top=[a_i^\top\ z_i].

\end{equation}
Then $B^\top B=I_{d+1}$.  With
\begin{equation}
 h_i=\lVert b_i\rVert_2^2,
 \qquad q_i=1-h_i,
 \qquad R=\sum_{i=1}^m q_i a_i a_i^\top,

\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
 \alpha=\frac{m-s}{m-d},
 \qquad \beta=\frac{s-d}{m-d},
 \qquad \gamma=\frac{m-s}{m-d-1},

