{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:40:21.313766+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6993a242a84ead8521c077e3b80b2a4ae5024743971599890d9194e9bfa1a304","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 2 of arXiv:2604.08623, 'Central limit theorem for the Allen-Cahn equation with supercritical random initial condit'] Let $u$ be the solution to \eqref{eq:AC} with initial condition as above. Then, for any $t>0$ and 
  $x\in \mathbb{R}^d$, $u(t,x)$ is Malliavin differentiable. Furthermore, for all $y\in \mathbb{R}^d$ 
  the Malliavin derivative $D_{y} u$ solves
  \begin{equation}
    \partial_t D_{y} u(t,x) = \Delta D_{y} u(t,x) - 3\lambda u(t,x)^2 D_{y} u(t,x), \quad D_{y} u(0,x) = \rho(x-y).
  \end{equation}
  At the level of the rescaled solution $u_\eps$ defined in \eqref{eq:rescaled_u}, we have for any 
  $\eps > 0$, $t>0$ and $x,y\in \mathbb{R}^d$,
