{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:13:22.531688+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_69d28209ca6054c093c10b7962e469cec449ba3c959c7e8db15eae2ef9f63ff5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop good_cube_property of arXiv:2506.07158, 'The diffusivity of supercritical Bernoulli percolation is infinitely differentiable'] Given $d \geqslant 2$, $\mathfrak{p} \in (\mathfrak{p}_c, 1]$, $\mathsf{r} \in (\frac{4}{3}, 2)$, and $N \in \mathbb{N}$, there exist constants $C_{Me},\varepsilon_{Me}$ and $\{C_{Sc,k}, K_k, s_k\}_{k\geqslant 0}$ depending on $\mathfrak{p}, d, \mathsf{r}, N$ and a sequence of good cubes $(\mathcal{G}^{(N)}_k)_{k \geqslant 0}$ 
