{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.349942+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_69d443637366e8728ca9bb3e0b8f2fea1ef32ebc959f9067409411e6cd62d910","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th:non-conservative of arXiv:2412.01489, 'One- and two-particle spectral gap identities for the symmetric inclusion process and rela'] For all graphs $G=(V,(c_{xy})_{x,y\in V})$, and site weights $\alpha=(\alpha_x)_{x\in V}$, $\omega=(\omega_x)_{x\in V}$ with $\omega\neq 0$, we have
