{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.896081+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_69d5c052d1f63795b33ce9616b0cd982f8f873d7ac9427ebd48c4ac920983991","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 44 of arXiv:2508.04938, 'Perfect t-embeddings of doubly periodic Aztec diamonds'] Let~$0\leq \ell x'+i'\leq \ell N-1$,~$0\leq 2y'+j'\leq 2\ell N-2$,~$1\leq \ell x+i\leq 2\ell N-1$ and~$0\leq 2y+j\leq 2\ell N-1$, with~$i,i'=0,\dots,\ell-1$ and~$j,j'=0,1$, and set~$w=w_{\ell x'+i',2y'+j}$ and~$b=b_{\ell x+i,2y+j}$. Then 	
\begin{align}
& K^{-1}(w_{0,2y'+j'},b)
