{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.145958+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_69d628567989a18a822a52dd86f745a2dc3e1ce89990fb6a76423cbb29747df2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary corollaryatthebeginning of arXiv:2411.16103, 'Non-commutative Stein's Method: Applications to Free Probability and Sums of Non-commutati'] Let $ \mu_{k,n}$, with $k,n\geq 1$ be centered probability measures with uniformly bounded supports, such that 
\begin{align*}
\sum_{k=1}^{n}\int_{\mathbb{R}}x^2\mu_{k,n}(dx)=1,
\end{align*}
for all $n\geq 1$. Then, we can find a  constant $C>0$, independent of $n$, such that for large enough $n$, 
\begin{equation}
d_{TV}(\mu_{1,n}\boxplus\cdots\boxplus \mu_{n,n},\mathbf{s}) \leq C\sum_{k=1}^nm_{3}[\mu_{k,n}],
\end{equation}
where $d_{TV}$ denotes distance in total variation. In particular, if the $\mu_{k,n}$ are constant over $k$, 
\begin{equation}
d_{TV}(\mu_{1,n}\boxplus\cdots\boxplus \mu_{n,n},\mathbf{s}) \leq Cn^{-1/2}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:47:12.028828+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_69d7efc93b66defd77b204eaa7d84c6b98abb7d077eacb9e07fada20396fe4c9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:1* of arXiv:2512.09219, 'Strong confluence of geodesics in Liouville quantum gravity'] Fix $q\in (0,1/5)$ and $\Phi\in (0,1/10)$. 
   Then for all $b \in (0,1)$ sufficiently small (depending only on $q,\Phi$), the following is true. For all $z\in \mathbb{C},r>0$, there exist deterministic (depending only on $z,r,q,\Phi,b$) points $u_+,u_-,v_+,v_-$ satisfying $u_+,u_-\in B_{\Phi r}(z-r)$ and $v_+,v_-\in B_{\Phi  r}(z+r)$ such that the balls of Euclidean radius $2br$ around $u_+,u_-,v_+,v_-,u,v$ are all pairwise disjoint and the intersection of the following events, which we call $G_r(z)$, occurs with probability at least $q$.
   \begin{enumerate}
   \item  $\mathscr{X}_{u_-,v_-}^{u_+,v_+}$
   \item  $\Gamma_{u_+,u}\cup \Gamma_{u_-,u}\subseteq B_{\Phi r}(z-r)$ and $\Gamma_{v,v_+}\cup \Gamma_{v,v_-}\subseteq B_{\Phi r}(z+r)$.
   \item  $\mathrm{dist}(\Gamma_{u,v_+}\cup \Gamma_{u,v_-}, \{u_+,u_-\})\geq 2br$ and $\mathrm{dist}(\Gamma_{u_+,v}\cup \Gamma_{u_-,v}, \{v_+,v_-\})\geq 2br$

   \item $\mathrm{dist}(\Gamma_{u_-,u}\cup \Gamma_{u_+,u}, \Gamma_{v,v_-}\cup \Gamma_{v,v_+})\geq 2br$
   \end{enumerate}
   Further, the points $u_+,u_-,v_+,v_-$ can be chosen such that the family of events $\{G_r(z)\}_{z\in \mathbb{C}, r>0}$ is translation and scale invariant.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:37:08.317490+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_69d95bca0310b50a969da2d606c7db2fe4c6fe7057ae2f87ecfd8418af71a23a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:nonproductannulus of arXiv:2608.30973, 'Pseudo-Anosov flow and dynamics on guts'] Assume that \(M\) admits an almost pseudo-Anosov flow \(\varphi\) without perfect fits, and \(S\) is an embedded compact oriented taut surface in \(M\) positively transverse to \(\varphi\).
