{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:46.417805+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_69e20d670209ed448df19ebdea6c4c64a52ce0433507654656202563be82c690","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 8 of arXiv:2608.20252, '2608.20252'] A set $A$ belonging to $C([0,T], \Omega)$ or $\mathcal{D}([0,T],\Omega)$ is compact exactly when
