{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:03.891679+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_69fbe761617fbd4d20d8bf87758f3fff96367df3b6e06387a8a0a7601e5d552d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 (Cram\'er-type moderate deviation) of arXiv:2606.18866, 'Cram\'er-Type Moderate Deviations for Engel's Series via a Martingale Approach'] There exists an absolute constant $C>0$ such that the following holds. For every positive sequence $(b_n)_{n\geq 1}$ satisfying $b_n=o(\sqrt n)$, for all sufficiently large $n$, uniformly for $0\le x\le b_n$,
