{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:01:25.654079+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6a5b9aad69fb0edd78f60a31db6ce80af6584e3369f6e5b006641f4ce0f2ad77","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lm:Complex-Analysis-Lemma of arXiv:2605.16162, 'Deconfinement For $\mathrm{SO}(3)$ Lattice Yang--Mills at Strong Coupling'] Suppose $f$ is a holomorphic function on the disk $\mbb{D}(0,r)$ with $|f(0)|\geq m>0$ and $\sup_{z \in \mbb{D}(0,r)}|f(z)|\leq M <\infty$. Then for any $\epsilon \in (0,r)$ there exist a collection of disks $\{D_i\}$ of radii $r_i$ with $\sum_i r_i <\epsilon$ such that
