{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.364304+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6a73a04d05dc01af3c88b1bf71ffb184bac3261f92e01744d77a0225bf8e7f68","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:V_by_M of arXiv:2412.01645, 'Regularisation by Gaussian rough path lifts of fractional Brownian motions'] Let $F \in \mathcal{C}^2$. There exists a random variable $\Theta$ such that for all $x \in {\mathbb{R}}^d$, $s\in [0,1]$ and ${\color{blue}M}=(M, M') \in \mathcal{D}^{2H_-}_B([s,1])$, if $V$ is a solution of (equation eq:general_equation_Jacobian of the paper), then 
