{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.439663+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6a745cbbd9d7f42747c6bc3d20ce46cfd2c23faff9c4c07f64bd925179dfef0e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem repLin of arXiv:2509.26254, '$K$-Branching Random Walk with Noisy Selection: \\ \Large Large Population Limits and Phas'] For $g \in \mathcal{D}$, define $\omega(g):= \sup_{z \in \mathbb{R}}(g(z) + z)$. The following hold:
