{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.326473+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6a78b9303a9818cb80c18ef2f23a4be21f29652dff3bade1cb5985750fe64bab","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:intermediate_estimate_pressure_deterministic of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] Under the assumptions of Theorem (t:caccioppoli of the paper), for all $\alpha\in (0,1)$ and $\beta\in (\alpha,1]$, it holds that, a.e.\ on $\beta I\times \Omega$, 
