\end{align*}
Moreover, the constant $\tilde{\mathbf{C}}$ depends on $\lambda$, $C$ and $\mathbf{C}(\nu)$ given in (ass_meanfield of the paper) and is independent of $N\in\mathbb{N}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:27.032334+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6a80f7beef8acc665f75197f48f89a265987e6e76902f0c6f79a9af2e890e42b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition compapinningz of arXiv:2505.13382, 'The localization transition for the directed polymer in a random environment is smooth'] Given $p\in[1,2]$, there exit constants $C,u_0>0$ such that for all $u\in[0,u_0]$,
