{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:28:08.695680+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6a8e355e120770ee6c239753ea502b791f4d2818108447c1e47524a9a6661752","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2607.29536, 'Multi-hop visibility through the vacant set of Poissonian obstacles'] There exist positive constants $c=c(d,N,\mathrm{law}(\mathcal C))$ and $C=C(d,N,\mathrm{law}(\mathcal C))$ such that for any 
