{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:36:31.226184+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6aa8cf1b44a0c2d5be17bee3bf0a94336faa7c1256fa5fe20c94d35437f68f0d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2609.00537, 'Explicit Exponential Sum Estimates and Approximate Functional Equations for the Zeta Funct'] Let $N$ be a positive integer and $0<y<N+1$, and $\Delta=N+1-y$. We have the following estimates:

   \begin{equation}

-  \frac1{y(N+1)} 
- \frac1y \frac{\Gamma'}{\Gamma}(\Delta) \leq \sum_{\nu>N}\frac{1}{\nu(\nu-y)} - \frac1y  \log(N+1)

\leq 
  - \frac1{2y(N+1)} - \frac1y\frac{\Gamma'}{\Gamma}(\Delta). 
\end{equation}

\begin{align}

 \sum_{\nu>N} \frac{1}{\nu(\nu-y)^2} 
 \le& \frac{1}{y} \left( \frac{1}{\Delta^2} + \frac{1}{(\Delta+1)^2} + \frac{1}{\Delta+1} \right)  - \frac{1}{y^2} \left( \log(N+1) - \frac{1}{N+1} - \frac{\Gamma'}{\Gamma}(\Delta) \right).  \\

 \sum_{\nu>N} \frac{1}{\nu(\nu-y)^3} 
 \leq & \frac{1}{y} \left( \frac{1}{\Delta^3} + \frac{1}{(\Delta+1)^3} + \frac{1}{2(\Delta+1)^2} \right) 
 - \frac{1}{y^2} \left( \frac{1}{\Delta^2} + \frac{1}{\Delta+1} \right) 
 \nonumber \\
 & + \frac{1}{y^3} \left( \log(N+1) - \frac{1}{2(N+1)} - \frac{\Gamma'}{\Gamma}(\Delta) \right). \\

 \sum_{\nu\ge1} \frac{1}{\nu(\nu+y)^k} \leq & \frac{\log(y+1) + \gamma}{y^k} - \frac{q_k(y)}{2y^k(y+1)^{k-1}}  ,\ \text{for}\ k=1,2,3,
\end{align}
with
$q_1(y)=(y+1)^{-1}$, $q_2(y)=1+2y$, $q_3(y)=1+3y+3y^2$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.581244+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6aa96593272b6173b6e24d1a67557bf93a4a2d9caa5acec0caefdd1e8cbebfb2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemmanekvneneoneon of arXiv:2608.30443, 'On smooth holosphere solutions to compressible Euler equation'] The function $\Theta_{\rm main}$ is {positive and strictly increasing} on $[0,\frac 12]$. Moreover, pick universal constants $\frac{1}{\delta},\Theta^*\gg1$ {then for all} $0<b<b^*(\Theta^*,\delta)$, the unique solution to 
