{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:44:12.649076+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6aa9dee135a8de33e41d09980f5e44f0fbacdbc3322bd8e99db25a44556e73ab","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:most-dimred-good of arXiv:2512.04371, 'Constructive Approximation under Carleman's Condition, \\ with Applications to Smoothed An'] Suppose that  $m \gg \log(k/\epsilon)/\gamma^2$, then with probability at least $99\%$ over the randomness of $Q$, $1 - \epsilon$ proportion of the points $Q x$ satisfy that for all $i \in [K]$
