{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:09:15.295239+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ab38cf904d136a3b4364941c92d188c694942939a25fc36dd5047943a1aa89c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Tm Ito of arXiv:2411.05441, 'Sticky diffusions on star graphs : characterization and It\^o formula'] Let $X(t) = (i(t), x(t))$ be the process generated by (equation generator2 of the paper) and (equation eq:domain of the paper) with $\eta > 0$, started at $X(0) = \mathsf{x} \in \Gamma$, and let $f \in C_{b}^{1,2}(\mathbb{R}_+ \times \Gamma)$. Then,
	\begin{equation}
