{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:36:23.123904+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ac343b8acd0ad59cb23bf8929b95c679921bacf545bef5a58f9bb7acef5ff62","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm of arXiv:2506.18207, 'Cartan's Path Development, the Logarithmic Signature and a Conjecture of Lyons-Sidorova'] Under the same assumption of Theorem (windingangletheorem of the paper). If $\theta$ is piecewise $C^1$ on $[0,T]$ and $\theta_T-\theta_0\in(4k\pi+\pi,4k\pi+3\pi)$ for some integer $k$, then $\gamma$ has finite radius of convergence for its logarithmic signature.
\begin{proof}
It is implied by Corollary (ODEequivalence of the paper), Remark (piecewiseC2path of the paper) and the calculation in (equation signcalculation of the paper). Actually, we have 
\begin{equation*}
\begin{aligned}
&\int_l^{l+\pi}\rho_T^\lambda\cos(\varphi_T^\lambda-\zeta)d\zeta\\
\to&~e^{\lambda T}\prod_{k=1}^{n-1}\cos\left(\frac{\theta_{T_k+}-\theta_{T_k-}}{2}\right)\int_l^{l+\pi}\cos\left(\zeta-\frac{\theta_0}{2}\right)\cos\left(\zeta-\frac{\theta_T}{2}\right)d\zeta\\
=&\frac{e^{\lambda T}\pi}{2}\prod_{k=1}^{n-1}\cos\left(\frac{\theta_{T_k+}-\theta_{T_k-}}{2}\right)\cos\left(\frac{\theta_T-\theta_0}{2}\right).
\end{aligned}
\end{equation*}
W.L.O.G. we can assume the all the intersection angles $|\theta_{T_k+}-\theta_{T_k-}|<\pi$ for any $k$. Actually, we have to assume this to make the ODE system consistent on each piece $\gamma|_{[T_k,T_{k+1}]}$, otherwise the condition has to change. Because $\prod_{k=1}^{n-1}\cos\left(\frac{\theta_{T_k+}-\theta_{T_k-}}{2}\right)>0$, it follows that
$$
\int_l^{l+\pi}\rho_T^\lambda\cos(\varphi_T^\lambda-\zeta)d\zeta\to-\infty~~~\Longleftrightarrow~~~\cos\left(\frac{\theta_T-\theta_0}{2}\right)<0,
$$
which finishes the proof.
\end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:25:45.002330+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ac5ab1cd5836359c277434de59422a87c2d8597538db18b868a858a4b6502c4","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 32 of arXiv:2605.11801, 'A non-local singular non-linear Fokker-Planck PDE'] Let  $g \in C_T  \shc^{(-\beta)+}  $, $f_T \in  \shc^{(1+\beta)+}$.
	We say that $f  \in C_T  \shc^{(1+\beta)+}$ is a weak solution of \eqref{eq:PDE} if, for all $\varphi \in \mathcal S(\R^d)$,  $f$ satisfies
	\begin{align}
		&\langle  f_T,\varphi\rangle -\langle f(t),\varphi\rangle +\int_t^T \langle f(s) ,\frac12\Delta \varphi \rangle ds+ \int_t^T \langle \nabla f(s) B(s),\varphi\rangle ds    
		= \int_t^T\langle g(s),\varphi\rangle  d s, 
