	for all $t\in[0,T]$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:23:25.633617+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ac5b3c97e66775f9711017527b47e028e7a925a52139d2857ef249bf27e53f2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem L1 of arXiv:2609.01350, 'New classes of trace-form permutation polynomials and their compositional inverses'] Let $a, b \in \mathbb F_{2^n}$ , $b \neq 0$ and $f(x) = x^3 + ax + b, g(y) = y^2 + by + a^3$. Let $y_1$, $y_2$ be two roots of $g(y)$. The factorizations of $f(x)$ are characterized as follows:
\begin{enumerate}
\item $f = (1, 1, 1)$ if and only if ${\rm Tr}_2^{2^n} \left( \frac{a^3}{b^2} \right) = {\rm Tr}_{2}^{2^n}(1)$, and $y_1, y_2$ are cubes in $\mathbb F_{2^n}$ (resp. $\mathbb F_{2^{2n}}$) if $n$ is even (resp. odd);
\item $f = (1, 2)$ if and only if ${\rm Tr}_2^{2^n} \left( \frac{a^3}{b^2} \right) \neq {\rm Tr}_2^{2^n}(1)$;
\item $f = (3)$ if and only if ${\rm Tr}_2^{2^n} \left( \frac{a^3}{b^2} \right) = {\rm Tr}_2^{2^n}(1)$, and $y_1, y_2$ are not cubes in $\mathbb F_{2^n}$ (resp. $\mathbb F_{2^{2n}}$) if $n$ is even (resp. odd).
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:54:15.659503+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6acae3de64585c80bdd3f4259af0c44c52537bb1831fa9bbc717e34d63b7f509","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 of arXiv:2608.09700, 'A general paracontrolled ansatz for singular SPDEs'] One first sets
