{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.273599+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6af0c67f704638acf1c71d062f31fc2770177183dfa82a59921a91a608cfccd6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition proposition_RN_time of arXiv:2411.16452, 'Interface scaling limit for the critical planar Ising model perturbed by a magnetic field'] Let $t \geq 0$. The Radon-Nikodym derivative of ${\mathbb{P}}_{h}^{(\Omega,a,b)}$ with respect to ${\mathbb{P}}_{\operatorname{SLE}_3}^{(\Omega,a,b)}$ restricted to the $\sigma$-field $\sigma(\gamma(s): 0 \leq s \leq t)$ is given by
