{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:22:48.866782+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6b1b48bb436bd77177c5dbf8acdf9c35a402dd2d3b31048fb5c7e02e2fa80090","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 (One-mode Laguerre rigidity) of arXiv:2608.29143, 'Least Variability in a Polynomial-Square Class\\ of Rational Kernels'] Let \(a_*\in\Pcal_m\setminus\{0\}\) be a real optimizer, and let \(R_*\) be defined by \eqref{var:eq:R-def}. Assume the coefficient stationarity condition \eqref{var:eq:Euler-integral} and the scale-stationarity condition \eqref{rig:eq:scale-stationarity}. Then $\deg a_*\in\{m-1,m\}$.
More precisely, exactly one of the following alternatives holds:
\begin{align}
    \deg a_*&=m-1,
    &R_*a_*&=c\Lag_{m+1},\\
    \deg a_*&=m,
    &R_*a_*&=c\Lag_{m+2},
\end{align}
for some nonzero real constant \(c\).","status":"unverified"}

