{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:46:12.276133+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6b1f40d5818fc735ecb9e54222dbc5ad39ade93e66ede3d776c83ad2a29b0d1d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 32 of arXiv:2604.22159, 'Adapted optimal transport between filtered Gaussian processes'] [Adapted Brenier coupling between elements of $\cFG$] 
Let $\bX = \bG^{a, L}$ and $\bY = \bG^{b, M}$ be elements of $\cFG$. An adapted Brenier coupling between $\bX$ and $\bY$ is an element $\pi \in \Cpl_{\mathrm{bc}}(\bX, \bY)$ such that for all $t \in [N]$ and ($\pi$-almost) all $\omega_{1:(t-1)}^{\bX}, \omega_{1:(t-1)}^{\bY} \in \bR^{(t-1)d}$, the conditional distribution
\begin{equation} 
\pi_{t}(\dd \omega_{t}^{\bX}, \dd \omega_{t}^{\bY} \mid \omega^{\bX}_{1:(t-1)}, \omega^{\bY}_{1:(t-1)})
\end{equation}
of $(\epsilon_{t}^{X}, \epsilon_{t}^{Y})$ given $(\epsilon_{1:(t-1)}^X, \epsilon_{1:(t-1)}^Y) = (\omega^{\bX}_{1:(t-1)}, \omega^{\bY}_{1:(t-1)})$ solves the optimal transport problem
\begin{equation}
\inf_{\gamma \in \Cpl(\cN_d(0, I), \cN_d(0, I))} \int \| (\hat{X}_{t} + L_{t,t}\omega_{t}^{\bX}) - (\hat{Y}_{t} + M_{t,t}\omega_{t}^{\bY}) \|_2^2  \gamma(\dd \omega_{t}^{\bX}, \dd \omega_{t}^{\bY}).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.358888+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6b20bfd48525b6aec978b47d2c08e7a0acda47d54de7767d24aaacaf3f188dcb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition of arXiv:2509.23069, 'Every cutoff profile is possible'] Consider the sequence of FIT Markov chains $((Y^{(n)}_t)_{t\geq 0})_{n\geq 8}$ defined above. For every integer $q\geq 2$ and every $c\in {\ensuremath{\mathbb R}} $, as $n\to \infty$ we have 
    \begin{equation}
