{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:15:34.383590+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6b2549d324ef714dd1506767f35c30ea3f4f5c3132212246c8c913d00a3d42f0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 22 of arXiv:2609.03243, 'Weighted Ces\`aro type operators on the weighted Bergman spaces in the unit ball'] Let   $0<p<\infty$  and $r_k=1-2^{-k}$, $k\geq 1$. Define
\begin{equation*}
f_k(z)=\frac{(1-r_k^2)^{(n+1+\alpha)/p}}{\big(1-r_k\langle z,\xi\rangle\big)^{2(n+1+\alpha)/p}},\quad z\in\mathbb{B}_n.
\end{equation*}
Then for any sequence $\{c_k\}\in \ell^p$, $\sum\limits_kc_kf_k\in A_{\alpha}^p(\mathbb{B}_n)$ and 
\[
    \left\|\sum_{k}c_kf_k\right\|_{p,\alpha}\lesssim \Big(\sum_{k}|c_k|^p\Big)^{1/p}.
\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:24:20.641987+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6b26d5b7bf9a6a44aa79f2c2f2ec35159a1a69b92f97e6d3b0f42c96e223a440","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition of arXiv:2608.10415, 'Continuous random variables'] Given two algebras $(A,tr)$ and $(B,tr)$, the following hold:
