{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:43:53.593520+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6b475c5f749e4f2fc799bb0dc4819d4a4863586ae5a3e1940ad063760ac907ef","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:gammas of arXiv:2512.12902, 'Non-equilibrium fluctuations for the \\stirring process with births and deaths'] Let  $i,j\subset \{1,\dots,n\}$, $\zeta>0$,  $\epsilon<1$ and $\underline x=(x_1,\dots,x_n)$. Under {\bf Assumption 1} given in (equation Ass1 of the paper), for any {$0\leq \lambda\leq t$}, the following estimates hold:

