{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:00.614093+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6b4d2f9c17fa948ba325d9c2cc5e085fcc85b6b7a1ff931a7ed9c4ddf579f8cc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 16 ({\cite[Proposition 53) of arXiv:2510.27589, 'Geodesic switches and exceptional times in dynamical Brownian last passage percolation'] {BB23}}]

For any $(p,q)\in S_{n,\mu}$, let $\underline{V}^{\mathrm{ELPP}}_n(p,q)$ denote the set of points $z$ which are to the right of $\Gamma_p^q$ and satisfy $\Gamma_z^q\cap \{z: |\phi(z)|\leq n\}=\Gamma_p^q\cap \{z: |\phi(z)|\leq n\}$. Then there exist positive constants $C,c,K,\theta,\alpha$ such that for all $\varepsilon^{\alpha} n\geq K$, we have
