{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:05:57.807128+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6b932676b82a14fee2326951aab99bd028199d5bb94cb5f4c0ae4fe466dca00e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 of arXiv:2608.30570, '2608.30570'] A submanifold $\Sigma^n$ in ${\mathbb R}^{n+k}$ is a \textbf{translating soliton} for the mean curvature flow if there is a constant unit vector ${\bf T}\in {\mathbb R}^{n+k}$, such that
