{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:20:07.956554+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ba344c12fc5d1a017cb926d28138162f947c6bdc659ebd5f151a4e94abc97e2","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2608.30346, '\textbf{Classification complexity of homeomorphism group actions}'] Let \(G\) be a Polish group acting continuously on a Polish space \(X\). The action of \(G\) on \(X\) is \textit{turbulent} if
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item[(T1)] every orbit is meager,
        \item[(T2)] every orbit is dense, and
        \item[(T3)] every local orbit is somewhere dense, that is for any open \(U \subset X\), \( x \in U\) and open \(1_G \in V \subset G\), \(\mathcal{O}(x,U,V)\) is somewhere dense.
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:25:44.979339+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ba37630d36ab8f3aeaa2c0e990354cf501d50d48e17e7d536bf3f0d52840e1b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 35 (Quadratic layer second derivative) of arXiv:2605.11451, '2605.11451'] Let $L,D,W$ be $C^1$ functions on an interval $I\subset(0,\infty)$, with $L>0$, $D\ge0$, $W\ge0$, and assume all level roots below are simple. If $I$ is noncompact, assume the integrals below are finite and the truncation limits over compact exhaustions of $I$ have vanishing tails. Define, for $x>0$ and $q=x^2$,
\[
 F(x)=\int_I W(R)\frac12\Big((L(R)^2-(x+D(R))^2)_+ +(L(R)^2-(x-D(R))^2)_+\Big)\,\dd R,
\]
and $G(q)=F(\sqrt q)$. Then, in the distributional sense,
\begin{align}
4x^3G''(q)=&\ x\sum_{|L-D|=x}\frac{W(R)L(R)}{|(L-D)'(R)|}
+x\sum_{L+D=x}\frac{W(R)L(R)}{|(L+D)'(R)|} \notag\\
&\quad -\int_{\{|L-D|<x<L+D\}}W(R)D(R)\,\dd R.
\end{align}
Endpoint and repeated-root cases follow by the approximation procedure described in the proof.","status":"unverified"}

