{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:31:49.847637+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6baa0f91b2616b3570ee99e77ba06089930dee3fae38ce74a8d979bd7045aaa9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop: existence of solutions of arXiv:2608.23756, 'Measure-valued fluid limits for partial service queues\\with correlated patience and servi'] Let $\rho \in \mathcal{M}_F^+(\mathbbm{R}_+^2)$ be a probability measure that is stochastically smaller than the probability measure with density $g$. Specifically, 
