{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.385801+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6bba14ee03fc143c835ab0212bd4d9e782ac4d73fe2c3c86cf7eecc8d6397101","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma trans-lem of arXiv:2509.23086, 'On Optimal Markovian Couplings of L\'evy Processes'] Let $\mathcal{A},\mathcal{B}\in \mathcal{G}^\Lambda_2(\mathbb R^d)$, $m_\mathcal{A},m_\mathcal{B}\in\mathbb R^d$ be their mean vectors, and $\mathcal{J}\in\Gamma(\mathcal{A},\mathcal{B})$ be a Feller coupling of two L\'evy generators. For any $h=(\tau,\tau')\in\mathbb R^{2d}$, it holds 
