{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:15:46.791664+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6bceeb05f25f3a7704bc2d07658e8517fe2bdb1a9560b3f60b01c295841e4a72","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[OPEN PROBLEM - not a proved fact. Stated in arXiv:2511.05386, 'CLT for $β$-ensembles with Freud weights, application to the KLS conjecture in Schatten balls' (conjecture environment labelled conj:KLS).] There exists a universal constant $\mathbf{C}_\mrm{univ}>0$, such that for all $d\geq 1$, $f$ smooth on $\R^d$ and $\mu$ an absolutely continuous with respect to the Lebesgue measure and log-concave probability measure on $\R^d$:
 \begin{equation}
