{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:38:57.118117+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6bdd35ee2aff0c31424586f28805f1dc45199323a786aaaec38834df298f7f28","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 26 of arXiv:2604.04823, '2604.04823'] For any sufficiently large~$a\geq 1$, there exist $\hat\epsilon (a), \eta, \hat  \gamma,\lambda > 0$ such that for all~$\epsilon, h, \gamma$ with
    \begin{equation}
