{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:38:04.528655+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6c06cc08a67eb0cabc0a761848719766d0108aac715dd4eea1b69d17203b873b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2607.18011, 'From local giants to locality in long-range percolation'] \thlabel{lem:projected_network}
    Let $G$ be a transitive graph of polynomial growth with $d = 2$, let $J : V \times V \to \mathbf{R}_+$ be transitive and integrable, and suppose that $J(x,y) = O (d_G(x,y)^{-2 \alpha})$ with $\alpha > 1$.

