{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.578955+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6c0e57bdf66f7224bccae3e8c8b98bb11c765bd9ef5eb2682f5d0783b67f386e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: Delta_1 Roots of arXiv:2608.30443, 'On smooth holosphere solutions to compressible Euler equation'] Assume (equation eq: Parameters of the paper). For all $\sigma\ge 0$, the equation $\Delta_1(w,\sigma)=0$ has exactly three distinct root branches $w_1(\sigma)<w_2(\sigma)<w_3(\sigma)$ which satisfy the following:\\\\
\underline{relative positions}: $\forall \sigma \ge 0$, 
\begin{equation}

 -w_1(\sigma)\leq 0<w_e<w_2(\sigma)\leq 1<r\leq w_3(\sigma).
\end{equation}
\underline{monotonicity}: $\forall \sigma>0$, \ \ 
\begin{equation}

w_1'(\sigma)<0, \ \ w'_2(\sigma)<0, \ \ w_3'(\sigma)>0\ \ \mbox{for}\ \ \sigma>0.
\end{equation}
\underline{asymptotics}:
\begin{equation}

\left|\begin{array}{lll}
\displaystyle w_1(\sigma)=-\frac{dw_e}{r}\sigma^2+\mathcal O(\sigma^3),\\
\displaystyle w_2(\sigma)=1-\frac{d(1-w_e)\sigma^2}{r-1}+\mathcal O(\sigma^3),\\
\displaystyle w_3(\sigma)=r+\frac{d(r-w_e)}{r(r-1)}\sigma^2+\mathcal O(\sigma^3),
\end{array}\right. \ \ \mbox{as}\ \ \sigma \to 0
\end{equation}
and 
\begin{equation}

\left|\begin{array}{lll}
\displaystyle w_1(\sigma)=-\sqrt{d}\sigma +\mathcal O(1),\\[1mm]
\displaystyle w_2(\sigma)=w_e+\mathcal O(\sigma^{-2}),\\[1mm]
\displaystyle w_3(\sigma)=\sqrt{d}\sigma +\mathcal O(1)
\end{array}\right.\ \ \mbox{as}\ \ \sigma\to +\infty.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:15.338740+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6c0ec1d1a43be8cfbc1fe35e9850f108505f83b10da7cf385214f66d75179dcd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 6 of arXiv:2506.15044, '2506.15044'] Let $\mathcal{D}$ be a class of processes, and $X\in \mathcal{D}^\mathbb{C}$. Suppose that $(\tau_n)$ is an FS for $\mathbb{C}$.
\begin{enumerate}
  \item [$(1)$] $(\tau_n,X^{\tau_n})$ forms a CS for $X$.
  \item [$(2)$] If $\mathcal{D}$ is stable under stopping and localization, then $(\tau_n,X^{\tau_n})$ forms an FCS for $X\in\mathcal{D}^\mathbb{C}$.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

