{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:24:34.411615+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6c1811de2faf11292adb7e447181317b7a225ad1feadd11a3c854e48cd66101f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 25 of arXiv:2608.31070, 'Sub-Laplacians on Compact Lie Groups: Heat Kernels, Distance, and Zeta Determinants'] For every compact connected two-step pair $(G,L)$, there are $c>0$ and $N\ge0$ such that, as $t\downarrow0$,
		\begin{equation}
