{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:53.157222+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6c185061bde418b78b120cf6d03f68f93296885b77af0de64c0e3641bf7fa6f4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 13 of arXiv:2607.02108, 'A Two-Color Lift of the Shifted \texorpdfstring{$t$}{t}-Schur Measure'] For fixed $\lambda$ in the support of the $\lambda$-marginal,
\begin{equation}
        \Prob_q(\mu\mid\lambda)
        =\frac{Q_\mu(qX)Q_{\lambda/\mu}(X)}{Q_\lambda[X+qX]},
        \qquad \mu\subseteq\lambda.
\end{equation}
Consequently,
\begin{equation}
        \EE[u^B\mid\lambda]
        =\frac{Q_\lambda[X+uqX]}{Q_\lambda[X+qX]}.
\end{equation}
In particular,
\begin{equation}
        \EE[B\mid\lambda]
        =q\frac{\partial}{\partial q}\log Q_\lambda[X+qX],
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
        \Var(B\mid\lambda)
        =\left(q\frac{\partial}{\partial q}\right)^2
        \log Q_\lambda[X+qX].
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:06:18.015503+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6c1ca46a5cc75e22415405b3b3607de3b79e7fe10bc81af60820b6326eab4ef7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 8 (Laguerre inversion of the factorial Hankel matrix) of arXiv:2608.15137, '2608.15137'] Let $P\leq Q$ be positive integers, put $r=Q-P$, and define
\[
 H_{ij}=(P+Q-i-j)!,
 \qquad 1\leq i,j\leq P.
\]
Define
\[
 L_k^{(r)}(x)
 =
 \sum_{\ell=0}^k
 (-1)^\ell
 \frac{(k+r)!}{(k-\ell)!(r+\ell)!\ell!}x^\ell.
\]
Then $H$ is invertible and
\begin{equation}
 \sum_{i,j=1}^P
 x^{P-j}(H^{-1})_{ji}y^{Q-i}
 =
 y^r
 \sum_{k=0}^{P-1}
 \frac{k!}{(k+r)!}
 L_k^{(r)}(x)L_k^{(r)}(y).
\end{equation}
Moreover,
\begin{equation}
 \begin{aligned}
 \sum_{k=0}^{P-1}\frac{k!}{(k+r)!}
 L_k^{(r)}(x)L_k^{(r)}(y)
 &=\frac{P!}{(P+r-1)!}\\
 &\quad{}\times
 \frac{L_{P-1}^{(r)}(x)L_P^{(r)}(y)
 -L_P^{(r)}(x)L_{P-1}^{(r)}(y)}{x-y},
 \end{aligned}
\end{equation}
with the diagonal value defined by continuity. After multiplication by $\ee^{-y}$, the left side of \eqref{eq:hankel-laguerre-inversion} is the terminal equal-time finite-rank block in Theorem~\ref{thm:arbitrary-path-kernel}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:22:08.521201+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6c1d2bf1ac5c6447bc78683d8ad59b978174b2a616b5f5c2e0bf158b0440cc03","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:PTASEP-seed-linear of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] Let $H = \ell^2(\mathbb{Z})$.  The seed functions
