{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:29:21.908033+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6c346a6091808508ca8644fbcf75f827a946509c700d6ecc15dc54142d5a6623","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2608.01081, 'The Optimal Rate in the Averaged Random-Marginal Central Limit Theorem for Log-Concave Mea'] There is a universal constant $C$ such that, for every $n\ge1$ and every
