		\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:41:29.055796+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6c46a92bb89522e13eb4c3cea4bdaf95818cc282fd51de204513a95805a22e66","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 26 of arXiv:2608.26619, 'Uniqueness of Positively Curved Ancient Ricci Flows on Surfaces with Boundary'] If $v:\old\times(-\infty,0)\rightarrow\bR$ satisfies \eqref{eq_symmetry_v}  with $v(\cdot,t)\xrightarrow{C^\infty(\mathbb{D})} 0$ as $t\rightarrow -\infty$, and we define $\phi(x,t)=\frac{v(x,t)-v_R(x,t)}{x_1}$ as in Lemma \ref{lem_neumann}, then there exists some $T<0$ and $\gamma>0$ such that for any $-\infty<s<t\leq T$ we have
