{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:33:17.671600+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6c6b06a4d1cc5050844dfbab5a7b3980917d5c5bfb0b46dd1dd9088dd2e9d630","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 5 of arXiv:2607.10725, 'From the Airy line ensemble to the Gaussian free field'] For $x_1, x_2, t_1, t_2 \in \mathbb{R}$, we define the {\em extended Airy kernel} by 
