{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.287891+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6c9634935202ff72bcff77e50797117108f3cc2335aad5817061c2350f42a517","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:not:symProb of arXiv:2412.07710, 'An H-theorem for a conditional McKean-Vlasov process related to interacting diffusions on '] The space $\mathcal{M}_{\kappa, d}$  is the set of probability measures $\nu \in \mathcal{P}((\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d)^{1 + \kappa})$ that satisfy the following two properties:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item (Leaf Exchangeability) For any permutation $\tau$ on $\{1, \ldots, \kappa\}$, we have
        \begin{equation}

            \nu(dx_0, dx_{\{1, \ldots, \kappa\}}) = \nu(dx_0, dx_{\{\tau(1), \ldots, \tau(\kappa)\}}).
        \end{equation}
        \item (Edge Symmetry) $\bar{\nu}$ satisfies
        \begin{equation}

            \bar{\nu}(dx_0, dx_1) = \bar{\nu}(dx_1, dx_0).
        \end{equation}
    \end{enumerate}
    In addition, given $T \in (0, \infty)$, we define the space $\mathcal{M}_{k,d}^T$ to be the set of measures $\mu \in \mathcal{P}((\mathcal{C}_T^d)^{1 + \kappa})$ such that $\mu_t \in \mathcal{M}_{\kappa, d}$ for all $t\in [0, T]$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:42:55.300509+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6c978c7dbd62103832d64e29d52b714e6cd8eaf7746e1b59ee108497b250e0f2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 9 (Similarity-gauge invariance) of arXiv:2609.02362, '\textbf{Farthest-cell triplet entropy: high-dimensional shell limits and hyperbolic curvat'] Under a change of length unit $\metric'=c\metric$ with $c>0$, let
