{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:06:55.278424+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6c9ce1b1d8408a53c06b307e1de2243997d54b70fd8aea52df55e8056ba93b90","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:newS of arXiv:2601.08184, 'Wasserstein-p Central Limit Theorem Rates: From Local Dependence to Markov Chains'] Let $\{X_i\}_{i=0}^{n-1}$ be an $\mathbb{R}^d$-valued sequence such that $\sup_{0\le i\le n-1}\mathbb{E}\big[\|X_i\|^2\big] < \infty.$ Define the normalized variables $U_i := X_i/\sqrt{n}$ for $i\in\{0,\dots,n-1\}$ and $W := \sum_{i=0}^{n-1} U_i .$ Assume that $\mathbb{E}[W]=0$ and $\operatorname{Var}(W)=I_d$. Then,
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{W}_1\bigl(\mathcal{L}(W), \mathcal N(0,I_d)\bigr)
\;\lesssim\;
\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}\mathbb{E}\left[
\|U_i\|\mathcal{W}_2^2\bigl(\mathcal{L}(W), \mathcal{L}(W \mid U_i)\bigr)
\right].
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.462164+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6c9d58d0931568780b7ae7272634affb5057a29c6de65e98538deb6f7cf756d8","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 11 ({\cite[Section 2) of arXiv:2609.02561, 'NON-NEF LOCI IN MIXED CHARACTERISTIC'] {Les}}]
Let $D$ be an $\R$-Cartier $\R$-divisor.
We say that $D$ is:
\begin{enumerate}
\item
$f$-ample if its numerical class lies in the real cone generated by numerical classes of $f$-ample line bundles;
\item
$f$-nef if $(D.C)\geq 0$ for every irreducible curve $C\subset X$ that is closed in $X$ and satisfies that $f(C)$ is a closed point of $S$;
\item
$f$-big if $D|_{X_{\eta}}$ is a big $\R$-Cartier $\R$-divisor on $X_{\eta}$;
\item
$f$-pseudo-effective if $D|_{X_{\eta}}$ is a pseudo-effective $\R$-Cartier $\R$-divisor on $X_{\eta}$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.656589+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ca0b64444f7c6b64916217ae7ebc4acb27fa6e485fde3aad12ceb30b0f00d33","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 44 of arXiv:2609.01389, 'K-stability and birational rigidity of Fano 3-fold weighted complete intersections'] The defining polynomials of $X$ can be written as
