{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.114908+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ca3ced1e9d8b35788cec850fe4fd334d75be76d58b4ce342e0a76ec7bdfc74d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem LM41 of arXiv:2608.16170, '\bf On hitting time distributions of Markov processes with sub-Gaussian heat kernel bounds'] Let $X$ be a Borel right process on $(E,d)$ satisfying (AC), (H1a) and (H1b).

Let $B\subset E$ be a nearly Borel set of finite $1$-order capacity. Then for any $\lambda>0$, there exists a unique finite, positive measure $\nu^{(\lambda)}_B$ on $E$ with $\mathrm{supp}[\nu_B^{(\lambda)}]\subset \overline{B}$ such that
\begin{equation}
     p_B^{(\lambda)}(x):=\mathbb{E}^x[\mathrm{e}^{-\lambda \sigma_B}]=\int_E u_\lambda(x,y)\nu_B^{(\lambda)}(\mathrm{d} y),\quad \forall x\in E.
 \end{equation}
In particular, for any $\lambda>0$, 
\[
{\mathbb{P}}^x\left[\sigma_B\le t\right] \ge \emph{Cap}_{(\lambda)}(B)  \inf_{y\in \overline B} \int_0^t \mathrm{e}^{-\lambda s} p(s, x, y)\mathrm{d} s,\quad \forall t>0,x\in E.
\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:10:05.718829+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ca4ea6acb107feaf2d51cac58751fd766ae80626252807fe8992adea1442a27","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2608.17449, 'Spectral Simplicity and Joint Eigenvalue Densities\\ for a Non-Gaussian Brownian Time Chan'] As defined above, $\Omega_{\rm can}^{\rm G}$ and $M_g^{\rm G}$ satisfy
\begin{equation*}
