{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:11.409089+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ca9cb21daf5b86b205b693f2223eea8c6d785c769e54e3200bee1eb97453253","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 3 (In-expectation consequence and sharp global scale) of arXiv:2606.07931, 'Pointwise Complexity for Gaussian Fields:\\Upper Envelopes, Algorithmic Lower Bounds, and '] Under the assumptions of Theorem~\ref{thm:pointwise-gaussian}, there exists an absolute constant \(C>0\) such that
