{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:17.255625+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6cbc87cecccbf1699da4218eeeb2ab983a9b6a93e9a89d82bb9469a02cad3356","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition BB_HH of arXiv:2603.12774, 'Synchronization by noise for stochastic differential equations driven by fractional Browni'] For \( 0 < H < 1 \), let \( C_0^\infty(\mathbb{R}^-, \mathbb{R}^d) \) denote the space of smooth, compactly supported functions \( \omega: \mathbb{R}^- \to \mathbb{R}^d \) satisfying \( \omega(0) = 0 \). For \( \omega \in C_0^\infty(\mathbb{R}^-, \mathbb{R}^d) \), define
	\begin{align}
		\Vert \omega \Vert_{\mathcal{B}_H}
		:= \sup_{s,t \in \mathbb{R}^-} 
		\frac{|\omega(t) - \omega(s)|}
		{\sqrt{1 + |t| + |s|}\, |t-s|^{\frac{1-H}{2}}}.
	\end{align}
	The space \( \mathcal{B}_H \) is defined as the closure of \( C_0^\infty(\mathbb{R}^-, \mathbb{R}^d) \) with respect to this norm and is a separable Banach space.","status":"unverified"}

