{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:19:00.924237+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d337565d866d3e838c3ccb582873eb52906ff59966aeea8e0976d9d794d814c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 31 of arXiv:2608.20613, 'Random walks on wreath products \\and spectral gaps for coloured interchange processes'] Let $a_n(G)$ be the number of $\Sn_n$-spherical irreducible representations of $W_n(G)$, and let $f_n(G)$ be the number of these representations self-dual.  Then every minimal gap-determining family for $W_n(G)$ has cardinality $(a_n(G)+f_n(G))/2$.  Moreover,
