{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.055536+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d39b5746d5408b38e1e0a8ac1483407da88b35e700e132e0e4080dbd5487ca2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 12 (Limit of quadratic variation) of arXiv:2607.01629, 'Quadratic fluctuations of speed-change Kawasaki dynamics'] For every $f\in C^{\infty}\left(\T^{2d}\right)$, the limit quadratic variation $\left\langle{\mathcal M}(f)\right\rangle_t$ is characterized by
