{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:38:57.117191+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d3f9f485e8b95e3b958effe8d957d6f8ee01a1004bd465f25b861650c535cfd","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 14 of arXiv:2604.04823, '2604.04823'] Let~$\chi$ be as in Definition~\ref{d:P-perturb-def} and fix 
    \begin{equation}
        \tilde a = \paren*{2\frac{\lambda_{d-1}}{\lambda_u}\norm{\chi'}_{L^\infty}}^\frac{1}{2}\quad\text{and}\quad \rho\defeq 2(1+\tilde a)\,.
    \end{equation}
    For any $a,\epsilon>0$ such that $\rho a\sqrt{\epsilon}<r_0/2$, define~$\hat P\colon \T^d \to [0,\infty)$ by
