{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.314927+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d49cc1fd312efd108bcf0ce0165203edeea464889335a548b8ddab275912b78","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition pro:2 of arXiv:2411.14921, 'A boundary Harnack principle and its application to analyticity of 3D Brownian intersectio'] For each $w>0$, there exist $M_0=M_0(w)<\infty$ and $a_3=a_3(w)>0$ such that for $x\in\partial \mathcal B_0$ and $n'\geq n\geq 1$,
