{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:15:08.951511+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d54cbc488221550d0144c3a17f97c8c70a54bdbfe385010110e8957d070496e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Definition_virtual_block of arXiv:2411.10829, 'Airy$_\beta$ line ensemble and its Laplace transform'] For a block process $\vec \mathbf p$, a compatible \emph{virtual block process} is a vector $\vec\boldsymbol{\upsilon}=(\boldsymbol{\upsilon}_1,\ldots, \boldsymbol{\upsilon}_m)\in (\mathbb R_+\cup \{\varnothing\})^m$ satisfying the following conditions: for each $\ell \in \llbracket 1,m\rrbracket$,
\begin{itemize}
    \item if $\boldsymbol{\upsilon}_\ell\neq \varnothing$, then $\mathbf Q_{\ell-1}+\boldsymbol{\upsilon}_\ell < \min\bigl( \bigcup_{j=1}^{m+\mathbf u}\mathbf \Delta_{j,\ell}\cup \{\mathbf Q_\ell\}\bigr)$;
    \item if $\ell=1$, or $\ell>1$ and $\mathbf p_\ell(\mathbf Q_{\ell-1}-)=0$, then $\boldsymbol{\upsilon}_\ell=\varnothing$.
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:26.943498+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d55c8c638a32d19633d3ccb5dad7095fcb89b1a618fe1e97952deee3c5abb98","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:+-ord of arXiv:2505.09604, 'Exceptional force, uncountably many solutions in the KPZ fixed point'] On the event $\Omega_1$, for all $\xi \in \Xi$ and $b \in \mathcal{F}^\xi$, 
 \begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*), font=\normalfont]
   \item If $x_1 < x_2$ and $g_{(x_1,t)}^{b,L}(s) = g_{(x_1,t)}^{\xi +,L}(s)$ for all $s \le t$, then $g_{(x_2,t)}^{b,L}(s) = g_{(x_2,t)}^{\xi +,L}(s)$ for all $s \le t$.
   \item  if $x_1 < x_2$ and $g_{(x_2,t)}^{b,L}(t) = g_{(x_2,s)}^{\xi -,L}(t)$ for all $s \le t$, then also $g_{(x_1,t)}^{b,L}(t) = g_{(x_1,t)}^{\xi -,L}(s)$ for all $s \le t$. 
    \end{enumerate}
    The same holds if we replace $L$ with $R$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.333600+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d569ad2ec053d9d1f7588066cc85b0cdcb2b1617fb5154704b6ec8e50b33810","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma ABlongconnection of arXiv:2603.05467, 'Thresholds for colouring the random Borsuk graph'] Let $ \lambda>\lambda_c $ and $ \varepsilon,\delta>0 $ be arbitrary with $ \lambda\geq \delta $. Then, there exists a $ k=k(\lambda,\varepsilon,\delta) $ such that for all large enough
	$ \ell\geq\ell_0(\lambda,\varepsilon,\delta,k) $ it holds that
	\begin{equation*}
		\mathbb{P}_{\lambda,\delta,R}(E_{\ell,k,R})>1-\varepsilon,
	\end{equation*}
   for all admissible $ R $ with $B(x,k) \subseteq R $ for some $ x\in B(\underline{0},\ell) $. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:49:05.413938+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d5ae81aa2a085365e896a06718ce882e0817e772c726c92dca650d44c5e63bd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:peierls_argument of arXiv:2601.07808, 'Supercritical long-range percolation on graphs of polynomial growth: the truncated one-arm'] \label[lemma]{lem:peierls_argument}
    Let $G$ be a transitive graph of polynomial growth with $d \geq 2$.

    There exists $c_{\mathrm{pei}} = c_{\mathrm{pei}}(G) > 0$ such that

    \begin{equation}

        \#
        \{
            A \in \mathcal{A} 
            : 
            A \ni x, 
            \# \partial A = m
        \}
        \leq 
        \exp(c_{\mathrm{pei}} m)
    \end{equation}  

    for all $x \in G$ and $m \in \mathbf{N}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.894815+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d5b73dd56bec40992b2d9475f0884ce005dfd5489842fff8f127f6d51de4496","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 28 of arXiv:2508.04938, 'Perfect t-embeddings of doubly periodic Aztec diamonds'] Let~$w_0, b_0, w_{n-1}, b_{n-1}$ be the boundary vertices of the reduced Aztec diamond~$A'_n$. Then
\begin{align} 
K^{-1}|_{\partial_n}:=\frac{K_{\operatorname{reduced}}^{-1}(w_0, b_0)\cdot K_{\operatorname{reduced}}^{-1}(w_{n-1}, b_{n-1})}
{K_{\operatorname{reduced}}^{-1}(w_0, b_{n-1})\cdot K_{\operatorname{reduced}}^{-1}(w_{n-1}, b_0)} 
\end{align}
is invariant under the shuffling algorithm. More precisely, if the reduced Aztec diamond~$A'_{n-1}$ obtained from~$A'_n$ by the shuffling algorithm described above, then
\[K^{-1}|_{\partial_{n-1}}=K^{-1}|_{\partial_n}.\]
In particular, $K^{-1}|_{\partial_{n}}=K^{-1}|_{\partial_{2}}=-X_{v^*}$, where $X_{v^*}$ is the face weight of the only face of the reduced Aztec diamond~$A'_2$ obtained from~$A'_n$ by the shuffling algorithm.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:15:16.647898+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d5c6dadb4e30ab8c14edb6a30c08910c2bd7fb855f4e44bab110228efd44f11","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2608.30736, 'Stability results for distribution-dependent stochastic Volterra equations'] Under the assumptions of Theorem~\ref{theorem:approximation} for all compact $K \subset \bR^d$ there is an $C > 0$ such that
  \begin{align*}
    \bE[|X_n(t,x)-X_n(t',x)|^p] & \leq C|t'-t|^{\gamma p},\\
    \bE[|M_n(t,x)-M_n(t',x)|^p] & \leq C|t'-t|^{\gamma p},\\
    \bE[|A_n(t,x)-A_n(t',x)|^p] & \leq C|t'-t|^{\gamma p},
  \end{align*}
  for all $n \in \bN$, $x \in K$, $(t,t')\in \Delta_T$, $p \geq 1$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:46:25.317361+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d5c93666d656cdff3ffb5f36fc0b5ca1e1ee4297cd7cef2022f6e3d71942d43","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor co:spectral-dimension of arXiv:2604.14122, 'The scaling limit of random walk and\\ the intrinsic metric on planar critical percolation'] Let $\beta$ be the scaling exponent of the CLE$_6$ resistance metric defined in~[my2025diffusion]. Let $\mathrm{P}_0$ denote the law of the simple random walk on the IIC starting at $0$, let $\mathrm{p}_{2t}(0,0)$ denote its return probability after $2t$ steps, and let $\tau_n$ denote its hitting time of $\partial B(0,n)$. Under $\mathbf{P}_{\mathrm{IIC}}$, almost surely,
    \begin{align*}
    \mathrm{p}_{2t}(0,0) &= t^{-\frac{91/48}{91/48+\beta}+o(1)} \quad\text{as } t\to\infty ,\\
    \quad \mathrm{E}_0 \tau_n &= n^{91/48+\beta+o(1)} \quad\text{as } n\to\infty .
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.280551+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d5d0977fe5705887a87e04662634eae5760a1b4e807e2297e35e5061a526aa6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem L^2 of arXiv:2603.14302, 'On Partition Functions for Time-Inhomogeneous Branching Random Walks'] [Time-inhomogeneous $L^2$ Critical Parameter $\bar{\beta}_2$]

The $L^2$-critical parameter in time-inhomogeneous environment, defined by:
\begin{equation*}
\bar{\beta}_2 := \sup_{\beta \geq 0} \left\{ \sup_{n \geq 0} \mathbb{E}\left[ \left( W_n^\beta \right)^2 \right] < \infty \right\}
\end{equation*}
exists and equals to $\bar{\beta}_2 = \sqrt{\log d}$ (in particular, the $L^2$ critical parameters in both cases coincide).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:00:22.779137+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d5e19e93428f3e547bc813e8c9d7a0ce9620552bf555c200bc5749193d05d6f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem::Paffian_mixed of arXiv:2411.01467, 'Conformal covariance of connection probabilities \\ in the 2D critical FK-Ising model'] Let $x_1^a<x_2^a<\ldots<x_{N}^a<x_{N+1}^a<x_{N+2}^a$ be vertices in $a\mathbb{Z}\cap \mathbb{R}$. Consider Ising model\footnote{The results in Lemma~(lem::Paffian_mixed of the paper) hold for generic inverse temperature $\beta\geq 0$.} on $a(\overline{\mathbb{H}}\cap \mathbb{Z}^2)$ with the mixed boundary condition~(equation eqn::Ising_bc_mixed of the paper). If $N=2n$, then we have 
	\begin{align*}
		\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{H}}^{(a,\mathbf{m})}\left[\sigma_{x_{1}^a}\cdots \sigma_{x_{2n}^a}\right]=\sum_{\varpi\in\Pi_n}\mathrm{sgn}(\varpi)\prod_{\{c,d\}\in \varpi}  \mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{H}}^{(a,\mathbf{m})}\left[\sigma_{x_c^a}\sigma_{x_d^a}\right].
	\end{align*}
	If $N=2n+1$, then we have 
	\begin{align*}
		\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{H}}^{(a,\mathbf{m})}[\sigma_{x_1^a}\cdots \sigma_{x_{2n+1}^a}]=\sum_{\varpi\in\Pi_{n+1}}\mathrm{sgn}(\varpi) \mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{H}}^{(a,\mathbf{m})}[\sigma_{x_{c'}^a}] \times\prod_{\{c,d\}\in \varpi\atop 
		d\neq 2n+2} \mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{H}}^{(a,\mathbf{m})}\left[\sigma_{x_c^a}\sigma_{x_d^a}\right],
	\end{align*}
	where $c'$ denotes the index paired to $2n+2$ in $\varpi$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:28:08.659100+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d5fc32f224c39b50a4a46fd36f2b41607bd385182e857488c4b7c450c3a708b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 7 of arXiv:2607.29327, 'Fractal Random Variables\\ Defined by Probability Distributions of Digits\\ of Their $G_2$'] If matrix of transition probabilities $||p_{in}||$ contains only one zero,
  then random variable $\tau$ has

  1) a pure discrete distribution with a countable point spectrum
  \begin{equation}

    D_\tau = \{\Delta^{G_2}_{(1-i)}, \;
      \Delta^{G_2}_{\underbrace{\scriptstyle ii...i}_k(1-i)}, \; k\in N\},
  \end{equation}
  if
  $p_{[1-i]i}=0$;

  2) singularly continuous distribution of Cantor type
  with a self-similar fractal spectrum
  \begin{align}

    \nonumber
    S_{\tau} &= C[G_2, \overline{[1-i][1-i]}] \\
    &= \{x=\Delta^{G_2}_{\alpha_1...\alpha_n...}, \;
      \alpha_k\alpha_{k+1}\ne \overline{[1-i][1-i]} \; \forall k\in N\},
  \end{align}
  whose Hausdorff--Besicovitch dimension is a solution of equation
  \begin{equation}

    |g_i|^x+|g_0g_1|^x=1,
  \end{equation}
  if
  $p_{[1-i][1-i]}=0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:26.259279+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d644cca4ed888b1461ae3a2d258d2c399e3ee3e295842f7fcd9d24f8213bcf2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 93 of arXiv:2605.23308, 'Convergence rate estimates for semigroups and heat kernels associated with resistance form'] Suppose that $\mu$ satisfies $\rm{(A1)}$ and
take $x\in F$ and $B(x_0,r)\neq F$. Then the following hold.
\begin{itemize}
  \item Under $\rm{LRES}(\theta)$, we have $E_x[\sigma_{B(x_0,r)^c}]\geq \left(\frac{1}{4}c_{\rm{LR}}\right)^{1+s_0}c_l r^{(1+s_0)\theta}.$
  \item Under $\rm{URES}$, we have $E_x[\sigma_{B(x_0,r)^c}]\leq  c_u c_{\rm{UR}}r^{1+s_1}$.
\end{itemize}
In particular, if both of those hold, we have $(1+s_0)\theta\geq 1+s_1$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:09:15.295390+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d66633d717300f90e6e90cad38eb66db206e6c1fefbfa0efd82bb354e50e8df","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop Feynman-Kac of arXiv:2411.05441, 'Sticky diffusions on star graphs : characterization and It\^o formula'] Let $T > 0$ and $u \in C^{1,2}_b((0,T) \times \Gamma) \cap C_b([0,T] \times \Gamma)$  be a solution to
 \begin{equation}
  \begin{cases}
   -\partial_t u(t,\mathsf{x}) - L u(t,\mathsf{x}) = f(t,\mathsf{x}) \quad & \textnormal{for all } t \in (0,T), \, \mathsf{x} \neq \mathsf{v}, \\
   u_i(t,0) = u_j(t,0) \quad & \textnormal{for all } 1 \leq i, j \leq N, \, t \in (0,T), \\
   -\eta \partial_t u(t,\mathsf{v}) - \sum_{i=1}^N \rho_i \partial_x u_i(t,0) = \eta \theta(t) \quad &  \textnormal{for all } t \in (0,T), \\
   u(T, \cdot) = u_T,
  \end{cases}
 \end{equation}
 with $f \in C([0,T], PC(\Gamma))$, $u_T \in C_b(\Gamma)$ and $\theta \in C([0,T])$. Then
 \[
  u(t,\mathsf{x}) = \mathbf E \left[u_T(X(T)) + \int_t^T f(s,X(s)) \mathbf 1_{\{X(s) \neq \mathsf{v} \}} + \theta(s) \mathbf 1_{\{X(s) = \mathsf{v} \}} ds \big \vert X(t) = \mathsf{x} \right ],
 \]
 where $X$ is the sticky diffusion generated by $L$ with stickiness $\eta$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.354621+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d6749b984721f5bcc8bd137e6636849261698cff1d83d962f37f577c1a5e7a9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:control_mesoscopic of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] Suppose that Assumption (ass:forcing_regularity_iteration of the paper) holds. Let $\mu>0$, $r\in (1,\infty)$ and $p_0\in (2,p)$.
Fix $0<\gamma_0< (1-\frac{2}{p}-\frac{d}{q})\wedge (1-\frac{2}{p_0})$.  
Then there exist constants 
$$
L_0\geq 1\qquad \text{ and } \qquad \eta\in (0,1/4],
$$ 
depending only on $\mu,p,q,r,p_0,d$ and $\gamma_0$, for which the following assertion holds whenever $N\geq 1$ and $m\geq 1$ satisfy 
$$
N^{-1}\leq \eta^{m-1} L_0^{-1}.
$$
For all local solutions $(v^N,\pi^N,(\widetilde{\pi}^N_{k,\alpha})_{k,\alpha})$ to the stochastic Stokes system (equation eq:turbulent_Stokes_scaling_original_iteration of the paper) on $Q$, it holds that 
\begin{align*}
\Big({\mathbf E} \Big\|v^N -\fint_{\eta^\ell B} v^N  \Big\|_{\underline{L}^2(\eta^\ell Q)}^{r}\Big)^{1/r}
 \leq \eta^{\ell \gamma_0}
\mathcal{L}_{Q}^\#,\\
\Big({\mathbf E} \Big\|\pi^N -\fint_{\eta^\ell B} \pi^N  \Big\|_{\underline{L}^2(\eta^\ell I;\underline{H}^{-1}(\eta^\ell B))}^{r}\Big)^{1/r}
 \leq \eta^{\ell \gamma_0}
\mathcal{L}_{Q}^\#,\\
\Big({\mathbf E} \Big\|\Big( \widetilde{\pi}_{k,\alpha}^N -\fint_{\eta^\ell B} \widetilde{\pi}_{k,\alpha}^N\Big)_{k,\alpha} \Big\|_{\underline{L}^{p_0}(\eta^{\ell} I;\underline{L}^2(\eta^\ell B; \ell^2))}^{r}\Big)^{1/r}
 \leq  \eta^{\ell \gamma_0}
 \mathcal{L}_{Q}^\#,
\end{align*}
for all $\ell\in \{1,\dots,m\}$,
where $\mathcal{L}_{Q}^\#$ is the sharp Lebesgue-energy of $(v^N,\pi^N,(\widetilde{\pi}^N_{k,\alpha})_{k,\alpha})$ at (large) scale $Q$, i.e.,\begin{align}
\nonumber
\mathcal{L}_Q^{\#}
=&\Big( \max\Big\{{\mathbf E} \|F \|_{\underline{L}^p(I;\underline{L}^q(B))}^r,\,
{\mathbf E} \|G \|_{\underline{L}^p(I;\underline{L}^q(B))}^r , \,
{\mathbf E} \Big\|v^{N} -\fint_{B} v^{N}\Big\|_{\underline{L}^2(Q)}^r
,\\

&{\mathbf E} \Big\|\pi^{N}-\fint_{B} \pi^{N}\Big\|_{\underline{L}^2(I;\underline{H}^{-1}(B))}^r,\, 
{\mathbf E} \Big\|\Big( \widetilde{\pi}_{k,\alpha}^{N}-\fint_{B} \widetilde{\pi}^{N}_{k,\alpha} \Big)_{k,\alpha}\Big\|_{\underline{L}^{p_0}(I; \underline{L}^2(B;\ell^2))}^r \Big\}\Big)^{1/r}.
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.897274+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d6833f661a179b9ff47484bdac5cb393f6d65eebde41499e190d7e6efef8088","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 59 of arXiv:2508.04938, 'Perfect t-embeddings of doubly periodic Aztec diamonds'] For~$z\in \CC\backslash \RR$, let~$u=(u_1,u_2)$ and~$v=(v_1,v_2)$ be right and left eigenvectors of~$\Phi(z)$, respectively, associated with the same eigenvalue. Then  
\begin{equation*}
\im(u_1\overline{u_2})\im \left(\frac{v_1\overline{v_2}}{z}\right)>0.
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:04:59.429827+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d6e9bf92b170ab6850a889c25cfcfd87c972b958a61d3485e75af7ca74a1f2b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem weak_convergence_alpha_quantile of arXiv:2605.20471, 'Note on the Weak Convergence of Hyperplane $α$-Quantile Functionals and Their Continuity i'] Let $\alpha \in (0,1),t>0,\gamma \in \mathbb{R}^d$. Let $X^n\Rightarrow X$. Suppose that for all $\varepsilon >0$ we have, alternatively:
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item $P(M_{t,\beta}(X)>M_{t,\alpha}(X)+\varepsilon)\to 0$ as $\beta \downarrow \alpha$ or,
		\item $P(X \in C_{\mathbb{R}^d}[0,\infty))=1$;
	\end{enumerate}
	Then $M_{t,\alpha}(X^n)\to^{\textnormal{w}}M_{t,\alpha}(X)$ in the usual sense.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:11:09.326834+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d740b8295a17e9be2098f062f5208c32c1292f7f81afaf1857698c9a2fc3d1c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lem-1d-soln of arXiv:2411.06301, 'Inverting the operation of conditioning a branching process on extinction'] Let $k\in \mathbbm N$ such that $\mathbbm P_k[X_k(1) \geq 2] > 0$, which in particular holds for $k=1$. There exists a unique $\eta_k  \in (0,\infty)$ satisfying 
\begin{equation}   
g_k(0,\dots, 0,\eta_k , 0 ,0,\dots) = \eta_k 
\end{equation} 
where here the input of $g_k$ has 0s in all components but the $k$th, which is $\eta_k $. 
Furthermore, for each $d\geq k$, 
\begin{equation}  
\lambda_k^d \leq \eta_k  .
\end{equation}  
Finally, if $t > 1$ is as in Assumption~(item-gf-perturb-infty of the paper) and $\phi,\psi$ are as in Assumption~(item-gf-growth-infty of the paper), then for all integers $d \geq k \geq 1 $, 
\begin{equation}  
\lambda_k^d \leq \phi(k) \log t + \log\psi(k)  .
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:00.616568+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d7b0100e7427214d46a11b3675bf80c745f8e7db4b64f4de07c7935e253532e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 50 of arXiv:2510.27589, 'Geodesic switches and exceptional times in dynamical Brownian last passage percolation'] Fix $\delta\in (0,1/10]$. Then there exist positive constants $n_0,\ell_0$ such that for all $n\geq n_0,\ell\geq \ell_0, 0<\beta<n$, we have
  \begin{equation}

        \PP(\TF_\ell(\Gamma_{\0}^{(\beta n,n),t})\leq \beta\ell^{2/3+\delta}\textrm{ for all } t\in [0,1])\geq 1-Ce^{-c\ell^{3\delta}}.
  \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:45.032857+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d7b3fac1cbd4ddd2a5342f3e4f52875ce414f80e4384483371cc3bdb841ebb1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 22 (Extremum Principle for rough functions) of arXiv:2606.07290, 'Boundary behaviour of the Volterra square-root process'] Let $f \in S_{L, \gamma}$. If $f(t) \geq 0$ for all $t \in (0, t_*]$ and $f(t_*) = 0$ for some $t_* \in (0, T)$, then
\begin{equation}
    (D_L f)(t_*) \le 0.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:00:46.839632+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d7bae4d573868a9b3233851d6a4dcb7b761c1e94bd5a2d17862e01742de4880","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 6 of arXiv:2608.13374, 'Nearly Sharp Comparison Results for sliced and max-sliced Wasserstein distances'] Fix $\epsilon > 0$. For every $\theta \in \mathbb{S}^{d-1}$ and datum $(u,z,r) \in \mathbb{S}^{d-1}\times \R^d \times \R_{> 0}$ with $\rho = r\epsilon$,
\begin{equation}
    \lVert{\theta_\#(\la^{(\rho)}_{(u,z,r)}-\la_{(u,z,r)})\rVert}_{\mathrm{KR}} \leq C_{d,g} r \min\sbrac{\epsilon, \frac{\epsilon^{d+2}}{\beta^{d+1}}},
\end{equation}
where $\beta := (1 - \abrac{u,\theta}^2)^{1/2}$ and the second term in the minimum is interpreted as $+\infty$ when $\beta = 0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:30:36.797564+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d7d5b97d949751c55cc57774b14b65d67e8550da0ca2d5cfaf76088da3b0849","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 36 (Deterministic compactness criterion for $\phi$) of arXiv:2607.10486, 'Weak martingale solutions to stochastic Navier-Stokes-Cahn-Hilliard system with transport '] Let us consider the topological space $(\bZ_{T,2},\mathscr{Z}^2)$ defined in \eqref{eqn-Z_T2}. A set $\mathcal{K}_2$ is $\mathscr{Z}^2$-relatively compact in the intersection space $\bZ_{T,2}$ if the following three conditions hold:
\begin{trivlist}
\item[(i)] $\sup_{\phi \in \mathcal{K}_2} \sup_{s \in [0,T]} \lvert \phi(s) \rvert_{\newone{H}}< \infty$,
\item[(ii)] $\sup_{\phi \in \mathcal{K}} \left[\int_0^T \Vert  \phi(s) \Vert_{\newone{V}}^{\beta}\,\d s \right]<\infty$, i.e. $\mathcal{K}_2$ is bounded in $L^\beta(0,T;\newone{V})$,

\item[(iii)] $\lim_{\delta \to 0} \sup_{\phi \in \mathcal{K}_2} \mc_{\newonep{V}}(\phi,\delta)=0$.
\end{trivlist} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:40:26.991372+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d7e1e461922b93624599e0c4d80d281a6da839e4f9c721e2a6dc7961230b58c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem-UpperLDPbound of arXiv:2604.14318, '\large The free energy of the interacting Bose gas:\\\medskip a variational description \\'] Assume the situation and the notation described in Section~(sec-Purpose of the paper). That is, $\Lambda_N$ is a centred box with volume $|\Lambda_N|\sim N/\rho$ for some $\rho\in(0,\infty)$, and is decomposed into the subboxes $z+W_R=z+[-R,R]^d$ for some $R\in(0,\infty)$ with $z\in 2R\mathbb{Z}^d\cap\Lambda_N$. We consider particle boundary condition and indicate it by \lq par\rq. Fix a large parameter $M\in(0,R/2)$ and fix  $\xi\in {\mathcal M }_1({\mathcal L }_W^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({M}})}}}\times{\mathcal S }_W^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({M}})}}})$ such that $ \langle  {\mathfrak N}^{\ssup{\ell,{\mathcal S }}}_{\partial W},\psi\rangle<\infty$, where $\psi=\partial\Pi_W^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({\mathcal S }})}}}(\xi)\in  {\mathcal M }_1({\mathcal T }_W)$, and assume that $\psi$ is $W$-admissible.  Then, for any sufficiently large $R$, there is $\psi_N\in {\mathcal M }_1({\mathcal T }_W)$ that converges to $\psi$ as $N\to\infty$ such that
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\liminf_{N\to\infty}\frac 1{|\Lambda_N|}&\log{\tt Q}^{\ssup{\Lambda_N,{\rm par}}}_{M}\Big(\partial\Xi^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({\mathcal S }})}}}_{N,R} =\psi_N\Big)\geq -\frac{C_M}{R^{d/2}}+\frac 1{|W|}\langle\psi,\mathfrak p_{W,M}\rangle,
\end{aligned}
\end{equation} 
where we recall (equation pMdef of the paper) and introduce 
\begin{equation}
\mathfrak p_{W,M}(\mu)=\sum_{i\in I}\log p_{x_i}^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({W,M}})}}}(l_i,y_i),\qquad \mu=\sum_{i\in I}\delta_{(x_i,l_i,y_i)}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:31.979104+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d7fa5bc2bf379656859df41da04646c25f184d4d735a991fa077c443c7e527b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 14 of arXiv:2606.11389, 'Instability of a nonlinear oscillator with small friction and small additive noise'] For the system \eqref{add eps} there exists $K_1$ such that for all $0 < \e \le 1$ and $(x_0,y_0,v_0)$ with $v_0 \neq 0$  
  $$
  \limsup_{t \to \infty} \left| \frac{1}{t} \Lambda_\e(t) - \frac{\e^{2/3}}{t} \int_0^t \chi_\e(h_s)Q_0(x_s,y_s,\phi_s)ds \right|  \le K_1 \e^{4/3}
  $$
almost surely. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.242846+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d7fc25f7a9b5f037fad9756d1263832325190295c7b60fa96411b4cb68c0d4a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop opti_problem_231 of arXiv:2604.23751, 'Large deviation principles for pattern-avoiding permutations, and limit shapes for constra'] The action $A_{\beta}$ has a unique minimizer $\varphi_\beta$ in $\mathcal{E}$. 
