    Moreover, the SDE admits a stochastic flow of diffeomorphisms $\{X^\kappa_{s,t}(x,\omega)\}$ on $\T^d$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:58:24.508602+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d9921e425541147b7f27cfe5bbcf176d438341922fbe563b764a8d0fa9e33dd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lm:Schwconvergencetailprob of arXiv:2601.09537, 'Gene genealogies in haploid populations evolving according to sweepstakes reproduction'] Suppose a haploid population of constant size $N$ evolves according to Def~(hschwpop of the paper). 
Let $X_1, \ldots, X_N$ be the random number of juveniles produced independently  by the $N$ current individuals according to  
Eq~(equation eq:4 of the paper), write  $S_N := X_1 + \cdots + X_N$, and    $\nu_1$ for  the random number of
surviving offspring produced by  an arbitrary  individual. Let   $B(a,b) =\Gamma(a)\Gamma(b)/\Gamma(a+b)$ denote  the beta function. 
Then,  for any   $x \in (0,1)$,    $1 \le \alpha < 2$, and  $\left(  \ensuremath{\mathds{1}_{\left\{ \alpha= 1 \right\}}}\log(N) + \ensuremath{\mathds{1}_{\left\{ 1 < \alpha < 2 \right\}}}N^{\alpha - 1}\right)  c_N \sim 1$, 
\begin{displaymath}
\begin{split}
