\end{split}
\end{displaymath} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.312289+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d9b1e734053af9163002680d9caf0223ee73a63cac35c73e9e3a83afccf0553","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma harnack of arXiv:2411.14921, 'A boundary Harnack principle and its application to analyticity of 3D Brownian intersectio'] Let $D$ be a bounded domain. Let $\phi$ be a bounded continuous function on $\partial D$. Let $f$ be a bounded continuous function on $D\cup\partial D$ that is harmonic in $D$ and converges to $\phi$ on regular points of $D^c\cap\partial D$. Then for all $x\in D$,
