{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:22:48.887467+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6da4c96d25039d89055eca76898cb4de225062bdbf5f5169f7fcf7b6dc8d4cff","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 30 of arXiv:2608.29157, 'Dilator-based analysis of $\KP$'] Let $\kappa$ be a linear order with a designated member $\ttOmega\in \kappa$. We define the terms in $\calL^u_{\kappa,\ttOmega}$ as members of $\bfL(u)_{\{\alpha\in \kappa\mid\alpha<\ttOmega\}} \cup \{\ttL(u)_\ttOmega\}$.
