		\mathbb{E} \left[ \Delta \widetilde{C}_k | \mathcal{F}_k \right] &= \frac{1}{\varepsilon_k n} \left(  \sqrt{ \mathrm{e}}\widetilde{B}_k - \widetilde{C}_k \right) + O \left( \frac{\varepsilon_k^{1/2}}{\varepsilon_k n} \max \left( |\widetilde{B}_k|, |\widetilde{C}_k| \right) \right) + O \left( \frac{\varepsilon_k^{3/4}}{\varepsilon_k n} |\widetilde{A}_k| \right) + \left( \frac{n^{-1/30}}{\varepsilon_k n} \right), 
	\end{align}
	where the constants implied by the $O$ notation are absolute. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:34:20.689556+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6dabc6d0897f20a913c2caf4a55da4174bc84d37815eee58c1c70c62f5c79382","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2609.02193, 'State-law dynamics of McKean-Vlasov stochastic reaction-diffusion equations on $\mathbb R^'] Let $X=L^2(\mathbb R^n)$ and $q>2$. For $R>0$, set
	$B_R=\{x\in\mathbb R^n:|x|<R\}$, and interpret
	$\|w\|_{H^1(B_R)}$ as the extended Borel functional on $X$
	obtained by assigning the value $+\infty$ whenever
	$w|_{B_R}\notin H^1(B_R)$. Suppose that
	$\mathcal B\subset X\times\mathcal P_2(X)$ satisfies the following conditions:
	\begin{itemize}
		\item[(i)] for every $R>0$,
		\begin{align*}
			\sup_{(u,\mu)\in\mathcal B}
			\Big[
			\|u\|_{H^1(B_R)}^2
			+
			\int_X\|v\|_{H^1(B_R)}^2\,\mu(dv)
			\Big]<\infty;
		\end{align*}

		\item[(ii)]
		\begin{align*}
			\lim_{R\to\infty}
			\sup_{(u,\mu)\in\mathcal B}
			\int_{|x|>R}|u(x)|^2\,dx=0;
		\end{align*}

		\item[(iii)]
		\begin{align*}
			\lim_{R\to\infty}
			\sup_{(u,\mu)\in\mathcal B}
			\int_X\int_{|x|>R}|v(x)|^2\,dx\,\mu(dv)=0;
		\end{align*}

		\item[(iv)]
		\begin{align*}
			\sup_{(u,\mu)\in\mathcal B}
			\int_X\|v\|_X^q\,\mu(dv)<\infty.
		\end{align*}
	\end{itemize}
	Then $\mathcal B$ is relatively compact in $X\times\mathcal P_2(X)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:00:22.774366+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6db011d585cb686720b5a956451ae0a391ed92bfdc7401f35428c29cfc3b1e05","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary coro:order-interval-metric-equivalence of arXiv:2411.01364, 'Global Dynamics of Granular Media Equations via Stochastic Order'] Let $[\mu,\nu]$ be an order interval and $\{\rho_n\}_{n\geq1}\subset[\mu,\nu]$, $\rho\in[\mu,\nu]$. Then the following convergences are equivalent.
