{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:21:56.733510+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6db736f4053cbb2327fa2d1b867797f7f2d5d125f927a7fd778d4f8c6d9c501b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma le:hf_approx_equicont of arXiv:2507.15589, 'Tightness of approximations to metrics on non-simple conformal loop ensemble gaskets'] Let $(W,d_W)$ be a compact metric space. Suppose we have a sequence of non-empty compact subsets $K_n \subseteq W$ each equipped with a bounded function $f_n\colon K_n \to Y$. Suppose that there is a sequence $r_n \searrow 0$ such that
 \begin{enumerate}[(i)]
  \item There exist $0_Y \in Y$ and $M \in (0,\infty)$ such that $\sup_{x \in K} d_Y(f_n(x),0_Y) \leq M$ for every $n$.
