{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.288238+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ddb7413f054935ec9aa943ca75ccf30e348e89b50a9e115cb3326c85674354d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 33 (Besov-variation embedding) of arXiv:2606.22964, 'Signature McKean--Vlasov stochastic differential equations'] Let $q>1$, $\alpha\in(1/q,1)$, and let $x\in C([0,T],E)$, where $(E,d)$ is a metric space. For $0\leq s<t\leq T$, define
