{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:55:37.883949+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6de254ddb20a71f0dbd9beeb09610d5270cd011c7665a38e1e15955db711f686","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lm:tail_exponential of arXiv:2605.09377, 'A factorization formula for the partition function in the semi-discrete parabolic Anderson'] Let $f(t)$ be an integer-valued function such that there are $\rho_2 > \rho_1 > 1$ for which $e^{\rho_2 - 1} < \rho_1^{\rho_2}$ and $\rho_1 t < f(t) < \rho_2 t$ for all $t$ sufficiently large. Then, we have for $\lambda \in (0, 1 - \rho_2 (1 - \ln(\rho_1)))$    
