{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:01:25.657839+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6deb67930f813a8fb9037a3040a8a9a02ad907211ec7f52338d88bdca66a07e4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem Lemma: Joining nilbundles of arXiv:2605.16921, '${\ASL_n}(\mathbb Z)$ invariant random subsets of $\mathbb Z^n$'] Let $(Z, \eta)$ be a joining of $X$ and $Y$ over $\Omega$: that is, a $\mathbb{Z}^d$-system equipped with measure-preserving $\mathbb{Z}^d$-equivariant maps $\psi: Z \to X$ and $\phi: Z \to Y$ satisfying $\pi_X \circ \psi = \pi_Y \circ \phi$, so that the diagram
