{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:11:44.346865+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6e03c13d2b385947ab5033f6d44153ce3e6b581f0b26dec17e653fc9ea106933","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 7 of arXiv:2609.03098, 'Standing waves for Schr\"odinger equations with Kato class potentials and $L^\infty$-bound'] There exists a constant $R_{Q,\infty} >0$, depending on the potential $V$ and the constant $M>0$ from condition \eqref{F-L-infty-bdd}, such that for any full solution $u:\R\to H^1(\R^N)$ of the equation \eqref{main-eq}, that is bounded in the space $H^{1}(\R^{N})$, the following estimate holds
