{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.049732+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6e18f5583cb122a0dc7f3d598d457a3494683ce2e0c538aa1ed67ff40bf4b1dc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Mylem 9 of arXiv:2607.00495, 'Rank deficiency of Bernoulli random matrices for growing corank'] Let $m, n \in \mathbb{N}$ be such that $m \le n$ and let $M$ be an $m \times n$ matrix with independent Bernoulli($p$) entries. Then for all $\varepsilon >0$, there exist $c_{\ref{Small ball probability for Comp vectors}} >0$ depend on $p$ and $\varepsilon$ such that for all $\frac{1}{2}$-almost orthogonal system $v_1, \dots,v_l \in S^{n-1}$, we have
    \begin{align*}
        \mathbb{P}\left( \Vert Mv_{j}\Vert_{2} \le c_{\ref{Small ball probability for Comp vectors}} \sqrt{m} \text{ for all } j \in [l]   \right) \le (1-p+\varepsilon)^{lm}.
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:22:48.882606+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6e1996eb25ba77e4f0216ca22f5a324de6f6256ca65e7f35ac051de49bdcb10c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 9 of arXiv:2608.29157, 'Dilator-based analysis of $\KP$'] Let $D$ be a dilator. We define a linear order $\psi^+(D)$ inductively as follows: For each $\sigma\in D(\psi^+(D))$, we have $\psi(\sigma)\in \psi^+(D)$. 
    For two $\psi(\sigma),\psi(\tau)\in \psi^+(D)$, we define 
    \begin{equation*}
        \psi^+(D)\vDash \psi(\sigma)<\psi(\tau) \iff D(\psi^+(D))\vDash \sigma<\tau.
    \end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:45:05.585794+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6e200263a1d321d510a31c4923be3df043d6c085dc446dd554561a99382f5eaf","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 20 of arXiv:2608.05679, 'Small ball probabilities and Chung's law of the iterated logarithm for Gaussian Volterra p'] Assume that Condition \eqref{eq constant cond} holds, and set 
$$\tau = \min \left\{ \frac{H}{6},\; \frac{1}{4}\bigl(\alpha+\frac12 \bigr) \right\}.$$
Then there exist positive constants $c_{5,6}, c_{5,7}$, and $c_{5,8}$ such that, for every  $u>t>0$, $\theta>0$, and  $\eta\in (0, c_{5,6}^{-1})$,
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
&\mathbb{P} \Bigl\{ \left\{ M(t) \leq \theta t^H \right\} \cap \left\{ M(u) \leq \eta u^H \right\} \Bigr\}\\
&\le c_{5,6}\exp \left[ -c_{5,7}\left( \frac{u}{t} \right)^{\tau} \right]
+ \varphi(\theta) \varphi(\eta) \exp\left (c_{5,8} \left( \frac{u}{t} \right)^{-\tau}  \eta^{-\frac{2}{2\gamma+3}-1}\right). 
\end{split}
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:05:52.451505+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6e21aaceffd2626c05fa31044b77682382fd0e7ffebeb9cc04811eee7d8a28e8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lm:recursionforCk of arXiv:2505.00198, '\ttl'] If $\theta>0$, then the sequence $C_k$ defined in (equation eqn-Ck-MMr of the paper), satisfies
\begin{equation}
C_0 =1, C_1 = 1 + \frac{\gamma}{\theta}  
\end{equation}
and, for $k \ge 1$, 
\begin{equation} 
\theta  C_{k+1}- (k + \theta + \gamma)   C_k +  k  C_{k-1} =0.  
\end{equation}
Furthermore, we have
\begin{equation}
\theta C_{r} - r\alpha C_{r-1} >0.  
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:12:09.059381+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6e21b738dd2c9f3df2a5218c6887b215b66a3174124468079467a9316cc73bd0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:boolean-no-go of arXiv:2608.20480, 'When Clean Data Hurts: Learning with Monotone \\ Corruptions Beyond Binary Classification'] Let $r$ be even. Suppose a binary partial class contains distinct points $x_1,\ldots,x_r$, a concept $h_0$ that is nonstar on all of them, and, for every $B\in\binom{[r]}{r/2}$, a concept $h_B$ that is nonstar on the whole row and satisfies
\[
    h_B(x_t)
    =
    \begin{cases}
        h_0(x_t),&t\notin B,\\
        1-h_0(x_t),&t\in B.
    \end{cases}
\]
Then the class has partial VC dimension at least $r/2$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:22:21.889559+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6e24917e27cb01823871512c80791059477ccbc457faf056e3525c353a018011","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:uplowAron of arXiv:2411.11345, 'Real Gaussian exponential sums via a real moment map'] Let $A_1,\ldots,A_n\subset \mathbb{R}^m$ be finite sets, let $\alpha_j\in\mathbb{R}_{>0}^{A_j}$ for $j=1,\ldots,n$, let $d_1,\ldots,d_n$ be positive integers and write $d:=\sum_{j=1}^n d_j$. Then for every admissible random field $\mathcal{X}\randin C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^m,\mathbb{R}^{m-1})$ independents of all the exponential sums, and every open set $U\subset \mathbb{R}^m$ we have 
  \begin{equation}
    \sum_{j=1}^n \frac{d_j}{\sqrt{d}}\, \mathbb{E}\#\sol{\mathcal{E}_{\alpha_j},\mathcal{X};U} \leq \mathbb{E}\# \sol{\mathcal{E}_{\alpha_1}^{\odot d_1}\odot \cdots \odot \mathcal{E}_{\alpha_n}^{\odot d_n}, \mathcal{X}; U}\leq \sum_{j=1}^n \sqrt{d_j}\, \mathbb{E}\#\sol{\mathcal{E}_{\alpha_j},\mathcal{X};U} 
  \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:44:17.170019+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6e24ec1e96ee0a12a179f127c04203528f1741ee4f34ddb0fb55c64047fdc672","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 12 of arXiv:2604.18871, 'Quantitative approximation of the Vlasov(--Fokker--Planck)--Navier--Stokes system by stoch'] Let Assumption~\ref{assump-particles}\ref{hyp:ICu0} holds and let $(\Omega,\mathcal{F},(\mathcal{F}_{t})_{t\geq 0},\PP)$ be a filtered probability space satisfying the usual conditions. Let $(B^i)_{i\in \N}$ be a family of independent $(\mathcal{F}_{t})_{t\geq 0}$-Brownian motions and let $(X^i_{0},V^i_{0})_{i\in \N}$ be $\mathcal{F}_{0}$-measurable random variables in $\T^d\times \R^d$. Then for each fixed $N\in \N^*$, there exists $\Omega_{N}\in \mathcal{F}$ and a unique process $(u^N,X^{1,N},V^{1,N},\dots,X^{N,N},V^{N,N})$ such that $\PP(\Omega_{N})=1$ and 
\begin{itemize}
\item for all $\omega\in \Omega_{N}$, $u^N$ is the unique solution of the mild equation~\eqref{eq:mildeq};

\item for all $\omega\in \Omega_{N}$, for each $i\in \{1,\dots, N\}$, $(X^{i,N},V^{i,N})$ solves the ODE from~\eqref{Part};

\item $(u^N,X^{1,N},V^{1,N},\dots,X^{N,N},V^{N,N})$ is measurable and adapted to the filtration $(\mathcal{F}_{t})_{t\geq 0}$.

\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:21:06.884209+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6e269f8754165dab59668ab13d90cf64df42b5e7895e0a9997e43d515a6e37ba","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 6 (Algorithmic guarantee) of arXiv:2608.21466, 'Spectral partitioning for $k$-block averaging kernels of finite Markov chains'] Let $k\in\llbracket 2,n-1\rrbracket$.
The output of Algorithm~\ref{alg:multiway-sweep} satisfies
\begin{equation}
    0\leq F(\widehat{\mathcal O}_F)-F_k^*
