{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.636776+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6e2fe3e8a91208f52b03e6a0954c32cea2d7ccb6552cea68b4b2fce1cb74fa76","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 29 of arXiv:2609.01362, '{Double cluster swapping for spin models: \\Pfaffian relations and sharpness}'] Let $\eps > 0$. Then, there exists $C = C(\eps,P,\G)$ such that 
