{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.500760+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6e30dc41c4f2b20684b4e1452c02a8f8db956bcdfe512229a3e8f3024f4174ed","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 30 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] Let $E$ be another Banach space. Then for all
\begin{align*}
(Y,Y') \in \scrd_X^{2\alpha}([0,T],W) \quad \text{and} \quad (Z,Z') \in \scrd_X^{2\alpha}([0,T],E)
\end{align*}
we have the relation
\begin{align}
((Y,Z),(Y,Z)') \in \scrd_X^{2\alpha}([0,T],W \times E),
\end{align}
where the Gubinelli derivative is given by $(Y,Z)' = (Y',Z')$, and we have the estimates
\begin{align}
\| (Y,Z), (Y,Z)' \|_{X,2\alpha} &\leq \| Y,Y' \|_{X,2\alpha} + \| Z,Z' \|_{X,2\alpha},
\\  | (Y,Z), (Y,Z)' |_{X,2\alpha} &\leq | Y,Y' |_{X,2\alpha} + | Z,Z' |_{X,2\alpha},
\\  \interleave (Y,Z), (Y,Z)' \interleave_{X,2\alpha} &\leq \interleave Y,Y' \interleave_{X,2\alpha} + \interleave Z,Z' \interleave_{X,2\alpha}.
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.773752+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6e349d2487c7cd3a2dad9ffb9f12549f091a2229cd60c829dbacdf80c7e4e015","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop propCinfty of arXiv:2609.01464, 'Removability of non-isolated singularities for Einstein metrics and RCD spaces'] For every integer $n\geqslant 2$, $0<\alpha<1$,  and $\mathcal{K}>0$, $\rho_0>0$, $0\leqslant c<n-2$ there is $0<\delta<1$ such that the following holds. 

    Let $(X,\mathrm{d},\mathcal{H}^n)$ be an $\mathrm{RCD}(-\eta,n)$ space, with $\eta\geqslant 0$ such that:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $\Sigma \subset X$ satisfies (def:Codimension of the paper) with $k=2$ and the choices of $\mathcal{K},\rho_0,c$ above: in particular, $\Sigma$ has codimension greater than $2$. Moreover, $X\setminus\Sigma$ is (locally isometric to) a smooth Riemannian manifold;
        \item $|\mathrm{Ric}| \leqslant \eta$ on $X\setminus \Sigma$.
    \end{enumerate}
    Let $x\in X$, and let $\{f_i\}_{i=1}^n$ be harmonic functions on $B_2(x)$. Set  
    \[ 
    D:=\sum_{i,j} \fint_{B_1(x)} |\nabla f_i \cdot \nabla f_j - \delta_{ij}|\mathrm{d}\mathcal{H}^n.
    \]
    Assume $D+\eta^{1/2}\leqslant \delta$. Then the following hold:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item The vector-valued function $f:=(f_1,\ldots,f_n):B_{1/2}(x)\to \mathbb R^n$ is a biLipschitz homeomorphism onto its image, and $f(B_{1/2}(x))\subset\mathbb R^n$ is an open set.
        \item Let $g^{ij}:=\nabla f_i\cdot\nabla f_j$. Then
        \[
    g^{ij}\circ f^{-1}
    \]
    (a priori smooth only on $f(B_{1/2}(x)\setminus\Sigma)$), can be extended to a $C^{1,\alpha}$-function on the whole open set $f(B_{1/2}(x))$.
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.757987+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6e351863b1e8af2bcf81020bb855613d297f0c15cc64edc54ad3966bfd0f06d7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma_localized_eigenvector_local_law of arXiv:2504.00512, 'Localization-delocalization transition for a random block matrix model at the edge'] In the setting of (theorem_localized_eigenvector_localization of the paper), and under the definitions in (equation eq:z1 of the paper) and (equation definition_shift_eigenvector of the paper), the following estimate holds for some constant $C>0$ that does not depend on $\varepsilon$:   \begin{equation}
        \begin{aligned}
            \mathbb{E}\avg{\left({\im G_0}\right){\widetilde{\Lambda}}\left({\im G_1}\right){\widetilde{\Lambda}}}\prec N^{C\varepsilon}N^{-5/3}k^{2/3}\lVert A \rVert_{\text{\rm{HS}}}^2\le N^{-1-2\varepsilon_A+C\varepsilon} ,
