{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:38:58.695452+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6e4211a691833b6e165d07e446468abd5b0f50ca57e1d87175ed3549d26b3854","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:ffp of arXiv:2510.22778, 'Free denoising diffusion models'] For $t>0$ the measure $\mu_{t}$ has a continuous density $\psi_{t}$
(Lemma~(lem:regularise of the paper)), and the family $(\mu_{t})_{t>0}$ solves, in the sense of
distributions,
\begin{equation}
  \partial_{t}\psi_{t}(x)
  =\tfrac12\beta(t)\,\partial_{x}\big(x\,\psi_{t}(x)\big)
  -\beta(t)\,\partial_{x}\big(\psi_{t}(x)\,H\mu_{t}(x)\big),
\end{equation}
equivalently $\partial_{t}\mu_{t}+\partial_{x}\big(\mu_{t}V_{t}\big)=0$ with velocity
field
\begin{equation}
  V_{t}(x)=-\tfrac12\beta(t)\,x+\beta(t)H\mu_{t}(x)
  =-\tfrac{\beta(t)}{2}\big(x-\xi_{\mu_{t}}(x)\big).
\end{equation}
In terms of the Cauchy transform $G_{t}=G_{\mu_{t}}$ on $\mathbb{C}^{+}$,
\begin{equation}
  \partial_{t}G_{t}(z)+\beta(t)\,G_{t}(z)\,\partial_{z}G_{t}(z)
