{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:25:44.967969+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6e7a8603d8888761373a0caed756d1f33863fb3c93dbfd64e4c845debebcf9e0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2605.11279, 'Flocking with Multiple Types: Competition, Fluid Limits and Traveling Waves'] Suppose $Z\sim \expo(1)$ and $v_-=0$. For each $t\in\real^+$, let $G_\pm(t) := H_\pm(-t)$. A traveling wave $H = \parens*{H_+, H_-}$ with mass partition $(\rho^+,\rho^-)$ and speed $\gamma$ is characterized by the following system of first-order ODEs:
