{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:42:47.764749+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6e7e2e9621ddb4bb9b023b0f3a1c16bf9acf18a2e59ddc2af28fd6012ac95299","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 (Change of measure) of arXiv:2604.12797, 'A free boundary problem for the mean-field limit of diffusing particles with nonlinear bou'] Fix $T>0$, $n\geq 1$, $i\in \{1,\ldots,n\}$, and consider $Z^{i,n}$ from \eqref{eq:Z_i_n}. There exist a probability measure $\Q^{i,n}$ on $\hat{\mathcal{F}}_T^{i,n}$, equivalent to the restriction of $\Prob$ to $\hat{\mathcal{F}}_T^{i,n}$, so that $Z^{i,n}$
