{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:24:20.648146+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ea6f520695ea49a41d6789c8460920d48efd43fa9f78c400419ce762f88217e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:smallpmono of arXiv:2608.11378, 'On the most likely geodesic in last passage percolation'] Assume $d=2$. There is $p_{n} > 0$ such that if $\omega_x \sim \mathrm{Ber}(p)$ with $0 < p \le p_n$, we have for all paths $\pi,\, \gamma \in \Gamma_n$ the implication
