{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:22:01.659613+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6eb1ad83213beceebe05cc3bdddeb4148876965a3f08a4af6960a5da6a1dc06b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:g-bound of arXiv:2603.01823, 'on a fractional stochastic heat equation arising from the disordered pinning model'] For the transition density $g_\rho(t,x)$ of a $1$-dimensional $\rho$-stable process, we have the following uniform upper and lower bounds:
\begin{equation}
\frac{C_1t}{\left(t^{\frac{1}{\rho}}+|x|\right)^{1+\rho}}\le g_\rho(t,x) \le \frac{C_2t}{\left(t^{\frac{1}{\rho}}+|x|\right)^{1+\rho}}\leq C_2t^{-\frac{1}{\rho}},\quad\forall~x\in\mathbb R~\text{and}~t>0,
\end{equation}
where $C_1,C_2$ are positive constants depending only on $\rho$. Moreover, for $t\leq T$, the lower bound can be simplified by $g_\rho(t,x)\geq \frac{C_1t}{\left(T^{1/\rho}+|x|\right)^{1+\rho}}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:16.151534+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6eb6eda6da394da5882f2241dd62fb3d39699f43fc9ed573c93be9752d4a44e7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 21 of arXiv:2604.13454, 'Invariant and periodic measures in classical spin systems on infinite lattices with highly'] Let $k\in\mathbb{N}$, $x\in\ell^{2\theta}_{\rho}(\mathbb{Z}^+)$ and $T\geq0$ be given.  Then for all $\epsilon>0$, there exist $\delta>0$ and $V\in\mathbb{N}$ satisfying: whenever $n\geq V$ and $y\in\{z\in\ell^{2\theta}_{\rho}(\mathbb{Z}^+);\Vert z-x\Vert_{2,\rho}\leq\delta\}$, we have 
        \begin{equation*}
            \mathbb{E}\sup\limits_{t\in[0,T]}\Vert X_{(k)}^{(n),x}(t)-X_{(k)}^{(n),y}(t)\Vert_{\mathbb{R}^{\Lambda_k}}^2\leq \epsilon.
        \end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

