{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:17.375014+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6eb9cfe0c62c1307363fd06b2a8ea94b60532f45c9a65cd94c626c84d09c77df","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 5 of arXiv:2606.04636, 'A Thomson-type variational principle for diffusion coefficients'] $V_{0}$ is the space of admissible flows with vanishing
divergence, that we write formally as
\begin{equation}
V_{0}=\left\{ \phi\in\cH_{2}:\left\langle \div\phi,\div\phi\right\rangle =0\right\} .
\end{equation}
For $\phi\in\cH_{2}$, $\left\langle \div\phi,\div\phi\right\rangle =0$
should be understood by the completion under $\left\langle \cdot,\cdot\right\rangle $.
That is, there exists a sequence $(\phi_{n})_{n\in\N}$ of flows with
well defined divergence that converge in $\cH_{2}$ to $\phi$, such
that $\left\langle \div\phi_{n},\div\phi_{n}\right\rangle \xrightarrow{n\to\infty}0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:06:18.027823+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ebe5266cf9a15ded8e5794477c6f70a9283296cda4c34606286855a444af020","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2608.15616, '\textbf{Compact Support Property of Super-Brownian Motion with Irregular Drift}'] Let $n\geq 1$ and let $(X^0, \ldots X^n)$ be a solution to \eqref{eq:SPDE_n} such that conditionally on $\mathcal{F}_\infty^{k-1}$,  $X^k$ is a solution to \eqref{eq:SPDE_k_gen} for $1\leq k \leq n$. Then, for any $1\leq k \leq n$ and any  $\psi^k, \phi^k\in \mcC_c^+(\R)$, it holds that 
		\begin{equation}
		\begin{split}
		&	\E\Big[\exp\Big(- \langle X^k_t, \phi^k \rangle - \int_0^t \langle X^k_s, \psi^k\rangle ds\Big)\Big| \mathcal{F}^{k-1}_\infty\Big] \\
		& \quad = \exp\Big(- \langle X_0^k, V_t(\phi^k, \psi^k)\rangle -\int_0^t\langle g_s^k, V_{t-s}(\phi^k, \psi^k) \rangle ds\Big), 
		\end{split}
		\end{equation} 
		where $V(\phi^k, \psi^k)$ is the solution to 
		\begin{equation*}
			\begin{split}
				&\partial_t V_t(x) = \frac{1}{2}\Delta V_t(x) - \frac{1}{2}(V_t(x))^2 + \psi^k(x), \quad t >0, x\in \R\\
				&V_0 \equiv \phi^k.
			\end{split}
		\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:45:02.035983+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ec13b3c66d2db29632cad0e4d6e37499d41b50cc3d7800b07cc7c213168fe7f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma LEM:AEC of arXiv:2512.23957, 'Concentration and fluctuations of sine-Gordon measure around topological multi-soliton man'] Let $F$ be a bounded, continuous function and $\delta_\varepsilon=\eta\sqrt{\varepsilon \log \frac 1\varepsilon}$, defined in (equation LDPIN2 of the paper). Then
\begin{align*}
\mathbb{E}_{ \nu^\perp_{ \xi_1,\dots,\xi_k } }\Big[F(v) e^{\frac 1\varepsilon \mathcal{E}_{\xi_1,\dots,\xi_k}(v)  } \textup{Det}_{\xi_1,\dots,\xi_k}(\sqrt{\varepsilon}v), \, A_\varepsilon^c, \, \| \sqrt{\varepsilon}v \|_{L^2} < \delta_\varepsilon   \Big] \lesssim e^{-c K^2 |\log L_\varepsilon| },
\end{align*}

\noindent
uniformly in $\xi_1, \dots,\xi_k \in [-\overline L_\varepsilon, \overline L_\varepsilon]^k $, where  $\mathcal{E}_{\xi_1,\dots,\xi_k}$ and $\textup{Det}_{\xi_1,\dots,\xi_k}$ are defined in Proposition (PROP:cha of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.365608+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ec3ca2079e5f5c394db831053464af315b6aacb83d100a84f5ef85be2e87273","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem theo:jog loh of arXiv:2606.02472, 'Correlated uniform attachment trees'] For all $\varepsilon >0, K\in \N$ there exists $m \in \N$ such that for a uniform-attachment tree $(T_n)_{n\in \N}$ one has
    \begin{align*}
        \mathbb{P}\left(  A_K(T_m) = A_K(T_n) \text{ for all } n \geq m \right) > 1 - \varepsilon .
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.701191+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ec72f45f630d592dea970f40e7fe057e216e5ae091dafc5719c557dabc531b6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor GHProps of arXiv:2411.18563, 'Lower tails for triangles inside the critical window'] Under Condition~(ConditionThm1 of the paper), the following events hold wvhp with respect to $G \sim \mu_{\lambda,\zeta}$. Setting $\overline \Delta:=\mathbb{E}_{\lambda,\zeta} \Delta(G)$,
\begin{enumerate}
\item  $\delta(G) = (1+o(1))\Delta(G) =(1+o(1))\overline\Delta$,
\item $\alpha_{G_v,\lambda,\zeta}=(1+o(1))\alpha(\overline\Delta,\lambda,\zeta)$ for all $v\in V(G)$,
\item $\rho_{G_v,\lambda,\zeta}=(1+o(1))\rho(\overline\Delta,\lambda,\zeta)$ for all $v\in V(G)$.
\end{enumerate}
In particular, $\mathbb{E}_{\lambda,\zeta}(\alpha_{G_v,\lambda,\zeta})=(1+o(1))\alpha(\overline\Delta,\lambda,\zeta)$ and $\mathbb{E}_{\lambda,\zeta}(\rho_{G_v,\lambda,\zeta})=(1+o(1))\rho(\overline\Delta,\lambda,\zeta)$ for all $v\in V(G)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:40:26.989238+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ec887733e8ad1b951dbafd789ecb264d0c1e3fc75f1906e8eafd927b61e9618","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop lem-rewrite of arXiv:2604.14318, '\large The free energy of the interacting Bose gas:\\\medskip a variational description \\'] Fix $\beta\in(0,\infty)$. Let $ v\colon[0,\infty)\to (-\infty,\infty] $ be measurable and bounded from below, and let $ \Lambda\subset\mathbb{R}^d$ be measurable with finite volume (assumed to be a torus for periodic boundary condition). Then, for any $N\in\mathbb{N}$, and $ {\rm bc}\in\{{\rm per},0\} $,
\begin{equation}
