{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:00:22.777139+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ecc0c9d1b08dc4f9919c2ed8acad684f1b609648803e7e8b0ec7c3c51db8529","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:local-dissipation-at-a of arXiv:2411.01364, 'Global Dynamics of Granular Media Equations via Stochastic Order'] Assume that $W(x)=\frac{\theta}{2}x^2$ and the confining potential function $V\in C^2(\mathbb R;\mathbb R)$ satisfy the following conditions:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item [(i)] There exists $a\in \mathbb{R}$ such that $V'(a)=0$ and $V''(a)>0$;
        \item [(ii)] $\liminf_{|x|\to\infty}\frac{V'(x)}{x|x|^{\delta}}>0$ for some $\delta>0$.
    \end{enumerate}
    Then, there exists $r_a > 0$ such that for any $0 < r \leq r_a$, there are $\theta_r > 0$ and $\sigma_r > 0$ such that for all $\theta \geq \theta_r$ and $\sigma^2(x) \leq \sigma_r$ for all $x \in \mathbb R$, the equation (equation eq:mvsystem of the paper) is locally dissipative at $a$ with radius $r$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:44:17.353558+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ecca9f98e448e432fc5492dc2b69eb9f87e1d5cbd2123caa8fbf0304e31560c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem T1 of arXiv:2608.22945, 'A Momentum-Based Variance-Reduced Algorithm for Federated Multiobjective Optimization'] Suppose that Assumptions (A1 of the paper)--(A2 of the paper) and (A3 of the paper) hold, and that $f_s(x)$ has a lower bound $f_s^{\rm min}$ for all $x\in \mathbb{R}^d$. Let $\Delta := \max_{s \in [S]} (f_s(x^0) - f_s^{\min})$. If we set
\begin{align}
	& \beta =\left( \frac{M K L^2 \left(1+D^2\right)^2\Delta^2}{\sigma^4 T^2} \right)^{1/3}<1,  \quad \gamma=\min\left\{\frac{1}{2L},\frac{1}{L}\sqrt{\frac{\beta KM}{54}}\right\},  \nonumber \\
	&\quad \eta KL
	\le
	c_\eta
	\min\left\{
	\beta,\,
	\frac1{\sqrt K},\,
	\sqrt{\frac{\beta}{M}},\,
	\beta^{3/4}
	\left(
	\frac{L\Delta}{(KM)^{1/2}T}
	\right)^{1/2}
	\right\}, \nonumber
	\end{align}
where \(c_\eta>0\) is a sufficiently small absolute constant, and choose	$B=\left\lceil \frac{K}{T\beta^2}\right\rceil$, then Algorithm (VSOMD of the paper) admits the convergence guarantee
\begin{align*}
\mathbb{E}\left[\mathcal{G}(x_a)\right]&
\lesssim\left(\frac{L\left(1+D^2\right)\sigma\Delta}{KMT}\right)^{\frac{2}{3}}(1+S^2)+\frac{LS^2\Delta}{T} \\
&\quad+
\frac{(1+S^2)G_0^2}{T} +
\frac{(1+S^2)\sigma^2}{KM}
\left(
\frac{MKL^2(1+D^2)^2\Delta^2}{\sigma^4T^2}
\right)^{2/3},
\end{align*}
where  $G_0^2:=\frac{1}{S}\sum_{s\in[S]}\left\|\nabla f_s(x^0)\right\|^2.$
\footnotetext[1]{The notation $\lesssim$ absorbs numerical constants.}
Alternatively, if $B=\Theta(KT)$ and $ \beta = \max\left\{\, \frac{1}{T},\; \left( \frac{M K L^2 \left(1+D^2\right)^2\Delta^2}{\sigma^4 T^2} \right)^{1/3} \right\}$, then Algorithm (VSOMD of the paper) admits the convergence guarantee
\begin{align*}
  \mathbb{E}\left[\mathcal{G}(x_a)\right]&\lesssim \frac{\sigma^2(1+S^2)}{KMT}+\left(\frac{L\left(1+D^2\right)\sigma\Delta}{KMT}\right)^{\frac{2}{3}}(1+S^2)\\&\quad+ \frac{LS^2\Delta}{T}+\frac{(1+S^2)G_0^2}{T} + \frac{(1+S^2)\sigma^2}{KMT^2}.
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:38.363219+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ed0316f191b151082ea8e0dc3b73f2aeae8a4c986b51208eabfc9b0a4d2bbf4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 20 (Finite volume OZ for a single cluster boundary) of arXiv:2604.21669, 'Discontinuous transition in 2D Potts:\\ II. order-order interface convergence'] Let \(0<J<U\) satisfy \(\sinh 2J=e^{-2U}\). There exist \(c_0,c>0\) such that, for any sequence \(\frac{\sqrt{n}}{c_0}\geq k_n\geq c_0\ln(n)\), there exists\(n_0\geq 1\) such that for any \(n\geq n_0\), \(m_n \geq c_0n\), there exists a probability measure \(\tilde{\bndMeas}_n\) on \(\SetRootMarkBackCont \times \SetRootMarkForwCont\) satisfying
	\begin{itemize}
		\item \(\tilde{\bndMeas}_n\) is supported on pairs of simple paths \((\eta_L,\eta_R)\) with \(\norm{\displace(\eta_L)}_{\infty},\norm{\displace(\eta_R)}_{\infty} \leq k_n^2\),
		\item defining \(v(\eta_L,\eta_R) = v_R-v_L-\displace(\eta_L)-\displace(\eta_R)\), for any \(f\) function of \(\Gamma_+\),
		\begin{multline*}
			\Big|\sum_{m\geq 0}\sum_{\eta_L,\eta_R} \tilde{\bndMeas}_n(\eta_L,\eta_R) \tilde{\OZ}_{v(\eta_L,\eta_R)}^+\big[f(v_L + \eta_L\concatenate\bar{\eta}_1^M \concatenate \eta_R)\big]
			\\
			-\Phi_{n}\big[f(\Gamma_+)\bgiven v_R\in \calC\big]\Big|
			\leq
			\norm{f}_{\infty}e^{-ck_n},
		\end{multline*}where \(\eta_1^M \sim \tilde{\OZ}_{v(\eta_L,\eta_R)}^+\).
	\end{itemize}
	The same result holds for \(\calC',\Gamma_-, v_L',v_R'\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

