{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:37:08.312573+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ed848aff642c8498c3e1fdaff0dd406ebbf3568cde18c130bc5e85ee4478dd1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma w_t of arXiv:2608.29507, 'Denoising as Projection: Constrained Optimization with Gradient-Guided Diffusion'] Define
    \begin{align*}
        w_t := \frac{\eta^{-1}D^2}{2(1-\eta\mu c)}\sigma_t^2,
    \end{align*}
    then under the conditions specified in Theorem (theorem: convergence-guided-diffusion of the paper) and for $\widetilde{\eta}$ defined as in (equation eq:subspace-dynamics of the paper), we have that 
    \begin{align*}
         w_{t-1} \le (1-\widetilde{\eta} \mu c)w_t - \frac{(\sigma_t^2 - \sigma_{t-1}^2)\eta^{-1}D^2}{2}.
    \end{align*}
    \begin{proof}
        For simplicity, denote $C:= \frac{\eta^{-1}D^2}{2}$, hence
        \begin{align*}
            &w_{t-1} \le (1-\widetilde{\eta} \mu c)w_t - \frac{(\sigma_t^2 - \sigma_{t-1}^2)\eta^{-1}D^2}{2}\\
            \Longleftrightarrow\quad & \frac{C}{1-\eta\mu c} \sigma_{t-1}^2 \le  (1-\widetilde{\eta} \mu c)\frac{C}{1-\eta\mu c} \sigma_{t}^2 - C(\sigma_t^2 - \sigma_{t-1}^2)\\
           \Longleftrightarrow\quad  & \left(\frac{1}{1-\eta\mu c}-1\right)\sigma_{t-1}^2 \le \left(\frac{1}{1-\eta\mu c}-1\right)\sigma_{t}^2 - \frac{\widetilde{\eta}\mu c }{1-\eta\mu c}\sigma_{t}^2\\
           \Longleftrightarrow\quad  & \frac{\eta\mu c}{1-\eta\mu c} \frac{\sigma_{t-1}^2}{\sigma_t^2} \le \frac{\eta\mu c}{1-\eta\mu c}  -  \frac{\widetilde{\eta}\mu c }{1-\eta\mu c}\\
           \Longleftrightarrow\quad &\frac{\widetilde{\eta}\mu c }{1-\eta\mu c}  \le \frac{\eta\mu c}{1-\eta\mu c}\left(1- \frac{\sigma_{t-1}^2}{\sigma_t^2}\right)\\
           \Longleftrightarrow\quad &\epsilon \le \left(1- \frac{\sigma_{t-1}^2}{\sigma_t^2}\right) = (1-(1-\epsilon)^2) = 2\epsilon - \epsilon^2
        \end{align*}
        Given that $\epsilon < 1$, we have proved the inequality holds.
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.186481+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6edac3f9b3785b2867403ceeb997c3cb73c5e4d0de2dc62fd537ab18f1e96a9d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2510.20492, 'Heterochromatic two-arm probabilities for metric graph Gaussian free fields'] For any $d\ge 3$, $D\subset \widetilde{\mathbb{Z}}^d$, $n\ge 10$ and $v,w\in \widetilde{\mathbb{Z}}^d\setminus D$ with $|v-w|\ge 2n$, 
