{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.249166+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ee36cacb2054eb46607f5028b8c30e02cdab9ba6c4f476d74647432ab082021","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 28 of arXiv:2604.15191, 'Quantitative Stability of Many-Marginal Schr\"odinger Bridge'] Let $(\phi^\mu_{j}, \psi_{j}^\mu)$ and $(\phi^\nu_{j}, \psi^{\nu}_{j})$ be the Schr\"odinger potentials for solving $\eot_{\varepsilon_j}(\rho^\mu_{t_{j-1}}, \rho_{t_j}^\mu)$ and $\eot_{\varepsilon_j}(\rho_{t_{j-1}}^\nu, \rho_{t_j}^\nu)$ with $\varepsilon_j = t_{j} - t_{j-1}$, respectively. Then,
    \begin{align}
