\stackrel{}{=} \sum_{j=1}^m \frac{1}{\varepsilon_j}\bigg[\eot_{\varepsilon_j}(\rho_{t_{j-1}}^\nu, \rho_{t_j}^\nu) - \int_{\mb T^d}\phi_j^\mu\,\dd\rho_{t_{j-1}}^\nu - \int_{\mb T^d}\psi_j^\mu\,\dd\rho_{t_j}^\nu\bigg] + \sum_{j=0}^m  \KL(\rho_{t_j}^\nu\,\|\,\rho_{t_j}^\mu).
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:38:57.119938+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ee719a53736062952ef323e2b34e3627c9d71011d50ca3c42a21e9ef4bd7816","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 9 of arXiv:2604.04840, 'Bounding the Gap Between Zeros of the Variable-\\Parameter Confluent Hypergeometric Functi'] Consider real parameters $a^*<0$, $b>0$ and $z>0$ such that $\Phi(a^*,b,z) = 0$. Then the integral $I = \int_0^z t^{b-1} e^{-t} \Phi^2(a^*,b,t) dt$ can also be written as

