    where
    \begin{equation*}
        h(z,y_0,t_0):=\exp\left((x^2-z^2+t_0)\frac{1-2\gamma\theta}{4\theta}- y_0\frac{1-4\gamma^2\theta^2}{8\theta^2}\right).
    \end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:05:57.817014+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6f0bebc8aadd1c5eab460b43fe188d246d2e36b3186d13abbc79a4b60cc9c584","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 23 of arXiv:2608.30570, '2608.30570'] Let $\Sigma$ be a complete properly immersed  translating soliton in ${\mathbb R}^4$ satisfying
