{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.240561+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6f28a76cc45ff72b8b3d124b2277697aababb7d623b4821e2ee210fa708c6c8c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Propo 11 of arXiv:2604.14752, 'Strong and weak rates of convergence in the Smoluchowski--Kramers approximation for stocha'] Let $\beta\in(0,1]$ such that the condition~\eqref{eq:condition_beta} from Assumption~\ref{ass:noise} holds. For all $p\in[1,\infty)$, $T\in(0,\infty)$ and all $\alpha\in[0,\beta)$, there exists $C_{p,\alpha}(T)\in(0,\infty)$ such that, if for all $\epsilon\in(0,1)$ the initial value $x_0^\epsilon$ is a $\mathcal{F}_0$-measurable random variable, which satisfies $\underset{\epsilon\in(0,1)}\sup~\E[\|x_0^\epsilon\|_{\HH^\alpha}^{2p}]<\infty$, then one has
