{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.236197+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6f2ded376f6550ef2477959ffd94c7507bbaf423ddabd3edc8cceec2efa6c3d5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 4 (Boltzmann entropy) of arXiv:2604.14427, 'A criterion for proving entropy chaos on path space'] Given a measure $\mu$ on $E=\R^d$ with density $\rho$ with respect to the Lebesgue measure on $E$, if $\rho$ has a finite moment of order $k>0$, then
