{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:53.186389+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6f31f9076f64053ee5aab1b107104ced9cf771a744bc0ca0036f288a1dfa2108","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 12 of arXiv:2606.30364, 'Distributional comparison for non-commutative infinitely divisible probability measures'] For a probability measure $\mu \in \mathcal{P}_{\infty}(\R) $, its $\circledast$-cumulants $\kappa_n^{\circledast}[\mu]$ are defined recursively through the moment-cumulant formula 

