{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:41:03.266793+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6f40e2ef007d889b5d12f3ed6fd68ac0da92c98e6e999d88bae94fb75fb1f21b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2411.08303, 'The discrepancy in min-max statistics between two random matrices with finite third moment'] For $\beta, \delta>0$, $F^{\beta\delta}:\mathbb{R}^{n \times m} \rightarrow \mathbb{R}$ defined by

		$$F^{\beta \delta}(x)=-\frac{1}{\beta \delta}\log\sum_{i=1}^{n}(\sum_{j=1}^{m}\exp(\beta x_{i,j}))^{-\delta}.$$ For every $x \in \mathbb{R}^{n \times m}$

		\begin{align}
