where $t(v), h(v)$ as in ((eq:tvhv of the paper)) and the functions $F_1, F_2$ are as in ((eq:Lambda1 of the paper)) and ((eq:Lambda2 of the paper)).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:28.465982+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6f6563970b525dd234daf0c0673385c8d549ae51da47b8058df93a06e671e206","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2606.29131, '2606.29131'] Suppose that \eqref{t1-3-1} holds for some $\beta>0$. Let $\Upsilon_\e^3 f(x,y)$ be defined by \eqref{e2-3-8}. Then, there exists a positive constant $C_4:=C_4(\beta)$ such that for every $f\in \M_\beta$, $x\in \R^d$ and $y\in \T^d$,
