{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:47:53.352579+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6f6769660d01478eab9189778cb4b92bf56859641cf639c250c641ee43c0ee0f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 7 of arXiv:2607.15903, 'Uniqueness for nonlinear Fokker-Planck equations with general diffusion terms and their as'] Under Hypotheses (\textbf{\romannumeral1}'),(\textbf{\romannumeral2}), (\textbf{\romannumeral3}'), (\textbf{\romannumeral4})-(\textbf{\romannumeral5}), for each $u_{0} \in \mathcal{P}\cap L^{\infty} $, NFPE (\ref{1}) has a unique distributional solution
