{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.712044+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6fad85146e5335923cdcdd438d7b877ec0889bb3e32a6da6bac15423627fc4a2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem theorem_localized_eigenvalue of arXiv:2504.00512, 'Localization-delocalization transition for a random block matrix model at the edge'] In the setting of (theorem_localized_eigenvector_localization of the paper), for any constants $\varepsilon>0$ and $\varepsilon_0\in\left({0,2\varepsilon}\right)$, we have that
