{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:35:10.786114+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6fce65fc887a52c8ffa930fba0ccf696989243a82e76f06166e1dbff920b8620","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 8 of arXiv:2604.00598, 'Allowing for Imprecision in the Game-theoretic Characterisation of the Poisson Process'] For all natural numbers~\(k\in\nats\), time points~\(t_1, \dots, t_{k+1}\in\posreals\) such that \(t_1<t_2<\cdots<t_{k+1}\) and gambles~\(g\in\bfns[k+1]\),
