{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.813020+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ffc31c707f0818e57d622b75476aeec8f118fb600eb68a078d79272eb034e9c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma log-lower-bound of arXiv:2504.02207, 'Finite-Time behaviors of M/M/$n$ Queue: Mixing Time, Mean Queue Length and Tail Bounds'] Given $x \in \R$ such that $0 \leq x \leq \frac{1}{2}$, we have
    \begin{align}
