{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:29:21.949151+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7014c81f6057361130269f9fcca5af0e85eafd701eea120452e6815c6142d4b5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 29 of arXiv:2608.01860, 'A Variational Characterization of a Gibbs Measure related to the Aviles-Giga Functional'] Let $\mu$ be a probability measure on $X$. Then the functional $F:L^\infty(X)\to \R$, $f\mapsto \log\left(\int_X\exp(f(x))\ \mu(dx)\right)$ is continuous, convex and for $\gamma\in P_\mu(X)\subset (L^\infty(X))'$ the Fenchel conjugate is of the form
