{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:40:59.389172+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_701c46d3e9df34a167504db1a7d9af5807cbff1ad264680ebcd6d2adc39bd97c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 7 (The burglar Drivers) of arXiv:2609.03968, 'A one-parameter family of local-time conditioned processes : the generalized Brownian burg'] Let $\nu\in\R$, and let $z,z_0\in\overline\R=\R\cup\{\pm\infty\}$. The \emph{burglar Driver} of parameter $\nu$, starting from $z$ and targeting $z_0$, is the continuous diffusion on $\overline \R$ which satisfies $D_0 = z$, evolves according to the SDE
\begin{equation}

\dd D_t = \exp\left(\cosh(D_t)\right)\dd B_t+ \exp\left(2\cosh(D_t)\right)(1-\nu)\sign(D_t-z_0)\dd t.
\end{equation}
for $B$ a usual Brownian motion, and is instantly reflected at the boundaries $\pm\infty$. In the case of a boundary target $z_0=\pm\infty$, we stop it at the time $T(D):=\inf\{t\geq 0, D_t = z_0\}$, and otherwise let it run until $T(D)=+\infty$, which corresponds to the final time of the driver $D$ for the target $z_0$ as defined in Lemma \ref{lemmatech}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:42:39.098837+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_702708b17eaab1d5635eaad9965059633c3fdca25e6e18ed2dcf80cbe7bf6e87","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor of arXiv:2412.08497, 'Time discretization of Quadratic Forward-Backward SDEs with singular drift'] Under Assumption (assum5.1 of the paper) and for $N$ large enough, the following holds
		\begin{align*}
