{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:49:17.485828+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_707723cd69dbe190e50db93c71a6a763255b26e2eb3e13ef01b41e231f7e5a78","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2605.28377, 'Geometric functionals of Brownian motion on Hermitian symmetric spaces of non-compact type'] Let $(X(t))_{t \ge 0}$ be a Brownian motion on $\Omega$, and let $\lambda_i(t)$, $1 \le i \le r$, be the spectral values of $X(t)$. Then, there exists a Brownian motion $(\alpha(t))_{t \ge 0}$ in $\mathbb{R}^r$ such that 
