{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:50:36.764397+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7078ea965686caa3284fe14e6563b1bf2fd7c195bfc1b1ad30c19cb5b766f079","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 (Hasse-Davenport identity) of arXiv:2609.04155, 'The subconvexity problem for symmetric square\\ $L$-functions in Level aspect'] Let $\F_q$ be the finite field, $N$ be a divisor of $q-1$, $\psi$ be a non-trivial additive character of $\F_q$, and $\psi_N$ be the additive character $\psi_N(x):=\psi(Nx)$. Let us denote by $\rho_1, ..., \rho_N\in \hat{\F_q^\times}$ of order dividing $N$. Then for any multiplicative character $\chi$ of $\F_q^\times$, we have
        \begin{equation}
            -\eps(\psi_N, \chi^N) = \eps_N(\psi)\prod_{j=1}^{N}\eps(\psi, \chi\rho_j),
        \end{equation}
        where
        \begin{equation*}
            \eps_N(\psi)=q^{-1/2}\prod_{j=1}^N\eps(\psi, \rho_j)^{-1}\in S^1.
        \end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

