{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:01:25.652619+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7081e56fbb4cdc266c2d240ec00eba0e9238fb78b6b772fc6d24b0b908d25aa8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm4.2 of arXiv:2605.16160, 'Revisiting Toeplitz and Hankel random matrices via $*$-convergence of circulant-type matri'] Let $\{n^{-1/2}T_n^{(j)}\}_{1\leq j\leq k}$ be iid non-symmetric Toeplitz matrices whose entries satisfy Assumption I. They 

