{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:06:42.727561+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7084507f900882586ae4bc8d16d32d6c9fff446e84666885cce763acbdbd689d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma exponential-estimate-lemma2 of arXiv:2411.04500, '\LARGE Probabilistic Approaches to The Energy Equality in Forced Surface Quasi-Geostrophic'] Let $ \varepsilon, \delta(\varepsilon)>0$. Suppose that $\theta_{\varepsilon,\delta(\varepsilon)}$ is a stochastic generalized Leray solution of (equation SPDE-SQG of the paper) in the sense of Definition (def-stochastic-leray of the paper), with initial data $ \theta_{\varepsilon, \delta(\varepsilon)}(0) $ satisfying Assumption (Gaussian-initial-data of the paper). Fix $\sigma\in(0,1/2)$ and $l>3+2\beta-\alpha$. Then there exists $\eta_0>0$ such that for every  $\eta\in[0,\eta_0]$, under the scaling regime (equation scaling-delta of the paper), we have 
	\begin{equation}
		\varepsilon\log\mathbb{E}\Big(\exp\Big\{\frac{\eta}{\varepsilon}\|\theta_{\varepsilon,\delta(\varepsilon)}\|_{W^{\sigma,2}([0,T];H^{-l}(\mathbb{T}^2))}^2\Big\}\Big)\leqslant C(\eta,T), 
