{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:44:17.188191+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7090354b2d0b281db51af4cb9c6f7ad2d5eac983e84ab65ef7456f9bcd5351ae","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2604.18871, 'Quantitative approximation of the Vlasov(--Fokker--Planck)--Navier--Stokes system by stoch'] There exists $C>0$ such that for any measurable $f$ from $ \T^d\times \R^d \to \R$ and any $N\in \N^*$, it holds:

