{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:33:11.996011+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7094d24cae6d29ef29c6254206f7b2661214a887c49137cd1f731e496503d595","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:stopping of arXiv:2609.02820, 'Sharpness and critical scaling of parking'] Let $X$ be the simple random walk. For every configuration $\eta\in\mathbb R^{\mathbb{Z}^d}$, every $n\geq0$ and $x\in\mathbb{Z}^d$,
