{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:38:13.638531+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_70db6d71c350c5da9970ea18cf2006403182b990e521cf9c259d615fcd93683d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2609.00687, 'A unification of Euler-Maclaurin and Euler-Boole summation formulas'] Let $n,q\in\mathbb{N}$ and $m\in\mathbb{N}_{0}$. Let $\chi$ be a Dirichlet character modulo $q$. Then, for $\lambda\in\mathbb{C}\setminus\{0\}$,
\begin{eqnarray}
\sum_{k=1}^{nq}\chi(k)\lambda^{-k}k^{m}&=&\frac{\lambda^{-qn}}{m+1}\sum_{k=0}^{m}\binom{m+1}{k}(-1)^{k}\beta_{k,\chi^{-}}(\{0\}_{\chi},\lambda)(nq)^{m+1-k}\nonumber\\
&&+\frac{(-1)^{m+1}\beta_{m+1,\chi^{-}}(\{0\}_{\chi},\lambda)(\lambda^{-nq}-1)}{m+1}.
\end{eqnarray}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:23:03.041343+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_70dbf42a9f597c320d27d7f816ccc7b5731a560a9bff8b4c451ef7188036cd47","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 44 of arXiv:2605.03236, 'Stochastic It\^o Equations and Parabolic Second-Order Equations with singular Drift'] For  $\mu \in[0,1]$,   stopping time $\tau$,  and any $\rho\in(0,\rho_{b}]$  we have
