{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.729639+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_70e6c2721085deacd416088d4f9eda8cd9eb93dbf5d9228895c2933c9f22511e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:NL-MP of arXiv:2604.25851, '{Non-uniqueness of nonlinear Markov processes in the sense of McKean associated with parab'] Let $\mathcal P_0 \subseteq \mathcal P$. A \emph{(time-homogeneous)  nonlinear Markov process} is a family $\{P^\zeta\}_{\zeta \in \mathcal P_0} \subset \mathcal P(\mathcal C)$ such that, setting $\mu^\zeta_t := P^\zeta_t$ for all $(\zeta,t) \in \mathcal P_0 \times \mathbb{R}_+$,
    \begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*), font=\normalfont]
        \item $\mu^\zeta_0 = \zeta$ for all $\zeta \in \mathcal P_0$;
        \item $\mu^\zeta_t \in \mathcal P_0$ for all $t > 0, \zeta \in \mathcal P_0$;
        \item the \emph{(time-homogeneous) nonlinear Markov property} holds, i.e.,
        \begin{equation}
        P^\zeta(\pi_{t+s} \in A | \mathcal F_s) ( \cdot) = P^{\mu^\zeta_s,\pi_s(\cdot)}(\pi_t \in A)\quad P^\zeta-\text{a.s.},\quad \forall s,t \geq 0, \, \zeta \in \mathcal P_0, \, A \in \mathcal B(\mathbb{R}^d),
    \end{equation}
    where for $\zeta \in \mathcal P_0$, $\{P^{\zeta,y}\}_{y\in \mathbb{R}^d}$ is the disintegration family of $P^{\zeta}$ with respect to $\pi_0$.
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.270651+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_70e97e7004435dd74ffd3e708a7af1000f8f2c4583ca17a7e8418effc97febad","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:propagation_xi of arXiv:2607.08914, 'Linear spreading speed in non-monotone population models'] Let $\xi^{\pm}_{k}$ be \emph{comparison density profiles}. For
