{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:16.158502+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_70f7ce52fa48996fd3e89951aa1f9b39b840e75303b47acc246ee07b0a02d763","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 ({\cite[Lemma~A.2) of arXiv:2604.13845, 'Minkowski content construction of\\ the CLE gasket measure'] {kms2023nonsimpleremovability}}]

Fix $n \in \N$, $r_0 > 0$, and $K \subseteq \h$ compact.  There exists a constant $C = C(n,K,r_0)$ so that the following is true.  Suppose that $z_1,\ldots,z_n \in K$ are distinct.  For each $1 \leq i \leq n$ there exists $n_i \in \N$ and $s_{i,k},r_{i,k} \in [0,r_0)$ such that $0 < s_{i,k} < r_{i,k}$ for $1 \leq k \leq n_i-1$ and $0 = s_{i,n_i} < r_{i,n_i}$ so that the annuli $A(z_i, s_{i,k}, r_{i,k})$ are pairwise disjoint and
\begin{equation}
 \prod_{i=1}^n \frac{\prod_{k=1}^{n_i-1} s_{i,k}}{\prod_{k=1}^{n_i} r_{i,k}} \leq C \prod_{i=2}^n \frac{1}{\min_{i' < i} |z_i - z_{i'}|}
\end{equation}
with the convention $\prod_{k=1}^{n_i-1} s_{i,k} = 1$ if $n_i = 1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.359616+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_70fb83ce020a9c896dfcf12817326f69161b11fa60aaed4ff485b042108070a4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma compactness-K of arXiv:2605.14149, 'The mean-field limit of online stochastic vector balancing'] For any finite constant $c\geq 0$, the set
