{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:32:35.603514+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7123c7860ca92ce2e3712cde9675066e1e6eb2c8ae281044cd82766fbf1321d7","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2606.13264, 'Interference Queueing Networks: A Replica Mean-Field Approach in the Symmetric Setting'] We say that $Q$ is associated if for any $f$ and $g$ increasing real function for the partial order on $\mathbb{N}^N$, and $t \in \mathbb{R}^+ $
