{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:22:21.887216+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_712c050084fbffc9b74671348d64c3a5b2b00feb46e21f9a0b25e2bd3c77c2b9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:esol is volg P of arXiv:2411.11345, 'Real Gaussian exponential sums via a real moment map'] For all open set $U\subset \mathbb{R}^m$, we have
  \begin{equation}
    \esol{\mathcal{E};U}=\frac{1}{2^{\tfrac{m-2}{2}}s_m} \int_{\mu(U)}\sqrt{det D^2_p \Phi^*} \, \mathrm{d} p
  \end{equation}
  where $\Phi^*:\interior(P)\to \mathbb{R}$ is the Legendre transform of $\Phi$ and where $s_m$ denotes the $m$-dimensional volume of the unit sphere $S^m\subset \mathbb{R}^{m+1}$. In particular, we have, for $U=\mathbb{R}^m$:
  \begin{equation}
    \esol{\mathcal{E};\mathbb{R}^m}=\frac{1}{2^{\tfrac{m-2}{2}}s_m} \vol_g(P)
  \end{equation}
  where $\vol_g(P)$ denotes the Riemannian volume of $P$ for the metric given for all $p\in P$ by $D^2_p\Phi^*$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:48:30.921054+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_712d9a5c993a5d307481c162168481e4d2dc42ad783d822276b77f242ff11a0f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defin 13 of arXiv:2609.00974, 'On Algebraic Integrability\\ of Vector Fields \\ with Rational Function Coefficients\\ tha'] We introduce a notation for an $n$-coefficients of an element.
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Let $k$ be a field. Let $K$ be $k[x]$, or $k((x))$ Laurent series. Let $n$ be an integer.
    Let $f\in K$ be given by $f=\ldots+a_{-1}x^{-1}+a_0+a_1x+a_2x^2+\ldots$, where $a_i\in k$. We define:
    \begin{equation}
        [x^{n}]f \coloneqq a_n \in k.
    \end{equation}
    \item Let $K$ be a generic point of a curve with a coordinate $x$, or $k((x))$.
    Then, $1,x,x^2,\ldots,x^{p-1}$ is a $p$-basis of $K$ over $K^p$.
    Let $n\in \{0,1,\ldots,p-1\}$. Let $f\in K$. It has a unique presentation of the form $f=a_0+a_1x+a_2x^2+\ldots+a_{p-1}x^{p-1}$, where $a_i\in K^p$. We define:
    \begin{equation}
        \widetilde{[x^{n}]}f \coloneqq a_n \in K^p.
    \end{equation}

\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

