{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:33:06.543310+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7173e274106cbcf125448b27175c7df525b3e0cc91f14edb62617f9d43f41bbd","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 21 (Neck detection) of arXiv:2608.25971, 'Positive \texorpdfstring{$\tau$}{tau}-bi-Ricci curvature and Mean curvature flow with surg'] Fix $\eps>0$, $k\in\mathbb N$, $L\geq10$, and $\Theta>0$.  There exist
  \begin{equation*}
  \eta_{\mathrm{neck}}
  =\eta_{\mathrm{neck}}(n,\alpha,\eps,k,L,\Theta)>0
  \end{equation*}
  and
  \begin{equation*}
  H_{\mathrm{neck}}
  =H_{\mathrm{neck}}(n,\alpha,\eps,k,L,\Theta)<\infty
  \end{equation*}
  with the following property.

  Let $(p,t)$ be a point of a smooth flow satisfying the hypotheses of this
  section, and set
  \begin{equation*}
  r=\frac{n-1}{H(p,t)}.
  \end{equation*}
  Assume that $ \mathcal P\bigl(p,t,2(L+2)r,\Theta r^2\bigr)$  
  is defined.  If
  \begin{equation*}
  H(p,t)\geq H_{\mathrm{neck}}R^{-1},
  \qquad
  \lambda_1(p,t)\leq\eta_{\mathrm{neck}}H(p,t),
  \end{equation*}
  then $p$ is the center of an $(\eps,k,L)$-neck of radius $r$ at time $t$.
  If $\Theta\geq L^2$, then after rescaling by $r^{-1}$ the flow on the
  corresponding backward cylinder over $[-L^2,0]$ is $\eps$-close in
  parabolic $C^k$ norm to a round shrinking cylinder whose radius at time
  zero is one.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:07:35.010144+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_71794f69b0177487013489875c0036e5035516d6c3b67b927d86e8063bf54c31","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 10 of arXiv:2609.02850, 'Canonical-row Chern flow on Bott--Samelson towers:\\ realizable-volume models for Schubert'] Let $|\alpha|=d$, let $i\ne j$, and suppose $\alpha_i,\alpha_j\ge1$.  Then
\begin{equation}
 c_\alpha^2
 \ge c_{\alpha+e_i-e_j}\,c_{\alpha-e_i+e_j}.
\end{equation}
Thus the nonzero coefficients on every affine root line form a log-concave
interval with no internal zeros.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:33:06.542622+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_717ca05fa26784b8f25f58f2a0a271ae04f3c7f2dd290ec237cfa4e12f3d48a5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 11 ($\tau$-bi-Ricci Poincar\'e inequality) of arXiv:2608.25971, 'Positive \texorpdfstring{$\tau$}{tau}-bi-Ricci curvature and Mean curvature flow with surg'] For every $\eta>0$ there exists
$\gamma=\gamma(n,\alpha_0,\eta)>0$ with the following property.
Let
\begin{equation*}
 X:M^n\longrightarrow\Hh^{n+1}_{\kappa}
\end{equation*}
be a smooth closed two-sided hypersurface immersion satisfying
$H>0$, $H\geq n\kappa$, and \eqref{eq:uniform-taubiric}.  Suppose that
$u\in W^{1,2}(M)$ vanishes almost everywhere outside the set
\eqref{eq:acylindrical-region}.  Then, for every $\varrho\geq1$,
\begin{equation}
 \gamma\int_Mu^2H^2\,d\mu
 \leq
 \int_M\left(
 \varrho^{-1}|\nabla u|^2
 +\varrho u^2\frac{|\nabla A|^2}{H^2}
 \right)d\mu.
\end{equation}
The constant $\gamma$ is uniform for
$0\leq\tau\leq2$ and $0\leq\kappa\leq1$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:32:11.151214+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_717cd704b0a470c2776ef7bd06f79d26566bdb5ff146129ac88c1184f5669af8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition le:distance of arXiv:2510.13733, 'Internal Diffusion Limited Aggregation \\ with Critical Branching Random Walks'] For any  $d \geq 1$ there exist constants $c, C > 0$, only depending on the dimension $d$, such that for any $R \geq 1$,
