\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:10.185623+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_717e9f1cf56359d36f226193235fc960dec2f71715fc60ca59be435c53d20d73","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 109 of arXiv:2605.03236, 'Stochastic It\^o Equations and Parabolic Second-Order Equations with singular Drift'] If $f\geq0$ is independent of $t$, $p\in [d_{0},\infty]$, then for   $\lambda\geq \varkappa_{0}^{2}\rho_{b}^{-2}$
