{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:58:40.873197+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_71b711eeb3b77120963f63496d4d95ac4ed6b2b75962c6546727b2f2fe4595b7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop Zph2 of arXiv:2605.10617, 'Logarithmic scaling of selective sweep curves:\\ from tents to houses'] Assume that $Z_1^N$ starts in $\big\lfloor\tfrac {\log N}{\varphi_N}\big\rfloor$.
    Then for any $T$, $\delta>0$
    \begin{equation}
    \lim_{N\to\infty} \mathbb{P} \Big(  \sup_{t \leq T} \Big| \log_N^+(Z^N_{1} (t \varphi_N^{-1} \log N)) - (b+at) \Big| >\delta \Big)
