{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:12:46.875637+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_720ff1f7c9e6455a53bfbbbc22ded0e99ff5204b7a28d467885433e9131b5b97","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm_path2 of arXiv:2608.08532, 'Constrained Maximum Weight Paths in Random Geometric Graphs'] Let~\(\epsilon_1,\epsilon_2\) be as in~((f_eq of the paper)) and suppose~\(r_n \geq \frac{1}{n^{\beta}}\) and~\(L_n = \frac{\zeta_n}{r_n} \geq 1\) for constant~\(0 < \beta < \frac{1}{2},\) as in~((rn_cnd of the paper)). Also suppose there are constants~\(C_0,x_0 > 0\) and~\(s > 4,\) such that the edge weight ccdf~\(F_c\) satisfies
\begin{equation}
F_c(ax) \leq \frac{C_0}{a^s} F_c(x)
\end{equation}
for all~\(a > 1\) and~\(x > x_0.\) For every~\(\kappa, \lambda > 0,\) there is a constant~\(\mu > 0\) such that
\begin{equation}
