{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:00:46.839137+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7210bcedf63a1c24fd005dcbd8133ea402b2ec5fb8d446db7ede53535fcd2e8c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 3 of arXiv:2608.13374, 'Nearly Sharp Comparison Results for sliced and max-sliced Wasserstein distances'] Let $d \geq 2$. For any $K \geq 1$, there exist a finitely supported probability measure $\nu$ and a probability measure $\mu$ on $\R^d$ with $K_{\mu,\nu} \asymp_d K$ such that Condition~\ref{cond:voronoi}  holds and
