{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:47:07.715232+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_72160fb8dd3d2b8139bbf7a362d8ba41943fe6e94f84a8e93457c23b7ef17ad6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2608.06392, '2608.06392'] Let $g:\mathbb R_+\to\mathbb R_+$ be locally integrable, ultimately monotone, and $\int_0^\infty g(t)\,dt<\infty$.
    Assume that for some constant $K>0$,
\[
    g(t)\sim{K}\,\frac{L(t)}{t}  \qquad \text{as} \quad t\to\infty,
\]
    where $L\in\mathcal{SV}_\infty$. Then
\begin{equation}
    {\mathcal{L}g(0)-\mathcal{L}g(s)}\sim{K}\int_{1/s}^\infty\frac{L(u)}{u}\,du
    \qquad \text{as} \quad s\downarrow{0}.
\end{equation}

    Conversely, if
\begin{equation}
    {\mathcal{L}g(0)-\mathcal{L}g(s)}\sim{C}\int_{1/s}^\infty\frac{L(u)}{u}\,du
    \qquad \text{as} \quad s\downarrow{0}
\end{equation}
    for some $C>0$, then
\begin{equation}
    g(t)\sim{C}\,\frac{L(t)}{t} \qquad \text{as} \quad t\to\infty.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:06:42.717701+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_72161311d44310ce6b0e3ae568c9bbfc071e6e84d61b6cc1144a3115bf21009b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition bd of arXiv:2411.04116, 'Poisson genericity in numeration systems with exponentially mixing probabilities'] The mixing property for $\mu$ implies that there is a constant  $R>0$ such that, for every $u,v\in\Omega^*$, for every $i,\ell\ge 1$,
 \begin{equation}    \nonumber    \mu(x\in \Omega^\mathbb N: I_i(x,w) I_{i+\ell}(x,v) = 1) \le R
 \mu_{\left| u \right|}(u) \mu_{\left| v \right|}(v).
  \end{equation} 
We call this the bounded distortion property and we say that $R$ is the bounded distortion constant.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:43:18.952481+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_721954ba6d54d8c1eb69ceac030a017fe61f10e3714d1c48b7eee810ffba15f5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem mainth of arXiv:2609.02541, 'A note on the norm of the embedding of $\text{PW}^2$ into $\text{PW}^q$'] For any $q>2$
    \begin{align*}
    M_q = \sup_{\substack{f\in PW^2\\ \|f\|_2=1}}\|f\|_q^q \leq \Lambda_q := \int_0^{\infty} (\lambda'(x))^{q/2}dx,
    \end{align*}
where $\lambda(s)$ denotes the best $L^2$ concentration in $PW^2$ on $[-s/2,s/2]$, i.e.,
$$\lambda(s):=\sup_{\substack{f\in PW^2\\ \lVert f\rVert_2=1}}
 \int_{-s/2}^{s/2}|f(x)|^2 dx.$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.239246+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_721c60f270b018093ff241eac8ab983b8dc45ad7b52da9245e81d3e27aee02d9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition eq:clark-ocone_sig of arXiv:2604.22528, 'Malliavin calculus for signatures with applications to finance'] Let $F = \bracketsig[T]{\bm{\ell}}$ with $\bm{\ell} \in \TA[d+1]$. Then, $F \in \mathbb{D}^{1, 2}$ and
    \begin{equation}
