{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:38:17.796618+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_721c621afb311e0f7acd84fb8b8890fe6a10544c474997e0b0208a6381b3ca07","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:two_delta=1/gamma of arXiv:2509.23496, 'Crossing probabilities in geometric inhomogeneous random graphs'] The two-edge crossing probabilities satisfy
    \begin{align*}
        \pi_{(u),R}^{(2)} &\asymp  \pi_{(u),R}+ u^{-\gamma} R^{d(2-\delta-\gamma)} \log R \\
        &\asymp \begin{cases}
                    u^{-\gamma} R^{d(2-\delta-\gamma)} \log R , & \text{ on } \{R^{-d}\le u\}\\
                    u^{-1} R^{d(1-\delta)}\log R & \text{ on } \{ R^{d(1-\frac 1 \gamma)} \log R\le u\le R^{-d}\}\\
                    1 & \text{ on } \{u\le R^{d(1-\frac 1 \gamma)}\log R\},
                \end{cases}\\
        \pi_{r,R}^{(2)}&\asymp \pi_{r,R}+ r^{d\gamma} R^{d(2-\delta-\gamma)}(\log R)^{1-\gamma}(\log r)^\gamma\\
        &
        \asymp \begin{cases}
                    r^{d\gamma} R^{d(2-\gamma-\delta)} (\log R)^{1-\gamma}(\log r)^\gamma & \text{ on } \{r \leq R (\log R)^{\frac{-1}{d(1-\gamma)}}\},\\
                    r^d R^{d(1-\delta)} (\log R)^2 & \text{ on } \{R (\log R)^{\frac{-1}{d(1-\gamma)}} \leq r \leq R/2 \}.
                \end{cases}
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:30:08.063613+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_721f70974171d0d4b7ebfddc64d02d8fd8af742dd0e7d5961dddf89da42df620","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2608.12415, 'Sharp Phase Transition for Ellipsoid Fitting'] For the base iteration, we define $
	\mathsf{Proper} \mathcal{L}^*(M^{-1}\eta )$ to be the weighted linear combination of the following terms in the $3$-way concatenation in $\frac{r+s}{s^2-ru} \cdot A^{-1}\eta$ :
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item Proper concatenations such that each non-trivial gadget in $A^{-1}$-path is an $\alpha$-gadget;
		\item Linearization of well-behaved intersections such that each non-trivial gadget in $A^{-1}$-path is an $\alpha$-gadget without interior $\beta$-gadget.
