	Let $\mathsf{ProperShape} \mathcal{L}^*(M^{-1}\eta )$ denote the collection of underlying proper shapes.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:01:54.388768+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_721fbdd817e3194f8a287568cd67ebc0263643073a00f21a117c888ab990463b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem alpha=0 of arXiv:2411.02156, 'Martin boundary of a degenerate Reflected Brownian Motion in a wedge'] Suppose $\gamma_2(x_{max}, Y^\pm(x_{max})) \neq 0$. 
