{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:20:15.624052+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7221b7d918bb5f44df2f37dd10be2d54b17e2565ad9c36a94c5a4ae5ec327513","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:no-additive-intro of arXiv:2609.00889, 'Dominant-Degree Conditions for Ramsey--Tur\'an Factors of Non-Directed Cycle Orientations'] For every fixed integer $s\ge2$ and every real constant $C$, there are arbitrarily large multiples $n$ of $2s$ and $n$-vertex oriented graphs $D$ such that
 $\sigma_{\mathrm{Ore}}^*(D)\ge\frac34n+C,$
but $D$ has no $C_{2s}^{\mathrm{ad}}$-factor.  More precisely, the constructions satisfy
\[
\sigma_{\mathrm{Ore}}^*(D)\ge
 \begin{cases}
 \frac34n+\frac34\alpha(D)-2, & s=2,\\[1mm]
 \frac34n+\frac14\alpha(D)-\frac32, & s\ge3.
 \end{cases}
\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:13:22.505316+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7225dc77e92aef369878cae9adab7574cc17fe25151233445e5f581aeff2f4ea","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def.algorithm of arXiv:2505.15283, 'Quantization of Probability Distributions via Divide-and-Conquer: Convergence and Error Pr'] Let $T^f(\mu,0) = \delta_{f(\mu)}$ and for $n\geq 1$ let 
\begin{equation}
    \mu^{(n),f} :=T^f(\mu,n) = \mu(\Omega_-)T^f(\mu_-,n-1)+\mu(\Omega_+)T^f(\mu_+,n-1)
\end{equation}
and we let $F^{(n),f}(x) := \mu^{(n),f}(-\infty,x]$ denote the corresponding CDF.  If $\mu(\Omega_\pm) = 0$ the procedure terminates prematurely and sets $\mu^{(n),f}=\delta_{f(\mu_\mp)},\ \forall n\geq 0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:26.922750+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7226adaf6c4288453cc4c0a6762bf1c2b6176d90ee97c5c51349a4d0c96bd006","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:ordrIn of arXiv:2505.09604, 'Exceptional force, uncountably many solutions in the KPZ fixed point'] The following holds on the event $\Omega_1$ for all $\xi\in\mathbb{R}$, $s\in\mathbb{R}$, and $x_0 <  y_0 \in\mathbb{R}$. For these choices, define
           \begin{equation}
           \begin{aligned}
                 \mathfrak t_{RL}&=\inf\{r>s:\tau^{\xi,+}_{(x_0,s)}(r)=\tau^{\xi,-}_{(y_0,s)}(r)\}\\
               \mathfrak t_{LL}&=\inf\{r>s:\tau^{\xi,-}_{(x_0,s)}(r)=\tau^{\xi,-}_{(y_0,s)}(r)\}\\
               \mathfrak t_{RR}&=\inf\{r>s:\tau^{\xi,+}_{(x_0,s)}(r)=\tau^{\xi,+}_{(y_0,s)}(r)\}.
           \end{aligned}
           \end{equation}
           Then, 
       \begin{align}

           \tau^{\xi,+}_{(x_0,s)}(r)&\geq \tau^{\xi,-}_{(y_0,s)}(r) \quad\text{for}\quad r\in [\mathfrak t_{RL},\infty), \quad\text{and, moreover,} \\

           \tau^{\xi,+}_{(x_0,s)}(r) &=  \tau^{\xi,-}_{(y_0,s)}(r) \quad\text{for}\quad r\in [\mathfrak t_{RL},\mathfrak t_{LL}\wedge \mathfrak t_{RR}] 
       \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:05:28.146609+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_722824cae545079ab34aa5d4c47c0b618bb6a95e4df4a3ac0a2f0f90f2619d30","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:2 of arXiv:2602.00988, 'Wealth exchange under ceiling and flooring constraints: a modified Bennati–Dragulescu–Yako'] Let ${\bf p}(t) = \{p_n(t)\}_{n\geq 0}$ be a classical solution to the system of nonlinear ODEs (equation eq:law_limit of the paper)-(equation eq:two-classes of the paper) with ${\bf p}(0) \in V_\mu$, we have
\begin{equation}
\sup\limits_{t\geq 0} \sum\limits_{n\geq 0} K^n\,p_n(t) \leq \max\left\{\frac{K^{b+1}+K^a}{1-\mu/b},\sum_{n\geq 0} K^n\,p_n(0)\right\}
\end{equation}
for all $K > 1$, provided that $\sum_{n\geq 0} K^n\,p_n(0) < \infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:37:15.468213+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_722d40e80889429a31ebfee265e6220f5edb87392a798c5e80a510510d9430d2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2607.12384, '2607.12384'] Let \(u\) be the solution to equation \eqref{eq:main equation}, and let \(G\) denote the
	corresponding heat kernel defined in \eqref{eq:G=integral}. Assume that \(d=1\).
	Fix \(T>0\), \(p\ge2\), and let \(0\le s<r\le T\), \(y,z\in\mathbb R\).
	Assume that the Malliavin derivative of \(u\) satisfies
	\begin{equation}
		\|D_{s,y}u(r,z)\|_p^2
		\le C G_{r-s}^2(z-y)
		+ C\int_s^r\int_{\mathbb R}
		G_{r-r_1}^2(z-z_1)\,
		\|D_{s,y}u(r_1,z_1)\|_p^2\,dz_1\,dr_1,
	\end{equation}
	for some constant \(C>0\) depending on \(T\) and \(p\). Then there exists a
	constant \(C_{T,p}>0\), depending on \(T\) and \(p\), such that
	\begin{equation}
		\|D_{s,y}u(r,z)\|_p^2
		\le C_{T,p}\,(r-s)^{-\frac \beta \alpha}\,G_{r-s}(z-y),
	\end{equation}
	and consequently
	\begin{equation}
		\|D_{s,y}u(r,z)\|_p
		\le C_{T,p}\,(r-s)^{-\frac{\beta}{2\alpha}}\,G_{r-s}(z-y)^{\frac 1 2}.
	\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.528157+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_722d71205f0f9758785ac9438dea549bc6660b9514b67f272bee085bbb39eb46","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Conjecture 1 of arXiv:2609.02610, 'The frame set of the first Hermite function'] The frame set of the first Hermite function is given by
  \begin{equation}
    \cF(h_1)
    =\left\{a,b\in(0, \infty):
      ab<1
      \text{ and }
      ab\neq\frac{q-1}{q}
      \text{ for every }q\in\Z_{\geq2}
