{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:03:35.745599+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_722d7be7aa17cf0c74df09acae77624e2f7446faf0432091df29be75a33b88f7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:localNumeratorComm of arXiv:2609.02743, 'Sharp mean-field estimates for diffusive log/Riesz gases in the Hilbert--Schmidt regime'] There exists $\beta_{\mathrm{loc}}=\beta_{\mathrm{loc}}(\mu,v,n)>0$ such that for every $0<\gamma\le\beta_{\mathrm{loc}}$ and every $\sigma\in\{\pm1\}$,
