{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.610716+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_722dee1194ff5bd65ce595fd3097ddb6bd0310b44644d742f3e49d5cb747eeff","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 17 of arXiv:2607.08536, 'Soft edge limit of the Laguerre beta-ensemble at the lower edge'] Let $\ma{s}=(s_{ij})$ be a continuous, symmetric, positive semi-definite $d\times d$ matrix-valued function on $\R^{d}$, $\ma{b}:\R^{d}\rightarrow \R^{d}$ a continuous function. Let $X(t)$ be an It\^{o} diffusion with generator
     $$Af=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i,j}s_{ij}\partial_{i}\partial_{j}f+\sum_{i}b_{i}\partial_{i}f, \qquad f\in C_{c}^{\infty}(\R^{d}),$$
    and initial distribution $\nu$.

    Suppose $X_n(i), i\ge 0$ is a Markov chain in $\R^d$ with increments $Z_n(i+1)=X_n(i+1)-X_n(i)$ such that for each $r>0$
        \begin{equation}
        \begin{split}
            \sup_{|x|\le r}\left|m_n\ev[Z_n(i)|X_n(i-1)=x]-\ma{b}(x)\right| &\rightarrow 0,\\
            \sup_{|x|\le r}\left|m_n \ev[Z_n(i)Z_n(i)^{\top}|X_n(i-1)=x]-\ma{s}(x)\right|&\rightarrow 0,\\
            \sup_{|x|\le r}\left|m_n\ev[|Z_n(i)|^{4}|X_n(i-1)=x]\right|&\rightarrow 0,\\
        \end{split}
    \end{equation}
    uniformly for $i/m_n$ on compact subsets of $\R_+$ as $n\to\infty$, and $X_n(0)\Rightarrow \nu$ in law. Then 
    we have
     \begin{align}
       \left( X_n({\lfloor t m_n\rfloor}, t\ge 0) \right)\Rightarrow \left(X(t), t\ge 0\right)
     \end{align}
     in law, with respect to the Skorokhod topology on compact subsets of $\R_+$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

