{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.402503+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7238be0f38b78363f98597f226963138987b6e000ce8e8cffd37290a7b8abb9c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor: ReductionBounded of arXiv:2603.26932, 'On the satisfaction frequency of spectral characterization conditions'] Suppose that $\bM_{p,\beta} \sim \operatorname{SymHaar}(R_{p,\beta}^{n\times n})$. 
    Let it be understood that $\rank_q(\cdot)$ refers to the rank over $\bbF_q \cong \bbZ[x]/(p\bbZ[x] + \beta(x)\bbZ[x])$. 
    Then, for every $k\leq n$,  as random $R_{p,\beta}$ modules, 
    \begin{align}
        \bbP\Bigl(\coker\bigl(\bM_{p,\beta},\bigr) \in  *  \mid \rank_{q}\bigl(\bM_{p,\beta}\bigr) = n-k\Bigr) = \bbP\Bigl(\coker\bigl(\bK  \bigr) \in  * \Bigr),
    \end{align}
    where $\bK$ is a symmetric $k\times k$ matrix with entries Haar distributed on $pR_{p,\beta} + \beta(x) R_{p,\beta}$. 
    That is, 
    \begin{align}
        \bK  \sim  p\operatorname{SymHaar}(R_{p,\beta}^{k\times k})  + \beta(x) \operatorname{SymHaar}(R_{p,\beta}^{k\times k}).   
    \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.335441+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7239221a6ead93469218bb88aa5dfc4186d905df2cefc762d9d919a2a95d6f81","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma approx balls from segments with unif explo of arXiv:2609.04138, 'The conformally invariant metric on $\CLE_4$ I:\\ subsequential limits of the non-simple C'] We have for all $t \in \BQ_{\ge 0}$ and all $\alpha \in \SCS'$, a.s.,
	\begin{equation*}
