{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:55.640068+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_724d3219f9e84215690d0041a5d86a5a0a1468a613b01591ae1ff81814082fc2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 9 (Mean-field convergence with converging coefficients) of arXiv:2605.23529, 'Generalized Bessel-Dunkl diffusions'] Let the finite systems be given by \eqref{eq:mf:root-sde}, with the same $1/N$ mean-field scaling, but with $\sigma,b,k$ replaced by coefficients $\sigma_N,b_N,k_N$. Assume \ref{ass:mf:exist} and \ref{ass:mf:initial}. Assume also that $k_N$ is symmetric, that all coefficients satisfy the growth bounds \eqref{eq:mf:growth-sigma}-\eqref{eq:mf:growth-k} uniformly in $N$, and that, for every $T,R>0$,
    \begin{align}
        \lim_{N\to\infty}
        \sup_{\substack{0\le t\le T\\ |x|\le R}}
        \left|\sigma_N^2(t,x)-\sigma^2(t,x)\right|
            &=
            0,
        \\
        \lim_{N\to\infty}
        \sup_{\substack{0\le t\le T\\ |x|\le R}}
        |b_N(t,x)-b(t,x)|
            &=
            0,
        \\
        \lim_{N\to\infty}
        \sup_{\substack{0\le t\le T\\ |x|\le R,\ |y|\le R}}
        |k_N(t,x,y)-k(t,x,y)|
            &=
            0,
        \\
        \lim_{N\to\infty}
        \sup_{\substack{0\le t\le T\\ 0\le x\le R}}
        |k_N(t,x)-k(t,x)|
            &=
            0.

    \end{align}
    Then the conclusions of Theorem~\ref{thm:mf:classical} remain valid, with the same limiting equation \eqref{eq:mf:limit-equation}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:31:20.614239+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_724f97b5f19d21e0450bd89b126262847a86c5f80c30e85898cce7618cc74064","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 9 of arXiv:2608.25785, 'Proper Actions on Homogeneous Spaces of the Upper Triangular Matrix Group via Coarse Geome'] For each $n\in \Z_{\geq 1}$ and $i,j\in [n]$ with $i\leq j$,
