{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:27:14.778677+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_72899580cbd270277b94aaac284e57901947640c51093d75b756912e77f8a7fb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 (Uniqueness at Bayes, and the multiplicity certificate) of arXiv:2608.23094, 'One Inverse Step is a Convex Program:\\ Bayes-Limit Calibration of Diffusion Inversion'] For every data law and every schedule with $\abar_T>0$ the fixed point \eqref{eq:fixedpoint} is unique at the Bayes limit, and a trained score admits a second solution only if
