{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:33:01.785782+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_72962bfc0b377d0ab13e11882d09c45174b629f93292c0d4cf1fb4a585d601cf","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 44 (Wiener chaos, infinite-dimensional version) of arXiv:2605.14630, '2605.14630'] For any $n\geqs 1$, we denote by $\cH_n$ the subspace of 
$\cH = L^2(\Omega,\cF,\fP)$ spanned by the random variables 
