{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:19:00.857063+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_72977c65a3e8294a2e116fd30adf105b8d9642bad9ea7d6e4680443a86806142","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 (Path-space mixed coincidence identity) of arXiv:2608.20337, 'Information on trajectories:\\ martingales and random times'] For $Z_T$ of~\eqref{eq:pathZ} with $0 < Z_T(\alpha) < \infty$, for every horizon $T$, every collection of positive $\cF_T$-measurable factors $(\Pi_{i,T})_{i=1}^W$, and every path measure $Q \ll P|_{\cF_T}$,
\begin{equation}
  \log Z_T(\alpha)
  = \sum_{i=1}^W \alpha_i\,\E_Q[\log \Pi_{i,T}]
    - \KL(Q\|P|_{\cF_T})
    + \KL(Q\|Q_T^\alpha),
\end{equation}
where $Q_T^\alpha$ is the Gibbs law
\begin{equation}
  \frac{\dd Q_T^\alpha}{\dd P|_{\cF_T}}
  = \frac{\prod_{i=1}^W \Pi_{i,T}^{\alpha_i}}{Z_T(\alpha)}.
\end{equation}
The residual $\KL(Q\|Q_T^\alpha) \geq 0$ vanishes if and only if $Q = Q_T^\alpha$, so the identity is equivalent to the variational form $\log Z_T(\alpha) = \sup_{Q \ll
P|_{\cF_T}}\bigl\{\sum_i \alpha_i\,\E_Q[\log \Pi_{i,T}] - \KL(Q\|P|_{\cF_T})\bigr\}$,
attained uniquely at $Q_T^\alpha$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:50:36.766377+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_729a0508f27b189c2bfca811df8c1dcfbb214b0a0792660e1956b91d3a3171bd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 27 (Small $D$ and large $T$) of arXiv:2609.04155, 'The subconvexity problem for symmetric square\\ $L$-functions in Level aspect'] Let $D\leq p^{\delta_1}$, and $T\geq p^{\delta_2}$ for some $\delta_1$, and $\delta_2>0$. We have,
