{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:38:57.119342+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_729fe90966b3144efa7bb20c9eeeae0f17899b04da16ebdc4b02d0f98bb04d52","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 of arXiv:2604.04840, 'Bounding the Gap Between Zeros of the Variable-\\Parameter Confluent Hypergeometric Functi'] The function $\Phi(a,b,z)$ is related to Whittaker's $\mathcal{M}$ function, defined as \cite{Buchholz}\footnote[2]{The normalizing factor $\Gamma(1+\mu)$ ensures that $\mathcal{M}_{\varkappa, \mu/2}(z)$ is defined even when $\mu$ is a negative integer.}

