{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.989464+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_72e4e14b899ea3e446de23f02fd8b31e2403793fd39c9e5a21f402222f692b4e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 81 of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] Let $ p  = p(n) = (1 + \epsilon)/n$ with $n^{-1/3} \ll \epsilon \ll n^{-s}$, for some $s > 0$. Denote by $\cT_p$ a realization of the unweighted ($\beta = 0$) UST on $\cC_1(p)$. Then there exists some constant $c =c(s)> 0$ such that
