{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.756134+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_72ef21747fec6db6907e4a2504a519f99b31ea5dafd2b8fd9c7722f4aa992eb9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:abstract-simple-splitting of arXiv:2608.02459, 'Response Calculus for Spectral Simplicity\\ and Joint Eigenvalue Densities'] Under (equation eq:countable-direction-space of the paper) and
(equation eq:direction-annihilator of the paper), for every multiple positive
eigenvalue $\Lambda$ of $A_\mu$ there exists $q\in\mathcal Q$ such that
\begin{equation}
 B_q^\Lambda(\mu)
 =-\kappa\LambdaP_\Lambda^\mu
 \operatorname{Mult}_q|_{E_\mu(\Lambda)}

