{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:55:37.870282+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_72efd0bb1799289407013d59d4a3ae803576b6abe8c5b031d835ebc88551b2a5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:path_prob of arXiv:2605.06511, 'Logarithmic Mixing of Random Walks on Dynamical Random Cluster Models'] Let $n \in \mathbb{N}$ be sufficiently large and $G = (V, E)$ a $d$-regular graph on $n$ vertices. For all $\mu > 0$, $t \geq 0$, $x > 0$, $e = \{u, u'\} \in E$ such that $B_R(u)$ has at most one cycle, and $(\eta, v) \in \{0, 1\}^E \times V$, then
		\begin{align*}
			& \mathbb{P}\left[\xi_{u, e}^{\mathrm{path}}\left(t, t + x\right) \mid \left(\eta_t, X_t\right) = \left(\eta, v\right)\right] \\
			\geq&\ \left(1 - 2K \left(p + (1-p)e^{-\mu x}\right)^{{R}/{2}}\right) \mathbb{P}\left[S_{t+x} \left(R, K\right) \mid \left(\eta_t, X_t\right) = \left(\eta, v\right)\right].
		\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:09:23.952198+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_72f167a07b9cb3c608fc043778a40108bfcf78b0e89e5f04bbd4cb6355b8a4b0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 4 of arXiv:2607.21759, 'Marchenko--Pastur law for tensor powers of exchangeable unconditional vectors'] Let $d$ be fixed, and let $\mathbf X = (X_1,\dotsc,X_n)$ be the exchangeable unconditional base vector. If 
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $\E X_1^2 \to 1$, 
        \item  $\E(X_1^2X_2^2) - \E(X_1^2)\E(X_2^2) \to 0$, and
        \item  there exists some $\epsilon > 0$ such that $\sup_n \E(\abs{X_1}^{4d + \epsilon}) < \infty$,
    \end{enumerate} then the three conditions in \cref{thm:main} are satisfied, and we have with probability $1$ that \[\ESD(K_{\PrincipalT}) \wkconv \mu_{\MP(c)}.\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:25:06.117009+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_72f2583cc58677107e1080fbf11a17e072b460cffd9f48417fd5555dba06ec2d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 (Bartlett spectrum) of arXiv:2608.22342, 'Completely Positive Entropy and Fourier Central Limit Theorems for Stationary Random Measu'] Let $\eta$ be stationary with local second moments. There is a unique positive
translation-bounded Radon measure $\sigma_\eta$ on $\bR^d$ such that
\begin{equation}

    \int (\mathbb S f)^\circ\,\overline{(\mathbb S g)^\circ}\,d\eta
    =\int_{\bR^d}\hat f(\xi)\overline{\hat g(\xi)}\,
      d\sigma_\eta(\xi),
    \qquad f,g\in\mathcal S(\bR^d).
\end{equation}
In particular,
\begin{equation}

    \Var_\eta(\mathbb S f)
    =\int_{\bR^d}|\hat f(\xi)|^2\,d\sigma_\eta(\xi).
\end{equation}
