{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:16:18.652512+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_72fb618539262ebe9226b3b752cdcba7b801e6b59ce601e2e142f809dd556489","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 2 of arXiv:2607.24533, 'Colored Markov-Modulated Brownian Motion for Preemptive Workload Stacks'] {Suppose that Assumptions~\ref{assump:intensity} and~\ref{assump:stability} hold.}
Then, using the active-time MMBM of Lemma~\ref{lem:active-censoring} and iterating from $c=C$ down to $c=2$, the depletion probability matrix defined in \eqref{eq:Phi-y} admits the representation
\begin{align*}
\vect{\Phi}_c(y)=e^{\vect{U}_c y},\qquad y>0,
\end{align*}
where $\vect U_c$ is the unique depletion exponent solving
\begin{equation}

\tfrac12(\vect{\Delta}_{\sigma}^{(c)})^2\vect U_c^2
+\vect{\Delta}_{\mu}^{(c)}\vect U_c
+\widetilde{\vect T}^{(c)}
=\vect0,
\end{equation}
for which $0$ is a simple eigenvalue with right eigenvector $\e$, and all nonzero eigenvalues lie in the open left half-plane.

{At color $1$, under the corresponding conditions in Assumption~\ref{assump:stability}:}
\begin{itemize}
\item \emph{Hold-and-jump model.} Color $1$ is depleting, and \eqref{eq:layer-qme} and {\eqref{eq:neg_drift}} again give a unique depletion exponent $\vect U_1$, with $\vect\Phi_1(y)=e^{\vect U_1 y}$, $y>0$.

\item \emph{Regulated-base model.} Color $1$ is regulated rather than depleted, and there is instead a unique stationary regulated-MMBM decay exponent $\vect K_{\mathrm{reg}}$ solving
\begin{equation}

\tfrac12 \vect{K}_{\mathrm{reg}}^{2}(\vect{\Delta}_{\sigma}^{(1)})^{2}-\vect{K}_{\mathrm{reg}}\vect{\Delta}_{\mu}^{(1)}+\widetilde{\vect{T}}^{(1)}=\vect{0},
\end{equation}
with eigenvalues in the open left half-plane, giving the anchor density
\begin{equation}

\vect{\nu}^{\mathrm R}(x)=\vect{g}_{\mathrm{reg}}e^{\vect{K}_{\mathrm{reg}}x},
\qquad x>0,
\end{equation}
where $\vect{g}_{\mathrm{reg}}$ satisfies the reflecting boundary condition
\begin{equation}

\vect{g}_{\mathrm{reg}}\left(\tfrac12\vect{K}_{\mathrm{reg}}(\vect{\Delta}_{\sigma}^{(1)})^{2}-\vect{\Delta}_{\mu}^{(1)}\right)=\vect{0},
\end{equation}
fixing its direction up to scale.
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:49:15.411592+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_72fc64856e0211321a8a3a54c7eb988149c143526c207525e71ccbbc6d57de69","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary anisotropic Lp Sobolev corollary of arXiv:2608.27248, 'Optimal Transport and the ABP Method in Higher Codimension'] Under the assumptions of Theorem (Polya Szego theorem of the paper), every
