{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:47:22.257979+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_73456c86c9609a4806193c709a384e03137730be6a79d1e24c6d78b75b86f1e1","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 120 (Complex slope) of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] For any $u \in \mathbb{C}$, define 
		\begin{flalign}

                  	f_0 (u) = \displaystyle\frac{(\mathfrak{q}^{u-b - c} - 1) (\mathfrak{q}^{u} - 1)}{(\mathfrak{q}^{u+a} - 1) (\mathfrak{q}^{u - b} - 1)}; \qquad U(u) = \mathfrak{q}^{u} \cdot \displaystyle\frac{f_0 (u)}{1 - f_0 (u)}; \qquad V(u) = \displaystyle\frac{\mathfrak{q}^{u}}{1 - f_0 (u)}. 
