{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.625602+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_734edc0b651a912f8c5c0b6e4b3d6707cbde3575d5a535182ac2abb3d9bde8c9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lem: 1226-1 of arXiv:2411.03512, 'Ergodicity and Mixing of Sublinear Expectation System and Applications'] For $\phi\in C_{lip}(\mathbb{R}^d)$ with Lipschitz constant $l_{\phi}$, let $v_n^Z$ be defined by (equation 1225-2 of the paper)-(equation 1225-3 of the paper). Then for $\epsilon>0$, there exists a function $f_n^{(\epsilon)}:\mathbb{R}^d\times \mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}$ such that for $ t>\epsilon+\frac{1}{n},$ $ x\in \mathbb{R}^d$, $f_n^{(\epsilon)}(t,x)\geq -\frac{C_{\zeta}l_{\phi}}{n\epsilon}\big(\hat{\mathbb{E}}[|Z|]+\hat{\mathbb{E}}[|Z|^2]\big)$  and 
		\begin{equation*}
