        \item Each vertex of the remaining graph has a degree larger than $C \sqrt{D^{(n)}/n}$;
        \item Condition on the degree sequence of the remaining graph, its law is given by the configuration model.
    \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:52:47.255297+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_73524c9e474601ef6d9300fddebd6f182d18b485145ff5371304d8c53a6a2a81","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 8 of arXiv:2609.01101, '2609.01101'] There is $A_0\ge1$ such that, uniformly for
