{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.330568+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_73571f1347014965642cf059b537a3dfb9a224089503ce980556559f06f3ddda","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:incrementIt of arXiv:2606.01937, 'Stationary fluctuations for an exclusion process with mass and energy conservation'] For any $\varphi\in\mathscr{S}(\mathbb{R} )$, any $0\le s<t\le T$, the diffusive term defined in (equation eq:It of the paper) satisfies
