{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:06:42.724786+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7357e57b29c3c577cb194874624bb2f4913ef336fc5b38d3f0431d0bcfe3be15","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary theorem: affine_weigh of arXiv:2411.04238, 'Holomorphic jump-diffusions'] Let $X=(X_t)_{t\in[0,T]}$ be an $S$-valued jump-diffusion with characteristics $(b,a,K)$ and extended generator $\mathcal A$. Fix a weight function $v$ in the sense of Definition~(def2 of the paper). Assume that $b_j,a_{ij}\in\mathcal O(S)$, $K$ is a kernel with holomorphic jump size, and let $F$ be the corresponding non-negative measure on the measurable space $E$.  Fix $\varepsilon>0$ and suppose that for each $z\in P^d_{R(S)+\varepsilon}(0)$, there exists $\delta_z>0$ such that
 \begin{align}
         &\int_E  \ \sup_{w\in P^d_{\delta_z}(z)}  \|j_\varepsilon(w, y)\|\land\|j_\varepsilon(w, y)\|^2 \ F(d y)<\infty,\\
  &\int_E  \sup_{w\in P^d_{\delta_z}(z)} 1_{\{\|j_\varepsilon(w, y)\|> 1\}} \exp(m \ v(\|w+j_\varepsilon(w, y)\|))\ F(d y)<\infty,
  \end{align}
  for some $m\in \mathbb R_+$. Let $G\in (0,\infty]^d$ satisfy (equation eqnG of the paper) and set
\begin{align*}
    \mathcal{V}:=H_v(P^d_G(0)) \qquad \text{and}\qquad 
