{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:04:30.606968+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_736b26edc1a8355f4ac842a2ddb97c4ff3093e36a541e957c7c2d996f9857d01","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop p:xrigidity of arXiv:2411.10586, 'A convergence framework for Airy$_\beta$ line ensemble\\ via pole evolution'] For any ${\mathfrak d}, C_*>0$, there exist small $\delta,c>0$ and large $C>0$, such that the following holds.
Take any particle-generated $\{Y_t\}_{t\in{\mathbb R}}$ satisfying (a:SDE of the paper), and large $T>0$. Conditional on the event that $Y_{0}$ is $({\mathfrak d}, C_*)$-Airy-like,
with probability at least $1-e^{-c(\log T)^2}$, we have
\begin{enumerate}
    \item The poles of $\{Y_t\}_{t\in[T, 2T]}$ give a line ensemble $\{x_i(t)\}_{i\in \mathbb{N}, t\in[T,2T]}$, and  for each $t\in[T, 2T]$ and $w\in\mathbb{H}$,
    \begin{align}
        Y_t(w)=\sum_{i=1}^\infty\left(\frac{1}{x_i(t)-w}-\frac{1}{{\mathfrak a}_i}\right)-\frac{\Ai'(0)}{\Ai(0)}.
    \end{align}
    \item For each $t\in [T, 2T]$, $i\in\mathbb{N}$, $y\le C$, we have that  
\begin{equation}
|x_i(t)-{\mathfrak a}_i|\leq \frac{C(\log T)^{40}}{i^{\delta}},
\end{equation} 
and
\begin{equation}
|\{i\in\mathbb{N}:x_i(t)\in [y-1, y+1]\}|\leq C\sqrt{|y|+1}.
\end{equation}

\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

