{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:37.367866+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_73d522e530257fae0f7b98bc942a97a902da22381f6851da1e978ab767b8e1ca","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2606.18433, '\bfseries \Large On a class of Reflected Mean-Field Stochastic Differential Equations with'] For all $ t \in [0,T]$, and $\zeta,\zeta' \in\mathbb{L}^2(\Omega,\mathcal{F}_t,\mathbb{P};\bar{G})$, There exists a constant $C>0$ such that
