{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:06:55.290295+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_73eb6d9c606d0a37ce6b0f0313f95ea05c57bc17a9fa52e86437154c1bcbf0ba","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:pos of arXiv:2602.17579, 'Non-equilibrium functional inequalities for finite Markov chains'] Let $M$ be a generator of an irreducible Markov chain on a finite state space $\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}$ and $\zeta\in \mathcal{P}_+(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}})$. Let $\zeta_*=\min_z\zeta(z)$ and  $M_*=\min \{M(z,z')\,:\,z,z'\in \ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}, \, M(z,z')>0 \}$ be the smallest positive rate in $M$. 
    \begin{enumerate}[label=(\arabic*)]
        \item  We have the lower bound
        \begin{equation} 
            \alpha_{\gPI}(\zeta)
  \geq \frac{ \zeta_* M_* }{|\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}|}.
        \end{equation}
        \item Using $\lambda_{\zeta}$ for the spectral gap of $-M^\zeta$ and $\alpha_{\sLSI}(M^\zeta)$ for the standard LSI constant (defined in Lemma~(lem:symGen of the paper)) we have 
        \begin{equation}
            \alpha_{\gLSI}(\zeta)
            \geq 2\alpha_{\sLSI}(M^\zeta)
            \geq \dfrac{\lambda_{\zeta}}{1 + \dfrac12 \log\dfrac{1}{\zeta_*}}
            = \dfrac{ \alpha_{\gPI}(\zeta) }{1 + \dfrac12 \log\dfrac{1}{\zeta_*}}
  \geq \dfrac{ \zeta_* M_* |\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}|^{-1} }{1 + \dfrac12 \log\dfrac{1}{\zeta_*}}.
        \end{equation}
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:55:18.932944+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_73ec499d1578f54383168720411795acf25d0805a37409aa9f65e63d6014d82c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:B-inverse of arXiv:2602.07920, 'On the position matrix of single-shelf shuffle and card guessing'] The matrix $B$ is invertible. Its inverse $B^{-1}$ is lower triangular with
