\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.610401+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_73eccf6b50095987bcdbe8794ad12a3a940b17b5132f6f09521b0cda5d5d5202","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma-6.14 of arXiv:2412.08964, 'Phase transition and critical behavior in hierarchical\\integer-valued Gaussian and Coulom'] Let~$\beta>\beta_\text{\rm c}$. For each~$A>0$ there exists~$\delta_0>0$ and $\epsilon_0>0$ such that,  for~$\Sigma_0$ defined by~$A$ and any $\delta,\delta'\in(0,\delta_0]$, 
