{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.242921+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_73f3cd37746d7d2676860a618c8e9d654c762faaf893b1310dcb62509ef09bc3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem reversible and tilted MC of arXiv:2604.23751, 'Large deviation principles for pattern-avoiding permutations, and limit shapes for constra'] Let $X$ be a finite state space, $q\ge1$, and $f:X\to\mathbb R_+$.
    Write $\mu^f$ for the $(q,f)$-tilted measure on $X$, that is, $\mu^{q,f}(x) \propto q^{f(x)}$ for all $x\in X$.
    If $p : X^2 \to [0,1]$ is a transition kernel, denote by $\tilde p$ the transition kernel characterized by:
    \begin{align*}
        \forall (x,y)\in X^2,\quad
        \tilde p(x,y) = 
        \left\{
        \begin{array}{ll}
            p(x,y) & \text{if }x\ne y \text{ and }f(y)\ge f(x) \,;\\
            p(x,y)q^{f(y)-f(x)} & \text{if }x\ne y \text{ and }f(y)< f(x) \,;
        \end{array}
        \right.
    \end{align*}
    and $\tilde p(x,x)$ is adjusted so that this defines a transition kernel.
    If $p$ is reversible for the uniform measure on $X$, then $\tilde p$ is reversible for the measure $\mu^{q,f}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:26:52.681149+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_73f464130fb0b03a9a7a7e12f9ca7f4cc1ebc9140bf87cd7d65515cc8abb3f73","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 4 of arXiv:2609.03777, '2609.03777'] The map $\bar\delta$ is a derivation of $\ha^{\geq2}_\ast$.  Under the isomorphism \eqref{eq:H-polynomial}, it is given by
