{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:42:39.100348+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_73f8c4c80b1194381e7c08d010de51c9d1d5aeddcc67f6fa148aef6a400b0644","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2412.08886, 'On domination for (non-symmetric) Dirichlet forms'] Let $({\mathscr E},{\mathscr F})$ and $({\mathscr E}',{\mathscr F}')$ be two Dirichlet forms on $L^2(E,m)$. 
\begin{itemize}
\item[(1)] We say that ${\mathscr E}'$ is \emph{subordinate to} ${\mathscr E}$ if ${\mathscr F}'\subset {\mathscr F}$ and (equation eq:21 of the paper) holds for all non-negative $f,g\in {\mathscr F}'$.  Furthermore, ${\mathscr E}'$ is \emph{strongly subordinate to} ${\mathscr E}$ if, in addition,  ${\mathscr F}'$ is dense in ${\mathscr F}$ with respect to the ${\mathscr E}_1$-norm.
\item[(2)] We say that ${\mathscr E}$ is a \emph{Silverstein extension} of ${\mathscr E}'$ if $\mathrm{b}{\mathscr F}'$ is an algebraic ideal in $\mathrm{b}{\mathscr F}$ and ${\mathscr E}={\mathscr E}'$ on $\mathrm{b}{\mathscr F}'\times \mathrm{b}{\mathscr F}'$.  
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:58.356323+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_73f8d0d2a662969ff31ed0359b11433eeb3d2d6f9c5dd80cb36f028ae3d38248","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2506.18313, 'A stochastic model for the diffusion of competing opinions with trend-following, oppositio'] Assume for all $\varepsilon > 0$ that
\begin{equation}

    \displaystyle\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{1}{v_n} \dE\left[\vert\Delta Z_n\vert^2 \mathbb{I}_{\{\vert\Delta Z_n\vert\geq\varepsilon\sqrt{v_n}\}}\vert\mathcal{F}_{n-1}\right] < \infty \ \  \text{ a.s.},
\end{equation}
and for some $a>0$ that,
\begin{equation}

    \displaystyle\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{1}{v_n^a} \dE\left[\vert\Delta Z_n\vert^{2a} \mathbb{I}_{\{\vert\Delta Z_n\vert\leq\sqrt{v_n}\}}\vert\mathcal{F}_{n-1}\right] < \infty \ \  \text{ a.s. }
\end{equation}
Then, as $n$ diverges, $(Z_n)$ satisfies that
\begin{equation}
\displaystyle\lim_{n\to\infty}\displaystyle\frac{1}{\log v_{n}}\sum_{k=1}^n \left(\frac{v_{k}-v_{k-1}}{v_{k}}\right) \mathbb{I}\left\{\frac{Z_k}{\sqrt{v_{k-1}} } < x \right\} = G (x) \ \  \text{ a.s.,}
\end{equation}
where $\mathbb{I}\{\cdot\}$ denotes  the indicator function of events and $G$ stands for the distribution function of a normal random variable $N(0,\sigma^2)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:07:48.547749+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_73fa7bac0e196989ee19dd74180a0291f2940c3e3c4b77fbbcaf5b916e26e459","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 16 ($\rashlexpctparam$ local stability of  $\emprashomonset$ at $x$) of arXiv:2609.01397, 'Measuring consistency via ensemble margin and local prediction variability: Auditing decis'] Given  a Rashomon set $\emprashomonset$, a test point $x \in \dtest$, a perturbed sample of $x$, $\localtest \in \ltwohsphere(x,\sigma)$, and a small constant $\rashlexpctparam > 0$, $\emprashomonset$ is said to be locally $\rashlexpctparam$ stable if, 
