{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:53:30.663919+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_746cf12127d1302723f0ca48fd01ca9d23e4a7657c92412105f821c6e0decbff","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Dfn def:BregQerrorchap2 of arXiv:2506.01746, '\bf Optimal Bregman quantization: existence and uniqueness of optimal quantizers revisited'] Let $r\!\in (0, +\infty)$.  Let $P$ be a probability distribution supported by $U$ and let $X:(\Omega,{\cal A}, \mathbb{P})\to \mathbb{R}^d$ be a $P$-distributed random vector. Assume
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{E}\big(|F(X)| \vee |X|\big)^{\frac r2}  < + \infty.
\end{equation}
\noindent $(a)$  Let $\Gamma\subset U$ be  a finite subset of $U$ (also called {\em quantizer}). The $(r,\phi_{_F})$-mean quantization error for the Bregman divergences $\phi_{_F}$ of the distribution $P$ induced by $\Gamma$ is defined by 
\begin{equation}
    e_{r,n}(\Gamma, P,\phi_{_F}) =  \left[\int_U \min_{a \in \Gamma}  \phi_{_F}(\xi,a)^{\frac r2} P(\mathrm{d}\xi) \right]^{\frac{1}{r}}= \left[ \mathbb{E} \, \min_{a\in \Gamma}\phi_{_F}(X,a)^{\frac r2}\right]^{\frac 1r}<+\infty.
\end{equation}

\smallskip
\noindent $(b)$ The optimal $(r,\phi_{_F})$-mean quantization error for Bregman divergences at level $n\!\in {\rm I\hspace{-0.50ex}N} $ is defined by
\begin{equation}
    e_{r,n}(P,\phi_{_F}) = \inf_{ |\Gamma|\leq n}  e_{r,n}(\Gamma, P,\phi_{_F}).

\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:06.326089+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_746cfc7168c55437e137e5f8c340c80d8dc95a2956af6dc3a7eba014ad7f6da8","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 10 of arXiv:2607.06242, 'Exponential mixing and Freidlin--Wentzell large deviation principle for Markov cocycles'] For every $k\in\mathbb N$, $\mu,\nu\in \mathcal{P}_{V}$, one has 
    \begin{align*}
      \W_{D_{\Theta^k\sigma}}&\left(\mu Q_\sigma^{(k)}, \nu Q_{\s}^{(k)}\right)\leq h \W_{D_{\s}}(\mu,\nu), \quad m\text{-a.s.}, 
    \end{align*}
    where $h=(1+\varkappa\L)^{1/2}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.274514+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_746d1d08a60abac2f5cdd8cca1d3a97a3d313c58386a08bee6739c454908d379","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma_moments_infty of arXiv:2411.16452, 'Interface scaling limit for the critical planar Ising model perturbed by a magnetic field'] Let $\xi \in \{-,+\}$. Almost surely, for any $k \geq 1$,
