{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.609927+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_747c2e7a2327b7f664eb66a9fccc440a81d90f7a82383930b61edc467b857864","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma-1.5 of arXiv:2412.08964, 'Phase transition and critical behavior in hierarchical\\integer-valued Gaussian and Coulom'] Suppose $\boldsymbol\lambda\in\Sigma'$ and~$A\in(0,1)$ are such that $\sup_{q\ge0}\lambda(q+1)/\lambda(q)\le A$. For all $r\ge1$ and~$q_1,\dots,q_r\ge0$ we then have
