{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:31.958490+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7489007627da32c32e0b2de8cd2bb425c2981dcae15bd8a67d19c8fef092ab08","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lm 14 of arXiv:2512.02286, 'Pfaffian Transition Probability and Correlation Kernel of TASEP in Half-space'] The functions defined by \eqref{eq:Q-kernel},\eqref{eq:p-kernel} and \eqref{eq:R-kernel} satisfy the following recurrence relations
	\begin{align}
        \begin{split}
    		Q_{i+1,j}(s_{i},x_{j})-Q_{i+1,j}(x_{i},x_{j}) & = \sum_{y_i=s_i}^{x_i-1} Q_{i,j}(y_i,x_j), \\
    		Q_{i,j+1}(x_{i},s_{j})-Q_{i,j+1}(x_{i},x_{j}) & = \sum_{y_j= s_j}^{x_j-1} Q_{i,j}(x_i,y_j), \\
    		U_{k+1}(s)-U_{k+1}(z) & = \sum_{y= s}^{z-1} R_{k}(y), \\
    		p_{k+1}(s)-p_{k+1}(z) & = \sum_{y=s}^{z-1} p_k(y).
        \end{split}
	\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:52:23.592105+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_748a5de5511e68fba7ee1b32fdec7f58499d428f8f6f139b76d5d9d99d2c3d6c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm equivalence of arXiv:2602.22342, 'Sum of Gaussian vectors and large sets'] The following are equivalent: as $n\to \infty$,
