{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:12:09.045046+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_74a2b48ab43bd5d47d7bb3055453e1e8b5d231e67db393cf4129d9019be2512f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:smoothcycle of arXiv:2608.25279, 'Provable Non-Acceleration of Standard Strang\\ Splittings of Kinetic Langevin Dynamics'] Assume the hypotheses of Lemma~(lem:interiorcycle of the paper), and let $m\ge3$ satisfy the strict cycling condition (equation eq:strictPK of the paper). Then there exist distinct points $x_0^\circ,\ldots,x_{m-1}^\circ\in\mathbb R^2$ on the unit circle, a potential $U\in\mathcal U_\kappa^2$, and constants $r_0>0$, $b_\ast<\infty$ such that, with indices modulo $m$,
\begin{equation}
 x_{j+1}^\circ=(1+\beta)x_j^\circ-\beta x_{j-1}^\circ-s\nabla U(x_j^\circ),
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
 \nabla U(x_j^\circ+u)=\nabla U(x_j^\circ)+u,
 \qquad \lvert u\rvert\le r_0,
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
 \nabla U(x)=x+w(x),\qquad \sup_{x\in\mathbb R^2}\lvert w(x)\rvert\le b_\ast.
\end{equation}
Consequently, $\nabla^2U=\mathrm{Id}_2$ on each ball $B(x_j^\circ,r_0)$, and the Jacobian of the deterministic heavy-ball update
\begin{equation*}
 (x,y)\longmapsto
 \bigl((1+\beta)x-\beta y-s\nabla U(x),\;x\bigr)
\end{equation*}
at every cycle state $(x_j^\circ,x_{j-1}^\circ)$ is
\begin{equation}
 \mathsf A_1=
 \begin{pmatrix}(1+\beta-s)\mathrm{Id}_2&\;-\beta\mathrm{Id}_2\\
                 \mathrm{Id}_2&\;0\end{pmatrix}.
\end{equation}
Therefore, the Jacobian of the $m$-step update at each cycle state is $\mathsf M=\mathsf A_1^m$, and
\begin{equation*}
 \rho(\mathsf M)
 =\rho(\mathsf A_1)^m
 \le\rho_{\mathrm q}(s,\beta;\kappa)^m
 <1.
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.930323+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_74a5d404009ab99e150c4f658cef53cd49bd9d694409629ceeb7bda7f6f98a4a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2505.21774, 'The friendship paradox for trees'] Let $S_k$ and $\tilde{X}$ be as defined in Theorem \ref{thm:densities-on-infinite-trees}, and let $X$ be a random variable drawn independently from $p$. Subject to \eqref{eq:mono} the following hold:
\begin{itemize}
\item[(a)] 
For each $\tk$ in the support of $\tilde{p}$, the function 
\begin{equation}

k \mapsto \PP\big(\tk + S_X - X(X+1) > 0 \mid X > k\big) \text{ is non-increasing on the support of } p.
\end{equation}
In particular, the function 
\begin{equation}

k \mapsto \PP\big(\tX + S_X - X(X+1) > 0 \mid X > k\big) \text{ is non-increasing on the support of } p.
\end{equation}
\item[(b)] 
For any non-negative discrete random variable $Y$ that is independent of everything else, 
\begin{equation}

\PP(Y > k) \geq \PP\big(Y > k \mid \tX + S_Y - Y(Y+1) > 0\big),  \qquad k \in \N_0.
\end{equation}
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.591455+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_74a5da7e2b9236fe8aaa87f37736aa686c1a8bfc8336433dc0a778df5131be03","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lemma_density_wall_influence_times of arXiv:2412.03370, 'TASEP with a general initial condition and a deterministically moving wall'] Suppose $x^f_{\alpha T}(T) \simeq \xi T$ and $f$ fulfils Assumption~(assumpt:2.1.1 of the paper) with parameters $\alpha_0 < \dots < \alpha_n$. Then, it holds
	\begin{equation} 
	\rho^f_r(\xi) = \sqrt{ \frac{\alpha}{\alpha_0}} \ \text{ and } \  \rho^f_l(\xi) \leq \sqrt{\frac{\alpha}{\alpha_n}}. 
	\end{equation}   
	In the definition of $\rho^f_r(\xi)$, the limit for $\eta \downarrow 0$ exists. If $x^f_{\alpha T}(T)$ is in the interior of the region affected by the wall and Assumption~(assumpt:2.1.1 of the paper) is fulfilled with $\varepsilon \leq \alpha_n$, then this is also the case for $\rho^f_l(\xi)$, and we have $ \rho^f_l(\xi) = \sqrt{\alpha \alpha_{n \vphantom{0}}^{-1}}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:20.863927+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_74a8126a8aef99d2c20ce105cd7f80ddf2be1ae0f8ecb5172110c4ab38fc13f6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 7 of arXiv:2506.10856, 'The space of multifurcating ranked tree shapes: enumeration, lattice structure, and Markov'] The number of $t$ vectors in the string representation of multifurcating ranked tree shapes with $K$ internal nodes and $N$ leaves with $K_{0}(t)=k_{0}$ and $K_{1}(t)=k_{1}$ is the number $A_K(k_{0},k_{1})$ that satisfy the following recursion:
\begin{align} 
    A_K(k_{0}, k_{1}) &= A_{K-1}(k_{0}-1, k_{1}) \times (K-k_{0}-k_{1}) + \\
    &\qquad A_{K-1}(k_{0}-1, k_{1}+1)\times (k_{1}+1) + \nonumber \\
    &\qquad A_{K-1}(k_{0}, k_{1}-1)\times k_{0}.  \nonumber
    \nonumber
\end{align}
with initial values: $A_K(1,K-1)=1$, $A_K(K-1,0)=1$. If $(k_0, k_1) \notin \mathcal{K}_K$, then $A_K(k_0, k_1)=0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:55:27.258200+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_74ac62ed6aa1f58d690911f40ed7568d4bad4b50dc98c10a912608c2c18859a1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:3 of arXiv:2410.23250, 'Strict inequalities for arm exponents in planar percolation'] Let $k\ge 1$ and $t\in[t_k,2t_k]$. For every $x\in B_k$ and every $y\in B_k'$, we have
