{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.240231+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_74ad550b2d1809fe48443c660837bb5999471755bd606722353cfe9e1d53b968","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:diamond of arXiv:2604.22528, 'Malliavin calculus for signatures with applications to finance'] Let $X$ be an $\mathbb{R}^d$-valued continuous semimartingale. Then, for all words ${\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{u_1}}}, {\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{u_2}}} \in V$, letter ${\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{k}}} \in \alphabet[]$, and $\bm{\ell}, \bm{\ell}' \in \TA$,
