for every $n \in \mathbb{N}_+$, where $L_n:=n^{1 - \lambda}$. Furthermore, if $H \in C_c^2(\mathbb{R})$, the role of $\widehat{C}$ is fulfilled by some constant $C(H)$ satisfying \eqref{Cinvshift}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:27:11.202896+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_74ee7b9a099352ffadeba7624b52ac2b02c2d0e2e32bfb993a545b0acace9697","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma null-vector-at-1 of arXiv:2605.19894, 'Sharp Spectral Thresholds for Multi-View Spiked Wigner Models'] When $\mathsf{SNR}\rbr{\lambda,B}>1$, we always have $ \cQ(1)=I_L - \sqrt{\Lambda} \sbr{B \odot M(1)} \sqrt{\Lambda}\succeq 0$ and $\cQ(1) w =0$ for
