{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:04:55.802997+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7504d4c7a5558483f5f7274801f2828eca47d887f2a6fa9602521b8931dd048d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemm l:cond-var-comparison of arXiv:2607.18194, 'Temperature chaos in directed polymers'] Let $X$ be a random variable such that $\mathbb{P}(|X|>m) \leqslant Ce^{-cm^{3/2}}$ for some $C,c>0$ and all $m\geqslant0$.
    Let $Y,Z$ be random $d$-dimensional vectors on the same probability space as $X$, for some $d\geqslant 1$.
    We have
    \begin{align*}
        \Bigl|
            \mathbb{E}[\Var(X|Y)] - \mathbb{E}[\Var(X|Z)]
        \Bigr|
        \leqslant C'\,\mathbb{P}(Y\ne Z)^{0.9}
    \end{align*} 
    for some $C'>0$ depending only on $C,c$.
    (The exponent $0.9$ can be replaced with any $\kappa<1$.) (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:34:45.617168+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_75090fd5a7f9c83d9f72b6a4cff79c0c8eb95da937f8d506c742d4391048bd90","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:face-integral of arXiv:2609.01825, 'On everywhere locally soluble varieties \\ in families over toric bases'] We say that a vector $\vec\ell\in \mathbb{R}^s$ is \emph{of convergent type} for the face $\cal F$ if the integral
\begin{equation}
	\int_{\cal F} \prod_{i=1}^s t_i^{\ell_i} d \mu,
\end{equation}
where $d\mu$ stands for the $d$-dimensional Lebesgue measure on the face $\cal F$,
is finite.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.321106+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_750a798b3be3ae3d6db4cd724ccdac952dabde28c6994381f81a51657c4ce50e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem t:IntroGirsanov2 of arXiv:2411.14936, 'Massive Particle Systems,\\Wasserstein Brownian Motions,\\ and the Dean--Kawasaki Equation'] In the setting of Assumptions~(ass:IntroSetting of the paper) and~(ass:QPPIntro of the paper), suppose further that~$\mssW$ is a diffusion with generator~$\mssL$.
Assume~$0<\phi^2<\infty$ is in the domain of the Dirichlet form of the measure representation~$\mu_\bullet$, i.e.\ of the solution to the free Dean--Kawasaki equation with singular drift~(equation eq:IntroSPDE of the paper).
Then, the Dean--Kawasaki-type equation
\begin{equation}
\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mu_t= \mathsf{div}(\sqrt{\mu_t}\, \xi)+\sum_{x\in \mu_t} \mssL'\delta_x \mathop{}\!\mathrm{d} t + \mathsf{div}\paren{\mu_t\, \mssd\frac{\delta \phi}{\delta\mu_t}(\mu_t)} \mathop{}\!\mathrm{d} t
\end{equation}
admits a unique (analytically weak) solution~$\mu_\bullet^\phi$, which is the Girsanov transform of~$\mu_\bullet$ by weight~$\phi$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.356194+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_750b6d3c5aa9c4c1367a33d7be3800509cc38552e152e25e8034acd575ce426c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:time_regularity of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] Fix $R,M,\mu>0$, and let $p,q\in (2,\infty)$ be such that (equation eq:condition_pq_subcritical_scaling_cutoff of the paper) holds.
For all $b\in (2,\infty)$ and $T\in (0,\infty)$, let $w_{{\rm cut}}^N$ be the unique global $(p,q)$-solution to (equation eq:navier_stokes_cutoff of the paper) provided by Lemma (l:global_cutoff of the paper) for some $u_0\in \mathcal{B}_{p,q}(M)$. 
Set 
\begin{equation}

\mathcal{M}^N(t)\stackrel{{\rm def}}{=}\sum_{k,\alpha} \theta_k^N \int_0^t (\sigma_{k,\alpha}\cdot \nabla) w_{{\rm cut}}^N\,\mathrm{d} W^{k,\alpha}_s.
\end{equation}
Then there exist constants $K_T,\kappa,\gamma_0,\gamma_1>0$ independent of $u_0\in \mathcal{B}_{p,q}(M)$ and $N\geq 1$ such that 
\begin{align}

{\mathbf E} [\|\mathcal{M}^N \|_{C^{\gamma_0}(0,T;H^{-\gamma_1})}^{b}]
&\leq K_T N^{-\kappa b} (1+\|u_0\|_{B^{1-2/p}_{q,p}}^{b}),\\

{\mathbf E} [\|w_{{\rm cut}}^N \|_{C^{\gamma_0}(0,T;H^{-\gamma_1})}^{b}]
&\leq K_T (1+\|u_0\|_{B^{1-2/p}_{q,p}}^{b}),
\end{align}
where $\gamma_0,\gamma_1$ are additionally independent of $T>0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

