{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:39:18.538164+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_75253f9a942680fab377165fdf9985cbc4f3efce8e051ca4b81c3292882c31a1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 6 of arXiv:2609.02327, 'On the counting function of square-full numbers'] {\cite{RS}}
			For $\frac{1}{2}\leqslant \sigma \leqslant 2$, $T$- sufficiently large, there exists a $T^{\ast}\in [T,T+T^{\frac{1}{3}}]$ such that  the bound
			\begin{equation}
				\log (\zeta(\sigma\pm it))\ll(\log \log (T^{\ast}))^2 \ll (\log \log (T))^2
			\end{equation}
			holds uniformly for $\frac{1}{2}\leqslant \sigma \leqslant 2$ and thus we have
			\begin{equation}
				|\zeta(\sigma\pm i T^{\ast})|^{\pm1}\,\,\ll\exp \left (c (\log \log T)^2 \right)
			\end{equation}
			on the horizondal line  $t=T^{\ast}$ uniformly for $\frac{1}{2}\leqslant \sigma \leqslant 2$. This implies
			\begin{equation}
				\frac{1}{|\zeta(\sigma\pm i T^{\ast})|}\ll \exp \left (c (\log \log T)^2 \right)
			\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:30:36.806944+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_752836494a451ae11e4a1aae93010d16342fdef4611c9c9fdb9fffb5994f473e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 72 of arXiv:2607.10486, 'Weak martingale solutions to stochastic Navier-Stokes-Cahn-Hilliard system with transport '] Assume that  $\rU$ is a topological vector space and $\rU^\prime$ its topological dual.
