{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:41:29.055668+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7542f07b78d78bd3142660aaa177536b1c30a69ef73cf1113d77c2037236a892","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 25 of arXiv:2608.26619, 'Uniqueness of Positively Curved Ancient Ricci Flows on Surfaces with Boundary'] If $v:\old\times(-\infty,0)\rightarrow\bR$ satisfies \eqref{eq_symmetry_v}, then the function
\[
\phi:\old\longrightarrow\old,\qquad \phi(x,t)=\frac{v(x,t)-v_R(x,t)}{x_1}
\]
is even in the $x_1$ coordinate and satisfies
\begin{equation}
\begin{cases}
\phi_t=A\Delta\phi+B\cdot\nabla\phi+C\phi\quad&\text{in }\old\times(-\infty,0),
\\
\partial_r\phi=0\quad&\text{on }\partial \bD\times(-\infty,0),
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
where
\begin{align*}
A&=(1+v)^{-2},
\\
B&=2(1+v)^{-2}\frac{\nabla x_1}{x_1}-(1+v)^{-3}\nabla(v+v_R),
\\
C&=\frac{\alpha(v)-\alpha(v_R)}{v-v_R}\Delta v_R+\frac{\beta(v)-\beta(v_R)}{v-v_R}|\nabla v_R|^2-(1+v)^{-3}\nabla(v+v_R)\cdot\frac{\nabla x_1}{x_1}.
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:32:11.127030+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_754620931fdfb7456e9e5c96d2893ade74cf87c9ec2e0b2a35fe6c7adf69432f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:sq_of_PSD_matrices of arXiv:2510.06891, 'Multivariate CLT for L\'evy processes: convergence rates without moment assumptions'] Let $\bm{N}_1,\bm{N}_2$ be symmetric positive semi-definite matrices. Define $\bm{N}_3\coloneqq\bm{N}_1+\bm{N}_2$ and, for $i\in\{1,3\}$, let $\bm{M}_i$ be symmetric positive semi-definite matrices satisfying $\bm{M}_i^2=\bm{N}_i$. Then $\bm{M}_3-\bm{M}_1$ is positive semi-definite and
\[
\sqrt{\mathrm{tr}\big((\bm{M}_3-\bm{M}_1)^2\big)}
\leqslant\mathrm{tr}(\bm{M}_3-\bm{M}_1).
\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.397259+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7549a47729cf12d82fb35f4489b59b2c9aa15f8ee354ef9fe0ac331a93706b7f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 2. thm: convergence in the vague topology of arXiv:2412.08236, 'Aging and sub-aging for Bouchaud trap models on resistance metric spaces'] [{[Noda_pre_Metrization]}] 
  The function $d_{V}^{S, \rho_{S}}$ is a complete, separable metric on $\mathcal{M}(S)$.
  Let $\mu, \mu_{1}, \mu_{2}, \ldots$ be 
  Radon measures on $S$.
  Then these conditions are equivalent:
  \begin{enumerate}
    \item $\mu_{n}$ converges to $\mu$ with respect to $d_{V}^{S, \rho_{S}}$;
    \item $\mu_{n}^{(r)}$ converges weakly to $\mu^{(r)}$ for all but countably many $r>0$;
    \item $\mu_{n}$ converges vaguely to $\mu$, that is, for all continuous functions $f : S \to \mathbb{R}$ with compact support,
      it holds that 
      \begin{equation}
        \lim_{n \to \infty} \int_{S} f(x)\, \mu_{n}(dx) = \int_{S} f(x)\, \mu(dx).
      \end{equation}
  \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.230772+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_754b1c14f9e3623c1c6d7111f2467b5b1a200618dcd1f7e2234e7a6ac42baaa4","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 21 of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] For $p>0$, let $\mathbb{T}^{(p)}$ denote the $1$-dimensional torus of length $p$, and recall that
 \begin{equation*}
     (\mathbb{T}^{(p)} \times \R)^{2}_{\uparrow} = \left\{ (x,s;y,t) \in \big(\mathbb{T}^{(p)} \times \R\big)^2 \colon s<t \right\} . 
 \end{equation*}
Then we define the $\boldsymbol{p}$\textbf{-periodic directed landscape} as
\begin{equation*}
   \Lpp(x,s;y,t) := p^{-1/2}\Lp_1(px,p^{3/2}s;py,tp^{3/2})
\end{equation*} for all $(x,s;y,t) \in (\mathbb{T}^{(p)} \times \R)^{2}_{\uparrow}$, where $\Lp_1$ is a $1$-periodic directed landscape on  $(\mathbb{T} \times \R)^2_{\uparrow}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:38:13.630695+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_754bb3cca93142ff37d3fc30d2fbdb74d125b809d3254aad8cc83f176feab3e8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 11 of arXiv:2609.00598, 'Supercritical mean--field limit for magnetized Hamiltonian dynamics'] Let $f_{\varepsilon}\in W^{1,\infty}([0,T]\times \mathbb{T}^{2}\times \mathbb{R}^{2})$ be a non-negative solution, with finite second velocity moment and sufficient decay as \(\lvert\xi\rvert\to\infty\), to  \eqref{magnetized vp with quasineutral scaling}, 
and let the total energy be defined by 
\begin{align*}
\mathcal{F}_{\varepsilon}(t):= \frac{1}{2}\int_{\mathbb{T}^{2}\times \mathbb{R}^{2}}\left\vert \xi\right\vert^{2}f_{\varepsilon}(t,x,\xi)\ \dd x\dd \xi
+\frac{\varepsilon}{2}\int_{\mathbb{T}^{2}}\left\vert \nabla_{x} 
\Phi_{\varepsilon}\right\vert^{2}(t,x)\ \dd x.    
\end{align*}
Then
\begin{align*}
\frac{\dd}{\dd t}\mathcal{\mathcal{F}}_{\varepsilon}(t)=0 
\qquad \mbox{for all}\ t\in [0,T],   
\end{align*}
that is,
\begin{align*}
\mathcal{F}_{\varepsilon}(t)=\mathcal{F}_{\varepsilon}(0)
\qquad \mbox{for all}\ t\in [0,T].     
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:42:39.097658+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_754cd902de0bd734093a100b8e7e9fa79160397b8ad168a53753d029424a82aa","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi Lyapunov function of arXiv:2412.08497, 'Time discretization of Quadratic Forward-Backward SDEs with singular drift'] Let $g:[0,T]\times \mathbb{R}^d\times \mathbb{R}\times\mathbb{R}^d\rightarrow\mathbb{R}$ be a Borel function and $\bold{c}>0$ be a constant. A pair $(h,k)$ of non negative functions with $h\in W^{1,2}_{loc}(\mathbb{R})$ and $k$ a Borel function is said to be a $\bold{c}\text{-Lyapunov}$ pair for $g$ if $h(0)=0,$ $h'(0)=0$ and 
					\begin{align}
						\frac{1}{2}h''(y)|z|^2-h'(y)g(t,x,y,z) \geq |z|^2 -k,
					\end{align} 
					for all $(t,x,y,z)\in [0,T]\times \mathbb{R}^d\times \mathbb{R}\times\mathbb{R}^d\rightarrow\mathbb{R},$ with $|y|\leq \bold{c}.$ We will denote $(h,k)\in \text{\bf Ly}(g,\bold{c})$.","status":"unverified"}

