{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.725329+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_75591712fc5f2b032ec40d442509cb99a3459163afe2cadc0d18e3a239180e23","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2411.17653, 'Exclusion processes with non-reversible boundary: hydrodynamics and large deviations'] Fix $T>0$ and $\gamma\in\mathscr{M}_{ac}$. Let $\rho\in  {\mathcal{D}}([0,T], \mathscr{M}_{ac})$ be such that $I_{[0,T]}(\rho|\gamma)<\infty.$ Then, $\rho(0,x)=\gamma(x).$ Moreover, for each $M>0$, $G\in C^2([0,1])$ and $\varepsilon>0$, there exists a $\delta>0$ such that 
    \begin{equation*}
        \sup_{\rho:I_T(\rho|\gamma)\leq M}\sup_{|t-s|\leq\delta}|\langle \rho_t, G\rangle-\langle \rho_s, G\rangle|\leq \varepsilon.
    \end{equation*}
    In particular, $\rho$ belongs to $C([0,T],\mathscr{M}_{ac})$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:44.552331+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_755e9694e4c7cb3ac17210f4301d3a4be75885796acec5fbb65d997cf5bd48a2","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 27 of arXiv:2604.01978, 'Homogenized Transformers'] For all $k\in \naturals$, we denote $\mathfrak{X}^{k}((\S^{d-1})^n)$ the set of vector fields admitting a derivative of order $k$, endowed with the norm 
    \begin{equation*}
        \|V\|_{\mathfrak{X}^{k}((\S^{d-1})^n)}\coloneqq \max_{X\in (\S^{d-1})^n}\left(\|V(X)\|+\max_{j\in[k]}\|\nabla^{j}V(X)\|\right)
    \end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

