{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.779661+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_758a9043625d4e56d483aa53f685012ddfb6ad9dabfb214fce411bda8277d3e3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma L2lemma of arXiv:2411.18359, 'Large systems of symmetrized trapped Brownian Bridges and Schr\"odinger processes'] If $\langle W,p \rangle<\infty$, then
    \begin{equation}
        \Tilde{J}_W^{{\scriptscriptstyle{({q}})}}(p)\geq \sup_{f\in{\mathcal C }_{\rm b}(\mathbb{R}^d)}\Bigl\{\beta\langle f,p\rangle -\int_{\mathbb{R}^d}\int_{\mathbb{R}^d} q({\rm d} x,{\rm d} y)\,\log\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x}\Bigl[{\rm e}^{\int_0^{\beta}(f-W)(B_s)\,{\rm d} s};B_\beta \in {\rm d} y\Bigr]}{{\rm d} y}\Bigr\}.
