			\end{equation*}
		\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:32:18.868175+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_75f06fbde08ebf67a21715410993d36650246a62199636e063a39524cce5c388","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 75 of arXiv:2609.03875, 'Measure theory without infinities'] Let $\mu_1$ and $\mu_2$ be positive premeasures such that $\q{\mu_1} = \q{\mu_2}$, $\eta_1 = \as[\mf R]{\mu_1}$, and $\eta_2 = \as[\mf R]{\mu_2}$.
