{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:47:12.026938+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_762df78754b30d2dfd140ac78d1309866e2f287e06c4f0663fd57c34dd81cd41","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:cyl-ball of arXiv:2512.06984, 'Infinite Dimensional Multifractal Analysis of the Wiener measure'] Let $ \bar{\omega} \in \Omega$. For every $ \varepsilon > 0 $ and every $n$ such that $ \Delta_n ( \bar{\omega} ) < \varepsilon $, we have
