{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:05:28.287809+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_762f2b6056002b2a46cd3efae3fa93278a95b6a2935645aa4cf1a6ff63a6887c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop PropIntegerMoments of arXiv:2602.08739, '\large \bf MOMENTS OF C$\beta$E FIELD PARTITION FUNCTION, $\mathsf{Sine}_{\beta}$ CORRELAT'] Let $\beta,\delta,s>0$ and $m \in \mathbb{N}$ be such that $2s(2\delta-(m+1)s)>\beta$ and $4m(\delta-m s)s>\beta$. Then, we have, as $N \to \infty$,
