{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:26.943727+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7649eb11788c335c1a564ceae5352d3166d3e19effae82055cac00db2634e9a2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary c:cutoff_geod of arXiv:2505.09604, 'Exceptional force, uncountably many solutions in the KPZ fixed point'] The following holds on the event $\Omega_1$. Let $\xi \in \Xi$, and $b \in \mathcal{F}^\xi$. If for some $t \in \mathbb{R}, \tau_t^{b,L} \in \mathbb{R}$, then
