{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.645165+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7660a52960183c6892384edb73bbd8254fbe1076932d8b955e94745eb68ca12a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm main2 of arXiv:2411.13926, 'Random walks on random walks:\\ non-perturbative results in high dimensions'] Consider the RWRW model  on $\mathbb{Z}^d$ with $\lambda \in [0,\infty)$. 
\begin{itemize}
\item[a)] (weak) annealed Functional Central Limit Theorem (waFCLT):\\
If $d\geq 5$ and there is an $\alpha \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d$ such that the variance of $\alpha \cdot X_n$ diverges, then there is a slowly varying function  $h\colon [0,\infty) \rightarrow \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}$ such that
\begin{equation}
\left( \frac{\alpha \cdot X_{\lfloor nt\rfloor}- \alpha \cdot v\lfloor nt\rfloor}{\sqrt{nh(n)}} \right)_{t \in [0,1]} \overset{P_{\ensuremath{\mathbb{P}}}}{\implies} (B_t)_{t \in [0,1]}
\end{equation}
where $\overset{P_{\ensuremath{\mathbb{P}}}}{\implies}$ denotes convergence in distribution under the annealed law $P_{\ensuremath{\mathbb{P}}}$ as $n\rightarrow \infty$ with respect to the Skorohod topology and  $(B_t)$  is a standard Brownian motion on $\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}$.\\  
If, moreover, $d\geq 9$, then there is a $\sigma \in (0,\infty)$ such that $h(n)=\sigma$. 
\item[b)] annealed Functional Central Limit Theorem (aFCLT):\\
If $d\geq 9$ and $(X_t)$ is truly d-dimensional, then 
\begin{equation}
\left( \frac{ X_{\lfloor nt\rfloor}- v\lfloor nt\rfloor}{\sqrt{n}} \right)_{t \in [0,1]} \overset{P_{\ensuremath{\mathbb{P}}}}{\implies} (B_t^{\Sigma})_{t \in [0,1]}
\end{equation}
where $(B_t^{\Sigma})$ is a Brownian motion on $\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d$ with covariance matrix $\Sigma>0$.
\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:36:12.190276+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7666901258790871698abca42247967c3ff13cb2e5dde424cb5e234cfc6ccbc5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 (Scaled barrier convergence) of arXiv:2609.03916, 'Halfspace Theorems for Anisotropic Minimal Surfaces and Perimeter Minimizers'] The scaled barriers satisfy
