{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:36:31.230495+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_76ca3466175c0d7bd7d0721920ed2419eef95b2ecb77b087fa69933794335648","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2609.00537, 'Explicit Exponential Sum Estimates and Approximate Functional Equations for the Zeta Funct'] Let $N$ be a positive integer and $0<y<N+1$, and $\Delta=N+1-y$. Then
