{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.421814+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_76f0a860559b31bf3219bd503bab2118b250edbdb439738a039cb99e634dd1a1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:three_term_relation of arXiv:2507.22011, 'Random Lozenge Waterfall:\\Dimensional Collapse of Gibbs Measures'] We have
	\begin{equation}

		\mathfrak{a}(x)\hspace{1pt}
		\mathcal{F}_n(x-\tfrac12)
		+
