{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:23:27.792323+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_76f917696da7fd95c6c6af8dbf1486ad115766032c45cd6eb72890c5bf40fcad","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:measurability-pattern of arXiv:2606.10973, 'Quasisymmetric rigidity of the Brownian sphere'] We may choose $b_1$ sufficiently small so that there exists a sufficiently small parameter $b_2 \in (0, b_1)$ for which, with probability strictly greater than $1/2$,
