{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.775396+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_76fd666a04d3bec9f02b6eed90df51f168f734c39b6627a91e09d73314c00a42","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 16 of arXiv:2603.25400, 'One-arm probabilities for the two-dimensional metric-graph and discrete Gaussian free fiel'] For any $h\in\mathbb R$, let $\hat h=\frac h4(1+3\mathbbm1_{h\le\sqrt{\log N}})$. Define the event
    \begin{equation}
        \mathcal H_N^h:=\{\exists t\in[\sigma_1,\sigma) \mbox{ such that }\overline M_t<(\hat h-3c_1)\,\overline H_N(U,\mathcal I_t)\},
    \end{equation}
    where $c_1$ is from Lemma \ref{lem:pin}. Then, there is some $c>0$ such that for all $x>0$,
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb P^x[\mathcal H_N^h]\lesssim\begin{cases} N^{-1},&h\le\sqrt{\log N};\\e^{-ch^2},&h>\sqrt{\log N} .\end{cases}
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:19:46.229014+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_76ffb4e91be5f07f6f14f04ce349a21353fe6ef9c8f7e53406295d06e36eacdc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 18 of arXiv:2507.08909, 'Annealed almost periodic entropy'] In the setting of Definition~\ref{dfn:cond-log-det-ent}, if $E,F,G$ are pairwise disjoint finite subsets of $S$, then
\begin{align}
\rmH_Q(E\cup F\mid G) &= \rmH_Q(E\mid G) + \rmH_Q(F\mid E\cup G) \\
&\le \rmH_Q(E\mid G) + \rmH_Q(F\mid G) 
\end{align}
(including the possibility that any of these expressions could be $-\infty$), and
\begin{equation}
\rmH_Q(E\mid G) - \rmI_Q(E\,;\,F\mid G) = \rmH_Q(E\mid F\cup G)
\end{equation}
(including the possibility of $-\infty$ on either side).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.120257+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_770082ba36a8b3a8dbb4eaafcfda225ef6cc4389e2b81726e2cda3cda9733734","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma propI of arXiv:2608.17031, 'A shape theorem for periodic branching diffusion'] The following holds:
\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
    \item The function $I_e(\lambda)$ is finite for every $\lambda\in \mathbb{R}$, and $I_e$ is strictly convex and differentiable. Moreover, for every $\lambda\in \mathbb{R}$, there exists $\lambda^*\in \mathbb{R}$ such that
    \begin{equation*}
        I_e(\lambda)=\sup_{\eta \in \mathbb{R}} \{ \eta \lambda - [\gamma((\lambda_e+\eta)e)-\gamma(\zeta_e)]\}= \lambda \lambda^* - [\gamma((\lambda_e+\lambda^*)e)-\gamma(\zeta_e)]. 
    \end{equation*}
    \item For any $\lambda\in \mathbb{R}$, $I_e(\lambda)\geq 0$ and $I_e(\lambda)=0$ if and only if $\lambda=c^*(e)$, where $c^{*}(e)$ is defined in (equation eq:prelimCriticalSpeed of the paper). Furthermore, $I_e$ is strictly decreasing on the interval $(-\infty,c^*(e))$ and strictly increasing on the interval $(c^*(e),+\infty)$.
    \item For any constant $\beta>0$, there exists $\delta=\delta(\beta)\in (0,1)$ such that for any $\kappa\in (0,\delta)$, 
    \begin{equation*}
        I_e(c^*(e) - \kappa ) < \kappa \beta\quad\text{and}\quad I_e(c^*(e) + \kappa ) < \kappa \beta. 
    \end{equation*}
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:00:22.781940+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7702746d7fe1b3647598316960d299d6cda5a2975bd9e21f669f1df288cd88c7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor Finite Dimensional Distributions of arXiv:2411.01633, 'On the Limit of the Tridiagonal Model \\for $\beta$-Dyson Brownian Motion'] For any fixed $j \in \mathbb{N}$ and times $t_1,\dots ,t_j \in [0,T]$, we have
