{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:47:40.716818+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7719beb845e7c88b05e70062a61ed7f702c659a4e124e9cc00bd40aabf1f01b3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:exMetr of arXiv:2604.16206, 'Extrapolation of max--stable random fields with Fr\'echet marginals'] Let  the random vector $\mathbf{X}$ be as in Theorem (Em:MC:l of the paper).
    For every vector $\mathbf{w}=(w_1,\ldots,w_n)\in \mathbb{R}_+^n$ and $\gamma_k\in[0,w_k]$,  $k=1,\ldots,n$,   
    it holds
    \begin{equation}
 \mathcal{E}_{H_\alpha} (M(\mathbf{w},\mathbf{X}), \gamma_k X_k)= \frac{1}{\gamma_k^\alpha +1}-\frac{1}{l_\mathbf{X}(\mathbf{w}^\alpha)+1}.
\end{equation}
 Let the extended random vector $\mathbf{X}_e=(X_0,\mathbf{X})$ be max--stable   with $H_\alpha$--distributed marginals and tail dependence function $l_{\mathbf{X}_e}$. For $\gamma_0\geq 0$, we have
    \begin{align}
    \mathcal{E}_{H_\alpha} (M(\mathbf{w},\mathbf{X}), \gamma_0 X_0)= \frac{1}{\gamma_0^\alpha+1} +\frac{1}{l_\mathbf{X}(\mathbf{w}^\alpha)+1}- \frac{2}{l_{\mathbf{X}_e}((\gamma_0^\alpha,\mathbf{w}^\alpha))+1}.
    \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:48:27.276968+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_771bb2e5d09e8f1f1d0354e044f6f705733b1499d1a476ad3d5d1ba32db05eed","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 3 of arXiv:2604.24664, 'Absolute continuity of Rosenblatt measures'] Let $\alpha \in (0, 1)$ and $f: [0, T] \to \Rbb$. The \emph{left} and \emph{right Riemann--Liouville fractional derivatives of $f$ of order $\alpha$} are defined by
	\begin{align*}
		(I^{-\alpha}_{0+} f)(x) &= \frac{1}{\Gamma(1-\alpha)} \frac{\d{}}{\d{x}} \int_0^x (x-y)^{-\alpha} f(y) \d{y},
		\\
		(I^{-\alpha}_{T-} f)(x') &= \frac{1}{\Gamma(1-\alpha)} \frac{\d{}}{\d{x'}} \int_{x'}^{T} (y-x')^{-\alpha} f(y) \d{y},
	\end{align*}
	for almost all $x,x' \in [0, T]$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:51:52.060390+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_771fe0d23b0ecd5c11811aebfdfe5223c450397e11ee9b69fddcc9604e57650f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thKM of arXiv:2607.14792, 'On the degree distribution of large tentacular Bienaymé--Galton--Watson trees'] Let $\eta$ be an offspring distribution such that $\eta(0) >0$ and $\eta(1) >0$ and denote by $F$ its generating function. Let $(S_n)_{n\geq0}$ be a random walk started from $S_0=0$ with step distribution $\eta$. Assume $k_n=o(n)$ and $k_n\rightarrow \infty$. Then
    \begin{equation}
    \sup_{k\geq -k_n} \left| \sqrt{k_n} \frac{b_n^{k_n+k}}{F(b_n)^{n-k_n}}\mathbb{P}\left(S_{n-k_n} = k_n+k\right) - \frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}e^{-\frac{k^2}{2k_n}}\right| \xrightarrow[n \rightarrow \infty]{} 0,
\end{equation}
where $b_n$ is defined by
 \[b_n\frac{F'(b_n)}{F(b_n)}=\frac{k_n}{n-k_n}.\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:47:22.244633+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7724e094f1dc46d773a722e3136b19166c7d89e7ab524e9fe4ecf8dda55f5b52","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 1 of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] For any $\delta>0$, there exist constants $\kappa > 0$ and $C = C(\delta)>0$ such that the mixing time of the single-flip Glauber dynamic on tilings of the hexagon $\mX$ satisfies
