{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:44.957912+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_77580b9f1874069462c5d1973fc9cb583266b3c0ac09cd6fb6b854cce95aa23a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 (Banach-valued decoupling for Wick squares) of arXiv:2606.26065, 'Localized Centered Second-Chaos Operators'] Let $B$ be a separable Banach space.  Let $(x_{ij})_{1\le i,j\le m}\subset B$, let $(G_i)_{i=1}^m$ be a standard real Gaussian family, and let $(g_i)_{i=1}^m$ and $(h_j)_{j=1}^m$ be two independent standard Gaussian copies.  Then, for every $1\le p<\infty$,
\begin{equation}
 \left\|\sum_{i,j=1}^m x_{ij}\bigl(G_iG_j-\E[G_iG_j]\bigr)\right\|_{L^p(\Omega;B)}
 \le C_{\rm dec}
 \left\|\sum_{i,j=1}^m x_{ij}g_ih_j\right\|_{L^p(\Omega;B)},
\end{equation}
where $C_{\rm dec}$ depends only on the order-two decoupling theorem, and not on $m$, on the Banach space $B$, or on $p$.  In particular, after symmetrizing the same-family kernel, a completely Wick-centered square may be estimated through its decoupled version.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:11:09.320212+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7758f588e93e289f336f9f719d69ea2cbc160d33ebd1057baacd5679f80b8b6f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma le:estimate-log-IG of arXiv:2411.06195, 'Restrictions of some reinforced processes to subgraphs'] \mbox{}\\
  For $W>0$ and $X_W\sim \operatorname{IG}(W^{-1},1)$, one has 
  \begin{align}

    E[\log X_W]=&-\log W-\int_0^\infty\frac{e^{-u}}{u+2W}\, du
                  =e^{2W}\int_0^{2W}(\log t+\gamma)e^{-t}\, dt+{c_2}
  \end{align}
  with ${c_2}$ and $\gamma$ specified in Theorem (thm:from-r-to-l of the paper).
  Furthermore, the following bounds hold
  \begin{align}

    -\log(W+\tfrac12)\le E[\log X_W]&\le\min\{-\log W,{c_2}\}\quad\text{for }W>0,\\

    {c_2}+4W(\log W+{c_2}-1) \le E[\log X_W]&\le{c_2}\quad\text{for }0<W\le\tfrac12 e^{-\gamma},\\

    \lim_{W\to 0}E[\log X_W]&={c_2}.
  \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:12:08.990227+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_775a2ef8b144787e7483c37afe42f0c2e98b96af8234dff073605c3e28e11a4b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lem_riemannPersistenceUpperBound of arXiv:2608.17463, 'Persistence probabilities of fractional L\'evy fields indexed by hyperbolic space and othe'] The persistence probability of the fractional L\'evy field $(X_H(\eta))_{\eta\in K}$ on the relatively compact set $K$ of a connected Riemannian manifold $\mathcal{M}$, where $O$ is in the interior of $K$, satisfies
    \begin{align*}
        \prob{\sup_{\eta\in K} X_H(\eta) < \varepsilon} \leq \varepsilon^{\frac{d}{H} + \mathdutchcal{o}(1)}, && \text{ for } \varepsilon \searrow 0.
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:15.483297+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_775b2552730b88a2de09ab01821692207667041c83e099517de4f557aa5ba898","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 41 of arXiv:2509.01797, 'Relation between Wick powers and excursion clusters of the 2D GFF'] Let be $\eta>0$, $\varepsilon\in (0,1)$ and $b\geq (2v)\vee(2\lambda)$.
Let $j\geq 1$.
Then
\begin{equation}

\E\Big[\Big\Vert\ind_{U_{0,b,\varepsilon}} 
V_{A_{0,b}}^{j}
\Big\Vert_{H^{-\eta}(\C)}^{2}\Big]^{1/2}
\leq \dfrac{j C_{j}}{2^{j-1}\pi^{j+1/2}}\big\Vert\ind_{D}\big\Vert_{H^{-\eta}(\C)}\,
\Big(
\dfrac{32 b^{2}}{\pi}
\Big)^{j}
\Big(
1\vee
\Big(
\dfrac{\pi}{32 b^{2}} \vert\log\varepsilon \vert
\Big)
\Big)^{j-1}
\varepsilon^{\pi/(32 b^{2})},
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}

C_{j} = 
\int_{0}^{+\infty}
\Big(
1 + y\Big)^{j-1}
e^{-y}\,dy.
\end{equation}
Similarly,
given a deterministic smooth cutoff function $f_{0}:D\rightarrow [0,1]$, compactly supported in $D$,
and $\varepsilon\in (0,1)$, with
\begin{displaymath}
\varepsilon\,\leq \inf_{z\in\operatorname{Supp}(f_{0})}\CR(z,D),
\end{displaymath}
we have
\begin{multline}

\E\Big[\Big\Vert f_{0}\ind_{\widetilde{U}_{0,b,\varepsilon}} 
