{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:35:19.875268+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_778baabbf47cae38a54d75bc9540648e43b745a2511568ec1ce9ec29a74aeacb","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn hext of arXiv:2608.27939, 'Entropy and domination for quasi-Hitchin representations'] Let $\mathcal{P}(g_1,g_2)$ be the (possibly infinite) collection of plaques separating $g_1$ from $g_2$, with the linear order induced by the transverse orientation. A map $$M:\mathcal{P}(g_1,g_2) \to \mathrm{SL}_n(\mathbb{C})$$
