{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.416760+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_779c8f9169e3dacb73272d92069a7f9c57019f7c5883d77b7f884df619bf9a81","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:inverse_kasteleyn_matrix of arXiv:2507.22011, 'Random Lozenge Waterfall:\\Dimensional Collapse of Gibbs Measures'] {borodin-gr2009q}}]

	The inverse Kasteleyn matrix is expressed through the two-dimensional correlation kernel
	$\widetilde{K}$ (equation eq:K_kernel_two_dimensional of the paper)
	as follows:
	\begin{equation}

		\mathrm{Kast}^{-1}\left( s,x;t,y \right)
		=
		\frac{G(s,x)}{G(t,y)}
		\frac{\mathbf{1}_{s=t}\mathbf{1}_{x=y}- \widetilde{K}(s,x;t,y)}{\mathsf{w}_{q,\kappa}(x-\tfrac s2+1)},
	\end{equation}
	where
	$(s,x)$ and $(t,y)$ are the coordinates of a black (resp., white) triangle.
	The factor $G$ is
	\begin{equation}

		G(t,x)\coloneqq
		\frac{1}{\sqrt{\widetilde{w}_t(x)}}
		\frac{(-1)^{x} \kappa^{-t}
		q^{x(T+N-t-1)+t(S/2-1/2)+t(t+1)/4} \left(1-\kappa^2 q^{2x-t-S+1}\right)}
		{(\frac{1}{q}; \frac{1}{q})_{S+N-1-x} (q;q)_{T-S+x-t} (\kappa^2 q^{x-T+1}; q)_{T+N-t}}.
	\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:47:12.032921+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_77a184c2e62d33efa5f14ca1f2530cb264905aea4c1c6e18ee0172e3fcc9bf8f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop-Burkholder inequality of arXiv:2512.17727, 'Stochastic transport equation with L\'evy noise'] For every $p \ge 2$,
