 \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:51:11.978050+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_77a3c568eb3d0203e3c70c028602b8a876e78c10f853e65b260a473615bf7e77","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 56 (Finite Brownian blocks) of arXiv:2608.08756, 'Infinite-Dimensional L\'evy Area and Spectral Ancestry'] Let
\[
 \mathcal L^{(d)}
 :=\operatorname{Alt}_2\int_0^1B_t\otimes\mathop{}\!\mathrm dB_t
\]
for standard Brownian motion in \(\mathbb R^d\), with the same
half-commutator normalization as in
\eqref{cc:eq-critical-martingale-area}.  There are numerical constants
\(a,\eta,c_0>0\) such that
\begin{align}
 \mathbb P\left\{s_{\lfloor\eta d\rfloor}
       (\mathcal L^{(d)})\geq a\right\}&\longrightarrow1,
 \\
 \mathbb P\left\{s_k(\mathcal L^{(d)})
       \geq c_0\frac d k,\ 1\leq k\leq m\right\}
