{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.628585+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_77bbf10e02cc5dcdaa14a3a94af5dbd9f66934a57eb696114c6e1e5ee4a7e7f9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:Lq-J-thin of arXiv:2411.03609, 'Asymptotically optimal Wasserstein couplings for the small-time stable domain of attractio'] Consider the coupling $(\bm{D}^{\bm{X},\kappa},\bm{D}^{\bm{Y},\kappa},\bm{J}^{\bm{X},\kappa},\bm{J}^{\bm{Y},\kappa})$ defined in~(equation eq:comp_Poisson_measures of the paper) and~(equation eq:thining_coupling_defn of the paper). Then
