{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:31:14.334821+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_77cb130f0573541a9bf30e3153608e0595a62cd8fd9e7afcb5a167a87925564b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem func_assumptions of arXiv:2606.17425, 'Order statistics for edge eigenvectors of Wigner matrices'] Let $\widetilde{\mathcal{L}}_{\tau} = (\mathcal{L}_{\tau}^1, \dots, \mathcal{L}_{\tau}^K) : {\mathbb R}^{\#_{J}} \to {\mathbb R}^K$ be an $N$-dependent family of smooth functions parametrized by $\tau > 0$, whose components $\mathcal{L}_{\tau}^l, l = 1, \dots, K$ each satisfy the bound, 
