{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.700123+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_77e76de63f96939ecedcd8ec68d2024070c0b7dae6f4d20e2898082f60acd051","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop lem:transfer of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] Given $\eta \in (0,\tfrac{1}{2}-\gamma)$, there exists $c=c(\eta) > 0$ such that, if $k$ is large enough, for any $2 \leq T \leq {\rm e}^{ck^\gamma}$, $n \geq k$ and $x,\widetilde{x} \in {\rm D}_n$ with $x \in {\rm B}^-[\widetilde{x};T-1]$ and $\overline{{\rm B}^+[\widetilde{x};T]} \subseteq {\rm D}_n$, one has  
	\begin{equation}
		\frac{\mathbb{P} \Big( \big\{ Z_t[x;1] = (u,\overline{y})\big\} \setminus \mathrm{NR}^{\eta,[2,T-1]}_{n,t}(x) \,\Big|\,Z_t[\widetilde{x};T] = (v,\overline{z}) \Big)}{\mathbb{P} \Big( \big\{ \sqrt{\widehat{T}_{(v)}(1)} = u\big\} \setminus \mathcal{T}^{\eta,[2,T-1]}_{(v)}\Big)}=h_{k}(\overline{y})(1+O({\rm e}^{-ck^\gamma}))
	\end{equation} uniformly over all $t > 0$, $(u,\overline{y}) \in \mathcal Z_k[1]$ with $0 \leq \widetilde{u}_k \leq {\rm e}^{ck^\gamma}$ and $(v,\overline{z}) \in \mathcal Z_k[T]$ with $1 \leq \widetilde{v}_k \leq {\rm e}^{ck^\gamma}$, where $h_k$ is as in~(equation eq:defhk1 of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

