{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.885984+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_77e8f2882685608b962703bddcb419d996cdc7df2be0a2e8662655d83f8dc81f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def: cycle conditon of arXiv:2411.06861, 'Quenched invariance principle for random walks in random environments admitting a cycle de'] A random vector $\Psi\colon \Omega \times \mathcal{N} \to \mathbb{R}$, satisfies the \emph{cycle condition} if for any sequence $(x_{0}, \cdots, x_{n})$ in $\mathbb{Z}^{d}$, with $x_{0} = x_{n}$ and $(x_{j-1}, x_{j}) \in \vec{E}_d$, $1 \leq j \leq n$, it holds that

