{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:32:20.722938+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_77fe10f8513b8c7eace8974fa030382d310d225d6a4098d155fe9b6b02e917a3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 34 of arXiv:2609.00285, 'Multicrossing complex of knot and secant classes'] The \emph{secant $(m,l)$-invariants} of the knot $K$ are defined by the formula
\begin{equation}
    \sigma_i(K;m,l)=\sum_{\phi\in Hom_{m,l}(G_K,G)} \phi(\sigma_i(K)),\quad i=2,3,4.
\end{equation}
Here $\sigma_2(K;m,l)$ is considered as a multi-subset of $H_2(G,m,l)$, i.e. an element of $\Z_{\ge 0}[H_2(G,m,l)]$, $\sigma_3(K;m,l)$ is considered as a multi-subset of $H_3^-(G,m,l)$, and $\sigma_4(K;m,l)$ is considered as a multi-subset of $H_4^+(G,m,l)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:32:35.566304+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_77fe171d237c6f1f6b4d609109b6cd5ffe269355d1d312d309a4b4fabd51c7f0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition pro.clock-resolvent-L2 of arXiv:2605.26082, 'Quantitative Einstein relation for reversible diffusions in a random environment'] There exists $C<\infty$ such that, for $\mathbb{Q}$-a.e.\ $\omega$ and every $m,h\in\mathbb{N}$ and $\rho\ge 1$ with $m\ge\mathcal{X}_\mu(\omega)$ and $\lambda=\rho 3^{-m}$, the clock resolvent $q_m$ defined by~(equation eq.clock-resolvent of the paper) satisfies
			\begin{equation}
			\|q_m\|_{\underline L^2(\square_{m+h})}\le C\rho^{13/12}3^{(7/12-\beta_h/2)h-(\beta_h/2)m}\, .
		\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.224208+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_77ff2a27f5102d542aca7498894bfdc7121d0c9d95968888d0d8cc53f817fbe7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:R(t) of arXiv:2506.15949, 'On the passage times of self-similar Gaussian processes on curved boundaries'] $\mathscr{R}(t)<\infty$ for one, hence all $t>0$, if and only if
