{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:58:40.871851+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_78035cd90d32dc5e2eb7e42282b1ba1a4352765bca254c871c2fa9c468e40aa2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:clconvhull of arXiv:2605.10491, 'Zero-couplings of infinite measures with cyclically monotone support and multivariate regu'] Let $\psi : \mathbb{R}^d \to \mathbb{R} \cup \{\infty\}$ be a closed convex function and let $D \subset \mathbb{R}^d$ be such that $D \cap \operatorname{dom} \psi \ne \varnothing$. Define the function $\phi$ by $\phi = \operatorname{cl}(\operatorname{conv} g)$, where $g(x) = \psi(x)$ if $x \in D$ and $g(x) = \infty$ if $x \in \mathbb{R}^d \setminus D$. Then $\phi$ is a closed convex function with the following properties:
	\begin{enumerate}[label=(\alph*)]
		\item $\phi \geqslant \psi$;
		\item $\phi(x) = \psi(x)$ for $x \in D$;
		\item $\partial \phi(x) = \{ v \in \mathbb{R}^d : \forall z \in D, \, \psi(z) \geqslant \psi(x) + \langle{z-x,v}\rangle \} \supset \partial \psi(x)$ for $x \in  D$;
		\item $\operatorname{dom} \nabla \phi \subset \operatorname{dom} \partial \psi$;
		\item $D \cap \operatorname{dom} \nabla \phi \subset \operatorname{dom} \nabla \psi$ and $\nabla \phi(x) = \nabla \psi(x)$ for all $x \in D \cap \operatorname{dom} \nabla \phi$.
	\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

