{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:00.617612+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_784e65f3c5c3a104fe749080000e6b97b75781e57246a4318f574968a108a685","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 65 of arXiv:2510.27589, 'Geodesic switches and exceptional times in dynamical Brownian last passage percolation'] There exist a constant $c_k$ such that for all $1\leq t\leq n^{1/10}$, we have
