{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:58:24.522989+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_78a78376ccf4b58bf6e271aad6c76a56593f5efebc9718d69d174942c815ef17","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:uniformity of arXiv:2601.13426, 'A uniformity principle for spatial matching'] Given any constant $\gamma \geq \max\{1,\xi^{-1}\}$, for any two service range vectors $\mathsf{R}, \mathsf{R}' \in [0, \gamma]^n$ satisfying $\mathsf{R} \succeq \mathsf{R}'$ and $\|\mathsf{R} ^\downarrow - {\mathsf{R}'}^\downarrow\|_1 > \theta n$, where 
