{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:51:15.018624+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_78c2a2cda013f3a31699516fd0bd8daefd76ae72d4fbbcdf43bd014ff90eea07","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm thm3.6 of arXiv:2609.03751, 'Sparse bounds for maximal rough singular integrals'] {MR4245601}}]
Let \([K]=\{K_s:s\in\mathbb Z\}\) be a family of kernels satisfying
(equation equ3.1 of the paper) and (equation equ3.3 of the paper). Suppose that
\(1\leq p_1,p_2<\infty\) and
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
    C_L[K](p_1,p_2)
    :=\sup_{\mathcal Q,t_1,t_2}
    \Bigg\{
    \sup_{\substack{
        \|b\|_{\dot{\mathcal X}_{p_1}(\mathcal Q)}=1\\
        \|f\|_{\mathcal Y_{p_2}(\mathcal Q)}=1}}
      \bigl|
        \mathcal Q[K]_{t_1}^{t_2}(b,f)
      \bigr|
    +
    \sup_{\substack{
        \|f\|_{\mathcal Y_\infty(\mathcal Q)}=1\\
        \|b\|_{\dot{\mathcal X}_{p_2}(\mathcal Q)}=1}}
      \bigl|
        \mathcal Q[K]_{t_1}^{t_2}(f,b)
      \bigr|
    \Bigg\}
    <\infty,
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
where the outer supremum is taken over all stopping collections
\(\mathcal Q\) and all bounded measurable integer-valued truncation
functions \(t_1,t_2\). Then
\begin{equation}
    \|T_\star[K]\|_{(p_1,p_2)\text{-}\mathrm{sparse}}
    \lesssim
    \|[K]\|_{r,\star}+C_L[K](p_1,p_2).
\end{equation}
The implicit constant in (equation equ3.7 of the paper) is independent of
\(p_1\) and \(p_2\). In our application \(r=2\) is fixed. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:53.184297+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_78c63da13b7a72500ab8eb1099c4264f84b34dcb7585f1c2bca06cb88087eb2c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2606.30080, 'Ergodicity of reflected stochastic reaction-diffusion equations driven by space-time white'] Assume that (S1)--(S3) and (H3) hold. Let $p>2$. Define
  \begin{align*}
    h_{+}(u):=
  \begin{cases}
