{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:43:53.623821+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_78cebbbb137b75313477d8e0562b1ee1630074d1ad1a22b9732a5060bb579f4d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition eq the jensen inequality of arXiv:2512.13200, 'Martingales on a Euclidean manifold with a boundary and reflected BSDEs in non-convex doma'] Let Assumption (ass:3 of the paper) hold, and let $\xi$ be a random variable with values in $\bar{\mathcal{D}}$. Then, there exists a unique minimizer of
