{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:23:05.301221+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_78d3de707da80e037625b5c1de9db4f6ed16c93f9b8be19fa2edb9f3504aac28","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 21 (Baseline-corrected posterior cloning) of arXiv:2608.21709, 'Posterior Information Dynamics of Diffusion Models for Linear Inverse Problems'] Define the conditional cloning observable
\begin{equation}

\phi_r(t)
=
\E_{Z_t\mid r}
\left[
\sum_{c\in\{\pm1\}}P(C=c\mid Z_t,r)^2
\right].
\end{equation}
Then
\begin{equation}

\phi_r(\infty)
=
\alpha_+^2+
\alpha_-^2
=
\sum_cP(C=c\mid r)^2.
\end{equation}
Therefore the dynamic class-speciation signal is
\begin{equation}

\Delta\phi_r(t)=\phi_r(t)-\phi_r(\infty),
\end{equation}
or, when \(\phi_r(\infty)<1\),
\begin{equation}

\widetilde\phi_r(t)
=
\frac{\phi_r(t)-\phi_r(\infty)}
{1-\phi_r(\infty)}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.652550+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_78d4aed39f873f1fa310b486d825857a00a609bd9d7332981f365311fbc68f48","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:S^d-regular-def of arXiv:2411.12076, 'Explicit solutions of the SI and Bass models on sparse Erd\H{o}s-R\'enyi and regular netwo'] Let 
	$[S^{ \text{\rm d-reg}}]  := 1- f^{ \text{\rm d-reg}}$. Then for any $ j \in \cal M$, 
