{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:04:30.545598+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_796a00fa47798297e8260461136974674e28c2b871610dc043d720b537913425","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: Concentration of spin overlaps under tp extr. of arXiv:2411.10271, '$A$-localized states for clock models on trees and their extremal decomposition into glass'] There exists a sequence of spacings $r=(r_i)_{i\in \mathbb{N}}$, in general depending on the model parameter, such that for any thinned branch $(\Lambda_n^r)_{n\in \mathbb{N}}$ with $\sum^\infty_{n=1}\frac{1}{|\Lambda_n^r|}<\infty$, the following holds. For $\mu_A$-almost every $\omega\in \Omega$, for $\pi(\cdot|\omega)$-almost every realization of $\sigma$, we have 
