{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:03:39.776623+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_79c83206998783c4810f3ce0f883d3a0122a971b0b49630b4dcbbb8db827fad9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor shuffling-sg-with-iid of arXiv:2411.03065, 'Growing conditioned BGW trees with\\ log-concave offspring distributions'] Let $(\mathbb{X},\mathcal X,\nu)$ be a probability space, and let $\psi$ be a measurable $\mathbb{X}$-shuffling rule.
