{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:11:11.682629+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a29567398896162b22b9fec02b24fd4f73c0d7b83b6e5b44a7111a0f02a7d6e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:BI-decomposition of arXiv:2609.00560, 'Distribution of Kaneko's val function'] For every $f\in M_0^!(\Gamma)$,
	\begin{align}
		I_f(\gamma) &= \int_{\calA} f(z) \sum_{k=1}^{s(\gamma)} \left( \frac{1}{z-w^{(k)}}-\frac{1}{z-\widetilde w^{(k)}} \right)\,\mathrm{d} z.
