{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:23:27.795146+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a2b1c1089100e16b18519a58eb751f6664f2b956f9e89da47c8e03c4fe4d135","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l.EL of arXiv:2606.11043, 'Thick points under Gaussian free field dynamics'] Take $(\Psi,x,t)$ sampled from $\mathcal{Q}_{\varepsilon}^{\gamma}$. The conditional law of $(x,t)$ given $\Psi$  is 
    \begin{equation}

        \nu_{\varepsilon}^{\gamma,N}(dxdt):=\frac{\exp\left(\gamma \Psi_{\varepsilon}(x,t)
        -\frac{\gamma^2}{2}\mathbb E[(\Psi_{\varepsilon}(x,t))^2]\right)
        }{\mu_{\varepsilon}^{\gamma}(D_T)}dxdt.
    \end{equation}
    And on the other hand, the law of $\Psi$ conditionally on $(x,t)$, is equal to 
    \begin{equation}

        \hat{\Psi} + \gamma \mathrm{cov}(\cdot, \Psi_{\varepsilon}(x,t)),
    \end{equation}
    where $\hat{\Psi}$ has the law of the SHEF on $Ps(D, [0,T])$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:11:11.682734+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a2e500dd5fa6caec9a8d26716294fa14c05849a91957dfa78727ea780c6a86c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:BHI-block of arXiv:2609.00560, 'Distribution of Kaneko's val function'] For $\omega = (x,y,\epsilon) \in \Sigma$, put $a(\omega) \coloneqq \lfloor 1/x \rfloor$ and $u(\omega) \coloneqq Tx$. For $a \geq 1$, $0 < u,y < 1$, and $z \in \calA$, define
	\begin{align*}
		B_a^{(0)}(z;u,y) &\coloneqq \sum_{m=1}^a \left( \frac{1}{z-(m+u)^{-1}}-\frac{1}{z+(a-m+y)^{-1}} \right),\\
		B_a^{(1)}(z;u,y) &\coloneqq \sum_{m=1}^a \left( \frac{1}{z-(m+u)}-\frac{1}{z+(a-m+y)} \right).
	\end{align*}
	For $f\in M_0^!(\Gamma)$, define
	\[
		\Phi_f(\omega) \coloneqq \int_{\calA} f(z) B_{a(\omega)}^{(\epsilon)} \bigl(z;u(\omega),y\bigr)\,\mathrm{d} z.
	\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:57:07.197270+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a2e7cb6f3d9d7a899fd8dbb10fc62ace701f037bd784a6b1d351832b17036c3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:DKS-polymer-weights of arXiv:2509.04333, 'The limiting law of the Discrete Gaussian level lines'] Fix $\delta > 0$. Let $z$, $z_r$ for $r = 1, \ldots, N$ be complex numbers such that $|\Re z| < 2 - \delta/\beta'$. Let $s$ be a real number in $[0, \delta/3]$. For any interval $I \subset [0, N]$ with integer endpoints, define
		\begin{equation*}
			\hat X_{N, s}(I) := (\prod_{r \in I} Q_{z_r})^{-1} \sum_{\Gamma: J(\Gamma) = I} {\widehat q}^n_z(\Gamma)\exp(s|I|)\,.
		\end{equation*}
		Then, there exists some $\beta_0$ and constant $c$ such that for all $N$, $\beta \geq \beta_0$, $z$, $z_r$, and all such intervals $I$, we have
		\begin{equation*}
			|\hat X_{N, s}(I)| \leq \exp(-(\beta - \beta_0)(|I| - 1))\,.
		\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:57:51.747886+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a3064d17ed2b8896ec884d6b41e4f1c432c76d8f596d3a79e0eefc79eea2aa4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2608.30138, 'High-frequency wave propagation for the viscoelastic wave equation with singular memory'] For $k=0,1,\dots$, let $F\in C([0,T];H^k(\Omega))$, and
assume that \eqref{m-int-k} holds with $k+1$ in place of $k$. 
Then the Volterra equation 
\begin{equation}   
\Delta_{\sigma_\eps} u (t) -  \eps\nabla \cdot \int_0^t \mathfrak{m}(s,\cdot) \nabla u(t-s)\,\d s=F(t)
\end{equation}
has a unique solution $u\in C([0,T]; \, H^{k+2}(\Omega)\cap H_0^1(\Omega))$. Moreover, the norm of the solution operator $F\mapsto u$ is uniformly bounded in $\eps\in [0,\eps_0]$, for $\eps_0\ll1$ possibly depending on $m$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.578168+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a307a337b1aa2cf80a93052ece71ac0f5d3ba11bb1c723b5c5b6758675fe228","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition p:GirsanovDFSimple of arXiv:2411.14936, 'Massive Particle Systems,\\Wasserstein Brownian Motions,\\ and the Dean--Kawasaki Equation'] Fix~$\mbfs\in\mbfT_\circ$.
A stochastic process
\[
\boldsymbol\mssV^\mbfs= \tparen{\Omega,\msF,\msF_\bullet, \mbfY^\mbfs_\bullet, \seq{P_{\mbfx}}_{\mbfx\in \mbfM_{\boldsymbol\varphi}},\zeta}
\]
with state space~$\mathrm{em}^{-1}(\msP^\pa_\iso\cap \msP_\phi)$ is a solution to the martingale problem for $\tparen{\widehat\boldsymbol\mssL^{\boldsymbol\varphi},\mcC_b(\mbfT)\otimes\Cyl{}{}}$ if and only if, for every~$i\in{\mathbb N}$,
\[
f(Y^i_t)-f(Y^i_0) = \int_0^t (\mssL f)(Y^i_r) \mathop{}\!\mathrm{d} r - \int_0^t \boldsymbol\varphi(\mbfs,\mbfY_r)^{-1}\, \widehat\boldsymbol{\mathsf{\Gamma}}_\pi\big({\boldsymbol\varphi,\car_\mbfT\otimes\, \ev(f)}\big)(\mbfs,\mbfY^i_r)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d} r \,\mathrm{.}
\]

\begin{proof}
The forward implication holds choosing~$\mbfu=\car_\mbfT\otimes \ev(f)$ in~(equation eq:c:Girsanov:1 of the paper).
The converse implication is a standard application of the diffusion property for~$\big({\widehat\mcL^\phi_\pi,\msD(\widehat\mcL^\phi_\pi)}\big)$ together with the It\^o formula for continuous ${\mathbb R}^d$-valued semi-martingales, similarly to the proof of Theorem~(t:DK of the paper)(i:t:DK:3 of the paper)$\implies$(i:t:DK:2 of the paper).
\end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:20:55.630623+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a3240fecfeac34c55ad2c55626a9a0a9cd213deb95ccb578ee533e82796b4db","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:iso of arXiv:2411.07809, 'Pirogov--Sinai Theory Beyond Lattices'] Suppose $G$ is infinite, one-ended, quasi-transitive, and has
