{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:01:54.288568+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a34b0a33c42a45b54bd0845d3673177b304ad7037b091c345116144a0bbf583","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem X^p-2sm1 of arXiv:2411.01849, 'A tamed-adaptive Milstein scheme for stochastic differential equations with low regularity'] For any $p>0$, there exists a positive constant $C_p$, which does not depend on $\Delta$, such that for any $s>0$, it holds that 
