{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:42:39.095539+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a3c0449d6d26a61b6c9ec046987e4b1f524a5551ccb9448d1ef53d4920f869b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop cor 5.7 of arXiv:2412.08497, 'Time discretization of Quadratic Forward-Backward SDEs with singular drift'] Under Assumption (A1), the solution $(X_t^x,0\leq t\leq T)$ to equation (equation 2.1 of the paper) is Malliavin differentiable and for any $p\geq 2$ there is a constant $C$ only depending on $p,d ,T$ such that
