{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:49.203181+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a4fe0120900450cd34e1da7b13c6a0f082235fc50f4a68c62a448afa3b79ac2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2604.26898, '\bf Stochastic Scaling Limits and Synchronization \\by Noise in Deep Transformer Models'] There exists a constant $\mathsf c > 0$, depending on $T$ but independent of $L$ and $N$, such that for all $i$:
