{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:43:18.739238+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a69a46d7ad56b798fdf3fc5f04911226cec6f447aff5d8ef0376a97851ff19a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi def:min_incomp_pairs of arXiv:2609.02346, 'Regularised double shuffle relations for planar \AZVs{}'] Let $T\in\mathcal{PT}_{\N^*}$ be a non-empty planar tree which is not a ladder tree. Then we can uniquely write 
  \begin{equation*}
   T=B_+^{n_1}\circ\cdots\circ B_+^{n_p}(T_1\cdots T_k)
  \end{equation*}
  for some non-empty planar trees $T_1,\cdots,T_k$ and $k\geq2$. Let $a$ be the root of $T_1$ and $b$ be the root of $T_2$. Then we call $(a,b)$ the \emph{minimal incomparable pair} of $T$.
  And so $T$ can be written

  \begin{equation*}
   T=B_+^{n_1}\circ\cdots\circ B_+^{n_p}(B_+^{n_a}(F_a)B_+^{n_b}(F_b)F)
  \end{equation*}
  where $F_a$, $F_b$ and $F$ are planar forests, eventually empty. Then we set as in~[Fan25]
  \begin{align*}
   T_b^a & := B_+^{n_1}\circ\cdots\circ B_+^{n_p}\left(B_+^{n_a}(B_+^{n_b}(F_b)F_a)F\right), \\
   T_a^b & := B_+^{n_1}\circ\cdots\circ B_+^{n_p}\left(B_+^{n_b}(B_+^{n_a}(F_a)F_b)F\right), \\
   T_{a+b} & :=B_+^{n_1}\circ\cdots\circ B_+^{n_p}\left(B_+^{n_a+n_b}(F_aF_b)F\right).
  \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:32:34.762648+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a6a8454ce5a983422afc80456774edade571be7a47b63a90679016d2de634d2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition Th:semigroup of arXiv:2411.08220, 'Nonlocal operators with Neumann conditions'] For $x\neq 0$, $t>0$ and $f\in \mathcal{B}^+(\mathbb{R}_*)$, we have
