{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.319654+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a6d297a1bae37e6302bd5e276e060135d425414a2ac7e202f9cae3954df9ff2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:inv-NWU of arXiv:2411.14926, 'Convex combinations of random variables stochastically dominate the parent for a new class'] A random variable $X$ is super-heavy-tailed if and only if
