{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:18:19.226843+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a74f37d153d005ac39cd5cf6ad613d69955a1e7e8415f18fd39ff100abad054","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 25 of arXiv:2608.29086, '2608.29086'] [$INT(U)$]
Given $U \subset A$. $INT(U)$ denotes the collection of all integral molecules whose supports are contained in $U$, i.e.,
\begin{equation*}
