{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.326573+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a80e644d9bcf7bb0707a6bfd6dacec81cdcd4ccf42d3d68099dc02d2efa0510","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem t:GeneralForm of arXiv:2411.14936, 'Massive Particle Systems,\\Wasserstein Brownian Motions,\\ and the Dean--Kawasaki Equation'] Let~$(M,\tau)$ be a metrizable Lusin topological space endowed with a $\sigma$-finite Borel measure~$\sigma$, and~$\msP$ be the space of all Borel probability measures on~$M$ endowed with its usual narrow topology.
Further let
\begin{enumerate*}[$(a)$, leftmargin=2em]
\item $\msA\subset L^2(\sigma)\cap \mcC_b(\tau)$ be an algebra of continuous functions, dense in~$L^2(\sigma)$;
\item $\big({\mssL,\msD(\mssL)}\big)$ be a self-adjoint Markov diffusion operator on~$L^2(\sigma)$ such that~$\mssL\msA\subset\msA$;
\item $\hFC{\msA}{0}$ be the algebra of cylinder functions on~$\msP$ defined as in Definition~(d:StandardFC of the paper);
\item $\mcS$ be a $\sigma$-finite Borel measure on~$\msP$ such that~$\tclass[\mcS]{\hFC{\msA}{0}}\subset L^2(\mcS)$.
\end{enumerate*}

Then,
\begin{enumerate}[$(i)$, leftmargin=2em]
\item the operator~$\tparen{\widehat\mcL, \hFC{\msA}{0}}$ defined by the right-hand side of~(equation eq:l:DiffusionP:0.4 of the paper) takes values in~$L^2(\mcS)$.
\end{enumerate}

Further assume that the measure~$\mcS$ is such that
\begin{enumerate}[$(a)$, leftmargin=2em]\setcounter{enumi}{4}
\item $\hFC{\msA}{0}$ is dense in~$L^2(\mcS)$
\item the operator~$\tparen{\widehat\mcL, \hFC{\msA}{0}}$ is $L^2(\mcS)$-symmetric.
\end{enumerate}

Then, the following assertions hold:
\begin{enumerate}[$(i)$, leftmargin=2em]\setcounter{enumi}{1}
\item the quadratic form~$\tparen{\widehat\mcE,\hFC{\msA}{0}}$ defined by~$\widehat\mcE(u,v)\eqdef \ttscalar{u}{-\widehat\mcL v}_{L^2(\mcS)}$ is closable on~$L^2(\mcS)$ and its closure~$\big({\widehat\mcE,\msD(\widehat\mcE)}\big)$ is a Dirichlet form with generator the Friedrichs extension of~$\tparen{\widehat\mcE,\hFC{\msA}{0}}$;

\item the Dirichlet form~$\big({\widehat\mcE,\msD(\widehat\mcE)}\big)$ admits carr\'e du champ operator
\[
\widehat\mcG(u,v)_\eta= \int \mathsf{\Gamma}^z\big\lvert_{z=x} \big({u(\eta+\eta_x\delta_z-\eta_x\delta_x), u(\eta+\eta_x\delta_z-\eta_x\delta_x)}\big) \mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\eta(x) \,\mathrm{,}\;\,\quad u,v\in \hFC{\msA}{0}\,\mathrm{.}
\]
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.768248+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a8218a1513e8a606c9a310dc53266ad4614797250e5c105fec68e794fcc8e7b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Step1 of arXiv:2609.01464, 'Removability of non-isolated singularities for Einstein metrics and RCD spaces'] Let $(Z,d,\mathfrak{m})$ be as in (Setting of the paper), and let us assume it verifies the global Sobolev inequality (equation eqn:GlobalSobolev of the paper) in (assumptions of the paper). Then we have the following:
