{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:32:23.873882+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a95ac7c84fab110bb99cf56ebdb792b22d426b1c874adcfa9a137a2d0772703","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor torus of arXiv:2603.27144, 'On the critical fugacity of the hard-core model on regular bipartite graphs'] For each $C_{0}>0$ there exist $C_{1},C_{2}>0$
such that for each dimension $d\ge2$ and even $L\ge2$: The event
\begin{equation}
