{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:47:40.663351+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7aa458233043015f4683c55b27abd499c128da973ce2d490a3fec98aebea7e9a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:nointersectAT of arXiv:2604.15146, 'Renormalised two-point functions of CLE$_4$ gaskets'] Let $\widetilde F_{\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2}$ denote the event that at least two different odd CLE$_4$ gaskets of the family of CLE$_4$ gaskets constructed in Theorem (thm:twopointAT of the paper) intersect both 
$\mathbb{D}(z_1, \varepsilon_1)$ and $\mathbb{D}(z_2, \varepsilon_2)$. Then
\begin{itemize}
    \item Let $E_{\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2}^{\rm{odd},k}(z_1,z_2)$ denote the event that the $k$-th odd nested CLE$_4$ gasket intersects 
    $\mathbb{D}(z_1,\varepsilon_1)$ and $\mathbb{D}(z_2,\varepsilon_2)$. Then there is a constant $C > 0$
    such that for all $k \geq 1$,
    $$\mathbb{P}(\widetilde F_{\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2} \cap E_{\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2}^{\rm{odd},k}(z_1,z_2)) \leq C(\varepsilon_1\varepsilon_2)^{1/4}\left(\mathbb{P}(E_{\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2}^{\rm{odd},k}) + \1_{k \geq 2}\mathbb{P}(E_{\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2}^{\rm{odd},k-1})\right).$$
    \item Further, for some $\widetilde C > 0$, 
    for all $\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2 > 0$ sufficiently small, 
$$\sum_{k \geq 1}\mathbb{P}(E^{\rm{odd},k}_{\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2}(z_1,z_2)) < \widetilde C\mathbb{P}(E_{\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2}^{\rm odd}(z_1,z_2)).$$
    \item In particular, $\mathbb{P}(\widetilde F_{\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2})$ is bounded by $C(\varepsilon_1\varepsilon_2)^{1/4}\mathbb{P}(E_{\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2}^{\rm odd}(z_1, z_2))$ for some $C > 0$ as $\max(\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2)\to 0$. 
\end{itemize}
Further, the same holds when we replace odd by even everywhere. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:53.182787+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7aa504bbf74089d9439330d84ad49451097ff2547db05705e591f859d8d8d832","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 2 of arXiv:2606.30080, 'Ergodicity of reflected stochastic reaction-diffusion equations driven by space-time white'] Let $\{\sigma(s,y): (s,y)\in\mathbb{R}_+\times [0,1]\}$ be a random field such that the stochastic integral against space-time white noise is well defined. Then for any $p>2$, $\beta>0$ and $\alpha>0$ satisfying $\frac{1}{2p}<\alpha<\frac{1}{4}$, there exists a constant $C_{p,\beta,\alpha}>0$ independent of $t$ such that for any $t\geq 0$,
  \begin{align}
    & {\mathbb{E}}\left[\sup_{x\in [0,1]}\left|\int_0^t\int_0^1 e^{-\beta (t-s)}p_{t-s}(x,y)\sigma(s,y)\,W(ds,dy) \right|^p\right] \nonumber\\
    \leq & C_{p,\beta,\alpha} \sup_{s\in [0,t]}\left(\int_0^s (s-r)^{-2\alpha-\frac{1}{2}} e^{-2\beta (s-r)} \sup_{z\in[0,1]}\left\Vert \sigma(r,z)\right\Vert_{L^p(\Omega)}^2\,dr\right)^{\frac{p}{2}} .
  \end{align}
In particular, for any $T>0$, 
  \begin{align}
     & \sup_{t\in [0,T]}\left\Vert \sup_{x\in [0,1]}\left|\int_0^t\int_0^1 e^{-\beta (t-s)}p_{t-s}(x,y)\sigma(s,y)\,W(ds,dy) \right|\right\Vert_{L^p(\Omega)} \nonumber\\
    \leq  & C_{p,\beta} \sup_{s\in [0,T]} \sup_{y\in[0,1]}\Vert \sigma(s,y)\Vert_{L^p(\Omega)},

  \end{align}
where the constant $C_{p,\beta}$ is independent of $T$ and can be bounded by
\begin{align}
  C_{p,\beta} < \frac{\sqrt{4p}}{\pi}\left(\frac{1}{2\sqrt{\pi}}\right)^{\frac{1}{p}+\frac{1}{2}} \frac{1}{\beta^{\frac{1}{4}-\frac{1}{2p}}} \times \left(\Gamma\Big(\frac{p-2}{6p}\Big)\right)^{\frac{3}{2}}, 
\end{align}
where $\Gamma(\cdot)$ is the gamma function.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.567389+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7aa5cdb12c6b2e05f4da381be33724431a84e83db59a88f3ae56630b307f7b20","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 24 of arXiv:2608.26516, '2608.26516'] For a regularizer $\psi$ and target $h$, let $\operatorname{Sel}_\psi(h)$ denote the collection of all hypotheses in $\CH$ that are most-preferred by $\psi$ on an $h$-realizable sample. That is,
\[
    \operatorname{Sel}_\psi(h)
    :=
    \left\{
        g\in\Hc:
        \begin{array}{l}
        \text{there exists a realizable sample $S$ labeled by $h$}\\[-0.1em]
        \text{such that }
        g\in\argmin_{u\in\vs(S)}\psi(u)
        \end{array}
    \right\}.
\]
Then the \edefn{selected ordered disagreement dimension} of $\psi$ is 
\[
    d_{\mathrm{SOD}}(\psi)
    :=
    \sup_{h\in\Hc}
    \VC\{\Delta(g,h):g\in\operatorname{Sel}_\psi(h)\}.
\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:25:55.420193+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7aa6001481d58d713494d53a8d891f28ccf07840aa092e6247f7a555c5ba181d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 3 of arXiv:2607.28215, 'Almost stochastic dominance via optimal transport'] For two $E$-valued random variables $X,Y$ we define
