{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.122042+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7aacf2dc62a94b28398cfb0c6e565f95d15bfdcdad754072642286b398a7dbe9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:radial-qf of arXiv:2608.18293, 'Critical tensor covariance at the Marchenko--Pastur threshold'] Under (equation eq:base-assumptions of the paper) and (equation eq:critical-scaling of the paper), there exists a deterministic sequence $\varepsilon_n\to0$ such that for every deterministic complex $p\times p$ matrix $A$,
\begin{equation}
  \mathbb{E}\left|
  \frac{x^{\mathsf T}Ax}{p}
  -R_n\frac{\operatorname{Tr} A}{p}
  \right|^2
  \le \varepsilon_n\|A\|_{\mathrm{op}}^2.

\end{equation}
For all sufficiently large $n$, one may take
\begin{equation}
  \boxed{\quad
  \varepsilon_n=\bigl(\sqrt{\delta_n}+\sqrt{\kappa_n}\bigr)^2,
  \quad}

\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}
  \delta_n=\frac{vd}{n-d}e^{vd^2/(n-d)},
  \qquad
  \kappa_n=
  \frac{8d(n-d)}{n(n-1)}
  \exp\!\left(\frac{2vd^2}{n-d}\right).

\end{equation}
Both terms tend to zero.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.576388+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7ab1aea024ce75cfbd36af7e81684aeb96b7070f308eadeea86cf5211338081f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma FCLT of arXiv:2412.08932, 'Gaussian heat kernel asymptotics for conditioned random walks'] There exists a construction of the random walk $(S_n)_{n\geqslant 0}$ on the initial probability space
together with a continuous time Brownian motion $(B_t)_{t\geqslant 0}$ such that for any $s>0$ and $n\geqslant 1$,
\begin{align*}
\bb{P} \left( \sup_{0\leqslant t\leqslant 1} \left| S_{[nt]} - \sigma B_{nt} \right| > \sigma n^{1/2 - s}  \right)
 \leqslant  \frac{c_{\delta,s}}{ n^{ \frac{\delta}{2} - (2+\delta) s} }, 
