{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.788465+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7ab31dea35268499d44ff42fcb05af18f94b9d01325c06f3a7dfb61c06848d97","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:tailrl-binary-recovery of arXiv:2609.02987, 'Tail Likelihood Reinforcement Learning'] Suppose $r_i\in\{0,1\}$ and let
$M:=\sum_{i=1}^N\mathbbm{1}\{r_i=1\}$. If $M>0$, then every successful
rollout receives weight $1/M$ and every unsuccessful rollout receives weight
zero. Hence the uncentered TailRL{} estimator reduces to
\begin{equation}
g_{\mathrm{TailRL}}^{(N)}(x)
=
\frac{1}{M}
\sum_{i:r_i=1}S_i,

\end{equation}
which is the MaxRL estimator. After mean-centering, successful rollouts have
weight $1/M-1/N$ and unsuccessful rollouts have weight $-1/N$. If $M=0$,
all uncentered and centered weights are zero.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:42:47.775753+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7ab3a1cabb5d5ef62c4d726f67178917b5cd45670b7a467ffbc1892df4b51605","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Dfn 23 (Exact lumpability and exact lumping) of arXiv:2604.12853, 'Coupling Markov Chains \\with a Common Image Chain'] Let $f:A \twoheadrightarrow B$ be a surjection between countable sets. 
    We say that $P\in\SM(A)$ is \textbf{exactly lumpable} under $f$ with respect to $(\nu_z)_{z \in B}$ if $\nu_z \in \PM(f^{-1}(z))$ for each $z \in B$ and there exists $Q \in \SM(B)$ such that for every $z,z' \in B$ and every $x' \in f^{-1}(z')$, the \emph{exact lumping equation} holds:
    \begin{equation}

        \sum_{x\in f^{-1}(z)} \nu_z(x) P(x,x')  = Q(z,z') \nu_{z'}(x')\,.   
    \end{equation}
    We say $P$ is exactly lumpable under $f$ to $Q$ if such a family $(\nu_b)_{b \in B}$ exists for which \eqref{eq: EL discrete} holds. 

    For $\upalpha \in \PM(A)$, we say that
    $\MC(\upalpha,P)$ \textbf{lumps exactly} under $f$ to the chain $\MC(f_*(\upalpha),Q)$
    if there exists a family $(\nu_z)_{z\in B}$ and a matrix $Q$, that together satisfy equation~\eqref{eq: EL discrete}, such that $\upalpha$ is a convex combination of the measures $(\nu_z)_{z \in B}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.780509+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7ab63bd25dc8667f14254e9937df378d3536996116d57b1430890ccf2d9e3fac","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma limlo of arXiv:2411.18359, 'Large systems of symmetrized trapped Brownian Bridges and Schr\"odinger processes'] If $\phi:{\mathcal X } \to \mathbb{R}$ is lower semi continuous and the Large Deviations lower bound holds with $I:{\mathcal X } \to [0,\infty]$ then
\begin{equation}
    \liminf_{\epsilon \to 0}\epsilon\log \mathbb{E}[e^{\frac{\phi( Z_\epsilon)}{\epsilon}}]\geq\sup_{x\in {\mathcal X }}\{\phi(x)-I(x)\}
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:18:19.227929+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7ab71130a6424039291fcc41a6b8082bb1ac31ac5cfa6e40993e4b59f186c616","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 34 of arXiv:2608.29086, '2608.29086'] [$RM(Obj(Mol))$]
A \textit{rigid motion} is a geometric operation on a solid object that changes its position and orientation in space while maintaining its shape, size, but not its chirality ("handedness"). Rigid motions include translations and rotations, and reflections. $RM(Obj(Mol))$ denotes the collection of all rigid motions of elements of $Obje(Mol)$, i.e.,
\begin{multline*}
RM(Obj(Mol)):=\{ \tau \in MAP(Obj(Mol)) \ |\  \tau \text{ is a rigid motion} \}\\
 \subset MAP(Obj(Mol)),
\end{multline*}
where $MAP(Obj(Mol))$ denotes the collection of all mappings from $Obj(Mol)$ to $Obj(Mol)$. 
Given $m \in Obj(Mol)$ and $\tau \in RM(Obj(Mol))$. $\tau(m)$ denotes the molecule obtained by transforming $m$ by $\tau$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:12:09.049797+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7ab989b0a129862866acec6886f571be40ca73d336e668610ca6a88385bfcfd9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:transfer of arXiv:2608.25279, 'Provable Non-Acceleration of Standard Strang\\ Splittings of Kinetic Langevin Dynamics'] Fix $\kappa>1$ and OBABO parameters $h,\gamma>0$ with $h<2/\sqrt\kappa$, and set $\beta=e^{-\gamma h}$, $s=h^2(1+\beta)/2$, and $\tau^2=h^2(1-\beta^2)$. Suppose $U\in\mathcal U_\kappa^d$ for $d\in\{1,2\}$ satisfies Assumptions~(ass:cycle of the paper) and~(ass:monodromy of the paper) with these parameters $(s,\beta)$ and that, in addition, there are $\lambda_\ast\in[1,\kappa]$ and $b_\ast>0$ with
\begin{equation}
 \nabla U(x)=\lambda_\ast x+w(x),
 \qquad \sup_x\lvert w(x)\rvert\le b_\ast.
\end{equation}
Then for $U_R(x)=R^2U(x/R)$ and $Q_R=Q_{h,\gamma}^{U_R}$ there are constants $c_0,C_0>0$, independent of $R$, such that $Q_R$ has a unique invariant law $\pi_R$ and, for every $R\ge1$ and every $j\in\mathbb Z$, there exist two initial states $z_R^{(j)},z_R^{(j+1)}\in\mathbb R^{2d}$, constructed explicitly in (equation eq:cyclepair-general of the paper)-(equation eq:cyclevelocity-general of the paper) below from the cycle points with indices $j$ and $j+1$, such that at least one of them, denoted by $z_R$, satisfies
\begin{equation*}
 W_2(\delta_{z_R},\pi_R)\le C_0(1+R),
\end{equation*}
and
\begin{equation*}
 \norm{\delta_{z_R}Q_R^n-\pi_R}_{\mathrm{TV}}\ge\frac38,
 \qquad
 0\le n\le N_R:=\left\lfloor\frac1{16}e^{c_0R^2}\right\rfloor.
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:21:06.854915+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7abbcdab6272cd98c77fd509028952fd460c9b94bcea76c1b754a15654164155","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 4 (Strong solution) of arXiv:2608.21014, 'The stochastic Cahn--Hilliard equation in critical spaces'] Suppose that Assumption~\ref{Assumption:semilinear:evolution:equation} is satisfied for some $p\in[2,\infty)$ and $\kappa\in [0,p/2-1)\cup\{0\}$. For $T<\infty$, a pair $(u,\sigma)$ is called an $L^p_\kappa$-strong solution of~\eqref{eq:semilinear-stochastic-evolution} if $\sigma\colon\Omega\to[a,T]$ is a stopping time and $u\colon [a,\sigma]\to X_0$  is strongly progressively measurable, 
    \begin{equation*} u\in L^p(a,\sigma, w_\kappa^a;X_1)\cap C\big([a,\sigma];X_{1-\frac{1+\kappa}{p},p}\big),
    \end{equation*}
    and a.s.\ for all $t\in [a,\sigma]$ it holds that 
    \begin{equation}
        u(t)-u_a +\int_a^t Au(s)\,\dd s = \int_a^t F(s,u(s))\, \dd s +\int_a^t\1_{[a,\sigma]}(s) G(s,u(s))\, \dd W(s).
    \end{equation}
    For $T=\infty$, $(u,\sigma)$ is called an $L^p_\kappa$-strong solution of~\eqref{eq:semilinear-stochastic-evolution} if $\sigma\colon\Omega\to [a,\infty)$ is a stopping time and $u\colon[a,\sigma]\to X_0$ is strongly progressively measurable with $u\in L^p_{\loc}(a,\sigma,w_\kappa^a;X_1)\cap C([a,\sigma]\cap[a,\infty);X_{1-\frac{1+\kappa}{p},p})$ and~\eqref{eq:def:semilinear:strong:solution} holds a.s.\ for all $t\in [a,\sigma]$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:40:21.312940+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7abd397c15e4e8a165eb90214802016c43c2941dd575bced879abfce8c7d2fd1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 34 of arXiv:2604.08127, 'Asymptotics of Brownian occupation measures \\ with unusually large intersections'] The distributions of $Z_t = (\widetilde{L}_t , t^{-1}\| \ell_t \|_q)$ satisfy an LDP in $\widetilde{\mathcal{X}}_{\le 1} \times [0, \infty]$ with rate function
