{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:38:04.525269+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7ace914ed835e6a89f80b5b2100519a0a53b3df702ee5b36ba40c24a55bed9a7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition eq:theta_upper_semi_continuity of arXiv:2607.18011, 'From local giants to locality in long-range percolation'] \thlabel{prop:theta_upper_semi_continuity}
    Let $G$ be a transitive graph of polynomial growth, and suppose that $J : V \times V \to \mathbf{R}_+$ is a transitive kernel.

    Let $\beta \in \mathbf{R}_+$ and let $\beta_n \to \beta$.

    Let $(G_n,J_n)_{n \in \mathbf{N}}$ be a sequence of transitive graphs and kernels converging locally to $(G,J)$ with $(J_n)_{n \in \mathbf{N}}$ uniformly integrable. 

    Then

    \begin{equation}

        \limsup_{n \to \infty} 
        \theta(\beta_n,G_n,J_n) 
        \leq 
        \theta(\beta,G,J).
