{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:40:59.357134+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7ad5eea8e92a6360888e498f37ddbc5aadac69342c24ae71c6b8b0fe10f5db4e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 (Large-trace spectral structure) of arXiv:2609.03958, '2609.03958'] Let $n\geq 2$ and $K\geq 0$. Suppose that $\lambda\in \Gamma_2$ satisfies $\lambda_1\ge\cdots\ge\lambda_n\geq -K$ and $\sigma_2(\lambda)=f$ with $f_0\leq f\leq f_1$ for two constants $f_1\geq f_0>0$.  Then there exists  $S_0 >0$ depending only on
$n$, $K$, $f_0$ and $f_1$ such that whenever $\sigma_1(\lambda)\geq S_0$, we have 
$$\frac{\sigma_1(\lambda)}{n}\leq  \lambda_1\leq \sigma_{1}(\lambda),$$
$$-K\leq\lambda_i  \leq n \frac{2(f_1+(n-1)^2K^2)}{S_0}+(n-2)K,\qquad i\geq2,$$
\begin{equation}
  \frac{f_0}{2\sigma_1(\lambda)}\leq  \sigma_{1;1}(\lambda)\leq  \frac{2n(f_1+(n-1)^2K^2)}{\sigma_1(\lambda)},
\end{equation}
$$\frac{1}{2}\sigma_1(\lambda)\leq \sigma_{1;i}(\lambda)\leq 2\sigma_1(\lambda),\qquad i\geq2.$$
In fact, we can take 
\begin{equation*}
  \begin{split}
    S_0&=\max \Big \{2n(n-1)K, \sqrt{\frac{n-2}{n-1} } \frac{2n(f_1+(n-1)^2K^2)}{\sqrt{f_0}},  \\
      & (n-2)K+\sqrt{4nf_1+(4n(n-1)^2+(n-2)^2)K^2}\Big \}.
  \end{split}
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:38.630212+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7ad76f5d54ccba77f42f348c9e5652c782c168dcf777b021fcd5ac2fe29a1cff","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 of arXiv:2506.17045, '\LARGE{On bivariate Archimax copulas: Level sets, mass distributions and related results}'] Let $\psi \in \mathbf{\Psi}$ be a non-strict generator, $A \in \mathcal{A}$, $C_{\psi,A} \in \mathcal{C}_{am}$, $\fg^0$ be defined as in eq. \eqref{eq:fct_g_t}, $R$ be defined according to eq. \eqref{eq:definition_L_R} and $g^R$ be defined as in eq. \eqref{eq:fct_f}. Then the following assertions hold:
