{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:37.368515+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7aebd1ad0e700bb4df056166dc3dd903719ef358c9a8442467b3b725346e65df","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 4 (Size-biased law) of arXiv:2606.18458, 'Stable size-biasing and the positive scale-mixture order of generalized Gaussian laws'] Let $Y\ge0$ satisfy $0<\E Y<\infty$. The $Y$-size-biased version $Y^*$ of $Y$ is the positive random variable whose law is defined by
\[
