Equivalently, by (equation eq:slope_with_or_without of the paper), $s$ is the slope per white vertex over all of $\mathbb{T}(n,\Lambda)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:13:22.527433+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7b0fef500ad2986ce12b3d557e12dbc889b8be2074180801b30abcfa3598041f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma le:Borel_Contelli of arXiv:2506.07158, 'The diffusivity of supercritical Bernoulli percolation is infinitely differentiable'] Let $B_n$ be a series of event satisfying 
