{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:57:30.959428+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7b28ce4504f8daa31d890f33fcc1caf300c8b982b57392146846842f8e15441b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2608.12070, 'Central limit theorems for a heavy-tailed subcritical Galton-Watson process with state-dep'] Suppose the process $\mathbf{X}=\{X_n:n\geq0\}$ is defined by \eqref{111} and satisfies {\bf (B)}. Then as $n\to \infty$,  
