{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.607885+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7b4334c6578773a0ecc98e48d92722ab74a967c48ce31f41822bc2e6e3464ee7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 18 of arXiv:2609.01358, 'Regularized spectral expansion of a Rankin--Selberg period and moments'] The term $I_2^{\mathrm{C}}(s)$, initially defined for large $\Re(s)$ in Proposition \ref{prop:before-meromorphic-continuation} admits a meromorphic continuation to the whole complex plane and, in a neighbourhood of $\Re(s)=0$, it is given by
