{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:24:45.893132+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7b54f41598b55b512b4625b5869231bca48a04c0314aa2606b6d8bc8dc3fd8ae","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary eq:continuous and discrete decomposition of M of arXiv:2509.02996, 'Group-averaged Markov chains: mixing improvement'] Assume $P\in \mathcal{S}(\pi)$. Let $G$ be any finite group acting on $\mathcal{X}$. Under Assumption (assum:pi and G of the paper), suppose the state space $\mathcal{X}$ is continuous, $\mathfrak{m}$ has no positive point mass, and $P$ has the form of (equation eq:continuous and discrete decomposition of P of the paper) with $A_{gx}=gA_x$, then for $M$ satisfying
