{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.590075+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7b9cfec8d31ea9bd10c03fa75b0bee158f301c35fdd3822f6ea5093570e27348","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Conjecture Belinsky, 1997 of arXiv:2608.30575, 'A Counterexample to Belinsky's Conjecture on Ces\`aro Means at Lebesgue Points'] Let $(a_k)$ be a convex increasing sequence of positive integers. Then
