{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:11.413310+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7ba7b55675bababa32b993d615f02c05b6773ba5f04f2adaa12f596a631b7068","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 12 of arXiv:2606.08115, '2606.08115'] For every vector $\ov{y}$ from the closure of the cone $MK$ and for every $\delta > 0$ there exists parameter $C = C\left(\ov{y}, \delta\right)$ such that for every $\ov{x} \in MK$ the inequality $\mathrm{dist}\left(\ov{x}, \partial MK\right) > \delta$ implies that
\begin{equation}

