{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:55:18.958516+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7bb3de2d5a86e5f9c0e8db7374f2bf000e0d7cbab1b528ea5cdb3b3b99a6d88f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Control by discrete anisotropic semi-norms of arXiv:2602.08591, 'The Yang--Mills measure on compact surfaces as a \\ universal scaling limit of lattice gau'] For all $N\geqslant 0$, we have 
    \[\|A_N\|_{\alpha;\beta}\leqslant \frac{12^{2p}}{2^{N(2-2ps)}}\sum_{\substack{0\leqslant n < m \leqslant 2^N-1\\0\leqslant k , l \leqslant 2^N-1}}\frac{\left\vert A_N(k2^{-N}\xrightarrow{m2^{-N}} l2^{-N})-A_N(k2^{-N}\xrightarrow{n2^{-N}} l2^{-N})\right\vert^p}{\vert l-k \vert ^{1+ps}(m-n)^{1+ps}}.\]

