{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:20.952559+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7bbe22ed6cf13185ce64d677bafd1f2ee9316a72e749267c794dd0d8b09458e0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 15 (Malliavin derivative estimates) of arXiv:2604.05234, 'Quantitative propagation of chaos and universality for asymmetric Langevin spin glass dyna'] Let $X$ be the unique strong solution to \eqref{eq: averaged dynamics 1}. Then $X \in \bbL^{1, 2}_T$ and there exists $C \in (0, \infty)$ depending only on $(A, \beta, T, C_{\textup{Lip}})$ such that for arbitrary $i=1,\dots,N$, 
