{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:07:48.565859+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7bde4d179ef18fdabc1c36e2406eec1330785f9ada2a73ebcd92f7b0bd0734fa","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 24 (Functional Santal\'o inequality for unconditional log-concave measures) of arXiv:2609.01460, 'On cost-induced Santal\'o-type inequalities \\ in Polish measure spaces'] Let $\mu$ be a probability measure on $\R^n$ with an unconditional, log-concave density with respect to Lebesgue measure. Let $f\in\mathcal{F}(\mathcal{K}_e^n)$ and let $g:\R^n\to\R_+$ be measurable. Suppose that $\Omega:\R_+\to\R_+$ is measurable and non-increasing and that
