{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:34.571717+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7bf35928c8441b0f16394548c902a5a81cb62aff8715a1008dd50a0e68dd3310","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 21 of arXiv:2606.14443, 'SEMICLASSICAL LIMIT OF POLYAKOV-LIOUVILLE MEASURE and Q-Curvature Uniformization ON EVEN-D'] Let $(\psi_j)_{j\in\N}$ be a complete $L^2$-orthonormal system consisting of eigenfunctions of~$\mathsf p$, each with corresponding eigenvalue~$\nu_j$. Let $(\xi_j)_{j\in \N}$ be a sequence  of independent and identically distributed standard Gaussian variables. For each~${\ell} \in \mathbb{N}$, we define the random test function
