{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:15.351688+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7bf701d0e343573c3da6bba56b9c124ae6de7c25e4a8b4e40e7744088260740a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 23 of arXiv:2506.15736, 'Coming down from infinity for coordinated particle systems'] Suppose a coordinated particle system $(X(t))_{t \geq 0}$ on a finite set of sites $V$ has no death and no reproduction. Assuming that $|X(t)| < \infty$, the expected rate of change in total number of particles at time $t$ is given by

    \begin{align*}
         \lim_{h \downarrow 0} \frac{1}{h}E\left[\sum_{v\in V} X_v(t+h) - X_v(t) \Big| X(t)\right]=-\sum_{v \in V} \psi_v(X_v(t)),
    \end{align*}

    \noindent where $\psi_v$ is the non-asymptotic processing speed of the $\Lambda_v$-coalescent.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:55.641221+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7bf8ae05297c4f680dc83fdb7d66e61c25c38e4017cb0df2d7cf0ac718c32e1a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 27 (Elimination and zero occupation on one face) of arXiv:2605.23529, 'Generalized Bessel-Dunkl diffusions'] Assume \ref{ass:k:dom} and \ref{ass:face:sign}. Let $S\in\mathfrak S$, and let
