and every connected component of \(C\) contains at least one endpoint.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:57:49.857953+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7c47ecab54db0f61f90771559507a97065ca7a063849b8868e8f0fec1e486710","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop ch5-p30 of arXiv:2410.23995, 'Sample path properties of parabolic SPDEs with non constant coefficients'] Let $\Gamma$ satisfy $({\bf H_\Lambda})$ and $({\bf \bar{H}_\Gamma})$.
 Let
$Z = (Z(t,x),\, (t,x)\in[0,T]\times D)
$ be a jointly measurable adapted process such that
\begin{equation*}
\sup_{(t,x)\in[0,T]\times D}E(|Z(t,x)|^p) < \infty.
\end{equation*}
Fix $\delta\in\left]0,\frac{1-\eta}{2}\right[$ and for $(t,x)\in [0,T]\times D$, define
\begin{equation}

Y_\delta(t,x) = \int_0^t \int_{D} \Gamma(t,x;s,y) (t-s)^{-\delta}Z(s,y) W(ds,dy).
\end{equation}
Then the stochastic process $(Y_\delta(t,x),\, (t,x)\in [0,T]\times D)$ is a well-defined jointly measurable adapted process such that, for any $p\in[2,\infty[$,
\begin{equation}

\sup_{(t,x)\in [0,T]\times D} E\left(\left\vert Y_\delta(t,x)\right\vert^p\right) < \infty.
\end{equation}
In addition, the following formula holds:
\begin{align}

&\int_0^t \int_{D} \Gamma(t,x;s,y)Z(s,y) W(ds,dy)\nonumber\\
&\qquad  = \frac{\sin(\pi\delta)}{\pi} \int_0^t ds\, (t-s)^{\delta-1}\int_{D} dy\,  \Gamma(t,x;s,y)\, Y_\delta(s,y).
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

