{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:37.355860+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7c491b703695436360e9feb5a985acd735bab88c320867ef3784d2c58d1168c2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 38 of arXiv:2606.17501, 'Critical spectral behavior and large deviations for geometric $\alpha$-stable processes'] Let $B(R)$ be the open ball of radius $R$ centered at the origin. 
  Let $C^{B(R)}(\theta)$ be the spectral function restricted to the open ball $B(R)$,
