Without loss of generality, we assume that $\varphi_p'(\cdot)\le \varphi_{p+1}'(\cdot)$ for $p \in \mathbb{N}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:28.478088+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7c5283dd6fc83a643c9e66c4f601880b94b943ca3d2642b45b314dad12455682","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 97 (Covariance--Gram identities) of arXiv:2606.29292, 'Intrinsic Gaussian Tensor Geometry and Random Operator Spectra'] Under the preceding assumptions,
\begin{equation}

 \norm K^2
 =\int_{X^2}
 \gamma(x,y)^mA(x,y)\conj{B(x,y)}
 \,d\mu(x)d\mu(y).
\end{equation}
In particular, the integral is real and nonnegative.

Let $J_j:\cH\to\cH_j$ identify $\cH$ with labelled copies and set
$\widetilde K=\Dec_mK$.  For $S\subset[m]$, $k=|S|$, define
\[
 h_{S,x}:=\bigotimes_{j\in S}J_j\eta_x,\qquad
 h_{S^c,x}:=\bigotimes_{j\in S^c}J_j\eta_x,
\]
\[
 d_{S,x}:=\conj{h_{S,x}}\otimes b_x,\qquad
 u_{S,x}:=h_{S^c,x}\otimes a_x.
\]
The synthesis operators
\begin{align}
 U_S:L^2(X)&\to\cH_{S^c}\otimes\cE,
 &U_Sf&:=\int_Xf(x)u_{S,x}\,d\mu(x),\\
 V_S:L^2(X)&\to\conj{\cH_S}\otimes\cC,
 &V_Sf&:=\int_Xf(x)d_{S,x}\,d\mu(x)
\end{align}
are Hilbert--Schmidt and, up to canonical tensor permutations,
\begin{equation}

 \Flat_S(\widetilde K)=U_SV_S^*.
\end{equation}
Their vector-valued Gram kernels are
\begin{align}
 \ip{u_{S,x}}{u_{S,y}}
 &=\gamma(x,y)^{m-k}A(x,y),\\
 \ip{d_{S,x}}{d_{S,y}}
 &=\conj{\gamma(x,y)}^{\,k}B(x,y).
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.363398+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7c56d939705e4570b5307508536c12e536007563f1cadce0d9268f8383da4f00","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:phi-x of arXiv:2412.01645, 'Regularisation by Gaussian rough path lifts of fractional Brownian motions'] There exist constants $C=C(H_-,\| \sigma\|_{\mathcal{C}^2})$ and $q=q(H_-)$ such that for all $(s,t) \in [0, 1]^2_{\leq}$, $x \in {\mathbb{R}}^d$,  we have 
