{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:58.449577+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7c5dc1bbf6cd4c948762ac7b7b66b1f178dd41cf52783b871c16dbc4c78f8996","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop.prop2.9 of arXiv:2604.24743, 'The impact of disorder and non-convex interactions on delocalisation of height functions'] Let $k \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{N}}$. Given an edge $\{ y, z\} \in E$, we denote by $\widetilde G$ the graph obtained by adding $k$ new vertices on the edge $yz$ (see Figure~(fig:addingvertices of the paper)). We denote by $\widetilde J$ the collection of conductances on the graph $\widetilde G$ defined as follows:
\begin{itemize}
