{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:06:42.719428+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7caa7ee084b1fedc6c569ebadba88627f7c3b545725a39e480b74bdf252f4063","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition l:dotprodbound of arXiv:2411.04116, 'Poisson genericity in numeration systems with exponentially mixing probabilities'] Let $X_1,X_2,\dots $ a sequence of random variables defined on $(\mathbb X, \mathcal{F},\mathbb P)$ taking values on alphabet $\Omega$. Let   $\Delta$ be the matrix of $\eta$-mixing coefficients with $\|\Delta\|<\infty$.  Let $c=(c_i)_{i\ge 1}\in \ell^2$ and $\varphi:\Omega^\mathbb N \to \mathbb R$ 
