{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:32.011390+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7ce10c09d82af17a895f65dcb2e7081272f61224268a6376ddc6d44b6acc1250","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 19 (\cite{Pommerenke}, Theorem 3.7) of arXiv:2512.02855, 'Loewner--Kufarev entropy and large deviations of the Hastings--Levitov model'] Let $f:\Delta\to D$ be conformal and $\partial D$ be locally connected. Then    $f(\partial\Delta)$ has a cusp at $f(1)\neq \infty$ if and only if 
