{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:07.297730+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7ce30cbb5fe699f10c2cb7d873aaf9112d513e336b2868ba33d91d8af6db0a0f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 (Theorem~2.3 in \cite{forien_stepping_2019}) of arXiv:2606.23242, 'Correction to ``The stepping stone model in a random environment'' - limit theorems for th'] Fix $ T > 0 $ and assume that $ \xi^n_0 $ is deterministic and converges to $ x_0 \in \R $.
