{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.358634+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7d147b53c09e21e7a571b6f7f4719644b25716a661fed94cfa95d942fbf46ebf","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem.vinf.convex of arXiv:2605.14149, 'The mean-field limit of online stochastic vector balancing'] For each $t_0 \in [0,1]$, $\mathcal{V}^{\infty}(t_0,\cdot)$ is $L$-convex, meaning that for any square-integrable random variables $X_0,X_0'$ defined on some common probability space $(\Omega, \mathcal{F}, \mathbb{P})$, we have
    \begin{align*}
        \mathcal{V}^{\infty}\Big(t_0, \mathcal{L}\big(\lambda X_0 + (1-\lambda) X'_0 \big) \Big) \leq \lambda \mathcal{V}^{\infty}\big(t_0,\mathcal{L}(X_0)\big) + (1-\lambda) \mathcal{V}^{\infty}\big(t_0,\mathcal{L}(X'_0)\big),
    \end{align*}
    for $0 \leq \lambda \leq 1$. Moreover, $\mathcal{V}^{\infty}(t_0,\cdot)$ is even, in the sense that
    \begin{align*}
        \mathcal{V}^{\infty}(t_0, \mathcal{L}(X_0)) = \mathcal{V}^{\infty}\big(t_0,\mathcal{L}(-X_0)\big).
    \end{align*}
    As a consequence, $\mathcal{V}^{\infty}(t_0,\cdot)$ obtains a global minimum at $\delta_0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.989696+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7d169c4e822e22300a2743fe0ac2224d77ee90b12ae04a1d638e1b8632dc25da","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 84 (Rayleigh’s monotonicity principle) of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] Let $\weight, \weight'$ be weights on $G$ with $\weight(e) \leq \weight'(e)$ for all edges $e \in E$. If $A,B \subset V$ are two disjoint sets, then
