{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:18:19.198842+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7d1935a3976a0d33ab6170bf7e4821108fdab7654bbafc0900ae483f89bbc10d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Maintheorem 1 of arXiv:2608.28964, '2608.28964'] For the equation \eqref{eq NS},\eqref{eq xi} with $\xi=\eta^{s}$ given by \eqref{eq eta_s}, and any $B_0>0$, there exists an integer $N=N(B_0)\in\N^+$ such that the following holds. If $\{b_j\}_{j\in\N^+}$ satisfies
