{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:19:56.699905+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7df06b74550654b3008cadfb50ad67e2ad34c7565641f9b562b10d03a8f78fb2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 30 (Inverse Function Theorem) of arXiv:2608.30990, 'Convergence of symmetries: nilpotency, dimension, and perfectness'] Let $U \subset \mathbb{R}^n $ be an open set and $\Theta : U \to \mathbb{R}^n$ a differentiable function with  $\Theta ( 0 ) = 0 $ and 
