and $\widetilde{T}_n=S_n\wedge \widetilde{S}_n,\;n\in \mathbf{N}^+$. In this case, we say that the expression of \eqref{HM-expression-2} is independent of the choice of the FCS $(T_n, H^{(n)})$ for $H\in\mathcal{P}^\mathbb{B}$ and the inner FCS $(T_n,M^{(n)})$ for $M\in(\mathcal{M}_{\mathrm{loc}})^{i,\mathbb{B}}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:44:17.169165+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7df82f7d163da860130ee67a2c5baf1624ef322ebf97652026dc05d7627a9673","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2604.18871, 'Quantitative approximation of the Vlasov(--Fokker--Planck)--Navier--Stokes system by stoch'] With the same assumptions and notations as in Theorem~\ref{th:convBessel},
assuming further that $\sup_{t\in[0,T]} \big\| m_0(F_t) \big\|_{L^\infty_{x}}$ is finite, the following holds:

\begin{itemize}
\item If $\sigma>0$, then for any $q\in [1,+\infty)$, there exists $C = C(q,d,\gamma,p,A,\sigma)>0$ such that for any $N\in \N^*$,
\begin{align*}
\Big(\E & \sup_{t\in[0,T]} \big\|u^{N}_t-u_t \big\|_{L^2_{x}}^{2q}\Big)^{\frac{1}{q}} + \Big(\E \Big|\int_{0}^{T} \big\| \nabla (u_{s}^{N}- u_{s}) \big\|_{L^2_{x}}^{2} \dd s \Big|^{q}\Big)^{\frac{1}{q}}\\
& \leq C \bigg( \big(\E \big\| u^{\circ,N}-u^\circ \big\|_{\gamma, p}^{2q}\big)^{\frac{1}{q}} +   \big(\E \big\| \langle v \rangle^{k} (F_{0}^{N}-\vartheta^N\ast F^\circ) \big\|_{L^{2}_{x,v}}^{2q}\big)^{\frac{1}{q}}\\
&\quad + N^{-2(\alpha-\beta)} +N^{-2\beta(\gamma-\frac{d}{p})} + N^{-(\frac{1}{2} - d\beta -(d+1)\alpha)} + \ratetilde^2 \bigg) + C \rate^2 .
\end{align*}

\item If $\sigma=0$, then for any $q\in [1,+\infty)$ and any $\varepsilon>0$, there exists $C = C(q,d,\gamma,p,A,\varepsilon)>0$ such that for any $N\in \N^*$,
\begin{align*}
\Big(\E & \sup_{t\in[0,T]} \big\|u^{N}_t-u_t \big\|_{L^2_{x}}^{2q}\Big)^{\frac{1}{q}} + \Big(\E \Big|\int_{0}^{T} \big\| \nabla (u_{s}^{N}- u_{s}) \big\|_{L^2_{x}}^{2} \dd s \Big|^{q}\Big)^{\frac{1}{q}} \\
& \leq C \bigg( \big(\E \big\| u^{\circ,N}-u^\circ \big\|_{\gamma, p}^{2q}\big)^{\frac{1}{q}} +   \big(\E \big\| \langle v \rangle^{k} (F_{0}^{N}-\vartheta^N\ast F^\circ) \big\|_{L^{2}_{x,v}}^{2q}\big)^{\frac{1}{q}} +\ratetilde^2 \\
&\quad + N^{-2(\alpha-\beta)} + N^{-2\beta(\gamma-\frac{d}{p})+\varepsilon} + N^{-(\frac{1}{2} - d\beta -(d+1)\alpha)}
\bigg) \, \frac{1}{1-\tilde\gamma} e^{CT\big(1+\sigma_{N}^{-2} + \sigma_{N}^{-\frac{1}{1-\tilde\gamma}}\big)}
 + C \rate^2.
\end{align*}

\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:52:47.257742+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7df8636797d1fc90af7d5988058ef550e9be164ae23de47408c59fe5a209269c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Coro 2 (Case of $\Rr^d$) of arXiv:2609.01105, 'Obstruction to quasi-invariance of Gaussian measures under transport flows on Riemannian M'] Assume that~\((M,g)\) is the Euclidean space $\Rr^d$ equipped with the flat metric. Then the following statements are equivalent: 
\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
    \item Gaussian measure $\mu_\alpha$ is quasi-invariant under the flow of \eqref{eq:transport}; 
    \item Gaussian measure $\mu_{\alpha}$ is invariant under the flow of \eqref{eq:transport}, that is, for all $t \in \mathbb{R}$ there holds $\mu_\alpha^t = \mu_{\alpha}$;
    \item vector field $u$ is of the form $u(t,x)=a(t) x + b(t)$ for some $a \in L^1_{\rm loc}(\mathbb{R},A_d(\mathbb{R}))$, where~\(A_d(\Rr)\) is the set of skew-symmetric matrices, and $b \in L^1_{\rm loc}(\mathbb{R},\mathbb{R}^d)$.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:40:22.388763+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7df9ded94b43d3695d7caf7f1bd281e056e5083db506ba757ad3cb31d4a88348","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lem-subspace of arXiv:2506.18827, 'Random walk reflected off of infinity, with applications to uniform spanning forests and s'] Fix a finite, non-empty set $\mathcal A\subset\mathcal V\mathcal G$. 
Let
\begin{equation} 
  \mathring\Theta_{\mathcal A}  := \mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft\{ \theta \in \Theta : \text{$\theta = \nabla f$ for some $f : \mathcal V\mathcal G \to \mathbbm R$ with $f|_{\mathcal A} \equiv 0$} \aftergroup\egroup\originalright\} . 
\end{equation} 
Then $\mathring\Theta_{\mathcal A}$ is a closed linear subspace of $\Theta$. The orthogonal complement $\mathring\Theta_{\mathcal A}^\perp$ is described as follows. We say that $\eta \in \Theta$ is an \textbf{cycle modulo $\mathcal A$} if there exists a path $P : [0,N]\cap\mathbbm Z \to\mathcal V\mathcal G$ such that either $P(0) = P(N)$ or $P(0) , P(N) \in \mathcal A$ with the following property. For each $e = (x,y) \in \overrightarrow{\mathcal E}\mathcal G$, $\eta(e)$ is equal to the number of times $i$ such that $(P(i-1) ,P(i)) = (x,y)$ minus the number of times $i$ such that $(P(i-1), P(i)) = (y,x)$. Then $\mathring\Theta_{\mathcal A}^\perp$ is the closure of the linear span of the set of cycles modulo $\mathcal A$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.401988+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7df9fa04b7b9c5272b63cd9e055f9b5632f042199689cbee8902e654a505e26c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: BlockDiagonalDecomposition of arXiv:2603.26932, 'On the satisfaction frequency of spectral characterization conditions'] Consider a matrix $\bM \in \sO^{n\times n}$ that is symmetric, $\bM = \bM^{\T}$. 
    Then, for every $k\leq n$, it holds that $\rank_q(\bM) = n-k$ if and only if there exists invertible $\bG \in \operatorname{GL}_n(\sO)$ such that 
    \begin{align}
        \bG^{\T}\bM\bG = \begin{pmatrix}
            \bQ & 0 \\ 
            0 & \bK
        \end{pmatrix}
    \end{align}
    for some symmetric $\bK \in \mathfrak{m}^{k\times k}$ and invertible symmetric $\bQ \in \operatorname{GL}_{n-k}(\sO)$.","status":"unverified"}

