{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:38.363302+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7dfcc6f2e8580a880f8119797444eef34e2e2ebe4f1a07fda28e2c7435ce9e45","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 21 (Mixing) of arXiv:2604.21669, 'Discontinuous transition in 2D Potts:\\ II. order-order interface convergence'] Let \(0<J<U\) satisfy \(\sinh 2J=e^{-2U}\). There exist \(c,C\in (0,+\infty)\) such that for any \(n,m_n\geq 1\), \(F\subset F'\subset \bbE_{n-1,m_n-1}\), and any events \(A\) supported on edges in \(F\), and \(B\) supported on the edges of \((F')^c\),
	\begin{equation*}
		\Big|\frac{\Phi_n(A\given B)}{\Phi(A)} -1 \Big|\leq C \sum_{e\in F} e^{-c\rmd(e,(F')^c)},
	\end{equation*}as soon as the R.H.S. is less than \(0.1\).
	In particular, for any dual simple path \(\gamma^*\) from \(v_L'\) to \(v_R'\) using only edges in \(*\FVEdges_n\), any \(F\subset\gamma'_{\shortuparrow}\cap \bbE_{n-1,m_n-1}\), and any event \(A\) supported on edges in \(F\),
	\begin{equation*}
		\Big|\frac{\Phi_n^{\gamma'}(A)}{\Phi(A)} -1 \Big|\leq C \sum_{e\in F} e^{-c\rmd(e,(\bbE_{n,m_n}\setminus (\gamma'\cup \gamma'_{\shortdownarrow}))^c)},
	\end{equation*}as soon as the R.H.S. is less than \(0.1\). The equivalent claim holds for \(\Phi_n^{\gamma}\) with a path \(\gamma\) from \(v_L\) to \(v_R\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:51:52.062122+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7dfd27b90ca42011367e6bdb8b02d1906bce8afaf4d3941b1a145f066050f008","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:OSSS of arXiv:2607.14993, 'Sharp phase transition for percolation with short-range dependencies'] Let $\mu$ be a monotonic\footnote{See [gri06] for the definition and properties of monotonic measures. A measure is monotonic if and only if it has the FKG property.} measure on $\{0, 1\}^E$ where $E$ is finite. Let $T$ be a decision tree computing an increasing random variable $f$. Then
