{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.054778+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7e11c42d184df752a68e94bcf880e6fa859e4a41e203118bf2863b32fedc770c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 5 of arXiv:2607.01629, 'Quadratic fluctuations of speed-change Kawasaki dynamics'] \begin{enumerate}
			\item \cite[Proposition 4.3 (1)]{gu2025relaxation}:
			The local corrector $\phi_L^z$ is a local function and  $\F_{(\Lambda_L^z)^-}$-measurable.
