			\end{align*}
		\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:48:00.299248+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7e13859db277e00ab6c0e2cd4f880fbf4b9f69e20c995ed50dc3c4f2c33268c3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop curious CY4 vanishing virt classes of arXiv:2609.03152, 'Experiments with membranes, maps and sheaves'] Suppose, there are divisors $D_1,D_2$ with zero-dimensional intersection $D_1\cap D_2$ satisfying $\cL_i = \cO_S(-D_i)$, $i\in\{1,2\}$. Further suppose that $D_2$ is a smooth curve. Let $\Gm$ act trivially on $X$ and with opposite weights $\pm\epsilon$ on the fibres of $\cL_2$ and $\cO_S$. Then for all effective curve classes $\beta$ with $\cL_i \cdot \beta < 0$, $i\in\{1,2\}$, we have
