{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.896433+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7e2c5e1ee8c027d434f9d25b28d86814bc5c463301a60b0245ee143cd0cccb9c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 48 of arXiv:2508.04938, 'Perfect t-embeddings of doubly periodic Aztec diamonds'] Let~$(\xi, \eta) \in [-1,1]^2$ denote macroscopic points in the Aztec diamond. The \emph{action function} is given, for~$q = (z, w) \in \mathcal{R}$, by
