{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:16:53.620015+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7e5f49567bba6699347d650ca094145bdbb9b57325fba0dffda1b8585e1f8cb3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:S of arXiv:2412.05491, 'Near-critical and finite-size scaling for \\ high-dimensional lattice trees and animals'] Let $d>2$,
$\eta >0$,
$L \ge L_2$,
and $z\in [\frac{1}{2},1)$.
Then
\begin{align} 
m_S(z)^2 \sim \frac{2d}{\sigma_L^2} (1-z)
	\qquad \text{as $z\to 1$,}
\end{align}
and there are constants $K_S > 0$, $a_S \in (0,1)$ (independent of $L$)
and $\delta_2 = \delta_2(L) > 0$ such that
\begin{equation} 
