{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:40:26.991794+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7e7f5a222d5e2e73bc27ce1b74cae93e6389c6d23e89fd2686f0ba6a382e0550","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem-expnumbershreds of arXiv:2604.14318, '\large The free energy of the interacting Bose gas:\\\medskip a variational description \\'] There is a $C\in(0,\infty)$ such that, for any $P\in{\mathcal M }_1^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({\rm s}})}}}({\mathcal S })$, and for any $R\in\mathbb{N}$,
