{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:37:08.953219+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7e80438c9e6f10eca9fb99249a2eeec48ce5d0461f994aa37a5f55c269f68502","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:empirical_current of arXiv:2609.01581, 'Concentration of additive functionals of Stratonovich-type'] For a bounded, continuously differentiable vector field with bounded
derivatives, $U\in C^1_b(\mathbb{R}^d;\mathbb{R}^d)$, the \emph{current-type functional} (or empirical
current) is the Stratonovich integral
\begin{align}
  \overline{J}_t(U)
  \equiv \frac{1}{t}\int_0^t U(X_s)\circ\mathrm{d} X_s,

\end{align}
with $J_t(U)=t\overline{J}_t(U)$ the corresponding time-accumulated observable,
where $\circ$ denotes Stratonovich integration and $U(X_s)\circ\mathrm{d} X_s=\sum_i U_i(X_s)\circ\mathrm{d} X^i_s$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:00:30.502206+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7e8399b419ff07e081353200c7c376f4bace64ac1bf46a6ca1294914d8ecf548","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 10 of arXiv:2607.04730, 'Variance gamma approximation to sums of triplewise independent random variables'] Let $X_i$ and $Y_i$ be two rvs as defined in \eqref{def:X_i,Y_i}. Then
    \begin{equation}
 \mathbb{E} [X_i^{3}]=\mathbb{E} [Y_i^{3}] = \frac{1 - \frac{2}{l}}{\sqrt{\frac{m}{l}(1-\frac{1}{l})}}, \qquad l\ge 2 .       
    \end{equation}
    \noindent Moreover, 

    \begin{align}
\mathbb{E} [|X_i^{3}|]= \mathbb{E} [|Y_i^{3}|] \leq \sqrt{\frac{l}{m}}, \qquad l\ge 2.
    \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:32:19.921309+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7e8645d7bbe07318dc10fd8e2f7a0eaf630031284422f99f939ce65522be0dd7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2608.02927, 'Thinning Operation via the Poisson-F\"ollmer Process'] [Harrem\"oes, Johnson and Kontoyiannis \cite{HJK1}] 
If $T=\E X$ and $H(X|\pi_{T}) < \infty,$ then 
\begin{displaymath}

    H \Big( \sum_{i=1}^{n} T_{1/n}(X_{i}) \big| \pi_{T} \Big) \longrightarrow 0 
\end{displaymath}
as $n\rightarrow \infty,$ where $(X_{i})_{i \ge 1}$ iid copies of $X.$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:35:04.168701+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7e8903937a4c6ced047b2b163fc76e002a8542a631844328a1423135a2284a68","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:small-doubling of arXiv:2609.00399, 'Shannon's problem on the monotonicity of entropy and a Conjecture of Tao'] Let $X_1,X_2,\ldots$ be i.i.d.\ finitely supported variables in an abelian
group, and retain the notation above.  Let $n\geq1$ and $C\geq0$.  If
$d_n\leq C$ and $Q=S_n$, then, for an independent copy $Q'$ of $Q$,
\begin{equation}
 H(Q+Q')-H(Q)\leq nC,
 \qquad
 \exp\{H(Q+Q')-H(Q)\}\leq e^{nC}.
\end{equation}
Moreover, $H(Q)\geq H(X_1)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:38:58.702732+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7e8b2d07f4a7f4bfb84e80778e46228cead22e91dc33c6882cfc6af6f51fd35b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:transition of arXiv:2510.22778, 'Free denoising diffusion models'] Let $\rho=\tfrac12(\delta_{-a}+\delta_{a})$ and $\nu=\rho\boxplus\gamma_{v}$, $v>0$.
Then $\supp\nu$ is the union of two disjoint intervals if $v<a^{2}$ and a single
interval if $v\ge a^{2}$. The critical variance is
\begin{equation}
  v^{*}=a^{2}.
\end{equation}
