{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:47.658136+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7e8c5adc7cd22c0a565532774b64d2d72e87f06a872441e402c3aa6bf9566828","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 (Moderate Deviation Principle) of arXiv:2605.08629, 'Moderate deviations for the Maki--Thompson rumour model'] Assume \eqref{bn-condition}, then the sequence $\{Z_n\}_{n\ge 1}$ satisfies a moderate deviation principle with speed $b_n^2$ and rate function
    \begin{equation}
        J(x) = \frac{x^2}{2\sigma^2}, \quad x\in\mathbb{R},
    \end{equation}
    where $\sigma^2$ is given by \eqref{eq-sigma2}. That is, for every Borel set $B\subset\mathbb{R}$,
    \begin{align}
        -\inf_{x\in B^\circ} J(x) &\le \liminf_{n\to\infty} \frac{1}{b_n^2}\log\mathbb{P}(Z_n \in B) \notag \\
        &\le \limsup_{n\to\infty} \frac{1}{b_n^2}\log\mathbb{P}(Z_n \in B)
        \le -\inf_{x\in \overline{B}} J(x),
    \end{align}
    where $B^\circ$ and $\overline{B}$ denote the interior and closure of $B$, respectively. In particular, for any $z>0$,
    \begin{equation}
        \lim_{n\to\infty} \frac{1}{b_n^2}\log\mathbb{P}\bigl(|Z_n| \ge z\bigr) = -\frac{z^2}{2\sigma^2}.
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

