{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:09:43.676620+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7eae4a92c9566744544720b3648a9c73dd37b54dd0b2f309470cb4968bc4c8f0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem SMR-finite time-delayed blow-up of arXiv:2605.28194, 'Delayed Blow-up in 3D Fluids via Pseudo-Transport Noise'] Let $a\in [-1,0)\text{ and }2b+a>-\frac{1}{2}$. Fix $T>0, \frac{4}{2(2b+a)+1}<p<\infty$,
