{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:38:23.614761+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7f251648e1b07c718509b35479b09b616a095a36912b4efe680a2dc415dc1752","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop EHI:p:h1 of arXiv:2511.08956, '\textbf{Towards a characterization of elliptic Harnack inequality for jump processes}'] Let $X$ be an isotropic unimodal L\'{e}vy jump process on $\mathbb{R}^d$. If (equation EHI:e:regularJumps of the paper) holds for all $r>0$, then for all $L>1$, there exists a constant $C_{(EHI:p:h1 of the paper)}(L, c_j)$ (depending on $L$ and $c_j$) such that for all $r_0>0$, $r \in (0, Lr_0]$, $x \in B(0, r)$, and $w \in B(0, r)^c$, we have
