Then, $a_n^{-1/2}M_n\xrightarrow{d} \mathcal{N}(0,\Lambda)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.625265+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7f2fae44b35c9c30d546f2109b960554357fdb83ca8d65f39f9b35b3a4752371","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary Coro: 0127 of arXiv:2411.03512, 'Ergodicity and Mixing of Sublinear Expectation System and Applications'] Let $\{X_t\}_{t\geq 0}$ (resp. $\{X_k\}_{k\geq 0}$) be a d-dimensional $\alpha$-mixing identical process (resp. sequence) on a sublinear expectation space $(\Omega,\mathcal{H},\hat{\mathbb{E}})$ such that $\hat{\mathbb{E}}[|X_0|^{1+\beta}]<\infty$ for some $\beta\in (0,1]$ and $v\in C_b^{1,1+\beta}(\mathbb{R}_+\times \mathbb{R}^d)$ be the solution to equation (equation PDE of the paper) with $p(a)=\hat{\mathbb{E}}[\langle a, X_0\rangle]$. Assume that $\{t_k\}_{k\geq 1}$ (resp. $\{m_k\}_{k\geq 1}$) is a $(\gamma,\delta)$-admissible subsequence for some $0<\gamma<1, \delta>0$ and set
		\begin{equation*}
			Y_k:=X_{t_k} \ (resp. \ Y_k:=X_{m_k}),  \ \ S^Y_n=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^nY_i.
		\end{equation*}
		Then for $n\geq N_0$, we have
		\begin{equation}
			\begin{split}
				v(1,0)-\hat{\mathbb{E}}[\phi(S^Y_n)]&\geq 
				-C(c_1,\gamma,\beta)n^{-\beta}\int_0^1|\nabla_xv(s,\cdot)|_{\beta}ds\times \hat{\mathbb{E}}[|X_0|^{1+\beta}]\\
				&\ \ \ \ -c_X|\nabla_xv|_{\infty}ne^{-\alpha c_2(\ln n)^{1+\delta}}-2c_1l_{\phi}n^{-(1-\gamma)}\hat{\mathbb{E}}[|X_0|]+\underline{f},
			\end{split}
		\end{equation}
  where  $c_X,c_1,c_2$ are from (equation equ: alpha-mixing of the paper), (equation eq:admissible of the paper),
		$\underline{f}=\inf_{\{0\leq t\leq 1,x\in \mathbb{R}^d\}}f(t,x)
	$ with $f$ defined as in (equation PDE of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

