{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:00:46.830550+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7f5bd9fc298847cd7fce04667839efbe86e9bf7ee5e22044a19dee7872e860e6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 7 of arXiv:2608.13358, 'Extreme points of sets of probability measures and $\phi$-divergences'] Let $\Omega$ be finite and $\cF$ be the power set.\
    \begin{enumerate}
    \item[a)] There exists a measure $q\in \cM$ with $p'\ll q$ for all $p'\in \cM$.
