    }","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:14:46.351759+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7f78d578ecbf3411a3fd9bc97782d7c115fe7788a2dde0a59be8e740850e1f0c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:hybrid-gap of arXiv:2608.10184, 'The sharp SAT/UNSAT phase transition in random ellipsoid fitting'] There are constants $e_\gamma,c_\gamma>0$, depending only on $\gamma$, such that for every $0\le r\le k_d$, with
