{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:33:43.748464+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7fa558004e5576be20a6c8df29cf9acc818118569451885eb24a1e8c097df65a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:permutation-nilpotent of arXiv:2608.28169, 'characteristic polynomial of self-normalized random matrices'] Let ${\mathbf Y}_n^{(0)}$ be a one-hot matrix. Then, up to conjugation by permutation matrices, ${\mathbf Y}_n^{(0)}$ admits the decomposition in upper triangular form  
    \begin{equation*}
        {\mathbf Y}_n^{(0)} = \begin{pmatrix}
            N & * \\
            0 & P
        \end{pmatrix}\,,
