{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:14:46.348624+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7fc06185b950085761a41a24752c225e046ba766dd275c84d3815cc3574fd4f9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:heads of arXiv:2608.10184, 'The sharp SAT/UNSAT phase transition in random ellipsoid fitting'] Fix $C_0<\infty$ and set $K_d=\lfloor C_0d\log d\rfloor$.  With probability tending to one, simultaneously for every $J\subseteq[n]$ with
$|J|\le K_d$,
\begin{equation}
w\bigl(\mathcal{K}_{\kappa_1}\cap\ker\mathcal{W}_J\cap\mathbb{S}_{\mathrm{F}}\bigr)
\ge w\bigl(\mathcal{K}_{\kappa_0}\cap\mathbb{S}_{\mathrm{F}}\bigr)-o(d)
\ge(\sqrt\alpha+3\eta)d.
