{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.568062+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7fc94de46f24c475f003407dca3e6f103ce42f1a8964fe00d0125de3326f7358","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2412.03366, 'Regularity of Weighted Tensorized Fractional Brownian Fields and associated function space'] For  $s\in (0,1)$ and $\alpha \in [0,1]$, we define the  weighted tensorized H\"older space $T^{s, \alpha}C(\mathbb{R}^2)$ as the space of functions $f: \mathbb{R}^2 \to \mathbb{R}$ of $L^{\infty}(\mathbb{R})$ such that there is $c>0$ with
    \begin{align*}
&|f(x_1+h_1,x_2+h_2)- f(x_1, x_2+h_2) - f(x_1+h_1,x_2)+ f(x_1,x_2)| \\
& \hspace{6cm} \leq c \, \min\{|h_1|,|h_2| \}^{(1+\alpha)s} \max\{|h_1|,|h_2| \}^{(1-\alpha)s},
    \end{align*}
    and 
$$|f(x_1+h_1,x_2)- f(x_1,x_2)| \leq c \, |h_1|^{(1+\alpha)s} \quad \text{and} \quad |f(x_1,x_2+h_2)-  f(x_1,x_2)| \leq c \,  |h_2|^{(1+\alpha)s}$$
for all $x_1,x_2,h_1,h_2 \in \mathbb{R}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:31.957630+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7fceafc6b7c540c27fa8b6b982dc337d2a0e0349f9921aed7c6134b1c544b52f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 3 (Theorem~\ref{thm:cond prob Fredholm pf empty} in the main text) of arXiv:2512.02286, 'Pfaffian Transition Probability and Correlation Kernel of TASEP in Half-space'] Let $N>0$ be a fixed even integer. Let $\Psi(x,y)=Q_{1,1}(x,y)$ with $Q$ defined in \eqref{eq:Qintro}, and let $\Phi_0(x),\dots,\Phi_{N-1}(x)$ be a family of polynomials where $\Phi_k$ is of degree $k$. Assume that these polynomials satisfy the following skew-biorthogonality relations:
    \begin{align}
        \begin{split}
            \sum_{x,y=1}^\infty \Phi_{2i}(x) \Psi(x,y) \Phi_{2j}(y) & = 0, \\
            \sum_{x,y=1}^\infty \Phi_{2i+1}(x) \Psi(x,y) \Phi_{2j+1}(y) & = 0, \\
            \sum_{x,y=1}^\infty \Phi_{2i}(x) \Psi(x,y) \Phi_{2j+1}(y) & = -\delta_{i,j},
        \end{split}
    \end{align}
    for all $0\leq i,j< N/2$. Furthermore, for a fixed integer $m\geq 0$, let $\{p_1,\dots,p_m\}\subseteq\{1,\dots,N\}$ be indices denoting particle labels such that $p_1<p_2<\cdots<p_m$. Then the half-line TASEP with empty initial conditions has conditional joint distribution given by a Fredholm Pfaffian of the form
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{P}\left[\bigcap_{k=1}^m \left\{X_{t}(p_k) > a_k\right\} \given \abs{X_t} = N\right] = \pf\left(J - \bar\chi_a K\bar\chi_a\right)_{\ell^2(\{p_1,\dots,p_m\}\times \mathbb{N})},
    \end{equation}
    where $\bar\chi_a(p,x) = \mathbbm{1}_{x\leq a_p}$ and $a_1,\dotsc,a_k\geq0$. The correlation kernel $K$ is given explicitly in terms of the $\Phi_{i}(x)$ polynomials in Section~\ref{se:EmptyIC}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:02:08.132981+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7fcee8544cf53d04e7f1a7a1b7e9c6a6df1695676bf9654aff82f68e08da6147","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2608.27569, 'Laplace and Dolbeault operators on Sasakian manifolds'] Let $(M^{2n+1},g,\xi )$ be a compact Sasakian
manifold. For $0\leq r,s\leq n$ and $t\in \{0,1\}$, let $H_{\overline{
\partial }}^{r,s,t}\left( M\right) $, respectively $H_{\partial
}^{r,s,t}\left( M\right) $, be the cohomology groups defined by
\begin{equation*}
H_{\overline{\partial }}^{r,s,t}\left(M\right) =\frac{\ker(\overline{
\partial }:\Omega ^{r,s,t}\rightarrow \Omega ^{r,s+1,t})}{\limfunc{im}
(\overline{\partial }:\Omega ^{r,s-1,t}\rightarrow \Omega ^{r,s,t})},~\text{
respectively }H_{\partial }^{r,s,t}\left( M\right) =\frac{\ker (\partial
:\Omega ^{r,s,t}\rightarrow \Omega ^{r+1,s,t})}{\limfunc{im}(\partial :\Omega
^{r-1,s,t}\rightarrow \Omega ^{r,s,t})}.
\end{equation*}
Then the natural map $\Omega^{r,s,t}\to  H_{\bullet
}^{r,s,t}\left( M\right); \omega \mapsto \left[ \omega \right] $ induces isomorphisms 
\begin{eqnarray*}
