all of which are finite dimensional. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:06:07.076354+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7fd34367484698b497275617f2c99df5034a8ecab0d7090b6e79640fc456f483","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 (Multivariate hard-edge determinant field) of arXiv:2608.27641, 'Hard-Edge Determinant Fields and Second-Moment Universality for Random Matrix Ratios'] Under the assumptions above, there exists a random element
\[
Q_{\boldsymbol{\Sigma}}
\in
\operatorname{Hol}\left(\mathbb{C}^r\right)
\]
such that
\begin{equation}
Q_{\boldsymbol{\Sigma}}^{[K]}
\overset{\mathbb{P}}{\rightarrow}
Q_{\boldsymbol{\Sigma}}
\quad
\text{in }
\operatorname{Hol}\left(\mathbb{C}^r\right),
\qquad
Q_n
\overset{\mathrm{d}}{\rightarrow}
Q_{\boldsymbol{\Sigma}}
\quad
\text{in }
\operatorname{Hol}\left(\mathbb{C}^r\right).

\end{equation}
Moreover,
\(
Q_{\boldsymbol{\Sigma}}\left(\boldsymbol{0}\right)=1
\text{ almost surely}.
\)

For every nonzero
\(\boldsymbol{v}\in\mathbb{C}^r\), define
\[
\sigma_{\boldsymbol{v}}^2
:=
\boldsymbol{v}^\top
\boldsymbol{\Sigma}
\overline{\boldsymbol{v}}.
\]
Then \(\sigma_{\boldsymbol{v}}>0\), and
\begin{equation}
Q_{\boldsymbol{\Sigma}}
\left(\,\cdot\,\boldsymbol{v}\right)
\overset{\mathrm{d}}{=}
Q\left(
\sigma_{\boldsymbol{v}}\,\cdot
\right)
\qquad
\text{in }
\operatorname{Hol}\left(\mathbb{C}\right),

\end{equation}
where \(Q\) is the scalar limiting entire function from
Theorem~\ref{thm:determinant-field}. Consequently,
\[
\mathcal{Z}\left(
Q_n\left(\,\cdot\,\boldsymbol{v}\right)
\right)
\overset{\mathrm{d}}{\rightarrow}
\sum_{Z\in\operatorname{Gin}_{\infty}}
\delta_{Z/\sigma_{\boldsymbol{v}}}
\qquad
\text{in }
\mathcal{N}\left(\mathbb{C}\right).
\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.235362+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7fd3a6056b75fe4f2e4c76596c6cea4e5317a170077d3b3e958395c7e6f9798c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:estimateoffro of arXiv:2604.22510, 'Asymptotics of Multi-Scale McKean--Vlasov Diffusions with Super-Linear Kernels: a Lifted S'] For any $p\geq 2$, there exist constants $\beta, C_p>0$ such that for any $\mu\in\mathscr{P}_{\kappa}({\mathbb R}^n)$, $\gamma\in\mathscr{P}_p({\mathbb R}^m),y\in{\mathbb R}^m$,
	\begin{equation}
		\sup_{t\geq 0}\tilde {\cal E}|Y_{t}^{\mu,\gamma}|^p\lesssim_p(1+M_p(\gamma)),
	\end{equation}	
	\begin{align}
		\tilde {\cal E}|Y_{t}^{\mu,\gamma,y}|^p\leq e^{-\beta t}|y|^p+C_{p}(1+M_p(\gamma)).
	\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:43:04.733228+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7fd3ba6894161ed6b00458fea5d78d9c3559ff49c14d5ba69ac121a632ad899b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 13 (Upward and downward exit problems under reflection) of arXiv:2605.18136, 'L\'evy processes with partially stochastic resetting'] For $a, b \in \mathbb{R}$, the following limits, in terms of the resolvents ${r}_b^{(q+\lambda)}$ and  ${r}_a^{(q+\lambda)}$ defined in Section \ref{reflection},  hold
		\begin{itemize}
