{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:07.264018+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7fd64da6e198fd6b92073d448702d5c1ee3add292c165e0e5e2e3006dc6f5487","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 38 of arXiv:2604.19738, 'Phase Transitions in the Fluctuations of Functionals of Random Neural Networks \\'] Let $(f_n)_{n\in\mathbb N}$ be a sequence of real-analytic functions on $(-1,1)$. Assume that
\begin{enumerate}
