\end{enumerate}
Then $f$ is real analytic on $(-1,1)$, with $f^{(k)}(0)\ge0$ $\forall k\ge k_0$ and the radius of convergence of $f$ at $0$ is at least $1$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:47:32.881846+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7fd6d1d843c870dd4af3596c36aeb80b524268437047c8e65c677c2cd13ad27e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 18 (Baker) of arXiv:2609.02478, 'Improved Weyl bounds on short intervals'] Let $P(X)=\alpha_kX^k+\cdots+\alpha_1X$ and let $M\ge2$.  If
