        \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:59:45.562138+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7fe5a258db0fdc729c79254193e39b4b3622941c1bc96c0ef95eb9576c87e6fc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm: martingale representation of arXiv:2411.17109, 'On the maximal correlation of some stochastic processes'] Let $F$ be a square-integrable $\mathcal{F}^{X}_{T}$-measurable random variable. Then there exist square-integrable predictable processes $\varphi^{X}$ and $\psi^{X}$ such that almost surely,
\begin{align*}
F&=E[F]+\int_{0}^{T}\varphi^{X}(t)\,\mathrm{d}B^{X}_t+\int_{0}^{T}\int_{\mathbb{R}\setminus\{0\}}\psi^{X}(t,x)\widetilde{N}^{X}(\mathrm{d}t,\mathrm{d}x)\notag\\
&=E[F]+\int_{0}^{T}\varphi^{X}(t)\,\mathrm{d}B^{X}_t+\int_{0}^{T}\int_{\mathbb{R}\setminus\{0\}}\int_{\mathbb{R}}\psi^{X}(t,x)\widetilde{N}(\mathrm{d}t,\mathrm{d}x,\mathrm{d}y).
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.089812+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7fe600c652852e519ef4a01f892120c9bdca9971c068b8992eb1dfbfe007fe2d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2411.12623, 'Random signed measures'] [exchangeable random signed measure] A random signed measure $\xi$ on $\mathbb{R}^d$ is separate exchangeable if and only if 
	\begin{equation*}
		(	\xi(A_{i_1}\times\cdots\times A_{i_d}))\stackrel{d}{=}(	\xi(A_{\pi_1(i_1)}\times\cdots\times A_{\pi_d(i_d)}))\quad \textnormal{for $(i_1,...,i_d)\in\mathbb{N}^d$}
	\end{equation*}
	for any permutations $\pi_1,...,\pi_d$ of $\mathbb{N}$ and any intervals $A_j=[h(1-j),hj]$ with $j\in\mathbb{N}$ and $h>0$. When $\pi_1=...=\pi_d$, $\xi$ is called jointly exchangeable.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:15:36.158142+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7fea8c88e358bd796075797304cf26f333144045ae2b58a220a84b69db027d28","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 10 (Uniform nonlinear resolver) of arXiv:2609.01589, 'Uniform stability of expanding simple waves for Euler--Poisson--Boltzmann: a singular comp'] Let $s\ge3$.  There are $\eta_P>0$ and $C>0$, independent of
$0<\eps\le\eps_0$, with the following property.  If
$r\in H^s(\Om)$, $\norm r_{H^s}\le\eta_P$, and $n^a+r$ stays positive,
then \eqref{eq:nonlinear-poisson} has a unique solution
$\psi\in H^s(\Om)$ with $\eps\nabla\psi\in H^s(\Om)$ and
\begin{equation}
  \norm\psi_{H^s}+\eps\norm{\nabla\psi}_{H^s}
  \le C\bigl(\norm r_{H^s}+\norm{\cR_\phi^a}_{H^s}\bigr). 
\end{equation}
The map $r\mapsto\psi$ is locally Lipschitz in the same norms.  Moreover, if
$r\in H^{s}$ and the fluid equations give $\pa_tr\in H^{s-1}$, then the
time-differentiated equation gives
\begin{equation}
  \norm{\pa_t\psi}_{H^{s-1}}
  +\eps\norm{\nabla\pa_t\psi}_{H^{s-1}}
  \le C\bigl(\norm{\pa_tr}_{H^{s-1}}+\norm r_{H^s}
  +\norm{\pa_t\cR_\phi^a}_{H^{s-1}}\bigr). 
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:43:18.802389+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7ff159e1841241b20262c8d04c246c9efae7b1d7ddb8c2e04b4270dc4b5cceb9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition rn:distinct-tail of arXiv:2609.02386, 'On the Growth of Denominators of Simultaneous Best Diophantine Approximations in the Eucli'] If $Q_{M+1}<Q_1+Q_s$, then the classes
        $$
            \overline L_s,\ldots,\overline L_{M+1}\in\mathbb F_2^{n+1}
        $$
