{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:39:18.535951+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7ff25bc39949e25d3c01e7e5c11caa3cd7f7815bf3d952860e9c2fccbc8dbf8a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 23 of arXiv:2609.02294, 'Existence and Blow-Up for Non-linear Fokker-Planck with Controlled Drift Divergence'] Let $\bar s=\frac{\|u(0)\|_1}{\|u(0)\|_\infty}$, $A:=\dfrac{k\,a_p(T)}{a_d\,k_c}$, and define
