{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.085279+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_800e04ef06f6a4a83435075faa0bfb61090e39ee2dd4e6428acf072525b43290","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Conjecture of arXiv:2606.11677, 'Feynman--Kac formula for the heat equation with a one-center point interaction in $d=3$.'] Let $\Sigma\subset {\mathbb{R}}^d$ be a compact set which is not a removable set for $\Delta$ in $L^2({\mathbb{R}}^d)$. Then, there exist a self-adjoint extension  of $\Delta|_{C_c^\infty({\mathbb{R}}^d\backslash \Sigma)}$ in $L^2({\mathbb{R}}^d)$, $\widetilde{\Delta}$, and  a measure valued process $\left\{\mathcal{X}_t\right\}_{t\geq 0}$ such that  \begin{align*}
\mathtt{E}_{\delta_x}[\mathcal{X}_t(u_0)]=\widetilde{u}(t,x)
\end{align*}
for any $t>0$ and any $x\in {\mathbb{R}}^3\backslash\Sigma$, where $\widetilde{u}$ is the solution to \begin{align*}
\partial_t u=\frac{1}{2}\widetilde{\Delta}u,\quad u(0,x)=u_0(x).
\end{align*} (Stated as a conjecture by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.471565+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_800ef39a764f06c0d88a7882c444043286782693ce773433c3caee30dcac6902","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 33 of arXiv:2609.02561, 'NON-NEF LOCI IN MIXED CHARACTERISTIC'] With notation as above, let $S^0 \subset S$ be an open subset with $f(\Gamma)\cap S^0 \neq \emptyset$. Set $X^0 := f^{-1}(S^0)$, $D^0 := D|_{X^0}$, $f^0:=f|_{X^0}$, and ${\Gamma}^{0} := \Gamma \cap X^0$.
