{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.238111+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_800f6bfa91ff1647ae4d739331b0f24b6b3a002a42e5a1af1e4c50f32f71f544","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 40 of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] Let $\hfixp_0 \in \UCp$ and $\Lp$ be a periodic directed landscape on $(\mathbb{T} \times \R)^{2}_{\uparrow}$. Then define the random function $(y,t) \mapsto \hfixp(\hfixp_0;y,t)$ for all $y\in \mathbb{T}$ and $t >0$ by
