{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:42:47.752087+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8032c13c6128dffaff7d439b6c910245a6d4f3592328f19a770689f6ed473222","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 (Semilocalization) of arXiv:2604.11682, 'Semilocalization for inhomogeneous random graphs'] Suppose that Assumptions \ref{hyp:upperbd-weights} and \ref{hyp:behavior-m21} hold. For any $\nu > 0$ there exists $C_{\nu} > 0$ such that the following holds with $\nu$-high probability. For any normalized eigenvector $\b q$ of $A$ with associated eigenvalue $\lambda$ and for any $\eta \leq |\lambda|/2$ we have
