{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:48:30.923173+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_803a74a609f13712cc02d6b3af8f33e0a75e9d0b382844cded9aac478e004392","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 19 (Main Theorem for $n=1$) of arXiv:2609.00974, 'On Algebraic Integrability\\ of Vector Fields \\ with Rational Function Coefficients\\ tha'] Let $k$ be a field of characteristic zero. 
    Let $f\in k(x)$, $f\ne 0$. 
    Let $PHD(\frac{1}{f})=P+L+H$ with ${L}=\sum_{i=1}^d \frac{c_i}{x_i-a_i}$, see Theorem \ref{thm: PFD}.

    Let $D=f\frac{\partial}{\partial x}:k(x) \to k(x)$ be a derivation. 

    Then the following are equivalent:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item There is a finite type model of $k$ over integers, such that for all all maximal ideals $q$ from an open dense subset of the model, $D$ reduces modulo $q$ and we have $\mu_q\in \overline{k(q)}$, where $D^p=\mu_q D$.
        \item One of the following is true:
        \begin{enumerate}
            \item $L=0$.
            \item $P=H=0$, and the vector space spanned by the residues of $\frac{1}{f}$, the vector space $\op{Span}_\mathbb{Q}(c_1,c_2,\ldots,c_d)\subset \overline{k}$, has dimension $1$ over rational numbers.
        \end{enumerate}
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:46:12.282876+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8041f59c4e1aece3a8f0fe279033e710c54e9230c45d60cc127559af9f5832b9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 25 (Level-barrier) of arXiv:2604.22567, 'Sign-balance of random Laplace eigenfunctions'] There exist numbers $C>0$, $T_{0}>0$ sufficiently large, only depending on $\Mcc$, with the following property. Let $T>T_{0}$, 
