{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:30.013383+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8054855f550ca0e69baa4021125130bc537752b9adcdbbe218ceafa832f8c3cf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 25 of arXiv:2605.04359, 'Well-posedness of reflected BSDEs with default time and irregular barrier: An application '] Assume that conditions of Theorem \ref{Comparison for BSDEs} hold and that $K^1$ and $K^2$ are two regulated, optional, increasing processes in $\mathcal{S}^2$. If there exist a triplet $\left(Y_t^i, Z_t^i,U^i_t\right)_{0 \leq t \leq T}, i=1,2$, that belongs to $\mathcal{S}^{2,\alpha}_{\beta} \times \mathcal{H}^{2}_{\beta} \times \mathcal{U}^{2}_{\lambda,\beta}$ satisfying the equations
