	\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:28:33.843201+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_805ecccb793599219ae62238aeae16ddfb06b55b23ffa9cae709a98c2599bd40","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:10 of arXiv:2504.12293, 'Near-existence of bigeodesics in dynamical exponential last passage percolation'] There is a positive constant $C$ such that for each $n\in \mathbb{N}$, there is a deterministic point $\mathfrak{q}_n\in \mathrm{Box}_{n}$ for which
