{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:48:00.299185+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8061088e2b4f27f5ade3ad7b0a97f801d74b48844e9d879958ecaa946c2fa45b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Conj curious CY4 vanishing PT of arXiv:2609.03152, 'Experiments with membranes, maps and sheaves'] Suppose $(Z,\mathsf{T})$ is Calabi--Yau and let $\beta$ be an effective curve class in $Z$ so that the moduli space \smash{$\overline{M}{}_g^\bullet(Y,\beta)$} of stable maps to the fourfold with possibly disconnected domain and no contracted connected components is proper for all $g\geq 0$. Then 
