    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:07:48.564361+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8067310126f1a51dece2a3a4841d85cd9181a3f19fa608fed9747ce6808098cd","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 14 of arXiv:2609.01460, 'On cost-induced Santal\'o-type inequalities \\ in Polish measure spaces'] Let $K \in \mathcal{C}^n$ and $L \in \mathcal{B}(\R^n)$. Define $M(K,L) = \sup_{x\in K, y\in L} \langle x, y \rangle$. Then,
    \begin{equation}
    \vol(K)^{\frac{1}{2}} \vol(L)^{\frac{1}{2}} \leq \vol(\B) M(K,L)^{\frac{n}{2}}.
    \end{equation}
    If $0<\vol(L)<\infty$, then there is equality if and only if one has, up to removal of null sets, that $K$ is a centered ellipsoid and $L=M(K,L)K^\circ$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.578459+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_806845cfce2995ace0e8860f3cb82ef64ee5d2608e9f1d62724eefe63629fdef","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition d:OnePlusMoment of arXiv:2411.14936, 'Massive Particle Systems,\\Wasserstein Brownian Motions,\\ and the Dean--Kawasaki Equation'] Let~$\tau\colon {\mathbb R}^+\to{\mathbb R}^+$ be a Borel-measurable function satisfying
