{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:10.976031+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_808331de60f544654061577b24c61cfcbe8f3e7759cbc137b2ada72c3f4f8b81","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 24 of arXiv:2606.13648, 'Stochastic dominations for FK percolation and sharp thinning thresholds for the Ising ener'] Take $C_1=\prod_{e=0}^n(1+q_e)$, $C_{-1}=\prod_{e=0}^n(1-q_e)$ and $Z=\sum_{F\in\F}q_F$ where $\F\subset{\mathcal P}(E)$ is the set of subsets of $E$ of even cardinality and $q_F=\prod_{e\in F}q_e$ for $F\subset E$. We have that $C_1+C_{-1}=2Z$ and
