{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:18:19.220804+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8091eaefacb63313a029c9420cb5d3b993651d8267c58756d898000f4954ee0f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 of arXiv:2608.29086, '2608.29086'] [Mesh $M_0$]
A \textit{triangular mesh} $M$ is a triplet 
\begin{equation*}
(Tri(M),\ Edge(M),\ Ver(M)), 
\end{equation*}
where 
\begin{align*}
&Tri(M) \text{ is the collection of all triangles of $M$},\\
&Edge(M) \text{ is the collection of all edges of the triangles in $Tri(M)$}, \\ 
&Ver(M) \text{ is the collection of all vertices of the edges in $Edge(M)$}. 
\end{align*}
$M_0$ is the triangular mesh obtained by dividing $\mathbf{R}^2$ into equilateral triangles (Figure \ref{figure1} (a)). In particular, $M_0$ is defined in $\mathbf{R}^2$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:26:52.655089+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8098c368b31395e550727e13c6e2ac08efa730af96d28e5f10169659bc7b6abb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 16 of arXiv:2609.03713, 'A Sharp Mass Threshold for Boundedness in a Critical Quasilinear Chemotaxis Model with Ind'] Let $M>0$ and suppose there is a sequence $(u_l,w_l)_{l\ge 1}$ in $\mathcal{S}_{M,rad}$ satisfying
