{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:05:28.236196+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_80cab7a20d3ebb00caf3747394b6abf87d90ab394219d8f5ec1d0b80cc84d688","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop: martingale property of multiple integrals of arXiv:2602.04429, 'Disordered systems and (subcritical) polynomial chaos\\ with heavy-tail disorder'] {}
The process $({\ensuremath{\mathbf X}} ^{(a)}(\ensuremath{\mathbf{f}}))_{a\in (0,1]}$ is a time-reversed càdlàg martingale with respect to the filtration ${\ensuremath{\mathcal F}}  = ({\ensuremath{\mathcal F}} ^{(a)})_{a\in (0,1]}$.
