{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:52:08.680488+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_80cadeae2373c5e22a37ce02ddda1e8c840f352828cee81614956ed731e8d8ee","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 22 of arXiv:2608.30077, 'Lie groupoid integration of singular isometries of the Poincaré disk'] We define now the groupoid $\mathcal{G}_{n} \coloneq X_{n} / \sim_{n}$.
    The equivalence relation $\sim_n$ includes composition with loops in $\psu$  winding $n$-times around the origin:
