{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:20:07.900625+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_80d18c911ec26ebe2b50d6083130cb098a2c57e1f8c2f8df537e7e6abf817049","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma NSPl1min of arXiv:2608.23765, '\texorpdfstring{Tight Majorizations and Convergence Rates\\ of Nuclear Norm Minimization I'] Assume that the measurement operator $\mathcal{A}: \mathbb{R}^{d_1 \times d_2} \longrightarrow \R^m $ satisfies the NSP of order $r$ of (def:NSP:statement of the paper) for some $\eta_r<1$. Then  for all $\mathbf{Z},  \mathbf{X}  \in \mathbb{R}^{d_1 \times d_2}$ such that $\mathcal{A} \left( \mathbf{Z} \right) =  \mathcal{A} \left(\mathbf{X} \right)  $ it holds that

