{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:48:24.618313+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_80e13873470792f7af8c11a06ffb6addb012d6d28833c40cff6fdac82637f179","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:uniqueness_new of arXiv:2601.04997, 'Fluctuations of the Boundary-Driven Symmetric Zero-Range Process from the NESS'] For $\theta\ge1$, there exists a unique (in law) stochastic process $\mathscr{Y}$ in the space of continuous distributions $\mathcal{C}([0, T], \widetilde{S}')$ such that (equation eq:Y_covariance of the paper) holds for functions in $\widetilde{S}$ and, for every $H\in \widetilde{S}$, the stochastic processes $\{\mathscr{M}^*_t(H), t\in[0, T]\}$ and $\{\mathscr{N}^*_t(H), t\in[0, T]\}$ defined by
\begin{equation}
    \begin{split}
    &\mathscr{M}^*_t(H):=\mathscr{Y}_t(H)-\mathscr{Y}_0(H)-\int_0^t\mathscr{Y}_s\left(\Phi'(\bar\rho_\theta)\Delta H\right)\de s-\mathscr{Z}^{\theta, 0}_t(H)-\mathscr{Z}_t^{\theta, 1}(H),
    \\&\mathscr{N}^*_t(H):=\mathscr{M}_t^*(H)^2-t\left\| H\right\|_{L^{2, \theta,*}}^2
    \end{split}
\end{equation}
are $\mathcal{F}_t$-martingales, with the ${L^{2, \theta,*}}$-norm  defined through the inner product
\begin{align*}
    \scal{H, G}_{L^{2, \theta, *}} := \;2\int_0^1 \Phi(\bar\rho_\theta(u))H'(u)G'(u)\de u&+\left\{\alpha+\lambda\Phi(\bar\rho_\theta(0))\right\}H(0)G(0)\boldsymbol{1}_{\{1\}}(\theta)
    \\&+\left\{\beta+\delta\Phi(\bar\rho_\theta(1))\right\}H(1)G(1)\boldsymbol{1}_{\{1\}}(\theta).
\end{align*}
Here, for $i\in\{0, 1\}$, the processes $\mathscr{Z}_t^{\theta, i}$ are defined by 
\begin{equation}
    \mathscr{Z}_t^{\theta, i}(H) := \mylim_{\varepsilon\to 0}\int_0^t c_N^{\theta, i} (H,s)
    \mathscr Y_s(\Phi'(\bar\rho_\theta)\iota_\varepsilon^0) \de s,
\end{equation} 
with $c_N^{\theta, 0}(H, s):=H_s'(0)-\boldsymbol{1}_{\{1\}}(\theta)\lambda H_s(0)$ and $c_N^{\theta, 1}(H,s):=H_s'(1)+\boldsymbol{1}_{\{1\}}(\theta)\delta H_s(1)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:55:27.166959+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_80e167fd1f2c5925dae016970196e7949c02b12e5f40d6fd656c2d3fc6d4f9d3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition V_N torsion-free of arXiv:2609.04072, 'Oort's conjecture for split unitary Shimura varieties'] Assume that $n \geq 3$, then the congruence subgroup $V_N$ is torsion-free unless one of the following conditions is satisfied.
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $(g,p)=(2,2)$ and $m\in \{1,n-1\}$.
        \item $g=1$ and $m\in \{1,n-1\}$
        \item $(g,p)=(1,2)$ and either $m \in \{2,n-2\}$ or $n=7$ and $m \in \{3,4\}$ or $n=8$ and $m \in \{3,5\}$.
    \end{enumerate}
    Furthermore, in Case (3) the torsion elements of $V_N$ are precisely $\{\pm 1\}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:33:43.760490+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_80e2d0f15fa30e1cd1da9b3787aab34c6b27cbecbc4593b77802f27686e358bb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corr thisgivesthat of arXiv:2609.02682, 'LDP for tensor forms'] Given a sequence of graphs $G_n$ and a fixed graph $H$ above, set $Q_n$ by (equation eq:333 of the paper) and set $\widetilde{G}_n:=G_n/\lVert G_n\rVert_1$. Let $W^{(2)}_{\widetilde{G}_n}\in L^1([0,1]^2)$ be defined as in (equation eq:funext of the paper). Suppose the following assumptions are satisfied: 
\begin{align}
    \limsup_{n\to\infty}\,\lVert W^{(2)}_{\widetilde{G}_n}\rVert_{q\Delta} < \infty \qquad \mbox{and} \qquad \lVert W^{(2)}_{\widetilde{G}_n}-W_\infty^{(2)}\rVert_{\square^*}\overset{n\to\infty}{\to} 0, 
\end{align}
for some $q>1$ and $W_\infty^{(2)}\in L^1([0,1]^2)$. Then for any ${\boldsymbol \alpha}\in \mathbb{R}^c$, the  statistic
${\boldsymbol\alpha}^\top {\boldsymbol N}(H,G_n,{\bf{X}})$ satisfies an LDP with speed $n$ and the good rate function from (equation eq:i2 of the paper), with $G_{W_{\infty,\mathbf{1}_r}}$ replaced by $G^{(2)}_{{\infty},r}$, $1\le r\le c$ defined as
\begin{align}
    G^{(2)}_{{\infty},r}(\boldsymbol{f}):=\int_{[0,1]^v}\prod_{\{i,j\}\in E(H)} W^{(2)}_{\infty}(x_{i},x_{j})\prod_{a=1}^v f_r(x_a)\, d x_a.
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:09:49.801547+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_80f0bdfea66b63e8307dea397322ecede188d44952d2d416d69ea2bf83f41b07","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 11 of arXiv:2609.03070, 'Variants of order semicontinuity in Banach lattices'] $F$ is $r$-semicontinuous if and only if the common order and uo closure of $\Ba_{F}$ is contained in $r\Ba_{F}$. Moreover, the following conditions are equivalent:
