            h & \text{if } l\ge 3.
        \end{cases}
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.771672+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_810a0c5770235d0c6d400f0478e08792f317c115e936bc4adb4fde9991232ade","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor main2 of arXiv:2411.18359, 'Large systems of symmetrized trapped Brownian Bridges and Schr\"odinger processes'] Fix $ \beta \in (0,\infty) $. Then, as $ N\to\infty $, under the measure $ \mathbb{P}_{{\mathfrak m},N,W}^{\ssup{{\rm sym}}} $ defined in (equation transsym of the paper), the mean of occupation measures, $ Y_N $, satisfy a Large Deviations Principle on $ {\mathcal M }_1(\mathbb{R}^d) $ with speed $ N $  and rate function $ J^{{\scriptscriptstyle{({\rm sym}})}}_{W,{\mathfrak m}} :{\mathcal M }_1(\mathbb{R}^d)\to \mathbb{R} \cup \{\infty\}$ given by:
\begin{equation}
J^{(sym)}_{{\mathfrak m},W}(p):=J^{(sym)}_{{\mathfrak m}}(p)+\langle W,p\rangle-\inf_{p\in{\mathcal M }_1(\mathbb{R}^d)}\Bigl\{J^{(sym)}_{{\mathfrak m}}(p)+\langle W,p\rangle\Bigr\}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:23:05.304141+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_810cb5cdc44a57b2801965f71f9fddb11d64984ee50a79edf86946eba9fff4b1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2608.21905, '\bf Ruin theory incorporating MIPP-type jumps'] Assume $c\ge E[\xi]$, then we have
