{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.813130+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_811e3601946c54e7fe6a884fe055197848342de9dd57469006cf533e588dbd22","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma mgf-above-n-asymptotic of arXiv:2504.02207, 'Finite-Time behaviors of M/M/$n$ Queue: Mixing Time, Mean Queue Length and Tail Bounds'] Let $\delta$ be a given positive real number, $n \geq 2$ be a positive integer and denote $\lambda = n-n^{1-\alpha}$ where $\alpha \in (0,+\infty)$. We have
