{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.392152+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8120b31d5bec1811c1fe31fd090d40f164952a298c704dd5fa9d5e7695240c41","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition p:diffeo_conjugation of arXiv:2606.11503, 'Percolation on hierarchical lattices'] Let $U, \tilde{U} \subset \mathbb{R}$ be open sets and consider a $C^{k+1}$ diffeomorphism $f:U \to \tilde{U}$, for some $k \geq 1$. Assume there exists $u_{\star} \in U$ such that $f(u_{\star}) = u_{\star}$ and such that $\zeta = f'(u_{\star})$ satisfies $|\zeta| \neq 1$. There exists a $C^{k}$ diffeomorphism $h: V \to \tilde{V}$ between open neighborhoods of $u_{\star}$ and the origin such that $h(u_{\star}) = 0$ and such that
\begin{equation}
f(x) = h^{-1} \Big( \zeta h(x) \Big), \quad \text{for all } x \in V.
\end{equation}
Furtheremore, the diffeomorphism $h$ is unique up to multiplication by constants. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:43:53.576927+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8124b1cda49dbd1a11db3112e53933e079aefb888aac6a8778c0a32e0239409c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2512.09308, 'On asymptotic behavior of solutions to random fractional Riesz-Bessel equations with cycli'] [seneta2006regularly]
