{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:06:07.098136+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_815373576c123783240dedf36a6ced16c4dd8d713ef949ef4061aa7bdced4a8c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2608.28198, 'Performative Privacy: When Differential Privacy Maximizes Utility'] Given the aggregated empirical mean mechanism, the exact probability that a specific individual data point $z$ is purged (i.e., its log-likelihood ratio breaches the threshold $\tau$) conditioned on $Z_t$ is given in closed form by:
