{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:48:24.561722+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_81795022541ea5d18c4fa0a4a64732a36bb7eb221712563aaa2a038aa1b92d3a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma L:compare_T_S of arXiv:2512.21977, 'Repeat times and a two-weight UST model'] Let ${\ensuremath{\mathcal T}} $ be a random spanning tree with law as in (equation eq:PomegaT of the paper), and denote by $S_1, S_2, \ldots$ components chosen at random as in Section~(S:size_biased_GNP of the paper). If $t_1$ denotes the first repeat time of the process $(S_i)_{i\geq 1}$, then with $\ensuremath{\boldsymbol{\mathrm{P}}}_{\ensuremath{\mathcal T}} $-probability at least $1 - n^{-1}$
