{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:32:11.130865+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_818607699e389fa9ad49d3a2255daeb7338fa77b69b1adbc81a3037b3a83e741","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:var of arXiv:2510.09818, 'On the Fourier dimension of fractional Brownian graphs'] [LL25]
Let $H \in (0,1)$ and consider a fractional Brownian motion $B$ with Hurst parameter $H$. There exists a constant $C_H>0$ depending only on $H$ such that for all integers $n \ge 1$, for all $0<t_1<\cdots<t_n$, and for all $a_1, \dots, a_n \in \mathbb R$
\begin{align*}
	\mathrm{Var}\left( \sum_{j=1}^n a_j B_{t_j}\right) \ge \frac{C_H^{n-1}}{n} \sum_{j=1}^n (a_j+\cdots+a_n)^2 (t_j-t_{j-1})^{2H},
\end{align*}
where we have used the convention $t_0=0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

