{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:39:11.688884+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_819584cca52ed3ca00e70f84daad6abeba172ac4eb187bf4a3c285a2e7ce0bcc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 102 (Fixed-order moment scaling for the classical It\^o tower) of arXiv:2608.04993, '2608.04993'] For every integer $k\ge0$ and $q\ge2$, there is
$C_{k,q}=C_{k,q}(\Lambda,B,T)$, independent of $P$ and $s$, such that
for $s\le t\le T$,
\begin{equation}
 \left\|\sup_{s\le r\le t}
 \|\mathrm I_{s,r}^{P,(k)}\|_2\right\|_{L^q(P)}
 \le C_{k,q}|t-s|^{k/2}.
\end{equation}
For $k\ge0$ and $s\le u\le v\le T$,
