{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:47:01.664620+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_81a7711b9bcbe442e4a9180a0f895749c101274f92dff36ffba6bd6f1126b82d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 15 of arXiv:2604.23656, 'Doubly Reflected Backward SDEs Driven by $G$-Brownian Motion with Quadratic Generator'] Suppose that $\xi$, $f$, $g$ satisfy (H1)-(H3) and $L$, $U$ satisfy Assumption \ref{assLU}. Then the doubly reflected $G$-BSDE with data $(\xi,f,g,L,U)$ has a unique solution $(Y,Z,A)\in S^\infty_G(0,T)\times BMO_G\times \cap_{\alpha\geq 2} S^\alpha_G(0,T)$. Moreover, for any $\alpha\ge 2$, we have
	\begin{align*}
		\lim_{n\rightarrow \infty}\hat{\mathbb{E}}\left[\sup_{t\in[0,T]}|Y_t-\bar{Y}^n_t|^\alpha\right]=0, 
	\end{align*}
	where for each $n\in\mathbb{N}$, $(\bar{Y}^n,\bar{Z}^n,\bar{A}^n)\in S^\infty_G(0,T)\times BMO_G\times \cap_{\alpha\geq 2} S^\alpha_G(0,T)$ is the solution to the following reflected $G$-BSDE:
	\begin{equation}
		\begin{cases}

			\bar{Y}^n_t=\xi+\int_t^T f(s,\bar{Y}^n_s,\bar{Z}^n_s)ds+\int_t^T g(s,\bar{Y}^n_s,\bar{Z}^n_s)d\langle B\rangle_s\\
			\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ -n\int_t^T(\bar{Y}^n_s-U_s)^+ds-\int_t^T \bar{Z}^n_sdB_s+(\bar{A}^n_T-\bar{A}^n_t), \\
			\bar{Y}^n_t\geq L_t, \forall t\in[0,T], \{-\int_0^t (\bar{Y}^n_s-L_s)d\bar{A}^n_s\}_{t\in[0,T]} \textrm{ is a non-increasing $G$-martingale}.
		\end{cases}
	\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:07:56.656310+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_81a96da75024df858bb5f80876fe98034b024cb9090a496ab5a79e3f98b1035c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th:strong_LLN of arXiv:2411.04690, 'Asymptotic distribution of the derivative of the taut string accompanying Wiener process'] Let a function $\varphi$ be continuous almost everywhere, locally bounded and satisfy the condition of power growth (equation eq:power_bound of the paper). 
