{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:42:47.754232+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_81abfb1e4bdd3c6d6c37172d7801cb7fbdffcda3da4e710df12ade22686760eb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 29 of arXiv:2604.11682, 'Semilocalization for inhomogeneous random graphs'] Let $\nu > 0$. There exists $C_{\nu} > 0$ such that with $\nu$-high probability,
