{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.085203+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_81b8c7ccf26392eb984b378c1b725ef5b68aa3983f770555036a4fb0d588c4af","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2606.11677, 'Feynman--Kac formula for the heat equation with a one-center point interaction in $d=3$.'] The Bessel capacity of a compact set $\Sigma\subset {\mathbb{R}}^d$ with index $(\gamma,p)$ for $p>1$ is defined by \begin{align*}
\mathrm{Cap}_{\gamma,p}(\Sigma)=\sup\left\{\nu(\Sigma):\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^d}\text{\rm d} x\left(\int_{\Sigma}G_\gamma(x,y)\nu(\text{\rm d} y)\right)^{q}\leq 1\right\},
\end{align*} 
where $q=\frac{p}{p-1}$ and \begin{align*}
G_\gamma(x,y)=a_\gamma\int_0^\infty t^{\frac{\gamma-d}{2}}e^{-\frac{|x-y|^2}{2t}}\frac{e^{-\frac{t}{2}}}{t}\text{\rm d} t
\end{align*}
($a_\gamma>0$ is a constant) and the supremum is taken over {all finite measures}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:26:26.737898+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_81ba356433ef0db2dd7415847b62abefdc5318821d890ee022e9a7b8a8c571e0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:Woodbury of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] Let $K$ be dressing compatible with $(\Psi, \Phi)$,
