{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:38:08.471213+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_81e9cce34e390dc1057e658726a8c189a5ca5f4bab176653b07fca1e8592420a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:auc-min-vs-max:hbar-constant-time of arXiv:2609.02304, 'Bayes-Optimal BER and AUC: \\Estimation and Evaluation of Estimators'] For each $j \in \set{1, \dots, n}$, 
  let $(j)$ denote the index of the $j$-th smallest element in
  $\set{\eta_{1}, \dots, \eta_{n}}$,
  i.e., $\eta_{(1)} \leq \dots \leq \eta_{(n)}$,
  and let $S_{i}$
  be the $i$-th prefix sum of 
  $\set{(\eta_{(j)} - \theta)^{2}}_{j=1}^n$,
  i.e.,
  $S_{i}
  \coloneqq 
  \sum_{j=1}^{i} (\eta_{(j)} - \theta)^{2}$.
  Then, $\bar{h}_{(i)}$ 
  can be expressed as
  \begin{equation}

    \bar{h}_{(i)}
    =
    \frac{1 - 2 \theta}{2 (n - 1)}
    \left[
      (2i - n) (\eta_{(i)} - \theta)^{2} + S_{n} - 2 S_{i}
    \right]
    \text{.}
  \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:30:28.826749+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_81f07ffc086ed035c5f68a8dab7eeac965e08fed765683887b6fd9d912ac836e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 11 of arXiv:2609.02105, 'Contact fundamental forms and \\ adjoint varieties'] Let us use the coordinates and the 1-form $\theta$ on the Heisenberg group $\sH$ in Lemma \ref{l.coordi}.   
