{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.489903+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8255d03dc03a30a58f5795bfbfafbd144058f61f9b6fa28d0b527771744427fa","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 215 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] The fundamental solution $\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}(z_1,z_2)$ depends only on $H$, $\boldsymbol{\Theta}$ and $\alpha_1 < \beta_1 < \cdots < \alpha_H < \beta_H$. It does so in a smooth way, and satisfies
 \begin{equation}

