{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:48:30.900286+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_828acf336ae3527f1226f9dddc617a3beb104f0d6b63d45af781defa25fe3d5a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 13 of arXiv:2609.00867, '2609.00867'] Let \((\rho_t)_{0\le t\le T}\) be a classical solution in probability densities
of \eqref{eq:first-order-coulomb-pde}, and set
\(\psi_t:=\log\rho_t+\beta g*\rho_t\).  Suppose that
\[
 \sup_{0\le t\le T}\left(
 \norm{\rho_t}_{L^\infty}
 +\norm{D^2\psi_t}_{L^\infty}
 \right)<\infty.
\]
Let \(F^N\) be an entropy solution in the sense of
Definition~\ref{def:coulomb-entropy-solution}.  There exists \(C_T\ge1\),
independent of \(N\), such that, for every \(0\le t\le T\),
\begin{equation}
 \frac1{2N}\Ent(F^N(t)\mid\rho_t^{\otimes N})-\frac{C_T}{N}
 \le\mathcal E_N(t)
 \le e^{C_T t}\mathcal E_N(0)+\frac{C_T}{N}.
\end{equation}
If \(F^N(0)=\rho_0^{\otimes N}\), then
\begin{equation}
 \sup_{0\le t\le T}\left(
 \abs{\mathcal E_N(t)}
 +\frac1N\Ent(F^N(t)\mid\rho_t^{\otimes N})
 \right)
 \le\frac{C_T}{N}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:20:55.608594+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_828cdacb33810e68b9e6ff62311ff97872c4ae8fcda5de5a816fc97cded54ce0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma zygmund-marcinkiewicz of arXiv:2411.07737, 'On Asymptotic Behavior of Extinction Moment of Critical Bisexual Branching Process in Rand'] Let $\{ \xi_n \}_{n = 1}^{\infty}$ be a sequence of i.i.d. r.v. with $\ER \abs*{\xi_n}^{\alpha} < \infty$, where $1 \leq \alpha \leq 2$, and $\ER \xi_n = 0$ for all $n \in \mathbb{N}$.
    Then, there is a constant $c_{\alpha} > 0$ such that
    \[
        \left( \ER \abs*{ \sum_{i = 1}^n \xi_i } \right)^{\alpha}
        \leq \ER \abs*{ \sum_{i = 1}^n \xi_i }^{\alpha}
        \leq c_{\alpha} \sum_{i = 1}^n \ER \abs*{\xi_i}^{\alpha}.
    \] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.630514+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_828e68b3354f5c390e293aed397cefebdf972c3431ccbfdbb838daabc98d9c85","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop P:two-point-bd of arXiv:2604.10020, 'The directed landscape in half-space'] Take $n \in \mathbb{N}$, parameter $\alpha \ge 1/2 - n^{-1/6}$, and $x, y, z_0 \in \llbracket0, n/100 \rrbracket$, $a > 0$ satisfying
\begin{equation}

C_0 \max \left(\frac{z_0^2}{n}, \frac{z_0 |y-x|}{n}, z_0(1/2 - \alpha)\vee 0 \right) < a < C_* z_0,
\end{equation}
where $C_0>0$ is a universal constant, and $C_*>0$ is any large enough number.
Then for a constant $c>0$ depending only on $C_*$, we have
$$
\mathbb{P}\left(\max_{z \in\llbracket0,z_0 \rrbracket} \left|\bar X[x, 1; y + z, n]_\textsf{L} - \bar X[x, 1; y, n]_\textsf{L} \right| \ge a \right) \le 2\exp(- c a^2/z_0) + 2 \exp(-c \sqrt{n}).
$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.576780+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_828f2a2fcbaa9a1402166c4011e06fabbb9e1512dacf71266a944ea56ca12673","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lem-bound for V-001 of arXiv:2412.08932, 'Gaussian heat kernel asymptotics for conditioned random walks'] There exists $c>0$ such that, for any $x \geqslant 1$, 
