{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:13:22.519612+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_82a4560d841e36de2c4f7b9b1e9c73ad6a44583ccf815b95d70892027d58ac7a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop mle of arXiv:2505.16585, 'Expanded regimes of area law for lattice Yang--Mills theories'] Let $s \in \mc{S}_\Lambda$ be non-null, $\mbf{e}$ be an edge of $s$, and $K : \mc{P}_\Lambda^+ \ra \N$ be a plaquette count. We have that
