{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:58:01.553016+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8321896471927ec299c8479b2d1278dcaeed607179b2720678b61ec97383c497","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 10 of arXiv:2608.27143, 'An approximate zero bias transformation for random sums: Applications to sampling with out'] Let $n_1, n_2, n_3\in \mathbb{N}$ be such that $n_1< n_2< n_3$. Let $X_1,X_2,\ldots$ be mean zero random variables with finite variances.
