{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:14:46.353495+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_83234ba023ecb06c1c567f7e95516e2efb262445054fd2181c71645554ab0c6c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:finite-prior-free-entropy of arXiv:2608.10184, 'The sharp SAT/UNSAT phase transition in random ellipsoid fitting'] Fix $\beta>0$, $C_0<\infty$, $\kappa>0$, and $\Lambda<\infty$. Let $z_1,\ldots,z_n\stackrel{\mathrm{iid}}{\sim}\mathcal{N}(0,I_m)$ and set $W_i = (z_i z_i^\top - I_m)/\sqrt m$, and let $G_1,\ldots,G_n$ be independent $\operatorname{GOE}(m)$ matrices, independent of the $W_i$. Then, as $m \to \infty$,
