{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:30:36.746277+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8328d45147cdc63167ea3fc494dd7fec08c06421e251cff9248c8c2a6902b125","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 (Bulk limit) of arXiv:2607.08696, 'Spectrum of Directed Inhomogeneous Random Graphs'] Suppose that Assumption \ref{ass:rank-one} holds, and that either Assumption \ref{assumption:bulk-poly} or Assumption \ref{assumption:bulk-sparse} hold. Then the empirical spectral distribution of $A_n/\sqrt{\scaling}$ converges weakly in probability to a deterministic probability measure $\mu$ on $\mathbb C$. The measure $\mu$ is characterized by its logarithmic potential:
