{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:16:18.644415+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_835828edfe263cb149d870519bd5c6e1344274c84a6a2c01b74b1b1edd5cd568","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 (Main theorem) of arXiv:2607.23980, 'Sharp small-deviation inequalities for sums of independent\\nonnegative random variables'] Let $n\ge1$, let $X_1,\ldots,X_n$ be independent nonnegative random variables with $\E X_i\le1$, and put $S=\sum_iX_i$. For $\delta>0$, set
