{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:43:53.592347+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8360a52c6eb5eecf91f79b7a895b9ac4b11d7da71301563163ec31004ab337e4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:vestimate3_difference of arXiv:2512.12902, 'Non-equilibrium fluctuations for the \\stirring process with births and deaths'] Let  $K\geq 2$ be a fixed  integer number, $n,m\geq 1$ and $\zeta>0$. For any initial product measure $\mu^{\epsilon}$ satisfying (equation Ass1 of the paper), and times  $0<s<r\leq T$, there exists $\tilde\Delta>0$, such that when $r-s\leq \tilde\Delta$
