{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:40:22.403487+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_836512be74ae18407000c7107cc31b73b6b69c2f6f144752b0fe60f9302d3d91","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lem-to-infty of arXiv:2506.18827, 'Random walk reflected off of infinity, with applications to uniform spanning forests and s'] Almost surely, the following is true for each finite set of vertices $\mathcal A\subset \mathcal V\mathcal G$. 
