where $\mathcal{K}>0$ independent of $N$ but depends on $\kappa$. 
Moreover, for any two quasi-regular weak   solutions $f_1, f_2,$   of  (equation Ito-FP_eps-V2 of the paper)  with    the same    initial data    $f_0$,  if   $(f_i(t),\varphi)$    is  $\overline{\mathcal{G}}_t$-adapted, for both    $i=1,2$ and for    any $\varphi\in V_0$, then   $f_1=f_2.$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:53:10.209155+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_836ac8c50d53aac5f887f43fe405012f837808d5bb27873acdf617f383f29c4c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem Cobound of arXiv:2608.29013, 'Weighted Homology and Cohomology of Weighted Polyhedra'] Let $(X,\lambda)$ be a descending type weighted polyhedron. For any cochains $\phi\in \mathcal{W}^p(X,\lambda)$ and $\psi\in \mathcal{W}^q(X,\lambda)$, we have
