where $\mathcal{C}_p^p=2^{p-1}B_p^p\left(m_2^{p/2}\vee m_p\right)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:40.044161+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_836d67a47470791e3561fd713f4e9a50629bc31affa24c155da6e5a8226ec6e0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 19 of arXiv:2510.24244, 'Statistical properties of Markov shifts: part II-LLT'] There are positive constants $\del_0,c_1,c_2,C_1,C_2$ such that for every finite sequence of functions    
$(v_j)_{j=n}^{n+m-1}$ with $a:=\max\|v_j\|_{j,\omega}\leq \del_0$ 
  we have the following. 
Set $\cA_{j}(g)=\cL_j(e^{iv_j}g)$ and 
$
\cA_{n}^m=\cA_{n+m-1}\circ \cdots\circ\cA_{n+1}\circ\cA_n.
$
Then
\begin{equation}

C_1e^{-c_1\mathrm{Var}(S_{n,m} v)}\leq \|\cA_{n}^{m} \|_{\om} \leq C_2  e^{ -c_2 \mathrm{Var}(S_{n,m} v)}
\end{equation} 
where $S_{n,m}v=\sum_{k=0}^{m-1}v_{n+k}\circ T_n^k$ and $\|\cA_{n}^{m}\|_{\om}$ is the operator norm of $A_n^m$ with respect to the norm $\|\cdot\|_{n,\om}$ on the domain and $\|\cdot\|_{n+m,\om}$ on the range. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.896177+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_836e411279fb67781e6648d5a4b877977e9877be4a0a404160447dc25dc585ac","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 45 of arXiv:2508.04938, 'Perfect t-embeddings of doubly periodic Aztec diamonds'] For the boundary points, we have
