{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.895397+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_836f20f8f41b51967085d36b1b295682be213bee5b55e25730a361547b4a73a3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 35 (\cite{BB23, BB24a}) of arXiv:2508.04938, 'Perfect t-embeddings of doubly periodic Aztec diamonds'] There is a diffeomorphism~$\Omega:\mathcal F_R\to \mathbb H^-$, such that for~$z\in \mathbb H^-$,
