{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:17:13.060934+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8374ca979c232c5159a8580d6f16e97ef6947a39ff7dd64d518373277a325c9d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm offdiagflucsameside of arXiv:2508.04954, 'Conditional exponential directed last passage percolation under a one-point upper large de'] [Off-diagonal two-point fluctuations]  
Fix $a,b > 0$ and $\ell> \bar{\mathcal{L}}(a,b)$. 
Let the function $h(x,y)$ and the positive numbers $\mathrm m$, $\mathsf{\sigma}$, and $\mathsf{c}_{\pm}$ be as defined in Theorems (thm:LLN of the paper) and (thm:diagfluc of the paper). 
Then, for two distinct points $(x_1, y_1), (x_2, y_2)\in (0,1)^2$ and two real numbers $\mathrm r_1, \mathrm r_2\in {\mathbb R}$, 
\begin{equation*}
\begin{split}
    &\lim_{N \to \infty} \mathbb{P} \left[\frac{\mathcal L(x_iaN, y_ibN) - h(x_i,y_i)N}{\sqrt{2} \mathsf{\sigma}   N^{1/2}} > \mathrm r_i, \ i=1, 2 \bigg| \mathcal{L}(aN, bN)= \ell N \right] \\ 
    &\qquad  \quad 
    = \begin{dcases}  \mathbb{P} \left[ \mathsf{c}_{+} \mathbb{B}^{\mathrm{br}}\left(\frac{\mathrm m y_i- x_i}{\mathrm m -1} \right) > \mathrm r_i,  i=1,2 \right] 
    \qquad &\text{if $\frac{1}{\mathrm m} < \frac{y_1}{x_1}, \frac{y_2}{x_2} < 1$,} \\
    \mathbb{P} \left[ \mathsf{c}_{-} \mathbb{B}^{\mathrm{br}}\left(\frac{\mathrm m x_i- y_i}{\mathrm m -1} \right) > \mathrm r_i,  i=1,2 \right]
\qquad &\text{if $1 < \frac{y_1}{x_1}, \frac{y_2}{x_2} < \mathrm m$,}
    \end{dcases}
\end{split} \end{equation*}
where $\mathbb{B}^{\mathrm{br}}$ is a standard Brownian bridge, and $\mathrm m$ is the constant defined in (equation eq:critical_slope of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.820140+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8377abd74a6cac4c9d0a3dfd671c810a1e997c65e6e38ba0281d337a16034750","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop thm: mminf-mixing of arXiv:2504.02207, 'Finite-Time behaviors of M/M/$n$ Queue: Mixing Time, Mean Queue Length and Tail Bounds'] Let $\pi_{t, \infty}$ be the queue length distribution at time $t$ of the continuous-time $M/M/\infty$ system with the arrival rate $\lambda$ and the service rate $\mu$ and let the stationary distribution be $\nu_\infty$, we have if $\lambda/\mu \in \Z^+$ then:
