{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.384559+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_838164e794e1ed4ffc6b6767a1db5de21e3ea0a2a675004fc75f2712088648b2","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition $2$-cyclical monotonicity of arXiv:2509.23086, 'On Optimal Markovian Couplings of L\'evy Processes'] A measurable set $E\subset \mathbb R^{d}\times \mathbb R^{d}$ is \emph{$2$-cyclically monotone} if for any finite sequences $\{(x_k,y_k)\}_{k=1}^N\subset E$, and any permutations $\sigma$ on $\{1,2,\cdots, N\}$, it holds
	\begin{align*}
		\sum_{k=1}^N \frac 12  |x_k-y_k|^2 &\le \sum_{k=1}^N \frac 12 |x_k-y_{\sigma(k)}|^2.
	\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.916190+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8382368eb1ac5809328da5b345f3f3ac1e795621b4fbc00c4d34a90ca60d0ac2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm|multipleFlips of arXiv:2504.08935, 'Higher-Order Derivatives of First-Passage Percolation with Respect to the Environment'] Assume that $\overrightarrow v\in W^m$ has all distinct components. Assume that $j$ is not a component of $\overrightarrow v$. Assume that $\overrightarrow \gamma$ and $\overrightarrow \delta$ are elements of $\{a,b\}^m$. Then, 
