{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:22:21.889160+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8382c775183700aeaac0b49bc9371123dbdb4ce51d2fbdd1b9fa733453afb6fd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor: tensor power of arXiv:2411.11345, 'Real Gaussian exponential sums via a real moment map'] Let $A_1,\ldots,A_m\subset \mathbb{R}$ be finite sets, let $\alpha^i\in \mathbb{R}_{>0}^{A_i}$, $i=1,\ldots,m$ and let $\alpha:=\alpha^1\otimes\cdots\otimes\alpha^m\in \mathbb{R}_{>0}^A$ where $A=A_1\times\cdots \times A_m\subset \mathbb{R}^m$. Then for every open sets $U_1,\ldots,U_m\subset\mathbb{R}$, writing $U:=U_1\times\cdots\times U_m$, we have:
  \begin{equation}
    \mathbb{E}\mathbb{S}\left\{\mathcal{E}_\alpha;U\right\}=\frac{m!b_m}{ 2^{m}}\prod_{i=1}^m\esol{\mathcal{E}_{\alpha^i};U_i}.
