{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:52:47.265588+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_83b1c99797624bdc3b5fecc30b8824145e9954a78188357bce43be2839f3692c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 27 of arXiv:2609.01114, 'Unbalanced spectral Tur\'an problem for color-critical graphs with prescribed large maximu'] Let	$ V_i':=V_i\setminus (L\cup K) $. Then, for every $i\in[p]$, every $j\in[p]\setminus\{i\}$, and every $v\in V_i'$, we have
	\begin{equation*}
		d_{V_j'}(v)\geq
		\begin{cases}
			\bigl(\frac1p-16\varepsilon\bigr)D, & \text{if } p=2,\\
			\bigl(\frac1p-20\varepsilon\bigr)D, & \text{if } p\geq 3.
