{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:20.954835+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_83fced74df35c202c8d5e8c31fd8264296e12e93f7c823ed677bda7a4fc8b674","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2604.09365, 'Cotlar martingale transforms and related singular integrals'] Suppose $Z=(Z^1, \dots, Z^n)\in \bC^n$  is a conformal martingale with the orthogonality property \eqref{off:diagonal}.
