{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:37:14.781594+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_840fed5ea653189a4e216202da5089dda68eb90dccf7104d818ce6c1665c3e65","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 5 of arXiv:2607.11275, 'The limit law of the maximum of discrete partial-sums distribution II'] If $\mathbb{E}S_N<0$ and $s\in\mathbb{C}$ is such that $|s|\leqslant 1$ and $s\neq0$, then

