{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:20:15.719017+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_841b19966de0864facead39fd63ff66f34f89e450f32af3bd705955d8daa769a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary of arXiv:2609.00973, 'The Vlasov-Maxwell point charge system : study of the spherically symmetric case'] Let $\varepsilon>0$ small enough, and $\gamma$ be a local solution to (equation equation_non_linear_gamma of the paper) with initial data $\gamma_0$. Assume that $\gamma_0$ satisfies, for all $\omega\in \mathcal{I}$,
