{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:00.613444+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_841bb5c3730521075aaebe045ccd455935d7708fabc2bb3c1a31b7e8c8c3a3d0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 7 of arXiv:2510.27589, 'Geodesic switches and exceptional times in dynamical Brownian last passage percolation'] For any $\beta>0$, as processes in $ (x,m)\leq (y,n)\in \ZZ_\RR$, we have the distributional equality
