{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:48:35.818427+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8424462e5d1cdee543c0521d9fe60a1cf0c3b1971ce2c9d8cc2f954b481d307f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:mat-slln of arXiv:2411.09516, 'Sharp Matrix Empirical Bernstein Inequalities\footnote{NeurIPS 2025 Poster}'] Let $ \mathbf{S} _n = \sum_{i=1}^n  \mathbf{Z} _i$ be a matrix martingale and $\{U_n \}$ an increasing positive predictable process on $\mathcal{F}$. For any $p\in[1,2]$, on the set
