{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:47:01.615780+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8428a639742eaac0737694b3ba5c15f1e3b70782f93d2152b9309253395ee52b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 6 of arXiv:2604.22644, '2604.22644'] Let $D_1$ be the duration of the first excursion regardless of whether it terminates at $0$ or $N$, i.e., $D_1=\min\{\theta_1,\tau_N\}$. The expected value of the first hitting time to $N$ is given by:
