{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:21:45.380385+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_843aa762acb981eb0e3a4f4377324113238e2bff55b35ede27371c68429e3361","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 25 of arXiv:2607.27535, 'Universal topological statistics on \\ triangulated singular spaces'] The set $k \cdot \ordsimp{d}$ triangulates into FK-simplices as follows:
    \begin{align} 
        k \cdot \ordsimp{d} = \bigcup_{I \subseteq \indexset{d-1}} \bigcup_{\substack{\vecbf n \in \vecbf N_{d, k} [I] \\ \permelt \in \permgrp_d [I]}} (\vecbf n + \permelt \ordsimp{d})
    \end{align}
    where $\vecbf N_{d, k} [I] \subset \ZZ^d$ and $\permgrp_d [I] \subseteq \permgrp_d$ are defined as:
    \begin{align*}
        \vecbf N_{d, k} [I] =& \bigg\{(n_1, \ldots n_d) \in \ZZ^d \>\bigg|\> k-1 \ge n_1 \ge \cdots \ge n_d \ge 0 \text{, and } (i \in I \iff n_i = n_{i+1}) \bigg\} \\
        \permgrp_d [I] =& \bigg\{ \permelt \in \permgrp_d \>\bigg|\> i \in I \implies \permelt^{-1}(i) < \permelt^{-1}(i+1) \bigg\}
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:52:32.262704+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8446ca3ca7a405a052e0bf8ada01aa1c6da5f7e144333b8f720344fc090b751e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition D:APM of arXiv:2609.03939, 'Arithmetic probability measures'] A measure $\mu \in \mathcal{P}(K)$ is called an \emph{arithmetic probability measure}
if there exists a sequence $\{\alpha_n\}$ of
algebraic {\bf integers} satisfying the following conditions:
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
\item  $\deg \alpha_n \to \infty$ as $n \to \infty$;
\item  For every neighborhood $U$ of $K$, there exists $N \in \mathbb{N}$ such that
$\mathcal O(\alpha_n)\subset U$ for all $n\geq N$;
\item  The normalized counting measure on $\mathcal O(\alpha_n)$ converges to $\mu$ 
in the weak* topology as $n \to \infty$, i.e.,
for every bounded continuous function $f: \mathbb{C} \to \mathbb{R}$,
\[
\lim_{n \to \infty} \frac{1}{\deg \alpha_n} \sum_{\gamma \in \mathcal O(\alpha_n)} f(\gamma)= \int f(z) \, d \mu (z).
\]
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

