{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.588138+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_845d9402ce98ff80783b9e03b72ee670d17ebe7fb736811f681fd9e0ff706b85","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm Thm_fsop of arXiv:2608.30548, 'Finite speed of propagation and waiting time phenomena for stochastic porous media equatio'] Let $u$ be the unique kinetic solution to (equation Eq_SPME_intro of the paper) under the assumptions (equation equation_n_m_together of the paper)--(equation Eq_ass_B3 of the paper). Then $u$ has finite speed of propagation.  Furthermore, if, for a given $x_0 \in \mathbb{T}^d\setminus \mathrm{supp}(u_0)$, there exists $r_0>0$ such that
