{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:03:39.768438+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_84623479fa904e34de5175988fa9c135b40884ce7e2335ca4ce0a82bf7dc3186","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def: graph model 1 of arXiv:2411.02898, '\vspace{-1.5cm}The connectivity and phase transition in inhomogeneous random graphs of fin'] Let $m$ be a positive integer, $\bm{a} = (a_1, \dots, a_m)$ a length $m$ vector with positive entries, and $\bm{c} = (c_{kl})_{1\leq k, l \leq m}$ a $m \times m$ symmetric matrix with non-negative entries. Consider simple graphs (i.e. graphs with no loops or multiple edges) with fixed labeled vertices 
