{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:51:15.020710+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_84ef8f8a13b7d5d10fdb5b3589e2bba2babcd4f66f987eb8c0a97b654f8561ce","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Thm:ProjectedGDEquivalence of arXiv:2609.03762, '\vspace*{-2cm} Projected Riemannian Gradient Descent for the Bures--Wasserstein Barycenter'] Let $f : \mathrm{PD}(d) \to \mathbb{R}$ be differentiable, $g := f \circ \pi$, and $(\eta_t)_{t \geq 0}$ a sequence of step sizes.
        Let $(S_t)_{t \geq 0}$ be generated by Projected BW-GD from $S_0 \in [\alpha I, \beta I]$,
        \begin{equation} 
            S_{t+1} = \mathrm{clip}_{\alpha, \beta}\Big[ \left[I - 2 \eta_t \nabla f(S_t)\right] \, S_t \, \left[I - 2 \eta_t \nabla f(S_t)\right] \Big],
