{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:58:44.403274+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_84ff1dfbdbdd08b820b1862bc8eaed38723cabe29c4bfe2382da90b4cb620a2a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2609.02842, 'Global Well-posedness and Asymptotic Analysis of a Damped Nonlinear Wave Equation with a C'] Let $\vartheta_0\in D(\mathcal{A})\cap\mathcal{M}$ and $\vartheta_1\in H_0^1(\varOmega)$ with $(\vartheta_0,\vartheta_1)=0$. 	Let $\vartheta$ be the unique strong solution of \eqref{asym1}. Then there exists a sequence $\{t_n\}_{n\in\mathbb{N}}$, $t_n\to\infty$ as $n\to\infty$ and $\vartheta_{\infty}\in H_0^1(\varOmega)\cap\mathcal{M}$  such that 
