{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:23:27.793700+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_850a005664a1ac8b5fc890fe252fe33b410720fe502e3fc34139ab28776c5db3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop ContOUGFF of arXiv:2606.11043, 'Thick points under Gaussian free field dynamics'] The process $(\Phi_{\varepsilon}(x,t))_{\varepsilon>0, x\in D, t\in \mathbb R}$ has a continuous modification (which we also identify with $\varPhi$). Furthermore, 
