{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:11.423548+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_85793db6149f04beb3fbc00ea96e818f796840cd65d60050971fabaa7836200b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 29 (Convergence and separation of the discrete population map) of arXiv:2606.09121, 'Truncated Signature Information for Mixed Fractional Brownian Paths'] For a finite scale set $\mcH=\{h_0,\ldots,h_{L-1}\}$, define
\[
    \Gamma_{\mcH}^{(n)}(\theta)
    :=\bigl(q_\theta(h_j),R_\theta^{(n)}(h_j)\bigr)_{j=0}^{L-1}.
\]
Then
\begin{equation}
    \Gamma_{\mcH}^{(n)}(\theta)
    =\left(
        \sum_{r=1}^Kv_rh_j^{\alpha_r},
        \sum_{r=1}^Kv_r\kappa_n(\alpha_r)h_j^{\alpha_r}
      \right)_{j=0}^{L-1}.
\end{equation}
For every fixed $\theta$,
\begin{equation}
    \|\Gamma_{\mcH}^{(n)}(\theta)-\Gamma_{\mcH}(\theta)\|
    \le C_{\theta,\mcH}n^{-\min\{1,\alpha_1\}}.
\end{equation}
If Assumption \ref{ass:compact} holds, then
\begin{equation}
    \sup_{\theta\in\Theta_K}
    \|\Gamma_{\mcH}^{(n)}(\theta)-\Gamma_{\mcH}(\theta)\|
    \le C_{\mcH,\Theta_K}n^{-\min\{1,\alpha_-\}}.
\end{equation}
Consequently, if $\mcH$ contains at least $K$ distinct positive scales, then for every $\epsilon>0$ there exists $n_0=n_0(\epsilon,\mcH,\Theta_K)$ such that, for all $n\ge n_0$,
\begin{align}
    &\inf_{\substack{\theta,\theta'\in\Theta_K\\
                     \|\theta-\theta'\|\ge\epsilon}}
    \|\Gamma_{\mcH}^{(n)}(\theta)-\Gamma_{\mcH}^{(n)}(\theta')\| \\
    &\qquad\ge \frac12
    \inf_{\substack{\theta,\theta'\in\Theta_K\\
                     \|\theta-\theta'\|\ge\epsilon}}
    \|\Gamma_{\mcH}(\theta)-\Gamma_{\mcH}(\theta')\|
    >0.
\end{align}
Thus sufficiently fine interpolation preserves positive separation at every prescribed parameter resolution $\epsilon$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:49:17.501015+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_857a368f917099b2d86ac74092460d4d6924a722a9f81353483ee898e4ce1117","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2605.30030, 'Critical exponents for planar random-cluster model with cluster-weight~$q=4$'] There exists~$C>0$ such that for every~$\ep \ge \delta>0$ and every event~$A$ depending on~$B_{2\eps}(0)$,  
