    h_q =  \sum_{\substack{\sigma \in {\Pi}(k_1,\dots,k_m)\\ A\subseteq \sigma_{\geq 2} \\ |A| +|\sigma_1|=q }} H(\sigma, A; f_1, \dots, f_m) ,
    \end{equation}
    where we have adopted the notation (equation e:sym of the paper) and $h_0= \mathbb{E}[\Phi]$; in particular, $h_K = {\rm sym}(f_1\otimes\cdots\otimes f_m)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.240941+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_85aebe4a8d21fd1eb9924bb35bfc4640d0ee725b9531d24db8041fe5ca3f1462","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2604.14752, 'Strong and weak rates of convergence in the Smoluchowski--Kramers approximation for stocha'] Let Assumptions~\ref{ass:fLip} and \ref{ass:mapping-f} be satisfied. Then for all $h\in H$ and $\kappa\in[0,1)$, there exists a constant $C_{\kappa}(T)\in(0,\infty)$ such that for all $0\le s\le t\le T$ one has 
