{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:41:29.017726+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_85b22b8b4236a1b97842409706ef1dd99d2af8ab79fa4f77f1a1e8fb7fbc149e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 13 of arXiv:2608.26288, 'Muon with Finite Newton--Schulz: The Smoothing Benefit in Nonsmooth Nonconvex Optimization'] Suppose~\cref{ass:oracle} and~\cref{ass:smooth} hold, $\lVert G_s\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leq G_{\mathrm{op}}$ almost surely for every $s$, and fix $\epsilon>0$.
