{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.572213+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_85bb394e4cdc82ff80792f5a5a6e0b0fff8f9245dd6790268b8807f5ed67e994","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 14 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d\geq 2$ and $G=(V,E)$, $H=(V',E')$ be two subgraphs of $\mathbb Z^d$ such that $G\subset H$. Then, for every $A\subset V$, every $J\in (\mathbb R^+)^E$, $J'\in (\mathbb R^+)^{E'}$ satisfying $J_e\leq J_e'$ for $e\in E$, and every $\mathsf{h},\mathsf{h}'\in (\mathbb R^+)^{V(H)}$ satisfying $\mathsf{h}_x\leq \mathsf{h}'_x$ for $x\in V$, one has
\begin{equation}
	\langle \sigma_A\rangle_{G,J,\mathsf{h}}\leq \langle \sigma_A\rangle_{H,J',\mathsf{h}'}.
\end{equation}
Moreover, if we further assume that the restriction of $J'$ to $E$ is equal to $J$, then for every $v\in V$, one has
\begin{equation}
	\langle\sigma_v\rangle^+_{H,J'}\leq \langle \sigma_v\rangle_{G,J}^+.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

