{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:40.359649+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_85cfb55a4a01a894ed81a7ddb5c32127dd569e4d7aca5bef1b50e032ae9a318d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 25 of arXiv:2511.09517, 'From Cannings model to Brownian motion conditioned on local time profile'] For any $1\le k\le q_n(h^*)$, the process $(X^{(k)}_{h^*-j} : 0 \le j \le h^*)$ is a Markov chain with respect to $(\mathcal{G}^{(k)}_{h^*-j} : 0 \le j \le h^*)$. Moreover, for any $1 \le j \le h^*$, its transition probabilities satisfy
