{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.247571+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_85e5d889d2c3d67fab8b85c8dc8038d88ae505bb4015f1f5e62a33bc30a0b08e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition jets of arXiv:2507.10545, 'KPZ equation from a class of nonlinear SPDEs in infinite volume'] \fsp We say that {\small$\mathsf{F}:\R^{\Z}\to\R$} is a \emph{local function} if there exists a subset $\mathbb{I}\subseteq\Z$ independent of $N$ such that for any {\small${\boldsymbol{\phi}}\in\R^{\Z}$}, the value {\small$\mathsf{F}[{\boldsymbol{\phi}}]$} depends only on {\small${\boldsymbol{\phi}}_{\x}$} for $\x\in\mathbb{I}$; we often refer to {\small$\mathbb{I}$} as the \emph{support} of {\small$\mathsf{F}$}. 

Fix any {\small$\mathfrak{k}=0,1,2$}. We let {\small$\mathrm{Jet}_{\mathfrak{k}}^{\perp}$} tbe the set of local functions whose {\small$\mathfrak{k}$}-jet is zero, i.e. {\small$\mathsf{F}\in\mathrm{Jet}_{\mathfrak{k}}^{\perp}$} if and only if

\begin{align*}
\partial_{\sigma}^{\ell}\E^{\sigma}\mathsf{F}[\bphi]|_{\sigma=0}=0 \quad\text{for all } \ell=0,\ldots,\mathfrak{k}.
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:17.757294+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_85e7e9ac936193afc42b7449f440c1dff988f3cc0d500812e0bcabe206276358","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 (CLT) of arXiv:2511.05386, 'CLT for $\beta$-ensembles with Freud weights, application to the KLS conjecture in Schatte'] Let $p\geq 2$, and $f\in \mathcal{C}^3(\R)$ with at most exponential growth, \emph{i.e.\@} there exists $C>0$ such that $\abs{f(x)} \leq Ce^{C\abs{x}}$ for any $x \in \R$. Then, the following convergence holds in terms of moments:
		\begin{equation}
			L_N(f) \xrightarrow[N\rightarrow\infty]{} \mc{N}\left(m_V(f),\sigma^2(f)\right) 
		\end{equation}
		where the mean and the variance of the limiting Gaussian distribution are given by:
		\begin{align*}
			m_V(f)&\coloneqq\left(\dfrac{1}{2}-\dfrac{1}{\beta}\right)\int_{-1}^{1}\Xi^{-1}[f]'(x)\diff\mu_V(x)\\
			\sigma^2(f)&\coloneqq\dfrac{1}{\beta\pi^2}\iint_{[-1,1]^2}\left(\dfrac{f(x)-f(y)}{x-y}\right)^2 \cdot \dfrac{1-xy}{\sqrt{1-x^2}\sqrt{1-y^2}}\diff x\diff y
		\end{align*}
		where the operator $\Xi^{-1}$ is given explicitly in Lemma~\ref{lem:inverse_master_op} (taking $\alpha=1$ for $p>2$ and $\alpha=0$ for $p=2$). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:39:11.682316+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_85e8455a1ba8bff1aceca593c48aad6f57b85adcce8023861559167c8ea2f88e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 55 (Dimension-free tensor error transform) of arXiv:2608.04993, '2608.04993'] Let $P\in\Smax$, let $q\ge2$, and let $Z$ be a predictable continuous
$H$-valued process such that
\[
 \left\|\left(\int_0^T\|Z_r\|_H^2\,\dd r\right)^{1/2}
 \right\|_{L^q(P)}<\infty.
\]
Define the $\mathcal S_2(H)$-valued error transform
\begin{equation}
 \mathcal E^P(Z)_t:=\int_0^t Z_r\otimes\dd X_r.
\end{equation}
Then
\begin{equation}
 \|\mathcal E^P(Z)\|_{\mathbb S^q(P;\mathcal S_2)}
 \le C\bigl(\sqrt{q\Lambda}+B\sqrt T\bigr)
 \left\|\left(\int_0^T\|Z_r\|_H^2\,\dd r\right)^{1/2}
 \right\|_{L^q(P)},
