{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.310229+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_85f398e0cd69ab1b92550a670bccae913c56b38712839376b786ce8bb4bd3de1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2603.14302, 'On Partition Functions for Time-Inhomogeneous Branching Random Walks'] (Upper bounds)
        Let $(a_n)_{n \in \mathbb{N}}$ be a sequence of real numbers such that $|a_n| \to \infty$ as $n \to \infty$. Suppose that for every $\alpha \in (0,1)$, we have:
