\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:38:57.117041+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8609ef322172faa15c77690ff0f26677263b1a9db1aad98e38f3ceba3b6ef51b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2604.04823, '2604.04823'] Under Assumptions~\ref{a:criticalpts}--\ref{a: nondegeneracy} on~$U$, the following properties hold.
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item 
        $\partial\Omega$ is a $(d-1)$-dimensional manifold of class~$C^5$.

        \item 
        There exists~$r_0 > 0$ such that for any
        \begin{equation}
            x\in \Gamma_{r_0}\defeq \set{y\in \T^d\st \dist(y, \partial\Omega) < r_0}\,,
        \end{equation}
        there exists a unique projection~$\xi(x) \in \partial\Omega$ satisfying
        \begin{equation}
            \dist(x,\partial\Omega) = |x-\xi(x)|\,.
        \end{equation}
        Moreover,
        \begin{equation}
            \xi \in C^4(\Gamma_{r_0}, \partial\Omega)\,.
        \end{equation}

        \item 
