{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:45:17.697364+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_862051529fc394307423ff230d4d5e6fd9280229db518d4e723afd54c0dbf3b5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma beta-lem2 of arXiv:2604.08462, 'Convergence of $k$-point functions in\\ high dimensional percolation'] Let $G$ be any  real function defined on vertex subsets of $B(2K)$; suppose $x_1, x_2 \notin B(2K)$. For each edge $f$, we have
