{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:41.019509+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8620caf699563748cdec895692c3286d5f2ca50f6eab2175e55841ba7d0ead91","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2-l07 of arXiv:2412.04015, 'Linear fluctuation of interfaces in Glauber-Kawasaki dynamics'] For all $N\ge 1$, 
\begin{equation}

L^*_N {\mathbf 1}\; =\;  U \;+\;  K\, \Upsilon \;,
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}

\begin{gathered}
{\color{blue} U (\eta)} \,:=\,
\sum_{x\in {\mathbb T}^d_N} \big\{  (\Delta_N \varrho) (x)\,
+\, K\, G_0(x)\, \big\}  \, \zeta_x 
\\
{\color{blue} \Upsilon (\eta)} \,:=\,
\sum_{j=1}^d \sum_{x\in {\mathbb T}^d_N}  G_{1,j}(x) \, \omega_{x} \, \omega_{x+e_j}
\,+\,
\sum_{x\in {\mathbb T}^d_N}  G_2(x) \, \omega_{x-e_1} \, \omega_{x} \,
\omega_{x+e_1} \;,
\end{gathered}
\end{equation}
and $\Delta_N$ stands for the discrete Laplacian, $(\Delta_NG)(x) =
N^2 \sum_{1\le j \le d} [ G(x+e_j) + G(x-e_j)  - 2 G(x) ]$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:48:35.812378+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_862217f166756548f907777a388cf00c4d412dea19cf03cbca267ae65d5095ba","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main_bd_integral of arXiv:2411.09482, 'Anomalous Regularization in Kazantsev-Kraichnan Model'] Let $d\ge 2$, $s\in (0,d/2)$ and $\alpha\in (0,1)$ with $s+\alpha>1$. There exist $\eta_{d,s,\alpha}\in \mathbb{R}$, $\rho_{d,s,\alpha}\ge 0$ such that the matrix-valued integral $\mathbb H_{d,s,\alpha} (n)$ defined in (equation eq:H_def of the paper) satisfies for every $n\in\mathbb{R}^d\smallsetminus\{0\}$, for all $v\in \mathbb{S}^{d-1}$ with $v\cdot n=0$,
    \begin{equation}
        |v \cdot \mathbb H_{d,s,\alpha} (n) v +\eta_{d,s,\alpha}|n|^{-2s+2-2\alpha}| \leqslant \rho_{d,s,\alpha}|n|^{-2s}.
    \end{equation}
    The constant $\eta_{d,s,\alpha}$ takes the form, for some $C_{d,s,\alpha}>0$,



    \begin{multline*}
        \eta_{d,s,\alpha} = C_{d,s,\alpha} \Big(  (d-1)(s+\alpha-1)(d+2-2s-2\alpha) -\alpha(d-1)(d+2\alpha) +4\alpha (s+\alpha-1) \Big)
    \end{multline*}
    hence $\eta_{d,s,\alpha}$ is strictly positive if and only if (hp:main_hp of the paper) on $d$, $s$ and $\alpha$ is met. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:04.860995+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8622b96afd948c581412b2ee63ddf7e04504d09d84d6693ec3c834107cb34810","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prp 32 (\textit{cf.} {\cite[Proposition 4.3) of arXiv:2511.21496, 'Optimal local central limit theorems on Wiener chaos'] {OptimalBErates}}]
