{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:32:11.126134+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8627a41598b527b564feb136b9bf514ed6e482844c2746f5a7e6494c99ce9292","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem a4:thm:recovery of arXiv:2510.01838, 'Shadow and percolation I: discrete landscapes with independence'] There exists a deterministic application $\Psi : \overline{\mathbb{R}}^{\mathbb{Z}^2} \to \mathbb{R}^{\mathbb{Z}^2}$ such that the following holds. Let $X: \mathbb{Z}^2 \to \mathbb{R}$ and $\mu$ be such that Assumptions (a4:a:a1 of the paper) and (a4:a:a4 of the paper) hold, then
