{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:57:16.048192+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_862f8180e85429f4ba9bad74d747e8a00f12251da410a8321bbaf35b5299fee5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition number_of_simple_tight_closed_geodesics of arXiv:2506.02611, '\textbf{The tight length spectrum of large-genus random hyperbolic surfaces with many cusp'] For any $\mu_g \underset{g \to +\infty}{\rightarrow}\mu_c$ such that $\mu_c - \mu_g = o(g^{-2})$, any disjoint compact intervals $([a_i,b_i])_{1\le i \le n}$ and any $r_1,\cdots,r_n \ge 1$ we have
