{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:04.863670+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8630b1452598bed24dc664074eafd5cc6a7c94b74f5d5f189a95743147cdd75c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 27 (Uniform Harnack Inequality) of arXiv:2511.22156, ''] There exists constants $C_H,\theta>1$ which are independent of $n,r$ such that if $h$ is harmonic in $B(z,r)\cap \tilde{F}_n$, then
