{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:53:39.182875+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_86824ad23981db8df97d07c05d4475c785e5d67916592a156bd90308e7fecb02","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 (Overconfidence for $d \geq 1$) of arXiv:2608.26974, 'Why not to use the Gaussian kernel'] Let $d \geq 1$ and $\sigma = 0$.
