{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:55:27.166031+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8683106d24744664b0fa8b15187121dbbffeee53dba7304e5c4a7168fbde2e6b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition U delta density max case of arXiv:2609.04072, 'Oort's conjecture for split unitary Shimura varieties'] Let $s_0\in \llbracket 0,N-1\rrbracket$ and $\delta\in \operatorname{Hom}_{\breve{\mathbb{Z}}_p}(\Lambda_0,\Lambda_{s_0})$, and suppose that either:
