{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:01:39.421935+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_869ee5e54ad966f326621d1dc9522c0113ecb210ee02be696ff57131a6a44cdb","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma mix line and cycles of arXiv:2607.22156, 'A random matrix approach to lamplighter groups'] Let $C_{1},\cdots,C_{K}$ be test-graphs whose underlying graphs are cycles of length $c_{1},\cdots,c_{K}$ respectively. Let $L_{1},\cdots,L_{M}$ be test-graphs whose underlying graphs are lines of length $l_{1},\cdots,l_{M}$ respectively. We have the following equality,
        \begin{multline}
            \mathbb{E}\left[\prod_{k=1}^{K}\mathrm{Tr}^{0}(C_{k}(V_{N}))\prod_{m=1}^{M}\mathrm{Tr}^{0}(L_{m}(V_{N}))\right]=\\mathbb{N}^{K+M}\mathbb{E}\left[\prod_{k=1}^{K}\frac{c_{k}\eta_{c_{k}}}{N}\prod_{m=1}^{M}\left(1-\frac{\sum_{j=1}^{l_{m}-1}j\eta_{j}}{N}\right)\right]
        \end{multline}
        where $L:=\mathrm{max}\{c_{1},\cdots,c_{K},l_{1},\cdots,l_{M}\}$ and for all $1\leq j\leq L$, let $\eta_{j}$ is the number of cycles of length $j$ of $V_{N}$","status":"unverified"}

