{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:43:43.441480+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_86c09826511d182134f583ac99ab811958a69df9435ea9f3c3fbf169c8a7f4d2","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:heatkernel of arXiv:2509.04155, 'An Approach to Sub-Gaussian Heat Kernel Estimates via Analysis on Metric Spaces'] Let $(\mathcal{E},\mathcal{F})$ be a strongly local regular Dirichlet form on $L^2(X,\mu)$ and $\{P_t\}_{t > 0}$ be the associated Markov semigroup; see [FOT].
    A family of Borel measurable function $\{p_t\}_{t > 0}$, $p_t : X \times X \to [0,\infty]$, is a \emph{heat kernel} of $(\mathcal{E},\mathcal{F})$ if for every $t > 0$ the function $p_t$ is an integral kernel of $P_t$, meaning for all $t > 0$ and $f \in L^2(X,\mu)$,
    \[
    P_t(f)(x) = \int_X p_t(x,y)f(y)\, d\mu \quad \text{for $\mu$-almost every $x \in X$.}
    \]
    We say that $(\mathcal{E},\mathcal{F})$ satisfies the \emph{heat kernel estimates} (eq:HKMain of the paper) if there is a heat kernel $\{p_t\}_{t > 0}$ of $(\mathcal{E},\mathcal{F})$ and constants $C,C_1,C_2,c,\kappa > 0$ such that for all $t > 0$,
    \begin{align}
    \tag{$\textup{HKE}(\Psi)$}
    p_t(x,y) & \leq \frac{C}{\mu(B(x,\Psi^{-1}(t))}\exp\left( -C_1t\Phi \left(C_2\frac{d(x,y)}{t}\right) \right) \text{ for $\mu$-almost every $x,y \in X$}, \\
    p_t(x,y) & \geq \frac{c}{\mu(B(x,\Psi^{-1}(t)))} \text{ for $\mu$-almost every $x,y \in X$ with $d(x,y) \leq \kappa \Psi^{-1}(t)$}. \nonumber
\end{align}
    If $\Psi(r) = r^\beta$ for some $\beta \geq 2$, we write \hyperref[eq:HKMain]{$\textup{HKE}(\beta)$} instead.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:15:16.658550+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_86c2a1432083f8065323356bdeaa983cbce925a0283c49a2b2cdc3b3e7d4a3c3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 4 of arXiv:2608.30796, 'Tumor boundary instability induced by pressure feedback'] For fixed \(\lambda>0\) and \(\gamma>0\), the Fr\'{e}chet derivative
