{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:21:28.714968+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_86c42e94d1123451168bec627acd8a8bcfcd188cef8db93e8593a1dbcb29c073","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2605.03718, 'Potential Hessian Ascent III:\\ Sampling the Sherrington--Kirkpatrick Model at $\beta < 1/'] Let $\mu$ be a distribution on $\slice nk$. Define the \emph{down-up walk} as the Markov chain defined by the composition of the \emph{down} and \emph{up operators} $P_\mu = D_{k\to k-1}U_{k-1\to k,\mu}$, defined below.
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item The down operator $D_{k\to k-1}$ is defined by
        \[
D_{k\to k-1} (S,T) = \begin{cases}
    \frac{1}{k}, & \text{if $T= S\setminus \{i\}$ for some $i\in S$}\\
    0,&\text{otherwise.}
\end{cases}
        \]
    \item The up operator $U_{k-1\to k, \mu}$ is defined as the adjoint of $D_{k\to k-1}$ with respect to $\mu$. Explicitly, 
    \[
U_{k-1\to k,\mu}(T,S) =  \begin{cases}
    \fc{\mu(S)}{\sum_{j\in [n]\setminus T}\mu(T\cup \{j\})}, & \text{if $S = T\cup \{i\}$ for some $i\in [n]\setminus T$}\\
    0,&\text{otherwise.}
\end{cases}
    \]
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:23:37.803073+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_86c4d398c55be84b980fad9962214104d8d2225da1e5af1175bb14f134ccbfaa","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 (\cite{MMO26}) of arXiv:2609.03558, 'Local well-posedness of the higher-order nonlinear Schr\"{o}dinger equation on the half-li'] Suppose $0 \le s < \frac12$, $2 \le \lambda \le \frac{7-2s}{1-2s}$, and
$$
(\mu,r)=\left(\frac{6\lambda}{(1-2s)(\lambda-1)},\frac{2\lambda}{1+2(\lambda-1)s}\right).
$$
Then,
$$
\bigl\||\varphi|^{\lambda-1}\varphi\bigr\|_{L_t^1((0,T);H_x^s(\mathbb{R}))}
\le c(s,\lambda)T^{\frac{\mu-\lambda}{\mu}}
\|\varphi\|_{L_t^\mu((0,T);H_x^{s,r}(\mathbb{R}))}^{\lambda},
$$
and
$$
\bigl\||\varphi|^{\lambda-1}\varphi-|\psi|^{\lambda-1}\psi\bigr\|_{L_t^1((0,T);H_x^s(\mathbb{R}))}
\le c(s,\lambda)T^{\frac{\mu-\lambda}{\mu}}
\left(
\|\varphi\|_{L_t^\mu((0,T);H_x^{s,r}(\mathbb{R}))}^{\lambda-1}
+
\|\psi\|_{L_t^\mu((0,T);H_x^{s,r}(\mathbb{R}))}^{\lambda-1}
\right)
\|\varphi-\psi\|_{L_t^\mu((0,T);H_x^{s,r}(\mathbb{R}))}.
$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:02:11.352229+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_86c6530c9ae9e749c327b52fb73c7c2e0f8d7425900821189ed21ad0eda4ba81","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem bound-im-part of arXiv:2510.26123, 'Directed distances in bipolar-oriented triangulations:\\ exact exponents and scaling limit'] Let $f:\mathbb{N}_0\to[0,\infty)$ and set $S(k):=\sum_{y\ge k} f(y)$.
