{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.670121+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_86d657f404ea64884a9f65868864c4fe2107eb5e2fd3ec32b7235a8aa2e648c9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:g(k)-cauchy-schwarz of arXiv:2602.14998, 'Random geometric graphs with smooth kernels: sharp detection threshold and a spectral conj'] Let $g(k)$ and $a_{\boldsymbol{\ell}}$ be defined in ~((eq:def-g(k) of the paper)) and ~((eq:def-a-ell of the paper)) respectively. 
