{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.113615+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_86f1c4901f820ebc4e70f8f8ecdcff24b08ed9200fa8722b72cb416c6e337ea9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:pole-projected-positive-strip-closure of arXiv:2608.16119, 'Fully nonlinear parabolic equations under a fixed reference diffusion: weighted \texorpdfs'] Assume the coefficient and weight hypotheses
(equation eq:pole-coefficient-class of the paper) and (equation eq:pole-weight-threshold of the paper), with
$0\leq\alpha<1/2$.  Fix an integer $N_{\mathrm H}\geq1$,
