{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:22:48.867215+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_86f301d56f826a6d20441436c6a9ef459bae092db2820b882d7cf5b0a2760819","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2608.29143, 'Least Variability in a Polynomial-Square Class\\ of Rational Kernels'] Define
\begin{equation}
 w_n(s)=\exp\left(-\frac{\e^s}{2}\right)\Lag_n(\e^s),
 \qquad s\in\R.
\end{equation}
Then, the zeros of $w_n$ are $z_{1,n},\ldots,z_{n,n}$ and
\begin{equation}
 w_n''(s)+W_n(s)w_n(s)=0,
 \qquad
 W_n(s)=\left(n+\frac12\right)\e^s-\frac{\e^{2s}}4.
\end{equation}
Moreover,
\begin{equation}
 W_n(s)\leq\left(n+\frac12\right)^2,
\end{equation}
with equality only when $\e^s=2n+1$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:51:33.331798+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_86f36914ad19228038b66a748ecae7bcaff1f2c5987ad0208ee5aeae79af1c58","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lm:tensor-bil of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] Let $S\subset T$ be a cleft and let ${\mathcal{C}}^\otimes$ be an $S$-cocomplete symmetric monoidal $T$-$\infty$-category such that the tensor product is $S$-bilinear. Then also $\smash{{\mathcal{C}}_{/X}^\otimes}$ is $S$-cocomplete, and the tensor product is $S$-bilinear.
    \begin{proof}
        By [martiniwolf2022presentable]*{Corollary~A.1.4}, the underlying $T$-$\infty$-category of $\smash{{\mathcal{C}}_{/X}^\otimes}$ is $S$-cocomplete, and the forgetful functor is $S$-cocontinuous. Using that the latter is also conservative and symmetric monoidal, we immediately see that the tensor product on $\smash{{\mathcal{C}}_{/X}^\otimes}$ preserves $S$-colimits in each variable as this holds in ${\mathcal{C}}^\otimes$.
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

