{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:18:19.207764+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_872ac1e17a9e11f213873aa51d3983d6168cacde3999bfb41e81178ecae55d2a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 18 (Proposition \ref{prop:margin Z} in the main text) of arXiv:2608.28991, 'Jigsaw-CRL: Recovering Global Latent Causal Order from Fragmented Multi-Client Interventio'] For $Z$ generated by Eq.~\eqref{eq:gloabl latent}, let $Z_k=(Z_{(i)})_{i\in O_k}$. Then
\begin{equation}
Z_k = \bA_k Z_k + E_k,
\end{equation}
where
\begin{align}

    \bA_k
    &=
    [\bA]_{O_k,O_k}
    +
    [\bA]_{O_k,M_k}
    (\bI-[\bA]_{M_k,M_k})^{-1}
    [\bA]_{M_k,O_k}, \\
    E_k
    &=
    E_{O_k}
    +
    [\bA]_{O_k,M_k}
    (\bI-[\bA]_{M_k,M_k})^{-1}
    E_{M_k}.
\end{align}
Moreover, $E_k$ has mean zero and covariance
\begin{equation}

    \bSigma_k
    =
    [\bSigma]_{O_k,O_k}
    +
    [\bA]_{O_k,M_k}
    (\bI-[\bA]_{M_k,M_k})^{-1}
    [\bSigma]_{M_k,M_k}
    (\bI-[\bA]_{M_k,M_k})^{-T}
    [\bA]_{O_k,M_k}^{T}.
\end{equation}

Furthermore $\prec_k$, which is induced by $\bA_k$, is exactly the restriction of the $\prec$, which is induced by $\bA$,  to $\cV_k = O_k$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.886567+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_872b38442e775e8a5714d9f58ecfdc955f6f74a5acdb62358b40ea8c592cc9e4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main-approx of arXiv:2606.29557, 'Propagation of chaos for Belavkin equations beyond pure states'] Assume that
\begin{equation}
  \delta_N
  :=
  \left\|
    \rho_0^N-\gamma_0^{\otimes N}
  \right\|_1
  \longrightarrow0.

\end{equation}
Then propagation of chaos holds.  More precisely, for every fixed $n\ge1$ and
$T>0$, there exists a constant $C>0$ depending on $n, T,  h,V,L^{(1)},\ldots,L^{(m)},\eta $ 
