{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:55.640289+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8765b484c33753777eac20b67a59262f67ec8ee28527014da00ea15f76de7b47","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 13 of arXiv:2605.23529, 'Generalized Bessel-Dunkl diffusions'] Let $\qm(X)$ be defined in \eqref{eq:qproc:defn} and assume that $X(0) = x_0\in \Cc$ is such that $\qm(x_0)>0$. Then, for $t<  \taumz\wedge \tau_{\mathcal K}$, the process $\Qm = -\ln \qm(X)$ is a continuous semi-martingale with the local martingale part 
