{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:01:56.343701+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_87671ade7d0960693a70dce47da205a7ede5050199f062c334d5eb3cd646c096","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn def:witness of arXiv:2609.01499, 'On the rigidity of sloped height functions in $d\ge 3$ \\ and non-crossing surfaces'] Our witness $\mathcal W = (A,\epsilon, W(A), \iota)$ will consist of 
