  &= \mathbf{E}_0 \Big[ I \left[ E^{'',0}(F;u,v,x') \right] \Big] + \!\!\!\!\!\sum_{\{u'_0,v'_0\} \not\in E_W \cup \{u,v\}} \!\!\!\!\! p D(u'_0,v'_0) \\
  &\qquad\qquad  \mathbf{E}_0 \Big[ I \left[ E^{'',0}(F;u,v,u'_0) \right] 
       \tau^{\widetilde{\mathcal{D}}_0}(v'_0,x') \Big]. }","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.290892+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_876961a1a38a2a260ced5d0d081754a25f85de7c0171e7e1742ad7a1030b07ac","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 29 of arXiv:2606.23099, 'Path-dependent Affine Processes'] Assume that the linear growth condition \eqref{LG-condition-existence} holds and let $X = (X(t))_{t \in [0,T]}$ be a solution to \eqref{path_dependent_sde_existence}
    with $X(0)$ a $\ccF_0$-measurable random variable such that $E[\|X(0)\|^{2m}] < \infty$ for some $m \geq 1$.
    Then, for any $0 \leq s \leq t \leq T$, there exists a constant $C > 0$ depending only on $m, T, C_{LG}$ such that
    \begin{equation}
        E\left[\|X(t)-X(s)\|^{2m}\right] \leq C(1+3E[\|X(0)\|^{2m}])(t-s)^m.
    \end{equation}
    Moreover, $X$ admits a version (which we again denote by $X$) which is Hölder continuous of any order $\alpha \in [0, \frac{1}{2} - \frac{1}{2m})$.
    For each such $\alpha$, there exists a constant $c > 0$ depending only on $m, T, C_{LG}, E[\|X(0)\|^{2m}]$ such that
    \begin{equation}
        E\left[\left(\sup_{0 \leq s < t \leq T} \frac{\|X(t)-X(s)\|}{|t-s|^\alpha}\right)^{2m}\right] \leq c.
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:16:18.650498+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_876c57a35f146c81a2a758ed8c5b26583fdadf08095c9205f8d7d89cf3287012","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 7 of arXiv:2607.24170, '\large\bf ON NON-MONOTONICITY OF LOGARITHMIC ENERGY\\ FOR RANDOM MATRICES'] Let $f$ be a bounded probability density supported on $[-L,L]$, and
