{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.523044+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8770505697696aa7b4818a109e167208010b95113b88c209ea5af8482c4a916b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lem of arXiv:2411.03104, '{\bf Coupling Methods and Applications on Path Dependent McKean-Vlasov SDEs}\footnote{Supp'] Assume {\bf(H)}. Then (equation EQ31 of the paper) admits a unique strong solution and for any $T>0$, there exists a constant $C(T,N,k)>0$ such that
