{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:17:33.996930+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_87751e775eaaa9e2e4df8422d607306c7814fa295f4637ae23d6edb796f8287a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 8 of arXiv:2609.03403, 'Hyperpositive functions, sector bounded functions and a trace formula'] In the above notations and setting (and in particular $F$ is bounded in modulus), the space $\mathcal L(F)$ consists of the $\mathbb C^m$-valued functions of the form
