with $\text{H}_{m,M}$ as in (equation prim-B of the paper). For any $t\in[0,T]$, any $G:[0,T]\times \mathbb{T}\to\mathbb{R}$ such that  $c_{T,G}:=\int_{0}^T\norm{G_s}_{\infty}\mathrm{d} s<\infty$ and positive integer $L<\ell_N$ , it holds that 
\begin{align}
    \mathbb{E}_{\mu_N}
