{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:28:53.627608+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_878bd699e85bcab727b60289a08b41ae10536e1882003c601b568600949c174f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2605.13107, 'Discrepancy and Fisher information'] Let $K \subset \R^d$ be a convex, centrally symmetric set with nonempty interior. Let $v_1,\dots,v_n \in \R^d$ be fixed vectors, and let $\e_1,\ldots, \e_n$ be independent Rademacher random variables. Let $\pi(\cdot)$ be a probability density supported in the interior of $K$. Then there exists an online algorithm that discards some steps $\e_j v_j$ such that, for each $k$,
	$$
	\sum_{j \le k \text{ accepted}} \e_j v_j \in 2K
	\quad \text{deterministically},
	$$
	and
	\begin{equation}	
		\E \#\{\text{discarded}\}
		\le \frac{1}{2} \sum_{j=1}^n \sqrt{v_j^\tran \I_\pi v_j}, 
	\end{equation}
	where $\I_\pi$ denotes the Fisher information matrix defined in \eqref{eq: Ipi}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:48:24.621509+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_878fbae7aff9d047e8ee980eb0d5695990ca3d9e7d9aa49a28c8a05d50238e86","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary corol:semigroup_taylor of arXiv:2601.04997, 'Fluctuations of the Boundary-Driven Symmetric Zero-Range Process from the NESS'] For any $\theta\ge0$ and $H\in \mathcal{S}_\theta$, we have 
\begin{equation*}
    P_{t+\varepsilon}^\theta H=P_t^\theta H+\varepsilon \mathfrak{A}_\theta P_t^\theta H+o(\varepsilon, t),
\end{equation*}
where $o(\varepsilon, t)$ denotes a function in $\mathcal{S}_\theta$ such that $\mylim_{\varepsilon\to0}\frac{o(\varepsilon, t)}{\varepsilon}=0$ in the topology of $\mathcal{S}_\theta$. Moreover, the limit is uniform on compact time intervals. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:32:28.996583+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_879017d8863caf091c97a5d455cea0ba021d9f8fa0b3146744e99b1096907aa2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop smooth in sym of arXiv:2608.25471, 'Exact Hausdorff measures and fine geometry of collisions of independent Markov processes'] Assume that Assumption~(assum:main of the paper) holds.
