{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:58:09.905337+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_87983fd8f3aa624494f176bef62ae9e221d39cbff6e2976a508c5e082c32089e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main-poc of arXiv:2607.19583, 'Density-Dependent McKean--Vlasov Diffusions: Subgaussian Occupancy Bounds and Polynomial P'] Under Assumptions~(ass:coefficients of the paper) and (ass:density of the paper), there exists a constant $C_T<\infty$, independent of $N\ge2$, $0<h\le1$, $L$, and the shift locations, such that for $0\le t\le T$:
\begin{equation}
 \operatorname{Ent}\!\left(P_t^N\mid p_t^{\otimes N}\right) \le C_T\bigl(Nh^2(1+|\log h|)+h^{-d}+\log N\bigr).

\end{equation}
Consequently, for any $1\le k\le N$, the marginal entropy and total variation distance satisfy:
\begin{align}
 \operatorname{Ent}\!\left(P_t^{N,k}\mid p_t^{\otimes k}\right) &\le C_T k\left(h^2(1+|\log h|)+\frac{h^{-d}+\log N}{N}\right), \\
 \|P_t^{N,k}-p_t^{\otimes k}\|_{\mathrm{TV}} &\le C_T\sqrt{k} \left(h\sqrt{1+|\log h|}+\sqrt{\frac{h^{-d}+\log N}{N}}\right). 
\end{align}
Furthermore, if $b_i^N$ is the empirical drift in (equation eq:particle-system of the paper) and $\bar b_t(x)=-\Xi(p_t(x))\nabla\Phi(x)$, the time-integrated expected drift error obeys
\begin{equation}
 \int_0^T\mathbb E_{P_t^N}|b_i^N(X_t)-\bar b_t(X_t^{i,N})|^2\,\mathrm d t \le C_T\left[h^2(1+|\log h|)+\frac{h^{-d}+\log N}{N}\right].

\end{equation}
The constant $C_T$ tracks the application of Gronwall's inequality and may grow exponentially like $e^{C T}$ or $e^{C T}$ times a polynomial, depending on the parameters $T$, $d$, $C_\Phi$, $\kappa$, $K$, $L_\Xi$, $C_0$, $c_0$, $C_1$, $a_1$, and $m$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:01:22.587531+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_879e0492147bf95c4ff64a724d57fc16de41fccc79ca03e8d61911bff4f546df","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Global-solution-definition-SES of arXiv:2605.16963, 'Stochastic Euler Equations with Pseudo-differential Noise: Continuous and Discontinuous Pe'] An $\{\mathcal{F}_t\}$-progressively measurable $\mathbf{H}$-valued process $X=(X(t))_{t\ge0}$ with càdlàg paths in $\widetilde{\mathbf{H}}$ is called a global solution to (equation SES of the paper) with initial data $X_0 \in \mathbf{H}$ if the following conditions hold $\mathbb{P}$-$\mathrm{a.s.}$:
		\begin{enumerate}[label={\rm(\arabic*)},leftmargin=0.79cm]\setlength\itemsep{0.2em}
			\item $\sup_{t\in[0,T]}\|X(t)\|_{\mathbf{H}}<\infty$ for every $T>0$;
			\item the integral equation (equation SES of the paper) holds identically for all $t\ge0$ as an equality in $\widetilde{\mathbf{H}}$.
		\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.763722+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_879eff5a0eac75bdf2ad2b8b3030fd12a716a47ab0a16021e19faa7fffbfdf2d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l5.3 of arXiv:2411.19255, 'Moderate, large and super large deviations principles for Poisson process with uniform cat'] The family of random variables $\frac{1}{\varphi(T)}\big(\nu_1(T)-\nu_1(T-c\varphi(T))\big)$ satisfied LDP with
normalized function $\psi(T)=\varphi(T)$ and with rate function
