{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:21:56.740949+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_879f02c07ac92f1f4d986245ade0e0a813ba3eacc837aed61a4eadc03aa4adfd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma-convergence2PTS of arXiv:2507.19222, 'Convergence of the KMP model to the KPZ equation'] For all $x_{1},x_{2},y_{1},y_{2}\in \mathbb{Z}$ we have that
	\begin{equation}
		\lim_{\epsilon\to 0} \mathbf{p}_{\lfloor\epsilon^{-1}\rfloor}^{(2),\epsilon}\left((x_{1},x_{2})\to (y_{1},y_{2})\right)=\mathbf{p}^{(2)}\left((x_{1},x_{2})\to (y_{1},y_{2})\right)\,.
