{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:42:39.096749+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_879fdfc9809d2fc483569de2cbb413eeb8848417d9fe308721ae1a5cbbad08aa","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop ClassYM of arXiv:2412.08497, 'Time discretization of Quadratic Forward-Backward SDEs with singular drift'] Suppose Assumption (assum2.1 of the paper) holds. Fix $r >0$ and Let $\bold{x} = (x^{(1)},x^{(2)},\cdots,x^{(r)})$ and $p > 1$. Assume in addition the terminal condition $\xi$ is of the following form $\xi = \Phi(X_T^{(1)},X_T^{(2)},\cdots,X_T^{(r)})$, where $\Phi\in C^1(\mathbb{R}^{d\times r};\mathbb{R})$ is bounded and $(X_T^{(i)})_{1\leq i\leq r}$ solves (equation 2.1 of the paper) for each drift $b^{i}$, $1\leq i\leq r$ satisfying Assumption (A1). Assume furthermore that $g$ is continuously differentiable in $x$, $y$ and $z$. Then the couple $(Y,Z)$ solution to (equation 2.2 of the paper) is differentiable and for all $1\leq i\leq r$, the derivative process $(\nabla_{{x^{(i)}}} Y,\nabla_{{x^{(i)}}} Z) \in \mathcal{S}^p\times\mathcal{H}^p$ solves the following BSDE for any $p> p_0'$
				\begin{align}
					\nabla_{{x^{(i)}}} Y_t =& \nabla_{{x^{(i)}}} \Phi(X_T^{(1)},X_T^{(2)},\cdots,X_T^{(r)})\nabla_{{x^{(i)}}} X_T^{(i)} - \int_{t}^{T} \nabla_{{x^{(i)}}} Z_s \mathrm{d}W_s\notag\\
					&+ \int_{t}^{T} \langle \nabla g(s,{X}^{(i)}_s,Y_s,Z_s),\nabla_{{x^{(i)}}} \bold{X}_s^{(i)} \rangle \mathrm{d}s, 
				\end{align}
