{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:00:22.665054+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_87afce7dc2e1a53ed80f04e540d0312004195679b0e3064765ffe16c68ebb619","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:DOloc of arXiv:2411.00748, '\bfseries Central limit theorems for the nearest neighbour embracing graph in Euclidean an'] For $x \in \mathbb{X}^d$, define 
\[
    R(x,\eta) := \max\{R_1(x,\eta),2R_2(x,\eta)\},
\]
where
\begin{align*}
  &R_1(x,\eta) := \max_{z \in N(x,\eta)} d(z,x),\\
  &R_2(x,\eta) := \max\{d(z,y) : z\in \eta, x\in N(z,\eta+\delta_x),y\in N(z,\eta)\}.
