{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.597352+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_87bf5ef9a581d645731fa82f26033b3ced9baa5c589fce256ba3258e6f901b57","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem Lemma2.1 of arXiv:2411.15724, 'Wasserstein Convergence Rates for Empirical Measures of Random Subsequence of $\{nα\}$'] There exists a constant $C > 0$ such that for any $2 \leq p < \infty$ and $\nu \in \mathscr{P}(\mathbb{T})$,
