{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.574850+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_87cf17266d9ffe006b44b69f90ee1d90ba56ac09960f90780592e65f59c99075","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:variational characterization of arXiv:2509.04349, 'Precise asymptotics for the norm of large random rectangular Toeplitz matrices'] For all $u,w>0$,
\begin{equation}
\|\Sin_{u,w}\|_{2\rightarrow 2}=\sup_{\Lambda_u \in \mathcal{F}_u,\; \Lambda_w \in \mathcal{F}_w} \left(\int_{-\infty}^\infty \overline{\Lambda_u(x)}\Lambda_w(x)\,\mathrm{d}x\right)^{1/2}=:K_{u,w},
\end{equation}
where \( \mathcal{F}_c \) denotes the class of continuous, positive definite functions supported on \( [-c, c] \) and normalized so that \( \Lambda_c(0) = 1 \).\footnote{By Bochner's theorem (see p.~19 in [rudin62]), this class coincides with the characteristic functions (i.e., Fourier transforms of probability measures) supported on \( [-c, c] \).}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:52.744682+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_87d0238d6ad6553938c456a6a208db95f2369542b2523305351958534e708218","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2506.10511, '2506.10511'] For all $d\geq 1$ and all $\beta>0$, there exist constants $c_4=c_4(d,\beta)>0$ and $c_5=c_5(d,\beta)>0$ {\rm(}both depending only on $d$ and $\beta${\rm)} such that for each $i\in [1,K]_{\mathds{Z}}$, we have
