{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:33:17.673047+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_87d2b365d0cf65b20db4e1b2469bbcb3287fb02d24695ca2e43368871c3bf951","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 18 of arXiv:2607.10725, 'From the Airy line ensemble to the Gaussian free field'] Fix $m \geq 2$,  $\e \in (0,1)$,  $\delta \in \left(0,\tfrac{1}{2m}\right)$, and $A > 0$. Let $H_T$ be as in (\ref{Eq.HeightFunction}) and assume the same notation as in Definition \ref{Def.ITs}. Then, as $T \to \infty$,
\begin{equation*}
\E\bigl[H_T(t_1,x_1)\cdots H_T(t_m,x_m)\bigr] \longrightarrow P(t_1, x_1; \ldots; t_m, x_m)
\end{equation*}
uniformly for
\begin{equation*}
    (t_1,x_1;\ldots;t_m,x_m)
    \in
    \bigl([-A,A]^2\cap\{(t,x):x\le -T^{-\e}\}\bigr)^m
    \cap
    \Bigl\{
        \min_{i\neq j}|t_i-t_j|>T^{-\delta}
    \Bigr\}.
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:47:53.353651+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_87d36f3bec00a4a683afb5e8d7d5a295554d82120472ae55829048fc75e74691","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2607.16017, 'On large networks of integrate-and-fire neurons with short-term synaptic plasticity'] Grant Assumptions~\ref{ass:fmin}-- \ref{ass:minf} and assume moreover that there exists $0 < \lambda_\alpha'   \le \lambda_\alpha $ such that
