{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:59:45.428834+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_87fd7c195c5266a2cfadf56e56070ead0ba073863ab18ea9f61433eb80a50a96","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm thm_alphaIsAlwaysOpti of arXiv:2411.16464, 'Generating social networks with static and dynamic utility-maximization approaches'] For any individuals set $\mathscr{I} \in (\mathcal{E}, \innerproduct{.}{.}) \times \mathcal{U}_N$, and weight list $\alpha$ of dimension $n_N = \binom{N}{2}$ satisfying:
