{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.490931+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8804f12d2d60e78b9c5a40edfb2b50e40cd41331bfe427c58df8aec815988144","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop uniqueness of solution for single-location master loop equation in the 't Hooft limit of arXiv:2411.11676, 'Surface sums for lattice Yang--Mills in the large-$N$ limit'] Given any $L\geq 1$, there exists $\upbeta_*(L,d)>0$ such that if $|\upbeta|\leq \upbeta_*(L,d)$, then there is a unique function $\phi_{\infty}:\mathcal{S}\to \mathbb{R}$ such that 
