{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:11.635285+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_880ff07bb571ac79a12f1c83d70e45fde45b609e67aeaa220bd3e5a0b4fc592a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 26 of arXiv:2605.31088, 'On couplings for kinetic Langevin diffusions'] Let the Markov chain $(Z_k,\tilde Z_k)_{k\in \N}$ be given by the iterated one-shot coupling introduced in Section~\ref{sssec: iterated one-shot} applied to the Markov chains \eqref{eq: linear Markov chain}. The probability that the two chains have not met after $n$ steps is given by
