{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:07:48.545308+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_882f1afa8b8ec475d5e552cdc28ece7a0167d3e94f405256814d60b4046563e0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 4 ($\rashexpctparam$-stability of  $\emprashomonset$ at $x$) of arXiv:2609.01397, 'Measuring consistency via ensemble margin and local prediction variability: Auditing decis'] Given  a Rashomon set $\emprashomonset$, a test point $x \in \dtest$, and a small constant $\rashexpctparam > 0$, $\emprashomonset$ is said to be $\rashexpctparam$ stable at $x$ if, 
