{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:11.644512+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_882f9ad413d1542f2c0f64790ee1106d523ad471372fc5cbd56a5517933b3876","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 29 of arXiv:2605.31471, 'Convergence Rates of Continuous-Time Random Walks to Time-Fractional Diffusions with Unbou'] Let Assumption~\ref{asm:classical} hold. Consider a random walk with a one-step transition operator $U_h$ satisfying Assumption~\ref{asm:rw}.

