{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:05:52.434092+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8836ce77339e7f3a14d7df650987775f54a97bcab34b0ed6c8d904da1c441323","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition proposition4.12 of arXiv:2504.15992, 'Repeated singular values of a random symmetric matrix and decoupled singular value estimat'] Fix $0<\nu\leq 2^{-15}$, $c_0\leq 2^{-50}B^{-4}$, $d\in\mathbb{N},\alpha\in(0,1)$. Consider $k\leq 2^{-17}B^{-4}\nu\alpha d$ and a sequence of positive real numbers $\mathbf{t}=(t_1,\cdots,t_\ell)$. Consider a tuple of vectors $Y_1,\cdots,Y_{\ell}\in\mathbb{R}^d$ satisfying, for some $\alpha\in(0,1)$, $$\operatorname{LCD}_{L,\alpha}^\mathbf{t}(\mathbf{Y})\geq 256B^2\sqrt{\ell},\quad\text{where } L=(\frac{8}{\sqrt{\nu p}}+\frac{256B^2}{\beta})\sqrt{\ell}.$$
   Let $W$ be an $2d\times k$ matrix satisfying $\|W\|_{op}\leq 2$ and $\|W\|_{HS}\geq\sqrt{k}/2$. We also consider two random vectors $\tau\sim\Phi_\nu(2d;\zeta)$ and $\tau'\sim\Xi_{\nu'}(2d;\zeta)$ where $\nu'=2^{-7}\nu$. Let $\beta\in[c_0/2^{10},\sqrt{c_0}]$ and $\beta'\in(0,1/2)$.

    Then we have the following estimate
    \begin{equation}
        \mathcal{L}(W_\mathbf{Y}^T\tau,\beta\sqrt{k+2\ell})\leq (\frac{R}{\alpha})^{2\ell}(\prod_{i=1}^\ell t_i^2)\exp(4\beta^2(k+\ell))\left(\mathbb{P}(\|W^T\tau'\|_2\leq\beta'\sqrt{k})+\exp(-\beta'^2k)\right)^{1/4}
    \end{equation} where we take 
    $R=2^{36}B^2\nu^{-1/2}c_0^{-2}(\frac{8}{\sqrt{\nu p}}+\frac{256B^2}{\beta})$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:42:16.246632+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_88373768fda32bdeb5b3a4c826fc6ef7c17f13b1de50302542f481facf2099db","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:crit of arXiv:2607.01946, 'Second-order fluctuations for a phase transition in random partitions'] If $j_n = \floor{rn^{\alpha/(1+\alpha)}}$ for $r>0$, then
