where $| \cdot |$ denotes the Lebesgue measure. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:38:23.623727+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8865b7ce8d90a966cd9cb0e26bfb2288f98f65555bc9ac83c366ffe75079baa1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma EHI:l:G0upperbound of arXiv:2511.08956, '\textbf{Towards a characterization of elliptic Harnack inequality for jump processes}'] Let $X$ be an isotropic unimodal L\'{e}vy jump process on $\mathbb{R}^d$. For $r, r_0 > 0$ and all $x \in B(0, r)$, we have
