{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:45:10.069064+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_888530fbf7c9e39c72d1529b739afa48c5b7c0a3f38b7b66f14d1dff89226f60","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:existence of arXiv:2504.14457, 'Abstract'] Let $W$ be the noise introduced in Definition~(DO noise def of the paper). Let $H\in (a/4,1)$, where $a$ is defined in (equation eqn:a_param of the paper). The stochastic heat equation (equation eqn:DO process of the paper) has an almost-sure unique solution $u$ that satisfies\\
\begin{align}

\nonumber    u(t,x)&=\int_{\mathbb{R}^d} u_0(y)\cdot p_{h}(t,x-y)dy+\int_0^t\int_{\mathbb{R}^d}  u(s,y) \cdot p_{h}(t-s,x-y)W(dyds)\\
    &=w(t,x)+\int_0^t\int_{\mathbb{R}^d}  u(s,y) \cdot p_{h}(t-s,x-y)s^{H-1/2}W_0(dyds),
\end{align}
where $p_{h}$ is the heat kernel introduced in (equation heatkernel of the paper) and $w(t,x)$ is the solution to the deterministic heat equation given in (equation heatsolution of the paper). Also, $u$ satisfies 
\begin{align}
    \sup_{x\in \mathbb{R}}\sup_{0\leq t\leq T} \mathbb{E}(|u(t,x)|^2)<\infty  \hspace{5mm}  \text{for all } T>0.
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:53:00.815981+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8885cd4d06324516da1d4b97d24e3a8dcba51ad7e4956bb0055dfe4201afe7df","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:bound_gen_size_ind of arXiv:2607.16911, 'Multipartite random graphs with given degrees: local limit, revisiting the giant, distance'] Fix some $R\geq 1$. For any $\alpha,\beta>0$, take $\underline{a}_0=\Bar{a}_0=\alpha$ and $\underline{b}_0=\Bar{b}_0=\beta$, and define $\underline{a}_i,\Bar{a}_i,\underline{b}_i,\Bar{b}_i$ inductively for $i\geq 1$ as in (equation eq:inductive_def_seq_a of the paper) and (equation eq:inductive_def_seq_b of the paper), with $m=m_n$ and $m'=m_n'$ as defined in (equation eq:def_mn_mn' of the paper). Then
    \begin{align*}
        \liminf_{n \to \infty}\CProb{\underline{a}_t\leq \xi_{l(R+t)}\leq \Bar{a}_t,\underline{b}_t\leq \Xi_{R+t}\leq \Bar{b}_t\textrm{ for all }t\geq 1}{\xi_{lR}=\alpha,\Xi_R=\beta}\geq 1-O\left(\alpha^{1-2\gamma}\right),\\ \addtocounter{equation}{1}\tag{\theequation} 
