    where the constant hidden in the $O(\cdot)$ term above is universal, i.e., independent of $R, \alpha,\beta$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:44:17.353755+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_88869db430bdc61e5b0f900ccf78f7119f87bee72e5c3043dea00d266637df7a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition cor:second-der-ub of arXiv:2608.23554, 'Provably adaptive sampling with uniform and remasking \\ discrete diffusion models'] Let \((X_t)_{t \in [0, T]}\) be the uniform or remasking process. Then, for \(i \in [d]\) and \(t, v > 0\),
\begin{equation}

    \frac{\partial^2}{\partial t \partial v} \mathrm{I}(X_t^i\ ;\, X_v^{-i}) \lesssim -\left(1 + \frac{1}{1 - e^{-t}}\right)\frac{\partial}{\partial v} \mathrm{I}(X_t^i\ ;\, X_v^{-i}).
\end{equation}
Furthermore, if \(v \geq u\) with \(v - u \leq \kappa \min(1, u)\),
 \begin{equation*}
    -\frac{\partial}{\partial v} \mathrm{I}(X_t^i \ ;\, X_v^{-i})\biggr\rvert_{t=u} = -\left(1 + O(\kappa)\right) \frac{\partial}{\partial v} \mathrm{I}(X_t^i \ ;\, X_v^{-i}) \biggr\rvert_{t=v}.
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.299131+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_888798156a6adfb9b3f423aeb3350e82d20f52d03a48592c3b4a30d929f41dc6","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi admissible measure of arXiv:2604.21663, 'Large deviations for non-irreducible Markov chains on Euclidean spaces'] A measure $\mu \in \mathcal P(\mathbb R^d)$ is said to be \emph{admissible} if 
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item $\mu$ is absolutely continuous with respect to $\mathrm {Leb} $;
		\item $\supp\mu\subseteq \overline C$;
		\item for all $j\in \mathcal J$ such that $\mu(C_j)>0$, we have $\beta\leadsto j$;
		\item the relation $\leadsto$ is a total order on $\{j\in \mathcal J\ |\ \mu(C_j)>0\}$;
	\end{enumerate}
	The set of admissible measures is denoted by $\mathcal A\subseteq \mathcal P(\mathbb R^d)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.494780+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_88894ab9542f731bcd585b4aeb32658d34bd7cfbd0e896c471669ca04f1c4a94","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 24 of arXiv:2605.09459, 'Multipoint connectivity in the branching interlacement process'] Let $s$ be a positive integer. There exists a finite constant $C_s = C(u,d,s)$ such that for all positive $r < R$, and $x \in \mathrm{B}(R)$,
