{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.751784+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8890a44aa2b2d995b8b45f8f24c388d68ef7d87e98e4bf4b3ebfe9ac9e2c3133","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:error_bounds1 of arXiv:2411.17827, 'Ordered random walks and the Airy line ensemble'] Let $a < 1/2$, $\beta > 0$ and $\theta > \max(1, \beta/2)$.
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Suppose $\varepsilon \in (0, 1/2)$ and $2a < 1/2 - \varepsilon$.
There exists $t_0 > 0$ and $C > 0$ such that uniformly in $d(t) \leq t^a$ and $t > t_0$, 
for all $x \in W_{t,\varepsilon}$ with $\lvert x_j \rvert \leq t^{\theta}/\log(t)$,
\begin{align*}
\mathbf E_x[V(S(t)); \tau > t, \mathcal C_t^c] & \leq CV(x) e^{\theta t^{a} \log(2t)-t^{\beta/2}}.
