{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:17.758611+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_88aca7aa8d7293657aa7783b149002b1be9648110f5bd014e4c290716e33f050","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2511.05386, 'CLT for $\beta$-ensembles with Freud weights, application to the KLS conjecture in Schatte'] Let $p>2$.
		For any $\delta>0$ and any compact set $K_0 \subset \R$, there exists $C>0$ such that the following holds.
		For any $N,q \geq 1$ and $\alpha \in [0,1]$, if there exists $M>0$ such that, for any $x \in K_0$ and $y \in (0,\delta]$, with $z = x+\ii y$,
		\begin{equation} 
			\E_\alpha\left[\abs{s_N(z)-s_{V_\alpha}(z)}^{2q}\right] 
			\leq \left( \frac{M}{Ny} \right)^{2q},
