{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:30:08.102322+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_88d1b5053b7a2f725204c3e8044e7c6aac0fc18edfe0b107481bb4ffdca0c4c8","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Well-behaved Backtracking Intersections for SC Polynomials of arXiv:2608.12415, 'Sharp Phase Transition for Ellipsoid Fitting'] Given $\tau \in \mathcal{B}(K)$ that are backbone-dangling shapes, we say the composition $\tau\cdot \tau'$ forms a backtracking intersection if \begin{enumerate}
