{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:06:55.252034+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_88dcb2d774ce8d6cb3fe2fe52d0f32264d7630e75fceaf5a02ebbf65cbc557e5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:proto-ville of arXiv:2512.21026, 'Minimax Duality in Game-Theoretic Probability\thanks{Work in progress: mistakes are likely'] Let $(\mathcal{Y},\hat\mathcal{Z},T)$ be a sequentially normalized gamble space.
