{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:40.334460+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_88e8221abf8edbe458e58d0dd566e9550923721fc21d0c0ca8b25e8377d1ee1c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 (Non Uniform Exapnsions) of arXiv:2511.06414, 'Non-uniform Edgeworth expansions for weakly dependent random variables and their applicati'] We say that $W_n$ obeys the (non-stationary) Edgeworth expansion of order $r$ with power $s\geq 0$ if for every $x\in\bbR$,
