{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:22:21.882995+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_88e9bebf223c0fd13a2b725e6e5633452eb7a950f896c84a4d2e63af82d57f47","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:AT metric of arXiv:2411.11345, 'Real Gaussian exponential sums via a real moment map'] We say that the Gaussian random field $\mathcal{X}$ is \emph{non degenerate} if $\zeta_\mathcal{X}(x)$ is full dimensional for all $x\in M$. In that case, we define the \emph{Adler-Taylor} (AT) metric on $M$ to be the Riemannian metric such that for all $x\in M$, its unit ball $B_x\subset T_xM$ satisfy 
