{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:32:23.874466+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_890486887daaf6ddd0831b5802ec7bf5a843a68a096c87c0a12c4768f975e2ad","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm main_finite of arXiv:2603.27144, 'On the critical fugacity of the hard-core model on regular bipartite graphs'] There exist $C,c>0$ such that the following
holds for every $\lambda,C_{\mathrm{LE}},M_{\mathrm{LE}}>0$ and integer $\delta\ge2$.
Let $G=(V,E)$ denote a finite simple $\delta$-regular bipartite
graph, with bipartition $(\mathcal{E},\mathcal{O})$. Suppose that $G$ satisfies
the local expansion property with parameters $C_{\mathrm{LE}},M_{\mathrm{LE}}$. Then,
first,
\begin{equation}
\frac{1}{|V|}\log Z^{G}\le\frac{1}{2}\log(1+\lambda)+\frac{CC_{\mathrm{LE}}}{\delta}\left((1+\lambda)^{-\frac{\delta}{CC_{\mathrm{LE}}}}+\frac{1}{M_{\mathrm{LE}}}\right).
