{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:52:47.258108+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_891433a07638277a1f0d136841654687b4d11b60583b0c33948f74b6957c4211","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theo 5 (Feldman--H\'ajek) of arXiv:2609.01105, 'Obstruction to quasi-invariance of Gaussian measures under transport flows on Riemannian M'] \cite[Theorem 2.25]{DaPratoZabczyk2014}\\
Let~\(\nu_1\) and~\(\nu_2\) be two centered Gaussian measures over a Hilbert space $H$ with covariance operators~\(Q_1\) and~\(Q_2\). Then $\nu_1$ and $\nu_2$ are either mutually singular or mutually absolutely continuous with respect to each other. The latter happens if and only if 
\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
    \item measures~\(\nu_1\) and~\(\nu_2\) have the same Cameron--Martin space $Q_1^{\mez}(H)=Q_2^{\mez}(H)=:H_0$;

    \item $Q_1^{-\mez}Q_2^{\mez}(Q_1^{-\mez}Q_2^{\mez})^* - \mathbf{1} \in \mathfrak{S}_2(\bar H_0)$. 
\end{enumerate}
In the first item, $Q_i^{\mez}(H)$ is the range of the operator $Q_i^{\mez}$, and in the last item, $\bar H_0$ stands for the completion of $H_0$ under the $H$ norm, and the adjoint is understood with respect to $H$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:48:49.906109+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8917bba328bb68cf663087583db08ad4230fcfb99a76ce80b6e061b79e43ec06","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:tsai of arXiv:2511.08479, '\Large From disordered systems to the Critical 2D Stochastic Heat Flow'] Let $Z=(Z_{s,t}(\cdot, \cdot))_{s\leq t}$ be a stochastic process taking values in
the space of locally finite non-negative measures $M_+(\mathbb{R}^2\times\mathbb{R}^2)$ on $\mathbb{R}^2\times\mathbb{R}^2$
equipped with the vague topology   such that:
\begin{itemize}
\item[(1)] for any $s<t<u$, the random measures $Z_{s,t}$, $Z_{t, u}$ and $Z_{s, u}$ satisfy a
form of Chapman-Kolmogorov property $Z_{s, u} = Z_{s, t} \, \bullet \, Z_{t,u}$;
\item[(2)] for any $s<t<u$, $Z_{s,t}$ and $Z_{t,u}$ are independent;
\item[(3)] for any $s<t<u$, $1\leq n\leq 4$, and $\phi_i,\psi_i\in L^2(\mathbb{R}^2)$ for $i=1,\ldots,4$, the mixed moments
${\ensuremath{\mathbb E}} \big[\prod_{i=1}^n Z_{s,t}(\phi_i,\psi_i) \big]$ agree with that of the SHF with parameter $\vartheta\in\mathbb{R}$.
\end{itemize}
Then $Z$ has the same law as the Critical $2d$ Stochastic Heat Flow with parameter
$\vartheta$. Furthermore, $(Z_{s,t}(\cdot, \cdot))_{s\leq t}$ admits
a version that is almost surely continuous in $s\leq t$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:06:06.302096+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_891a07840c23b70d97d28d4f1406d95f5f449f4883f109129cc1b1a311a89fc1","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:fun_convergence of arXiv:2605.26048, 'Classification of the eternal solutions and multiple coalescing shocks in the KPZ fixed po'] Let $\mathcal T_\Phi$ denote the topology on the space $\Phi$ such that $\varphi_n \to \varphi$ if the following two conditions hold: 
