{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:15:34.386078+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8930703d7e195a06573ae5757b8cc5023beeabcf0769f0a106def3d30c26c3b9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 5 (\cite{kannanKL2021}) of arXiv:2609.03268, 'Poincare Polynomials of Heavy-Light Hassett Spaces'] Fix $m\ge2$ and $n\ge 4$ and consider the weight vector $w=w_{m,n}:=(1^m, \epsilon^{n-m})$. 
            Let 
            $$R=\Z[x_I: I\subsetneq \{2,\ldots, n\};\ \{2,\ldots, m\}\cap I \neq \varnothing; \ |I|>1]$$ 
