{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:26:47.149463+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_893249ebd902a9e55edd56d4dae2f85df423e73fe1aaf828992b7740699322cb","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 20 of arXiv:2608.29361, 'Convergence of the subcritical $\gamma$-LQG metric to the critical $2$-LQG metric as $\gam'] There exist universal constants $c_0,c_1>0$ such that the following holds for all $S>1,z \in \CC$, and all $t > 0$. A.s., we have that
