\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:47:40.717880+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8932734406117c095180b60421fef236f9b2e3d6fff4a5e9adafe50fa3c568ad","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition of arXiv:2604.16206, 'Extrapolation of max--stable random fields with Fr\'echet marginals'] The tail dependence function $l_{\mathbf{B}_T}$ of $\mathbf{B}_T=(B_{t_1},\ldots, B_{t_n})$  equals
    \begin{align*}
        l_{\mathbf{B}_T}((x_1,\ldots,x_n))&=\int_{\mathbb{R}^n}\bigvee_{j=1}^n x_j e^{z_j-\frac{1}{2}\sigma^2(t_j)}f_{\Sigma_n}(\mathbf{z})d \mathbf{z}\\
        &=\int_{0}^{+\infty}\left[1-F_{\Sigma_n}\left(\log\frac{y}{x_1}+\frac{\sigma^2(t_1)}{2},\ldots,\log\frac{y}{x_n}+\frac{\sigma^2(t_n)}{2}\right)\right]dy
    \end{align*}
   for $\mathbf{x}=(x_1,\ldots,x_n)\in\mathbb{R}_+^n$,  where  $\mathbf{z} = (z_1,\ldots,z_n)$, $d\mathbf{z} = dz_1\ldots dz_n$, and $\Sigma_n$ is the covariance matrix of the underlying Gaussian random vector $(Y_{t_1},\ldots,Y_{t_n}).$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:15:08.904982+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8933d58f8ef34bab1974464526e729f044508f2367f3205aeef79eb6df06025a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm matchingmatsourbound of arXiv:2411.10633, 'A Geometric Perspective on the Injective Norm of Sums of Random Tensors'] Let $M_1, \ldots, M_n$ be matchings on $[d]$, the respective adjacency matrices be $A_1, \ldots, A_n \in \mathbb R^{d \times d}$, and $E \coloneqq M_1 \sqcup \cdots \sqcup M_n$. Define $\mu \in \mathbb R^n$ by $\mu_i \coloneqq \vertM_i\vert$ and $\Delta \in \mathbb R^d$ such that $\Delta_i$ is the degree of vertex $i$ in the multigraph $([d],E)$ (including multiplicities). For $p \geq 4$ and $g_1, \ldots, g_n$ being i.i.d. standard Gaussians, we have
    \begin{equation}
