{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:31:02.807664+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_89b116b7462cbe344e1a3b9bef4a882058e2cee47f65128b98cebc774dceae4c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma priori-combine-2026-6-5 of arXiv:2609.01488, 'Stabilization by a background magnetic field: global well-posedness of the full compressib'] Let $M, N\geq3$. Assume $(\rho,\mathbf u,p,\mathbf h)$ is a smooth solution to   the system (equation no-heat-mhd3 of the paper) on $\mathbb T^3\times[0,T]$ for some $T>0$ satisfying (equation suppose-1 of the paper) and (equation rhoH-M of the paper). Then there is a positive constant $A_8$ satisfying $A_8\sim\|\rho_0\|^{2(N-1)}_{M}+1$ such that
\begin{align}
\frac{d}{dt}&\widetilde{\mathcal E}(t)+\frac{2}{3}\underline\rho\|\mathbf u_t\|^2_{N-1}+\frac{4}{3}\|\mathbf u\|_{N+1}^2\nonumber\\
&\lesssim\|\rho\|^2_{N-1}\|\mathbf u_t\|^2_{2}+(\|\rho_0\|_M\|\mathbf u\|_3\|\mathbf u\|_{N}+\|\rho\|_N\|\mathbf u\|^2_{3})\|\mathbf u\|_N+\|\rho\|^2_{N-1}\|\mathbf u\|^4_3\nonumber\\
&\quad+\|(\mathbf u,p,\mathbf h)\|^2_{3}\|(\mathbf u,p,\mathbf h)\|^2_{N}+(\|\rho_0\|^{2(N-1)}_{M}+1)(1+\|(\mathbf u,p,\mathbf h)\|_2)\|(\mathbf u,p,\mathbf h)\|_2^3\nonumber\\
&\quad+\|(\mathbf u,p,\mathbf h)\|_{3}\|(\mathbf u,p,\mathbf h)\|^2_{N},
\end{align}
and
\begin{equation}
\|(\mathbf u,p,\mathbf h)\|^2_N\leq \widetilde{\mathcal E}(t)\leq B_5\big(\|\rho_0\|^{2(N-1)}_{M}+1\big)\|(\mathbf u,p,\mathbf h)\|^2_N
\end{equation}
with $\widetilde{\mathcal E}(t):=A_8\mathcal A(t)+E_{N}(t)$. Here $B_5>0$ is a constant depending only on $\mathbb T^3$, $|\mathbf n|$, $N$, $\mu$, $\lambda$, $\gamma$, $\bar P$, $\underline{\rho}^{-1}$, $\bar\rho$, $M_0$, $r$ and $c$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:26:52.654162+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_89b506bda712d9b2991e86fb1eb668d54436054a292b3bf2d0f3507178043590","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 2 of arXiv:2609.03713, 'A Sharp Mass Threshold for Boundedness in a Critical Quasilinear Chemotaxis Model with Ind'] Let $p\in (2d,\infty)$ and assume that the initial value $(u^0,w^0)$ satisfies~\eqref{a1}. Then the corresponding solution $(u,w)$ to~\eqref{E} satisfies
