	In particular, this yields $\overline{M}(Q)$ is the unique projection of $M$ onto $\mathcal{M}(\pi,Q)$ under the squared-Frobenius norm. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:37:08.318478+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_89bc6beeca93aef1cfd86c075135ddf3fb173b11df7232681336ba80c006e39f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:facetinvariance of arXiv:2608.30973, 'Pseudo-Anosov flow and dynamics on guts'] Let \(M\) be an oriented connected closed 3-manifold and let \(\varphi\) be a pseudo-Anosov flow without perfect fits in \(M\). Suppose that \(z\in \mathcal{C}_{2}(\varphi)\) is primitive.

