{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:25:44.953564+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_89c0d8aa43c8310edd1699b255cdbde06dd01768241b0bce167e4a267454418d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2605.10609, '\Large \bf Stochastic curve shortening flow driven by a transport-type pure jump L\'evy no'] Let $u_0\in V$. Then there exists a unique strong solution $u$ to \eqref{c2eq6} in the sense of Definition \ref{s2 df1}. Moreover, $u\in L^2([0,\infty); W^{2,1}(\mathbb{T}))\cap
