{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.072888+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_89c363cd53d19d9cccc84f91066e2f3f88a80e9742cf2f279c859e6c1ffccff8","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition de:solution of arXiv:2411.12192, 'Sample path properties and small ball probabilities for stochastic fractional diffusion eq'] A jointly measurable process $\{u(t,x);(t,x)\in[0,T]\times\mathbb{R}^d\}$ is said to be a solution of the stochastic Cauchy problem
