  Here, we recall that $\tilde{p}(t,x):=p(-t,-x)$ and the symbol $\ast$ denotes the convolution.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:32:35.566163+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_89c5fae7fd6b472edf0a4f95e9d32ada491142fb3dd7de814ed0f5267a195007","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition pro.velocity-resolvent-infty of arXiv:2605.26082, 'Quantitative Einstein relation for reversible diffusions in a random environment'] There exists $C<\infty$ such that, for $\mathbb{Q}$-a.e.\ $\omega$ and every $(m,h,\rho)$ in the admissible regime~(equation eq.admissible of the paper), the velocity resolvent $u_m$ satisfies
