{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:47:07.701361+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_89e9156b700d77dca59fde31792843faa7023e361711318e722e62b9a17597fd","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 10 of arXiv:2608.06011, 'Strong averaging principle for multiscale time-inhomogeneous SDEs with multiplicative $\al'] A measure-valued function $\rho_t^{x}$ is said to be a $\tau$-periodic measure for the two parameter Markov semigroup $P^{x}(s,t)$ if it satisfies
