{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:58:38.147244+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_89effe19120339665332200d3817bfc0c3d8266d148a629dac11fe7f650297a2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:boosted small of arXiv:2606.24465, 'History estimation in random recursive trees:\\Pointwise approach via iterated Jordan cent'] There exists a constant $C>0$ such that for any $v\in [n]$ and for any $t \geq 1$, the random variable $\phi_n^{{\scriptscriptstyle{({2}})}}(v)$ satisfies 
