{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:32:20.735212+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_89f054a033855fae62a559959664629ce7edeaf4cc48795d9551b7e78027e8a2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 13 (McLeish, 1974) of arXiv:2609.00292, 'Extinction, Survival and Fluctuations for the Spatial Maki--Thompson Model on Infinite Gra'] Let $\{Z_{n,j}:n\ge1,\ 1\le j\le b_{n}\}$ be a martingale-difference
