{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:09:34.467752+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_89f0b2afed366578999b9d372dc9db05c167d7dcc73c94c6257cb7ca33a72cc8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:singulargap of arXiv:2505.12187, 'Speeding up quantum Markov processes through lifting'] Given an ergodic QMS generator $\mathcal{L}$ with an invariant state $\sigma \in \mathcal{D}_+(\mathcal{M})$, let $s(\mathcal{L})$ be the singular value gap of $\mathcal{L}$, $C \ge 1$ and $\nu > 0$ be constants in exponential convergence (equation ex:expdecay of the paper), and  let $t_{\rm rel}$ be the relaxation time (equation eq:trelax of the paper). Then, it holds that 
