{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:10.974266+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_89faab9af86101413fe03318bbf6936c9e72d58ebe6c79919a51a13053c189e3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 (Threshold for weak$^\dagger$ domination) of arXiv:2606.13648, 'Stochastic dominations for FK percolation and sharp thinning thresholds for the Ising ener'] Let $J \leq \tilde{J}$ be (edge-dependent) coupling constants, where the inequality holds pointwise. Then, for any parameter $p\in[0,1]^E$ with $p<p^\dagger(J):=1-\exp(-4J)$ pointwise, we have
