{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:37:28.989056+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8a15cddeab4d47ccf679a74877abece82e6be59a5c261d797ad6c6b74f0392a7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition \cite{Trinh-Trinh-Jacobi} of arXiv:2412.01015, 'Classical beta ensembles and related eigenvalues processes at high temperature and the Mar'] Assume that the initial measure $\mu_0^{(N)}$ converges weakly to a probability measure $\mu_0$. Then the following hold.
	\begin{itemize}
