{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:03:35.788330+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8a427e1bc63d6d738b86d84e3ef369f5d34e4b05fb4b9bdcec600713d33528c5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:common-spectral-localization of arXiv:2608.22910, 'A Commutator Framework for Selective Spectral Alignment in Deep Neural Networks'] Let \(A_\ell\) be symmetric on \(\mathbb R^{m_{\ell+1}}\). Then
\begin{equation}
\|[A_\ell,P_\ell]\|_F^2
=
\sum_{i,j=1}^{m_{\ell+1}}
(\lambda_{\ell,i}-\lambda_{\ell,j})^2
|u_{\ell,i}^\top A_\ell u_{\ell,j}|^2
=
2\sum_{i<j}
(\lambda_{\ell,i}-\lambda_{\ell,j})^2
|u_{\ell,i}^\top A_\ell u_{\ell,j}|^2.
\end{equation}
If \(I_{\mathsf a},I_{\mathsf b}\) are disjoint spectral index sets,
\(
\Pi_{\ell,\mathsf a}=\sum_{i\in I_{\mathsf a}}
u_{\ell,i}u_{\ell,i}^\top
\),
\(
\Pi_{\ell,\mathsf b}=\sum_{j\in I_{\mathsf b}}
u_{\ell,j}u_{\ell,j}^\top
\), and
\begin{equation}
\delta_\ell(\mathsf a,\mathsf b)
:=
\min_{i\in I_{\mathsf a},\,j\in I_{\mathsf b}}
|\lambda_{\ell,i}-\lambda_{\ell,j}|,
\end{equation}
then
\begin{equation}
\|[A_\ell,P_\ell]\|_F^2
\geq
2\delta_\ell(\mathsf a,\mathsf b)^2
\|\Pi_{\ell,\mathsf a}A_\ell\Pi_{\ell,\mathsf b}\|_F^2.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:15:34.382864+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8a443bd87ce484dde96fd92c28ff74f536028aa387454eff833e52684648d89e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2609.03243, 'Weighted Ces\`aro type operators on the weighted Bergman spaces in the unit ball'] Let $\lambda\in\mathbb{R}$, $\theta>0$ and $\mu$ be a finite positive Borel measure on $[0,1)$. Then
