{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:48:27.282797+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8a50dc6a4f091e46fa368ad79bb88c040246577d6cd5f856f1a4d05dc8c71e1d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2604.25336, 'Central limit theorem for slow-fast system under mixed fractional Brownian motion'] Let \(p\ge 2\) and \(\gamma\in(\frac{1}{2},H)\). Under \textbf{H1}--\textbf{H3}. As \(\epsilon\) tends to zero, there exists a \(\kappa>0\) such that
