\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:53.164086+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8a5f423da2c8b147688536b7fb2a40ce2cc344bef7f7bb46bafab9defc2c5a98","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 13 (Proportional blocks) of arXiv:2606.29530, 'Cutoff profiles for colored top-\texorpdfstring{$m$}{m}-to-random shuffles with growing bl'] Assume $m_n/n\to\alpha\in(0,1)$, and let $k_n$ be any integer sequence such that
