{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.038664+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8a5fd890826ea785e6f79919247aaff189ae5bdf07fcb92e6203a861af8283c1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 16 of arXiv:2606.31528, 'Well-posedness and stationary distribution of free stochastic differential equations'] Assume that Assumptions \ref{assumption:ass1} and \ref{assumption:ass2} hold. Then for any given $T>0$ the process $U_t$ given by \eqref{eq:converge} is a unique solution to the free SDE \eqref{eq:fSDE}, i.e., 
