\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.189748+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8a8302791c0500ebb8dfce4a0dd427a48cdcb08773de8dafe8ab0f7073f083c3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 33 (rigidity lemma) of arXiv:2510.20492, 'Heterochromatic two-arm probabilities for metric graph Gaussian free fields'] For any $d\ge 3$, there exist constants $\Cl,\cl>0$ such that for any distinct $v,v',w\in \widetilde{\mathbb{Z}}^d$ with $|v-w|\ge d$, and any events $\mathsf{A}$ and $\mathsf{A}'$ increasing with respect to $\mathcal{C}_{v}$ and $\mathcal{C}_{v'}$ respectively, 
  	\begin{equation}
  		\begin{split}
  		 	\mathbb{P}\big(\mathsf{A} \mid  \big\{v\xleftrightarrow{} w \Vert \mathsf{A}' \big\}\big) 
  			\le   & \Cref{const_app_switch1} \Big[  \mathbb{P}\big(\mathsf{A}  \mid  v\xleftrightarrow{} w  \big) + \mathrm{exp}\big( -\cref{const_app_switch2}|v -w |^{\frac{d}{2}-1}\big)\Big]. 
