{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:47:12.028408+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8a8dc3c64d8f5c75730f98da7482dd0b36767ddd6f7c0332d6dc24560b27bfc2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:5 of arXiv:2512.09219, 'Strong confluence of geodesics in Liouville quantum gravity'] Fix bounded open sets $U\subseteq V\subseteq \mathbb{C}$, $a\in (0,1), \ell>0$ and $\nu>0$. 
   Then, for any fixed $q>0$, conditional on the event $\mathcal{E}$, the following holds. With probability tending to $1$ as $\varepsilon\rightarrow 0$ faster than any positive power of $\varepsilon$ (at a rate depending only on $a,\ell,\nu,q,U$ and $V$), for all $\text{\usefont{U}{bboldx}{m}{n}z}\in (\varepsilon^q\mathbb{Z}^2)\cap U$ and all $w\in U$ satisfying $w\notin \mathcal{B}_{\tau_{16\ell}(\text{\usefont{U}{bboldx}{m}{n}z})}^\bullet(\text{\usefont{U}{bboldx}{m}{n}z})$, and for every $D_h$-geodesic $\Gamma_{\text{\usefont{U}{bboldx}{m}{n}z},w}$ from $\text{\usefont{U}{bboldx}{m}{n}z}$ to $w$, there exists $(z,r)\in \mathbb{C}\times [\varepsilon^{1+\nu},\varepsilon]$ such that 
\begin{align*}
