{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:32:34.760566+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8a90c8d499b250137ba5b5fe1e7c4333c0aa5eb0901279caf8f8234ffe4d08ff","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Neumann_problem of arXiv:2411.08220, 'Nonlocal operators with Neumann conditions'] Let $\alpha \in (0,1)\cup (1,2)$ and $f\in C_c(\mathbb{R}\setminus\{0\})$. Then, $G|f|<\infty$ on $\mathbb{R}\setminus\{0\}$ and $u = G f$ is the solution of the following Neumann problem for the fractional Laplacian
