{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:12:13.442120+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8a9bb066a5faf1172f1272015e1299fbf7440c8c1470162983d18dd3a2ae954e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 3 of arXiv:2608.28234, 'A note on the positivity of $Q$-curvature via the continuity method'] Let $(M, g)$ be a smooth closed Riemannian manifold of dimension $n=5$. Suppose $Y(M, [g]) > 0$ and $Y_{4}^{\ast}(M, [g]) > 0$. Assume further that there exists a conformal metric $g_0 \in [g]$ and a constant $t_0 \in (1, \frac{10}{3}]$ such that
\begin{equation}
t_0 \left(- \Delta_{0} J_0 + \frac{n-4}{2} J_{0}^2\right) + 4\sigma_2(A_0) > 0 \quad \text{and} \quad J_0 > 0.
