Here $\Delta_{0} := \Delta_{g_0}$, $J_0 := J_{g_0}$ and $A_0 := A_{g_0}$. Then there exists a conformal metric $\tilde{g}\in[g]$ with positive scalar curvature $\tilde{R} > 0$ and positive $Q$-curvature $\tilde{Q} > 0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:29:21.906790+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8aa2ce03eb18df7986ddad7e6f4eaed73bffc698dd7f7f081552a67be3361f41","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2608.00813, 'Convex order, log-convexity and Moments of Averages of Random Variables'] Let $a,b\in \z_{>0}^n$ be partitions of $m$. Let $A_j = a_1+\dots + a_j$, $B_j=b_1+\dots+b_j$ and $A_0=B_0=0$. Then a necessary and sufficient condition for
