{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:12:20.555894+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8aac1dc45a624fa5ee9a7480ef77c140daf876fb37f6751ba71b45a3b809eaab","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Valid ordering of arXiv:2603.28936, 'Composition of random functions and word reconstruction'] Given a partition $\mathcal{P}$ (random or not) of $[p]$, an ordering (permutation) $\sigma=(\sigma_1,\dots,\sigma_p)$ of $[p]$ is \emph{valid} for $\mathcal{P}$ if
