{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.094430+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8ab33e0fb50822e2f0ee242d6d4263de54fdc11867555d8abfc89dd3152248e2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:biOPE-varying of arXiv:2411.15830, 'Deformations of biorthogonal ensembles and universality'] Let  $(\mathcal X_n)_{n\in\mathbb N}$ be a sequence of biorthogonal ensembles of the form (equation def:wtP of the paper) with correlation kernels ${\mathsf K}_n$ with a varying reference measure $\mathrm{d}\mu_n$. Let $(\sigma_n)_{n\in\mathbb N}$ be a sequence of Borel measurable functions $\sigma_n:\mathbb K \to[0,1]$. If Assumption (assumption:sigmavarying of the paper) holds, then we have the limit
