{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:31:57.925194+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8ace80e3fa95b3c2e734d8ba2dc38c0e4156fcebb6a3eb1126f485953500b18b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:general-grav of arXiv:2510.18392, 'Hyperuniformity of random measures, transport and rigidity'] Let $ \mathsf{P} = \sum_{i}\delta _{ x_{ i}}$ a simple stationary point process of $ \mathbb{R}^{ d}$ with unit intensity for which some stationary $   \mathscr  C^{ 1}$ field $ F_{ \mathsf{P}}$ satisfies a.s.  (equation eq:fixed-repr-FP of the paper). Call $ B_{ i}$ the  {\it attraction basin} of $ x_{ i}$, i.e. the set of points attracted to $ x_{ i}$
\begin{align*}
 B_{ i} = \{Y (s),s\geqslant 0:Y\text{\rm{\color{black}  satisfies  (equation eq:coulomb-pde of the paper) and }}\lim_{ t\to \infty }Y(t) = x_{ i}\}.
