{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:24:45.929208+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8aec08ff76a13f150c8e11f7bc8b2b5e5a58b199e5fe090c30be594254aeac84","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm scp of arXiv:2509.10984, 'Weak Existence and Uniqueness for Super-Brownian Motion with Irregular Drift'] Suppose that almost surely, $X_0 = f \in \mathcal{C}_c^+(\mathbb{R})$. Let $(X_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be the solution to (equation eq:SPDE1 of the paper) with $h$ given by 
