{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:09:59.307738+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8aee67f9049d4acf8dbb7e298630bcb6c04c7491d793617e4d241504aec2d8ba","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop_optimality_criterion of arXiv:2608.08299, 'Non-linear optimal stopping with Bermudan strategies: the infinite horizon case'] Let $\nu^*$ be a \textbf{finite} stopping time. The finite stopping time $\nu^*$ is optimal for the problem (equation optimal_stopping_problem_k of the paper) with value $V(\theta_k)$ if the following three conditions hold:
