{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.902982+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b03e9e25db7a9c4a3cd816a0e5124deec2b2e2abf6cba6ae9ce086c5de9a243","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 50 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Under the assumptions of Lemma~\ref{Lemma_I_quadratic_Fourier}, for any $\varkappa > 0$ and $M >1$ we have
\begin{equation}

\max_{h\in[H]} \frac{\pi}{2} \cdot [\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{1/2}]_{h,h} \cdot \big|\nu([\hat{a}'_{h},\hat{b}'_{h}])\big| \leq \Bigg(-\bigg(\log M + \max_{h\in[H]} \frac{(\hat b'_h-\hat a'_h)^2}{8}\bigg) \cdot \mathcal{I}^{(2)}[\boldsymbol{\nu}]\Bigg)^{\frac{1}{2}} + \bigg(\frac{\mathcal{J}_{\varkappa}[\boldsymbol{\nu}]}{\varkappa M^{\varkappa}}\bigg)^{\frac{1}{2}},
