{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:30:14.228715+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b234fbf6cbb534d9c7f2b9c346798b95be8c1bfeca95b5942dfdf93bf883c12","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition replace-M-by-explicit-expression-in-tightness of arXiv:2608.23202, 'Locally finite Fixed points of Branching Brownian Motion'] Let $\Pi$ be a fixed point of BBM with drift $\lambda > \sqrt{2}$ and $\theta \in Dom_{\lambda}(\Pi)$. Then, the family of random variables $Z_t$ given by 

