{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:01:48.582958+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b2a72cabecb0b689f772190475d95804ce75c5c412509ed43f7f9a376980cb6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem criterion2 of arXiv:2606.30517, '\textsc{Convergence towards Ideal Poisson--Voronoi tessellations with a focus on Diestel--'] If the conditions of (lem:criterion1 of the paper) hold, then:
		\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]

			\item  $\nu\coloneqq  \lim_{\lambda\to 0}\mu_{\lambda}$ does not depend on the choice of $t(\lambda)$ up to multiplication by constants.
			\item  One necessarily has $t(\lambda) = \inf\{r: \lambda F(r)\geq 1\} + a + o(1)$ for some $a\in\mathbb R$. In this case, $\nu$ exists and 
			\begin{equation}

				\nu= \lim_{\lambda\downarrow 0} \mu_{\lambda} = \nu_0\otimes (e^{ab}\beta),
			\end{equation}
			where $\beta$ is the measure on $\mathbb R$ defined by $\beta((-\infty,r])\coloneqq e^{b r}$. 

		\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:38:58.707476+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b2d74bc9f7b91c9e4bef5b88614321e5f3dbad51f6fb83a16d756460f4101c6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:infvol2pt of arXiv:2511.06321, 'Torus scaling limits and the plateau of the critical weakly coupled $|\varphi|^4$ model in'] Let $d \ge 4$,  $\eta \in [0,1/2)$,  $L$ be sufficiently large and $g>0$ be sufficiently small.
