{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:49.202949+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b3a8d44cacd5915f10b51acf2a9f443127194c7d098c8cf7a1a95251be8d06a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2604.26898, '\bf Stochastic Scaling Limits and Synchronization \\by Noise in Deep Transformer Models'] Under Assumptions \ref{ass:att_reg} and \ref{ass1}, for every $N\in \mathbb{N}$, there exists a constant $\cN > 0$ such that for every $m, L \in \mathbb N$ and $T>0$:
