{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:09:23.966482+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b5bc2d07d4f117abd260ae8648958e3950a3d6f23d34791cf71403a3576aaf5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 of arXiv:2607.22416, 'A multi-player optimal stopping game based on a spider Brownian bridge'] A  skew Brownian bridge is a real-valued, continuous stochastic process $X=\{X_{t}\}_{0\leq t < 1}$ which satisfies the SDE
\begin{equation}
