 \right|=0.

\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:42:39.088510+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b6deed903eff2bc9ac96302e7d54bf6c12113910ca61642cd3d508c2ab07e55","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition sub-matrix-block-removal of arXiv:2412.08400, '\vspace{-1.0cm} Characterization of Exponential Families of \\ Lumpable Stochastic Matrice'] Let $F \in \mathcal{F}_\kappa^{+}(\mathcal{Y}, \mathcal{E})$ and a non-degenerate surjective lumping function $\kappa \colon \mathcal{Y} \to \mathcal{X}$.
\begin{description}
    \item[Sub-matrix.] 
    For $\mathcal{T} \subset \mathcal{X}$, we write
\begin{equation*}
\begin{split}
    \mathcal{Y}|_{\mathcal{T}} \triangleq \bigcup_{x \in \mathcal{T}} \mathcal{S}_{x} , \qquad 
    \mathcal{E}|_{\mathcal{T}} \triangleq \mathcal{E} \cap \left( \bigcup_{x,x' \in \mathcal{T}} \mathcal{S}_{x} \times \mathcal{S}_{x'}\right),
\end{split}
\end{equation*}
the resulting sub-graph is  ($\mathcal{Y}|_{\mathcal{T}}, \mathcal{E}|_{\mathcal{T}}$) and the sub-matrix $F|_{\mathcal{T}} \in \mathcal{F}_\kappa^{+}(\mathcal{Y}|_{\mathcal{T}}, \mathcal{E}|_{\mathcal{T}})$ is defined such that for any $(y,y') \in \mathcal{E}|_{\mathcal{T}}$, \begin{equation*}
    F|_{\mathcal{T}}(y,y') = F(y,y').
\end{equation*}
    \item[Block removal.]
    The matrix $F$ from which the block $(x_0, x_0') \in \kappa_2(\mathcal{E})$ has been removed is defined as 
$F^{\setminus (x_0, x_0')}\in \mathcal{F}_\kappa^{+}(\mathcal{Y}, \mathcal{E} \setminus (\mathcal{S}_{x_0} \times \mathcal{S}_{x'_0}))$ where for any $(y,y') \in \mathcal{E} \setminus (\mathcal{S}_{x_0} \times \mathcal{S}_{x'_0})$,
\begin{equation*}
        F^{\setminus (x_0, x_0')}(y,y') = F(y,y').
    \end{equation*}
\end{description}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:06:21.674735+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b6e2ec9938c2f02e5c69a12f54c8c445bd17407c165bc4c89cd04c8ccfe3e7a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 27 (Saddle localization admissibility) of arXiv:2607.20882, 'An Eyring--Kramers Law for the Hypoelliptic Third-Order\\ Langevin Diffusion'] The ansatz $f_{\eps,\vartheta}$ of
Lemma~\ref{lem:global-saddle-test-function} is smooth, $[0,1]$-valued, equal
