{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:38:58.717259+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b6f76fda7bb768edc5ee49431248a61c0bbbf15f84c1af2bcdd4ab69439d645","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:nuptcctty of arXiv:2511.06321, 'Torus scaling limits and the plateau of the critical weakly coupled $|\varphi|^4$ model in'] Let $\alpha \in [1/2,1]$,  $g$ be sufficiently small,  $\vec{\textbf{a}} \in \operatorname{HB}_{\epsilon_p}$ and $C_{\cD}$ be sufficiently large (independently of $L$).  Then there exists $ \vec\nu_{ptc}  = (\nu^{(\km_1)}_{ptc} )_{\km_1 \in  \kA_0 \cup \kA_1 } $ such that the following hold: with initial condition \begin{align}
