{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.239284+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b81735e877a23d07d3bc43216a6ab39141b1f0dded60a9bafd5e3b4ad7997a4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lemma_off_diagonals of arXiv:2506.17168, '{\bf Scaling limits for sample autocovariance operators of Hilbert space-valued linear pro'] Let $C_N$ be as in (equation eq:CN-vector of the paper). Consider a linear combination of an off-diagonal tuple
\begin{equation*}
\quad Q_{2}(C_{N}) \in L^2(\mathbb{Y}^2:\mathbb R^{(H+1)}), \quad Q_{2}(C_{N})(r,s) \doteq \sum_{j_{1} \neq j_{2}} C_{N}(j_{1},j_{2},r,s)\varepsilon_{j_{1}}(r) \varepsilon_{j_{2}}(s) .
