{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.615412+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8ba7084bbaf2245398c6ed6ae86535db6dd542b19cf62102acd3417246f3d457","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 4 of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] Given~$n\ge1$ and a sample~$\ell_{\tau_\varrho}$ on~$\T_n$ under~$P^\zero$, let~$Y_n$ denote the a.s.-unique maximizer of~$x\mapsto\ell_{\tau_\varrho}(x)$ on~$\BbbL_n$. Then~$\theta_n(Y_n)$ converges in law to a random variable~$U$ on~$[0,1]$ described as follows: Given a sample~$\{Z_{T_k}\}_{k\ge1}$ of the measures in Corollary~\ref{cor-1.3}, let~$K$ be the smallest~$k\ge1$ maximizing
\begin{equation}

k\mapsto \log Z_{T_k}\bigl([b^{-1},1]\bigr)-2k\log b+G_k
\end{equation}
where~$\log0:=-\infty$ and $\{G_k\}_{k\ge1}$ are i.i.d.\ standard Gumbel 
independent of $\{Z_{T_k}\colon k\ge1\}$.
Then $K<\infty$ a.s.\ and $U$ is uniform on~$[b^{-k-1},b^{-k})$ conditional on~$\{K=k\}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:03.893292+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8bad0343e6d7bb99379f45b7a9ad9cf550add7a8c34f8a04ba723c95a7159ad6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 4 of arXiv:2606.18877, 'Ergodic Properties of Non-Linear Density-Dependent Perturbations of the Ornstein--Uhlenbec'] Under the same assumptions as in Lemma~\ref{lem:unifbound}, there exists a unique probability density \(\pi\) solving the stationary form of~\eqref{eq:NFPE}. Moreover, \(\pi\in C^1(\R^d)\) and satisfies 
\begin{equation}
\pi(x)=g^{-1}(-\Phi(x)+\mu),\quad x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}
\end{equation}
where 
\begin{eqnarray}
g(r)=\int_{1}^{r}\frac{1}{s\,\Xi(s)}\,ds,\quad r> 0,
\end{eqnarray}
and $\mu$ is the unique number in $\mathbb{R}$ such that 
\begin{equation}
\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}g^{-1}(-\Phi(x)+\mu)\,dx=1.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:06:18.055668+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8bb0b05f8fc45c24cb00db657c09843bc4862299f652a4d921fad25c7ee7a8cf","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 27 (Uniqueness of the nonzero vector invariant law) of arXiv:2608.15914, 'Absorption cutoff and stationary singularities for rounded Gaussian random dynamical syste'] Fix $A>0$ and $N\geq1$ for which $K_{A,N}$ admits a nonzero invariant law
