{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:14:46.351044+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8bb8c1148e4d48b7dc1f3b35ad709378625d840e6e32217bf91b28c4f9945158","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:homogeneous-witness of arXiv:2608.10184, 'The sharp SAT/UNSAT phase transition in random ellipsoid fitting'] Assume that $x_1,\ldots,x_n$ span $\mathbb{R}^d$.  An ellipsoid fit exists if and only if there are $S\in\mathsf{S}^d$ and $b\in\mathbb{R}$ such that
