{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.635912+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8bc08ec7561dc5a53a2e6a636a614ad450784eaa81cdac9ee8f8886a62a13afe","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:semi-good of arXiv:2512.12124, 'A discontinuous percolation phase transition on the hierarchical lattice'] Let $a>0$ and let $J : \mathbb{H}_L \to \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}$ be a kernel so that $J\left(e\right) \geq \frac{a L \log (j)}{L^{2j}}$ for every edge $e$ with $|e|=L^j$. Then, for all $k\in \mathbb{N}$ there exists a constant $C=C(k,J)$ such that \begin{align}
