    & \mathbb{P}_{J} \left( \Lambda_{n,n+k} \textnormal{ has a cluster of density $\gamma$} \right) \leq C  n^{-a(1-\gamma)}
	\end{align}
    for every $n\geq 1$ and $\gamma \in \{L^{-k},2L^{-k},\ldots,1-L^{-k},1\}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.065148+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8bc100ecaa3da95890b97a945d40f87e3263201a8deb99a4cb366ae3b67f3528","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 29 (Bad nodes) of arXiv:2606.17452, 'Optional Stopping for Superhedging Supermartingales'] For a fixed node $(S,j)$, let
