{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:10:43.791845+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8bd1de7507f1ca4124ac00db5452b67130459d63b770b2d2b084017e25236bc6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:fluctu of arXiv:2412.04328, 'The critical Karp--Sipser core of Erdős--Rényi random graphs'] For all $\eta, \delta >0$, there exists $K_{\eta, \delta}>0 $ such that for $n$ large enough, we have 
