{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:46:12.274278+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8be085a1ae3254c948f59f6e1e00b2c11f56b7b68a6259511ff4b16471f4f8a5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 (Theorem 2.2 of \cite{AHP2024}) of arXiv:2604.22159, 'Adapted optimal transport between filtered Gaussian processes'] Let $\bG^{a, L}, \bG^{b, M} \in \cFG$ and $\pi \in \Cpl_{\mathrm{bc}}(\bG^{a, L}, \bG^{b, M})$. The following are equivalent:
