{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:24:45.935450+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8bff294ff836101cf89445ebe537c2c22d7c26ebd97f1352378aaaa3e551de78","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:pde_est of arXiv:2509.10984, 'Weak Existence and Uniqueness for Super-Brownian Motion with Irregular Drift'] Let $\mu$ and $\eta$ be two finite measures. Then the following holds:
