{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.589475+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8c1635349042e0f5eaf0850a85f7f4996e55d2f3757a5bd112f94bcdfab5a367","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2411.15485, '\bf\Large Stochastic Volterra Equations for Local Times of Spectrally Positive L\'evy Proc'] For each $\beta \in \mathbb{R}$ such that $\beta+ b>0$, there exists a constant $C>0$ such that for any $\delta >0$ and $t\geq 0$,
