{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:26.258245+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8c18ba9b4e91f73dd3b7ceee4917d69aee3880217647c0d4cfb346ec0daea3fa","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 76 of arXiv:2605.23308, 'Convergence rate estimates for semigroups and heat kernels associated with resistance form'] Let $\alpha>1$. Then, for any $\displaystyle E\in \left(0,\frac{2}{11}\left[(1-\alpha^{-1})\wedge \frac{1}{2}\right]\right),K\in (0,\infty)$, and $0<T_1<T_2<\infty$,
