{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:43:00.042207+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8c1b2599fe5db775f912cb5e168fe05e6ab411702b159b18a48b8d0538d06d48","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2609.00757, 'Improved bounds in Birch's theorem for forms in many variables'] Let \(\eps>0\), \(B\geq2\), \(1\leq H\leq B\), and \(0<t\leq1\).
Let \(a\in\ZZ\) and \(q\in\mathbb N\) with \((a,q)=1\), and put \(\lambda=(HB^{d-1})^{-1}\).
Define
\begin{equation}
 \Sigma_H=\max_{(t-B^\eps\lambda)_+\leq |z|
 \leq2t+B^\eps\lambda}
 \sum_{|\h|\leq HB^\eps}|S_{\h}(a/q+z;B)|.
\end{equation}
Then, for every fixed \(J\geq1\), we have
