{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:42:16.235719+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8c398c2724d148d1e6829e761f9fe5a95d403243b2ed9f7dbddee0c0c4bc9cd8","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem prop:uniform-time-avg-poc of arXiv:2607.00149, '\bf Uniform-in-time Propagation-of-Chaos for\\ Stein Variational Gradient Descent'] Let Assumption~(ass:poc of the paper) hold. Recall the constant $c_0$ from Lemma~(lem:finite-time-poc of the paper). Then, there exists a finite constant $C>0$ such that, for any $\delta>0$ and all sufficiently large $N$,
