\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.192126+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8c39ab7f1b0f8afc5ddbc309c3a4f64fd02f74eb0763f306087f3f9f9204d3a3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Coro 6 of arXiv:2510.21595, 'One-arm exponents of high-dimensional percolation revisited'] Let $d>6$ and $L\geq L_0$. There exist $c,C>0$ such that, for every $p\leq p_c$, and every $n\geq 0$, 
