{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.589255+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8c647e8cb9c742d92c007172ffda91509fcaabe5f32a165443ad1bd3dfc65e88","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] The potential $\varphi$ satisfies equation (equation eq:formula_hamiltonian of the paper) for any $n\in \IN$ and  $\mathsf{P}\in \mathcal P_{s,1}(\Gamma)$ with $\int\xi(\Lambda_1)^2\mathsf{P}(d\xi)<\infty$. Moreover, $\varphi$ satisfies assumption (assumption0 of the paper) for the function
