{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:37.667996+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8c7a45de44ad8b49b9654acba1f78e117a485ff304b40d85ce4afe461bf22cc8","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop cmj-package of arXiv:2609.00110, 'Phase Transition and Fluctuation Results for First-Passage Percolation on Spread-Out Cycle'] Fix $\varepsilon\in(0,1/2)$ and $y\in\mathds{R}$.
There exist non-negative random variables $W_{1,n},W_{2,n}$, defined on the probability space carrying the coupling above, such that
