{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:31:45.223101+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8c8a596353ed80c1ac6ecfd6e1f5f22849ecd6f6769fee8fd298908deec5dc49","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem universalbacks of arXiv:2412.06246, 'The smallest singular value for rectangular random matrices with Lévy entries'] Fix any $\delta>1$,  consider $N\geq\delta n$ and let $G$ be as in Definition (equation line276definition of the paper). Then there exists a subset of labels $\mathcal{D}\subset\{0,1\}^{N\times n}$ which satisfies, for a randomly generated label $\Psi$ such that each $\psi_{ij}$ is i.i.d. taking value in $\{0,1\}$ with $\mathbb{P}(\psi_{ij}=1)\geq \frac{3\delta+1}{4\delta}$, then there exists a positive integer $N_(equation universalbacks of the paper)\in\mathbb{N}$ such that for any $N\geq N_(equation universalbacks of the paper)$, 
    \begin{enumerate}
    \item For this random choice of label $\Psi$, $$\mathbb{P}(\Psi\in\mathcal{D})\geq 1-\exp(-w_(equation universalbacks of the paper)N).
    $$ \item For any fixed label $\Psi\in \mathcal{D}$ and any deterministic $N\times n$ matrix $G_0$, we have
    $$
\mathbb{P}_{\Psi}(\sigma_{min}(G)\leq h_(equation universalbacks of the paper)\sqrt{N})\leq \exp(-w_(equation universalbacks of the paper)N),
    $$\end{enumerate}
    where the constants $h_(equation universalbacks of the paper)>0,w_(equation universalbacks of the paper)>0,N_(equation universalbacks of the paper)\in\mathbb{N}$ depend only on $\delta$, $\alpha_(equation line276definition of the paper)$ and $\beta_(equation line276definition of the paper)$ and they are independent of the choice of the deterministic part $G_0$ and the label $\Psi\in\mathcal{D}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

