{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:54:28.042346+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8c8b70852af638bc08406e570ae56103cabc2976637714c25e104a838361a22f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma talagrand-bousquet of arXiv:2608.12056, 'Deviation inequalities for U-processes of growing order, with applications to half-space d'] [boucheron2013concentration]
Let $\mathcal F$ be a class of measurable real-valued functions and let $X_1,\ldots,X_N$ be i.i.d. Assume that $\mathbb{E}f(X_1)=0$ for all $f\in \mathcal F$ and that $\sup_{f\in \mathcal F} |f(X_1)|\leq U$ with probability $1$. Denote $Z=\sup _{f \in \mathcal{F}} \sum_{k=1}^N f\left(X_k\right)$.
Assume that $\sigma_\ast^2\geq N\sup_{f\in \mathcal F} \mathbb{E}f^2(X_1)$ and set $v = \sigma_\ast^2 + 2U\mathbb{E}[Z]$. Then for all $t\geq 0$, 
\begin{equation}

    \mathbb{P}\left(Z \geq \mathbb{E} Z + \sqrt{2 t v}+\frac{tU}{3}\right) \leq e^{-t}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:58:38.059944+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8c8f72f4abf9e5fd1c07f8454f93862a1a4a22481999cf5b2d4c7a2bb6e4f696","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:right-side-asymptotics of arXiv:2606.19507, 'The $t$-Split Two-Periodic Aztec Diamond Model'] The macroscopic boundary of the $t$-split two-periodic Aztec diamond to the right of the interface is governed by the saddle functions
