{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:22:21.890497+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8cd179fde4c5baad524a5a3fc41f147b0bf70572787f81c63940d4538faea87f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:BKKprob of arXiv:2411.11345, 'Real Gaussian exponential sums via a real moment map'] For all $U\subset \mathbb{C}^n$, we have 
  \begin{equation}
    \mathbb{E}\mathbb{S}\left\{\mathcal{E}^\mathbb{C};U\right\}=\frac{n!}{\pi^n}\int_U \det\left(\partial_z\bar{\partial}_z\Phi^\mathbb{C}\right)\, \mathrm{d} z.
  \end{equation}
  In particular, if $A\subset \mathbb{Z}^n$, then for all $V\subset\mathbb{R}^n$, we have 
  \begin{equation}
    \mathbb{E}\mathbb{S}\left\{\mathcal{E}^\mathbb{C};V\times i (-\pi,\pi)\right\}=n!\vol_n\left(\mu^\mathbb{C}(V)\right).
