{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:14:37.619279+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8cd7f44814a6bfb8fe2d3c6341d7c8f2a573f86b5a406ae542485f4c3b51997c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 24 of arXiv:2608.19065, 'Boundedly exchangeable graphs'] Let $B, C \in \widehat{\Bcal}(S)$ be disjoint such that $\pbb(\nu(B) = 0) < 1$, and let $f_{B \cup C}$ be sampling function for $\xi$ on $B \cup C$. Then, defining $T_B : [0,1] \to [0,1]$ by
