{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.894547+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8cedd2472515bbb4ab0fb80d6307dfe8b99beccd0a088804db59f892a243a16a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lowfrebi of arXiv:2606.31155, 'The well-posedness of stochastic Korteweg--de Vries equations revisited'] Let $0<T<1$. Then
		\begin{align*}
			&\quad\left\|P_1\int_{0}^{t} U(t-t')(u v)_x~d{t'}\right\|_{L_x^2 L^\infty_T}\\
			&\lesssim T^{1/2}(\|P_1u\|_{L_x^2L_T^\infty}+\|P_{>1}u\|_{X^{0,1/3}_T})(\|P_1v\|_{L_x^2L_T^\infty}+ \|P_{>1}v\|_{X^{0,1/3}_T}).
		\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:47:32.876084+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8cf1df43e64324c2188278c84be13b974fe00e395330ca3a7e77c5e7a668248e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 20 (Finite length of the classwise and all-lattice coefficient modules) of arXiv:2609.02449, 'Finite Directional Coefficient Modules over Euler Fibers of $A$-Hypergeometric Systems'] For every $\Lambda\in\mathfrak{L}_{\bm{\beta},\bm{w}}^{\mathrm{adm}}$, the module $M_{\Lambda,\bm{w}}^{\mathrm{dir}}$ has finite length.
Moreover, the all-lattice module $M_{\bm{\beta},\bm{w}}^{\mathrm{dir,all}}$ has finite length, and
