{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.780946+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8d276d53610e3c6a4328bf3c5d7ddeb2e626aae5904891d476954974e0e980f4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem prop_L of arXiv:2411.18374, 'Drawdowns of diffusions'] Let   $X$ be in class 1 or 2.

  Then the joint Laplace transform of $M_{\theta_\delta}$ and $\theta_\delta$ is given for $x\in I$,   $\delta>0$,  $\alpha>0$ and $\beta\geq 0$  by
\begin{equation}
    {\bf E}_x\left(\exp(-\alpha \theta_\delta -\beta M_{\theta_\delta})\right)=
    \frac{\psi_\alpha(x)}{\psi_\alpha(x\vee(\delta+l))} \int_{x\vee (\delta +l)}^\infty c_\alpha(y;\delta)\qquad\qquad\qquad
  \end{equation}
  \[\qquad\qquad\qquad \times  \displaystyle \exp\left(- \beta y-\int_{x\vee(\delta+l)}^y b_\alpha(z;\delta) \,dS(z)\right) dS(y)\]
where $\vee$ is the usual maximum operator, 
\begin{equation}

    b_\alpha(y;\delta):= \frac{\varphi_\alpha(y-\delta)\psi^-_\alpha(y)-\varphi^-_\alpha(y)\psi_\alpha(y-\delta)}
    {\varphi_\alpha(y-\delta)\psi_\alpha(y)-\varphi_\alpha(y)\psi_\alpha(y-\delta)}
\end{equation}
and
\begin{align}

    \nonumber
    c_\alpha(y;\delta)&:= \frac{\varphi_\alpha(y)\psi^-_\alpha(y)-\varphi^-_\alpha(y)\psi_\alpha(y)}
    {\varphi_\alpha(y-\delta)\psi_\alpha(y)-\varphi_\alpha(y)\psi_\alpha(y-\delta)}\\
    &
 =\frac{w_\alpha}
       {\varphi_\alpha(y-\delta)\psi_\alpha(y)-\varphi_\alpha(y)\psi_\alpha(y-\delta)}.
\end{align}
Moreover, for $y\geq x\vee (\delta +l)$ 
\begin{equation}

{\bf P}_x(M_{\theta_\delta}>y)=\exp\left(-\int_{x\vee(\delta+l)}^y\frac{dS(z)}{S(z)-S(z-\delta)}\right).

\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

