{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:11:02.358032+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8d888b7ff6008a3cdf437ea312467f5de12dd0cc7450f0db221bdb71b23d4057","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2507.09421, 'Stability of randomly switching stochastic reaction networks with asymptotically linear tr'] Let $X$ be a CTMC on $\mathbb S\subseteq \mathbb Z^d$. We say that $X$ \emph{converges exponentially fast} if
