{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:36.750096+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8d89ef6497ac74ac61a2c4c944cced449f79e967606fdaef7b4a6ad9e9359cf5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 36 of arXiv:2511.20322, 'Dissertation'] Let $b, \si \in G_1([0,\infty)\times \R^d) \cap G^\infty([0,\infty)\times \R^d)$, such that $b$ is $\R^d$-valued and $\si$ is $\R^{d\times d}$-valued.
