{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:48:24.293782+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8d8ed6b7f6e0957ce1772c5153988ab66ea915b46b44b22e88462ca040ece585","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition order of arXiv:2605.08624, 'On the sum-of-digits measures and Cusick's conjecture via stopped random walks'] Define two maps $L, R \colon 2\mathbb{N}+1 \to 2\mathbb{N}+1$ by
\begin{equation}
L(t) = 2t - 1, \qquad R(t) = 2t + 1.
\end{equation}
We define a partial order $"\preceq"$ on $2\mathbb{N}+1$ as follows:
 $s \preceq t$ if and only if either $s=t$, or there exists a finite sequence $w_1, \ldots, w_n \in \{L, R\}$
such that
\begin{equation}
t =w_n \circ \cdots \circ w_1(s).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.367898+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8d933d4732b5f6daaa756eb617c8fcd54b20eeb27958f941c4740c9185000f19","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:LSI of arXiv:2412.07710, 'An H-theorem for a conditional McKean-Vlasov process related to interacting diffusions on '] A measure $\theta \in \mathcal{P}(\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^m)$ satisfies a log-Sobolev inequality (LSI) with constant $C <\infty$ if for every continuously differentiable function $f: \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^m \rightarrow \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}$ such that $\mathbb{E}^\theta[f^2] = 1$, we have
\begin{align*}
    \mathbb E^\theta[f^2 \log f^2] \leq C \mathbb E^{\theta}[|\nabla f|^2].
\end{align*}
We use ${C}_{LS}(\theta)$ to denote the best possible constant $C$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:44:27.982415+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8d93d6446d8971ab907b7487ebac78e866b3e4c0ce346281aaf455633f0b4a77","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2607.13273, 'Asymptotics of transition densities for L\'evy processes with stochastic resetting'] For all $b>a\geq0$ and $c>0$ we have
