{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:16:46.113319+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8d9651c393cd23adfb3a8b0b11209f88af552e925b11a0c4235896cd31be440c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lm:1356 of arXiv:2604.12963, 'Shocks, instability, and the twenty networks\\ of infinite geodesics in the Directed Lands'] Let $\omega\in\Omega_0$, $\theta\in\Theta^\omega$, and $x_0,s_0\in\mathbb{R}$. Then for all  $r<t$ and $x$ in $\mathbb{R}$, setting $a=I_{(x_0,s_0)}^{\theta-}(t)$, we have
\begin{align}
\begin{split}
&W^{\theta-}(a,t;x,r)\ge W^{\theta+}(a,t;x,r)\\
&\qquad\qquad\Longleftrightarrow\ 
\sup_{y\ge a}\{\mathcal L(x,r;y,t)+W^{\theta+}(y,t;a,t)\}\ge\sup_{y\le a}\{\mathcal L(x,r;y,t)+W^{\theta-}(y,t;a,t)\}.
\end{split}
\end{align}
Similarly, if we set $a=I_{(x_0,s_0)}^{\theta+}(t)$, then
\begin{align*}
&W^{\theta-}(a,t;x,r)\le W^{\theta+}(a,t;x,r)\\
&\qquad\qquad\Longleftrightarrow\ 
\sup_{y\ge a}\{\mathcal L(x,r;y,t)+W^{\theta+}(y,t;a,t)\}\le\sup_{y\le a}\{\mathcal L(x,r;y,t)+W^{\theta-}(y,t;a,t)\}.
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.363633+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8d96b4261d4ad2c9be70c7e09c85a6a81f3c9d77b4233af85a952bb9ab2dd04c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:p_var_bounded_remainder of arXiv:2412.01645, 'Regularisation by Gaussian rough path lifts of fractional Brownian motions'] Set $\rho=1/H_- $. There exists a constant $C=C(H_-)$ such that  for all $(s,t) \in [0,1]^2_{\leq}$, ${\color{blue}X}=(X,X') \in \mathcal{D}^{2H_-}_B([s,t])$, and $F \in \mathcal{C}^2$,  we have 
