    S(\rho) = \int_{\mathbb{R}}  \mathcal{D}(\sqrt{\rho_{t}})dt,
\end{align*}
whenever $\rho = \rho_t(\theta) d\theta dt$ and set to $\infty$ otherwise. We write $S_+$ for the integral over $\mathbb{R}_+$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:39:11.688254+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8dc2548cfd4929e548bfa05bd460519bf00e341a320d3e5e89104488d7666128","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 98 (Fixed-envelope restriction of the spatial-profile capacity cores) of arXiv:2608.04993, '2608.04993'] The sublevels $\mathcal C_R$ of \eqref{eq:Hilbert-core-gauge} are
compact in the raw uniform topology, and
\begin{equation}
 c_{\Mmax}(\mathcal C_R^c)\le Ce^{-cR^2}.
\end{equation}
On every $\mathcal C_R$, for every $0<\theta<1$, the map
\[
 x\longmapsto\bigl(X(x),A(x),Q(x)\bigr)
\]
is continuous in
\[
 C_0([0,T];H)\times C^{0,2\alpha}(\mathcal S_2(H)_{\rm sk})
 \times C^{0,\theta}(\mathcal S_1(H)_{\rm sa}).
\]
For every $\nu>1$, the covariance component is also continuous as a map
\begin{equation}
 x\longmapsto Q(x):\mathcal C_R
 \longrightarrow C^{\nu\text{-var}}([0,T];\mathcal S_1(H)_{\rm sa}).
\end{equation}
Every covariance path in the core is trace-norm Lipschitz, with
\begin{equation}
 [Q(x)]_{1;\mathcal S_1}\le\Tr\Gamma,
 \qquad x\in\mathcal C_R.
\end{equation}
Moreover,
\begin{align}
 \sup_{x\in\mathcal C_R}
 \|J^{\eps_n}(x)-\widehat J(x)\|_\infty
 &\le C_R\eps_n^\gamma,
 \\
 \sup_{x\in\mathcal C_R}
 \rho_\alpha(S_2(Y^{\eps_n}(x)),\mathbf X^S(x))
 &\le C_R\eps_n^\kappa,
 \\
 \sup_{x\in\mathcal C_R}
 \|\mathsf E^{\delta_j}(x)-Q(x)\|_{\infty;\mathcal S_1}
 &\le C_R2^{-4j}.

\end{align}
Furthermore there is $C_*$ such that, with
\begin{equation}
 \Gamma_*(R,S)=1+C_*(1+R+S)^2.
\end{equation}
uniformly in the seam $s$,
\begin{equation}
 r_s\mathcal C_R\cup\theta_s\mathcal C_R
 \subset\mathcal C_{\Gamma_*(R,0)},
 \qquad
 x\in\mathcal C_R,\ y\in\mathcal C_S
 \Longrightarrow x\otimes_sy\in\mathcal C_{\Gamma_*(R,S)}.
\end{equation}
The first inclusion remains valid after pointwise substitution of a Borel
stopping time.  The limiting state obeys the exact stopping, shift, and Chen
concatenation identities on $G_*^\Gamma$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:48:24.616649+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8dc2fc4d3d487338d08282d1c67109bd32a79a4d9dbde3c39a556e4b4c676dfa","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma inv_measure of arXiv:2601.04997, 'Fluctuations of the Boundary-Driven Symmetric Zero-Range Process from the NESS'] Define the map $\bar\varphi_N:I_N\to[0, \infty)$ as 
\begin{equation}
   \bar\varphi_N(x):=\frac{-(\alpha\delta-\beta\lambda)(x-1)+\alpha\delta(N-2)+(\alpha+\beta)N^\theta}{\lambda\delta(N-2)+(\lambda+\delta)N^\theta}.
\end{equation}
For $\alpha, \beta, \lambda, \delta\ge0$, $\theta\in\mathbb{R}$ and $N\in\mathbb{N}$ satisfying
\begin{equation}
    \mymax\left\{\frac{\alpha\delta(N-2)+(\alpha+\beta)N^\theta}{\lambda\delta(N-2)+(\lambda+\delta)N^\theta}, \frac{\beta\lambda(N-2)+(\alpha+\beta)N^\theta}{\lambda\delta(N-2)+(\lambda+\delta)N^\theta}\right\}<\varphi^*,
\end{equation}
the measure (equation eq:nu of the paper) with fugacity profile $\bar\varphi_N$ is the unique invariant measure of $\{\eta_t^N, t\ge0\}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:42:47.754976+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8dc31facf7d8383b1e9b3218ac6ffbf62a86339bc6eac9020e5902049cba0913","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 38 of arXiv:2604.11682, 'Semilocalization for inhomogeneous random graphs'] For each vertex $x \in [N]$, define
  \begin{equation*}
    \hat{D}^{+}_{x} = \#\{y \in S_{1}(x) \col w_{y} \geq w_{x}\} = \sum_{y \neq x}\ind_{\{x \sim y, w_{x} \leq w_{y}\}}\,.
  \end{equation*}
  Let $\nu > 0$. With $\nu$-high probability, we have
