{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:04:30.607343+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8dcacab51fb4a3406aa98a3a2c5110e6788e024c9be4819e2a13e94c59e2993e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem l:approx of arXiv:2411.10586, 'A convergence framework for Airy$_\beta$ line ensemble\\ via pole evolution'] For any $\kappa'+\mathrm{i}\eta'\in {\mathcal D}$ as defined in (equation e:defcD of the paper) and any $t\in [T,2T]$, there exists $\kappa+\mathrm{i}\eta\in {\mathcal L}$ such that  $t\leq 2\kappa-2\eta^{-1-\delta}K$, and 
