{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:48:35.788864+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8dcd934004f154d700039ce3e6f5ddb861af426a142a00406892912ba5e035e3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lemma convergence of tilde mu n t of arXiv:2411.09260, 'The Hydrodynamic Limit of Hawkes Processes on Adaptive Stochastic Networks'] For any $\epsilon > 0$, define the event
 \begin{align}
\mathcal{U}^n_{\epsilon} = \bigg\lbrace  d_W\big( \tilde{\mu}^n_{T} , \mu_T \big) \leq \epsilon \bigg\rbrace  .
 \end{align}
 Then for any $\epsilon > 0$,
