{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:53.204807+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8de1f3985e9344d7f1b6d082c147d06809c0ac34e7574dcefc2773985ceee0ec","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 32 of arXiv:2606.12670, 'The censored stochastic six-vertex model and parabolic Kazhdan--Lusztig $R$-polynomials'] Consider the same setup as in Theorem~\ref{thm:labeling}, except there are only $N$ second-class particles.
