{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:17.372970+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8de3ada4cde84de989f5522ac1f121c1a23a8ea49fcd3293dcc2693953868d7c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 (Potter bound) of arXiv:2606.04179, 'Functional Scaling Limits of Interpolated Correlated Random Walks in Hölder Topology'] Let \(\slowVar:(0, \infty) \to [0,\infty)\) be a slowly varying function 
    and let \(a>0\). If \(\slowVar\) is bounded
    on \([a, b]\) for every \(b>a\), then for any \(\epsilon >0\) there exists
    \(x_0 = x_0(\epsilon, \slowVar) >0\) and \(A=A(x_0, \slowVar, a)\) such that
    \(\slowVar\) is positive on \([x_0, \infty)\) and
