{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:42:08.473798+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8df4656cb5469fc3cc9221a20d7456feab94c965501cf22edd68ebf05b16cdf2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary LemmaCondExpII of arXiv:2511.19391, 'Central limit theorem for supercritical Crump-Mode-Jagers processes counted with non-indiv'] Let $(u_{n})_{n \in \mathbb{N}}$ be any admissible ordering of $\mathcal{I}$ and let $\varphi$ be an $h$-dependent descendant characteristic, for some $h \in \mathbb{N}_{0}$, satisfying (C1 of the paper)-(C2 of the paper). Then, for $t \in \mathbb{R}$ and $k=0, \dots, h+1$, 
\begin{align}  
\mathbb{E}[\varphi_{u_{1}}(t-S(u_{1})) \mid \mathcal{G}^{(k)}_{0}] \stackrel{a.s.}{=}  \varphi^{(0)}_{u_{1}}(t-S(u_{1})),
\end{align} 
\noindent while for $i \geq 2$,
\begin{align} 
\mathbb{E}[\varphi_{u_{i}}(t-S(u_{i})) \mid \mathcal{G}^{(k)}_{i-1}] \stackrel{a.s.}{=}  \varphi^{(k)}_{u_{i}}(t-S(u_{i})).
