{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.820690+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8e131c7df4974b4d1cd73ce9d24438b55d260c20f12c39b4353a002c5a0482cc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary finite-time-idle-server-probability of arXiv:2504.02207, 'Finite-Time behaviors of M/M/$n$ Queue: Mixing Time, Mean Queue Length and Tail Bounds'] Let $\pi_{n,t}, \nu_n$ be the queue length distribution at time $t$ and the stationary distribution of the $M/M/n$ system with arrival rate $\lambda_n = n-n^{1-\alpha_n}$ and unit service rate respectively. Denote $r_n$ be a random variable denoting the number of idle servers, that is $r_n = \sqbr{n-q}^+$ where $q$ is the queue length random variable. For $\alpha_n = \alpha \in (1/2, \infty)$, we have
    \begin{align*}
        \P_{\pi_{n,t}}\sqbr{r_n > 0} \leq 4 e \pi n^{\frac{1}{2}-\alpha} + 2\sqrt{e \pi} n^{\frac{1}{4}-\frac{\alpha}{2}} e^{-C_n (\sqrt{n}-\sqrt{\lambda})^2 t} \chi(\pi_{n,0}, \nu_n)
    \end{align*}
    where $\lim_{n \rightarrow \infty} C_n = 1$ for $\alpha \in (1/2,1)$ and $C_n =1$ for $\alpha \in [1,\infty)$. 

    For $\alpha_n = \alpha \in (0,1/2)$, we have
    \begin{align*}
        \P_{\pi_{n,t}}\sqbr{r_n > 0} \geq 1-\kappa n^{\alpha - \frac{1}{2}} e^{-n^{\frac{1}{2}-\alpha}} - e^{-D_n t} \chi\br{\pi_{n,0}, \nu_n}
    \end{align*}
    where $\lim_{n \rightarrow \infty} D_n = 1/25$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:49:24.962315+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8e144ce8ae29220d94b882252ca3da436edf6ce5df0f6621330e43ce4b187d76","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem wang of arXiv:2609.03428, 'A New Sufficient Condition for Oriented Graphs Determined by Their Generalized Skew Spectr'] Let $G$ be a controllable simple graph, and let $d_n$ be the last invariant
