{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:27:14.806162+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8e14bd3a54716484eae9cabbf249830c207be71f38f7c218eba49ca3344a6a18","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2608.23301, 'On a Telegraph Process with Generalized Mittag-Leffler Waiting times and Velocity Driven b'] The absolutely continuous components of the conditional probability law of $X_{\alpha}(t)$, $t\geq0$ are given by its forward and backward densities as follows:
