     In particular, $h_n \in \mathbb{D}^{1,2}(H_{\mathcal{C}\mathcal{M}})$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:39:11.666823+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8e21ef61a9147fbfd296958ba5255dac12370926cb84604b319effde38d612cf","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 8 of arXiv:2608.04644, 'Khinchin's and Chung's Laws of the Iterated Logarithm at Time Zero for the Linear Stochast'] Recall that $H$ is defined in \eqref{def:H}. Suppose that  Condition \ref{hypo}  holds  and that $H<1$. Then there exists a constant
