{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.498656+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8e2a93a5cb1df0196c68e622bc4054f98e5ef18fe2b3c6ff7cf7ef061a715ce6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 25 of arXiv:2605.09706, 'A dyadic construction of a three-dimensional attractive point interaction Markov family'] For the function $P_t(r)$ defined in~\eqref{DefFreeHeat3d}, the following hold.
\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
    \item For every \(s,t>0\) and every \(a,b\in\R\),
\begin{align} 
\int_{\R}
P_s(a-r)\,P_t(r-b)\,dr
=
\frac{s+t}{4\pi st}\,P_{s+t}(a-b).
\end{align}

    \item Let $s>0$, $x\in\R^3\setminus\{0\}$, and let $F:(0,\infty)\to\R$ be measurable such that all integrals below are finite. Then
