{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:35:04.169777+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8e5baa5df09d9c2886b001edf3a632a7eb560de3b93bd8644a9e813b1f409a45","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:greedy-circle-net of arXiv:2609.00399, 'Shannon's problem on the monotonicity of entropy and a Conjecture of Tao'] Let $E\subseteq \mathbb T:=\mathbb R/\mathbb Z$ and let $0<\delta\leq 1$.
There is a finite family $\theta_1,\ldots,\theta_M\in E$ such that
\begin{equation}
 \|\theta_j-\theta_k\|_{\mathbb T}\geq\delta
 \quad (j\neq k),
 \qquad
 E\subseteq\bigcup_{j=1}^{M}
 \left\{\theta:\|\theta-\theta_j\|_{\mathbb T}<\delta\right\}.
\end{equation}
If $E=\varnothing$, one may take $M=0$; if $E\neq\varnothing$, then
\begin{equation}
 1\leq M\leq \delta^{-1}.
\end{equation}
In particular, when $\delta=(2N+1)^{-1}$ with $N\in\mathbb Z_{\geq0}$,
one has $M\leq 2N+1$.","status":"unverified"}

