\end{align}
which is an entire function in each coordinate. The coefficients in the Taylor series expansion   $\mathbf{q}(\lambda)=\sum_{j=0}^\infty \mathbf{s}_j \lambda^j$ are defined via the recursion 
\begin{align}
    \mathbf{s}_0&=-\frac{n+1}{2}\mathbf{A}_n^{-1}\mathbf{e}_n, \qquad \mathbf{s}_k=i \left(k \mathbf{I}-\tfrac{2}{n} \mathbf{A}_n\right)^{-1} \mathbf{B}_n \mathbf{s}_{k-1}, \qquad k\ge 1.
\end{align}
Moreover, 
\begin{align}
    \rho_{2n}^{(2)}(0,\lambda)=\frac{1}{4\pi^2}\left(1+2\;\mathbf{v}_n^\top\Re \mathbf{q}_n(\lambda)\right).
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

