{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.522599+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8e7e093a6155d9f338bcb7b4a187b93eb5df28e064b0442ef70bd044f421de56","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm RL of arXiv:2411.03104, '{\bf Coupling Methods and Applications on Path Dependent McKean-Vlasov SDEs}\footnote{Supp'] Assume {\bf (A)}. Then there exists an increasing function $c:(0,\infty)\rightarrow[0,\infty)$ such that for positive $f\in\mathscr{B}_b(\mathbb R^d)$,
