{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.579996+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8e807f5303ef3e4b9b78205213b6318df054f40464f0b45678491d5553cd5f1a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 8 of arXiv:2609.01296, 'Asymptotic safety regions for Gabor frames generated by Hermite functions'] Let $0< \delta < \eta < \frac{1}{3}$. Then there exists $n_{\eta,\delta}\in\N$ such that, for every $n\geq n_{\eta,\delta}$, the region
