is contained in the frame set of the $n$-th Hermite function. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:51:33.324751+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8e8102b14299bad52ada5576cfc8d36b0982cc67d397f00bd91181430618ebce","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma equiv-spectra-homotopy-po of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] Pushouts along unbased level h-cofibrations are homotopy pushouts in the $G$-equivariant model structure.
    \begin{proof}
        Consider a pushout as depicted on the left, where $i$ is an unbased level h-cofibration, and pick a factorization of $f$ as a cofibration $j$ followed by a \emph{level} weak equivalence $g$, leading to the iterated pushout depicted on the right:
        \[
            \begin{tikzcd}
                A\arrow[r, "f"]\arrow[dr,phantom,"\ulcorner"{very near end}]\arrow[d,"i"'] & B\arrow[d] &[3em] A\arrow[dr,phantom,"\ulcorner"{very near end}]\arrow[r, "j"]\arrow[d,"i"'] & X\arrow[dr,phantom,"\ulcorner"{very near end}]\arrow[d,"i'"]\arrow[r,"g","\sim"'] & B\arrow[d]\\
                C\arrow[r] & D & C\arrow[r]& Y\arrow[r,"h"'] & D\rlap.
            \end{tikzcd}
        \]
        If $H\subset G$ and $V$ is any $H$-representation, then $i(V)$ is in particular an h-cofibration in $\textbf{\textup{$\bm H$-Top}}$, whence so is $i'(V)$. As $g(V)$ is an $H$-equivariant weak equivalence, so is $h(V)$ by Lemma~(lemma:h-cof-compute-po of the paper), i.e.\ $h$ is again a $G$-equivariant level weak equivalence. This in particular shows that the original square is a homotopy pushout.
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:23.333935+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8e827a613a3387838b370708bc82fe131f99b1ef7738ecaef6dc18f43823affe","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 ({\cite[Proposition 2.9) of arXiv:2512.05466, 'Stochastic Flows and Marked Stable Processes'] {AWYskew}}]
