{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:56.350141+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8e899320329d27e88c28e5aa19f2d7e4ef8a546c3fbf296ca8bef58617e396f5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 38 of arXiv:2603.13798, 'Iterated Graph Systems (I): random walks and diffusion limits'] There are constants $n_{\mathrm{eld}},r_{\mathrm{eld}},t_{\mathrm{eld}},c_{\mathrm{eld}},C_{\mathrm{eld}}>0$ such that, for all $n\ge n_{\mathrm{eld}}$, all $x\in V(\Xi^n)$, all admissible radii $r\in(0,r_{\mathrm{eld}}]$, and all $t\in(0,t_{\mathrm{eld}}r^{\dimwalk(\Xi)}]$, we have
