In particular, the Poissonised walks $Y_t^{(n)}:=X_{N_{a_nt}}^{\Xi^n}$ are tight in $D([0,T],\Xi_{\mathrm M})$ for every $T>0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:44:17.358232+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8e926b804513b1ffcebaca7e5a2235b710032d7e85f0dd5db7f97a59d2883b8f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:learnability-ledger of arXiv:2608.23860, 'Revelation Control'] With the definitions above, the learned net value satisfies the exact identity
