{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:19:56.677145+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8ea3e9d54d93e1ce8f8a3aed31124fdda7bf7ee9d630292c1792376d488a1ebc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 21 (Canonical truncation morphism) of arXiv:2608.30875, 'A Decomposition Theorem for Topological Semi-small Maps'] Let $f : X \longrightarrow Y$ be a continuous map of topological spaces and let
