{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:45:05.586748+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8ea4083f993c8f130bd809f55a5b7cc9b416633ff2bfaa6fd70bb1e6c8d202d3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 24 of arXiv:2608.05679, 'Small ball probabilities and Chung's law of the iterated logarithm for Gaussian Volterra p'] \cite[p. 257, (7.11)--(7.13)]{Ledoux}
		  If there is a decreasing function $f: (0, \delta] \to (0, \infty)$ such that $$N(S,d_Z,\varepsilon) \le f(\varepsilon), \ \text{for all } \varepsilon \in (0, \delta],$$  and there are constants $K_2 \ge K_1 > 1$ such that
