{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:30:14.228298+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8ea497fa5e0c2d4839087b71e37edf579a3f9fa0e01fe27d1aab43717ead5088","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lemma-on-difference-U_M-for-critical of arXiv:2608.23202, 'Locally finite Fixed points of Branching Brownian Motion'] Given $b>0$, there exists $K, C_1, C_2>0$\footnote{We stress that we are here and in (equation quant-bound-for-super-critical-for-difference of the paper) writing ``there exists a $K>0$" rather than writing ``for all $K>0$". We expect (equation quant-bound-for-super-critical-for-difference of the paper), (equation quant-bound-for-difference-critical of the paper) to hold for all $K>0$ rather than only for $K$ large enough. We were able to verify (equation quant-bound-for-super-critical-for-difference of the paper), (equation quant-bound-for-difference-critical of the paper) only for large enough $K>0$, which will be sufficient for our purposes.} such that for all $t$ large enough and $z\in [-\frac{1}{4}\log t , b t]$,
    \begin{align}
        C_1 t^{-\frac{3}{2}} (z+\log t)e^{-\sqrt 2 z}e^{-\frac{z^2}{2t}}\le u_M(t,  &\sqrt{2}t + z - K ) - u_M(t, \sqrt{2}t + z + K ) \\ \nonumber & \le C_2 t^{-\frac{3}{2}} (z+\log t)e^{-\sqrt 2 z}e^{-\frac{z^2}{2t}}.
    \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:17:17.095379+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8ea4bc119dfe97fa65665add3dbf1c18aecb9c4fc1415ead48c744e565244212","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 22 of arXiv:2608.19976, 'Random valuations'] If $\Phi$ is a $\sigma$-continuous non-negative stationary isotropic
  ID valuation with independent increments, then the corresponding
  L\'evy measure on $\sC\times(0,\infty)$ is given by
  \begin{equation}

    \nu(\sC_L\times A)
    =\sum_{k=0}^{d} \int_A \int_{G(d,k)}
    \E(V_{d-k}(Y_{E,r}+\Pi_{E^\perp}L))\gamma_k(dE) a_{k,r}\mu(dr)
  \end{equation}
  for each compact set $L$ in $\R^d$ and Borel $A\subset(0,\infty)$,
  where $\gamma_k$ is the normalised Haar measure on $G(d,k)$,
  $Y_{E,r}$ is a random compact convex set in $E^\perp$ such that
  $Y_{RE,r}$ has the same distribution as $RY_{E,r}$ for each
  deterministic rotation $R$, and $a_{k,r}$ is a measurable non-negative
  function of $r>0$. If $K\in\Kd$, then
  \begin{equation}

    \nu(\sC_K\times A)=\sum_{k=0}^{d} \sum_{j=0}^{d-k}
    c_{0,d}^{d-k-j,k+j} 
    V_{d-k-j}(K) \int_A \E V_j(Y_{E,r})a_{k,r}\mu(dr).
  \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:15.338496+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8ea5b10b7cf4874f1e908ebc516337a3a193bef7e567c4747732bf8db6c86d2c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 3 of arXiv:2506.15044, '2506.15044'] Let $(\tau_n)$ be an FS for $\mathbb{C}$, $\mathcal{D}$ be a class of processes, and $X,Y\in \mathcal{D}^\mathbb{C}$. Suppose that $(T_n,X^{(n)})$ is an FCS for $X\in \mathcal{D}^\mathbb{C}$  (resp. a CS for $X$). Put $S_n=T_n\wedge \tau_n$ for each $n\in \mathbf{N}^+$.
\begin{itemize}
  \item [$(1)$] $X=Y$ if and only if for each $n\in \mathbf{N}^+$, $XI_{\llbracket{0,\tau_n}\rrbracket}=YI_{\llbracket{0,\tau_n}\rrbracket}$, or equivalently, $X^{\tau_n}=Y^{\tau_n}$.
  \item [$(2)$] $(S_n)$ is also an FS for $\mathbb{C}$, and $(S_n,X^{(n)})$ is also an FCS for $X\in \mathcal{D}^\mathbb{C}$ (resp. a CS for $X$) satisfying
       \begin{equation*}
       X^{S_n}=(X^{(n)})^{S_n}, \quad n\in \mathbf{N}^+.
       \end{equation*}
  \item [$(3)$] $X$ can be expressed as
      \begin{equation}
      X=\left(X_0I_{\llbracket{0}\rrbracket}+\sum\limits_{n=1}^{{+\infty}}X^{\tau_n}I_{\rrbracket{\tau_{n-1},\tau_n}
      \rrbracket}\right)\mathfrak{I}_\mathbb{C},\quad \tau_0=0.
      \end{equation}
      Furthermore, if $(\widetilde{\tau}_n)$ is also an FS for $\mathbb{C}$, then $X=\widetilde{X}$ where  $\widetilde{X}$ is given by
      \begin{equation*}
      \widetilde{X}=\left(X_0I_{\llbracket{0}\rrbracket}+\sum\limits_{n=1}^{{+\infty}}X^{\widetilde{\tau}_n}
      I_{\rrbracket{\widetilde{\tau}_{n-1},\widetilde{\tau}_n}
      \rrbracket}\right)\mathfrak{I}_\mathbb{C},\quad \widetilde{\tau}_0=0.
      \end{equation*}
      In this case, we say the expression of \eqref{x-expression-FS} is independent of the choice of FS $(\tau_n)$.
\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

