{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:25.283300+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8eaa9049afdbb626ea5ae86df57d2d98c36953f95a64f8c82aa167cba56d34af","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 20 of arXiv:2606.21778, 'Pontryagin Maximum Principle in Free Probability Theory'] Consider the fSDE \eqref{intro-freeCSDE-inform}, BSDE \eqref{eq:BSDE} and cost functional as defined in \Cref{sec:DiffProc:FunObj}. Let $\hat{U}\in\mathcal{U}$ and $\hat{X}$ the associated controlled diffusion. Assume $(\hat{Y},\hat{Z})$ is a solution of \eqref{eq:BSDE} such that
