	In particular,
	\begin{align*}
		\norm{\overline{P}-\Pi}_{F} &\geq \norm{(P_{la})_{ra}-\Pi}_{F}, \quad \norm{\widetilde{P}-\Pi}_{F} \geq \norm{(P_{la})_{ra}-\Pi}_{F}, \\
		\norm{P_{la}-\Pi}_{F} &\geq \norm{(P_{la})_{ra}-\Pi}_{F}, \quad \norm{P_{ra}-\Pi}_{F} \geq \norm{(P_{la})_{ra}-\Pi}_{F}. 
	\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:57:20.650554+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8ed4f7ad0a8598aa760740b528bbcf1e9671d77d17366610186b6e40a6fbab57","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop prop4.5 of arXiv:2411.09988, 'A Study in Markov Chains, Loop-Erased Random Walk and Loop Soups'] The following is a valid way to get the rooted loop soup.
