{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:45.028445+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8ed5de03eb209048d3e170cc962b2d2400ad29be71970aa91664920f5a1d0da4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 15 of arXiv:2606.06859, 'The rectangular finite free heat flow'] Suppose that $r(t) = \big(r_1(t) > \hdots > r_d(t) > 0\big)$ satisfies
    \begin{equation}
\dot{r}_k(t) = \gamma_1 \sum_{j\colon j\ne k}{ \left(\frac{1}{r_k(t)-r_j(t)} + \frac{1}{r_k(t)+r_j(t)}\right) } + \frac{\gamma_2}{r_k(t)}
\end{equation}
for all $t \ge 0$ and some $\gamma_1, \gamma_2 \ge 0$.  Then $r(t)$ also satisfies the \emph{Calogero--Moser equations of type $BC$} with an attractive potential,
\begin{equation} 
    \ddot{r}_k(t) = - 2\gamma_1^2 \sum_{j\colon j\ne k}{ \left(\frac{1}{\big(r_k(t)-r_j(t) \big)^3} + \frac{1}{\big( r_k(t)+r_j(t) \big)^3}\right) } - \frac{\gamma_2^2}{r_k(t)^3}.
\end{equation}
Conversely, any solution to (\ref{eq:CM-BC}) that satisfies (\ref{eq:1o-CM}) at $t = 0$ satisfies (\ref{eq:1o-CM}) for all $t \ge 0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:27.007017+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8ed6e194cc407ea6936b4aa111578f19f9ca104aa33e2807aea9a404858efe92","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lem7d of arXiv:2505.11700, 'Distribution of the cokernels of determinantal row-sparse matrices'] For every $1 \le r \le n-1$, we have
