{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:35:04.169696+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8f2c10adb10b19e0cc42f9c24fac15379f4c4c8daa026876ca5621b04c515597","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:near-period-absorption of arXiv:2609.00399, 'Shannon's problem on the monotonicity of entropy and a Conjecture of Tao'] Fix $k\geq1$, let $p$ be a countably supported probability mass function on $G$, and
