{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.583601+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8f3bfa7b68cad422b797979eaecb0b4d716ec161b6f1ffb7c27cf09a85289148","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Main.Thm01 of arXiv:2411.15485, '\bf\Large Stochastic Volterra Equations for Local Times of Spectrally Positive L\'evy Proc'] For each $\zeta\geq 0$, the process $L^\xi_\zeta$ equals in distribution to the unique non-negative continuous solution of the stochastic Volterra equation
 	\begin{eqnarray}
 	X_\zeta(t) \!\!\!&=\!\!\!& \zeta\cdot c \cdot W'(t)  
 	+  \int_0^\zeta\int_0^\infty \big( W(t)-W(t-y) \big) \, N_0(dz, dy)   + \int_0^t \int_0^{X_\zeta(s)}   W'(t-s) \, B_c(ds,dz) \cr
 	\!\!\!&\!\!\!& + \int_0^t \int_0^{X_\zeta(s)} \int_0^\infty  \big( W(t-s)-W(t-s-y) \big) \, \widetilde{N}_\nu(ds,dz,dy), \quad t\geq 0,
 	\end{eqnarray}
 	where $N_0(dz, dy)$ is a  Poisson random measure on $(0,\infty)^2$ with intensity $\bar\nu(y)\,dz\,dy$, $B_c(ds,dz)$ is a Gaussian white noise on $(0,\infty)^2$ with intensity $2c\cdot ds\, dz$ and $\widetilde{N}_\nu(ds,dz,dy)$ is a compensated Poisson random measure on $(0,\infty)^3$ with intensity $ds\, dz\,\nu(dy)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:48:24.618127+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8f3cbe140c4a8b4f037b323623bc848af3024945dc8fe6fb07df46cc4f01736b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:uniqueness of arXiv:2601.04997, 'Fluctuations of the Boundary-Driven Symmetric Zero-Range Process from the NESS'] For each $\theta\ge0$, there exists a unique (in law) stochastic process $\mathscr{Y}$ in the space of continuous distributions $\mathcal{C}([0, T], \mathcal{S}'_\theta)$ such that:    
\begin{enumerate}[i)]

    \item for every $H\in \mathcal{S}_\theta$, the stochastic processes $\{\mathscr{M}_t(H), t\in[0, T]\}$ and $\{\mathscr{N}_t(H), t\in[0, T]\}$ defined by
    \begin{equation}
        \begin{split}
        &\mathscr{M}_t(H):=\mathscr{Y}_t(H)-\mathscr{Y}_0(H)-\int_0^t\mathscr{Y}_s\left(\Phi'(\bar\rho_\theta)\Delta H\right)\de s,
        \\&\mathscr{N}_t(H):=\mathscr{M}_t(H)^2-t\left\|\nabla H\right\|_{L^{2, \theta}}^2
        \end{split}
    \end{equation}
    are $\mathcal{F}_t$-martingales, where $\mathcal{F}_t:=\sigma\{\mathscr{Y}_s(H): s\le t, H\in\mathcal{S}_\theta\}$,

    \item $\mathscr{Y}_0$ is a mean-zero Gaussian field with covariance given by, for $H, G\in\mathcal{S}_\theta$,
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{E}\left[\mathscr{Y}_0(H)\mathscr{Y}_0(G)\right]=\int_0^1 H(u)G(u)\chi_\theta(u)\de u,
    \end{equation}
    with $\chi_\theta$ given in (equation eq:chi of the paper).

\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.680369+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8f3d4d3a771c4929f77bbf1773e69711c2211baa660c00c5bd92a6ac3119111e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary of arXiv:2412.09235, 'A semiconcavity approach to stability of entropic plans and exponential convergence of Sin'] When the two marginals satisfy (equation conditio:caff of the paper) and $\Sigma\succ 0$, we have
