{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:41:29.053734+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8f5c11a1524bf46b06a9f7a76c4829ac472d93c978580349d6544746464b7dc0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 ($C^0$-estimate on $u_i$) of arXiv:2608.26619, 'Uniqueness of Positively Curved Ancient Ricci Flows on Surfaces with Boundary'] Let $g_i(t) = u_i(t)g_{0}$ denote the old solutions defined above. Then for each time $t_0<0$, we have the following $C^0$-estimate uniform in $i$:
