{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:22:21.891641+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8f946cd755960ad5476abd66084201aaa2a025b0aeb857c8a271c3c85105011e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma thm13.11 of arXiv:2411.11393, '\fontsize{16}{19} \selectfont On differentiability of reward functionals corresponding to '] Let $\mathfrak A$ denote the characteristic operator of $X$. Moreover, let $J\subset I$ be an open interval with $\tau^J<\infty$ $\mathbb{P}_x$-a.s.\ for all $x\in J$ and $\psi:J \to [0,\infty)$ a bounded measurable function. Assume that $\mathbb{E}_{\mathpalette\mathpalette\mathpalette\bigcdot@{.6}@{.6}@{.6}}[\psi(X_{t\wedge \tau^J})]\vert_J\to \psi$ weakly for $t\searrow 0$. We extend $\psi$ to $I$ by 0 outside of $J$, set $\tau:=\tau^J$ and
    \begin{align*}
        f(x):=\mathbb{E}_x\left[e^{-\int_0^{\tau}\psi(X_s)ds} g(X_{\tau}) \right]
