\end{equation*}

where $\tau_{\mathfrak a}$ denotes the first return time to $\mathfrak a$ after time zero. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:46:25.366064+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8fadfbaf88282de159056caa261d5e609990ad52c3368cb55682ad665bba9cd9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop translation-invariance of arXiv:2604.14122, 'The scaling limit of random walk and\\ the intrinsic metric on planar critical percolation'] Let $U\subset[0,1]^2$ be open and simply connected. Let $D_1$ be the support of $(\mathcal{X}\cap \overline{V},\mathfrak{d}_V)_{V\in\mathfrak{C}_U}$ and $D_2$ be the support of $U^*$. Let $\mu_U(\cdot\mid\cdot)$ be a probability kernel from $D_2$ to $D_1$ such that $\mu_U(\cdot\mid U^*)$ is a.s.\ equal to the conditional law of $(\mathcal{X}\cap \overline{V},\mathfrak{d}_V)_{V\in\mathfrak{C}_U}$ given $U^*$. Then for each $z \in \mathbf C$ such that $U+z\subset[0,1]^2$ one can choose versions of $\mu_U$ and $\mu_{U+z}$ such that for all events $A$ in $D_1$ and $u \in D_2$ we have
\begin{equation*}
    \mu_U(A\mid u)=\mu_{U+z}(A+z\mid u+z).
\end{equation*}
where $A+z$ denotes the event that the translated metrics $(\mathcal{X}\cap \overline{V}-z,\mathfrak{d}_{V}(\cdot+z,\cdot+z))_{V\in\mathfrak{C}_{U+z}}$ are in the event $A$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

