{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.583633+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8fcfb21fff13191b91f390a059057de6cd0cd831795b5c6267d21ff1255737b7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2609.01333, '2609.01333'] Let $\lambda > 0$. The functions  $e_k(t) := \cos(kt)$ and $\widetilde{e}_k(t):= \sin(kt)$ for $k \in \mathbb{N}$ are eigenfunctions of $L_\lambda$ To be more precise we have  \begin{align*}
