{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:41:03.290298+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8fdfdba510096b7572e92da1691bafe28bf24fda746bf7fe6cbb602a35bfe852","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop_SMA_1 of arXiv:2411.08846, 'On the Number of Crossings and Bouncings\\ of a Diffusion at a Sticky Threshold'] Let $X$ be the sticky Brownian motion of stickiness parameter $\rho>0 $, defined on the filtered probability space
	$(\Omega, \bF, (\bF_t)_{t\ge 0},\Prob_x) $ such that $\Prob_x $-a.s., $X_0=x $.
	Let $m_{\sqrt n \rho} $ be the measure defined for all $x\in \IR $ by
	\begin{equation} 
		m_{\sqrt n \rho}(\mathrm{d} x) = \,\mathrm{d} x + \sqrt n \rho \, \delta_{0}(\mathrm{d} x)
	\end{equation}
	and $(g_{n})_{n}$ a sequence of measurable real functions such that for all $x\in \IR$ 
	\begin{multline}

		\lim_{n \longrightarrow  \infty} \Bigbraces{ \frac{g_{n}^2(\sqrt n x)}{n} + 
			\frac{m_{\sqrt n \rho}(g^{2}_n)}{\sqrt n}  \\
			+  \frac{ \bigbraces{\int_{-\infty}^{+\infty} |x| g_n(x) \,\mathrm{d} x}  \big( 1 + \log(n) \big)  g_n(\sqrt n x)}{n}
			+   \frac{{   \big( 1 + \log(n) \big)  m_{\sqrt n \rho}(|g_n|)}}{\sqrt n}}
		= 0
	\end{multline}
	and $\lim_{n\to \infty}m_{\sqrt n \rho}(g_n) = M$.
	Then, for all $t \geq 0$,
	\begin{equation}
		\frac{1}{\sqrt n} \sum_{i=1}^{[nt]}g_n(\sqrt n \hfprocess{X}{}{i-1})  \xlongrightarrow[n \rightarrow  \infty]{\Prob_x}  M \loct{X}{0}{t}.
	\end{equation}
	Also, if~(equation eq_connd_gn_aggreg of the paper) holds and $\sup_n \bigbraces{m_{\sqrt n \rho}(|g_n|)} <\infty$ then the above convergence is localy uniform in time, in $\Prob_x$-probability. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:44:17.354300+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8fe0293ce38a62be11e11760e6e618d33ce607a6f1a038eeddeaea900b9e8f16","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main of arXiv:2608.23554, 'Provably adaptive sampling with uniform and remasking \\ discrete diffusion models'] Let \(0 = t_0 < t_1 < \ldots < t_N < T\) and suppose that for some \(\kappa \in (0, 1)\),  \(t_{k+1} - t_k \leq \kappa \min(1, T - t_{k+1})\) for all \(k \in \{0, \ldots, N - 1\}\). 
 Consider either of the following two processes:
     \begin{enumerate}
         \item \emph{Uniform}: \((q_t)_{t \in [0, T]}\) are the marginals of the uniform process,
         \item \emph{Remasking}: \((q_t)_{t \in [0, T]}\) are the marginals of the remasking process.
     \end{enumerate}
     Under~(asm:se-loss of the paper),~(alg:sampler of the paper) initialized from \(p_0 = q_{\mathrm{noise}}\) outputs a sample \(x_{T - t_N} \sim  p_{\mathrm{output}}\) such that
    \begin{align}

        \mathsf{KL}(q_{T - t_N} \| p_{\mathrm{output}}) \lesssim \mathsf{KL}(q_T \| q_{\mathrm{noise}})+ \varepsilon_{\mathrm{score}} + \kappa\mathrm{DTC}(X_0).
    \end{align}
    In particular, for \(T =  O\left(\log (\varepsilon^{-1}d \log S)\right)\), and corresponding choice of \(q_{\mathrm{noise}}\)\footnote{\(q_{\mathrm{noise}} = \mathrm{Unif}\{[S]^d\}\) for the uniform process and \(q_{\mathrm{noise}} = \mu^{\otimes d}\) with \(\mu(b) = \bI\{b \in [S]\} \nicefrac{e^{-T}  }{S} + \nu(T, b) (1 - e^{-T})\) for the remasking process.}, it suffices to take 
    \begin{equation*}
        N = \widetilde O\left(\frac{\mathrm{DTC}(X_0)}{\varepsilon}\right),
    \end{equation*}
    discretization steps to guarantee \(\mathsf{KL}(q_{T - t_N} \| p_{\mathrm{output}}) \lesssim \varepsilon_{\mathrm{score}} + \varepsilon\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:25:41.605205+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8fe22df0b41130fe7afa39f5faf6ef7a61bdd47c7be945577df93b5c096190c8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem percolation of arXiv:2608.13084, '\bf Branching random walk in random environment'] If $\{\#\mathcal{C}(0) = \infty\}$ happens with positive probability, i.e., $\theta_{{\mathbb Z}^d}(p)>0$, then
