{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:24:45.892510+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8ff5f57d241cb5e531378dd7f79c027def0ddbe101003c2ada63259b04888185","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:pythHS of arXiv:2509.02996, 'Group-averaged Markov chains: mixing improvement'] Let $G$ be a finite group with Haar measure $\mu$ that acts on $\mathcal{X}$ and $\pi$ is assumed to be $G$-invariant. Assume that $P,M$ (and hence $P_{da}$ by Proposition (prop:inheritance of properties of the paper)) are HS operators and $M,P_{da} \in \mathcal{D}(G,\nu)$, where the measure $\nu$ satisfies $(g,h) \overset{D}{=} (g^{-1},h^{-1}) \sim \nu$. We have
