{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:11:57.308072+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9012b114dd65d71947435dbd8a4342d87df372b16598f592c023d031e6f4fe69","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2607.22892, 'Mirror Langevin diffusions: Convergence rates and Markov chain approximations'] Assume that all the conditions of Theorem \ref{prop:PI} hold. Additionally, assume that 
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item[(a)] $\nabla^2 u$ is uniformly bounded above by $\alpha_0 I$, for some $\alpha_0 >0$. 
        \item[(b)] For some $\delta, \alpha_1 >0$, 
\begin{equation}
    \varphi_\alpha^*(x):=\left[  x \cdot \frac{\partial V}{\partial x} - \alpha x^T \nabla^2u(x) x \right]\ge \delta V(x) - \alpha_1.
