{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:49:06.317386+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9016245b4d87ad7e12cd8cd64a238f996986c843b1db509a0dedf12eae52bfb7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:characterization of arXiv:2601.10359, 'An Operator It\^o Formula for Volterra Gaussian Processes:\\ The Intrinsic Bracket via Cau'] Let $X$ be a centered Volterra Gaussian process for which the operator It\^o formula (Theorem~(thm:main of the paper)) holds. Suppose $\nu$ is a signed Borel measure on $[0,T]$ such that for all $\varphi\in C^3_b(\mathbb{R})$,
\begin{equation}
\varphi(X_t) = \varphi(0) + \delta(\varphi'(X)\Pi DX\cdot\mathbf{1}_{[0,t]}) + \frac{1}{2}\int_0^t \varphi''(X_s)\,d\nu(s)
\end{equation}
holds in $L^2(\Omega)$ for all $t\in[0,T]$. Then $\nu = \Gamma^X$ (i.e., $d\nu = d\Gamma^X$) on $[0,T]$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:09.860759+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_90192daa8a50d1311f8cbb594a993e8ae669d51186142b52cb5cad3132fc846a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2605.21209, 'Sensitivity analysis of Stochastic Fluid Models: \\Stationary and transient quantities wit'] For $s$ with $Re(s)>0$, the matrix $\frac{\partial}{\partial\btheta}\bPsi(s;\btheta)$ is the solution of the equation
