    then we have
    \begin{equation*}
        H\bigl(\Id+\psi_\Omega H(\Id+\Omega)\bigr)[\ttY] \sststile{\psi(\hat{\alpha}[\eta])}{\psi(\hat{\alpha}[\eta])} \bfL(u)_{H(f)}[\Gamma]^\eta,
    \end{equation*}
    where $A^\eta$ is the formula obtained from $A$ by replacing every occurrence of $\forall x\in \ttL(u)_\ttOmega$ to $\forall x\in \ttL(u)_{\psi(\eta)}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:49.843066+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9029af22af5830cf666eb8d670b7fd3391284926fdd99e3cc958973c82450d4e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 16 of arXiv:2506.13913, '2506.13913'] {The Markov property for Itô diffusions}{}
 Let \((\Omega, \mathcal{F}, \{\mathcal{F}_t\}_{t \geq 0}, \mathbb{P})\) be a filtered probability space and  \(\{X_t\}_{t \geq 0} \in \mathbb{R}^d\) an Itô diffusion defined on \((\Omega, \mathcal{F}, \mathbb{P})\). Then, for all \(0 \leq s \leq t\) and any bounded measurable function \(f: \mathbb{R}^d \to \mathbb{R}\), it holds that
