{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:16:18.664883+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_90331bdc3b6967f91b2a44c033068c7d1212af915263b75375bfc8384726f8eb","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 (Regular Lagrangian flow) of arXiv:2607.25685, 'Mimicking diffusion processes with differential equations'] $Z:[0,T]\times\R^d\to\R^d$ is a \emph{regular Lagrangian flow} (RLF) for a velocity field $v$ if
