{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:01:22.646823+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_903b95d801fd4b392c16e07dbe6aaa54fbc69761ad228cbd76968499b26cd6f9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:singular-block-obstruction of arXiv:2607.03639, '\vspace{-0.6in}An AI-Assisted Solution to the Signed BAR Conjecture: Uniqueness in the Har'] Consider an SRBM in $E=\mathbb R_+^d$ with positive definite covariance matrix, nonsingular completely-$\mathcal{S}$ reflection matrix $R$, and stationary probability $\pi_0$. Assume that the process is strong Markov, is Feller on \(C_0(E)\), and satisfies the quantitative recurrence conditions (equation eq:ce-ergodicity of the paper) and (equation eq:ce-regulator-bound of the paper). If $R_{AA}$ is singular for some nonempty proper set $A\subsetneq J$, then signed BAR uniqueness fails.

More precisely, there exists a finite signed BAR tuple $(\overline\pi,\overline\nu_1,\ldots,\overline\nu_d)$ such that
\begin{equation}
 \overline\pi(E)=0,
 \qquad
