{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:18:19.237079+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_909c4feb3092e6dfdafe0c13f9274779e74a9425e4cccceaa05b47a6cd90ba1a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 83 of arXiv:2608.29086, '2608.29086'] [$\prod\prod_{i<j} CONE(S_i \cap S_j)$]
Given $M \subset H_0$ and its open covering 
\begin{equation*}
V=\{S_i \subset M \ |\ i \in I \}.
\end{equation*}
$\prod\prod_{i<j} CONE(S_i \cap S_j)$ is the collection of all formal products of $\mathbf{R}$-valued functions on $|S_i \cap S_j| \subset \mathbf{R}^2$ ($i, j \in I,\ i<j$), i.e.,
\begin{multline*}
\prod\prod_{i<j} CONE(S_i \cap S_j):=
\left\{ \prod_{i \in \{i \in I | i<j\}}\prod_{i \in I} (f_{i, j}, S_i \cap S_j)\ |\  \right.\\
\left.\phantom{\prod_{i \in I}} \text{$f_{i, j}$ is a $\mathbf{R}$-valued function on $|S_i \cap S_j|$  ($i, j \in I,\  i<j$)} \right\},
\end{multline*}
where we write $(f_{i, j}, S_i \cap S_j)$ instead of $f_{i, j}$ to emphasize its domain.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:15:15.571649+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_909ea32025554bfb8b2abdac2832d3db59b4a4cd75307976af0c4c21a330b8d4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:goe-berry-esseen of arXiv:2507.12502, 'Quantitative Edge Eigenvector Universality for Random Regular Graphs: Berry-Esseen Bounds '] For the constrained GOE matrix $W$ with $W\mathbf{e} = 0$ and any deterministic unit vector $\mathbf{q} \perp \mathbf{e}$:
