{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:52:57.724139+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_90b0b6330b03b6835b12bac86415549e878a6c71328a67ad0e3e94a322e0d8d7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 39 (Scaling law for Nesterov) of arXiv:2609.02728, 'Momentum in large-batch training: Polyak enlarges the critical batch size, Nesterov improv'] \normalfont
Assume \(\eta<1\) and \(k\gtrsim\max(\eta^{-1}_\rho,(1-\rho)^{-1})\). Then
\begin{equation}

\mathbb E[\cE(\btheta_k)]\eqsim
\begin{cases}
(\eta_\rho k)^{-s}+\dfrac{\sigma^2}{B}\eta_\rho, & 1-\rho\gtrsim\sqrt{\eta},\\[2mm]
N(k)+(\eta_\rho k)^{-s}+\dfrac{\sigma^2}{B}\min\{\eta_\rho,\eta_\rho^{1/\beta}\}, & \dfrac{\eta}{B^\beta}\lesssim1-\rho\lesssim\sqrt{\eta},
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
where \(N(k)\) denotes the underdamped transient and satisfies \(0\leq N(k)\lesssim\min\{1,(\eta k)^{-s}\}\rho^k\). If \(1-\rho\lesssim\eta/B^\beta\), the dynamics are not risk stable. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.301134+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_90b15e0e83e24a0ce7f055c92021fae2dfccf79c6e7fb2632016d03fad69d769","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop rorw of arXiv:2604.21663, 'Large deviations for non-irreducible Markov chains on Euclidean spaces'] Let $d=1$.
