{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:49.833317+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_90bc4bdf15588efc05e2f40b1bed6df5cf81b59bdb9d9931261675444c91d970","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 7 of arXiv:2506.12632, 'Point process convergence of extremes in $K$-symmetric exclusion'] Suppose $p$ satisfies Condition \ref{lighttail}, $\nu$ satisfies Condition \ref{initialprofilecond}, and $\eta_0 \sim \nu_L$, where $L \uparrow \infty$ as $t \to \infty$. Let $0 \le m_0 < m_1 < \cdots < m_k$. 

