{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:26.251112+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_90cba8a8006c4f5b04acfdf6853c2b895511cf86d98caad23e5dc04f1f4c2948","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 3 of arXiv:2605.23222, 'On global solutions to the semidiscrete stochastic heat equation'] For $\beta$ sufficiently small, the following holds: There is an $\Fc$-measurable set $\Omega^{\textup{sol}} \subset \Omega^+$ with $Q(\Omega^{\textup{sol}}) = 1$ such that the function 
