{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.576181+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_90f006a6f15718de0d8606f81cd9717716925e922b23ca52ef2e91054047f6fe","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lem-properties-of-V-L of arXiv:2412.08932, 'Gaussian heat kernel asymptotics for conditioned random walks'] For any  $a\in \supp V$, there exist constants $c_1, c_2 >0$ such that, for any $n\geqslant 1$ and $x\in [a,\infty)$,
