{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:51:12.736518+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_90f1cd619e02b54bf286f4b536da6cc8cb3be4dca05aebf7540af14d3c690589","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 33 of arXiv:2605.02002, 'Glauber dynamics for random field Ising models on bounded degree graphs and MLSI'] Suppose the graph $G$ has $\alpha$-stretched-exponential growth and the RFIM $\mu_G$ satisfies $\operatorname{WSM}(C)$ for some $C>0$. Then we can find some $c_0=c_0(\alpha,C_\alpha,C)>0$ such that for any $\delta>0$, with $\mathbb{P}_h$-probability at least $1-\delta$ the following estimate holds. For any $T>0$ and test function $\varphi:\{-1,+1\}^V\to\mathbb{R}$, there holds
\begin{equation}
    \operatorname{Var}_{\nu_0}(\varphi)\leq (e^{-c_0}|V|/\delta)^{1/q}\mathbb{E}[\operatorname{Var}_{\nu_T}(
    \varphi)\mid h]^{\frac{1}{p}}\operatorname{osc}(\varphi)^{\frac{2}{q}},
\end{equation}
    where $p=e^{2T/c_0}$ and $q$ satisfies $1/p+1/q=1$. The expectation is taken with respect to the $\operatorname{SL}$ process $(\nu_t)_{t\geq 0}$ and we denote by $\operatorname{osc}(
    \varphi):=\sup_{x\in\{-1,+1\}^V}\varphi(x)-\inf_{x\in\{-1,+1\}^V}\varphi(x)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:47:01.663587+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_90f247e63c0783492b4849e34b746fa2919b48220207163ec27f71afacafc8aa","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 14 (\cite{LN}) of arXiv:2604.23656, 'Doubly Reflected Backward SDEs Driven by $G$-Brownian Motion with Quadratic Generator'] Suppose that $\xi$, $f$, $g$, $L$ and $U$ satisfy (A1)-(A4). Then the doubly reflected $G$-BSDE with data $(\xi,f,g,L,U)$ has a unique solution $(Y,Z,A)$. In fact, for any $2\leq \alpha<\beta$, we have $Y\in S^\alpha_G(0,T)$, $Z\in H_G^\alpha(0,T)$ and $A\in S_G^{\alpha}(0,T)$. Moreover,  we have
	\begin{align*}
		\lim_{n\rightarrow \infty}\hat{\mathbb{E}}\left[\sup_{t\in[0,T]}|Y_t-\bar{Y}^n_t|^\alpha\right]=0, 
	\end{align*}
	where for each $n\in\mathbb{N}$, $(\bar{Y}^n,\bar{Z}^n,\bar{A}^n)$ is the solution to the following reflected $G$-BSDE:
	\begin{equation*}
		\begin{cases}

			\bar{Y}^n_t=\xi+\int_t^T f(s,\bar{Y}^n_s,\bar{Z}^n_s)ds+\int_t^T g(s,\bar{Y}^n_s,\bar{Z}^n_s)d\langle B\rangle_s\\
			\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ -n\int_t^T(\bar{Y}^n_s-U_s)^+ds-\int_t^T \bar{Z}^n_sdB_s+(\bar{A}^n_T-\bar{A}^n_t), \\
			\bar{Y}^n_t\geq L_t, \forall t\in[0,T], \{-\int_0^t (\bar{Y}^n_s-L_s)d\bar{A}^n_s\}_{t\in[0,T]} \textrm{ is a non-increasing $G$-martingale}.
		\end{cases}
	\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:35:10.794164+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_90f2cc6be374ca3c7104b33a05ab4daf5c019df99fd336bb92240a4495c5ced2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 33 (Bounds on the matrix elements) of arXiv:2604.00635, 'Large deviations of the periodic Toda chain'] The following bounds hold,

