{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.586813+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_90f338d7b68ea7f423256efcf1f76b19731e4858311f97aedaae274d935c2c89","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 50 of arXiv:2603.00353, 'Aldous-type Spectral Gaps in Unitary Groups'] We have the following two formulas for $P$ in terms of $Q$:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item  $P = Q - t\frac{\partial Q}{\partial t}$.
        \item  For $t\in\R_{<1}$, $P = \left(1+\frac{nt}{1-t}\right)Q - \frac{t}{1-t}x\frac{\partial Q}{\partial x}$.
