{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.250886+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_90f5d895c81dd80b9be2e7386284ef3fa5803186bb58a3eb96e2e001a4904c9b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 8 of arXiv:2604.15226, '\bfseries Nonlinear Schrödinger equations with spatial white noise potential on full space'] Let $0<\mu\le1$. There exists a unique solution in $\CC(\IR,L_\mu^2(\IR^d)\cap H^1(\IR^d))$ to the linear equation \eqref{LinearEquation} for $v_0\in L_\mu^2(\IR^d)\cap H^1(\IR^d)$. Denoting as $S_t$ the associated flow, it satisfies
