{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:59:45.017649+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_90fc28a9b7ede62ce507e3b0b4844dc475232e4e75873461037fe265e421cd39","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:deconv-intro of arXiv:2605.15545, 'Crossover from subcritical to critical decay: \\ random walk, self-avoiding walk, percolat'] Let $d \ge 1$ and
let $M,K_{\mathrm{IR}},\zeta>0$ be given.
Suppose $(Q,g)\in \mathcal{Q}_{M,K_{\mathrm{IR}},\zeta}$.
Let $\eta$ and $\Lambda$ be given by (equation eq:def_Lambda-intro of the paper),
and let $x\in{\mathbb Z^d}$ be a nonzero vector in the same direction as $\eta$,
i.e., $\eta = \abs \eta \hat x$ ($\eta=0$ is permitted here).
If $d \le 2$, we further assume $\abs x \abs \eta \ge s_0$ for some $s_0 > 0$.
Then, as $\abs x \to \infty$,
\begin{equation} 
 G_{Q,g}  (x) :=
