{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:45:10.061505+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9113f4392e9e91f9f4bef2d1129fc68a6e478ac9c79229bd39c29ab83b5cdefd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:chaos of arXiv:2504.14457, 'Abstract'] There exists a unique mild Skorohod solution to (equation eqn:DO process of the paper) if and only if the  function $w(t,x)$ given by (equation e:h of the paper) is well-defined and the series   $\sum_{n=1}^\infty I_n(f_n(\cdot, t, x))$ converges in $L^2(\Omega)$ for all $t>0$, i.e.,  
