{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:55.640008+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_913e02cc206df0e36423a45727471f2cf0129eeab355d24aebdae666f566d2fe","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 8 (Mean-field convergence) of arXiv:2605.23529, 'Generalized Bessel-Dunkl diffusions'] Assume \ref{ass:mf:exist}-\ref{ass:mf:initial}. Then, for every $T>0$, the laws of $(\mu_t^{(N)})_{0\le t\le T}$ are tight in $C([0,T],\mathcal P(E_{\mathfrak r}))$. Moreover, every weak limit point $(\mu_t)_{0\le t\le T}$ satisfies, for every $f\in D$ and every $t\in[0,T]$,
