    The quotient $k(s,x)f'(x)/x$ is understood at $x=0$ as $k(s,0)f''(0)$.  In particular, every subsequential limit solves \eqref{eq:mf:limit-equation}. If \eqref{eq:mf:limit-equation} has a unique solution in $C([0,T],\mathcal P(E))$, then
