{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:09.855392+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_914b4c064a9fab5d710953ee2e5175c7991ff2aa1cef5792a3d65712089f0667","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 7 of arXiv:2605.20041, '\makeatletter \HRule \\[0.4cm] { \huge \bfseries Fourier Representations of Spectral Densi'] For all $n \in \mathbb{N}$, the Dirichlet kernel $D_{n}$ and the Fejér kernel $F_{n}$ are the trigonometric polynomials of degree $n$ defined for all $\theta \in \mathbb{R}$ by
\begin{flalign*}
D_{n}(\theta) &= \frac{1}{2}\sum_{l=-n}^{n}\e^{\mathrm{i}l\theta}=\frac{1}{2}+\sum_{l=1}^{n}\cos(l\theta)=\frac{\sin\hspace{-1.6pt}\left(\left(n+\frac{1}{2}\right)\theta\right)}{2\sin\hspace{-1.6pt}\left(\frac{\theta}{2}\right)}, \\
F_{n}(\theta) &= \frac{1}{n+1}\sum_{l=0}^{n}D_{l}(\theta)=\frac{2}{n+1}{\left(\frac{\sin\hspace{-1.6pt}\left(\frac{1}{2}(n+1)\theta\right)}{2\sin\hspace{-1.6pt}\left(\frac{\theta}{2}\right)}\right)}^{2}=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{l=-n}^{n}\left(1-\frac{|l|}{n+1}\right)\e^{\mathrm{i}l\theta}.
\end{flalign*}","status":"unverified"}

