{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.178146+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9157c0b05e8978adf5811b0e08e59ee7517c78ba320f5c89aa1169a1db50fefb","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition ex:mcmf of arXiv:2511.05223, 'Kac's Program and Relative Entropy Decay for Nonlinear Spin-Exchange Dynamics'] Fix an arbitrary partition $\ensuremath{\mathcal A}$ of $[n]$, and define the matrix $\ensuremath{\mathcal K}=\ensuremath{\mathcal K}_\ensuremath{\mathcal A}$ by 
