The proof is given in \cref{app:proof-control-kl}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:58.439286+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9159de487236f7c72b1bb92691d9b61916b2299d622df9e0583454b3c962cde0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition DEf.bernoullipercextend of arXiv:2604.24743, 'The impact of disorder and non-convex interactions on delocalisation of height functions'] Given a subset $\Lambda \subseteq \ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}^d}_n$, denote by $\mathbb{P}_{\Lambda,p}$ the independent probability measure on  $\left\{ 0 ,1  \right\}^\Lambda$ characterized by the identities
