{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:09:34.487815+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_915f1e57e6bc6f28791f74ccc68845fb922bfc64a7580707f250169467b63743","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn of arXiv:2505.14762, 'Multiple radial SLE($\kappa$) and quantum Calogero-Sutherland system'] Suppose $\Omega$ is a simply connected domain $(\Omega \subsetneq \mathbb{C})$, let $\partial \Omega$ be its Carathéodory boundary (prime ends) and consider the Schottky double $S=\Omega^{\text {double }}$, which equips with the canonical involution $\iota \equiv \iota_\Omega: S \rightarrow S, z \mapsto z^*$. 

Then, for a double divisor $\left(\boldsymbol{\sigma}^{+}, \boldsymbol{\sigma}^{-}\right)$, we define the associated divisor on the Schottky double $S$ by
\begin{equation}
\boldsymbol{\sigma} = \boldsymbol{\sigma}^{+} + \boldsymbol{\sigma}_*^{-}, \quad \text{where} \quad \boldsymbol{\sigma}_*^{-} := \sum \sigma_j^{-} \cdot z_j^*,
\end{equation}
and each $z_j^*$ denotes the image of $z_j$ under the canonical involution $\iota$ of $S$. Accordingly, $\boldsymbol{\sigma}_*^{-}$ is the pushforward of $\boldsymbol{\sigma}^{-}$ under $\iota$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.579676+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_916084d05da15c6a29d3cebdc08a78b930c6d6d169ca8101f92e939fc7857929","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: Diagonalization of arXiv:2608.30443, 'On smooth holosphere solutions to compressible Euler equation'] Assume (equation eq: Parameters of the paper). Let 
\begin{equation}

\left|\begin{array}{l}
w=w_3+W\\
