{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:02:17.907929+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_918c1a837dd58fc5a1ce53f12ee15c55791e093dd224eba91f5abd845aa392e9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm of arXiv:2602.08591, 'The Yang--Mills measure on compact surfaces as a \\ universal scaling limit of lattice gau'] Assume $\Sigma$ is a smooth closed compact surface, $f$ a Morse function on $\Sigma$ with adapted metric $g$ such that $V=\nabla f$ satisfies the Smale transversality condition and $1$ is the only Lyapunov exponent of $V=\nabla f$. 
For any $L>0$, there exists an order function $m\in C^\infty(T^*\Sigma)$ in the previous sense such that for all $k\in \{0,1,2\}$,
the resolvent $$\left(\mathcal{L}_V+z\right)^{-1}:\mathcal{H}^{m,k}\left( \Sigma\right)\mapsto \mathcal{H}^{m,k}\left(\Sigma \right)$$
has a meromorphic extension to the half--space $\Re(z)>-L$. Moreover for $\Re(z)>0$, the resolvent $\left(\mathcal{L}_V+z\right)^{-1}$ acting on $C^\infty(\Lambda^kT^*\Sigma)$ is given by the formula
\begin{equation}
  \left(\mathcal{L}_V+z\right)^{-1}\psi:=\int_0^\infty e^{-tz} \left(\varphi_f^{-t*} \psi\right) dt 
\end{equation}
for all $\psi\in C^\infty(\Lambda^kT^*\Sigma)$.

For every pair $\psi_1\in \mathcal{H}^{-m,k}, \psi_2\in \mathcal{H}^{m,2-k}$, we have the following asymptotic expansion~:
\begin{equation}
\int_\Sigma \psi_1\wedge \varphi_f^{-t*}\psi_2=\sum_{a\in \text{Crit}(f)} \left(\int_{\Sigma} \psi_1 \wedge U_a \right)   \left(\int_{\Sigma} S_a \wedge \psi_2 \right)+O\left( e^{-t} \Vert \psi_1 \Vert_{\mathcal{H}^{-m,k}} \Vert \psi_2 \Vert_{\mathcal{H}^{m,2-k}} \right)     
\end{equation}
where $(U_a)_{a\in \text{Crit}(f)}$ (resp $(S_a)_{a\in \text{Crit}(f)}$) are anisotropic Sobolev currents supported on the unstable manifolds $\overline{W^u(a)},a\in \text{Crit}(f)$ (resp stable manifolds $\overline{W^s(a)},a\in \text{Crit}(f)$). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

