\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.084169+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9199bd3f0357bb0ba1c1cf320d6b9406d65d4932560df5d5d95b465809dae636","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:meanconv of arXiv:2606.11677, 'Feynman--Kac formula for the heat equation with a one-center point interaction in $d=3$.'] For each $t>0$, $x\in {\mathbb{R}}^3$, $\delta>0$, we have \begin{align*}
