{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:36:31.230283+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_91cacadb52a71655da51f4f7f9ac39b9636f8b952e0bd1911c08f74cdf8b5ab5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 15 of arXiv:2609.00537, 'Explicit Exponential Sum Estimates and Approximate Functional Equations for the Zeta Funct'] Let $s = \sigma + it$ with $\s \in (0,1]$ and $t \geq t_0>0$. If $c>\frac{1}{2\pi}$ and $(ct)\in\Z+\frac{1}{2}$, then
