{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:15.346427+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_92077d6ed08d122136fa9108262f59a5d058396ec24a1b5396e92146683ed522","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 48 of arXiv:2506.15044, '2506.15044'] Let $Y\in \mathcal{S}^{i,\mathbb{B}}$, and $a,b\in\mathbf{R}$. Suppose that $H\in \mathcal{L}^\mathbb{B}(X)\cap\mathcal{L}^\mathbb{B}(Y)$ and $K\in \mathcal{L}^\mathbb{B}(X)$.
