{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:04:30.599118+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_92331d93e65f006fa8e7462a946872c05c9317d8daf34701a1ef609a97e13ebd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition of arXiv:2411.10502, 'Strategies in a mis\`{e}re two-player tree search game'] We have that $b_{k-1} \leq \frac{4}{k+1}b_{k-3},$ and that a limit exists for the sequence $(a_k).$ It follows that

