{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:53:54.888432+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_923bad3f0bfd5d4d448267451ab6eb0f8207c3a27efc4b424e0937427f3c2d95","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2607.17087, 'Transportation-cost inequalities for invariant measures of stochastic reaction-diffusion e'] Let $p_{t}(x,y)$ be the heat kernel of the operator $\frac{1}{2}\partial_{xx}$ on $[0,1]$ with the Dirichlet boundary condition, and
\begin{align*}
 P_t f(x) := \int_{0}^{1} p_{t}(x,y) f(y)dy, \quad x\in [0,1].
\end{align*}
Then for any $p> 1$,
\begin{align}
  \sup_{x\in [0,1]} |P_t f(x)| \leq C_{p\rightarrow\infty} t^{-\frac{1}{2p}}\Vert f\Vert_{L^p([0,1])},
\end{align}
where
\begin{align}
  C_{p\rightarrow\infty}:= (2\pi)^{-\frac1{2p}} \left(\frac{p-1}{p}\right)^{\frac{p-1}{2p}}.
\end{align}
The constant $C_{p\rightarrow\infty}$ can be bounded by
\begin{align}
  C_{p\rightarrow\infty} \leq \left(\frac{1}{2\sqrt{\pi}}\right)^{\frac{1}{p}}.
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:09:59.188392+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_923be0bc9fb8b28bb3e9f26e12321aff9a0977f219af8c4a9e79c3d1f6450c6e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:Irb of arXiv:2608.05262, 'The law of $(1+1)$D SOS with an area tilt in a wedge'] Fix $\varepsilon \in (0,\tfrac{1}{9})$, $\Delta=N^{2/3+\varepsilon}$, $a_0^+=N+\Delta$ 
and set
\begin{align*}

\mathfrak I_{\pm r} &:=\pm [a^+_{r}- \Delta,a^+_{r-1}-\Delta)\qquad(1 \le r \le K)\,,\\

\mathfrak I_{K+1} &:= \;\;\, (a^-_K+\Delta,a^+_K-\Delta) \,.
\end{align*}    
Consider the event 
\begin{equation}
A := \{ \underline{\widetilde \phi} (N)=\underline 0\} \cap A^- \cap A^+ \,,
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}

A^\pm := \big\{\widetilde \phi_{r} \ge \cdots \ge \widetilde \phi_{K} \ge 0
\quad \mbox{on} \quad \mathfrak I_{\pm r}, \quad \mbox{for} \quad 1 \le r \le K\big\} \,.
\end{equation}
Note that 
$\{\mathfrak I_r\}$ 
partitions $(-N,N)$ into $2K+1$ sub-intervals,
as depicted in (fig:tilde-phi-events-A-B of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:28.465207+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_923c0227c97ee32c1fa4cc1c6558b845b61fb8da150e490660a7888b599e81c5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2606.29131, '2606.29131'] Suppose that \eqref{t1-1-1} holds for some $\beta>0$. Let $\Upsilon_\e^1 f(x,y)$ be defined by \eqref{l2-1-3a}. Then there exists a positive constant $C_7:=C_7(\beta)$ such that for every $f\in \M_\beta$, $x\in \R^d$ and $y\in \T^d$,
