{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.769407+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_92559bc3edd78416577f3005cd30fc2a63a55976f77e8fd6d2c1447941ca1163","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi smooth of arXiv:2411.19543, 'Feller property and convergence for semigroups of time-changed processes'] {Revuz}}}}]
{\rm Let $\nu$ be a $\sigma$-finite Borel measure. We say that $\nu$ is \emph{smooth (in the strict sense)} if:
\begin{enumerate}
\item[\rm(1)] $\nu$ does not charge any semi-polar sets.
\item[\rm(2)] There exists an increasing sequence of Borel sets 
$\{E_n\}$ such that $X=\bigcup_{n=1}^{\infty}E_n$ and 
\begin{enumerate}
\item[\rm(a)] $\nu(E_n)<\infty$ for each $n\in\mathbb{N}$.
\item[\rm(b)] $\int_{E_n}G_1(x,y)d\nu(y)$ is bounded with respect to $x$.
\item[\rm(c)] Let $T_n:=\sigma_{X\setminus E_n}$ and $T:=\lim_{n\to\infty}T_n$. Then, it should hold 
\begin{align*}
\mathbb{P}_x(T\geq\zeta)=1\quad\text{ for any }\quad x\in X.
\end{align*}
\end{enumerate}
\end{enumerate}
}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:38:17.795113+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9256e37ab636e8ce7ab03f05ad8680e0d395b61ba43a551b78b84a6eadd88027","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:renormalization_constants of arXiv:2509.23496, 'Crossing probabilities in geometric inhomogeneous random graphs'] Let $0\leq\gamma<1$ and $1<\delta \leq\infty$ and assume $\gamma = 0$ and $\delta = \infty$ do not occur simultaneously. For every $a>0$ there exist constants $0<c(a)<C(a)$ (depending on $\gamma$ and $\delta$) such that
for all $0<u<1$  and $R>0$ we have
\begin{align}
     c(a) \pi_{(u),R} \leq & \pi_{(u),aR} \leq C(a) \pi_{(u),R}, \\
    c(a) \pi^{(2)}_{(u),R} \leq & \pi^{(2)}_{(u),aR} \leq C(a) \pi^{(2)}_{(u),R}.
\end{align}
 Moreover, for every $\varepsilon>0$ and $a,b>0$, there exist constants 
 $0<c(a,b,\varepsilon)<C(a,b,\varepsilon)$ (again, depending on $\gamma$ and $\delta$) such that, for $r,R>0$ with 
 $0<\frac{r}{R}\leq (1-\varepsilon)(\frac{b}{a}\wedge1)$, we have
 \begin{align}
     c(a,b,\varepsilon) \pi_{r,R} \leq & \pi_{ar, bR} \leq C(a,b,\varepsilon) \pi_{r,R}, \\
     c(a,b,\varepsilon) \pi^{(2)}_{r,R} \leq & \pi^{(2)}_{ar, bR} \leq C(a,b,\varepsilon) \pi^{(2)}_{r,R}.
 \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:32:11.128361+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9259eb3fb0fd54f7255e8afd85e8774fb3061cc6c41c7e166048acc616a33657","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition b2 of arXiv:2510.09818, 'On the Fourier dimension of fractional Brownian graphs'] Let $B$ be a fractional Brownian motion, with covariance function given by~(equation fBm:cov of the paper).
Recall that the graph measure $\mu_G$ of $B$ is given by (equation mu_G of the paper).
Then the image measure of $B$ is defined on Borel sets $F \subset \mathbb R$ by
\begin{align}
	\nu(F) = \mu_G([0,1] \times F) = \int_0^1 {\bf 1}_{\{B_t \in F\}} \, dt.
\end{align}
Its Fourier transform $\hat{\nu}$ is given for $\xi_2 \in \mathbb R$ by
\begin{align*}
	\hat{\nu}(\xi_2) = \int_0^1 e^{-2\pi i \xi_2 B_t} dt.
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:06:42.722667+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_926358afbaa1cef7b1446e3ddf5d844720fec5688113d8f6b0dbaa58ae7806cd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary coro1dimensional1 of arXiv:2411.04238, 'Holomorphic jump-diffusions'] Let $S\subseteq \mathbb R$ be a subset with an accumulation point in $\mathbb R$ and $X=(X_t)_{t\in [0,T]}$ be an $S$-valued jump-diffusion with characteristics $(b,a,K)$ and extended generator $\mathcal A$. Fix $\varepsilon>0$ and assume that $b_j,a_{ij}\in\mathcal O_\varepsilon(S)$ and 
\begin{align}
    \int_{\mathbb R}\xi^\beta K(\cdot,d\xi) \in \mathcal{O}_\varepsilon(S),\quad \text{for all }  \beta\geq2. 
\end{align}
Suppose furthermore that the following conditions hold true.
\begin{enumerate}
\item for all $x\in {S}$, $ \int_{|\xi|>1} \exp(|\xi|) K(x,d\xi)<\infty;$
    \item the real valued map
$\sum_{\beta\geq2}\frac{1}{\beta!}|h_{\mathbf{m}^\beta}(\cdot)|
$
is locally bounded on $P^1_{R(S)+\varepsilon}(0)$.
\end{enumerate}
Fix 
\begin{equation}
    G>\sup_{x\in {S}}\sup_{\xi\in \textup{supp}(K(x,\cdot))}|x|+|\xi|
\end{equation}
and set $\mathcal{V}$, $\mathcal{V}^*$ as in equation (equation eq:Vgeneralkernel of the paper).  Then $X$ is an $S$-valued $\mathcal{V}$-holomorphic process and
for all $\mathbf{u}\in\mathcal{V}^*$  
$$\mathcal{A}h_\mathbf{u}=h_{L(\mathbf{u})}|_S,$$
where $L:\mathcal{V}^*\rightarrow \mathcal{S}^*$  is the operator defined in equation (equation eq:Lgeneralkernel of the paper), whose explicit form for $d=1$ reads
\begin{align}
    L(\mathbf{u})_\alpha=(\mathbf{u}^{(1)}\ast \mathbf{b})_\alpha+\frac{1}{2}(\mathbf{u}^{(2)}\ast (\mathbf{a}+\mathbf{m}^2))_\alpha+\sum_{\beta=3}^\infty\frac{1}{\beta!}(\mathbf{u}^{(\beta)}\ast \mathbf{m}^\beta)_\alpha.
\end{align}
for all $\mathbf{u}\in\mathcal{V}^*$, $\alpha\in\mathbb{N}_0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:33:11.981584+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9264442c73bc2d3f0442b888746439197146484a194896110ed36241fd8ab3c4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition of arXiv:2608.19050, 'Online Permutation Embedding: \\ Optimal Stopping and Scaling Laws'] \begin{equation}\label{eq:beta+}
