{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:08.848853+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_926ad27731f9fc0cd8940e0030dad45ccee07946f5bc2f29eceabb7e790a857b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defination 7 of arXiv:2511.10814, '\Large \bf \boldmath\ \\ Convergence of the extended Kalman filter with small and state-de'] Let  $(A(t))_{t\ge 0}$  be  a family  of  measurable  locally  bounded processes with  values in the class of  $n \times n $  matrices, let $\zeta $  be  the matrix-valued  solution of \begin{equation}
