{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:06:18.050436+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9272eb390e77acdbd92b0d567533644fecd4f384612b4b196562f47602921194","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2608.15914, 'Absorption cutoff and stationary singularities for rounded Gaussian random dynamical syste'] Assume $0<A<A_c(N)$, and let $x_0\in\R^N$ be deterministic. Run the
  chain $X^{(N)}$ from $X_0^{(N)}=x_0$ and $Y^{(N)}$ from
