{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:21:56.724252+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_92b171beca2bac542dc7fb690f2e0723383b06e8c04b69ed22c4f67fa7c18e54","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:interior_intersection_left_first of arXiv:2507.15589, 'Tightness of approximations to metrics on non-simple conformal loop ensemble gaskets'] Fix $a_1 >0$, $p \in (0,1)$. Suppose that we have the setup of Section~(se:bubble_setup of the paper) with $(D,x_0,y_0) = (\delta\mathbf{D},-i\delta,i\delta)$. Let $z_1,w_1 \in \partial B(0,\delta/2)$. Let $\eta_{z_1}^{\theta_0}$ be the angle $\theta_0$ flow line starting from $z_1$, stopped upon exiting $B(0,3\delta/4)$. Let $\eta_{w_1}^L$ be the angle $+\pi/2$ flow line starting from $w_1$, stopped upon hitting $\eta_{z_1}^{\theta_0}$ or exiting $B(0,3\delta/4)$ (whichever occurs first). In case $\eta_{w_1}^L$ intersects $\eta_{z_1}^{\theta_0}$ in $B(0,\delta/4)$, let $\overline{w}$ denote the intersection point, and let $\overline{\eta}^R$ be the angle $-\pi/2$ flow line starting from $\overline{w}$, reflecting off $\eta_{z_1}^{\theta_0}$ in the opposite direction, and stopped upon exiting $B(0,\delta/4)$. Sample the internal metric in the regions bounded between $\overline{\eta}^R$ and $\eta_{z_1}^{\theta_0}$. 
Let $E^p$ be the event that the following hold.
\begin{itemize}
\item $\eta_{w_1}^L$ intersects the right side of $\eta_{z_1}^{\theta_0}$ with an angle difference of $\pi/2 - \theta_0$, and they do not intersect in any other way.
\item There exist $x',x,y,y' \in \eta_{z_1}^{\theta_0} \cap \overline{\eta}^R$ such that $(x,y) \in \intptsapproxbubble{U_{x',y'}}{\epsilon}$ as in~(equation eq:intpts_bubble of the paper) and $U_{x',y'} \subseteq B(0,\delta^{1+a_1})$ and $\metapproxacres{\epsilon}{U_{x',y'}}{x}{y}{\Gamma} \geq \median{\epsilon}+\epsilon^{-a_0}\mathbf{a}_{\epsilon}$.
\item The following event has conditional probability at least $p$ given $\eta_{z_1}^{\theta_0}$, $\eta_{w_1}^L$, $\overline{\eta}^R$, $X_\delta^{\theta_0}$, $X_\delta^{+\pi/2}$, and the values of $h$ on these sets:
\begin{itemize}
\item The flow line $\eta_0$ merges into $\eta_{z_1}^{\theta_0}$ before entering $B(0,\delta/4)$.
\item There exists a flow line with angle $+\pi/2$ starting from a point on $\eta_2$ that merges into $\eta_{w_1}^L$ before intersecting $\eta_0$.
\end{itemize}
\end{itemize}
Then $\mathbf{P}[E^p] = O(\delta^{{\alpha_{\mathrm{apr}}}})$ as $\delta \to 0$.","status":"unverified"}

