{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:48:43.563084+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_931177d5face5d7d88c0c750f037a4c3290aaead7e60dc4183a4999ef24b13be","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 11 of arXiv:2608.07239, 'Unified framework for asymptotically uniform iterative construction of generalised random '] Consider the iterative edge-colored graph process on $V$ and $\d^{(g)}$, $\d'^{(g)}$ and $X^{(g)}$ for $g=1,\ldots,\chi$. Let $x_{\max}^{(g)}$ be the maximum degree in $(V,X^{(g)})$, and let
		\begin{align}
			d_{\max}^{(g)}&:=\max\{d_1^{(g)},\ldots,d_n^{(g)},d_1'^{(g)},\ldots,d_{n'}'^{(g)}\},
			\\\Delta^{(g)}&:=d_{\max}^{(g)}\left(x_{\max}^{(g)}+\sum_{h=1}^{g}d_{\max}^{(h)}\right)+m^{(g)}\sum_{h=g+1}^{\chi}\frac{(d_{\max}^{(h)})^2}{m^{(h)}}.
		\end{align}
		Consider the asymptotics as $m_{\min}:=\min\{m^{(1)},\ldots,m^{(\chi)}\}\to\infty$, and assume that $\Delta^{(g)}=O((m^{(g)})^{\sfrac12}/(\log m^{(g)})^2)$ for $g=1,\ldots,\chi$. Then each iteration $g=1,\ldots,\chi$ has probability $O(\Delta^{(g)}/m^{(g)})$ of rejection. In particular, for $m_{\min}$ large enough, there exist edge-disjoint simple bipartite graphs for $g=1,\ldots,\chi$ with degree sequences $\d^{(g)}$ and $\d'^{(g)}$ on their parts and with no edges from $X^{(g)}$. Furthermore, any such graphs are sampled with probability $e^{O(\mathscr{E})}\mathscr{P}$, where $\mathscr{E}:=\sum_{g=1}^{\chi}\mathscr{E}(m^{(g)},\Delta^{(g)})$ and
		\begin{align}
			\mathscr{P}&:=\exp\Bigg(\sum_{g=1}^{\chi}\Bigg(\tfrac12\lambda_{\d^{(g)}}\lambda_{\d'^{(g)}}+\sum_{h=g+1}^{\chi}\lambda_{\d^{(g)},\d^{(h)}}\lambda_{\d'^{(g)},\d'^{(h)}}+\mu_{\d^{(g)},\d'^{(g)}}^{X^{(g)}}\Bigg)\Bigg)
			\\&\quad\cdot\prod_{g=1}^{\chi}\left(\frac1{m^{(g)}!}\prod_{i=1}^{n}d_i^{(g)}!\prod_{j=1}^{n'}d_j'^{(g)}!\right),
		\end{align}
		which is asymptotically uniform if $\mathscr{E}=o(1)$. The total number of such graphs is thus $e^{O(\mathscr{E})}\mathscr{P}^{-1}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:30:07.917553+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_931416bfdd1403863b542935b21d4fd3b50ac8a37e08901dbfc04979ecde4124","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem_irreg_nonoptimal of arXiv:2608.09105, 'Longest convex chains with i.i.d.\ points'] Assume (equation p_upper of the paper).
