{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:25:41.653757+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_933f1da333fb5e503fdaff82d31be20998a1398d56b2d680cbb055af6b52bae3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:existence-universally-stable-sequence of arXiv:2608.15923, 'Universality of two-dimensional Markovian holonomy fields'] Let $\Sigma$ be a compact smooth oriented Riemannian surface, possibly with smooth boundary, and let $o\in\operatorname{int}(\Sigma)$. There exists a sequence $(\mathcal T_n)_{n\geq1}$ of smooth triangulations of $\Sigma$, with one-skeleta ${\mathbb{G}}_n=\mathcal T_n^{(1)}$, such that:
