{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:49:06.307104+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_934c3ef2b9259e40e5d27de36e64fed99286efdbcdcfe7b23a59c6b7b6f5d181","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma timedecor of arXiv:2601.05361, 'Noise sensitivity in last-passage percolation'] For $i \in {\mathbb{N}}$, we denote by $\mathrm{pr}_i:\{0, 1\}^{{\mathbb{N}}}\to{\mathbb{R}}$ the map $x \mapsto x_i$. For all $t \geq 0$ and $f \in L^2$,
\begin{equation}
