{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:59:45.007166+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_939c667aba431bc80199f48430dc918e337688ecaa6e9ac5a8d80ef0bc87db02","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition Psi of arXiv:2605.12777, 'Mesoscopic Rates of Convergence for Complex Wishart Matrices at the Leftmost Spectrum Edge'] Let $\Psi(\zeta)$ be the perturbation introduced in (equation W-equa2' of the paper) where $\zeta$ is the L--G transform around $z_1$ as in (equation LG1 of the paper). Then the following large $\zeta$ (small $z$) expansions hold:
     \begin{equation}
