{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:40:22.389542+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_93a9f482e8293672aa834f3d3095f860cd631735c03f1765b5d9051756ff189e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lem-rw-consistent of arXiv:2506.18827, 'Random walk reflected off of infinity, with applications to uniform spanning forests and s'] The Markov chains $\{Y_j^n\}_{n\geq 0}$ defined above satisfy the following consistency condition. 
Let $1 \leq m\leq n $ and assume that $\{Y_j^m\}_{j \geq 0}$ and $\{Y_j^n\}_{j\geq 0}$ both start at the same vertex $z\in \mathcal V\mathcal G_m$. Let $J_0^{m,n}  = 0$ and inductively let
\begin{equation} 
J_k^{m,n}  := 
\begin{cases}
J_{k-1}^{m,n} + 1 \quad &\text{if $Y_{J_{k-1}^{m,n}}^n \in \mathcal V\mathcal G_m$} \\
\min\{j >  J_{k-1}^{m,n} : Y^n_j \in \mathcal V\mathcal G_m \} \quad &\text{if $Y_{J_{k-1}^{m,n}}^n \notin \mathcal V\mathcal G_m$} .
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
Then $\{Y^n_{J_k^{m,n}}\}_{k\geq 0} \overset{d}{=} \{Y^m_k\}_{k\geq 0}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.058378+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_93ab2f80ae1528b09f49069a39683eaa2ac4858750b70212dd1de93e0e9433a3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:pure-time-calibration of arXiv:2608.16119, 'Fully nonlinear parabolic equations under a fixed reference diffusion: weighted \texorpdfs'] Let $A\in W^{1,1}(0,T;\mathsf{S}^d)$ satisfy, for some
$0<\lambda\leq\Lambda<\infty$,
\begin{equation}
 \lambda I_d\preceq A(t)\preceq\Lambda I_d.

\end{equation}
For the zero-drift reference $b=0$, $a(t,x)=A(t)$, put
$\operatorname{Cov}_A(t):=\int_0^tA(s)\,\mathrm d s$, and denote its reference
process by $X^A$.  Then $\mu_t=N(x_0,\operatorname{Cov}_A(t))$, and
$\lambda tI_d\preceq\operatorname{Cov}_A(t)\preceq\Lambda tI_d$.  Put
\begin{equation*}
 e_A(t):=\lambda^{-1}\left\lVert \dot A(t)\right\rVert_{\mathrm{op}},
 \qquad
 h_A(t):=\frac1{\lambda t^2}
       \int_0^ts\left\lVert \dot A(s)\right\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,\mathrm d s,
 \qquad \chi_A:=e_A+h_A.
\end{equation*}
Then $e_A,h_A,\chi_A\in L^1(0,T)$.  For $K>0$, define
\begin{equation}
 \omega_{A,K}(t):=\exp\left(-K\int_t^T\chi_A(s)\,\mathrm d s\right).

\end{equation}
For every $K>0$, one has $\omega_{A,K}\in W^{1,1}(0,T)$; moreover, it is bounded
above and below by positive constants, and, for every $\alpha\geq0$,
$t^\alpha\omega_{A,K}$ is a
regular weight of order $\alpha$.  There is
$K_{\mathrm{hom}}=K_{\mathrm{hom}}(\Lambda/\lambda)>0$ such that every
$K\geq K_{\mathrm{hom}}$ gives the sharp calibration
\begin{equation}
 C_{t^\alpha\omega_{A,K}}(X^A)=C_\alpha^{\mathrm{Br}}
 \qquad\text{for every }\alpha\geq0.

\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:15:15.525980+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_93abb647b023e18a712f55edd9874b6570a939382c3d34e00cd60e949f36d3f7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 566 of arXiv:2507.01406, '{\Large On Iterated Lorenz Curves with Applications: The Multivariate Case }'] Under the \textit{Fr\'{e}chet-Hoeffding} \textit{upper-bound }iteration (\ref
