with the covariance function
\begin{align}
  {\rm Cov}\left(U_{0}(t,x), U_{0}(t',x')\right)&=\sum_{j=1}^{n}2c_1(\kappa_j)A_{j}K_{\frac{\kappa_j-1}{2}}(|w_j|)|w_j|^{\frac{\kappa_j-1}{2}}\nonumber\\
  &\times\int_{0}^{
  +\infty}\cos\lambda(x-x')E_{\beta}(-\mu t^{\beta}|\lambda|^{\alpha})E_{\beta}(-\mu (t')^{\beta}|\lambda|^{\alpha})d\lambda.
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:15:15.570574+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_93c673981b22b8c9315e0ace179b4fc1ef88b98056278bb27e009aae0e6fe25f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:edge-iso of arXiv:2507.12502, 'Quantitative Edge Eigenvector Universality for Random Regular Graphs: Berry-Esseen Bounds '] For $t \leq t_* = N^{-1/3+\varepsilon}$ and $z = E + i\eta$ with $|E-2| \leq N^{-2/3+\varepsilon}$ and $N^{-2/3} \leq \eta \leq 1$, we have for any deterministic $\mathbf{q} \perp \mathbf{e}$ with $\|\mathbf{q}\| = 1$:
\begin{equation}
\left|\langle \mathbf{q}, G_t(z)\mathbf{q}\rangle - m_{sc}(z)\right| \leq \frac{C(d,\varepsilon)}{N^{5/6-\varepsilon}}
\end{equation}
where $G_t(z) = (\tilde{H}_t - z)^{-1}$, $m_{sc}(z) = \frac{-z + \sqrt{z^2-4}}{2}$, and $C(d,\varepsilon) \leq Cd\varepsilon^{-5}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:22:21.906034+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_93c7d85dd3592eb81592480fa96c21b491c627bd42ccfa3cb9c8e01d879d51d1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Muirhead, Rivera, Severo of arXiv:2411.11429, 'Functional Central Limit Theorem for topological functionals of Gaussian critical points'] Assume Assumption (ass:gaussian-intro of the paper) holds. Then, Assumption (ass:perco of the paper) holds in the following cases:\begin{itemize}
\item $ d = 2$ and $ 0\notin  \text{\rm{\color{black} closure}}(I).$  
\item $ d \ge 3$ and $     \mathsf C(x)\ge 0$ and $ I\subseteq (-\infty ,-u_c^s)\cup (u_c^s,\infty )$. { We also assume that $q$ is invariant under permutations and sign changes of the coordinate axes. }
\item $ d \ge 3$ and $ I\subseteq (-\infty ,-u_c^s)$ for some $ u_c^s>u_c$ if $     \mathsf C(x)$ decays sufficiently fast.
\item $ d \ge 3$ and $ I\subseteq (u_c^s,\infty )$ for some classes of covariances of ``finite range''
\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:31:49.846229+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_93cbdc9dddcc37cc7cf9a0662f58ad5468011ff7018a87d3e0def5789f385d25","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem the: Kurtz's criteria of arXiv:2608.23756, 'Measure-valued fluid limits for partial service queues\\with correlated patience and servi'] Consider a sequence of processes $\setc{\boldsymbol{X}^N}{N \geq 1}$ in $D_\mathbbm{R}[0, \infty)$. If the following conditions are satisfied, then the sequence is tight.
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item[\normalfont{K1.}] For each rational $t \geq 0$, we have
		\begin{equation*}
			\lim_{K \to \infty} \limsup_{N \to \infty} P\left(\left|\boldsymbol{X}_t^N\right| > K\right) = 0.
		\end{equation*}

		\item[\normalfont{K2.}] For each $t > 0$, there exists $\beta > 0$ such that
		\begin{equation*}
			\lim_{\delta \to 0} \limsup_{N \to \infty} E\left|\boldsymbol{X}_{t + \delta}^N - \boldsymbol{X}_t^N\right|^\beta = 0.
		\end{equation*}
	\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:10.971849+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_93cf3b123b654b70ebe0079832ec3ed4276bddc088c928f63e455549113500a3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 43 (Kru{\v{z}}kov's interpolation lemma \cite{Kruzhkov1969ResultsCT}) of arXiv:2606.13459, 'Symmetric Cooperative Motion in Higher Dimensions'] Let $z \in L^{\infty}(\R^{d}\times[0,T])$. Assume that $z$ has a spatial modulus of continuity $\nu$ on $\R^{d}\times[0,T]$. Given $C>1$, if  $t_1, t_2 \in [0,T]$ are such that for all $\vp \in C^{\infty}_{c}(\R^{d})$,
	\begin{equation} 
		\left| \int_{\R^{d}} (z(x,t_2)-z(x,t_{1})) \vp(x) \, dx\right| \leq C\cdot\left(\sum_{i = 1}^{d} \norm{\partial_{x_{i}}^{2}\vp}_{L^{\infty}(\R^{d})}\right)\cdot |t_{2}-t_{1}|,
	\end{equation}
	then for all $\ve > 0$, 
	\begin{equation*}
		\norm{z(\cdot,t_{2}) - z(\cdot,t_{1})}_{L^{1}(\R^{d})} \leq 2C \cdot \left( \frac{|t_{2}-t_{1}|}{\ve^2} + \nu(\ve)\right).
	\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.240067+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_93d5c8206046cd3dad11880d3b3014589f04de5dda6d7addef790951a6c86732","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition ibp_proposition of arXiv:2604.22528, 'Malliavin calculus for signatures with applications to finance'] Let $G$ and $F$ be random variables such that $G \in \mathbb{D}^{1,2}(\mathbb{R})$, and let $h \in L^{2}(\Omega \times [0,T], \mathbb{R}^{d})$ be such that $\langle \mathbf{D} G, h\rangle_{L^2} \not= 0$ a.s. and $\dfrac{Fh}{\langle \mathbf{D} G, h\rangle_{L^2}} \in \mathrm{Dom}(\delta)$. Then, for any $f\in C^1_b(\mathbb{R}, \mathbb{R})$ we have
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{E}[f'(G)F] = \mathbb{E}\left[f(G)\delta\left(\dfrac{Fh}{\langle \mathbf{D} G, h \rangle_{L^2}}\right)\right].
    \end{equation}
    Moreover, if $\dfrac{F}{\langle \mathbf{D} G, h\rangle_{L^2}} \in \mathbb{D}^{1, 2}$ and $h \in \mathrm{Dom}(\delta)$, then
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{E}\left[f'(G)F\right] = 
        \mathbb{E}\left[
        f(G)\left(
        \dfrac{F\delta(h)}{\langle \mathbf{D} G, h \rangle_{L^2}}
        - \dfrac{\langle \mathbf{D} F, h\rangle_{L^2}}{\langle \mathbf{D} G, h\rangle_{L^2}}
        + \dfrac{F\left\langle \mathbf{D}\langle \mathbf{D} G, h\rangle_{L^2}, h\right\rangle_{L^2}}{\langle \mathbf{D} G, h\rangle_{L^2}^2}
        \right)\right].
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:49.210645+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_93d62edb35484d08ed0281429df5732aea85e65ec15ef922e28841a0082475b4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 25 of arXiv:2604.27242, 'Statistical Inference for Homogenization Limits Driven by Wiener or Hermite Processes'] For any \(3/4<H<5/6\) we have that, if \(u>v\)  
\begin{equation}
    \int_u^1 (s-u)^{H-3/2}(s-v)^{2H-2}ds < |u-v|^{3H-5/2}\beta(H-1/2, 5/2-3H)
\end{equation}
whereas if \(v>u\) we have that 
\begin{equation}
    \int_v^1 (s-u)^{H-3/2}(s-v)^{2H-2}ds < |u-v|^{3H-5/2}\beta(2H-1, 5/2-3H) 
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.898055+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_93dacf252d0bdc38291b482e02e06f186b93c56232b0c7a78fcff51b6546bb15","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theoremi 4 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Suppose that $N\rightarrow\infty$ with $\theta>0$ and $\kappa>0$ fixed in the discrete ensemble with Gaussian weight \eqref{eq_discrete_model_Gauss}. Let $f(x)$ be an analytic function and consider the random variable
\begin{equation}

 \sum_{i = 1}^{N} f(\ell_i) - N\int f(x)\dd\mu(x).
\end{equation}
If $\sqrt{2\theta\kappa} < \pi$, then \eqref{eq_linear_Gauss_intro} converges in distribution to a Gaussian limit with explicit mean and covariance given in Proposition~\ref{CLTGAUSSIANWEIGHT}. If $\sqrt{2\theta\kappa} > \pi$, then \eqref{eq_linear_Gauss_intro} converges as $N\rightarrow\infty$ towards a sum of two independent random variables: the first one is a deterministic affine function of a discrete Gaussian random variable; the second one is Gaussian with explicit covariance given in Proposition~\ref{CLTGAUSSIANWEIGHT2}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:45:01.977432+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_93ddcbd554c1a539f9331cf31579f836783ae7ce4ce0e43a737dde0ee8797e8e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem THM:2 of arXiv:2512.23957, 'Concentration and fluctuations of sine-Gordon measure around topological multi-soliton man'] Let $Q \in \mathbb{Z}$ with $Q\neq 0$, $L_\varepsilon=\varepsilon^{-\frac 12+\eta}$, and let $F$ be a bounded and continuous function. Then 
\begin{align*}
\lim_{\varepsilon \to 0} \int F( \sqrt{\varepsilon}^{-1}(\phi- \pi^\varepsilon(\phi) ) ) \rho_\varepsilon^Q (d\phi)=\int F(\phi) \mu_{\text{OU}} (d\phi), 
\end{align*}

\noindent
where $\mu_{\text{OU}}$ is the Ornstein–Uhlenbeck measure 
\begin{align*} 
\mu_{\text{OU}} (d\phi)=Z^{-1}\exp\Big\{ -\frac 12 \langle  \phi, (-\partial_x^2+1)\phi  \rangle_{L^2(\mathbb{R})}  \Big\} \prod_{x \in \mathbb{R}} d\phi(x).
\end{align*}

\noindent (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.587543+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_93df625765564945388e967134e304b1701fe3f20fe919b4b1422b30d24bbc6a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop subprop of arXiv:2608.30518, 'Grow-up rates of inhomogeneous semilinear heat equations in the critical dimension'] There exists $\widetilde{T}>0$ independent of $\varepsilon$
