{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:04:55.802019+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_946f640012afb4f39c86a0b44f8a6fb6eb9f0d1a3356c566a4cce384665153f4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemm l:DL-mixing of arXiv:2607.18194, 'Temperature chaos in directed polymers'] {HP24}}]
        Fix $\varepsilon>0$.
        There exists a coupling of three directed landscapes $(\mathcal{L}^\varepsilon,\mathcal{L}_1^\varepsilon,\mathcal{L}_2^\varepsilon)$ such that $\mathcal{L}_1^\varepsilon$ and $\mathcal{L}_2^\varepsilon$  are independent, and such that there exists a random variable $X^\varepsilon>0$ satisfying
        \begin{align*}
            \mathcal{L}^\varepsilon(s,x;t,y) &= \mathcal{L}_1^\varepsilon(s,x;t,y)\quad \text{for all } s_1 \leqslant s < t \leqslant t_1 \text{ with } t-s \leqslant \varepsilon^{30} \text{ and all } x,y < b_1-X^\varepsilon,\quad\text{and}\\
            \mathcal{L}^\varepsilon(s,x;t,y) &= \mathcal{L}_2^\varepsilon(s,x;t,y)\quad \text{for all } s_1 \leqslant s < t \leqslant t_1 \text{ with } t-s \leqslant \varepsilon^{30} \text{ and all } x,y > b_1 + X^\varepsilon.
        \end{align*}
        Moreover, $\mathbb{P}(X^\varepsilon > m \varepsilon^{19}) \leqslant Ce^{-cm^3}$ for all $m\geqslant 0$, where $C,c>0$ depend only on $s_1,t_1,b_1$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:06:42.723090+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9477f57011ac15f2ba45ed1a053a43702b76882f0e058d7a2ced7fd160f4eb0a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th: moment formula holomorphic of arXiv:2411.04238, 'Holomorphic jump-diffusions'] Set $X_0=x_0\in S$, fix $\mathbf{u}\in \mathcal V^*$, and suppose that the following conditions hold true.
\begin{enumerate}\phantomsection
    \item The sequence-valued linear ODE
    \begin{align}
        \mathbf{c}(t)=\mathbf{u}+\int_0^tL(\mathbf{c}(s))ds, \qquad t\in [0,T],
    \end{align}
    admits a $\mathcal V^*$-valued solution $(\mathbf{c}(t))_{t\in[0,T]}$  such that
   \begin{align}
       h_{\mathbf{c}(t)}(x)=h_\mathbf{u}(x)+\int_0^th_{L(\mathbf{c}(s))}(x)ds,
   \end{align}
  for all $x\in S$, $t\in[0,T]$.

    \item The process $(N^{h_{\mathbf{c}(s)}}_t)_{t\in[0,T]}$ given in equation (equation eq:localmart of the paper) defines a true martingale for each $s\in [0,T].$
