{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:04.867676+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94780759fa6b021efe5b1f5e1004c5f3af6e0d2b38e40160e432c1eb6a5dbbf0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 47 (Aizenman-Barsky differential inequalities on the magnetization) of arXiv:2512.00213, 'On strong sharp phase transition in the random connection model'] Let $\gamma \in (0,1)$ and $t>0$ and assume that $\| d_\varphi\|_{\infty,1}<\infty$. Then we have
