{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:25:06.115514+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_948284cb6a1ae3eb61aef969e13c290a88bd7e4a7e0584eeb0073d1a57d215ee","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 (Measure-dependent coarse-scale laws) of arXiv:2608.22334, 'Recovering Weighted Tangent Geometry from a Single-Scale Score Field'] For fixed $c,\ell>0$ and $r\downarrow0$, finite positive constants satisfy
