{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:19:46.236176+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94889910eca615ba87935b9381b2f8766461876870bf8fb068831c3c8dc74857","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Dfn 90 of arXiv:2507.08909, 'Annealed almost periodic entropy'] For any finite subset $F$ of $\G$, we write $\S^\rm{u}_k(F)$ for the set of all positive semidefinite elements $Q$ of $\rmM_F(\rmM_k)$ that (i) have all diagonal blocks $Q(g,g)$ equal to $I_k$, and (ii) satisfy the symmetry
\begin{equation}
	Q(g_1,h_1) = Q(g_2,h_2) \quad \hbox{whenever}\ g_1,g_2,h_1,h_2 \in F\ \hbox{and}\ g_1^{-1}h_1 = g_2^{-1}h_2.
