{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:37:08.952231+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_949750252b9103e317541d101135bd4d7a00147ee997f9969d8e82dff24779a8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:tool_gao_bernstein of arXiv:2609.01576, '\normalfont Pointwise Majorization for sub-Weibull and Mixed Tail Processes with Applicati'] Let $X$ be the stationary diffusion in
Section (sec:pointwise_ergodic_diffusion of the paper). Suppose that it is reversible
with respect to $\pi$ and that,  $\exists\ 0<C_P<\infty$ such that
\begin{align}
\operatorname{Var}_\pi(h)
\le
\frac{C_P}{2}
\int_{\RR}a(x)|h'(x)|^2\pi(x)dx

\end{align}
for every locally absolutely continuous $h\in L^2(\pi)$ for which the
right-hand side is finite. Let $g$ be bounded and Borel with $\pi(g)=0$.
Then, for every $t,u>0$,
\begin{align}
\PP_\pi\cbr{
\left|
\frac1{\sqrt t}\int_0^t g(X_s)ds
\right|
>
2\sqrt{C_P}\|g\|_{L^2(\pi)}\sqrt u
+
\frac{C_P\|g\|_\infty}{\sqrt t}u
}
\le2e^{-u}.

\end{align}
If the long-run variance of $g$ equals $\cV_\pi(g)^2$, i.e., 
$\cV_\pi(g)^2
=
\lim_{t\to\infty}
\frac1t
\operatorname{Var}_{\PP_\pi}
\left(
\int_0^t g(X_s)ds
\right)$, then we have that
\begin{align}
\cV_\pi(g)^2
\le
2C_P\|g\|_{L^2(\pi)}^2,

\end{align}
and
\begin{align}
\PP_\pi\cbr{
\left|
\frac1{\sqrt t}\int_0^t g(X_s)ds
\right|
>
\cV_\pi(g)\sqrt{2u}
+
\frac{C_P\|g\|_\infty}{\sqrt t}u
}
\le2e^{-u}.

