Thus strict value is present exactly when the coarse information has positive probability of retaining refined posterior mass on both sides of the terminal decision boundary.  More quantitatively, let $A\in\mathscr H$ with $\mathbb P(A)>0$.  If for some $\delta>0$ and $\alpha,\beta>0$,
