{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:58:10.025253+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94d1e9d8f27c4ebfa195c3557919ea3c03ff26cbca194ea2ff55ccd357df81f6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:old of arXiv:2607.19844, 'Binomial probabilities at a fixed distance from the mode:\\ size-biasing and the complete '] Let $K\subset(0,1)$ and $H\subset\mathbb R$ be compact.  As $N\to\infty$, uniformly for admissible
