{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:42:39.105261+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94df2a205d201a80a150f82215a8f4899dd5e2912bcb61391ca140ff2eb925d3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary of arXiv:2412.08886, 'On domination for (non-symmetric) Dirichlet forms'] {Assume that both $({\mathscr E},{\mathscr F})$ and the active reflected Dirichlet form $({\mathscr E}^\mathrm{ref},{\mathscr F}^\mathrm{ref}_a)$ are quasi-regular on $L^2(E,m)$.}
The quasi-regular (not necessarily symmetric) Dirichlet form $({\mathscr A},\mathcal{D}({\mathscr A}))$ is sandwiched between $({\mathscr E},{\mathscr F})$ and $({\mathscr E}^\mathrm{ref},{\mathscr F}^\mathrm{ref}_a)$ if and only if there exists an ${\mathscr E}^\mathrm{ref}$-quasi-open set $G$ with $E_M\subset G$,  ${\mathscr E}^\mathrm{ref}$-q.e.,  and a smooth measure $\mu$ with respect to ${\mathscr E}^{\mathrm{ref},G}$ with $\mu(G\setminus E_M)=0$ such that
\[
\begin{aligned}
	&\mathcal{D}({\mathscr A})={\mathscr F}^{\mathrm{ref},G}_a\cap L^2(G,\mu),  \\
	&{\mathscr A}(f,g)={\mathscr E}^\mathrm{ref}(f,g)+\int_G \tilde{f}\tilde{g}d\mu,\quad f,g\in \mathcal{D}({\mathscr A}),
\end{aligned}\]
where $({\mathscr E}^{\mathrm{ref},G}, {\mathscr F}^{\mathrm{ref},G}_a)$ is the part Dirichlet form of $({\mathscr E}^\mathrm{ref},{\mathscr F}^\mathrm{ref}_a)$ on $G$.  Particularly,  $({\mathscr A},\mathcal{D}({\mathscr A}))$ is symmetric.","status":"unverified"}

