{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.078047+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94f9551f7176ebfe0081499ab06d9ca5ecf7dc9e8b47cb67cf46771fc9f5e951","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma le:an-asym of arXiv:2411.12192, 'Sample path properties and small ball probabilities for stochastic fractional diffusion eq'] Define $a_1=1$ and $a_{n+1}=a_n+ca_n^{\lambda}$ for  $n\in\mathbb{N}$, where $c>0$ and $0<\lambda<1$ are constants. Then,
