{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:01:48.649590+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_95108b92ef0686518682659729ea2755e22d3f60b1d940eb0389e83936818622","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:size_cluster_origin_complment_infinitecomponent of arXiv:2607.04002, 'Collisions of random walks in unimodular random graphs: applications to the random geometr'] Let $p>p'$ for some $p'$ close enough to 1. There exists a dimension-dependent constant~$a>0$ such that,
