{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.287048+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9539b13df2e3a3caba2ac15b83b4be3ef333e772cd0ae7b6cb923e5973ec9643","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:trelK of arXiv:2607.10801, 'Relaxation times of non-reversible\\ Markov processes'] Suppose that $k\in L^2(\mu\otimes\mu)$ is a symmetric, non-negative definite kernel and $K$ is the corresponding integral operator given by~(equation eq:K of the paper). Then for all $\varepsilon >0$,
