{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:54:18.290243+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_955082e6a0ff8319aacdf48e23b9e0d13b35dc130ad290fa2818d8d718acff87","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:CGLT of arXiv:2608.30166, 'Square Functions and Rectifiability\\ under Monotone Transformations of the Density'] {CGLT}}]
Let $\mu$ be an $n$-AD-regular measure in $\mathbb{R}^d$. Then $\mu$ is uniformly
$n$-rectifiable if and only if there exists a constant $c$ such that, for any ball
$B(x_0,R)$ centered at $\operatorname{supp}(\mu)$,
\begin{equation}
