{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:37:08.951925+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_957f4581bda93a552db4e6467f7093e685cee9f34c3b57672bea1b40316f6995","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:diffusion_mixed_tail of arXiv:2609.01576, '\normalfont Pointwise Majorization for sub-Weibull and Mixed Tail Processes with Applicati'] Under Assumptions (ass:diffusion_coefficients of the paper) and
(ass:diffusion_index_class of the paper), $d_1$ and $d_2$ are finite-valued
pseudo-metrics and $(\cF,d_1+d_2)$ is separable. The map
$(\omega,f)\mapsto Z_\tau(f)(\omega)$ is jointly measurable, its sample
paths are almost surely $(d_1+d_2)$-continuous, and $Z_\tau(0)=0$ almost
surely. Moreover, for every $f,h\in\cF$ and $u\ge0$,
\begin{align}
\PP_\pi\cbr{
|Z_\tau(f)-Z_\tau(h)|
>
u\,d_1(f,h)+\sqrt u\,d_2(f,h)
}
\le2e^{-u}.

\end{align}
Consequently, $\cbr{Z_\tau(f)}_{f\in\cF}$ is an anchored two-metric
mixed-tail process of orders $(\alpha_1,\alpha_2)=(1,2)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

