{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:20:55.700688+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_958964e4f2a815f761492630a9d1ce2facb3a59f1415eb42dc691d1ce0c2a465","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop FV734 of arXiv:2411.07809, 'Pirogov--Sinai Theory Beyond Lattices'] Suppose $G$ satisfies Assumption~(as:3 of the paper).
   For any $\tau$ sufficiently large, there exists $\lambda_\star = \lambda_\star(C_{\text{iso}}, D, \Delta,\tau)$ and an increasing
  sequence $(c_{n})_{n\geq 0}$ with
  $2\leq c_{n}\uparrow c_\infty \leq 3$ so that for  $\lambda_\textsf{e} > \lambda_\star$, $\lambda_{\textsf{o}}\in\mathcal{U}$, and all $n \geq 1$, the following statements hold: 
  \begin{enumerate}
  \item For $\gamma\in\mathcal C_{\leq n}$,
