{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:52:08.679818+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_958bc23f07c3dc4b2abcc3964cc9827a4291bb4f5776e8f9f6f5f111cd63dc8e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 19 of arXiv:2608.30077, 'Lie groupoid integration of singular isometries of the Poincaré disk'] We consider a family of Lie groupoids
   \begin{equation}
       \mathcal{G}_{n}' = X_{n} / \sim'
   \end{equation} where the equivalence relation 
    $ \sim'$ is defined as follows:
\begin{equation}
(u(t),z)\sim'(v(t),w)
    \end{equation}
    if and only if
$w=z$ and there exists a smooth homotopy $u(t,s)$ fixing the endpoints such that: 
\begin{equation*}
   u(t,0) = u(t), \quad  u(t,1) = v(t), \quad u(t,s)\cdot z^n \neq 0, \forall\ t,s.
\end{equation*}
The source and target maps of $\mathcal{G}_{n}'$ are defined by the formula
    \begin{equation*}
        \sigma'(u(t), z) = z, \quad \tau'(u(t), z) = z(1).
    \end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

