{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:05:28.199695+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_95a8a153dcf61babaf1a8f995a55df5a99b64722b422310fa9c0242d3a549352","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm: continuous polynomial chaos of arXiv:2602.04429, 'Disordered systems and (subcritical) polynomial chaos\\ with heavy-tail disorder'] Let \(\boldsymbol\zeta\) be a \(\gamma\)-stable Lévy white noise with \(\gamma \in (1,2)\).
