{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:19:42.450625+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_95a960097bdedb057782af7b65303cd87c09bfcbb334c29876d88be3594840fa","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 3 of arXiv:2609.03418, 'Sampling and Density Theorems for the Fractional Opdam--Cherednik Transform'] Let $\mu,\nu\in\mathbb R$, and define \begin{align} \mathcal I(\mu,\nu) := \int_{-1}^{1} G_{\mu}^{\alpha,\beta}(x) G_{\nu}^{\alpha,\beta}(-x) A_{\alpha,\beta}(x)\,dx . \end{align} 
