{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:45:32.064890+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_95aade687bb2e3bbea9d050976ced21dc4ad131b3abe916fcbc6983e99be7ae6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l.d_eps_Phi^eps of arXiv:2411.14105, 'Simultaneous replica-symmetry breaking \\ for vector spin glasses'] Let $(L,\alpha)$ be any composition of some $q\in\mathcal Q_\infty$ defined on $[0,T]$. Let $L':[0,T]\to S^{D}_+$ be any smooth increasing path. For each $\varepsilon\in[0,1)$, let $\Phi^\varepsilon$ be associated with $(L+\varepsilon L',\alpha)$. Let $\Phi=\Phi^0$ and let $X$ be the process associated with $(L,\alpha)$ with $X_0 = x_0\in\mathbb{R}^{D}$. We have
