{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.303290+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_95f16b4a837f90ac9d96a5814ed0ffd2522551f5c389c7149328a108ba142301","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor Corid4 of arXiv:2411.14766, 'Axis-Driven Random Walks on $\Z^2$ \\ (transient cases)'] Assume $0<\alpha<\nicefrac{1}{2}$, for any fixed $x$, $z=(x,1)$ or $z=(1,x)$ and $i$ large 
