{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:47:12.035184+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_95f48157c16ab9e66c9af5e8aa72759fd3f2086a75dd5ea65a81d60c849cf48c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor-civuole of arXiv:2512.17727, 'Stochastic transport equation with L\'evy noise'] Under the same assumptions as in Theorem (thm-stability of the paper).
There exists a subsequence of the sequence $\phi^{n}$,   still denoted by $\phi^{n}$, and a  $\mathbb{P}$-full set $\Omega' \subset \Omega$    such that for all $\omega \in \Omega'$, $p\geq1$ and $M>0$,
\begin{equation}

\lim_{n\to\infty} \int_{B_M}\sup_{t \in [0,T] } \, \Bigl[ |\phi_{0,t}^{n}(x)-\phi_{0,t}(x)\vert^p +  \Vert D\phi_{0,t}^{n}(x)-D\phi_{0,t}(x) \Vert^p \Bigr]dx=0,
\end{equation}
and, for any $n\in\mathbb{N}$,
\begin{equation}

 \int_{B_M}\sup_{t \in [0,T] } \, \Bigl[\Vert D\phi_{0,t}^{n}(x) \Vert^p+\Vert  D\phi_{0,t}(x) \Vert^p \Bigr]dx<\infty.
\end{equation}

There exists a subsequence of the sequence $\phi^{n}$,   still denoted by $\phi^{n}$, and a  $\mathrm{Leb}\otimes \mathbb{P}$-full set $A \subset \mathbb R^d\times \Omega$    such that for all $(x,\omega) \in A$,
