{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:04:30.593329+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9608b8f9dc4d65665f8cc7d4260762b965c52bd310be245c4ebf37525ddb82d3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:chaos-lns of arXiv:2411.10419, 'Lower bounds on the top Lyapunov exponent for linear PDEs driven by the 2D stochastic Navi'] Fix any $ \mathbf{q} >1 $. Consider the map $ \Phi $ as in (equation e:def-phi of the paper) with $ L [u] = u \cdot \nabla
