then, for any $T>0$, there exists a constant $C_T'>0$ such that
\begin{align}
\mathbb{E}\Big(\sup_{0\le t\le T}  |X_t|^{\beta}\Big)   \le C_T'(1+\mathbb{E}|X_0|^{\beta}).
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:01:39.419228+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_960bc1e6a2dab116c28e39e1217ff9db06251fe242c0be186c342ce763ea0938","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma continuityoflevelsets of arXiv:2607.21862, '\bf Uniform Large Deviations of Mckean-Vlasov Stochastic Fractional $(\alpha,p)$-Laplacian'] Let conditions  {\bf A} and {\bf B1}
