{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:32:34.787322+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_960dfb562064bb9ced4e560237b230b6ed7c0ff21d75c1b80fb4436ea17627d2","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:KLDobrushin of arXiv:2411.08295, 'Improving the convergence of Markov chains via permutations and projections'] Let $\pi \in \mathcal{P}(\mathcal{X}), P \in \mathcal{S}(\pi)$. Then the KL-divergence Dobrushin coefficient of $P$, $c_{KL}(P)$, is defined to be
