{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:38.364086+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_960ecb4244a3a7e8e7b839a2b7dda4f1497b663789ad155be0eb9c71e99d843f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 30 of arXiv:2604.21669, 'Discontinuous transition in 2D Potts:\\ II. order-order interface convergence'] There exist \(n_0\geq 1, c>0\) such that for any \(n\geq n_0\), \(x,x'\in \R^2\), \(y\in x+\Z^2\), \(y'\in x'+\Z^2\) with \(\norm{v_L-x} \leq 2\scale_n^2\), \(\norm{v_L'-x'} \leq 2\scale_n^2\), \(\norm{v_R-y} \leq 2\scale_n^2\), and \(\norm{v_R'-y'} \leq 2\scale_n^2\),
