{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.678784+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_96292f0191d242d9fec989e84add82632f344fee5bdd1bf82f7457aaad4c7ede","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:light:tails of arXiv:2412.09235, 'A semiconcavity approach to stability of entropic plans and exponential convergence of Sin'] Let $\mathcal{X}=\mathbb{R}^d$ and $\mathcal{Y}\subseteq\mathbb{R}^d$ be an open (connected, possibly unbounded) domain of $\mathbb{R}^d$ endowed with the Euclidean metric and assume that $\rho$ has light tails in the following sense: there exist $C,\delta>0$, $R\geq0$, $L\geq 0$ such that
