{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:50:44.855819+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_965b04c098ae041ad625e1b6a1617f330c6bf3bc9b6e5faafc99ae4210193a2e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 6 of arXiv:2607.16145, 'The Memoryless Best-Choice Problem'] Let $f_0$ be a c{\'a}dl{\'a}g nondecreasing function. If the function $b\mapsto J(f_0+b)$ has a stationary point $b^*$ then it is the unique maximum
