{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.086109+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_966412a2d880c5778e930e2748ff540e18f65db2894fe7a42bc483543472e912","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lm:kanke of arXiv:2606.12143, 'Continuous stochastic flows driven by white noise and their duals'] Under the assumptions of Proposition~(thm:conv_appro_1 of the paper), for any $T \ge r$ and compact set $K \subset {\mathbb R}$, there exists $C = C_{T,K} > 0$ such that
