        \Vert (A\circ \mathbf{1}_{L(\mathcal{K})})_{\mathbf{i}_{I^c}}\Vert_{\mathcal{J}}\le 2^{|\mathcal{K}|(|\mathcal{K}|-1)/2}\Vert A_{\mathbf{i}_{I^c}}\Vert_{\mathcal{J}}.
    \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:42.314210+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_96c7178e6eb85008356613850736f972bfbe723964dc70d22be642d4e002ee7a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 45 of arXiv:2608.05931, 'Effective Lagrangian regularity and the uniqueness threshold for random H\"older velocity '] Let $\alpha \in (\frac{1}{2},1)$ and suppose for some $K >0$ and all $j \in \N, n \in \{0,1,2\}$, we have the almost sure bound
\[\|\nabla^n u^j\|_{\mathcal{C}^0_{x}} \leq K 2^{(n-\alpha)j}.\]
    Then for any $y \in \T^d$, $\delta>0$,
    \[G_{y,\delta} := \begin{cases} \Big\{x \in \T^d : |x-y| < 1/8,\, U(y) \cdot (x-y) > 0, \text{ and } \frac{U(y)}{|U(y)|} \cdot U(x) >  2\delta\Big\} & U(y) \ne 0,\\ \emptyset & U(y) =0,\end{cases}\]
    where in the above we mean $x-y \in \R^d$ to be the smallest-norm representative of the equivalence class. Then for all $y \in \T^d$, $\delta>0$, there exists a random constant $M_{y,\delta}>0$ such that almost surely $M_{y,\delta}<\infty$ and for any curves $X^1_t, X^2_t$ solving
    \begin{equation}

        \dot X_t = U(X_t),
    \end{equation}
and any $T \in (0,1]$, if for all $t \in [0,T], X^i_t \in G_{y,\delta}$, we have that
    \[\sup_{t \in [0,T]} |X^1_t - X^2_t| \leq M_{y,\delta}|X^1_0 - X^2_0|.\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:50:48.849763+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_96cc34e98dce1352e588fc5a9beb4f8496736ed4c86627e665d55cec8ef20d75","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lemma:approx of arXiv:2607.09841, 'Mixing and cutoff for the systematic scan dynamics of the mean-field ferromagnetic Potts m'] Let $\hat \gamma_n = 1 - b/n$. Then, $|\gamma_n - \hat \gamma_n| = O(n^{-2})$ and for every $t \in [0, \dots, n\sqrt n]$,
