{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:48:24.311907+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_97040e02bc921a231b1aede7cb54d094f567a1f234867983e1caa89d412d7124","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:Riemann Xi of arXiv:2605.31356, 'P\'olya--Schur problems and free probability'] Let $f_{n}(z)=\Xi(2\log(n)^{-1} z)$, where $\Xi(z)=\xi\left(\frac{1}{2}+iz\right)$, \begin{equation}
