{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:52:23.601393+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_97152ef73a6ba980cb4be28f4b2e913a73a9dd027a6ceea5ccc9202a4365396b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Thm6.1 of arXiv:2602.23124, '\textsc{ Necessary and Sufficient Conditions for the Lacunary/Hereditary Laws of Large Num'] {\bf Necessity and Sufficiency in the WLLN for Exchangeable Sequences:}  For    real-valued, exchangeable functions $\,g_1, g_2, \cdots,$ the following are equivalent: 

  \smallskip

  \noindent
  {\bf (i)} {\rm WLLN:} There exist real-valued, ${\cal T}_*-$measurable ``correctors"   $\,D_1, D_2, \cdots\,$  such that, for each $\varepsilon >0\,,$  
\begin{equation} 

p_N^\dagger ( \varepsilon) \,:=\,  {\mathbb P} \bigg( \, \bigg| \frac{1}{\,N\,} \sum_{n=1}^N g_n - D_N \bigg| > \varepsilon  \bigg)\, \longrightarrow \, 0\,, \quad \text{as}~~ N \to \infty\,.
\end{equation}
{\bf  (i)$^\prime$} {\rm \textsc{Conditional} WLLN:} There exist  real-valued, ${\cal T}_*-$measurable ``correctors" $\,D_1, D_2, \cdots$  such that, for each $\varepsilon >0\,,$ 
 \begin{equation} 

 \mathbold{\Pi}_N^\dagger (\varepsilon) \,:=\,  {\mathbb P} \bigg( \, \bigg| \frac{1}{\,N\,} \sum_{n=1}^N g_n - D_N \bigg| > \varepsilon\, \bigg| \, {\cal T}_*  \bigg)\, \longrightarrow \, 0 \quad \text{as}~~ N \to \infty\,, \qquad \text{in $\,{\mathbb P}-$probability\,}.
\end{equation}
{\bf (ii)} With the notation of (equation 6.3 of the paper), (equation 6.4 of the paper), for every $\varepsilon >0$ we have {\rm both} 
 \begin{equation} 

\lim_{t \to \infty} T_t (\varepsilon) =0~~~\text{{\rm and}}~~ ~\lim_{t \to \infty} \Sigma_t (\varepsilon) =0\,,\quad \text{in $\,{\mathbb P}-$probability\,}.
\end{equation}
\noindent
{\bf (ii)$^{\prime}$}   With the notation of (equation 6.3 of the paper),  (equation 6.5 of the paper), for every $\varepsilon >0$ we have   {\rm both} 
  \begin{equation} 

 \lim_{t \to \infty} T_t (\varepsilon) =0~~~\text{{\rm and}}~~ ~\lim_{t \to \infty} V_t (\varepsilon) =0\,,\quad \text{  in  $\,{\mathbb P}-$probability\,}.
 \end{equation}
 {\bf (ii)$^{\prime \prime}$}   With the notation of    
(equation 6.4a of the paper), for every $\varepsilon >0$ we have  
 \begin{equation} 

\lim_{t \to \infty} R_t (\varepsilon) =0\,,\quad \text{in $\,{\mathbb P}-$probability\,}.
\end{equation}
{\bf (iii)} With the notation of (equation 6.3 of the paper),   for every $\varepsilon >0$ we have 
 \begin{equation} 

\lim_{M \to \infty} \frac{1}{M} \int_0^M   T_t (\varepsilon) \, \mathrm{d} t \,=\,0\,,\quad \text{in $\,{\mathbb P}-$probability\,}.
\end{equation}
{\bf (iii)$^\prime$} With the notation of (equation 6.4 of the paper),   for every $\varepsilon >0$ we have 
 \begin{equation} 

\lim_{M \to \infty} M \int_M^\infty   \frac{\,\Sigma_t (\varepsilon)\,}{t^2} \, \mathrm{d} t\,=\,0\,,\quad \text{in $\,{\mathbb P}-$probability\,}.
\end{equation}
 {\bf (iii)$^{\prime \prime}$}  With the notation of (equation 6.5 of the paper),   for every $\varepsilon >0$ we have 
 \begin{equation} 

\lim_{M \to \infty} M \int_M^\infty   \frac{\,V_t (\varepsilon)\,}{t^2} \, \mathrm{d} t\,=\,0\,,\quad \text{in $\,{\mathbb P}-$probability\,}.
\end{equation}

When any (therefore, all) of the conditions  (equation 6.12 of the paper)--(equation 6.16a of the paper)  hold, then so do {\bf (i)},\,{\bf  (i)$^\prime$}   with   $\, D_N \equiv \Delta_N\,$ \\ as  in (equation 6.2 of the paper)$;$ and then   $\,p_N^\dagger( \varepsilon) \equiv p_N ( \varepsilon) $ holds in (equation 6.11' of the paper),\,(equation 6.5'' of the paper), as does $\, \mathbold{\Pi}_N^\dagger (\varepsilon) \equiv  \mathbold{\Pi}_N  (\varepsilon)\,$ in (equation 6.5' of the paper),\,(equation 6.11'' of the paper). The  correctors  of (equation 6.11' of the paper),\,(equation 6.11'' of the paper) satisfy  $\,  \lim_{N \to \infty} \big( D_N  /  \sqrt{N\,} \, \big) =0\,$ in ${\mathbb P}-$probability. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

