{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:59:45.009788+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_97735b62177e856081d979571cdfd1b69639b28563f0983aebd9e828a4ae3b8f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary smallessoft of arXiv:2605.12777, 'Mesoscopic Rates of Convergence for Complex Wishart Matrices at the Leftmost Spectrum Edge'] Let $L_{a,N}$ be an LUE with parameters satisfying $\lim\limits_{N\rightarrow\infty}\frac{N}{N+a}=\gamma\in(0,1)$. Suppose $\lambda_{min}^N$ is the least eigenvalue of the $L_{a,N}$ and $TW_2(s)$ is the distribution function of the least eigenvalue of an Airy point process. Let $\tilde{\lambda}^N_{min}:=\frac{\lambda_{min}^N+\mu_L}{\sigma_L}$ be the left-soft-edge-scaled least eigenvalue of $L_{a,N}$. Then for large $N$,
    \begin{equation*}
        |\mathbb{P}\{-\tilde{\lambda}_{min}^N\le s\}-TW_2(s)|\le \frac{g(s,\gamma)e^{-s}}{N^{\frac{2}{3}}}.
    \end{equation*}
    where $g$ is the same function as in Theorem (LUE left soft of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:31:02.820130+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9775a877e431f53a6f9811c2bff422786c81ae92c947d9c4b7cd1852249de909","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:stable-factor-barrier of arXiv:2609.01690, 'Iterated-sumset spectra: The complete exponent law and its rank geometry'] Fix $k\geq5$, put $t=k-4$, and let $\mathcal L^{\mathrm{st}}_{h,k}$ be the
following explicitly defined set of labels.  Choose
$(u,v,b,c)\in U\times V\times B\times C$, define $p,q,r,s$ by
(equation eq:fullsparams of the paper), require $(p,q)=1$, and choose integer degrees
$a_i h\leq\ell_i\leq b_i h$ with $\gcd(p,\ell_i)=1$ for
$1\leq i\leq t$, where the fixed windows satisfy
(equation eq:prime-window-constants of the paper).  Starting from
$A_0=A_{p,q,r,s}$, define
\begin{equation}
 A_i=\Sigma_{\ell_i,p}A_{i-1}
 =\ell_i\mathbin{\cdot}A_{i-1}\cup\{p\}
 \qquad(1\leq i\leq t),
\end{equation}
and let $\mathcal L^{\mathrm{st}}_{h,k}$ be the set of all resulting labels
$|hA_t|$.  Put
\[
 \delta=1-\frac{1+\log\log2}{\log2}=0.086071\ldots.
\]
Then
\begin{equation}
 |\mathcal L^{\mathrm{st}}_{h,k}|
 \ll_k
 \frac{h^{k-1}}
 {(\log h)^\delta(\log\log h)^{3/2}}
 =o_k(h^{k-1}).
\end{equation}
Thus no refinement of collision estimates alone can give positive ambient
density from this stable full-residue chart.  This is a limitation of the
chart, not an upper bound for the full spectrum $\mathcal R(h,k)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:23:05.295609+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_977676a65dbf36adb809cd4248b727c698400dd5401ecb2755c96ab2f8f68444","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2608.21701, 'Superdiffusivity of random walks on the three-dimensional randomly oriented Manhattan latt'] There exists a constant $C<\infty$ such that, for every $m\ge0$, $z>1$, $\lambda\in(0,1)$, $n\ge0$, $j\in[3]^n$, $p\in\mathbb T_j^3$, and $k\in[3]$,
