{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:10:44.010860+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_977b6bb2eade23e4788b8147ab6c68577f574c8d30fc2242afbd37387a536fea","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Cauchy_cycle of arXiv:2412.04579, 'Solvable Families of Random Block Tridiagonal Matrices'] Let $n\ge 2$, and suppose that $b_i$, $1\le i\le 8$, are fixed nonnegative integers with $b_i=b_{9-i}$ and $\sum_{i=1}^4 b_i=n$. Let ${\mathcal P}_{\underline{b}}$ be the set of partitions $\underline{\mathcal{B}}=(\mathcal{B}_1,\dots, \mathcal{B}_8)$ of $[\![2n ]\!]$ with $|\mathcal{B}_i|=b_i$, $1\le i\le 8$. Then
