is the normalizing constant. Let $N(Z_nn)$ be a Poisson process with intensity $Z_n n$ and independent of the sequence $\{X^{n}_i,i\in{\mathbb N}\}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:59:24.053456+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_978111f2569dc80f9cb7b5a5e655cf53fa0931305afd11a28312b259ba194604","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:general of arXiv:2608.30888, 'Three-term asymptotics for discrete\\ Hardy--Rellich constants in high dimension'] For every fixed $\ell\geq1$, as $N\to\infty$,
