{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:05:52.415574+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9787b00cb522a2f3e0300bd6d19bfb5a4f42e5ea9de7629098d2176a916892ae","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem littlewood1stofford of arXiv:2504.15992, 'Repeated singular values of a random symmetric matrix and decoupled singular value estimat'] Fix $B>0$, $\gamma,\alpha\in(0,1)$ and $v\in\mathbb{S}^{n-1}$ with $D_{\alpha,\gamma}(v)\geq c\epsilon^{-1}$. Let $X\sim\operatorname{Col}_n(\zeta)$ with $\zeta\in\Gamma_B$. Then 
