{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:23.371406+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_978a127caf07bb20398273adb17a2ac7b4a24754fc4b2200e6f53784d5c39f21","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2512.08595, 'Small time asymptotics of spectral heat content of isotropic processes'] For any $f\in L^1(\R^d)$ with $f\ge 0$ and $\epsilon>0$, we have
