{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:45.034121+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_978ac852142331a57b63d3c5d684f10137d396d141a9964d741ce26b34d6a8bf","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2606.07839, 'Bounds on Spectral Gaps for Non-Reversible Markov Chains with Applications to Temporal Dif'] Let $P$ be a Markov kernel and  let $\nu$ be a probability measure. If there are positive numbers $\gamma$ and $\delta$ and an integer $m\ge 1$ such that
