{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.328598+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_979e4e71457c358aa74b9f456823ff346ff6ca60406bb218934160322730a73e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:heat_asymp of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] For $0<\alpha<2$, there exists a constant $c>0$ such that for all $x\in \mathbb G$ and $t>0$,
