{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:50:36.756912+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_97b30bfd3ba8c0800d299c5f6f4c6f84f49a86e879db838fbcee5b935f8ecebc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 38 of arXiv:2609.04153, '\vspace*{-3cm}Smooth autonomous fast dynamo action on the three-torus'] Let $K \subset \CC$ be compact, and let $\lambda \in K$. Then, for any $m \in \NN$, there exists $C_m>0$, $M \in \NN$, both independent of $\eps,\lambda \in K$, so that 
\begin{equation}

\|\mathcal{K}^m_{\lambda,\eps} B_0\|_{H^1(\TT^2)} \leq C_m\eps^{-M}\|B_0\|_{H^{-1/2}(\TT^2)}.
\end{equation}
Finally, if there exists $\lambda_0 \in \CC$, and $B_0 \in H^{-1/2}, B_0 \neq 0$ so that $\mathcal{K}_{\lambda_0,\eps}B_0=B_0$, then $\lambda_0$ is an eigenvalue of the elliptic operator 
$$
B \mapsto \eps \Delta B+B \cdot \nabla u-u \cdot \nabla B
$$
on $L^2(\TT^3)$, with associated eigenfunction $\mathcal{C}_{\lambda_0,\eps}B_0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:16:49.558173+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_97b4cb8d17a08e52a4890455366e25c249e6b353554ca075bf0635b1af845674","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defs 20 (Conditional closability) of arXiv:2509.06869, 'Infinite Interacting Brownian Motions and EVI Gradient Flows'] Let~$\QP$ be a Borel probability measure on~$\dUpsilon$ satisfying~\ref{ass:CE}. 

We say that~$\QP$ satisfies the \emph{conditional closability}~\ref{ass:ConditionalClos} if 
\begin{align}\tag*{$(\mathsf{CC})_{\ref{ass:ConditionalClosability}}$}
\EE{\dUpsilon(B_{r})}{\QP^\eta_{r}}(u)=\frac{1}{2}\int_{\dUpsilon(B_{r})} \cdc^{\dUpsilon(B_{r})}(u) \diff\QP^\eta_{r}\cquad u \in  \mcC_r^\eta \notag

\end{align}
is closable in~$L^2\ttonde{\dUpsilon(B_r),\QP^\eta_{r}}$ for every $r \in \N$ and $\QP$-a.e.~$\eta\in\dUpsilon$. 
The closure is denoted by

$\ttonde{\EE{\dUpsilon(B_r)}{\QP^\eta_{r}},\dom{\EE{\dUpsilon(B_r)}{\QP^\eta_{r}}}}.$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:59:45.456035+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_97b5c29ab3c59d54292597e44c5a3ac2c7a67cbdc629ab44be80a9caf9bccf4f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma MajoDistance of arXiv:2411.16541, 'The Hausdorff measure of the boundary of the Brownian disk'] For almost all $\omega\in \Omega$, we can find a constant $c(\omega)$, which depends on $\omega$, such that for every $s,t\in [0, 1]$:
