{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:10.026069+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_97bb9b0c91aee83278977a74ccf7330e22a1048c826b63156c86ba62c6bde048","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 22 of arXiv:2608.17374, '\textbf{On the Pseudo-Mixing of Kac's Walk}'] Let $X=(X_{1},\dots,X_{n})$ and $Y=(Y_{1},\dots,Y_{n})$ be vectors in $\mathbb{R}^{n}$. Then
