\item Now let  $S_+' \in \mathcal{S}_0$ be associated to $a':Z \to [0,\infty)$. If $a'_i \geq a_i$ for all $i \in Z$, then $(S_-,S_+')$ is called a right strengthening of $(S_-,S_+)$.  
