{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:29:27.995026+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9863c393dbc22c3d4c588ac0d3a9a56fb9eff5b9d387b13fa5539aefb0057aae","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 16 (Poincar\'e inequality for the full labeled Gibbs measure) of arXiv:2608.24863, 'Uniform Logarithmic Sobolev Inequalities for the 2D Coulomb Gas at the Diffusive Temperatu'] For every fixed $\beta>0$, every $N\ge2$, and every real-valued $f\in\mathsf D_{N,\beta}$,
