{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.330013+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_988cd647b1ac09a6390c25a4c7f4b46e5d62d97a15021707dfeb15e736cc3d71","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma renormalization of arXiv:2606.01937, 'Stationary fluctuations for an exclusion process with mass and energy conservation'] Let $f:\Omega\longrightarrow\mathbb{R}$ be a local function whose support is included in $\{0,\hdots ,\ell_0 -1\}$ for some $\ell_0\ge 1$. There exists a constant $C_{14}=C_{14}(\kappa ,\rho ,\mathcal{E} ,f)>0$ such that for any $t\in [0,T]$, and $\ell\ge \ell_0$ and any measurable function $v:[0,T]\longrightarrow\ell^2(\mathbb{Z})$, we have 
