{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:17.750782+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_989c82742a500fb4126bfc4f9153e646b3042514dcffb1f5a41731253699e9b7","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 10 of arXiv:2511.02725, 'Mixing of general biased adjacent transposition chains'] A vector $\vec{\ell}\in \R^{2n}$ is \vocab{$n$-admissible} if 
    \begin{align*}
         j-\ell_j^-  \le k-\ell_k^- \qquad \text{ and } \qquad j + \ell_j^+  \le k + \ell_{k}^+ \qquad \forall j<k\,.
    \end{align*}
    We let $\mathcal L_n$ denote the set of $n$-admissible vectors.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:17:33.984726+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_989d77dc21ce25a51ea140ce75e83a87d3c98f332daa94c9a5042e151251c0d1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 23 (Inner mass formula) of arXiv:2609.03339, 'Exterior Serrin Rigidity for the Homogeneous \texorpdfstring{$k$}{k}-Hessian Equation\\'] One has
