{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.436075+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_98a2949f72e907c3d22360894d430878b0964ad26a4a9a04ac13f7c497eab0ad","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary A025 of arXiv:2609.04138, 'The conformally invariant metric on $\CLE_4$ I:\\ subsequential limits of the non-simple C'] Let $\kappa \in (8/3, 4)$ and $\beta \in [-1, 1]$. Let $\rho^\prime$, $\rho_\BR$, and $\rho_\rL$ be as in~(A021 of the paper) such that $\beta = \beta(\kappa^\prime, \rho^\prime)$. Consider the following algorithm:
	\begin{itemize}
		\item One samples a $\cwBCLE_{\kappa^\prime}(\rho^\prime)$ in $\BH$. Then, inside each connected component of each true (resp.\ false) loop of this $\cwBCLE_{\kappa^\prime}(\rho^\prime)$, one samples an independent $\ccwBCLE_\kappa(\rho_\BR)$ (resp.\ $\cwBCLE_\kappa(\rho_\rL)$).
		\item Inside each (both true and false) loop of the $\ccwBCLE_\kappa(\rho_\BR)$'s and $\cwBCLE_\kappa(\rho_\rL)$'s of the previous step, one samples an independent $\cwBCLE_{\kappa^\prime}(\rho^\prime)$. Then, inside each connected component of each true (resp.\ false) loop of these $\cwBCLE_{\kappa^\prime}(\rho^\prime)$'s, one samples an independent $\ccwBCLE_\kappa(\rho_\BR)$ (resp.\ $\cwBCLE_\kappa(\rho_\rL)$). Then, we iterate this step.
	\end{itemize}
	Then the collection of all the true loops of all the simple BCLEs has the law of a nested $\CLE_\kappa^\beta$ in $\BH$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:23:05.282320+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_98a3870422fec0fd46c39738c8416694d2f4520c75d6a22b0086424d8598fbe7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 1 (Difference set) of arXiv:2608.21496, '2608.21496'] The set of all differences of two reliability surfaces is the $L^\infty$ unit ball:
