{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:13:22.535312+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_98b2a53a8f53e390e305b651253b2c0754b030215e2ee4352bf332f3369439f3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem.I_by_It of arXiv:2506.07158, 'The diffusivity of supercritical Bernoulli percolation is infinitely differentiable'] For every ${\scaleobj{1}{\square}}_m \in \mathcal{G}^{(N)}_{k}$ with $0 \leqslant h \leqslant k-2$, the following estimate holds
