		\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:09:49.861973+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_98b339ca0d686e4e922897812861a9810b1d23008e08440490287945f0d59a8d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2609.03084, 'Convergence rates to traveling waves for an FKPP model with nonlinear advection'] Let
        \begin{equation}
            \bar u_1(t, x) = U_*\left(x-2t + \frac{3}{2} \log t\right) + \frac{\gamma}{t}. 
        \end{equation}
        Then $\bar u_1$ is a positive supersolution of \eqref{main_eq} for $t > \frac{\gamma}{\delta}$, $x \leq 2t - \frac{3}{2}\log t - Z_\delta(t)$, and $Z_\delta$ given by \eqref{Z_delta}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:46:12.280829+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_98b5ccc95d0f68deb789e2cc934a9354d39d0322197fc59ba5aedc8bbe414f15","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 37 of arXiv:2604.22461, 'Large deviation principles for stationary solutions and invariant measures of a class of S'] Let $\mathcal{P}_{W}(\sC_{-\infty} \times \W)$ denote the Borel probability space on $\sC_{-\infty} \times \W$ satisfying the marginal distribution on $\W$ is $\P \circ W^{-1}$. Let $S_{\Gamma} \subset \mathcal{P}_{W}(\sC_{-\infty} \times \W)$ denote the collection of $\cF_{t}$-adapted solution measures with the constraint $\Gamma$. If $S_{\Gamma} $ is a convex non-empty set, then the following are equivalent:
 \begin{itemize}
  \item [i)] Pathwise uniqueness holds for $\cF_{t}$-adapted martingale solutions. This means that if there are two $\cF_{t}$-adapted process $X^1_t$ and $X^2_t$ defined on the same probability space such that $\nu_{1}:=\P \circ (W, X^1)^{-1}$ and $\nu_{2}:=\P \circ (W, X^2)^{-1}$ both belong to $S_{\Gamma}$, then $X^1=X^2$, $\P$-a.s..
  \item [ii)] Joint uniqueness in law holds, and there exists a $\cF_{t}$-adapted strong solution. This means that $S_{\Gamma}$ contains at most one measure, denoted by $\nu$, and $\nu$ corresponds to an $\mathcal{F}_t$-adapted process $X_{t}=\mathcal{G}(W)(t)$ such that the pair $(\omega, \mathcal{G}(W(\omega))$ satisfies the constraint $\Gamma$, where $\mathcal{G}: \W \rightarrow \sC_{-\infty}$ is a Borel measurable map.
 \end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:10.976250+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_98b663e6ca06bb17fc5b1adbb5639f7017200fac38c2e19f79766bcb554bdf0e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi 27 (Abstract Ising model) of arXiv:2606.13648, 'Stochastic dominations for FK percolation and sharp thinning thresholds for the Ising ener'] Let $E$ be a finite set, $\F$ be an HT structure on $E$ and positive coupling constants $J=(J_e)_{e\in E}\in (\R^+)^E$. An abstract Ising model on $(E,\F)$ with coupling constants $J$ is the probability distribution on $\V_\F$ defined by
	\begin{equation}
		\is(\upsigma) \propto e^{-H(\upsigma)},
	\end{equation}
	where the Hamiltonian is defined as
	\begin{align*}
	H(\upsigma)=-\sum_{e\in E}J_e\upsigma(e).
	\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:30:36.778365+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_98bc020f076ef070941a280baef5908804689c60a05151e0814698c756bab896","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 13 of arXiv:2607.10486, 'Weak martingale solutions to stochastic Navier-Stokes-Cahn-Hilliard system with transport '] Assume that $\rK$ is a separable infinite dimensional Hilbert space. A $\rK$-cylindrical Wiener process $W=(W(t): t \in [0,T])$ is a family of formal series
   \begin{equation}
      W(t)\coloneqq  \sum_{k=1}^\infty w_k(t) e_k, \;\; t \in [0,T], 
    \end{equation} 
    where  $\left(e_k: \; k \in \mathbb{N} \right)$ is an ONB of $\rK$ and $\left(w_k: \; k \in \mathbb{N} \right)$ is a sequence of iid standard Brownian motions on some fixed probability space. \\
    The space $\rK$ is often called the Reproducing kernel Hilbert space, or Cameron-Martin space, of the 
    cylindrical Wiener process $W$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:32:28.995555+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_98c060f5aa92d412084b69a23e23c089da1759fb0f7e2e3ddffc40dd311b3757","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm T typ gau of arXiv:2608.25471, 'Exact Hausdorff measures and fine geometry of collisions of independent Markov processes'] There exist deterministic constants $c_1,c_2\in(0,\infty)$ such that,
