{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:48:35.811780+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_98e4ca35014446fe36fab7e0eca07a56cc063ba9fa4be0e226775f639d29c265","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main of arXiv:2411.09482, 'Anomalous Regularization in Kazantsev-Kraichnan Model'] Let $d$, $s$ and $\alpha$ satisfy (hp:main_hp of the paper) and let $Q$ be the covariance function given by (equation eq:Q_spectrum of the paper). Then, the following hold.
