{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.676807+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_98f2330e85bd332e7b3f37081262dce66bb9472a98ba40eee1f4b4eb1894a9d1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:gaussian-vector-product-expectation of arXiv:2602.14998, 'Random geometric graphs with smooth kernels: sharp detection threshold and a spectral conj'] Let $g_1, \dots, g_k$ be i.i.d.\ $N(0, I_d)$ random vectors.
For a multigraph $H$ on $[k]$, let $E(H)$ denote the edge set of $H$ where edges between the same pair of vertices are distinct elements. 
Then we have
\begin{equation}

\expect{\prod_{(i,j) \in E(H)} \iprod{g_i}{g_j}} = \sum_{\pi \in \Pi(H)} (d)_{|\pi|} \prod_{B \in \pi} \prod_{i \in V(B)} \mu_{\deg_B(i)} ,
\end{equation}
where $\Pi(H)$ denotes the set of partitions of $E(H)$, $(d)_m$ denotes the falling factorial, $V(B)$ denotes the vertex set of (the graph induced by) $B$, $\deg_B(i)$ denotes the degree of vertex $i$ in $B$, and $\mu_m$ denotes the $m$th moment of $N(0,1)$. Moreover,
$$
\expect{\prod_{(i,j) \in E(H)} \iprod{g_i}{g_j}} \le d^{|E(H)|/2} \prod_{i \in V(H)} (\deg_H(i) - 1)!! .
$$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:24:34.412123+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_98fa7f9c536a65a1f8190235653577058dcea83407cbd7b4867a991f489235d7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 28 of arXiv:2608.31070, 'Sub-Laplacians on Compact Lie Groups: Heat Kernels, Distance, and Zeta Determinants'] The quotient in \eqref{zeta:orbit-coefficient} extends real analytically across the root hyperplanes. For each fixed $t>0$, the orbit-grouped image series converges absolutely and uniformly on compact subsets of the complex Cartan and is absolutely integrable after the Cartan reduction. There are integers $A,N\ge0$, depending only on $G$, and $C>0$ such that
