{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:49.207313+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_990016646faa2838e8f73b37b30c7242ec9b7f26be335bed485c8fec4d37c98f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 11 (Chaos asymptotics, \(H^*(m)<1/2\)) of arXiv:2604.27242, 'Statistical Inference for Homogenization Limits Driven by Wiener or Hermite Processes'] Let \(\delta(\varepsilon)>0\) be such that \(\delta(\varepsilon)\xrightarrow{\varepsilon\rightarrow 0} 0\) and \(\varepsilon/\delta\rightarrow 0\) as \(\varepsilon\rightarrow 0\). For \(\varepsilon\) small enough, for any \(0\leq r\leq m-1\),
\begin{equation}

\mathbb{E}[T_{2m-2r}^2]\leq D^{\mathrm{Diag}}_{H,m,r}\delta+D^{\mathrm{Off}}_{H,m,r}f(\delta,\varepsilon,m,r),
\end{equation}
with \(D^{\mathrm{Diag}}_{H,m,r}, D^{\mathrm{Off}}_{H,m,r}>0\) read off Lemmas~\ref{lem: second chaos m=1 H<1/2}--\ref{lem: asymptotics m>1 H<1/2}, and
\begin{equation}

f(\delta, \varepsilon, m,r) =
\begin{cases}
\delta(\varepsilon/\delta)^{2m(2-2H)-2} \quad &r< r_I\wedge r_S\\
\varepsilon^{2(m-r)(2-2H)} \quad &r> r_I\vee r_S\\
\delta^{2(m-r)(2H-2)}(\varepsilon/\delta)^{2m(2-2H)-2} \quad &r_S< r < r_I\\
\delta(\varepsilon/\delta)^{2(m-r)(2-2H)} \quad &r_I< r< r_S
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
The borderline cases \(r(2H-2)=-1\) or \(2(m-r)(2H-2)=-1\) carry the same orders up to logarithmic corrections: when \(r=r_I\) and \(r(2H-2)=-1\),
\[
f(\delta,\varepsilon,m,r) \sim
\begin{cases}
\delta(\varepsilon/\delta)^{2(m-r)(2-2H)}\log(\delta/\varepsilon)^2, & H^*(m)>1/4,\\
\varepsilon^{2(m-r)(2-2H)}\log(\delta/\varepsilon)^2, & H^*(m)<1/4;
\end{cases}
\]
when \(r=r_S\) and \(2(m-r)(2H-2)=-1\),
\[
f(\delta,\varepsilon,m,r) \sim
\begin{cases}
\varepsilon^{2(m-r)(2-2H)}\log(\delta), & H^*(m)>1/4,\\
\log(\delta)(\varepsilon/\delta)^{2m(2-2H)-2}, & H^*(m)<1/4;
\end{cases}
\]
and when \(r=r_I=r_S\) (so that \(H^*(m)=1/4\)), \(f(\delta,\varepsilon,m,r)\sim \varepsilon\log(\delta)\log(\delta/\varepsilon)\). In particular,
\begin{equation}

\mathbb{E}[(C_{\varepsilon, \delta}-\mathbb{E}[C_{\varepsilon, \delta}])^2]\lesssim \delta+\varepsilon^{2(2-2H)}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:20.966550+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9900368cef99a9576a1c149556b38575ca7a0f17d7696a4f31076f87ce8c7ef6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 29 of arXiv:2607.28614, 'Tampered Memory Elephant Random Walk on one-dimensional integer lattice'] Let $\theta^*$ be an equilibrium point for the mean field function $h$, that is, $\theta^* \in \{\theta: \, h(\theta)=0\}$, where $h$ is as in \eqref{Eq: recursion_general_SA}. Let $\theta_n$, $\Delta M_n$, and $r_n$ be as in \eqref{Eq: recursion_general_SA}, and $\theta_n \longrightarrow \theta^*, \text{ a.s.}$ as $n \to \infty$. 
Further, assume that 
\begin{equation}

h(\theta)= \left(\theta -\theta^*\right) Dh(\theta^*)+ o(\lvert \lvert \theta -\theta^*\rvert \rvert^{1+\epsilon}) \text{ as } \theta \rightarrow \theta^*, \text{ for some } \epsilon>0,
\end{equation}
and the following version of the Lindeberg-Feller condition holds
\begin{equation}

\frac{1}{n} \sum_{m=1}^n \E\left[\lvert \lvert \Delta M_m\rvert \rvert ^2 \mathbf{1}_{\{\lvert \lvert \Delta M_m\rvert \rvert \ge \epsilon \sqrt{n}\}}\mid  \FF_{m-1}\right] \longrightarrow 0, \text{ a.s. or in } L_1, \text{ for all } \epsilon>0.
\end{equation}
Let $\Gamma$ be a positive semi-definite matrix, such that,
\begin{equation}

\frac{1}{n} \sum_{m=1}^n \E \left[\Delta M_m \left(\Delta M_m\right)^\top \mid \FF_{m-1}\right]\rightarrow \Gamma, \text { a.s. or in } L_1. 
\end{equation}
Let the maximum eigenvalue $\rho^*=\frac{1}{2}$, and the error $r_n$ satisfy the following 
\begin{equation}

\sum_{k=1}^n r_k = o\left(\sqrt{\frac{n}{log n}}\right), \text{ a.s.}
\end{equation}
Then 
\begin{equation}

\frac{\sqrt{n}}{\sqrt{\log n}} \left(\theta_n -\theta^*\right)\stackrel{d}{\longrightarrow} N\left(0, \widetilde{\Sigma}\right) \text{(stably)},
\end{equation}
where 
\begin{equation}

\widetilde{\Sigma}= \lim_{n \to \infty}\frac{1}{\log n}\int_{0}^{\log n} {\left(e^{-(D(-h(\theta^*)-\frac{1}{2}I_d) u}\right)^\top \Gamma e^{-(D(-h(\theta^*)-\frac{1}{2}I_d) u} \mathrm{d}u}
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:38.630047+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_99005f19d2dbbbd105a984af713300054106382ced99fbb00cacca15939f599d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 1 of arXiv:2506.17045, '\LARGE{On bivariate Archimax copulas: Level sets, mass distributions and related results}'] Let $A \in \mathcal{A}$, $h_A$ be defined as in eq. \eqref{eq:fct_h} and let $L$, $R$ be defined according to eq. \eqref{eq:definition_L_R}. Then the following assertions hold:
