{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:32:35.575280+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_996e0bbb0da62ce562ee937458b7331448bfe9e8f78444173eb4dd25777282a9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:Wishart.unknown.alpha.estimator of arXiv:2606.04859, 'Stein's method for the Wishart distribution'] Let $n\geq 2$ and $\widehat{M} = \frac{1}{n} \sum_{k=1}^n \mathfrak{W}^{(k)}$. The Stein's method-of-moments estimators based on the linear probes in (equation eq:Wishart.linear.probe of the paper) together with $q$ and $\ell$ in (equation eq:Wishart.quad.log.probe of the paper), respectively, are given by
\begin{equation}
\widehat{\alpha}_{\mathrm{quad}} = \frac{\{\mathrm{tr}(\widehat{M})\}^2 + \mathrm{tr}(\widehat{M}^2)}{\overline{\mathrm{tr}(\mathfrak{W}^{ \, 2})} - \mathrm{tr}(\widehat{M}^2)}, \qquad
\widehat{\Sigma}_{\mathrm{quad}} = \frac{\widehat{M}}{\widehat{\alpha}_{\mathrm{quad}}},
\end{equation}
