{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:53:54.887410+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_99d2aed01afe475578cf95aef71305caf5cad40fb06329e821fe4373fa156ba5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 30 of arXiv:2607.17030, 'Stationary measures for log-gamma polymer on a strip and in half-space'] Let  $\tau_1,\tau_2,\dots,$ be i.i.d. random variables,  $\tau_j\simeq\mathrm{Beta}_{II}(\alpha,\alpha)$. Define $P_k=\prod_{j=1}^k \tau_j$ and $R_n=1+P_1+\dots+P_n$.
