{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:29:21.949583+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9a053478cd37cc62e107888ebf4eae2ad1c69e5ebbe4d39de3a08c6f4a65df7e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 31 of arXiv:2608.01860, 'A Variational Characterization of a Gibbs Measure related to the Aviles-Giga Functional'] Let $\alpha\in\{1,..,d\}^k$ with $k\in\N$ such that $\frac{k-1}{2k}d<1$. Then we have
