{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:06:07.098923+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9a1a366715e3a6734801cd96877b978043c9bccf03f353690fa31e90d4551b5d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 17 of arXiv:2608.28198, 'Performative Privacy: When Differential Privacy Maximizes Utility'] Assume $\Sigma\succ0$, $C_1(\gamma)>1$ which by theorem \ref{theo:noise_threshold_mia} is true when $\gamma \ge \gamma_c$, and also assume by mean field approximation, $N_t\ge N_0\bigl(C_1(\gamma)\bigr)^t$.
