{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:39:11.673252+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9a304a0b57233a542c665549dc0141fba0484abcf3c7a206cb9890f7b77b85d1","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 5 of arXiv:2608.04853, 'Minimal-Norm Extensions of Stationary Kernels on Subgroups of Locally Compact Abelian Grou'] We call a function $k:G \times G \to \R$ a kernel if there exists a Hilbert space $H_0$ and a feature map $\Phi_0:G \to H_0$ such that 
\begin{align*}
    k(x,y)=\langle \Phi_0(x),\Phi_0(y)\rangle_{H_0}, \qquad  \forall x,y \in G.
\end{align*}
We call a kernel $k$ stationary if there exists a function $\hat{k} \in L^1(\hat{G}) \cap L^\infty(\hat{G})$ with $\hat{k}: \hat{G} \to \R $ such that $\hat{k} \geq 0$ almost everywhere and 
\begin{align*}
    k(x,y)= \int_{\hat{G}} \hat{k}(\xi) \xi(x  -y) \d \xi, \qquad \forall x,y \in G.
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:53.441607+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9a32bf6438d6f10fb69d9cc9ef5323d60df77ab76d073478cb341a2cde9775fb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 29 of arXiv:2606.15425, 'Well-posedness of stochastic parabolic equations with gradient nonlinearities and applicat'] Let $({\bm z}, \tau)$ be a given local solution according to Definition \ref{def:localsol}. Then, for any stopping time $\sigma \leq \tau$ there exists a stopping time $\widetilde \tau \geq \tau$ and a local solution $\widetilde {\bm z} \in C_w([0,\widetilde \tau];B^{d/q}_{q,2p})$ such that on the event 
$$
E_\sigma \coloneqq \Set{\sigma < \tau < T, ~\lim_{t \to \tau}\Xi_\sigma(t,{\bm z}) < \infty}
$$ it almost surely holds that
$\widetilde \tau > \tau$ and $\widetilde {\bm z} \equiv z$ on $[0,\tau)$.","status":"unverified"}

