{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:57:16.039825+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9a401f5ff70017aac372437ca171a772d6016e28cf8fb8bfc7eaa381fe98ecec","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary main_corollary of arXiv:2506.02611, '\textbf{The tight length spectrum of large-genus random hyperbolic surfaces with many cusp'] For any sequence $(n_g)_{g \ge 0}$ such that $n_{g}/g^3 \to\infty$, there exists a sequence $(\mu_g)_{g \ge 0}$ such that $\mu_g \to \mu_c$ and $\mathcal{N}_{g,\mu_g} / n_g \xrightarrow[g \to \infty]{(\mathbb{P})}1$. Furthermore
