    \end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:00.618978+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9a646f9397383d3ede06f3592cbbe9978c460083e65eff21ee1b733350a04d95","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 85 ({\cite[Theorem 1.3, Corollary 2.13) of arXiv:2510.27589, 'Geodesic switches and exceptional times in dynamical Brownian last passage percolation'] {GH20}}]

Fix $\beta'\in (0,1/2)$. There exist positive constants $c,\theta$ such that for all $m\in [\![\beta' n, (1-\beta')n]\!]$, $|R|\leq cm^{7/9}$, $r\leq m^\theta$, $\sigma\in (0,1)$, $\varepsilon>0$, $m$ large enough, and with $M$ being defined by $M=\argmax_{y\in [R-rm^{2/3},R+rm^{2/3}]} Z_{\0}^{\n,\bullet}(y,m)$, we have
  \begin{align}

    &\PP(M\in [R-rm^{2/3}/3, R+rm^{2/3}/3], \sup_{|x-M|\in [\varepsilon m^{2/3}, rm^{2/3}/3]}( Z_{\0}^{\n,\bullet}(x,m)+ \sigma|x-M|^{1/2})\geq T_{\0}^{\n})\nonumber\\
    &\leq \log(r \varepsilon^{-1})\max\{ \sigma \exp(-hR^2r+ hr^{19}(1+R^2+\log \sigma^{-1})^{5/6}\}, \exp\{-hm^{1/12}\}\}.
  \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:33:01.775559+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9a697c83e64b821a4ed561bbadc803b3019a9c432d7cd2ab170aa3a1693ff261","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 (Gaussian random variable) of arXiv:2605.14630, '2605.14630'] Let $\R$ be the real line, equipped with the $\sigma$-algebra $\cB$ 
of Borel sets and Lebesgue measure $\6x$. A random variable $X:\R\to\R$ is a 
(one-dimensional) Gaussian random variable with mean $m$ and variance $\sigma^2$ if 
its law is  
\begin{equation}
 \mu(\6x) = \frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi\sigma^2}} \e^{-(x-m)^2/(2\sigma^2)} \6x\;.
\end{equation}
In that case, we write $X\sim\cN(m,\sigma^2)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:10:05.759799+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9a6a045a2cf434529f5835b3ce364aaa9f260560de9e456358b296bff88a59b4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2608.17493, 'Integrals of some compound processes'] Let $g:\mathbb{N}^2\longrightarrow \mathbb{R}$ and $k:\mathbb{R}\longrightarrow\mathbb{R}$ such that for $\varepsilon >0\ \exists\ N_\varepsilon$ s.t. $|g(h,n) - k(h/n)|<\varepsilon,\ n\ge N_\varepsilon,\ h=1,\dots, n$. Let $f:\mathbb{R}\longrightarrow\mathbb{R}$ s.t. $\int_0^1 |f(x)|\dif x<\infty$ and $\exists\ \int_0^1 f(x)k(x)\dif x$. Then, 
	\begin{equation*}
		\lim_{n\rightarrow\infty} \sum_{h=1}^n \frac{1}{n}f\Big(\frac{h}{n}\Big) g(h,n) = \int_0^1f(x)k(x)\dif x.
	\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.301831+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9a6c34a2eff32ffee7f03790cdb16a5b796a913e285e41b92fd11ac0408a86b0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm4.7 of arXiv:2604.22130, 'Reflected Stochastic Differential Equations Driven by $G$-Brownian Motion with Nonlinear C'] For each $p\geq 1$, we have
