{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:17:33.998121+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9a843780156bfdb8d66b917a265839bda020f80268b0a07fa1896876a2872c8c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 23 of arXiv:2609.03403, 'Hyperpositive functions, sector bounded functions and a trace formula'] Let $F\in \mathcal{ HP}_{T,t}$. Then $F(z)$ admits non-tangential limits almost everywhere on the imaginary
