{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:31:49.847799+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9a95c2c2100b8ea6a9b5147bd60c873e66d4620b919c1f29c1a09b7bce3cd5fd","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def: modified transport equation of arXiv:2608.23756, 'Measure-valued fluid limits for partial service queues\\with correlated patience and servi'] Fix $[a, b] \subset \mathbbm{R}_+$ and a Borel function $\map{\bar \boldsymbol{y}}{[a, b]}{[0, \infty]}$. Suppose that $\boldsymbol{\mu} \in D_{\mathcal{M}_F(\mathbbm{R}_+^2)}[a, b]$ is such that $|\boldsymbol{\mu}|$ satisfies (a) and (b) of Definition (def: fluid problem of the paper) and the integrals
	\begin{equation*}
		\int_a^t\int_{U_g} \left[\mathbbm{1}_{\left\{y \leq \bar \boldsymbol{y}_s\right\}}h_g^x(x, y) + h_g^y(x, y)\right]\boldsymbol{\mu}_s(dx, dy)ds
	\end{equation*}
	are finite for all $t \in [a, b]$. Let $\bar \boldsymbol{r}_s(y) \vcentcolon= \mathbbm{1}_{\left\{y \leq \bar \boldsymbol{y}_s\right\}}$ for all $s \in [a, b]$ and $y \in \mathbbm{R}_+$. We say that $\boldsymbol{\mu}$ solves the transport equation (equation eq: transport equation with given threshold of the paper) with prescribed threshold $\bar \boldsymbol{y}$ in the interval $[a, b]$ if
	\begin{equation}

		\begin{split}
			\angled{\varphi_t}{\boldsymbol{\mu}_t} &= \angled{\varphi_a}{\boldsymbol{\mu}_a} + \lambda_0 \int_a^t \varphi_s(0, 0)ds - \int_a^t \angled{\varphi_s\left[\bar \boldsymbol{r}_s h_g^x + h_g^y\right]}{\boldsymbol{\mu}_s} ds \\
