{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.666337+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9aa9b51184be860c905af6b36c1d294ba89e0bc7e25667b68a89fae39f4a4c35","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem cor:exp_conv_from_stab of arXiv:2412.09235, 'A semiconcavity approach to stability of entropic plans and exponential convergence of Sin'] Let $c(x,\cdot)$ be $\mathcal{C}^1(\mathcal{Y})$ and assume that there exist $\Lambda\in(0,+\infty)$ and $N\geq 2$ such that 
