{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.779518+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9aed9f6fd77e9277f99c107dac59d10f8513a599e675530a6e1fb8f8cc01b6e7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor corproofmin of arXiv:2411.18359, 'Large systems of symmetrized trapped Brownian Bridges and Schr\"odinger processes'] There exists a measure $q^*\in {\mathcal M }_1^{(s)}(\mathbb{R} ^d\times\mathbb{R} ^d)$ such that 
