{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:52.207281+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b17a7bd340ff2e93daf6d3a8a426fb901b0e0355251357e170075d29cc023ca","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2512.09136, 'On the Green's functions and Martin boundary structure of a planar diffusion in a disconti'] The Laplace transform $\phi^{z_0}(x)$ extends to a holomorphic function on $\C \backslash \big( (-\infty,\m] \cup [\M, +\infty) \big)$ and can be expressed as follows:
\begin{equation}
\phi^{z_0}(x) = -\frac{e^{xa_0 + Y^-(x)b_0\fc_{b_0> 0} +  Z^+(x)b_0\fc_{b_0<0}}}{\gamma(x,Y^-(x), Z^+(x))}.
\end{equation}
The points $\M$ and $\m$ are the branching points of $\phi^{z_0}$.
Furthermore, 
\begin{equation}
\phi^{z_0}_+(x,y) = \frac{-\gamma(x,y,Z^+(x))\phi^{z_0}(x) - e^{xa_0 + yb_0 \fc_{b_0 > 0} + z b_0 \fc_{b_0 < 0}}}{\gamma_+(x,y)}.
\end{equation}
Similarly, a symmetric expression holds for $\phi^{z_0}_-$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:54:15.648837+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b198b52d1bc2a9668870efe69ec8b28b61c456e0ef28efbbf5f5612aedb834d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2608.09419, 'Left-tail expansions for Schr\"oder branching processes with explicit convergence rates'] \lb{L1}
