{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:43:43.190575+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b225863b27c23c4fe9a63dd8dc847e146c6b75b6f93133d3c6e2edc1017dd8a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2506.21466, 'The Markov property for $\varphi^4_3$ on the cylinder'] For every $T\in(0,\infty]$ and $f \in C^\infty(\mathbb T^2)$, the \emph{renormalized boundary cost function} is the map  $\mathbb F^{0,f}_T: \mathbb L^0 \rightarrow \mathbb R$ defined by
