{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:30:08.063246+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b43ac3f0f80de2345c93b275aa93051393b2193eb5831ce2c688059bc06492d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:reverse-charging of arXiv:2608.12415, 'Sharp Phase Transition for Ellipsoid Fitting'] Fix a block in a given block-walk. We call a step \(u\to v\) \emph{reverse-charging} if the following conditions hold:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item the underlying edge is making its global last appearance in the walk;
        \item the global first appearance of the same underlying edge also occurs within the current block;
        \item that first appearance traverses the edge in the opposite direction, namely from \(v\) to \(u\).
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:09:34.497108+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b479a952a86845ddf097934bfc19781c74a09f9da2484390cfa68af75c8c266","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm Conformal Invariance under ${\rm Aut}(\mathbb{D}, 0)$ of arXiv:2505.14762, 'Multiple radial SLE($\kappa$) and quantum Calogero-Sutherland system'] For a rotation map $\rho_{\theta}$, the drift term \( b_i(\boldsymbol{\theta}) \) is invariant under \(\rho_\theta\), i.e.,
\[
b_i = \widetilde{b}_i \circ \rho_{\theta}.
\]

\begin{itemize}
    \item[(i)] The function \( h(\theta) \) in the null vector equation ((null vector equation angular coordinate constant h of the paper)) is rotation-invariant, and there exists a real constant \( h \) such that
   \begin{equation}
    h(\theta) = h.
   \end{equation}

