{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:25.278069+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b53c22ea1d9369405e49a0408694af745110a23c7225982fd0b7d4a5da0d53e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2606.21433, 'Central limit theorem for\\ the averaged Adam optimizer'] Let    $q\in(1-\beta,1]$ and let, for $\bz\in\ell_{\varrho}$,
\bas{
v^{*}(\bz)=\inf\Bigl\{(1-\beta)\sum_{k\in-\N_{0}\backslash\{r\}} \beta^{-k} z_{k}^{2}:r\in-\N_{0}\Bigr\}.
}
There exists a constant $C\in(0,\infty)$ only depending on the damping factors and $q$  such that for every innovation $(X,U)$, $\delta\in(0,\infty)$, $\theta,\theta'\in\R^{d}$ with
\bas{
\P(X^{(i)}(\bar\theta,U)^{2}\ge \delta)\ge q\text{, \ for all \ $\bar\theta\in\{\theta,\theta'\}$ and $i\in\{1,\dots,d\}$},
}
one has for every $\bx\in \ell_{\varrho}^d$ that
\bas{
|\Psi_\theta(\bx)-\Psi_{\theta'}(\bx)|&\le C \sum_{i=1}^d  \bigl(1+(\delta^{-1/2}+ v^*(\bx^{(i)})^{-1/2}) (\|\bx^{(i)} \|_{\ell_\varrho}+ \E[X^{(i)}(\theta,U)^2]^{1/2} )\bigr)  \\
&\hspace{6cm} \E[(X^{(i)}(\theta,U)-X^{(i)}(\theta',U))^2]^{1/2} 
}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:31.997376+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b543788844275cd6aee72d4b9615c08e24286a0ab63a1df92174de78844aa6e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2512.02322, 'Ursell functions in lattice gauge theory'] Consider Ising lattice gauge theory at inverse temperature $\beta \geq \beta_0$. Then, for any Wilson loops $(\gamma_i)_{i \in [n]}$, the Ursell function of the Wilson observables equals
    \begin{align}

