{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.501093+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b562d74c57a01487e7c48965fb7b259241db8f4fe6a14ceb79b7fe0d5261ea1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 35 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] For all $(Y,Y') \in \scrd_X^{2 \alpha}([0,T],L(V,W))$ we have
\begin{align*}
