        H_{n,m}&=\frac{4^n}{m+1}\frac{\tan^2\left(\frac{\pi}{m+1}\right)}{\left(1+\tan^2\left(\frac{\pi}{m+1}\right)\right)^n}+O\left(\frac{4^n}{m^3}\frac{1}{\left(1+\tan^2\left(\frac{2\pi}{m+1}\right)\right)^n}\right)\\
        &=\big(1+o(1)\big)\frac{4^n}{m+1}\frac{\tan^2\left(\frac{\pi}{m+1}\right)}{\left(1+\tan^2\left(\frac{\pi}{m+1}\right)\right)^n}
    \end{align*}
    where the $o(\cdot)$ and $O(\cdot)$ terms only depend on $h_n$, and are uniformly bounded over all such $m$.
    Moreover, the second asymptotic equality trivially holds when $m\in\{2,3\}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:43:00.048958+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b5a09e9009693e6910a0b5f41c89d81c09f91e0a434f5800f59e70947edb716","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 42 of arXiv:2609.00758, 'Deformations of Compact Calabi--Yau and Fano Varieties with Isolated Singularities'] Let $X$ be a compact complex $n$-fold with isolated Du Bois singularities, whose resolutions satisfy the $\partial\db$ lemma and such that $H^n(X^\reg,\C)\to H^{n+1}(X,X^\reg;\C)$ is surjective. Then for every good resolution  $(Y,E)\to (X,X^\sing)$ the connecting homomorphism
