{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:45:32.045706+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b5c72788dd850e7b8a453d3818ceae013d7b8a0f71e7c7694c427d10b9cccde","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition Limiting point process of arXiv:2411.13972, 'The Stochastic Bessel operator at high temperatures'] There is a random variable $M_0$ valued in the Borel sets of $]0,\infty[$, such that, for all fixed $\mu_1 < \ldots < \mu_k$,
