where $\sigma^2$ depends on the law of environment and G-W tree only. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:45:10.046898+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b6227bbb0622d041ec2c226abf0622470c2554514f9c309365dde645113cd57","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Beta function of arXiv:2504.14457, 'Abstract'] The Beta function is defined by the integral:
\begin{align}
\nonumber    B(x,y)&:=\int_0^1 t^{x-1} (1-t)^{y-1}\,dt\\
