$f:=\int^\infty_0 P_t\bar g {\mathord{{\rm d}}} t$ with $\bar g=g-\mu(g)$ and $g\in{\mathbf C}^\gamma$,
\begin{align}
\|f\|_{{\mathbf C}^{1}_{\rm log}}+\|f\|_{{\mathbf C}^{\beta+\gamma}_{\rm log}}
\lesssim_{C}\|g\|_{{\mathbf C}^\gamma}.
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:37:09.015042+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b86d34498dc9156af7aefff45aae6e266156af14c54049206d66a6d653dd2f9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:as_nondegeneracy of arXiv:2609.01697, 'Unique ergodicity of projective cocycles over the 2D stochastic Navier--Stokes equations'] For any $\alpha \in (0,1]$, $T > 0$, $N \geqslant 1$, and any initial condition $z_0 \in \mathcal{X}$:
  \begin{equation}
    \mathbb{P}\left( \inf_{\eta \in S_{\alpha, N, T}} \langle M_T(z_0) \eta, \eta \rangle > 0 \right) = 1 .
  \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.578835+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b8734ce40e886cc7ffdcc2cda6e0566cf691d9f1cd7b7803ca3b001dffd1653","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition d:Substationary of arXiv:2411.14936, 'Massive Particle Systems,\\Wasserstein Brownian Motions,\\ and the Dean--Kawasaki Equation'] Fix~$p\geq 1$.
A semigroup of transition kernel measures~$\mssh_\bullet$ is \emph{$p$-sub-stationary w.r.t.~$\mssm$} if
\begin{equation}
\int (\mssH_t f)^p \mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mssm \leq \int f^p \mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mssm \,\mathrm{,}\;\, \qquad f\in\mcB_b^+ \,\mathrm{,}\;\,
\end{equation}
and it is simply called $\mssm$-\emph{sub-stationary} if it is $1$-sub-stationary w.r.t.~$\mssm$.
If~$\mssh_\bullet$ is $\mssm$-sub-stationary, the measure $\mssm$ is called \emph{$\mssh_\bullet$-super-median}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:29:14.932607+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b891b51bf254369a00e42265f4a435768451328b7b5ab3c8bac35ecd8240707","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem flow of arXiv:2606.13442, 'Scaling limit of additive functionals for reversible non-gradient exclusion process: criti'] There exists a flow $\phi_\ell$ connecting $\delta_0$ to $p_\ell$ satisfying the following conditions.
		\begin{itemize}
			\item $\phi_\ell (x,y) = 0$ unless $x,y \in \Lambda_\ell$;
			\item There exists a finite positive constant $C_0 (d)$ such that
			\[\sum_{x \sim y} \phi_\ell (x,y)^2 \leqslant C_0 g_d (\ell),\]
			where
			\[g_d (\ell) = \begin{cases}
				\ell, \quad&\text{if } \;d=1,\\
				\log \ell, \quad&\text{if } \;d=2,\\
				1, \quad&\text{if } \;d\geqslant 3.
			\end{cases}\]
		\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:26:02.502747+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b8ab72fe6de7262d60e2021bbbb8c1e835665d7143b464b8e266945ef417f35","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm resolvealeph of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] Suppose $\Phi$ is $\aleph$-unobstructed. With the previous notation, there exists $\varepsilon > 0$ such that
\begin{align} 
    U^\varepsilon_\flat \times U^\varepsilon_\sharp \times U^\varepsilon_- \times U^\varepsilon_+ \times \{(w_1, \dots, w_{k_\circ})\} \times \mathbb{R}^{k_\aleph} \subset \mathcal{Z}(\Phi).
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.354883+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b8dedf555ccfdc6fae83ebbb5d843fc83b29ab4b5a1e556a5ddb8e8ca3ad6b6","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2509.23069, 'Every cutoff profile is possible'] Let $((X^{(n)}_t)_{t\geq 0})_{n\geq 1}$ be a sequence of ergodic Markov chains, in discrete or continuous time. We say that that $((X^{(n)}_t)_{t\geq 0})_{n\geq 1}$ exhibits a total variation \textbf{cutoff} at a (sequence of) times $\left( t_n \right)_{n \geq 1}$ if for every $\varepsilon>0$, we have 
    \begin{equation}
        \mathrm{d}^{(n)}\left( \left\lfloor (1-\varepsilon) t_n \right\rfloor \right) \xrightarrow[n\to \infty]{} 1 \quad \text{ and } \quad \mathrm{d}^{(n)}\left( \left\lceil (1+\varepsilon) t_n \right\rceil \right) \xrightarrow[n\to \infty]{} 0,
    \end{equation}
where for $n\geq 1$, $\mathrm{d}^{(n)}(\cdot)$ is the distance to stationarity for the chain $(X^{(n)}_t)_{t\geq 0}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.269581+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b8df30ac3e5e5687d80e813c27e2a462f03f5b92d1930e5d69c2c44f1eef729","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2604.15753, 'The truncation property and continuity for \\ the long-range contact process on $\mathbb{Z'] Let $\lambda \in \Lambda$ and $\delta>0$. Then, for any $L,T>0$ and $A \subset B_L$, a.s.\ on $H_{L,T}^{A}(k)$, $k \in \bN$, it holds that
\begin{equation} 
\bP_{\lambda,\delta} \left( \exists s>0 \colon A_s^A = \emptyset  \mid \cF_{L,T} \right) \geq \left(e(1+\lambda_{\infty})\right)^{-k}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:04.858128+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b8e2897b59322a3bf6ca0f44efa5a31ec8ecf9465e5b298d21ce6e0cecfcbd1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 8 of arXiv:2511.20875, 'Double $q$-Wigner Chaos and the Fourth Moment'] Let $X_k= I_0( f_k)$ and $Y_k= I_0( g_k)$ with $ f_k=f_k^* \in H^{\otimes m}$ and $ g_k=g_k^* \in H^{\otimes n}$ where $\tau_0(X_k^2)+\tau_0(Y_k^2)\to \sigma^2$ as $k\to \infty$ and $m,n\in \mathbb{N}$ have opposite parities.  
     Then the following are equivalent: \begin{enumerate}
          \item $\lim_{k\to \infty}\kappa_4(X_k+Y_k)=0$.
          \item  $\displaystyle{\lim_{k\to\infty} f_k \overset{p}{\frown} f_k = 0}$ in $H^{\otimes 2(m-p)}$ for $p=1,\ldots,m-1$ and $\displaystyle{\lim_{k\to\infty} g_k \overset{p}{\frown} g_k = 0}$ in $H^{\otimes 2(n-p)}$ for $p=1,\ldots,n-1$.
         \item $X_k+Y_k$ converges in distribution toward $ S(0,\sigma^2)$. 
     \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.990066+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b8e8f2bf78444fc6d3bf5cbd60555562ba166c45754422c53c98eb1f7f9fee2","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 89 (Transfer-impedance matrix) of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] Recall that we fixed an (arbitrary) orientation of the edges with $e^-$ and $e^+$ denoting the starting and ending points of an edge $e$. Let $v_e(\cdot)$ be the voltage on the vertices when a unit current flow $\theta_e$ is sent from $e^-$ to $e^+$, i.e.\ $v_e(\cdot)$ is the (unique) harmonic function on $V \setminus \{e^-, e^+\}$ with $v_e(e^-) = \effR{}{e^-}{e^+}$ and $v_e(e^+) = 0$. The transfer-impedance matrix $Y$ is a $|E| \times |E|$ matrix with entries given by
    \begin{equation*}
        Y(e,f) := w(f) \big[ v_e(f^-) - v_e(f^+) \big] = \theta_e(f^-, f^+).
    \end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.500659+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b909b627dde06f6fc902ff24edad9df702093f371b9015414ebce9b83277e98","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop : FdTmon/StrMon of arXiv:2412.03320, 'Large deviation principle at speed $n$ for the random metric in first-passage percolation'] Let $D_1, D_2 \in \RegPD$ be distinct pseudometrics satsifying $D_1 \le D_2$. If $\FdTmon(D_2)<\infty$, then
