{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:38:57.118196+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9bcc1afbf158d9269f7336e044e5d935577a338d321382d440301f06f0e8808b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 27 of arXiv:2604.04823, '2604.04823'] For any sufficiently large~$a\geq 1$, there exist $\hat\epsilon (a), \eta, \hat  \gamma,\lambda > 0$ such that for all~$\epsilon, h, \gamma$ with
