{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:16:46.117192+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9bdc69cf36e7171562135cba5d79ba4ae10a127effce6e8cbf4093eeaca7ba39","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem shockstoisland of arXiv:2604.12963, 'Shocks, instability, and the twenty networks\\ of infinite geodesics in the Directed Lands'] Let $\omega\in\Omega_0$ and $\theta\in\Theta^\omega$. Let $(z,t_2)\in\IG\theta$. Suppose that $\Upsilon_{(z,t_2)}\dir{L}{\theta}{-}$ and $\Upsilon_{(z,t_2)}\dir{R}{\theta}{+}$ are misordered.  Let
