{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:43:45.379517+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9bdca6e25e539c8dd4d664c1fa8fdcf7dd54572f21c235b95ecd8a0dbb68b11c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2609.03993, 'The Endpoint Fractional Riesz Estimate on the Hamming Cube'] Let $(T_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be a quatum Markov semigroup on $(\cN,\tau)$ and $(P_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be its subordinated
		Poisson semigroup, and assume $\Gamma_2\ge0$. Let $a:(0,\infty)\to\mathbb C$ be measurable.
