{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.501370+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9bf4f751aafe2ac77fd1ca45498146bccbfa84fc3018636fbdc707021c158ece","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary eq:subquadratic-local-cost of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[corollary]{cor:general-tail-obstruction}
Assume that the distinguished coordinate has law \(\mu\).  Suppose that
for some \(M<\infty\), \(\eta>0\), \(\delta>0\), and a sequence
\(a_k\to\infty\), (equation eq:conditional-remainder-cost of the paper) holds with
