{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:28:33.793380+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9c3b5afbd13e49b6f58d9c64b4e9726ff72f65d349ec1110b88abbd9ee9d51a3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:44 of arXiv:2504.12293, 'Near-existence of bigeodesics in dynamical exponential last passage percolation'] {GH24}}]

  Consider dynamical Brownian LPP defined using a family of independent Brownian motions $\{W_n^t\}_{n\in \mathbb{Z},t\in \mathbb{R}}$ independently evolving according to the Ornstein-Uhlenbeck dynamics. Use $\widetilde{\Gamma}_{\0}^{\mathbf{n},t}$  to denote a geodesic from $\0$ to $\mathbf{n}$ at time $t$. Consider the quantity $\mathcal{O}_n(t)= |\widetilde{\Gamma}_{\0}^{\mathbf{n},0}\cap \widetilde{\Gamma}_{\0}^{\mathbf{n},t}|_{\mathrm{hor}}$. Then for any fixed $\delta>0$, and for all $n$ large enough, we have
  \begin{align}

    &\mathbb{E} \mathcal{O}_n(t)= \Theta(n) \textrm{ for all } t<n^{-1/3-\delta},\nonumber\\
    &\mathbb{E} \mathcal{O}_n(t)=o(n) \textrm{ for all } t>n^{-1/3+\delta}.
  \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:20:55.585054+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9c3b910856169fcd941b7b819703d1f6ce1d5364d7c30779dab939a5885b201c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:sufficient-energy-3 of arXiv:2411.07680, 'Energy solutions of singular SPDEs on Hilbert spaces with applications to domains with bou'] We make Assumption (A) and additionally assume that $S$ is a core for $A$. Let $(u_t (f))_{t \geqslant 0, f \in  S}$ be an adapted process which satisfies conditions i., ii., iv. from Theorem~(lem:sufficient-energy of the paper) and also
