{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:48:24.617505+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9c497ae4492ba529d4a4bed65aa4975d1a987c9c08f578b42dcecdddd93c64a5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:S_theta of arXiv:2601.04997, 'Fluctuations of the Boundary-Driven Symmetric Zero-Range Process from the NESS'] Let $\mathfrak{A}_\theta$ denote the operator acting on smooth functions $f\in C^\infty([0, 1])$ via $\mathfrak{A}_\theta f(u):=\Phi'(\bar\rho_\theta(u))\Delta f(u)$, with $\Phi$ defined in (equation eq:Phi of the paper) and $\bar\rho_\theta$ given in Remark (remark:limit_density of the paper). We define the set $\mathcal{S}_\theta$ as follows: 
\begin{enumerate}[i)]

