The infimum is over all measurable estimators based on \(X_1,\ldots,X_n\sim \Pi_\xi\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:23:37.802499+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9c5718eb33b06934972040994c6080597537ee4664f5cbf54303a0154ffc16c6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 7 (Sobolev estimates) of arXiv:2609.03558, 'Local well-posedness of the higher-order nonlinear Schr\"{o}dinger equation on the half-li'] Let $b\in \{0,1\}$. Then, the unique solution of \eqref{cauchy2} satisfies the space estimate
