{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:10.191162+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9c57a428768b0b1b79995abb14d1e089fdc3f618770408cf161ca6e65288ba90","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 188 of arXiv:2605.03236, 'Stochastic It\^o Equations and Parabolic Second-Order Equations with singular Drift'] For any $i,s=1,2,...$, $t>0$, and 
$$
f(t_{1},...,t_{i})=\{
f^{k_{1},...,k_{i}}(
t_{1},...,t_{i}),k_{j}=1,...,d_{1}\},  
$$
 given
