{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:10:43.991399+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9c7d7ac6aab4a00dcab06c05d69007ad6722e1d8eff77dccc1e7971c71db671a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2412.04579, 'Solvable Families of Random Block Tridiagonal Matrices'] The ${\mathbb{F}}$-valued square root Wishart matrix with parameters $ m> n-1$ is the distribution of the $n\times n$ lower triangular matrix $\mathbf{X}$ with the following independent entries:
