{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:32:19.901046+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9c9e60c27c90433218791d658574bf1b9d72c8abe80f02b1d11de0032c5ce49b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2608.02319, 'Averaging Principle for Ordinary Differential Equations in a Multiscale Random Environment'] Let $0<s_1<s_2$, $0<t_1<t_2$, $x\in E$, $z\in\mathbb R^d$, then, for all $L,M>0$, $n,j\geq1$ and $j\geq k+1$ we have
\begin{align*}
