    Then, for each $z \in \mathbb{R}^d$, there exists a unique weak solution $X^z$ to the McKean--Vlasov SDE (equation gen-DDSDE of the paper) with the prescribed one-dimensional time marginals $\mathcal{L}(X^z_t) = u^z(t,x) \,\mathrm d x$, $t > 0$, and $X^z_0 = z$. 
    The family of solution path laws $\{P^z\}_{z\in \mathbb{R}^d}$, $P^z = \mathcal{L}(X^z)$, is a nonlinear Markov core for $\{u^z(t)\}_{t>0, z\in \mathbb{R}^d}$ and is uniquely determined by $\{u^z\}_{z \in \mathbb{R}^d}$ and (equation gen-DDSDE of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

