{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:30.077134+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9cf0e76628be290a8cfa3749e8b2b903d63aa810fe8f23d530d9f1961f520b94","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 8 of arXiv:2606.02570, 'Stochastic completeness for landmark space'] Suppose that the radial scalar function $k\colon [0,\infty)\to\R$ is smooth on $(0,\infty)$ and that it possesses a positive continuous Fourier transform $\widehat{k}\colon\R^d\to\R$. For $M>0$, we set
    \begin{displaymath}
