{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:49:15.470607+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9d3a096c544ac56b4e9c08c1db498370af4136c5a0f237ff9b6b1be3cfdd9c94","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:J^V momentum map of arXiv:2608.28278, 'Reduction of symmetric time-dependent Hamiltonian systems I: presymplectic principal $\R$-'] The momentum map $J:T^*Q \to \mathfrak{g}^*$ induces an $Ad^*$-equivariant momentum map $J^V: V^*\Pi \to \mathfrak{g}^*$ characterized by
