{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:59:45.011347+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9d3db034ada6821f442fa04f2149212310d35d3100dc4d57a83e5dafc750c109","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition W SPDE-1 of arXiv:2605.13479, '\LARGE Dean-Kawasaki Equation with Biot-Savart and Keller-Segel Interactions: Existence an'] Let $\mathcal{V}[\cdot]$ and $\rho_0$ be defined as in Definition (RKS smooth spde of the paper), for any $\varepsilon,\eta\in(0,1)$, a weak solution  $\rho$ of (equation SPDE-1 of the paper) with initial data $\rho(\cdot, 0)=\rho_0$ is a nonnegative, $\mathcal{F}_{t}$-predictable process that satisfies the following properties.
\begin{enumerate}
		\item Conservation of mass: almost surely for every $t\in[0,T]$,
		\begin{equation}
		\|\rho(\cdot,t)\|_{L^{1}_{\mathbb{T}^{2}}}=\left\|\rho_0\right\|_{L^{1}_{\mathbb{T}^{2}}}.
		\end{equation}




		\item Pathwise entropy dissipation estimates: almost surely, 
		\begin{align}
 \int_0^t\int_{\mathbb{T}^2}
