{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:20.862830+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9d4764ae3d1e02fb25aa9c57b1cd5cc0e42d1aae58363b0e752adc9fec936d1c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 22 of arXiv:2506.10817, 'On the Weak Error for Local Stochastic Volatility Models'] Let $h,T>0$ such that $\frac Th\in \mathbb{N}$.  For $k\in \{1,\dots,\frac Th\}$ let $\tilde \beta_k$ and $\beta_k$ be $\mathcal{F}_{kh}$ adapted and uniformly bounded by some $b>0$.
