{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:49:06.312266+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9d62279fa91a18c9a4c28cfdf547405eab6a60467689538fa570f1b34e250718","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th:approx-kin-form of arXiv:2601.07759, 'The value of random zero-sum games'] Let $\eta\in (0,1)$. Let $K_1$ and $K_2$ be convex cones in $\mathbb{R}^n$ and $Q\sim \mathcal{U}(O_n)$, then, denoting $a_\eta = \sqrt{8\log(4/\eta)}$, for $\eta\in (0,1)$,
\begin{align*}
    \delta(K_1)+\delta(K_2)\leq n-a_\eta\sqrt{n} \quad &\implies \quad \mathbb{P}(K_1\cap QK_2\neq\{0\})\leq \eta,\\
    \delta(K_1)+\delta(K_2)\geq n+a_{\eta}\sqrt{n}\quad &\implies\quad \mathbb{P}(K_1\cap QK_2\neq \{0\})\geq 1-\eta.
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

