{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:00.620779+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9d67eaf1b7533784b063881f4e878c4f97596989c9a6353057a9740c0e4f13d9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 14 of arXiv:2511.00764, 'Further Developments on Stochastic Dominance for Convex\\ Combinations of Infinite-Mean Ra'] Let $\bm X=(X_1, \ldots, X_n)$ be a vector of $n$ iid random variables with a common distribution $F$, and $A_1, \ldots, A_n$ be events with equal probability, which are independent of $\bm X$. If $F\in\mathcal{H}^\ast$, then, for all $\bm \th\in \Delta_n$,
