{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:50:30.559703+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9d75e9ce5e5393f13cd11f8d4a2040d1b22261d305b9af803936ef46e960292a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2605.30321, 'A Bayesian Proof and Interpretation \\ of Talagrand's Majorizing Measure Theorem'] \cite{Talagrand1987}For any centered and separable Gaussian process $(G_t)_{t \in T}$ when $T$ is endowed with the canonical pseudo-metric \[
