{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.274737+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9d7623f51150ae4a2fcb5acc1fa7f8d3eaa69e7e758b9abd2e65404d02747aef","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop_ES_magnetic of arXiv:2411.16452, 'Interface scaling limit for the critical planar Ising model perturbed by a magnetic field'] Let $\hat {\mathbb{P}}^{\operatorname{free}}_{\delta, H}$ denote the law of the Edwards-Sokal coupling with external field $H \geq 0$. For $\omega: E(\Omega_{\delta}) \to \{0,1\}^{\vert E(\Omega_{\delta}) \vert}$ and $\mathcal{C} \in \mathcal{C}_{\delta}(\omega)$, we let $\sigma(\mathcal{C})$ denote the spin of $\mathcal{C}$ assigned by the coupling. We then have that
\begin{equation*}
    {\mathbb{P}}_{\delta, H}^{\operatorname{FK}, \operatorname{free}}(\mathcal{C} \longleftrightarrow g \vert \omega) = \tanh(H \vert \mathcal{C} \vert), \quad \hat {\mathbb{P}}_{\delta,H}^{\operatorname{free}}(\sigma(\mathcal{C})=+1 \vert \omega)= \frac{1}{2}+ \frac{1}{2}\tanh(H \vert \mathcal{C} \vert).
\end{equation*}
Moreover, conditionally on $\omega$, the events $(\{\mathcal{C} \longleftrightarrow g\})_{\mathcal{C} \in \mathcal{C}_{\delta}(\omega)}$ are mutually independent. Similarly, conditionally on $\omega$, the events $(\{\sigma(\mathcal{C})=+1\})_{\mathcal{C} \in \mathcal{C}_{\delta}(\omega)}$ are mutually independent. The Radon-Nikodym derivative of $\mathbb{Q}_{\delta,H}^{\operatorname{free}}$, the marginal law of ${\mathbb{P}}_{\delta,H}^{\operatorname{FK}, \operatorname{free}}$ on edge configurations $\omega: E(\Omega_{\delta}) \to \{0,1\}^{\vert E(\Omega_{\delta}) \vert}$, with respect to ${\mathbb{P}}_{\delta}^{\operatorname{FK}, \operatorname{free}}$ is given by
\begin{equation*}
    \frac{{\operatorname{d}} \mathbb{Q}_{\delta,H}^{\operatorname{free}}}{{\operatorname{d}} {\mathbb{P}}_{\delta}^{\operatorname{FK}, \operatorname{free}}}(\omega) = \frac{1}{\mathcal{Z}_{\delta,H}} \prod_{\mathcal{C} \in \mathcal{C}_{\delta}(\omega)} \cosh(H \vert \mathcal{C} \vert)
\end{equation*}
where $\mathcal{Z}_{\delta,H}$ is a normalization constant. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:47:22.258873+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9d7675e88e71e91d6828ff994aabc90d9d6ba91bf7a4e17eaf0ee2c8ce302c6a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 131 of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] For any $x \in [0,a]$, we have 
