{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:16.149861+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9d76d4de536e5c4422e3707bae909346171c33dcd3f7132534daa588b236c729","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2604.13454, 'Invariant and periodic measures in classical spin systems on infinite lattices with highly'] (finite-dimensional result) Assume  SDE (\ref{FSDE}) coefficients satisfy  Assumption \ref{A1}. Then there exists a unique invariant measure $\mu$ for $X^{(n),x}(t)$. Specifically, there exist constant $K,\alpha>0$ such that for the function $V_n(x)=1+x_1^2+\cdots +x_n^2$,
