{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:53.449532+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9d93c90982c90d225498b0a9671893057b14727a931715c435931c5d27a7ccc5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 20 (Subspace stability of the algebraic discrepancy body) of arXiv:2606.16005, '\bfseries An Algebraic Matrix Spencer Theorem'] Let \(B_1,\ldots,B_n\) be self-adjoint contractions contained in a finite-dimensional \(C^*\)-algebra \(\mathcal A\) satisfying $\dim_{\mathbb C}\mathcal A\le C_0n$.
Let \(S\subseteq[n]\) be arbitrary with \(s:=|S|\), and  denote the discrepancy body $K_B(S)\subseteq\mathbb R^S$ by $K_B(S):=\{z\in \R^S:\left\|
\sum_{i\in S}z_iB_i
