$$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:19:00.889223+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9dd9675fb7f9f69935d34e8381fa589566dc47de9e5aa6b8c004ac9019e0e213","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 51 (Function-indexed martingales of a class-$(\Sigma)$
process~\cite{Nikeghbali2006essay}) of arXiv:2608.20337, 'Information on trajectories:\\ martingales and random times'] Let $X=N+A$ be of class $(\Sigma)$ and let $f\colon\R_+\to\R$ be Borel and locally bounded.  Then
\begin{equation}
  \int_0^{A_t} f(z)\,\dd z-f(A_t)\,X_t
  \;=\;-\int_0^t f(A_u)\,\dd N_u
\end{equation}
so the left-hand side is a local martingale null at $0$.
Conversely, let $X$ be a nonnegative local submartingale with $X_0=0$ and let $C$ be a continuous adapted nondecreasing process with $C_0=0$ such that $\int_0^{C_t}f(z)\,\dd z-f(C_t)X_t$ is a local martingale for every locally bounded Borel $f$.
Then $X$ is of class $(\Sigma)$ and $C=A$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:51:33.324884+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9dd9d92dbdc616e2634e12239ee611b2638aaae5c1bbc4af4ea3fab432afb412","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] The $\infty$-category ${\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}_G$ is stable.
    \begin{proof}
        As the underlying $\infty$-category of a model category, ${\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}_G$ is complete and cocomplete, with the localization preserving initial and final objects. Thus, ${\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}_G$ is pointed. Observe now that the $\infty$-categorical suspension functor on ${\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}_G$ is induced by the suspension functor on the pointset level (e.g.~since the left Quillen bifunctor $\textbf{\textup{Top}}_*\times\cat{$\bm{G}$-OrthSp}\to\cat{$\bm{G}$-OrthSp}$ describing the tensoring descends to a functor $\Spc_*\times{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}_G\to{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}_G$ preserving colimits in each variable and restricting to the identity on $\{S^0\}\times{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}_G$, and there is only one such functor). Thus, the claim follows by specializing the previous proposition to the 1-dimensional trivial $G$-representation.
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:50:48.845147+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9dda05aed1cb7eff81e83e5912af2e57f4620e8a4019e47ef0f52218d610ff97","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop.conv.int.eta of arXiv:2607.07598, 'Universal Central Limit Theorem for non-exchangeable interacting diffusions'] Suppose Assumption (assum.main of the paper) holds with $k\ge \lambda_d+2$. Let $(\eta^n)_{n\in{\mathbb{N}}}$ be a subsequence, still denoted by $(\eta^n)_{n\in{\mathbb{N}}}$, such that $\eta^n \stackrel{d}{\to} \eta$ in $C([0,T];{\mathcal{H}}^{-k})$. Then:
		\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
			\item  $\eta\in L^2([0,T];{\mathcal{H}}_w^{-(k-1)})$ a.s.
			\item 
			For every deterministic  $g \in L^\infty([0,T]; C_b^{k}({\mathbb{R}}^d))$,
			\begin{align} 
				\int_0^T \langle \eta_t^n, g_t\rangle_{{\mathcal{H}}^{-k}_w,{\mathcal{H}}^{k}_w}\,\mathrm{d} t
