{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:11.643462+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9de49062dd756ee5222687c41c426e849a8fd51bcc6d81f87a416a64c3461367","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 16 of arXiv:2605.31471, 'Convergence Rates of Continuous-Time Random Walks to Time-Fractional Diffusions with Unbou'] Let $(P_t)_{t\ge 0}$ be a strongly continuous semigroup on a Banach space $(X,\|\cdot\|)$.
    Assume there exist constants $M\ge 1$ and $\omega\in\mathbb{R}$ such that
    \begin{equation}
        \|P_t\|_{X\to X} \;\le\; M e^{\omega t}, 
        \qquad t\ge 0.
    \end{equation}
    Then, for every $\varepsilon>0$, there exists an equivalent norm 
    $\|\cdot\|_{*}$ on $X$ such that
    \begin{equation}
        \|P_t x\|_{*} \;\le\; e^{(\omega+\varepsilon)t}\, \|x\|_{*},
        \qquad x\in X,\; t\ge 0.
    \end{equation}
    In particular, with respect to $\|\cdot\|_{*}$, the semigroup $(P_t)_{t\ge0}$ is quasi-contractive.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:12:20.559923+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9de7ed18f433ebff728215be6677dc3fe7717988a80b3d0e9d490e722cbd1a5c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem T:Haus:meas of arXiv:2604.08129, 'Polarity of points for Gaussian random fields in critical dimension'] Let Assumptions (a:X of the paper) and (a:SLND of the paper) hold with $\sigma$ given by (equation sigma:gamma of the paper), where $d=N/H$ and $\gamma \le 1/d$. Let $I$ be a compact interval in ${\mathbb R}^N$. Then a.s., the range $X(I)$ has finite Hausdorff measure with respect to the gauge function $\phi(r)$ defined by
\begin{align}
    \phi(r) =  r^d (\log(1/r))^{1-\gamma d}\log\log\log(1/r).
\end{align}
In particular, $X(I)$ has Lebesgue measure zero a.s. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:57:07.198613+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9de8863d649504b69d65daa7c4346efd133a8ef9f4f6e413ae85048df5118b2a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:compare-tau of arXiv:2509.04333, 'The limiting law of the Discrete Gaussian level lines'] Fix $n \geq 0$ and any $\theta$. There exists $\varepsilon_\beta \to 0$ as $\beta \to \infty$ such that for sufficiently large $L$, we have
