{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.820816+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9dea47231a17de41bb4a7e6deccf8bab7903365be1857cd94bc71f12e364c7cf","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi def: poincare_inequality of arXiv:2504.02207, 'Finite-Time behaviors of M/M/$n$ Queue: Mixing Time, Mean Queue Length and Tail Bounds'] A CTMC admits a Poincar\'e constant $C_P$ if for all test function $f \in \ell_{2,\nu}$, we have
