{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.602087+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9df510fe8fef562b67f87dc8f97aae59d5ad9665a34875014679fdae213c1a33","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 34 of arXiv:2607.07283, 'Multi-time Markov renewal chains and stratified renewal theorems'] Under the regenerative exact-time assumptions, for every exponentially summable finite signed measure $r$ on $\N^d$ and every compact set $K\subset\R^d$,

