    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:32:11.128438+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9df9cdc1b492ad14b67f00efe9a1bdc26927a8a6afecb6c679ac7e83ce34c900","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition pr:Fdim of arXiv:2510.09818, 'On the Fourier dimension of fractional Brownian graphs'] [LL25].
For a generic process $B$, recall that the graph and image measures $\mu_{G}$ and $\nu$ are respectively defined by~(equation mu_G of the paper) and~(equation b2 of the paper).
Suppose for every $q \in \mathbb N$, there exists $C>0$ such that
\begin{enumerate}
\item (vertical bound) $\mathbb E[|\hat{\nu}(\xi_2)|^{2q}]\le C |\xi_2|^{-\gamma_2 q}$ for all $\xi_2 \ne 0$; and
\item (horizontal bound) $\mathbb E[|\hat{\mu}_G(\xi_1,\xi_2)|^{2q}] \le C |\xi_1|^{-\gamma_1 q}$ for all $\xi_1 \ne 0$ and $\xi_2 \in \mathbb R$.
\end{enumerate}
Then $\dim_{\rm F} G(B) \ge \min\{\gamma_1,\gamma_2\}$ a.s. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.612511+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9dfba382c1a06b53f05ce07348222a78b2aca486b18ddcf812d47bd2f0de6892","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 40 of arXiv:2607.08536, 'Soft edge limit of the Laguerre beta-ensemble at the lower edge'] For $2a_n+1> 2/\beta$ and $0< \eps\le 1$, we have 
