{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:49:15.414697+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e40767cfeef5dd5166f32cc53e8831707e8f3620cc247b31337bc8507e9663b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2608.27904, 'Instantons, indefinite 4-manifolds, and Dehn surgery'] A \textit{pointed instanton $SO(3)$-flow category} $(\mathcal{M}, p)$ is an instanton $SO(3)$-flow category for which each orbit is equipped with a choice of basepoint $p_\alpha\in\mathscr O(\alpha)$ satisfying the following conditions:
	\begin{itemize}
