        where $X \sim \mathrm{GOE}(m)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:44:17.354676+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e786e0e3514e6b1bbff5d2281e302e7a5b544a95bff2f1f474bf47e77f0d5aa","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main-approx of arXiv:2608.23554, 'Provably adaptive sampling with uniform and remasking \\ discrete diffusion models'] Let \((X_t)_{t \in [0, T]}\) be the CTMC corresponding to the uniform or remasking process. If  \(t_{k+1} - t_k \leq \kappa \min(1, T - t_{k+1})\) for \(k \in \{0, \ldots, N - 1\}\), then
    \begin{equation*}
        \sum_{k=0}^{N - 1} \cL_{\mathrm{approx}}^{(k)} \lesssim \kappa \sum_{k=0}^{N - 1}  \sum_{i \in [d]} e^{-(T - t_{k+1})} \mathsf{KL} \left( \mu_{X_0^i} \ \big\|\ \widehat\mu_{X_0^i} \ \Bigr|\  X_{T - t_k}^{-i}\,\right).
    \end{equation*}
    Here, for fixed \(i \in [d]\), \(\mathsf{KL} \left( \mu_{X_0^i} \ \big\|\ \widehat\mu_{X_0^i} \ \Bigr|\  X_{T - t_k}^{-i}\,\right)\) is the conditional KL divergence between \(\Pr(X_0^i = \, \cdot \mid X_{T - t_k}^{-i})\) and \(\widehat \Pr(X_0^i = \, \cdot \mid X_{T - t_k}^{-i})\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:49:17.491003+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e7a3f42828737e8f4663b130983e16c4febc3e3ff1b5fa36ab496f701c8f8c2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 (Triangular dependence of $\Gamma$ and $d\Gamma$) of arXiv:2605.28677, 'Weak universality for stochastic reaction-diffusion models\\ with long-range correlated no'] ~
