then, whenever $\boldsymbol i,\boldsymbol j\ne\boldsymbol0$,
$\boldsymbol i\ne\boldsymbol j$, and the coefficients
\begin{align*}
a_{\boldsymbol i\boldsymbol j}
&=\det(\boldsymbol i,\boldsymbol j)
\bigl(|\boldsymbol i-\boldsymbol j|^{-2}-|\boldsymbol j|^{-2}\bigr),\\
b_{\boldsymbol i\boldsymbol j}
&=\det(\boldsymbol i,\boldsymbol j)
\bigl(|\boldsymbol i-\boldsymbol j|^{-2}-|\boldsymbol i|^{-2}\bigr)
\end{align*}
are both nonzero, the operator
\begin{align*}
R_{\boldsymbol i,\boldsymbol j}
=a_{\boldsymbol i\boldsymbol j}E_{\boldsymbol i,\boldsymbol j}
-b_{\boldsymbol i\boldsymbol j}E_{-\boldsymbol j,-\boldsymbol i}
\end{align*}
is a limit of elements of $\mathfrak L$ in
$\mathcal B(H^1,L^2)$.  Consequently,
\begin{align}
\langle\beta,R_{\boldsymbol i,\boldsymbol j}\rho\rangle=0.
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:01:54.290758+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e8bd2505ca49ba30c1333425676612e53ee96af854991cda116d8493b6202fc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:ergodicity of upper of arXiv:2411.02030, 'Finite ergodic components for upper probabilities'] Let $(\Omega,\mathcal{F},V,T)$ be an UPPS. Then the following two statements are equivalent:
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item [(i)]$V$ is of finite ergodic components;
		\medskip
		\item [(ii)] there exist  $Q_1,\ldots,Q_n\in\mathcal{ M}(T)\cap\operatorname{core}(V)$ and $A_1,\ldots,A_n\in\mathcal{I}$ satisfying that  $\Omega=\cup_{j=1}^nA_j$, $Q_j(A_j)=1$, and $A_j\cap A_k=\emptyset$ when $j\neq k$ such that for any $B,C\in \mathcal{F}$,
		\begin{equation}
			\lim_{N\to\infty}\int\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=0}^{N-1} 1_B\cdot(1_C\circ T^i)dV=\sum_{j=1}^nQ_j(C)(V(\cup_{k=0}^jA_k\cap B)-V(\cup_{k=0}^{j-1}A_k\cap B)),
		\end{equation}
		where $A_0=\emptyset$.
	\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:43:18.803238+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e8cc49a43cdd2a5193f6c113b03edac8c576223a2ac70fe55d24a4fe73119de","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Conj index of arXiv:2609.02409, 'Membranes and Maps'] The constant-map contribution to the equivariant Gromov--Witten theory of $Z$ is given by
    \begin{equation}

        \exp\Big( 2 \, \GWargs{Z}{\mathsf{T}}{0} \Big)
        \sim
        \Exp\Big(
            \chi_{\mathsf{T}}\big(
                Z, T_{Z}^\vee - T_{Z}
            \big)
        \Big) \,.
    \end{equation}
    Here $\Exp$ denotes the plethystic exponential, and the symbol $\sim$ means that the logarithms of both sides have the same $\mathrm{o}(1)$ tail in their asymptotic expansions. (Stated as a conjecture by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.223451+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e918bc7c7c41d9335aeab2a863c1c1d867ad615ecee5f30121f1d1aaf762314","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 9 of arXiv:2607.17943, 'Coadjoint averaging and cross-scale fluxes in a fast-slow stochastic Euler-Arnold system o'] \emph{(Instantaneous Flux)}
We define the \emph{instantaneous flux} across the
shell level $K$ via the energy and enstrophy rates carried by the nonlinear dynamics \emph{(\ref{Eq:EulerArnoldZeitlinTruncated})}, i.e. 
\begin{equation}
\Pi_\mathcal{E}(K; \Omega)=-[D\mathcal{E}_{\leq K}(\Omega)]([\Psi, \Omega]) \ , \ 
\Pi_\mathcal{Z}(K; \Omega)=-[D\mathcal{Z}_{\leq K}(\Omega)]([\Psi, \Omega]) \ , \end{equation}
where $[DF(\Omega)](\Theta)=\left.\dfrac{d}{ds}\right|_{s=0} F(\Omega+s\Theta)$ is the Fr\'{e}chet derivative of $F: \su(N)\rightarrow \mathbb{R}$ at $\Omega\in \su(N)$ in the direction $\Theta \in \su(N)$; $\Psi = -A^{-1}\Omega$ and $A$ is defined in \emph{(\ref{Eq:InertiaOperatorZeitlinCase})} and the sign convention is chosen so that a positive flux
corresponds to a net transfer of energy or enstrophy from the low modes
$|k|\leq K$ to the complementary modes $|k|>K$, similar as in \emph{(\ref{Eq:Kraichnan2dTurbulence:EnergyFlux})}, \emph{(\ref{Eq:Kraichnan2dTurbulence:EnstrophyFlux})}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:57:28.704743+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e930071c0b2d05f71afaa9eb91b055af1fa591581e393edc7985270e71cc2f5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 27 of arXiv:2609.01128, 'Nonabelian Chabauty for the Thrice-punctured Line over Cyclotomic Fields'] Let $K=\bQ(\zeta_8)$ and $S=\left\{(1-\zeta_8)\right\}$. If $c_{\chi_i},c_{\kappa_i},c_{\mu_i}\ne 0$ for $i=1,2$ and $c_{\tau_\alpha\tau_\beta}\ne 0$, the depth-4 polylogarithmic Chabauty--Kim locus $X(\cO_K\otimes \bZ_p)_{S,\PL,4}$ is the solution set of the following equations in addition to \eqref{eq:keyeq} and \eqref{eq:depth3} (with the coordinates $(X_i,Y_i,Z_i,W_i,V_i)=(\log(z_i),L_1(z_i),L_2(z_i),L_3(z_i),L_4(z_i))$ for $i=1,2,3,4$):
\begin{equation}

\left\{
\begin{aligned}
& V_{1}+V_{2}+V_{3}+V_{4} = c_{4,1} (X_{1}+X_{3})(W_{1}+W_{2}+W_{3}+W_{4})  \\
& \quad + c_{4,2} (X_{1}-X_{3})(W_{1}+W_{2}-W_{3}-W_{4}) + c_{4,3} (X_{1}-X_{3})(X_{1}+X_{3})(Z_{1}+Z_{2})  \\[4pt]
& V_{1}+V_{2}-V_{3}-V_{4} = c_{4,4} (X_{1}-X_{3})(W_{1}+W_{2}+W_{3}+W_{4})  \\
& \quad + c_{4,5} (X_{1}+X_{3})(W_{1}+W_{2}-W_{3}-W_{4}) \\ &\quad+ c_{4,6} (X_{1}-X_{3})^{2}(Z_{1}+Z_{2}) + c_{4,7} (X_{1}+X_{3})^{2}(Z_{1}+Z_{2}) 
\end{aligned}
\right.
\end{equation}
where
\begin{gather}
c_{4,1} = \frac{c_{\tau_\alpha \kappa_1}}{2c_{\tau_\alpha} c_{\kappa_1} }, \quad
c_{4,2} = \frac{c_{\tau_\beta \kappa_2}}{2c_{\tau_\beta}c_{\kappa_2}}, \quad
c_{4,3} = \frac{c_{\tau_\beta\tau_\alpha\tau_\alpha\tau_\beta}}{2 c_{\tau_\alpha\tau_\beta} c_{\tau_\alpha} c_{\tau_\beta}}, \\
c_{4,4} = \frac{c_{\tau_\beta \kappa_1}}{2 c_{\tau_\beta} c_{\kappa_1}}, \quad
c_{4,5} = \frac{c_{\tau_\alpha \kappa_2}}{2 c_{\tau_\alpha} c_{\kappa_2}}, \quad
c_{4,6} = \frac{c_{\tau_\beta\tau_\beta\tau_\alpha\tau_\beta}}{2 c_{\tau_\alpha\tau_\beta} c_{\tau_\beta}^2},\quad 
c_{4,7} = \frac{c_{\tau_\alpha\tau_\alpha\tau_\alpha\tau_\beta}}{2 c_{\tau_\alpha\tau_\beta} c_{\tau_\alpha}^2}.
\end{gather} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:42:47.758946+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e96a6d095e4462dd01fef01a5d2d45ca405bdc21a7db545fb200754ceb83b4d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 22 of arXiv:2604.11921, 'Replica symmetry up to the de Almeida--Thouless line in the Sherrington--Kirkpatrick model'] \label[proposition]{prop:G-min}
