{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.077927+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e9b6bd6d0c8d222f15776fe00694f6a0e8ab0b847c6cd45abf715fc77cdb672","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma le:partial-fourier of arXiv:2411.12192, 'Sample path properties and small ball probabilities for stochastic fractional diffusion eq'] Recall that the fundamental solution $p(t,x)$ is given in (equation e:de-ptx of the paper). For all $t > s$, we have
  \begin{equation}
    \mathcal{F}\left[\frac{\partial}{\partial t} p(t-s,x-\cdot)\right](\xi)= \frac{\partial}{\partial t} \mathcal{F} p(t-s,x-\cdot)(\xi),
  \end{equation}
   and  if we assume $\alpha>1$, we also have
  \begin{equation}
    \mathcal{F}\left[\frac{\partial}{\partial x_i} p(t-s,x-\cdot)\right](\xi)= \frac{\partial}{\partial x_i} \mathcal{F} p(t-s,x-\cdot)(\xi),\text{ for all $i=1,\dots, d$.}
  \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.606531+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e9b9a6b1f9c74eddd921c180179126392cb9be6d885ebe67dc6f4e5e95c5247","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2607.08129, '2607.08129'] For $\rho\in(0,1/4)$, let $N_m=\lfloor(1+\rho)^m\rfloor$.  Then, on an event of probability one,
