{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:20:15.584062+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9ebad29170ef56e0988370aa14f6bea985f83cc18c6cdeaa9ce184c1a6ae8a67","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thmIntroProfile of arXiv:2609.00777, 'Universal murmuration and Hecke augmentation'] There is a single continuous function $G:(0,\infty)\to\mathbb R$ with the following property.
For every fixed integer $k\geq1$, let $X$, $Y$, and the prime $P$ tend to infinity while $P^k/X$ remains in a fixed compact subset of $(0,\infty)$.
For $k\geq2$, assume the short-window and growth conditions of Theorem~(thm:scaled-murmuration of the paper); for $k=1$, assume the conditions of Zubrilina~[Zubrilina2025].
Then, for normalized weight $2$ newforms of squarefree level in $[X,X+Y]$ with trivial nebentypus,
\begin{equation*}
\sqrt X\,
\mathbb E_{X,Y}
\bigl[\varepsilon(f)\lambda_{\operatorname{sym}^k f}(P)\bigr]
=
G\left(\frac{P^k}{X}\right)+o_k(1),
\end{equation*}
locally uniformly in $P^k/X$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.328840+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9ebc93a427e8d0d6589ed8a8d445faeccfc8c7d3a442e8c1a027e459464815c1","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:oriented_cone of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] Let $\mathbb G$ be a Carnot group and let $\mathbb H,\mathbb K$ be two
homogeneous subgroups of $\mathbb G$. We say that $\mathbb H$ and
$\mathbb K$ are \emph{complementary} if
\begin{align*}
\mathbb H\cap\mathbb K=\{e\}, \quad \mbox{and} \quad \mathbb G=\mathbb H\mathbb K.
\end{align*}
Assume moreover that $\mathbb K$ is a one-dimensional horizontal homogeneous
subgroup. Thus
\begin{align*}
\mathbb K=\exp(\mathbb RX)
\end{align*}
for some nonzero $X\in V_1$. Set
\begin{align*}
\mathbb K^+:=\{\exp(tX):t\geqslant0\}.
\end{align*}
For $p\in\mathbb G$ and $\beta,\rho>0$, we define the
\emph{oriented intrinsic cone} associated with the decomposition
$\mathbb G=\mathbb H\mathbb K$ by
\begin{align*}
\mathcal C_p^+(\beta,\rho;\mathbb H,\mathbb K)
:=
p\left\{
hk\in\mathbb H\mathbb K:
k\in\mathbb K^+,\ 
\|h\|\leqslant\beta\|k\|,\ 
\|k\|<\rho
\right\}.
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:32.010192+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9ebf9699f3752d758f398ed3998e64220f1112aa2a0b739b439afc2a7d7a4353","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 3 of arXiv:2512.02855, 'Loewner--Kufarev entropy and large deviations of the Hastings--Levitov model'] The maps $\Phi_n$ satisfy an LDP in $\Sigma'_T$ equipped with the topology of uniform convergence on compact subsets of $\Delta$, with rate $ 4/\varepsilon^2$, as $\varepsilon \to 0$, and good rate function given by
    \begin{equation}
    \cH^*_T(\Phi) = \inf_{\rho}\cH(\rho),
    \end{equation}
    where $e^T$ is the capacity of $K=\hat{\mathbb{C}} \smallsetminus \Phi(\Delta)$, and the infimum is over driving measures generating $\Phi$ via the Loewner--Kufarev equation on $[0,T]$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.356367+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9ebf97f297b27f794f1b611c08ac1c00fcbe6c37913844a10d7dff97810ee7d8","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition MSSAdaption_general of arXiv:2412.01635, 'On the Weak Convergence of the Function-Indexed Sequential Empirical Process and its Smoot'] Let $\nu \geq 1$, $\Psi \neq \emptyset$ and $W_1,...,W_n: \Omega \to \ell^\infty(\Psi)$ be arbitrary processes. If there exist $\alpha > 1$ and $g: \{1,...,n\}^2 \to \mathbb R$ which fulfill
	\begin{equation}
		\mathrm E^*\left\{ \norm{S_{i,j}^W}_\Psi^\nu \right\} \leq g^{\alpha}(i,j)
	\end{equation}
	for all $1 \leq i \leq j \leq n,$ and if it holds
	\begin{align*}
		\mathrm{(i')}&:~ g(i,j) \geq 0, \text{ for all } (i,j) \in \{1,...,n\}^2, \nonumber\\
		\mathrm{(ii')}&:~ g(i,j) \leq g(i,j+1), \text{ for all } 1 \leq i \leq j \leq n-1, \nonumber \\
		\mathrm{(iii')}&:~ g(i,j) + g(j+1,k) \leq Q g(i,k), \text{ for all } 1 \leq i \leq j < k \leq n, \nonumber
	\end{align*}
	for some $Q \in [1,2^{(\alpha-1)/\alpha})$, then there exists a constant $A$ that only depends on $\alpha, \nu,$ and $Q$ such that
	\begin{equation}
		\mathrm E^* \left\{\norm{M_{1,n}^W}_\Psi^\nu \right\} \leq A g^{\alpha}(1,n).
	\end{equation}
	One may take
	\begin{equation*}
		A = \left(1 - \frac{Q^{\alpha / \nu}}{2^{(\alpha - 1)/ \nu}} \right)^{-\nu}.
	\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:35:04.203016+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9ec0193043619893e5a9f00961d42823d9208e8ded70fff3921f652064406d68","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 12 (Rigidity \cite{GeRCP}) of arXiv:2608.03575, '2608.03575'] Let $(G,\Theta)$ be an ADT that satisfies ($Z_2$) and ($Z_4$). Let $\mathcal{P}$ and $\mathcal{P}'$ be two RCPs that realize $(G,\Theta)$. 
