{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:48:24.304130+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9eec7302ed562e51fa39f7d5d3b5b5024b3be4c2a85631051b8361af81df636f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma couplings for APCRW of arXiv:2605.26869, 'Law of Large Numbers for a random walk on dynamic environments with drift'] Let $K> 1$ such that $J \subseteq (K^{-1}, K)$, $\rho \in (K^{-1}, K)$, $\varepsilon \in (0, (K-\rho) \wedge \rho\wedge 1$, and $H, \ell, t \in \mathbb{N}$ be such that $\Cr{lower bound for t in sltc}\ell^2 < t < H/2$ and $(\rho + 3 \varepsilon/2)(t^{-1}\log t)^{1/2}\ell < \Cr{upper bound on t with epsilon in sltc}\varepsilon/4$.
Let $\eta_0, \eta'_0 \in \Sigma$ be such that for every interval $I \subseteq [0,H]$ of length $\ell$, we have that $\eta_0(I) \geq (\rho + 3\varepsilon/4)\ell$ and $\eta'_0(I) \leq (\rho + \varepsilon/4)\ell$. 
We then have a coupling $\mathbb{Q}$ of $\eta$ and $\eta'$ such that
\begin{equation}
    \mathbb{Q} \left( \eta'_t|_{[t, H-t]} \preccurlyeq \eta_t|_{[t, H-t]} \right)
    \geq 1 - 4H \exp \left( -\Cr{prob bound for G in sltc} (\rho + \varepsilon)^{-1} \varepsilon^2 \sqrt{t}/4 \right).
\end{equation}

We then also have that condition (pe:couplings of the paper) holds for the APCRW when $\nu = 1$. 
Additionally, $\mathbb{Q}$ is local, meaning that $(\eta_t, \eta'_t)|_{[t, H-t]}$ depends only on the initial conditions $(\eta_t, \eta'_t)|_{[0, H]}$.","status":"unverified"}

