{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:21:06.857871+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9f0cabac1be92f88ec82fcc79864c2f8cf761de294984adf0657d6dcb7f9e505","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2608.21063, '\textbf{Non-bijective scaling limits and phase transitions of planar maps}'] Let $h:\ndR\to[0,\infty)$ be a probability density that is continuous and whose Fourier transform has no zeros. Let $E$ be a Polish space. For every $n\ge 1$ and $k\in\ndZ$, let $Z_{n,k}$ be an $E$-valued random variable.

	Let $(A_n)_{n \ge 1}$ and $(B_n)_{n\ge 1}$ be integer-valued random
	variables, independent of $(Z_{n,k})_{n \ge 1, k \in \ndZ}$. Assume that there are constants $\mu_A,\mu_B,g_A,g_B>0$ such that for every $C>0$,
	\begin{align}

		\sup_{\substack{k\in\ndZ\\ |k - \mu_A n|\le C n^{2/3}}} \left| g_A n^{2/3}\Prb{A_n=k} - h\left( \frac{\mu_A n - k}{g_A n^{2/3}} \right) \right| \to 0,
	\end{align}
	and
	\begin{align}

		\sup_{\substack{k\in\ndZ\\ |k-\mu_B n|\le C n^{2/3}}} \left| g_B n^{2/3}\Prb{B_n=k} - h\left( \frac{\mu_B n-k}{g_B n^{2/3}} \right) \right| \to 0
	\end{align}
	as $n\to\infty$. Set $r = \frac{\mu_B}{\mu_A}$. For $\theta \in \ndR$ and all sufficiently large $n$, define
	\begin{align*}
		m_n(\theta) = \left\lfloor rn + \frac{\theta}{\mu_A}n^{2/3} \right\rfloor.
	\end{align*}
	Suppose that there is an $E$-valued random variable $Z$ such that, for every fixed $\theta \in \ndR$,
	\[
	Z_{n,A_{m_n(\theta)}} \convd Z.
	\]
	Then
	\[
	Z_{n,B_n} \convd Z.
	\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:15:55.056053+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9f0ce492288d7129b703f3633d4a92d859a729415ab4408f20d343b0ec37c6ba","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition recap of arXiv:2608.29708, 'Intuitionistic and Constructive Modal Logics for Classical Modal Logicians'] The satisfaction relations $\Vdash^i$, $\Vdash^{\text{c}}$, $\Vdash^{\text{h}}$, $\Vdash^e$ are defined as follows:
  \begin{itemize}
    \item For the $\bot$ case:
          \begin{itemize}
            \item $x \not \Vdash^\bullet \bot$, for $\bullet \in \set{ i, h, e }$.
            \item $x \Vdash^{\text{c}} \bot \mathrel{\;\ratio\Longleftrightarrow\;} x \in W_\bot$, where $W_\bot$ is the set of fallible worlds.
          \end{itemize}
    \item For the $\Box$ case:
          \begin{itemize}
            \item $x \Vdash^\iota \Box \varphi \mathrel{\;\ratio\Longleftrightarrow\;} \forall x' \geq x \, \forall y' \sqsupset x' \, (y' \Vdash^\iota \varphi)$, for $\iota \in \set{ c, i, h }$.
            \item $x \Vdash^e \Box \varphi \mathrel{\;\ratio\Longleftrightarrow\;} \forall y \sqsupset x \, (y \Vdash^e \varphi)$.
          \end{itemize}
    \item For the $\Diamond$ case:
          \begin{itemize}
            \item $x \Vdash^\iota \Diamond \varphi \mathrel{\;\ratio\Longleftrightarrow\;} \forall x' \geq x \, \exists y' \sqsupset x' \, (y' \Vdash^\iota \varphi)$, for $\iota \in \set{ c, i }$.
            \item $x \Vdash^\varepsilon \Diamond \varphi \mathrel{\;\ratio\Longleftrightarrow\;} \exists y \sqsupset x \, (y \Vdash^\varepsilon \varphi)$, for $\varepsilon \in \set{ h, e }$.
          \end{itemize}
  \end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:37:09.018028+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9f0dfbb5083b007c10a7a2606d984f5f0264ac5394612b3197e6fd15e55f4618","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:hms_coupling_criterion of arXiv:2609.01697, 'Unique ergodicity of projective cocycles over the 2D stochastic Navier--Stokes equations'] Let $P$ be a Markov operator on a Polish space $\mathcal{X}$ admitting two ergodic invariant measures $\mu_1$ and $\mu_2$, and let $m_i = P^{[\infty]}\mu_i$ for $i = 1,2$ be the associated path-space measures on $\mathcal{X}^\infty$. Then $\mu_1 = \mu_2$ whenever there exists a measure $\Gamma$ on the product path space $\mathcal{X}^\infty \times \mathcal{X}^\infty$ such that:
