{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.857385+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9f3c2d285d3885712ce1249240e0f8a9f5100a5903ed5948df92eed6148a0250","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm|SumLowerFourierLevels of arXiv:2504.08935, 'Higher-Order Derivatives of First-Passage Percolation with Respect to the Environment'] For every $n\in \mathbb N$, every $k\in\mathbb N$, and every $\zeta\in(0,1)$, the following holds
