{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.789312+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9fbd0b39dc3c1325572fe2d082cb1e8623d29f4389832cbd54adab45aa63779f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition ge1 of arXiv:2411.18374, 'Drawdowns of diffusions'] For $\rho>0$ and a measurable function  $f$ with compact support  it holds a.s.
\begin{equation}

\lim_{\delta\downarrow\rho}\frac{{\bf E}_0(f(M_{\hbox {\rm tanh\,}_\delta})\,|\, {\cal F}_{\hbox {\rm tanh\,}_\rho})-f(M_{\hbox {\rm tanh\,}_\rho})}{\delta-\rho}
={\cal A}_\rho f(M_{\hbox {\rm tanh\,}_\rho}),
\end{equation}
where ${\cal A}_\rho$ is  given by
\begin{align*}
