{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.832536+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9fec0d91cf8bab752d671c47c7df84b03f4ed8439b71d49b427b7e32861ae4e6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:Feller of arXiv:2606.29352, 'Exponential Mixing for 2D Stochastic Damped Euler Equation Driven by Bounded Noise'] The operator $P_i$ is sequentially weak$\star$ Feller in $W^{1,\infty}$, that is 
