{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:25:55.420079+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a00b53e2d1ba02ae4111a1094a4ad0e9a90cc343d33d599323c56096405effd5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 of arXiv:2607.28215, 'Almost stochastic dominance via optimal transport'] For a \emph{relation} $R_\preceq \subseteq E \times E$ we also write $x \preceq y$, if $(x,y) \in R_\preceq$. The relation $\preceq$ is called a \emph{preorder} if it has the following two properties:
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
\item $x \preceq x$ for all $x \in E$,
\item  $x \preceq y$ and $y \preceq z$ implies $x \preceq z$ for all $x,y,z\in E$.
\end{enumerate}
The relation $\preceq$ is called a (partial) \emph{order relation}, if it fulfills in addition the property that
\begin{enumerate}[resume*]
\item $x \preceq y$ and $y \preceq x$ implies $x = y$.
\end{enumerate}
Given a quasi-pseudo-metric $d$ one can define a preorder $\le_d$ via
\begin{align}
x \le_d y \quad \Longleftrightarrow\quad d(x,y) = 0.
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:43:53.623673+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a00e4e7e8b46e5c6dd786bd6bcaf8bf017efdc579257404dfce6d95b6040ca82","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop stability 2 of arXiv:2512.13200, 'Martingales on a Euclidean manifold with a boundary and reflected BSDEs in non-convex doma'] { Consider any adapted processes  $f=(f_s)_{s \in [0,T]}$ and $f'=(f'_s)_{s \in [0,T]}$ with $|f|^{1/2},\,|f'|^{1/2} \in \widebar{\mathscr{H}^{\infty}}^{\ensuremath{\mathscr{B}^{2}}}$, and let Assumption (ass:brownian-case of the paper) hold.}
