{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:39:11.675307+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a03c47219f9d2b071027f4c3e9ca6f53df97242bdcb4b871502c356831ab55cf","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 8 (Short-time existence) of arXiv:2608.04937, '2608.04937'] Let $p\in(1,2]$, and let $c_p$ and $C_p$ be the constants appearing in \textnormal{Propositions \ref{22lut2} and \ref{20lut19}}, respectively. Assume that $T\le 1$, $c_pT^{\frac{1}{2}}<1$, $C_pT^{\frac{1}{2}}<1$, and
