{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.524800+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a0682033ce4bbb25d51a4975da7c8ea53039c2b00a3fe7e4250bc0dd092dcdcb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop pr:stopping_time_lower_bound of arXiv:2411.03482, 'Ergodicity of 2D singular stochastic Navier--Stokes equations'] Suppose the initial data has a decomposition $u = u_{\mathfrak{r}} + u_{\mathfrak{s}}$ with $\|u_{\mathfrak{r}}\|_{\mathcal{C}^{-\kappa}} \leq 2\alpha_0$ and $\|u_{\mathfrak{s}}\| = \lambda$\,, then for any $a > 0$ sufficiently small, we have 
