{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:15.482892+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a07f13384b9f5e1bb29f13eb4d25a100edf6bbd7407d893722db51f784dd8bf0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 36 of arXiv:2509.01797, 'Relation between Wick powers and excursion clusters of the 2D GFF'] Let $n\geq 1$
and let $\alpha_{n}>\alpha_{n-1}>\dots >\alpha_{1}>\alpha_{0}=1$.
Let $(c_{0}, c_{1}, \dots, c_{n})$
be the unique solution (Vandermonde) to the linear system
\begin{equation}

\forall k\in \{0,\dots, n-1\},
\sum_{i=0}^{n} c_{i} \alpha_{i}^{-(k+1/2)} = 0,
\qquad
\sum_{i=0}^{n} c_{i} \alpha_{i}^{-(n+1/2)} = 1.
\end{equation}
Then
\begin{equation}

\psi_{2n+1, A} = \lim_{\varepsilon \to 0} (-1)^{n}\dfrac{2^{n} n! (n+1/2)}{(2\pi)^{n}}\vert\log\varepsilon\vert^{n+1/2}
\sum_{i=0}^{n} c_{i} \ind_{\Ns_{\varepsilon^{\alpha_{i}}}(A)},
\end{equation}
with convergence in $L^{2}(d\PP,\sigma(\Phi),H^{-\eta}(\C))$ for $\eta>0$.","status":"unverified"}

