{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:24:45.970375+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a08d86a34f4d8236f1ae5f0fedbef1e436056e346164570c7602345c49d9f6f1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:R5a of arXiv:2509.17319, 'Non-directed polymers in random environments with range penalties: the high-dimensional ca'] If any one of the following conditions holds:
\begin{itemize}
\item[(1)] $\alpha\in(0,d)$ and $(\zeta,\gamma)\in R_5$ with $\gamma>\zeta+\frac{d-\alpha}{\alpha}$,
\item[(2)] $\alpha\in(0,\frac{d}{2})$ and $(\zeta,\gamma)\in R_5$ with $\gamma>\frac{d-\alpha}{\alpha}$,
\item[(3)] $\alpha\in[\frac{d}{2},d)$ and $(\zeta,\gamma)\in R_5$ with $\gamma\geq\frac{d}{2\alpha}$,
\end{itemize}
then for $\xi=\frac{1+\zeta}{2+d}$, we have the following convergence in ${\ensuremath{\mathbbm P}} $-probability
\begin{equation}
