{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:58:09.902460+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a08fb24ea412ba335d90d7eb4b798f7b22de63f1f2576ce23a9356f7be78d68d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition \(\alpha\)-H\"older rough paths of arXiv:2607.19037, 'Semiclassical analysis for Yang--Mills \\ random connections on compact surfaces'] Let \(\alpha \in (\tfrac{1}{3}, \tfrac{1}{2}]\). The space of \(\alpha\)-H\"older rough paths over \(\mathfrak{g}\), denoted by \(\mathcal{C}^\alpha([0,1],\mathfrak{g})\), consists of pairs \((W,\mathbb{W}) =: \mathbf{W}\) such that
