{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:15:09.027617+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a093491fa42123712edce92faeea2276cd39c4a9ed3c0859b65c9954d9cb1af2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:defcLrev of arXiv:2411.10829, 'Airy$_\beta$ line ensemble and its Laplace transform'] For $(\vec p, \vec\upsilon, \mathcal H)\in \mathscr L_\epsilon$, the pre-image $\mathcal L^{-1}(\vec p, \vec\upsilon, \mathcal H)$ either is empty (due to the requirement of $J_\mathrm {VI.1}=J_\mathrm {VI.2}=J_\mathrm {VI.3}=\emptyset$ for $\mathscr B_\epsilon^*$), or consists of all the $\vec r\in \mathscr B_\epsilon^*$ obtained by specifying $\mathscr{H} $ to be any function on $\llbracket 0, Q_m\rrbracket$, satisfying
\begin{itemize}
    \item $\mathscr{H}(Q_\ell)=p^0(Q_\ell)$ for each $\ell\in\llbracket 0,m \rrbracket$, and in particular $\mathscr{H}(0)=\mathscr{H}(Q_m)=0$;
    \item $|\mathscr{H}(t)-\mathscr{H}(t-1)|=1$ and $\mathscr{H}(t)\ge p^0(t)$ for each $t\in \llbracket 1, Q_m\rrbracket$;
    \item $\mathscr{H}(t)=\mathscr{H}(t-1)-1=\mathcal H(t)$ for each $t\in \llbracket Q_{\ell-1}+1, Q_\ell\rrbracket$, $p^\ell(t)\neq p^\ell(t-1)$, or $t=Q_{\ell-1}+\upsilon_\ell$ when $\upsilon_\ell\neq\varnothing$;
\end{itemize}
and specifying the set $U\subset \llbracket m+1, N\rrbracket$ with $|U|=u$, as well as the bijection $\sigma:\llbracket m+1, m+u\rrbracket \to U$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:48:17.124502+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a09ec4b97ab7e0edea62b70276895455fc42f8fcbfd04b66de8cb418ddb195c9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 3 of arXiv:2605.27818, 'Exponential decay of mass for inertial coalescing particles with Hamiltonian noise'] A function $h\in C^3(\T)$ satisfies conditions (H1), (H2) and (H3) if and only if there
exists an integer $N\geq 1$ such that
\begin{itemize}
\item[1.] $h$ has exactly $2N$ zeros $a_1<a_2<\cdots<a_{2N}$ in $\T$,
all simple;
\item[2.] $h$ has exactly $2N$ critical points $b_1,\ldots,b_{2N}$,
interlaced with the zeros of $h$,  one $b_j$ in each open interval
$(a_j,a_{j+1})$. Moreover,  at each $b_j$, we have $h(b_i)h''(b_j)< 0$;
\item[3.] on each interval $(a_j,a_{j+1})$, $h$ has constant sign and $|h|$
is concave.
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

