{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:48:17.125352+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a0aa7df349ac42f5088f11ecd240753e1c23f14bab01228b7d1ce39d04a122b4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 15 of arXiv:2605.27818, 'Exponential decay of mass for inertial coalescing particles with Hamiltonian noise'] There exist $\eta_0,\vt_0>0$,  independent of   $R_0$ and $f_0$,  and a constant $\bar\kappa>0$ such that, for
