{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:55.639715+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a0b0ca1cbf77ead773f9343f5df50aedad8e1cb20620a607804363074d95647b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 (Existence in the degenerate case) of arXiv:2605.23529, 'Generalized Bessel-Dunkl diffusions'] Let $x_0\in\Cc$. Assume \ref{ass:cont}, \ref{ass:sigma}, \ref{ass:k:dom}, and \ref{ass:face:sign}. Then there exists a filtered probability space carrying an $N$-dimensional Brownian motion $B$ and a continuous $\Cc$-valued semimartingale $X=(X_1,\ldots,X_N)$, defined up to its lifetime $\life{X}>0$, such that 
