{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:10.034169+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a0b3ce6bd3aca451462591bc74730e782e8d990751b3de24850b61678e632798","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 28 of arXiv:2506.09609, 'Schramm-Loewner evolution contains a topological Sierpi\'nski carpet when $\kappa$ is clos'] There exists a constant $C_1 = C_1(\varrho) \geq 100$ such that the following holds for all $N \geq C_1$ and any vertex sets $\{\mathcal{A}_m\}$ satisfying Conditions~\ref{condition:fractal-1} and~\ref{condition:fractal-2}, and $k \geq 0$.

    \begin{enumerate}
        \item Any self-avoiding connected path at level $k$ whose $|\cdot|_\infty$-diameter is at least $N^k$ has length at least $N^{k/2}$. 

        \item For all $L \geq N^{k/2}$, the number of self-avoiding connected paths at level $k$ with length $L$ and starting from a fixed box is at most $(C_1)^L$. Moreover, any such path consists of at least $1/2$ fraction of boxes from $\mathcal{S}_0$. 
    \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.249460+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a0b400f774f32580782298d435ae5a8d6977a2350afccc9cf3b4b3fecb1b4f91","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:diff_of_V of arXiv:2512.21159, '\textsc{From multitype branching Brownian motions\\ to branching Markov additive processes'] With the notation of Lemma (lem:property of PF of the paper), each of the functions $\theta\mapsto \lambda(\theta)$, $\vec{Y}(\theta)$ and $\vec{V}(\theta)$ is infinitely differentiable on  $(0, \bar{\theta})$. Moreover, we have 
