{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.384826+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a0b60e9c364e59eca7a1b76733ac83c7d4527cbc7ac2bda3de9fff2371830f69","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition equivalentLevyCoupling of arXiv:2509.23086, 'On Optimal Markovian Couplings of L\'evy Processes'] Let $\mu,\nu\in \Lambda(\mathbb R^d)$ and $\gamma\in \Lambda(\mathbb R^{2d})$. The following are equivalent:

    (i) $\gamma\in \Gamma^\Lambda(\mu,\nu)$;

    (ii) for all bounded measurable functions $f$ that vanish on a neighbourhood of $0$, we have
    \begin{equation}
        \int_{\mathbb R^{2d}} f(x)d\gamma(x,y)= \int_{\mathbb R^d} f(x)d\mu(x),\qquad \int_{\mathbb R^{2d}} f(y)d\gamma(x,y)=\int_{\mathbb R^d} f(y)d\nu(x);
    \end{equation}

    (iii) for all bounded twice differentiable functions $f\in C_b^2(\mathbb{R}^d)$ that vanish on a neighbourhood of $0$, (equation marg-int of the paper) holds;

    (iv) for all bounded continuous functions $f\in C_b(\mathbb{R}^d)$ that vanish on a neighbourhood of $0$, (equation marg-int of the paper) holds;

    (v) for all bounded continuous functions $f\in C_b(\mathbb R^{d})$ such that $|f(x)|\le C|x|^2$ for some $C\ge 0$, (equation marg-int of the paper) holds. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:29:27.974289+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a0b68cd9ce9498956ab02d6872f2ab41d4ba96a5ec04bebd05356d342e31bf9d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 (KL calibration--refinement bound for occupancy ratios) of arXiv:2608.24858, 'Bellman Calibration for Marginalized Importance Weighting in Offline Reinforcement Learnin'] Suppose that \(w_\pi>0\) \(\nu\)-almost surely. For every normalized
