{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:51:44.765760+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a0c87c347f12051b60542ca1ec7819d0c445e8d866b8d04de2074eed504ba16d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 2 (\cites{Hei88, NX21}) of arXiv:2608.26723, 'Extrinsic upper bounds for the harmonic mean of eigenvalues in curved manifolds'] Let $M$ be an $m(\ge 2)$-dimensional closed orientable submanifold in an $n$-dimensional Riemannian manifold $N$ of the sectional curvature $K_N \le \delta$.
	If $\delta\le 0$, we assume that $N$ is simply-connected;
	if $\delta> 0$, we assume that $M$ is contained in a convex ball of radius $\le \pi/4\sqrt{\delta}$.
	Then the first nonzero eigenvalue $\lambda_1$ of the Laplacian on $M$ satisfies
	\begin{equation}
		\lambda_1\le \frac{m}{\vol(M)}\int_M\big(\delta+|\mathbf{H}|^2\big).
	\end{equation}

	Equality holds implies that $M$ is minimally immersed in a geodesic sphere of $N$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:36:31.223555+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a0c9c0cfcd5206f10bdca8155fb2ff51bfd09ccf0453108e9e158bceccd5ea3f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 (Profile and surface speeds) of arXiv:2609.00501, 'Uniqueness of Finite-Time Varifold Limits for the M\"obius-Invariant Willmore Flow'] Between a normal-gauge Hopf profile evolution and its corresponding
MIWF trajectory, the following identity holds:
\begin{equation}

