{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:20:55.559614+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a0db8d9f5323d77cd319c9ef44991bebddf711630ff61a2865b1790dce0084ac","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:B-rho of arXiv:2411.07680, 'Energy solutions of singular SPDEs on Hilbert spaces with applications to domains with bou'] Let $\rho : H \rightarrow V$ be a bounded operator and let $v \in H$. Let
  $(e_k)_k$ be an orthonormal basis of $H$. Then the following limits exist in
  $L^2 (\mu)$ and do not depend on the specific orthonormal basis:
  \begin{equation}
    \langle {:} B^{\rho} (\eta, \eta) {:}, v \rangle_{V^{\ast}, V} := \lim_{N
    \rightarrow \infty} \sum_{k, \ell \leqslant N} (\eta (e_k) \eta (e_{\ell})
    - \delta_{k, \ell}) \langle B (\rho e_k, \rho e_{\ell}), \rho v
    \rangle_{V^{\ast}, V} 
  \end{equation}
  and, if additionally $v \in V$, the same is true for
  \begin{equation}
    \langle {:} \tilde{B}^{\rho} (\eta, \eta) {:}, v \rangle_{V^{\ast}, V} :=
    \lim_{N \rightarrow \infty} \sum_{k, \ell \leqslant N} (\eta (e_k) \eta
    (e_{\ell}) - \delta_{k, \ell}) \langle B (\rho e_k, \rho e_{\ell}), v
    \rangle_{V^{\ast}, V}.
  \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.375889+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a0deff50edfc29d239731c1db0918d3446d69f3175e45310e5d9ca0759b611c7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:viscosity of arXiv:2412.01995, 'Exciting games and Monge-Amp\`{e}re equations'] The convex value function $v:[0,1) \times \Delta \to \mathbb R$ satisfies the dynamic programming principle, i.e., for any $(t,x) \in [0,1) \times \Delta $
    \begin{align*}
v(t,x)=&\textstyle  \inf_{\mathbb Q \in \mathcal{M}_{t,x}^{win}} \inf_{\tau \in \mathcal{T}_t^1} \mathbb E_{\mathbb Q}\left[ \int_{t}^{\tau} - \log \det \Sigma_u \, du + v(\tau,X_{\tau}) \right] \\
=& \textstyle \inf_{\mathbb Q \in \mathcal{M}_{t,x}^{win}} \sup_{\tau \in \mathcal{T}_t^1} \mathbb E_{\mathbb Q}\left[ \int_{t}^{\tau} - \log \det \Sigma_u \, du + v(\tau,X_{\tau}) \right],
    \end{align*}
    where $(X_t)_{t \in [0,1]}$ is the canonical process defined on the path space, and $\mathcal{T}_t^1$ denotes the set of stopping times with respect to the canonical filtration taking values in $[t,1]$. Moreover, the value function $v(t,x)$ is a viscosity solution to (equation eq:HJB of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:17:33.996776+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a0e11fdc5f0d589723092ff68282e00aee4b52e8fbf2843e5ddcdbc53b8d6a02","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 of arXiv:2609.03403, 'Hyperpositive functions, sector bounded functions and a trace formula'] In the setting and notation of the preceding paragraph, $M_S$ is a contraction if and only if the kernel
        \begin{equation}
