{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:03:35.813348+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a0f98ff8c6d1ef048613823d3770db6be195c388ec9fd03cb62e382d02f0bd9e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:localized-to-global-comparison of arXiv:2608.22910, 'A Commutator Framework for Selective Spectral Alignment in Deep Neural Networks'] At a fixed time, let \(A_\ell(x)\) be symmetric and square-integrable,
