{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:32:58.331752+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a1086fc140f226a016ee91eb5ffc91b7dd48c9c6f073c46e6a9ab91cf35e7641","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop classical solution semilinear PDE of arXiv:2505.12127, 'Generalised principal eigenvalues and global survival of branching Markov processes'] Suppose that $g:E{\rightarrow} {\mathbb R}$ is continuous and $\tilde f:{\mathbb R}\times E{\rightarrow} {\mathbb R}_{\geq 0}$ is bounded, non-negative, locally H\"older continuous and Lipschitz in the first variable uniformly over the spatial variable, i.e. 
