{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:46:36.161406+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a10973f988a57586e708f1c9040e99df21e96b2512b3928006c253d760cd4be0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop Prop_InfinitesimalSliceUniformisers of arXiv:2609.02848, 'The universal moduli space of non-degenerate $\Z/2\Z$~harmonic spinors'] For every $({\mathbf{p}}_0,[{\mathfrak l}_0]) \in \mathbf{Dir} \times \mathbf{Ram}$
  there is a \defined{local infinitesimal uniformiser};
  that is:
  an open neighbourhood $({\mathbf{p}}_0,[{\mathfrak l}_0]) \in \mathscr{U} \subseteq \mathbf{Dir} \times \mathbf{Ram}$ and
  a tame smooth map
  \begin{align*}
    \mathscr{F}^\mathbf{Ram}|_\mathscr{U} &\to \mathrm{Vect}(X) \\
    ({\mathbf{p}},[{\mathfrak l}];v) &\mapsto \bar v = \bar v({\mathbf{p}},[{\mathfrak l}];v)
  \end{align*}
  such that:
  \begin{enumerate}
  \item

    for every $({\mathbf{p}},[{\mathfrak l}];v) \in \mathscr{F}^\mathbf{Ram}|_\mathscr{U}$
    \begin{equation*}
      ({\mathbf{p}},[{\mathfrak l}];v) \cdot \mathrm{lift}_{\mathbf{p}}^K(\bar v) \in \mathscr{F}_{{\mathbf{p}},[{\mathfrak l}]}^{\mathbf{Sl}},
    \end{equation*}
  \item

    $\bar v({\mathbf{p}},[{\mathfrak l}];-)$ is $\mathbb{R}$--linear,
    and
  \item

    for every $({\mathbf{p}},[{\mathfrak l}];v) \in \mathscr{F}^\mathbf{Ram}|_\mathscr{U}$
    \begin{equation*}
      \Abs{\bar v({\mathbf{p}},[{\mathfrak l}];v)}_{H^{k+1}} \lesssim_k \Abs{v}_{H^k}.
    \end{equation*}
  \end{enumerate}  
  Moreover,
  given a compact subset $K \subseteq X {\backslash} \mathrm{Br}({\mathfrak l})$,
  the local infinitesimal uniformiser can be chosen such that
  $\bar v({\mathbf{p}},[{\mathfrak l}];v)|_K = 0$ for every $({\mathbf{p}},[{\mathfrak l}];v) \in \mathscr{F}^\mathbf{Ram}|_\mathscr{U}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

