\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:22:21.874779+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a11d7269fdf56c522b3a4f33e6f60363409dd3cb80ebf3404a16336c1fa75664","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2411.11345, 'Real Gaussian exponential sums via a real moment map'] The \emph{mixed volume} is the unique continuous application $\MV:\mathcal{K}(V)^m\to \mathbb{R}_{\geq0}$ that is symmetric and Minkowski linear in each of its argument and that is such that for all $K_1,\ldots,K_n\in \mathcal{K}(V)$ and $t_1,\ldots,t_n\geq 0$ we have 
\begin{equation}
  \vol(t_1K_1+\cdots+t_n K_n)=\sum_{i_1,\ldots,i_m=1}^nt_{i_1}\cdots t_{i_m}\MV(K_{i_1},\ldots,K_{i_m}).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:31:20.586797+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a11e095dfa3eea472c97c58733bda067518f44d1a07370c7371ff1cf852a2a29","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 3 (Riemann--Liouville fractional integral) of arXiv:2608.25164, 'A time-fractional Kalman filter'] For $\alpha>0$, the fractional integral of a locally integrable function $f$
