{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.330282+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a13098794cd978f670b88edf872bfd3181df20b499e6f7ca3219c94c5b4e1281","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition eq:martdecomp of arXiv:2606.01937, 'Stationary fluctuations for an exclusion process with mass and energy conservation'] For any $i\in \{1,2\}$, any test function $\varphi\in \mathscr{S}(\mathbb{R} )$ and any $t\in [0,T]$, the martingale $\mathcal{M}^{N,i}$ decomposes as
    \begin{equation}
        \mathcal{M}_t^{N,i}(\varphi ) = \mathcal{Z}_t^{N,i}(\varphi )-\mathcal{Z}_0^{N,i}(\varphi ) - \mathcal{I}_t^{N,i}(\varphi ) - \Lambda_t^{N,i} (\varphi ) + E^{N,i}_t(\varphi)
    \end{equation}
    where
    \begin{align}
        & \mathcal{I}_t^{N,i}(\varphi ) = (\kappa -1)N^{a-2}\int_0^t \mathcal{Z}_s^{N,i}(\Delta_N\varphi )\,\mathrm{d} s, \\
        & \Lambda_t^{N,i} (\varphi ) = N^{a-\gamma -\frac32} \int_0^t \sum_{x\in\mathbb{Z}} \big( \mathfrak{c}_i\tilde{h}_x^p(s)+\tilde{h}_x^e(s)\big) \nabla_NT_{v_iN^{a-1}s}\varphi\Big( \frac xN\Big)\,\mathrm{d} s, 
    \end{align}
    and $E_t^{N,i}(\varphi )$ is the remainder term coming from the replacement of the discrete gradient by its continuous counterpart, whose $L^2$-norm is of order $O(N^{2a-2\gamma -4})$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:43:43.363998+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a1314a455b98255ecd73e462e1629e12a0a14a01170992ef00ff9bb4b5e12226","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop p.gmc.coupling of arXiv:2507.16056, 'Conditional GMC within the stochastic heat flow'] There exists a coupling of the family $(M^{\theta}_{[s,t]})_{ \theta\in\mathbb{R}}$ such that, with $\mathscr{H}_{\theta}:=\sigma(M^{\phi}_{[s,t]}\,|\,\phi\leq\theta)$ denoting its canonical filtration,
\begin{align}

