{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:46:12.274921+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a15dc21c10254e4d508dbf9ecc0149a5eed1646e72849c3c493e95f4245897d0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 17 (Minimal Cholesky factor) of arXiv:2604.22159, 'Adapted optimal transport between filtered Gaussian processes'] Let $n \geq 1$ and $A \in \mathscr{S}_+(n)$. Then there exists a unique $L \in \mathscr{L}_+(n)$ with the following properties:
