then
\begin{equation}
    \lim_{t\downarrow 0}\frac{\mathbb{P}^{x_1}[\sigma_{B_1}\leq t]}{\mathbb{P}^{x_2}[\sigma_{B_2}\leq t]}=0. 
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:37:08.321352+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a17fb770955d793b0cb58d822469578443be8dc756c8562c9cf60ea9f9b5f663","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:barrier of arXiv:2608.31071, 'Global smooth solutions to the inhomogeneous Landau--Fermi--Dirac equation'] For any $m > 2$ and $\Lambda > 0$, define $b(v)$ via (equation defn:barrier of the paper). Suppose that $f \in C^2(\mathbb R^3)$ satisfies 
