{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:48:24.521537+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a1850abda30d6e27c9703d2b77b9b1bacf1fbef179da63d3c6e4742eabc3efca","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary eq:curve_evolution of arXiv:2512.17808, 'Zeros of polynomial powers under the heat flow'] Let us consider the setting of Corollary (cor:density of the paper), i.e.~let $D\subset \mathbb{C}\setminus B$ be a fixed simply connected domain such that $\Gamma_{i,j}^D(t)=\{z\in D:G(z,u_t^i(z))=G(z,u_t^j(z))\}\neq \emptyset$ for exactly one pair $1\leq i <j \leq d+1$, where $\Gamma_{i,j}^D(t)$  is a real analytic curve that separates $D=D_i\cup D_j\cup \Gamma_{i,j}^D(t)$ into two simply connected open domains $D_i$ and $D_j$ at time $t=t_0$. Further, for $z\in D$ we denote the two Stieltjes branches as $m_t^i(z)=\frac{z-u_t^i(z)}{t}$ and $m_t^j(z)=\frac{z-u_t^j(z)}{t}$ respectively. Then, for each $t_0$ such that $z(t_0)\in\Gamma_{i,j}^D(t_0)$ there exists $\varepsilon>0$ such that  \begin{align}
		\partial_t z(t)=\frac{m_t^i(z(t))+m_t^j(z(t))}2,\quad t\in[t_0-\varepsilon,t_0+\varepsilon],
		\end{align} 
with initial datum $z(t_0)$, has a unique solution that satisfies $z(t)\in\Gamma_{i,j}^D(t)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-09-07T12:18:10.807815+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a18aaf5d59e8afaa26db26f0e5315095e38f77556cf539cd77b56e3233bec600","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2512.19517, 'Spiking and Resetting'] For any $s>0$ and $\eta>0$, we have that 
