{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:36:31.229448+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a1df1cf970a7292c73c66711fe361a6ee6ab4b96f5364ffe433ff998ab3ade88","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2609.00537, 'Explicit Exponential Sum Estimates and Approximate Functional Equations for the Zeta Funct'] Let $x,y\in\R$ with $1\leq y< N+1$, $x\notin\Z$,  and let $N$ be a non-negative integer. Then
    \begin{align}
    & 
    \bigg|  \sum_{ \nu > N} \frac{e^{-2\pi i \nu x}}{\nu(\nu-y) }\bigg|  \leq Z_0(N,x,y) =  
   \frac{1}{y|\sin(\pi x)|} \left( \frac{1}{N+1-y} + \frac{1}{N+1} \right)
        ;\\
     & 
     \bigg| \sum_{ \nu=1}^{\infty} \frac{e^{-2\pi i \nu x}}{\nu(\nu+y) }\bigg|  \leq Z_1(x,y) =     
     \frac{1}{y|\sin(\pi x)|} \left( 1+\frac{1}{1+y} \right).
    \end{align}
    In the special case where $x\in\Z+\frac{1}{2}$ and $N+1-y \geq \frac{1}{2}$, the definitions can be replaced by the stronger estimates
    \begin{equation}
        \begin{split}
            &Z_0(N,x,y) =  \frac{1}{y}  \bigg| \frac{\Gamma'}{\Gamma}(N+1-y) - \frac{\Gamma'}{\Gamma}\left(\frac{N+2-y}{2}\right) - \log 2  \bigg|   +\frac{1}{y(N+1)} \leq \frac{1}{y}\left(\frac{\pi}{2} + \frac{1}{N+1} \right); 
\\
        &Z_1(x,y) =     
        \frac{\log 2}{y} + \frac{3}{2y(y+1)};
    \\%&
        \end{split}
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

