{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:31:14.338956+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a20a4aebf04f59c3c74f4a963ba66cd8403386c0fabfa1e124eb68789fb2d2bf","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition MBBM exceeding particles num for a subset of arXiv:2606.19207, 'Extrema of cooling branching Brownian motion and related Gaussian fields'] Let $\{\xi_\varepsilon^{\alpha,z}(t)\colon t\geq0,\ z\in V_\varepsilon\}$ be the MBBM defined in (equation eqM: MBBM of the paper), and recall $A_\alpha(\cdot)$ from (equation eqIntroduction: A(t) of the paper). Fix $T_r\geq s_0$, with $s_0$ as in Lemma~(lemma: covariance estimate for MBBM of the paper), and assume that $T_r=N_r\log 2$ for some $N_r\in\mathbb{Z}_+$. Then there exist constants $C,c>0$ and $T_*,\lambda_*>0$ such that, for every $N\in\mathbb{Z}_+$ with $T:=N\log 2\geq T_*$ and $\varepsilon:=2^{-N}$, every subset $\Lambda\subset V_\varepsilon$, and every $\lambda\geq\lambda_*$,
	\begin{equation}
		\mathbb{P}\Bigl(
		\max_{z\in\Lambda}\xi_\varepsilon^{\alpha,z}(T+T_r)
		\geq A_\alpha(T+T_r)+\lambda-n
		\Bigr)
		\leq Ce^{-c(\lambda-n)},
		\qquad n\in\mathbb{Z}_+,\quad n\leq\lambda,
	\end{equation}
	and
	\begin{equation}
		\begin{aligned}
			&\mathbb{P}\Bigl(
			\max_{z\in\Lambda}\xi_\varepsilon^{\alpha,z}(T+T_r)
			\geq A_\alpha(T+T_r)+\lambda-n
			\Bigr)\\
			&\quad\leq
			Ce^{-c(\lambda+n)}
			+C\lvert\Lambda\rvert
			\exp\bigl\{-d(T+T_r)-c\lambda+c(T+T_r)^\alpha(n+1)\bigr\},
			\qquad n\in\mathbb{Z}_+.
		\end{aligned}
	\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.597491+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a20cf1cd559a93c01612a9d2fe17dbaf3c21ac8cdad053a8fd6422311a79222c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 16 of arXiv:2607.07283, 'Multi-time Markov renewal chains and stratified renewal theorems'] The regenerative increment is called full-rank if $\mathcal L$ has rank $d$. If $\mathcal L$ is full-rank, its covolume is

\begin{equation*}
h_{\mathcal L}=|\Z^d/\mathcal L|.
\end{equation*}

The renewal lattice generated by complete cycles is

\begin{equation*}
\mathcal L_* = \mathcal L+\Z y_0,
\end{equation*}

and, when $\mathcal L$ is full-rank, its covolume is

\begin{equation*}
h_* = |\Z^d/\mathcal L_*|.
\end{equation*}

The regenerative increment is called renewal-aperiodic if $\mathcal L_*=\Z^d$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:45:05.498301+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a20cf4de93c53206c52bd14e13a3d4d6eafbfcade89626c5524924a9dc4cdcbd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2608.05039, 'A large deviation principle for a class of weighted means of random variables which conver'] Assume that $\beta_n \to 0$. Then
