{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:25:44.955306+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a220538ac01897e31b5d360dc93e18f3b6f9f7bbbadaf66b528d6f7a5719c38f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Teo 1 of arXiv:2605.11264, 'Uniform sampling of multitype continuous-time Bienaym\'e-Galton-Watson trees'] For any $k\geq 1$, $T\in \re_+$,  $r\in [d]$, we have
\begin{equation}
	\begin{split}
\mathbb{P}^{(k)}_{unif,T,r}&\paren{\Delta_T(n)}\\
&= \frac{1}{(k-1)!}\frac{1}{\mathbb{P}_{r}\paren{\ N_T\geq k}}\int_0^\infty(e^\phi-1)^{k-1}\Q^{(k),\phi\vec{1}}_{T,r}(\Delta_T(n))\E_{r}\left[N^{\floor{k}}_Te^{-\phi\vec{1}\cdot \bo Z_T}\right]{\rm d}\phi,
\end{split}
\end{equation}
where
\[
\begin{split}
\Q^{(k),\phi\vec{1}}_{T,r}(\Delta_T(n))&= \prod_{h=1}^n\prod_{m=1}^d\E_{m}\left[e^{-\phi\vec{1} \cdot \bo Z_{T-t_h}}\right]^{\ell_{h,m} -g_{h,m}}p_{i_h}(\bm \ell_{h})\bm \ell_{h}^{\floor{\bo g_h}}\\
		&\hspace{-1.5cm}  \times 
		\prod_{h=0}^{n-1}\prod_{m=1}^d\prod_{\substack{ q\leq g_{h,m}:\\ k_{v(h,m,q)}\geq 2}}\E_{m}\left[Z^{(c(v(h,m,q)))}_{t_{v(h,m,q)}-t_h} \prod_{j=1}^d\E_{j}\left[e^{-\phi\vec{1}\cdot \bo Z_{T-t_{v(h,m,q)}}}\right]^{ Z^{(j)}_{t_{v(h,m,q)}-t_h}-\delta_{c(v(h,m,q)),j}}\right]\\
	& \hspace{1.5cm} \times
	\frac{\prod_{h=1}^{n}\prod_{m=1}^{d}\E_{m}\left[N_{T-t_{h}}e^{-\phi\vec{1} \cdot \bo Z_{T-t_{h}}}\right]
		^{\#\{ q\leq g_{h,m}:k_{v(h,m,q)}=1\}}
	}{\E_{r}\left[N_T(N_T-1)\cdots(N_T-k+1)e^{-\phi\vec{1}\cdot \bo Z_{T}}\right]} \prod_{h=1}^n\alpha_{i_{h}} {\rm d}t_h,
	\end{split}
\]
 $t_{v(h,m,q)}$ and $c(v(h,m,q))$ are the spine splitting times  and type associated to the vertex $v(h,m,q)$.  When  $h=0$, we observe that $v(0)=\emptyset$, $g_{0,m}=\delta_{r,m}$ and $v(0, r, 1)=v(1)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:01:54.386778+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2245f7c32e18e4e3eb3791398847e30addf4d97a71d35485a8e6ef7fedafca0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lap_decroit of arXiv:2411.02156, 'Martin boundary of a degenerate Reflected Brownian Motion in a wedge'] Suppose (equation drift of the paper) to (equation simple of the paper).
