{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.117484+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a226e2a3e91a24a70743430195a55d19bda3daf8d04638e6b306d0d98b90c729","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:green of arXiv:2608.17022, 'Sharp hypocoercive convergence estimates for underdamped Langevin dynamics with specular r'] Let $\Omega\subset\mathbb{R}^d$ be a bounded Lipschitz domain and $U\in C^1(\overline\Omega)$, and write $Z_x:=\int_\Omega e^{-U}\mathrm{d} x$. For all $a\in H^1(\Omega)$ and $b\in H^2(\Omega)$,
