{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:12:46.882198+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a242295d860fc43c6fc4893137c8ba9bd64638e32aad704c00afd22c580f3b7e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition zerohypdef of arXiv:2608.09856, '\bf Mass erasure on measured $\bbR$-trees,\\ applications to L\'evy forests'] A metric space $(S, d)$ is called a \textit{$0$-hyperbolic space} if for all $\sigma_1, \sigma_2, \sigma_3, \sigma_4 \! \in \!  S$,  
