{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:47:53.349855+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a24a2440f05e97395161a4ea969a3d4489ca2cb9494ede2c0160b54f600df101","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 23 of arXiv:2607.15872, 'Existence of $q$-Bass martingales in the semidiscrete setting'] Let $h\in\RR^{n-1}_{\ge 0}$, $\nu\in\Prob_1(\RR)$, $q\in \Prob(\RR)$, such that $q \ll \lambda$ and  Assumptions \ref{ass:A1}--\ref{ass:A2} hold. Let $f$ be the corresponding $n$-atomic $q$-Bass map and fix $i \in \{1, \dots, n-1\}$. 
