{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.235472+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a28433c2112e574a0288b6a610de1351ce0a76718dcd5ac1cb17457de4456607","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 of arXiv:2604.14427, 'A criterion for proving entropy chaos on path space'] (see, e.g., \cite{CarlenCD,Carlen:162610})    
  The space of \emph{proper infinitesimal characteristics} is the set of pairs $(\rho(t),v(t))$,
  with $\rho: \RR^d \times \RR_+\rightarrow \RR_+$, $v:\RR^d\times \RR_+\rightarrow\RR^d$ functions
  satisfying the following properties:
  a \textit{continuity equation} in weak form,
  \begin{equation} 
    \int_{\R^d}f(x,T)\rho(x,T)dx-\int_{\R^d}f(x,0)\rho(x,0)dx=\int_0^T\int_{\R^d}(v(t)\cdot\nabla
    f)\rho(x,t)dx,
  \end{equation}
  and a \textit{finite energy condition},
  \begin{equation}
    \int_0^T\int_{\R^d} (|u(x,t)|^2+|v(x,t)|^2){\rho}(x,t)\dd x\dd t
    <+\infty,
  \end{equation}
  \noindent  with $u(x,t)=\frac{\nabla \rho(x,t)}{2\rho(x,t)}$, for all $T\geq 0$ and all $f\in
  C_0^{\infty}(\R^{d+1})$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:48:35.811450+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a287b643720aca336e0dad666221371e2a39f723f2ba3e429dcacbcaba118cef","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:sol of arXiv:2411.09482, 'Anomalous Regularization in Kazantsev-Kraichnan Model'] Fix $s\in (0,d/2)$ and $\alpha\in (0,1)$. An $\dot{H}^{-s}$-valued, probabilistically weak solution to (equation eq:KK of the paper) is a tuple $(\Omega,\mathcal{A},(\mathcal{F}_t)_t,\mathbb{P},W^\mathcal{K},M)$, where $(\Omega,\mathcal{A},(\mathcal{F}_t)_t,\mathbb{P})$ is a filtered probability space (satisfying the standard assumption), $W^\mathcal{K}$ is a $(\mathcal{F}_t)_t$-adapted Wiener process with covariance function $Q$ (given in (equation eq:Q_spectrum of the paper)), and $M$ is an $\dot{H}^{-s}_{\div}$-valued, $(\mathcal{F}_t)_t$-progressively measurable process $M$ such that $M\in L^2_t(\dot{H}^{-s}_{\div})\cap C_t(H^{-s-2}_{\div})$ $\mathbb{P}$-a.s.\ and
