{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:31:20.577922+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2951f92b2b459291a6393de1b37e768327d134096943b0f534fabc1dec259a2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 10 of arXiv:2608.25094, 'Noising-Denoising by Large Temperature Schr\"{o}dinger Bridges'] Let $(M,g)$ be either (1) $\mathbb{R}^{d}$ with \eqref{eq:OU} reference process, or (2) a compact manifold with reference process \eqref{eq:reference-process-intro} satisfying $U \in C^2(M)$. Let $\mu,\nu \in \cP_2(M)$ satisfy Assumption \ref{assumption}. The following limit holds
