{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:54:28.041903+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a297cc377f8d185923ba2cadb99a248105123551ffd5f937a4bb20d939ce6a60","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma covering_bound of arXiv:2608.12056, 'Deviation inequalities for U-processes of growing order, with applications to half-space d'] Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a VC-subgraph class of functions of VC dimension $V$ and with measurable envelope $F$. Then for any probability measure $Q$ with $\|F\|_{Q,2}>0$,
