{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:04:06.983684+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2d9042d17145687fc342ffcfac4707745f43151c3dbbfcc242c7fb26b914566","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm thm_global_sol of arXiv:2607.27472, 'The stochastic Keller--Segel system in critical spaces'] Assume that the parameters $s,s_v,q,q_v,p,\kappa$ satisfy (equation Eq_standard of the paper) and  (equation Eq_pc1_new of the paper)--(equation Eq_pc5_new of the paper), and let $g^{i}$, $i\in \{1,2\}$, satisfy Assumptions (Ass_noise of the paper) and (equation assumption_for_global of the paper). 
		Moreover, let $(u_0,v_0)$ as in (equation eq_IV of the paper) be $\mathfrak{F}_0$-measurable  and $((u,v),\sigma)$ be the $L^p_\kappa$-maximal solution  to (equation 25.06.19.16.01 of the paper) provided by Theorem (thm:local_wp of the paper). 
		{Then, for each $T <\infty$, there exists a constant $C_{T}>0$ such that for each constant $\varepsilon \in (0,1)$, if}
		\[
		\mathbb{E} \|(u_0,v_0) \|_{B_{q,p}^{d/q-2}(\mathbb{T}^d)\times B_{q_v,p}^{d/q_v}(\mathbb{T}^d)}^p \,\le\, C_{T} \varepsilon,
		\]
