{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.896948+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a31899203813772ebcf6162d01be0cb1678487edba9c63ccf08d894960ce68bc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 55 of arXiv:2508.04938, 'Perfect t-embeddings of doubly periodic Aztec diamonds'] Let~$(\xi,\eta)\in (-1,1)^2$ and~$x$,~$y$, be related by~\eqref{eq:global_coordinates_2xell}. If~$(\xi,\eta)$ is in the gas region corresponding to~$A_m$, for some~$m=1,\dots,g$, then  
