{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:04:30.600557+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a384d0b2cb165fd588d60536b0151d9faebac45997a7192e11b01febffacd008","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop p:Ytexp of arXiv:2411.10586, 'A convergence framework for Airy$_\beta$ line ensemble\\ via pole evolution'] For any particle-generated Nevanlinna function $Y:\mathbb{H}\to\mathbb{H}\cup{\mathbb R}$ with infinitely many poles $x_1\ge x_2\ge \cdots$, if i) $\sup_{i\in\mathbb{N}}|x_i-{\mathfrak a}_i|<\infty$; and ii) there exists a sequence of complex numbers $w_n\to\infty$ along any direction in $(0, 3\pi/4)$, such that $Y(w_n)-\sqrt{w_n}\rightarrow 0$, then
