{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.307949+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a3a4b0330beaacd7b7a55b527c59eead58d74afcbf5b6c5c10b87b5250e89793","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:priority_idleness of arXiv:2607.13748, 'Load Balancing with Individually Heterogeneous Servers'] The limiting fairness processes for the JSQ systems, where ties among idle servers are broken by routing to the fastest server (JFSQ) or the slowest server (JSSQ), respectively, are given by
