such that $B=AS$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:24:45.891564+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a3c8795d2d1fa0442bed08b260e60ac4cd241ffa1bc22be9338a52ff5b5328d2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:bisection of arXiv:2509.02996, 'Group-averaged Markov chains: mixing improvement'] Let $G$ be a locally compact topological group with Haar measure $\mu$ that acts on $\mathcal{X}$, and $\pi$ is assumed to be $G$-invariant. Under Assumption (assum:pi and G of the paper), assume $P$ and $M$ admit a transition density w.r.t. $\mathfrak{m}$ at any starting state $x$. Under these assumptions, we have, for $g,h \in G$,
