{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:37:51.451526+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a3c9402ffca998d19884d11488237c8d9b134be0f10150b57aabff932950cbec","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 17 (Interpretation of $\partial$ and $\#$) of arXiv:2604.03213, 'Asymptotic expansion for transport maps \\ between laws of multimatrix models'] If $Q \in \Tr^1(\cB)$, $(\cA,\tau)$ is a tracial von Neumann algebra, then $Q^{\cA} \in C^{\infty}\big(\cA_{c,\sa}^{\cB}; \cA\big)$ with respect to $\norm{\cdot}_{\cA,c}$ and $\norm{\cdot}_{\cA^{0,1}}$, and
\begin{equation}
    DQ^{\cA}(x)[y] = \partial Q^{\cA}(x,x)\sh y + \tau\otimes\id_{\cA}\left( \widetilde{\partial}Q^{\cA} \sh (y\otimes 1) \right) \qquad \left(x, y \in \cA_{c,\sa}^{\cB}\right),
\end{equation}
where $D$ denotes the Fr\'echet derivative---in particular, $D^0Q^{\cA}=Q^{\cA}$ and,
$$ D^jQ^{\cA}(x)[y_1,\dots,y_j] = \lim_{t\to 0} \frac{D^{j-1}Q^{\cA}(x+ty_j)[y_1,\dots,y_{j-1}] - D^{j-1}Q^{\cA}(x)[y_1,\dots,y_{j-1}]}{t}. $$
Besides, there exists a universal constant $C_j$ such that for all $x\in \cA^{\cB}_{c,\sa}$ with $\norm{x}_{\cA,c}\leq R$,
\begin{equation}

    \norm{D^jQ^{\cA}(x)[y]}_{\cA^{0,1}} \leq C_j \norm{Q}_{j,c,R} \norm{y_1}_{\cA,c}\dots \norm{y_j}_{\cA,c}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:44:17.163941+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a3ce6f14870f58905b971495d25d15ff8e75191f608886529cb92e136852a6d4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 8 (Bias and variance bounds) of arXiv:2604.17526, '2604.17526'] Let~$U$ be a double well potential that satisfies Assumptions~\ref{a:criticalpts}--\ref{a:massRatioBound}, and let~$\epsilon_1 \in (\epsilon_{\min}, \epsilon_{\max}]$.
  Let~$\nu > 0$ be a fixed constant.
  There exists constants~$\bar C_w = \bar C_w(U, \nu)$, and~$C_T = C_T(U)$ such that the following holds.
  For any~$\epsilon \in (\epsilon_{\min}, \epsilon_{1}]$ choose
  \begin{equation}
    K = \ceil[\bigg]{ \frac{1}{\epsilon \nu} }
    \quad\text{and}\quad
    T > \max\set[\Big]{
      t_{\mix, \epsilon_1}^\infty,
      C_T \paren[\Big]{\frac{1}{\epsilon} + \log K}
    }
    \,,
  \end{equation}
  and choose~$\epsilon_2$, \dots, $\epsilon_{K+1} = \epsilon$ so that~$\set{1/\epsilon_k}_{1 \leq k \leq K+1}$ are linearly spaced.
  Run Algorithm~\ref{a:aisLMC} with this choice of parameters and obtain the point~$X_K$, and unnormalized weight~$\tilde w_K$.
  Then, for all bounded measurable test functions~$f$, we have the bias and variance estimates
  \begin{align}
    \abs[\bigg]{\frac{\E \tilde w_{K} f(X_{K})}{\E \tilde w_{K}} - \ip{f, \pi_{\epsilon}}}
      &\leq 2^{2- T / t_{\mix, 1}^\infty} \norm{f}_\infty
    \,,
    \\

	\var\paren[\bigg]{\frac{\tilde w_{K} f(X_{K})}{\E \tilde w_{K}}}
	  &\leq 4 \bar C_w \norm{f}_\infty^2
	  \,.
  \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:53:00.840535+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a3cf3a68c7cfe97d9c6fd1c6f1cd2dd681b5375aa562fdc3bf275b7993e002e4","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Def: J of arXiv:2607.18635, 'Remainders of generalised Taylor expansions and a priori bounds for rough differential equ'] For any $\rho\in{\mathcal T}_b$ with $k+1$ leaves and $\ell\in\{1,\ldots,m_L(\rho)+1\}$ we define recursively a multi-index  
		$J_{\rho,\ell}:\{0,1,\ldots,k\}^\ell_<\to\mathbb{N}$ as follows: 
		\begin{itemize} 
		\item $J_{\bullet_i,1}=\un{(0)}$ and, given 
		$J_{V^-(\rho),m_L(\rho)}: \{0,\ldots,k-1\}^{m_L(\rho)}_<\to\mathbb{N}$, recall (equation V- of the paper),
			\item for $j\in\{0,\ldots,k\}$
			\[
			J_{\rho,1}(\,j) := \sum_{i_1<\cdots <i_{m_L(\rho)}<k} 
			\un{(i_1<j )}\, J_{V^-(\rho),m_L(\rho)}(i_1,\ldots,i_{m_L(\rho)})\,,
			\]
			\item for $\ell\in\{2,\ldots,m_L(\rho)\}$, $\boldsymbol{j}_\ell=(\,j_1,\ldots,j_{\ell})\in\{0,\ldots,k\}^\ell_<$:
			\begin{equation}
			J_{\rho,\ell}(\,\boldsymbol{j}_\ell) := \sum_{i_{\ell}<\cdots <i_{m_L(\rho)}<k} 
			\un{(\, j_\ell \le i_\ell)}\, J_{V^-(\rho),m_L(\rho)}(\,j_1,\ldots,j_{\ell-1},i_{\ell},\ldots ,i_{m_L(\rho)})\,,
			\end{equation}
			\item for $\boldsymbol{j}_{m_L(\rho)+1}=(\,j_1,\ldots,j_{m_L(\rho)+1})\in\{0,\ldots, k\}^{m_L(\rho)+1}_<$:
			\begin{equation}
				J_{\rho,m_L(\rho)+1}(\,\boldsymbol{j}_{m_L(\rho)+1}) := 
				J_{V^-(\rho),m_L(\rho)}(\,j_1,\ldots,j_{m_L(\rho)})\,.
			\end{equation}


		\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:25:55.461944+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a3cfa4bb3b68ca93298be12cb2423361be8cc5c87d0afa376476f08d0797c2f3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 16 (Weak initial trace condition) of arXiv:2607.28238, 'Well-posedness and large deviations for the obstacle problem of first-order stochastic con'] Let $(u,\nu)$ be the pair constructed in the proof of Theorem \ref{thm:existence-obstacle-solution}.

Then, we have
\begin{equation*}
