{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:01:56.342966+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a42f3083836d4101ca15ba49ad1504567d85f2ffe83844c6b1c6b8b810feb0ae","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm structural results-exponential-decay of arXiv:2609.01499, 'On the rigidity of sloped height functions in $d\ge 3$ \\ and non-crossing surfaces'] (Exponential decay)
    Suppose the same assumptions as in Theorem~(thm:main-localization of the paper). Let $\mu$ be a Gibbs measure with ergodic, minimal gradient measure of slope $\mathfrak{s}$. Then there exist $C,c>0$, depending only on $\beta_0(d)$ of~(equation eq:main assumption of the paper) and the dimension $d$, such that the following holds:
        \begin{enumerate}
            \item For each $v\in\mathbb{Z}^d$ and $t>0$,
            \begin{equation}
                \mu(|\phi_v - h(\mathcal L_v)|\ge t)\le Ce^{-ct}.
            \end{equation}
            \item Let $f_1,f_2:\mathbb{Z}^{\mathbb{Z}^d}\to[-1,1]$ be local in the sense that $f_i(\phi)$ depends only on the restriction of $\phi$ to a finite $\Lambda_i\subset\mathbb{Z}^d$, for each $i\in\{1,2\}$. Then
            \begin{equation}
                \mathbb{E}\left[|\mathrm{Cov}_{\mu | h_0, \alpha}(f_1(\phi), f_2(\phi))|\right]\le C\sum_{u\in\Lambda_1} e^{-cd(u,\Lambda_2)}
            \end{equation}
            where $\mathrm{Cov}_{\mu | h_0,\alpha}$ denotes covariance when $\phi$ is sampled from (the extremal measure) $\mu$ conditioned on $h_0$ and $\alpha$, where the expectation $\mathbb{E}$ is over $h_0$ and $\alpha$ and where $d(u,A)=\inf_{v\in A}\|u-v\|_1$ is the graph distance in $\mathbb{Z}^d$ from $u$ to $A$.
        \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.696927+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a43010c572a7fad9be702d49c0983e862d2d2fc0466481ea3083b9533a3db8dc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:CE-macro-DobrushinBC of arXiv:2606.06612, 'The limit shape and emergence of the \\ Discrete Gaussian level lines'] Fix $n\geq 0$ and $g\geq 0$. In the setting of (prop:CE-meso of the paper), under the relaxed condition $|\partial_{\mathtt v} F|\vee |\partial_{\mathtt v} V| \leq  O(L e^{\sqrt{\log L}})$ and the modified definition of the event $\ensuremath{\mathcal G}$ as
    \begin{align*} \ensuremath{\mathcal G} := \left\{|\gamma| \leq Le^{\sqrt{\log L}}\right\}\cap \bigcap_{i=0,1}\left\{|D_i \cap F| \leq \Big(\frac{3\beta}{{\widehat\pi}_\infty(\phi_o > H+1-n-i)}\Big)^2\right\}\,,\end{align*}
the following holds. The probability distribution $\mathfrak{p}_{V;F}^\eta$ on $\gamma\in\ensuremath{\mathcal G}$ given by 
		\begin{equation*}
