{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:49:05.488515+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a4314ad1bc9ed1511f0702c9e682454e27c54c77118a864f04220de4197b664b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem ito-convergence of arXiv:2601.19145, 'Stochastic Persistence in Infinite Dimensions'] Consider the setup of (general-mild-existence of the paper) and (def:yosida of the paper), and suppose $\theta_F = \theta_G = 0$. Let $\Phi: \mathcal{B} \to \mathbb{R}$ be twice continuously differentiable with linearly bounded first and second derivatives: $\|\Phi'(x)\|_{\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{B},\mathbb{R})} + \|\Phi''(x)\|_{\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{B},\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{B},\mathbb{R}))} \lesssim 1 + \|x\|_B$. Then for all $T > 0$, $p \geq 2$:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item $\lim_{n \to \infty} \mathbb{E}\Big[\int_0^T |\Phi'(x_n(t))F_n(x_n(t)) - \Phi'(x(t))F(x(t))|^pdt\Big] = 0$.
        \item $\lim_{n \to \infty} \mathbb{E}\Big[\int_0^T \|\Phi'(x_n(t))G_n(x_n(t)) - \Phi'(x(t))G(x(t))\|_{\mathcal{U}^*}^pdt\Big] = 0$.
        \item $\lim_{n \to \infty} \mathbb{E}\Big[\int_0^T |\operatorname{tr}_{G_n(x_n(t))}\Phi''(x_n(t)) - \operatorname{tr}_{G(x(t))}\Phi''(x(t))|^pdt\Big] = 0$. (For any operator $T$ on $\mathcal{U}$ we define $\operatorname{tr}_{T}\Phi''(x) = \sum_{j \geq 1} \Phi''(x)[Tu_j, Tu_j]$ where $(u_j)$ is an orthonormal basis for $\mathcal{U}$.)
    \end{itemize}
    Thus,
    \begin{align*}
        \int_0^t \Phi'(x_n F_n(x_n))ds + \int_0^t \Phi'(x_n G_n(x_n)) dW_s + \frac{1}{2}\int_0^t \operatorname{tr}_{G_n(x_n)}\Phi''(x_n)ds \\
        \to \int_0^t \Phi'(x)F(x)ds + \int_0^t \Phi'(x)G(x)dW_s + \frac{1}{2}\int_0^t \operatorname{tr}_{G(x)}\Phi''(x)ds
    \end{align*}
    in $L^p(\Omega; C([0,T], \mathbb{R}))$, where we omitted the dependence of $x_n$ and $x$ on $s$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:29:27.994700+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a431f23c2d7f97762eb2f1db578d03d30f8c8a689fd785150b43884688e379de","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 13 (Quadratic-moment form bound) of arXiv:2608.24863, 'Uniform Logarithmic Sobolev Inequalities for the 2D Coulomb Gas at the Diffusive Temperatu'] There is $C_U(\gamma,Q)<\infty$ such that, on the closed form domain,
