{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:05:37.779335+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a432c842b59ab83354007e775ff0625ba6dc5a2597f1d299555a836f9f01e401","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:ehr-factor of arXiv:2608.01253, 'The pseudo-quantum representation of \\finite reversible Markov chains'] Let $X_t^{(j)}\in\{a,b\}$ be the urn of ball $j$. The processes
$X_t^{(1)},\dots,X_t^{(n)}$ are independent two-state chains, each jumping $a\to b$
