{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:16.152266+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a4a81ae025c991aa3fb9cb895d7726ee207d2193d459db6b447fdd93e8fc5e56","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 30 of arXiv:2604.13454, 'Invariant and periodic measures in classical spin systems on infinite lattices with highly'] For any bounded cylindrically Lipschitz function $h\in C_{b,Lip}(\mathbb{R}^n)$ and arbitrary $s\geq 0$, there holds
