{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:12:46.882886+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a4c3ae1f514304c521edfebf2a8f2f771979c00d705243faf60fe53508fc6de3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma erasedmassdefintro of arXiv:2608.09856, '\bf Mass erasure on measured $\bbR$-trees,\\ applications to L\'evy forests'] Let $(T, d, \rho)$ be a rooted Polish $\mathbb{R}$-tree. Let $\mu \in \mathcal{M}_f (T)$ and let $h \in \mathbb{R}^*_+$. 
