{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:13:22.523507+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a4c9b3767e28e26c2cd52e90ebe8a4336a03db145d435845efb370789a1ef5d5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition String trajectory of arXiv:2505.16585, 'Expanded regimes of area law for lattice Yang--Mills theories'] A \textit{string trajectory} starting at $(s,K,Q)$ of length $l$ is a finite sequence
\begin{equs}
\Big((s_0,K_0,Q_0), (s_1,K_1,Q_1), \ldots, (s_l,K_l,Q_l)\Big),
\end{equs}
where $(s_0,K_0,Q_0)=(s,K,Q)$, and at each non-terminal step $i<l$, $s_i$ is non-null, and if $s_i$ is stuck in a minimal union of connected components $Q \sse P$, then $|Q|<\underbar{area}(s_i)$ and
\begin{equs}
(s_{i+1},K_{i+1},Q_{i+1}) \in \mc{R}(s_i,K_i,Q_i).
\end{equs}
In the case where $s_i$ is not stuck, then
\begin{equs}
(s_{i+1},K_{i+1},Q_{i+1}) \in \mbb{S}_{\pm}((s_i,K_i,Q_i),\mbf{e})\cup \mbb{M}_{\pm}((s_i,K_i,Q_i),\mbf{e})\cup\mbb{D}_{\pm}((s_i,K_i,Q_i),\mbf{e}).
\end{equs}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:30:36.807661+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a4ccfba8ab6652599b8389ab9705ca129e17ce915f20dabd1fadf34bab43aa97","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 78 of arXiv:2607.10486, 'Weak martingale solutions to stochastic Navier-Stokes-Cahn-Hilliard system with transport '] Let $\mathbb{P}$ be a probability measure on $\bZ$ such that conditions (i) and (ii) of Definition \ref{def-martingale problem} are satisfied. 
