{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:37:15.198471+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a4cddd392c82881fb853d4a37d7924212fca31c8d480e30d0e78024100ba8065","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2607.11773, '2607.11773'] Suppose that ({\bf H1})-({\bf H4}), \eqref{31_1}, \eqref{34_1}  and \eqref{dissip1-2} hold.
 Then there exists $\varepsilon_0 \in (0, \varepsilon^*]$ such that for every 
