    \end{equation}where we take $R=2^{38}B^2\nu^{-1/2}c_0^{-2}(\frac{8}{\sqrt{\nu p}}+\frac{256B^2}{\sqrt{c_0}}).$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:03.894233+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a4e2f89275737d286a4344383fc092d2cee0f6aadb54668627c655c806b6ce44","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 15 of arXiv:2606.18877, 'Ergodic Properties of Non-Linear Density-Dependent Perturbations of the Ornstein--Uhlenbec'] Consider the operator~\eqref{K-OU-operator} corresponding to the convariance function of the Ornstein-Uhlenbeck process. Its eigenvalues are given by 
