{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:44:17.160659+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a4f145ddf946ad0a4cb5361d27a9999a661688ed319e245565f99ff3e83520d0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 4 of arXiv:2604.16002, 'Normal approximation for iterated inner functions'] For any complex sequence $(a_n)_{n=1}^\infty$, and any positive integer $N$, it holds that: 
