as $r\to \infty$ for each pair of integers $p,q\geq 0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.146359+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a4f844bbb3fb14929c3b14b551625001e561fadafcd4202b484fb77c534a7b17","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:tauoveralphasfreeness of arXiv:2411.16103, 'Non-commutative Stein's Method: Applications to Free Probability and Sums of Non-commutati'] Let $\{A_n\}_{n\geq 1}$ be a sequence of subalgebras of $\mathcal{A}$. For $a\in \mathcal{A}$, denote the centering of $a$ by $\bar{a}:=a-\tau(a)$. We say that $\{A_n\}_{n\geq 1}$ are freely independent, or free, if
\begin{equation}
\tau[\bar{a}_1\bar{a}_2 \cdots \bar{a}_k]=0,
\end{equation}
for every choice of $a_1,\dots, a_k\in \mathcal{A}$ such that  $a_i\in A_{j(i)}$, with $j(1),\dots, j(k)$ satisfying $j(i)\neq j(i+1)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:21:45.304804+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a4fbe95c64b67e0580211ec92749347034fadf44e0dfa2f5a88578b407c704be","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2607.27082, '2607.27082'] There exists $C<\infty$ such that
