{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:44.556226+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a4fcfef66b0963a219b618d4bfbc2df246fdbae323608a4c155a236aede42492","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 27 of arXiv:2604.02312, 'A weak transport approach to the Schrödinger--Bass bridge'] The function $C_{\rm stat}^\beta\colon \R^d \times \cP_2(\R^d) \to \R$, defined by
    \begin{align}

        C_{\rm stat}^\beta(x,\eta) &:= \sup_{y \in \R^d} \left\{-q_\beta(x-y) + \inf_{\rho  \in \cP_2(\R^d)}\left\{ H(\rho \,|\, \gamma_y) + W_\beta(\rho,\eta)\right\}\right\} \\

        &= \inf_{\substack{\kappa \in \cP_2(\R^d),\\ \bar \kappa = \bar \eta}} \bigl\{H(\kappa\,|\,\gamma_x) + W_\beta(\kappa,\eta)\bigr\}
    \end{align}
    is a continuous standard weak transport cost and admits a $2$-growth bound. 
