{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:44:17.353920+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a56d901e5c545519b90c3ca04b56dcef9bbf678495efd86fa46753f3e6254eac","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary prop:main-approx of arXiv:2608.23554, 'Provably adaptive sampling with uniform and remasking \\ discrete diffusion models'] Fix \(k \in \{0, \ldots, N - 1\}\) in the time discretization \(0 = t_0 < t_1 < \ldots < t_N < T\). Consider the uniform or remasking process and let \(u = T - t_{k+1}\), \(\ell = T - t_k\). We have
