{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:45:17.711600+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a5a5c5526bbd2f975b44c6954a6fd1f6641a77b1486d90de98f1fc66d13b22d6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Bernstein of arXiv:2604.11761, 'The smallest singular value of signed random combinatorial matrices'] Let $Y_1, \ldots, Y_m$ be independent, mean-zero, subexponential random variables. Then, for every $t \geq 0$, we have
