{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:49.204071+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a5c9dd1e5b2095a84ceda684b4e1bccd11965a3198e1dc8510907c6bc524f160","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 (Matrix Bernstein) of arXiv:2604.27119, '\Large Applied Random Matrix Theory\relatedversion'] Consider a statistically independent family $(\mtx{X}_1, \dots, \mtx{X}_n)$
of $d_1 \times d_2$ random matrices, real or complex, 
that are centered and uniformly bounded: $\Expect[ \mtx{X}_k ] = \mtx{0}$ and $\norm{ \mtx{X}_k } \leq B$ for each index $k$.
Form the sum, and calculate its matrix variance statistic:
\begin{equation} 
\mtx{S} \coloneqq \sum_{k=1}^n \mtx{X}_k
\quad\text{and}\quad
v(\mtx{S}) \coloneqq \norm{ \Expect[ \mtx{SS}^* ] } \vee \norm{ \Expect[ \mtx{S}^*\mtx{S} ] }.
\end{equation}
Then the spectral norm of the sum satisfies the probability inequalities
\begin{gather} 
\Expect \norm{\mtx{S}} \leq \sqrt{2 v(\mtx{S}) \log(d_1 + d_2)} + \frac{1}{3} B \log(d_1 + d_2); \\

\Prob{ \norm{\mtx{S}} \geq t} \leq (d_1 + d_2) \exp\left( \frac{-t^2/2}{v(\mtx{S}) + Bt/3} \right)
\quad\text{for $t \geq 0$.}

\end{gather} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:31.997612+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a5d077e49d2ea37f54b8dce7fd1ef47f211d08b01fb8a43f13e8b5185cf8687b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2512.02322, 'Ursell functions in lattice gauge theory'] Consider Ising lattice gauge theory with parameter $\beta \geq \beta_0$. Then one can factorize $U_n$ as
\begin{equation}

        U_n^W(W_\gamma) = a_{\{[n]\}} (1 + V_n(W_\gamma)),
        \end{equation}
        where $V_n(W_\gamma)$ is defined by
        \begin{equation}

        V_n(W_\gamma) := \sum_{\substack{\mathfrak{P} \in \mathfrak{F}_n : \\ \mathfrak{P} \neq \{[n]\}}} b_\mathfrak{P}.
        \end{equation}
        Here the coefficients $b_\mathfrak{P}$, for $\mathfrak{P} \in \mathfrak{F}_n, ~ \mathfrak{P} \neq \{[n]\}$, are defined by
        \begin{equation}

b_{\mathfrak{P}} := \frac{a_{\mathfrak{P}}}{a_{\{[n]\}}} = (-1)^{|\mathfrak{P}|-1} (|\mathfrak{P}|-1)! \frac{\myexp \Big(- 2 \sum_{I \subseteq [n]} c_{I,\mathfrak{P}} \Psi_\beta[I]\Big)}{\myexp\big( -2 \sum_{I \subset [n]}\mathbbm{1}\{|I| ~ \text{odd}\} \Psi_\beta[I]\Big)}.
\end{equation}
Moreover, the coefficients $(b_{\mathfrak{P}})_{\mathfrak{P} \in \mathfrak{F}_n \setminus \{[n]\}}$ do not depend on the weights of the vortex clusters $\mathcal{V} \in \Xi[\{i\}]$ for any $i \in [n]$.","status":"unverified"}

