{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.285701+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a639a358064fd4b48c12a228615058013ff00b4cdde428ddb87e694b55714cce","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 (Inhomogeneous $p$-variation norm) of arXiv:2606.22964, 'Signature McKean--Vlasov stochastic differential equations'] Let $p\geq 1$. For any path $\mathbf{x}:[0,T]\rightarrow G^{\lfloor p\rfloor}(\mathbb{R}^k)$,
