{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:32:19.899600+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a68d71412b43a9fbd0dd4c2d6fc9cfbd9fd06587f65f56105e56a075d0b816f5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 1 of arXiv:2608.02319, 'Averaging Principle for Ordinary Differential Equations in a Multiscale Random Environment'] There exists a random process $\mathbf{X}^1 = (\Omega,\mathcal{F}^1,(\mathbf{X}_t^1)_{t\geq0}, (\mathbf{P}_x^1)_{x\in E})$ with state space $E\cup \{\Delta\}$ with lifetime $T_\Delta^1:=\inf\{t\geq 0,\mathbf X_t^1=\Delta\}$, and a random sequence of times $(\tau_k^1)_{k \geq 0}$ such that
