and the coefficient $\E X_1^4-3\,\E X_1^2X_2^2$ is strictly positive.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:38:57.117648+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a6adb99681b8b0450f563987d5ccc15d2f5b031364db44da947ff19f09861448","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 20 of arXiv:2604.04823, '2604.04823'] For any~$a\geq1$, there exists~$\hat\epsilon (a) > 0$ such that for any~$\epsilon$ and~$h$ with~$\epsilon < \hat\epsilon$ and~$h \leq \epsilon^2$, the following holds. If~$x \in \Omega$ satisfies
    \begin{equation}
