    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:27:11.423224+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a6b03ec99daf7e5561994511de023e57f85c4dd8c35af2a60a3811b28af53285","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition p: alpha mixing condition of arXiv:2605.22803, 'Persistence of asymptotic variance under transport:\\ from hyperfluctuation to stealthy hy'] Let $p\in[-d, 2]$. Suppose that there are $\gamma> d+\max(p,0), c>0$ such that
    \begin{align}
        \BE_{0}^{\Phi}[\|Z(0)\|^{\gamma}] &< \infty,\\
        \BE_{0,y}^{\Phi}[\|Z(0)\|^{\gamma}] &\leq c,\quad y\in\R^d\\
        \int \frac{\kappa(y)^{\frac{\gamma-2q}{\gamma}}}{1 + \|y\|^{2q-p}}\, \alpha_\Phi(dy) &< \infty,\quad q\in\N, q<\tfrac{d+p}{2}, 
