{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.635284+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a704a58f3a8fe4436b83e9daebed26ce02713ae5b0f43a26bab3cb688a9115fb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2609.01362, '{Double cluster swapping for spin models: \\Pfaffian relations and sharpness}'] Let $H \subset V$ with $|H| \leq 3$. Then, there exists $ K_{uu'} \geq 0$ for every $u,u' \in H$, $r_{u} > 0$ for each $u \in H$ and a constant $Z > 0$ such that
	\begin{equation}
		\left< \vp(A) \right>_{G} = \Big( \prod_{u \in A} r_u  \Big) \frac{1}{Z}\sum_{ \sigma \in \left\{ \pm 1 \right\}^H} \sigma(A) \exp\Big( \sum_{u,u' \in H} K_{uu'} \sigma_u \sigma_{u'} \Big) \quad \text{ for any $A \subset H$.}
