{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.777912+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a745926fb6467536e8be4d06a32d73f9fabf712fb7c2bd3f221b051fb2cf16f4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemm 6 (Rerooting formula) of arXiv:2603.25536, 'The $H^{2|2}$ monotonicity theorem revisited'] Let $\delta,b\in V$ and consider the measures $d\nu_\delta$ and $d\nu_b$ with different pinning points $\delta$ and $b$, defined in~\eqref{eq:mixing_measure}. If the variables $\bm{t}'$ and $\bm{t}$ are related by $t'_i=t_i-t_b$ for all $i\in V$, then
