{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.298496+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a7872ccf3eb5646cc0f471308408a2094a7cbe88cadfba0e2ff64f89f96335cb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem sDHD-th6.10 of arXiv:2604.21591, '\bf Long-time dynamics of stochastic 2D hydrodynamic-type evolution equations driven by mu'] Assume that the hypotheses of Theorem (2DHD-the3.3-0 of the paper) and condition (equation LSWs6.3 of the paper) hold. Then the non-autonomous dynamical system $\Psi$ generated by ((2DHD-1.1 of the paper)) possesses a unique $\mathscr{D}$-pullback measure attractor $\mathscr{A}=\{\mathscr{A}(\tau):\tau\in \mathbb{R}\}\in \mathscr{D}$ in $(\mathcal {P}_4 (H), d_{\mathcal{P}(H)})$. Moreover, for every $\tau\in \mathbb{R}$, $\mathscr{A}(\tau)$ has the following characterizations:
	\begin{align*}
		\begin{split}
			\mathscr{A}(\tau)
			=\omega(\mathcal{K},\tau)&=\{\psi(0,\tau): \psi \text{ is a } \mathscr{D}\text{-complete orbit of } \Psi\}\\
			&=\{\widehat{u}(\tau): \widehat{u} \text{ is a }  \mathscr{D}\text{-complete solution of } \Psi\},
		\end{split}
	\end{align*}
	where $\mathcal{K}=\{\mathcal{K}(\tau):\tau\in \mathbb{R}\}$ denotes the $\mathscr{D}$-pullback absorbing set of $\Psi$ provided by Lemma (sDHD-lemma6.8 of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

