{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:17:13.073514+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a78dbfe9606e1bc5dd954c80c69c9b26b89267a328240c191b21ad4b48ec4f2e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:F-via-HF of arXiv:2509.08928, 'The near critical random bond Ising model via embedding deformation'] {[CLR1] and [Che20] }  For each fixed $\kappa<1$, there exist constants $\gamma_0=\gamma_0(\kappa)>0$ and \mbox{$C_0=C_0(\kappa)>0$} such that the following alternative holds. Let $F$ be a s-holomorphic function defined in a ball of radius $r$ drawn over an s-embedding $\mathcal{S}$ satisfying the assumption $\textup{Lip}(\kappa,\delta)$ and some $\alpha \in \mathbb{T}$. Then, provided that $r\ge\operatorname{cst}\cdot\delta$ for a constant depending only on $\kappa$, one has the two following alternatives:

