{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.288408+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a79652f868a280d697e095c28553fe7cdb1d679ceef7f589e1ba6af8f88c275e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:LRW2 of arXiv:2607.10801, 'Relaxation times of non-reversible\\ Markov processes'] There exist universal constants $c,C\in (0,\infty )$ such that for all $d,n\in\mathbb N$ with $n\ge 2$ and all $\gamma ,\varepsilon\in (0,\infty )$, the  lifted random walk on $\mathbb{Z}_n^d$ satisfies
