{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:07:48.552830+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a796a800b881ddcb62059118ad34162d5660de8bead7d86235b410fa8b279d80","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 5 (Sharp function-field surjection moments) of arXiv:2609.01413, 'Sharp Threshold for Universality of Rational Canonical Forms over a Finite Field'] Let $(\alpha_n)_{n\geq1}$ satisfy
