{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:57:20.581449+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a7d5083c159c806757c562659662668dac22c9ea93bd48f6f228af45666ea794","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm BYY_MT of arXiv:2411.09640, 'Random Lipschitz functions on graphs with weak expansion'] Fix $v_0 \in V(C_{n,k})$, and let $f$ be chosen uniformly at random from $\mbox{\rm{Hom}}_{v_0}(G)$. Let $\psi:\mathbb N \rightarrow \mathbb R^+$ be such that $\lim_{n \rightarrow \infty} \psi(n)=\infty$. If $k=2\log n+\psi(n)$, then, as $n \rightarrow \infty$,
\begin{equation}\label{range.ub} \mathbb{P}[R(f)\le 3] = 1 - o_n(1).\end{equation}
On the other hand, if $k=2\log n-\psi(n)$ and $\psi(n)$ is monotone, then, as $n \rightarrow \infty$,
\[\mathbb{P}\left[R(f)\ge\frac{2^{\psi(n-2)/4}}{\psi(n)}\right] = 1 - o_n(1).\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:17.370064+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a7d50b81580f9cf7f99746386c5f0cb8809d321fe708c2a7f35168ac70124759","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 20 of arXiv:2606.03534, 'Construction and simulation of a path-valued model of dendrite development'] When $\ell_t$ is a Brownian motion absorbed at $\ell=0$ we have 
