{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:06:07.090355+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a8126a8f3283d29c11b0ea353da212aaf42d8fa31eadc67dc78bdfecb967793e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi 24 of arXiv:2608.28148, 'Flows and homotopies of Banach Lie algebroids'] We work over a Banach bundle $\pi\colon A\to M$. A \emph{time-dependent (local) section} of $A$ is a map 
$\mathfrak{u}\colon I\times U\to A_{U}$ where $I$ is an  interval of $\R$, $U \subseteq M$ open. Typically we will discuss time-dependent sections of class $C^{\ell,\infty}$, i.e. we have some regularity $\ell\in \N_0 \cup \{\infty\}$ in time and smoothness in $x$.

We say that a time dependent section $\mathfrak{u} \colon I \times M \rightarrow A$ \emph{extends a path $c\colon I\to A$}  if $\mathfrak{u}(t,\g(t))=c(t)$ for $\g (t) := \pi (c(t))$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:52:47.244689+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a814a09f87974dabe9dae2caaf510f7743b15c2ad9aef9a1c330e7c560370d21","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 19 (Hodge a priori estimates: null-form rhs) of arXiv:2609.01093, 'Ideal MHD below the classical well-posedness threshold'] Let $\Ufield,\Vfield$ be as above, recall $\sigma=s-1>(n-1)/2$, and let
$F[\Ufield]$ be the canonical Hodge representative \eqref{eq:FU}.  Then $F[\Ufield]\in C(I;L^4)$, with
\begin{equation}
 \|F[\Ufield]\|_{L^\infty(I;L^4)}\le C_\delta R^2 ,
\end{equation}
and, for every $\rpar\in[0,1]$ such that
$\Ufield\in H^{\sigma,1+\rpar}_{\breg}$,
\begin{equation}
 \|dF[\Ufield]\|_{L^2(I;Y^{\sigma,\rpar})}
 \le C_{\delta,\rpar} 
 \|\Ufield\|_{H^{\sigma,1}_{\breg}} 
 \|\Ufield\|_{H^{\sigma,1+\rpar}_{\breg}} .
\end{equation}
In particular at $\rpar=0$,
\begin{equation}
 \|dF[\Ufield]\|_{L^2(I;H^\sigma)}\le C_\delta R^2 .
\end{equation}
Finally,
\begin{equation}
 \|dF[\Ufield]-dF[\Vfield]\|_{L^2(I;H^\sigma)}
 \le C_\delta R(1+R) D .
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:28:34.916869+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a814ab0e17283b52680c700b69ce1faed22d904b810f6468fe27fecd31b5d734","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem DPP-path-stoch of arXiv:2412.05698, 'Controlled rough SDEs, pathwise stochastic control and dynamic programming principles'] Suppose that  (assum-path-stoch of the paper) holds. Then, for any $y \in \mathbb{R}^{d_Y}$,  $s\in[0,T]$, 
$h\in[0,T-s]$ and $i=1,2$, 

\begin{equation}
\bar{\mathcal{V}}(s,y;\omega)= {\ensuremath{\operatorname{essinf}}_{\eta \in \mathcal{A}^i}}\ \mathbb{E}[ \bar{\mathcal{V}}(s+h, \bar{Y}^{s,y,\bar{\eta}}_{s+h}; \cdot) \mid {\mathfrak F}^{\mathbf{W}}_T] (\omega) \quad\text{a.e. } \omega,
\end{equation}
where the left-hand side is continuous on $[0,T]\times \mathbb{R}^{d_Y}$ a.s. as in Theorem (rep-value-fct of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.957197+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a8174d4ac5245b696136fc1e4ef15def64cc4d7140f594cfe1439590f220b2bb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem eqn|UFirstElements of arXiv:2504.08938, 'Fourier Levels and Almost Sure Bounds on Higher-Order Derivatives in First-Passage Percola'] The first four elements of the sequence $\left(\mathcal U_n\right)$ and the first three elements of the sequence $\left(\mathcal L_n\right)$ are 
\begin{eqnarray}
