{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:07:48.548501+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a86ba63400983378e740ce2690ebcf1e434b03b1bbf5f129118d6fbb3201c080","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 22 (Prediction Variance~\citep{hamman2024quantifying,watson2023predictive}) of arXiv:2609.01397, 'Measuring consistency via ensemble margin and local prediction variability: Auditing decis'] The prediction variance of $\emprashomonset$ is the variance of model outputs for a given test instance $x$, and is defined as
