{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:32:19.937830+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a8b5231c39d29ed5134c960e71130f3d7f4660b44eee66882278234c3f4500cd","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 21 of arXiv:2608.02927, 'Thinning Operation via the Poisson-F\"ollmer Process'] Let $T = \E X >0,$ and assume that $X \sim f \dd \pi_{T}.$ If $f$ is bounded away from zero and infinity, then
