        \limsup_{n \rightarrow \infty} \Bigg[ n^{2}  H \Big( \sum_{i=1}^{n} T_{1/n}(X_{i}) |\pi_{T} \Big)  \Bigg] \le  \Big( \frac{\Var(X)}{T } - 1 \Big)^{2}.
    \end{displaymath}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:03:59.344534+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a8b99d3198e1399f24b6bb4577f5b5a4f35d15e5069f9af35303c8defc9bc2f2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Satz th:BBLM of arXiv:2507.08692, 'Some notes on higher order concentration of measure'] If $X_1, \ldots, X_n$ are independent random variables and $f = f(X) \in L^\infty({\mathbb P})$, with the constant $\kappa = \frac{\sqrt{e}}{2\,(\sqrt{e} - 1)}$, we have for any $r \ge 2$,
	\begin{equation*} 
		\lVert (f - \mathbb{E}f)_+ \rVert_r \le (2\kappa r)^{1/2}\, \lVert \mathfrak{h}^+f \rVert_r \quad \text{and} \quad


		\lVert (f - \mathbb{E}f)_- \rVert_r \le (2\kappa r)^{1/2}\, \lVert \mathfrak{h}^-f \rVert_r.
	\end{equation*}
	Consequently, this leads to 
	\[
	\norm{f - \IE f}_r \le (8\kappa r)^{1/2} \norm{\mathfrak{h}f}_r.
	\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:10.963855+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a8b9be35552ca0a70deb6a5b26355b2d6812ae2aa784a692f39cb5c74447fc2c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 of arXiv:2606.12720, 'On McDiarmid's Inequality under Dependence \\ via Approximate Tensorization of Entropy'] {Bounded Differences Property}

    A function $f : \mathcal X^n \to \R$ fulfills the bounded differences property if for $c_1,...,c_n \geq 0$ and all $i \in [n]$: 
    \begin{align*}
        \sup_{y, x_1,...,x_n \in \mathcal X} |f(x_1,...,x_n) - f(x_1,...x_{i-1} y, x_{i+1},...,x_n)| \leq c_i.
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.666268+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a8bb428c6955a0bf9ecc663976293ca509fba42f3b62ad37a1a2acb0f25865f3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:entropic_stability:gen of arXiv:2412.09235, 'A semiconcavity approach to stability of entropic plans and exponential convergence of Sin'] Let (ass:differentiability of the paper) hold and $\pi_\varepsilon^{\rho\nu},\,\pi_\varepsilon^{\rho\mu}$  be the  the unique optimizers in (equation EOT of the paper) for the set of marginals $(\rho,\nu)$ and $(\rho,\mu)$. If there exists $\Lambda>0$ and a non-negative function $\omega\colon\mathcal{Y}\times\mathcal{Y}\to \mathbb{R}$ such that 
\begin{equation*}
y\mapsto c(x,y)+\psi^{\nu}_\varepsilon(y)
\end{equation*}
is $(\Lambda,\omega)$-semiconcave uniformly in $x\in\supp(\rho)$, then
\begin{equation*}
\mathrm{KL}(\pi_\varepsilon^{\rho\mu}|\pi_\varepsilon^{\rho\nu})\leq \mathrm{KL}(\mu|\nu)+\frac{\Lambda}{2{\varepsilon}}\,\mathbf{W}_\omega(\mu,\nu)\,.
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:38.363752+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a8bf769dbd210c335398b440c1f6f8251ce6cc13b61bf7e09df4cc7a13125e56","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 26 of arXiv:2604.21669, 'Discontinuous transition in 2D Potts:\\ II. order-order interface convergence'] There are \(C\in (0,+\infty)\) such that for any \(n\geq 1\), \(i,i',j,j'\in \Z\) with \(i> i'\), \(j>j'\),
	\begin{equation*}
		q_{i,i'}^+(n,j,j')
		\leq
		\tfrac{C\min(i-i',\sqrt{n})\min(j-j',\sqrt{n})}{n^2}.
	\end{equation*}
	The same holds for \(\overleftarrow{q}^+\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:31:20.609806+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a8c0ddaa9b5906e36b463c4fec77e06da7c9f0f239c0e7fef7eacd30ca43aeab","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 15 (Jabin and Wang {\cite[Theorem 4) of arXiv:2608.25772, 'Propagation of Chaos and Gaussian Fluctuations for Mean-field Coupled Maps'] {JW18}}]
    Let $E$ be a Polish space and $\rho\in\mathcal{P}(E)$ be a probability measure on $E$. Suppose that $\phi:E\times E\to\R$ is a measurable function satisfying the following two cancellation rules:
    \begin{equation}
        \int_E\phi(x,y)\dd\rho(x)=0,\quad\forall y\in E;\qquad
        \int_E\phi(x,y)\dd\rho(y)=0,\quad\forall x\in E.
    \end{equation}
    Then there exists a constant $C_1>0$, such that when $\|\phi\|_{L^{\infty}}\leq C_1$, one has
    \begin{equation}
        \sup_{N\geq 2}\int_{E^N}   \rho^{\otimes N}(X_N)\exp{\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i,j=1}^{N}\phi(x_i,x_j)\right)}\dd X_N\leq C<+\infty,
    \end{equation}
    where $X_N=(x_1,x_2,\dots,x_N)$ for $N\geq 2$ and $C$ is a generic constant independent of $N$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:15:36.159702+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a8c2e120c0ccd5ef54e79db23de7ebbc362d04ca0f7ae20cf9e7faeb98cbb674","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 23 (Specific vorticity) of arXiv:2609.01589, 'Uniform stability of expanding simple waves for Euler--Poisson--Boltzmann: a singular comp'] Every classical solution of \eqref{eq:EP-mass}--\eqref{eq:EP-poisson}
satisfies
