  (\pa_t+u\cdot\nabla)\zeta=0. 
\end{equation}
Consequently,
\begin{equation}
  \sup_{t_0\le t\le T}\norm{\zeta(t)}_{H^{s-1}}
  \le C_{t_0,T}\norm{\zeta(t_0)}_{H^{s-1}}. 
\end{equation}
The constant is independent of $\eps$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:24:34.412430+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a8c3359ec6d8ae6f7d488c2255ee97f5de08386fcffaeccde38596fad5d16d72","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 30 of arXiv:2608.31070, 'Sub-Laplacians on Compact Lie Groups: Heat Kernels, Distance, and Zeta Determinants'] If $G$ is simply connected, then, for every $0<\tau\le1$,
		\begin{align}
