{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:20.956202+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a8dfda0280d13db1f5a8302c45a46959b8add39b3aba7a71390824977a6ccce0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 32 of arXiv:2604.09365, 'Cotlar martingale transforms and related singular integrals'] Let $A$ and $B$ be two  real-valued  $d\times d$ matrices.  We will say that the pair $(A, B)$ is $d\times d$ conformal if it satisfies the following two properties: 
