{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:07:48.567335+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a8e68dee16acbdbb2fe82991f197a7aedd77e70d2189b7efdd9592e12ddc0eae","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 35 of arXiv:2609.01460, 'On cost-induced Santal\'o-type inequalities \\ in Polish measure spaces'] Let $(X,d,\mu)$ be a Polish probability space with enlargement functions
$(R_s)_{s\geq 0}$ and associated function $\Theta$. 

Assume $A,B\in \mathcal{B}(X)$ are non-empty sets with
$0<\mu(A)\mu(B)\leq 1$.

Then,
\begin{equation}

    \mu(A)^{\frac12}\mu(B)^{\frac12}
    \leq
    2\Theta(d(A,B)).
\end{equation}
Moreover, if $A$ and $B$ are essentially disjoint, that is,
$\mu(A\cap B)=0$, then one has the sharp bound
\begin{equation}

    \mu(A)^{\frac12}\mu(B)^{\frac12}
    \leq
    \Theta(d(A,B)).
\end{equation}

Furthermore, assume that, for each $s>0$, the supremum defining $\Theta$ in
\eqref{eq:theta_def} is uniquely achieved at some $v_s\in(0,1)$ and that
$R_s(v_s)<1$. Then equality holds in \eqref{eq:enlargement_sharp} with
$0<\mu(A),\mu(B)<1$ if and only if the following conditions hold:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item If $d(A,B)=0$, then $\mu(A)=\mu(B)=\frac12$ and $B=X\setminus A$ up to a null set.

    \item If $d(A,B)>0$, then
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $\mu(A)=v_{d(A,B)}$ and $\mu(B)=1-R_{d(A,B)}(v_{d(A,B)})$;
        \item
        \[
            \mu(A_{<d(A,B)})=R_{d(A,B)}(\mu(A));
        \]
        \item
        \[
            \mu\bigl(B\Delta(X\setminus A_{<d(A,B)})\bigr)=0.
        \]
    \end{enumerate}
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:19:06.742155+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a8e6995e2676b2e47039bd57b1f5a10d411f08832a3ecd4aafcf31a6c3a28a84","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn Wconvergence of arXiv:2606.02340, 'Transitivity in Inhomogeneous Random Tournaments'] [lovasz_book]
    The {\it cut-distance} between two bounded functions $W_1, W_2 : [0, 1]^2 \rightarrow \mathbb R$ is 
    \begin{align}
    ||W_1-W_2||_{\square}:=\sup_{f, g: [0, 1] \rightarrow [0, 1]} \left|\int_{[0, 1]^2} \left(W_1(x, y)-W_2(x, y)\right) f(x) g(y) \mathrm dx \mathrm dy \right|. 
    \end{align} 
    The {\it cut-metric} between $W_1, W_2$ is defined as,  
    \begin{align*}
    \delta_{\square}(W_1, W_2):= \inf_{\psi}||W_1^{\psi}-W_2||_{\square}, 
    \end{align*} 
    with the infimum taken over all measure-preserving bijections $\psi: [0, 1] \rightarrow [0, 1]$, and  $W_1^\psi(x, y):= W_1(\psi(x), \psi(y))$, for $x, y \in [0, 1]$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:21:56.738304+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a8e76c7d2a8bd397aed3600296a09aaab46f2331591f7fe166fb9a75ba2a6026","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:double_flow_lines_interior of arXiv:2507.15589, 'Tightness of approximations to metrics on non-simple conformal loop ensemble gaskets'] Fix $p \in (0,1)$, $a'>0$. Let~$h$ be a GFF on~$\mathbf{D}$ with boundary values so that its flow line $\eta$ is an ${\rm SLE}_{\kappa}${} from $-i$ to $i$. Let $X^0_{0,1}$ be as defined in~(equation eq:fl_annulus of the paper). Let $I_\epsilon$ be the event that there exist two strands $\eta_{w_1}$, $\eta_{w_2}$ of $X^0_{0,1}$ so that the following hold.
\begin{itemize}
 \item The continuations of $\eta_{w_i}$, $i=1,2$, hit $B(0,\epsilon)$ before exiting $B(0,3/4)$ and without merging.
 \item The conditional probability given $X^0_{0,1}$ and the values of $h$ on $X^0_{0,1}$ that $\eta$ merges into $\eta_{w_1}$ before entering $B(0,1/4)$ and then into $\eta_{w_2}$ before entering $B(0,1/4)$ again is at least $p$.
\end{itemize}
Then there exists $\epsilon_0 > 0$ so that
\[
 \mathbf{P}[I_\epsilon] \leq \epsilon^{\alpha_{4,\kappa}-a'}  \quad\text{for}\quad \epsilon \in (0,\epsilon_0).
\]","status":"unverified"}

