				where $\bL_{\Pr_i}(u^i),$ $ i=1, 2$ represents the law of the random variable $u_i$ which takes values in $C([0,T];\Vp)\cap L^2(0,T;D(A))\cap L^{2p-2}(0,T;L^{2p-2}(\bO))$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:53:51.335019+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a900d044721a34171229a9f4a2b2a00a9ffa890a93565fcecbd81ffaee089e7a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:d_beta_defn of arXiv:2605.03896, 'Dimer models on astroidal zig-zag graphs'] Given such a \(\bm \beta\), define an element \(\bm D_{\bm \beta} \in \mathbb{Z}^{\bm \alpha}\) by
\begin{equation} 
     (\bm D_{\bm \beta})_{\bm \alpha_e} := -\bm d(\mathsf x)_{\bm \alpha_e}
\end{equation}
for all \(e \in E(N)\), where \(\mathsf x\) is any \(\beta_e\)-outer vertex. We say that \(\mathsf G_{c, \mathsf f_0}\) is \emph{admissible} if
