{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:33.750732+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a9278351e33b813af02a9d3d93d24857b307c40318b6d0f69bf8d1630fd80f9f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 20 of arXiv:2608.18834, 'The Parabolic Anderson Model's Total Mass at Small Times: Geometry, Fluctuations, and Reno'] Let $\ka\geq0$ and $t,\eps>0$ be fixed.
One has
\begin{align}

\mbf E\big[\msf M_{\ka,\eps}(t)\big]
&=\int_D\mbf E\left[\mbf 1_{\{\tau_D(B^x)>t\}}\mr e^{\frac{\ka^2}{2}\be^\eps_t(B)}\right]\d x,\\

