{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:13:31.949406+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a92f116d44ac7c1955d8c4551a3608fb4ce8a5cbc020e2eca62eac91be73317f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm EL_equations of arXiv:2506.12171, 'The multinomial dimer model'] The limit shape flow $\omega$ for $(R,b)$ is the solution to the following system of differential equations:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item the divergence equation, 
        \begin{align}
            \text{div}(\omega(x)) = \sum_{i=1}^d \pd{\omega_i}{x_i}(x) = 0;
        \end{align}
        \item a collection of ${d\choose 2}$ equations:
        \begin{align}
            \pd{}{x_i} \pd{}{s_j}\sigma(\omega(x)) - \pd{}{x_j}\pd{}{s_i}\sigma(\omega(x)) =0 
        \end{align}
        for all $i\neq j$ between $1$ and $d$.
    \end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:52.208606+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a9315215f75775b605b710396a54c79d08efc2a99d0f64b659df7439751af7ac","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 10 (Asymptotics for $\alpha \to \alpha_0,$ $\alpha_0 \in [0,2\pi\textnormal{) of arXiv:2512.09136, 'On the Green's functions and Martin boundary structure of a planar diffusion in a disconti'] }\backslash \mathcal M$, or $\alpha \to 0, \pi$ with $\alpha \in [0,2\pi\textnormal{]}\backslash \mathcal M$] 
Assume $x^+_{max} > x^-_{max}$ (cases A and D of Figure~\ref{anglesalphab}). Let $z_0 \in \R^2$ and let $0 \leq \alpha_0 < \alpha_b$. Then:
\begin{equation}
g^{z_0}(r\cos(\alpha), r\sin(\alpha))
\underset{r\to\infty \atop\alpha\to\alpha_0, \alpha \geq 0}{\sim} C'_{br}(\alpha_0) f_0(z_0)\frac{e^{-r(\cos(\alpha)x(\alpha_b) + \sin(\alpha)y(\alpha_b))}}{r^{3/2}
}
\end{equation}
where $C'_{br}(\alpha_0) = \left(\frac{\sin(\alpha_b)}{\sin(\alpha_b - \alpha_0)}\right)^{3/2}C_0$ (see \eqref{eq:C_0}) and where $f_0(z_0)$ is given by \eqref{f(z_0)branch}. 

Assume now $x^+_{max} < x^-_{max}$ (cases B and C of Figure~\ref{anglesalphab}) and let $\alpha_b < \alpha_0 \leq 2\pi$. Then,
\begin{equation}
 g^{z_0}(r\cos(\alpha), r\sin(\alpha))
\underset{r\to\infty \atop\alpha\to\alpha_0, \alpha \leq 2\pi}{\sim}  C'_{br}(\alpha_0)f_0(z_0)\frac{e^{-r(\cos(\alpha)x(\alpha_b) + \sin(\alpha)z(\alpha_b))}}{r^{3/2}}
\end{equation}
where $C'_{br}(\alpha_0)$ has the same expression and where $f_0(z_0)$ is given by \eqref{f(z_0)col}.

The symmetric results hold for $\tilde\alpha_b< \alpha_0 \leq\pi$ in the cases A and B and for $ \pi\leq \alpha_0 < \tilde\alpha_b$ in the cases C and D. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:46.469521+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a9333531b7567408af2fd0040d82b43b6d9416700fa3acaa8c277b1ad2263d2f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 78 (Identities involving the double-null frame and the null-geometry scalars) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] Let $\ReciprocalLunitAppliedtoTimeFunction, \ReciprocaluLunitAppliedtoTimeFunction, \ingoingmu, \MagnitueofinnerproductofnewLandnewuL$ be the double-null acoustic geometry scalar functions defined in Sect.\,\ref{SSS:NULLVECTORFIELDS}.  Then the following identities hold:
