{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:04:55.814076+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a9382a0a13010e5b9b64ae30452038af88a47f63cb63725fdb3b24f1d7eeeccd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemm l:quenched-weak-convergence of arXiv:2607.18194, 'Temperature chaos in directed polymers'] Almost surely, the un-normalized measures $M_{\beta,n}^\xi$ converge weakly to a finite measure $M_{\beta}^\xi$.
