{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:37:51.458609+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a93d4edf644fac9a1c639af66894c7c4d199ede84b90e2d30ea44c467ffb5b5a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 40 of arXiv:2604.03777, 'Equilibrium fluctuations for a multi-species particle system with long jumps'] Let $ \gamma >2$ and $0 \leq s \leq t \leq T$. Assume that $K_n \sqrt{n} \leq \widehat{C}$, for every $n \in \mathbb{N}_+$. Then there exists some $\delta_1 \in (0, \;1]$ and some $f: \mathbb{N}_+ \mapsto \mathbb{R}$ satisfying $\lim_{n \rightarrow \infty} f(n)=0$, such that
	\begin{align*}
		\mathbb{E}_{\nu_{\rho}} \Bigg[ \Bigg\{ & \frac{\Theta(n) K_n}{\sqrt{n}} \int_s^t \dd r \sum_x \sum_{y=x+1}^{\infty} [  H ( \tfrac{y - r v_n }{n}  ) - H ( \tfrac{x - r v_n }{n}  )  ] a(y-x)   \bar{\xi} _x^{\alpha}( \eta_r^n ) \bar{\xi} _y^{\beta}( \eta_r^n ) \\
		- & \frac{\Theta(n) K_n}{n \sqrt{n} } \sum_{z=1}^{L_n-1}  za(z) \int_s^t \dd r \sum_{x}   \nabla H ( \tfrac{ \lfloor x - r v_n \rfloor }{n}  )   \bar{\xi} _x^{\alpha}( \eta_r^n )  \bar{\xi} _{x+1}^{\beta}( \eta_r^n )   \Bigg\}^{2} \Bigg] \leq \widehat{C} (t-s)^{1 + \delta_1} f(n), 
	\end{align*}
	for every $n \in \mathbb{N}_+$ and every $L_n$ such that $L_n \geq n^{2/3}$. Furthermore, if $H \in C_c^2(\mathbb{R})$, the role of $\widehat{C}$ is fulfilled by some constant $C(H)$ satisfying \eqref{Cinvshift}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:37:08.320907+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a93e213c7632803afab4ba6234ef35e64fb00a3d8fed5dbfd1e7439648cd50bc","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition d.nonvacuum of arXiv:2608.31071, 'Global smooth solutions to the inhomogeneous Landau--Fermi--Dirac equation'] We say that a measurable function $g\in L^\infty(\Omega \times \mathbb R^3)$ satisfying $0 \le g(x,v) \le 1$ is \emph{non-vacuum} at $(x_0,v_0)$ of size $0 < \delta \le \nicefrac12$ and radius $r>0$ if 
    \begin{equation}
    \delta \leq g(x,v)
        \leq 1 - \delta \qquad \text{for each }(x,v) \in B_r(x_0)\times B_r(v_0).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:33:01.792954+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a940d33e76a69dc5b99019ed9e815e565a2b66a8c10555ca775f64ae2220afbf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 71 (Asymptotic series) of arXiv:2605.14630, '2605.14630'] For every $n\geqs0$ and $N\geqs1$, there exists a constant $M_n$, independent of $N$,
