{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:29:27.984338+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a947af2c24e63127b0813b9a028d402149f8dedbdd6a75ebd7f4961c24aebdab","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 8 (Gaussian local Sobolev inequality) of arXiv:2608.24863, 'Uniform Logarithmic Sobolev Inequalities for the 2D Coulomb Gas at the Diffusive Temperatu'] There exists $C_{\gamma,Q}<\infty$, depending only on $(\gamma,Q)$, such that, for every $R\ge1$,
