{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:52:08.670855+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a94a3a175ab5ae928885dcf029e10cf3b9c9b8516af14a6ac9521824ba1017bb","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 26 (Persistence of the retained fibration on a large block) of arXiv:2608.30027, 'Under Ricci flow, a 3-torus goes flat'] Fix \(\delta_0>0\), \(0<\lambda_{\mathrm{p}}<\delta_0/10\), and
\(\theta_{\max}>0\).  Let
\[
 \theta,\quad \beta_{\mathrm{fib}},\quad \eps_{\mathrm{fib}}
\]
be any fixed choice of constants for which
Lemma~\ref{lem:pointwise-fixed-fiber} holds with these parameters.

Let \(p(\tau)\), \(1\leq\tau\leq100\), be a parabolically rescaled
\(\delta_0\)-large block, and let \(q(\tau)=\Psi_\tau^*p(\tau)\) for a smooth
family of diffeomorphisms.  Let \(r(\tau)\) be a smooth family of invariant metrics for one fixed fibration
\(\pi:M\to S^1\).  Suppose
\begin{equation}
 d_{\TT^2}(r(1))<\theta
\end{equation}
and, for every \(\tau\in[1,100]\),
\begin{equation}
 \|q(\tau)-r(\tau)\|_{C^1(M,r(\tau))}<\beta_{\mathrm{fib}}.
\end{equation}
Suppose also that at every such \(\tau\) there exist an invariant metric \(h_B(\tau)\) and a torus fibration
\(\pi_B(\tau):M\to S_B^1(\tau)\) such that, for every
\(\pi_B(\tau)\)-fiber \(F_B\),
\begin{equation}
 \|h_B(\tau)-q(\tau)\|_{C^1(M,q(\tau))}<\eps_{\mathrm{fib}},
 \qquad
 \diam_{q(\tau)}F_B\leq\eps_{\mathrm{fib}}.
\end{equation}
Then, throughout the block,
\begin{align}
 d_{\TT^2}(r(\tau))&<\theta,                                    \\
 L(S^1,r_{S^1}(\tau))&\geq\lambda_{\mathrm{p}}.                     
\end{align}
Moreover, every \(\pi_B(\tau)\) is fiber-equivalent to \(\pi\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:07:35.011312+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a94ac915dabc1d905e55b954b0cd35d73dc8bae77545521aac23f690207b60a4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 28 of arXiv:2609.02850, 'Canonical-row Chern flow on Bott--Samelson towers:\\ realizable-volume models for Schubert'] Let $\epsilon\in\{0,1\}^{\ell}$.  For an occurrence $t$ of colour $j<n$,
