{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:40:26.998627+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a94c6bdd09a72f695285f396a6a07c47800524816fcd3b7ade88e686aa3fa65c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem-expnumbershreds of arXiv:2604.14318, '\large The free energy of the interacting Bose gas:\\\medskip a variational description \\'] There is a $C\in(0,\infty)$ such that, for any $P\in{\mathcal M }_1^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({\rm s}})}}}({\mathcal S })$, and for any $R\in\mathbb{N}$,
