{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:50:36.757596+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a9537c32a353cfe27f0bc771f77a47f6350fbace8bd79c86c05004365a655d89","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 42 of arXiv:2609.04153, '\vspace*{-3cm}Smooth autonomous fast dynamo action on the three-torus'] Fix $u \in \mathcal{D}$, $\eta>0$, $m_0 \in \NN$, and a compact set $K \subset \CC$ so that uniformly for $\lambda \in K$, $D^{m_0}_{u,\lambda}$ has Lasota--Yorke constant less than $1-2\eta$. Then, there exists $C>0$, so that uniformly for $\lambda \in K$, and all $\eps$ small enough, the operator $\mathcal{K}_{\lambda,\eps}$ satisfies the Lasota--Yorke estimate
\begin{align}
&\|\mathcal{K}^{m_0}_{\lambda,\eps} B_0\|_{\mathcal{E}_u \mathcal X} \leq (1-\eta)(1+C\eps^{\frac{1-2r-\delta}{2}})\|B_0\|_{\mathcal{E}_u \mathcal X}+C\|B_0\|_{\mathcal{E}_u \mathcal Y}\\
&\|\mathcal{K}^{m_0}_{\lambda,\eps} B_0\|_{\mathcal{E}_u \mathcal Y} \leq C\|B_0\|_{\mathcal{E}_u \mathcal Y}\\
