{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:24:20.641071+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a95cc142dcbb6615baa4875df9b19fac4e30e3d2a5438241edb958a764fa8409","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem of arXiv:2608.10415, 'Continuous random variables'] The sequence of cumulants $k_1,k_2,k_3,k_4,\ldots$ is as follows:
\begin{enumerate}
\item For $\mu=\delta_c$ the cumulants are $c,0,0,0,\ldots$

\item For $\mu=g_t$ the cumulants are $0,t,0,0,\ldots$

