where $c_{\gamma} := 1 - 2^{\gamma - 1}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:04.997769+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a9864cf2dd75090b88b1742b25ff2ef25743be5247d9b0d2984f1c66fb8572dd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 59 of arXiv:2604.01685, 'Probability with Measure\footnote{Lecture notes. University of Ljubljana.}'] Let $(\Omega,\FF,\mu)$ and $(\Omega',\FF',\mu')$ be $\sigma$-finite measure spaces. Then we have as follows.
		\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
			\item There exists a unique measure $\nu$ on $\FF\otimes \FF'$, denoted $\mu\times \mu'$,\footnote{The $\times$ in $\mu\times\mu'$ is not the cartesian product; lest we introduce nonstandard notation,  we cannot  avoid denoting different objects with the same symbol (as reprehensible and dangerous as this practice may be).} such that $\nu(A\times A')=\mu(A)\mu'(A')$ for all $(A,A')\in \FF\times \FF'$.
			\item Let $f\in (\FF\otimes \FF')/\mathcal{B}_{[-\infty,\infty]}$ and suppose

						\begin{enumerate}
				\item either $f\geq 0$ (Tonelli) or else
				\item $(\mu\times\mu')[\vert f\vert]<\infty$ (Fubini) or else
				\item  $\int\int f^-(x,x')\mu(\dd x)\mu'(\dd x')\land \int\int f^-(x,x')\mu'(\dd x')\mu(\dd x)<\infty$ (Tonelli-Fubini).
			\end{enumerate}
			 Then 
			$$\left(\Omega'\ni x'\mapsto \int f(x,x')\mu(\dd x)\right)\in \FF'/\mathcal{B}_{[- \infty,\infty]}\text{ and } \left(\Omega\ni x\mapsto \int f(x,x')\mu'(\dd x')\right)\in \FF/\mathcal{B}_{[-\infty,\infty]},$$
			$$\int f^-(x,x')\mu'(\dd x')<\infty\text{ for $\mu$-a.e. $x\in \Omega$ and }\int f^-(x,x')\mu(\dd x)<\infty\text{ for $\mu'$-a.e. $x'\in \Omega'$},$$ and 
		\begin{equation}
			\int f\dd(\mu\times \mu')=\int\int f(x,x')\mu(\dd x)\mu'(\dd x')=\int\int 
			f(x,x')\mu'(\dd x')\mu(\dd x).\\
			\end{equation}

			\end{enumerate}
			Furthermore, all the outer integrals appearing in \eqref{interchange} are well-defined. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:11:11.699161+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a987d211cd5c7274335747cc0ac5285a9aad8d74ab00360bbfbe4e227459187a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:nonresonance of arXiv:2609.00668, 'Rigidity of Euclidean Minimal Hypersurfaces under Nonuniform Diagonal Dilations'] The weights $g_1,\ldots,g_n$ are \emph{pair-sum nonresonant} if
\begin{equation}
g_i+g_j=g_k+g_\ell\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\{i,j\}=\{k,\ell\}
\end{equation}
for unordered pairs $i<j$ and $k<\ell$. Equivalently, the $\binom n2$ pair sums are all distinct.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:13:18.516606+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a98ca622abe32915f38db234f8c98c020e1818d2172635114b2fd81bfc721a86","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 24 of arXiv:2608.30602, '2608.30602'] Let $h_0(z)=\log z\,\chi(z)$ and $h_1(z)=\log z\,\tilde{\chi}(z)$, and let
$|v(x)|\lesssim\langle x\rangle^{-3-}$.
Then, for $j=0,1$, we have
\begin{equation*}
h_j(\lambda|x-y|)-h_j(\lambda a)+\lambda\,r_y(x)\,h_j'(\lambda a)
