for any $\epsilon<\frac{\tilde{\epsilon}}{4} \vee \epsilon_0$ and $\gamma \in [0,\frac{\lambda_1 (\gamma_0-\tilde{\gamma}_0) }{2}]$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:38.636627+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a9c06847a1c1da7ddbd32d22229cd29345e5a24220d3aa5f0750bfcc387267bd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2506.17470, 'The coalescent of a sample from a linear-fractional branching process'] Let  $\mathbf{T}_k$ be a $k$-sample tree. For any $x_1,\dots, x_{k-1} \in  \{1,\ldots, T\}$, let $\{y_1,\ldots, y_d\}$ be the set of its different values, $d< k$. Then, for any $m\ge 0$, 
\begin{equation*}
