{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.581956+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a9f846f27ba69a2b62d0532f1b4703035a5ca99251da84798febad7ea2b73adc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemamconvoutitio of arXiv:2608.30443, 'On smooth holosphere solutions to compressible Euler equation'] There exist universal constants $c_{\nu,a}>0$, $0<b^*(\nu,a)\ll 1$ such that the following holds: for all $0<b<b^*$, for all $0\le k\le K$, 
