{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:00:15.217696+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a9f8fb29b7a968e79d28bed655a8fbdf41ff5b3cdb040bfbb3fad570a93c7cb3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2607.18186, 'Small Counterexamples to the Gaussian Moments Conjecture'] For every $A\in\C[z]$ and $m\geq1$,
