{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:25:41.653688+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a9fac3eef57a7037a48d21b4eb6ec51a827573fad78e033825cb3fc2c7e1e6a5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:universally-stable-graph-sequence of arXiv:2608.15923, 'Universality of two-dimensional Markovian holonomy fields'] A sequence of embedded topological maps $({\mathbb{G}}_n)_{n\geq1}$ is called \emph{universally stable for regular loop families} if:
