\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.776545+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a9fb81016bc46aea3d3c885acfe3c1eeccc066f091745dd1fc7b193f5149b892","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:NBS of arXiv:2608.05089, 'Correlation decay in area-tilted line ensembles'] Suppose that $\mu$ is a {probability} {measure} on $\Omega \subseteq \mathbb{R}^N$ such
that for all {Lipschitz} continuous increasing functions
$f, g : \Omega \to \mathbb{R}$ and $\mathbf{x} \sim \mu$ we have
\begin{equation}
    \operatorname{Cov}\mleft[ f(\mathbf{x}), g(\mathbf{x}) \mright] \geqslant 0.
\end{equation}
Then for all {Lipschitz continuous} functions $F, G : \Omega \to \mathbb{R}$ (not necessarily increasing), we have
\begin{equation}
    \mleft| \operatorname{Cov} \mleft[ F(\mathbf{x}), G(\mathbf{x}) \mright] \mright|
    \leqslant \sum_{i,j=1}^N \operatorname{Lip}_i^\Omega(F) \operatorname{Lip}_j^\Omega(G) \operatorname{Cov}\mleft[ x^i, x^j \mright].
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

