{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:07:56.711234+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aa5182878dfed4b0ebccadeb4b43da1732c292c67b316cda6f30a75e12906faf","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:taurx of arXiv:2411.04773, 'Meeting of squared Bessel flow lines and application to the skew Brownian motion'] Let $r\in {\mathbb R}$. Almost surely: for all $x\ge r$ and $t\ge 0$,
\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
    \item $L_t^r\le x$ for all $t\in [0, \tau_x^r)$, $L_t^r=x$ for $t=\tau_x^r$ and $L_t^r>x$ for all $t>\tau_x^r$;
    \item $X^r_{\tau^r_x}=0$ and $B_{\tau^r_x}=x$;
    \item $\mathcal L(t,x)>\mathcal L(\tau^r_x,x)$ for $x<L_t^r$ and $\mathcal L(t,x)\le \mathcal L(\tau^r_x,x)$ for $x\ge L_t^r$. In particular, $L^r_t=\sup\{x>r\,:\, \mathcal L(t,x)>\mathcal L(\tau^r_x,x)\}\lor r$ where $\sup\emptyset=-\infty$ by convention;
    \item $\mathcal L(t,x)>\mathcal L(\tau_x^r,x)$ if and only if $t>\tau_x^r$;  if $\mathcal L(t,x)<\mathcal L(\tau_x^r,x)$, then $L_t^r<x$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:37:28.980521+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aa51975e4192bf033754ea78e8168d062d06acdde0c49df3be70fcd513172cec","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor WHnlambda of arXiv:2412.00610, 'Joint Poisson Convergence of Monochromatic Hyperedges in Multiplex Hypergraphs'] Let $\{H_n\}_{n\ge 1}$ be a sequence of weighted $r$-uniform hypergraphs as described above with vertices colored uniformly with $c_n$ colors as in (equation eq:cn of the paper). Suppose 
