{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.239916+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aa7a3bc3ed859b17919e4f7683bc949dd3d172a947c283102754c1fb954fed7e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:coordintate_OU of arXiv:2604.22528, 'Malliavin calculus for signatures with applications to finance'] The ``coordinate'' Ornstein--Uhlenbeck semigroup ${\bf T}_\vartheta^i$ and generator ${\bf L}^i$ are given by 
    \begin{equation}
        {\bf T}^i_\vartheta\sigW 
        = \exp\!\left(\frac{1 - e^{-2\vartheta}}{2}\,{{\bf\Psi}}^{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{0}}}}_{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{ii}}}}\right)
          {\bf J}_{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{i}}}}^{\vartheta}\sigW, \qquad     {\bf L}^i\sigW = 
