{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.615346+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aa7c240f55efb34201ce8b60d2de1106025ef00de7a5bdd85fa9f01213454b82","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 3 of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] Let~$\{T_k\}_{k\ge0}$ have the law of $\{\frac12|B_k|^2\}_{k\ge0}$ for~$B$ denoting a standard two-dimen\-sional Brownian motion. Let~$\{Z_{T_k}\}_{k\ge0}$  be a sequence of random Borel measures on~$[0,1]$ coupled with~$\{T_k\}_{k\ge0}$ so that \eqref{E:1.21a} holds as stated. Then
