{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:45:17.712012+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aa88841b5d2d901cf6403bddd255bff129457715a3381fa57253cc8fe83168a2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma CCLCD of arXiv:2604.11761, 'The smallest singular value of signed random combinatorial matrices'] {tran2020smallestsingularvaluerandom}}]
Let $a$ and $v$ be two vectors in $\mathbb{R}^n$ with $\|\mathrm{D}(a) \otimes \mathrm{D}(v)\|_2 \geq b n^{3 / 2}$ for some $b>0$. Let $L>0$ and $u \in(0,1)$. Then for any $\varepsilon \geq 0$, we have
