The constant $C>0$ here depends only on $b$ and $u$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:53.440021+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aa8b5dfc482ee1b85da88ea6e70ae45d36a6ceaff0dea8fa5cbd518054db7cfd","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 9 of arXiv:2606.15425, 'Well-posedness of stochastic parabolic equations with gradient nonlinearities and applicat'] For arbitrary $1\geq \rho > \theta > 0$ and $p \in [1,\infty]$,
