{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:22:21.886309+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aa9376ddfe9e97e0ff27c19c02f9f5ad806251a90b61323e8dc15cec2bb7ba14","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:decreasHypGRF of arXiv:2411.11345, 'Real Gaussian exponential sums via a real moment map'] Let $m>1$ and assume that $f_0(x)\neq 0$ for all $x\in M$ and let $t\in \mathbb{R}$ be a regular value of $\Phi_0$. Consider $S_t:=\Phi_0^{-1}(t)$ smooth hypersurface in $M$. For any admissible random fields $W\randin C^\infty(S_t,\mathbb{R}^{m-2})$ on $S_t$ and all open set $U\subset S_t$, we have:
  \begin{equation}
    \mathbb{E}\#\sol{\mathcal{X}_0|_{S_t},W; U}\leq \mathbb{E}\#\sol{\mathcal{X}|_{S_t},W; U}.
  \end{equation} 
   In particular
  \begin{equation}
    \esol{\mathcal{X}_0|_{S_t}; U}\leq \esol{\mathcal{X}|_{S_t}; U}.
  \end{equation} 
  In both cases, the inequality is an equality if and only if the right hand side is zero in which case every term is equal to zero.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:06:42.722742+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aa93d8822bce77df03cc14dbbfce2a33ad6ab5399fa510f5e0c2f482929d6bd8","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:kernelholojs of arXiv:2411.04238, 'Holomorphic jump-diffusions'] The jump kernel $K$ is said to have holomorphic jump size if it is of the form
   \begin{align*}
    K(\cdot,A)=\lambda(\cdot)\int_E 1_{A\setminus\{0\}} ( j(\cdot,y))F(dy),
\end{align*}
where,
\begin{enumerate}
\item $F$ is a non-negative measure on a measurable space $E$;
    \item $\lambda\in \mathcal{O}(S)$ and its restriction to $S$ is positive real valued;
    \item $j:S\times E \rightarrow \mathbb{R}^d$ such that $ j=j_\varepsilon|_{S\times E}$ for some $\varepsilon>0$ and some measurable function $$j_\varepsilon:P^d_{R(S)+\varepsilon}(0)\times E \rightarrow \mathbb{C}^d$$ with $j_\varepsilon(\cdot,y)\in H(P^d_{R(S)+\varepsilon}(0),\mathbb C^d)$ for each $y \in E$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

