{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:42:39.094153+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aacc1b4b7c830ff9dbae469546f08cdfc25a471c600b1e24a25845b7d62bd7d7","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi Dini of arXiv:2412.08497, 'Time discretization of Quadratic Forward-Backward SDEs with singular drift'] An increasing continuous function $\omega_f: \mathbb{R}_{+}\rightarrow \mathbb{R}_{+}$ is called a Dini function if 
				\begin{equation}
					\int_{0+} \frac{\omega_f(s)}{s}\mathrm{d}s < +\infty.
				\end{equation}
				A measurable function $\omega_f: \mathbb{R}_{+}\rightarrow \mathbb{R}_{+}$ is called a slowly varying function at zero if for every $\lambda >0$
				\begin{equation*}
					\lim_{s\rightarrow 0} \frac{\omega_f(\lambda s)}{\omega_f(s)} = 1.
				\end{equation*}
				A measurable function $f: \mathbb{R}^d \rightarrow \mathbb{R}$ is said to be Dini continuous if there is a Dini function $h$ such that 
				\begin{align}
					|f(x)-f(y)| \leq \omega_f(|x-y|).
				\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:21:56.720734+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aacdb59a7cf8ec40f30858b5e4cd62c6a45fe3b1725a763220a80ac2dfc12fbf","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:detect_intersection_left of arXiv:2507.15589, 'Tightness of approximations to metrics on non-simple conformal loop ensemble gaskets'] Let $z\in D$ and $r>0$ such that $2r < \delta^{1+a_3}$ and $B(z,r) \subseteq D$. Let $e \in \mathcal {E}^\delta_0(\mathcal {L})$ for some $\mathcal {L} \in \widehat{\Gamma}_0^\delta$, and suppose that $U_e \subseteq B(z,r/4)$. Then there exist $z_1 \in \partial B(z,r/2)$, $w_1 \in \partial B(z,r/4)$ such that one of the following is true.
\begin{itemize}
\item Let $\eta^{\theta_0}_{z_1}$ be the angle $\theta_0$ flow line of $h$ starting at $z_1$ and stopped upon exiting $B(z,3r/4)$. Let $\eta^R_{w_1}$ be the angle $-\pi/2$ flow line starting at $w_1$, reflected off $\eta^{\theta_0}_{z_1}$ in the opposite direction, and stopped upon exiting $B(z,r/2)$. Then $\partial U_e \subseteq \eta^R_{w_1} \cup \eta^{\theta_0}_{z_1}$.
\item Let $\eta^{\theta_0}_{z_1}$ be the angle $\theta_0$ flow line of $h$ starting at $z_1$ and stopped upon exiting $B(z,3r/4)$. Let $\eta_{w_1}^L$ be the angle $+\pi/2$ flow line starting at $w_1$. Then it hits $\eta^{\theta_0}_{z_1}$ before exiting $B(z,r/2)$. Let $\overline{w}$ denote the first hitting point, and let $\overline{\eta}^R$ be the angle $-\pi/2$ flow line starting at $\overline{w}$, reflected off $\eta^{\theta_0}_{z_1}$ in the opposite direction, and stopped upon exiting $B(z,r/2)$. Then $\partial U_e \subseteq \overline{\eta}^R \cup \eta^{\theta_0}_{z_1}$.
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:01:48.583076+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aacdf89e09a0c60fe3af991a33f9a8123aed14cee39449ec78c80384411f07b7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop precompact2 of arXiv:2606.30517, '\textsc{Convergence towards Ideal Poisson--Voronoi tessellations with a focus on Diestel--'] Assume $0\neq\nu=\lim_{n \to \infty} \lambda_n\iota_{t_n}^* \mu$, where $t_n\to\infty$.
