{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.269930+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aae56f65161aef96668115fed3a35f49caa8623f3208bdad7487ca1b2565c7f8","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 17 of arXiv:2604.15753, 'The truncation property and continuity for \\ the long-range contact process on $\mathbb{Z'] Let $\lambda \in \Lambda$ be resilient. Then for any $\delta<\delta_c(\lambda)$ there exists constants $C,c \in (0,\infty)$ such that, for any $t>0$ and $\hat{\lambda} \geq \lambda$, 
