{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:09:43.675620+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aaf1033fba48e144054c752972e6b6f48c2419038f2ad1a13af948d0b196bf05","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem scaling limit-cut-off of arXiv:2605.28194, 'Delayed Blow-up in 3D Fluids via Pseudo-Transport Noise'] Fix  $\nu,R_0,R,T>0$ and $ a<\frac{1}{2}<2b+a-\delta$, then $u^N$ converges in probability, in space $\mathcal{X}=L^2(0,T;H^{2b+a})\cap C([0,T];H^{2b+a-\delta})$ to the unique global strong solutions to the deterministic equation with hyperviscosity 
		\begin{equation}
			\left\{
			\begin{aligned}
				& \partial_t u + f_R(\|u\|_{H^{2b+a-\delta}})\Pi (u\cdot\nabla u) =-\frac{3\nu}{5}(-\Delta)^{1+a}u+\Delta u,\\
				& u(0)=u_0.
