{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:47:01.658845+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ab5b48245f7ee1b58a7027610c70fb2eb68553550199541d167e7f6f819e13f6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2604.23461, 'Scaling limit of Sinkhorn-rescaled Random Matrices \\ via Stability of Static Schrödinger '] Let $\phi, \phi' \in L^{\infty}_{>0}(\mu_0 \otimes \mu_1)$ be probability densities with cost functions $\kappa$ and $\kappa'$. For $t \in [0, 1]$, let
