{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:11:11.719883+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ab93af9da023ca5e229c6b88dd02ad5e8a74fa2c745ce408d24161fb93609c76","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:full-residual of arXiv:2609.00698, 'Kinetic Wedge Layers and Diffusive Limit of Neutron Transport in Polygonal Domains'] Assume (equation eq:realization-scale-chain of the paper). With the finite base assembly (equation eq:Ubase-finite-expanded of the paper) and the common coefficients (equation eq:Mless-finite-expanded of the paper), the composite source has the exact finite decomposition (equation eq:source-pieces-expanded of the paper) below and
