{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:16:46.138954+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ab9509e956abaf79124ab29247bd95faf15a1fce0733e4bd11f6b715b5920c38","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:sde-disc of arXiv:2605.03718, 'Potential Hessian Ascent III:\\ Sampling the Sherrington--Kirkpatrick Model at $\beta < 1/'] {chewi2024log}, [dalalyan2012sparse]}]

Fix a stepsize $h>0$ and let $t^-=h\left\lfloor\frac th\right\rfloor$.
Suppose that $f:\mathbb R^n\to \mathbb R^n$ is $L$-Lipschitz. 
    Consider the two SDE's in $\mathbb R^n$,
    \begin{align*}
        dy_t &= f(y_t) dt + dB_t\\
        d\widetilde{y}_t &= f(\widetilde{y}_{t^-}) dt + dB_t,
    \end{align*}
    where $y_0,\widetilde{y}_0\sim \rho_0$.
    Let $T=Nh$, $N\in \mathbb N$. 
    Then
    \begin{align*}
\operatorname{KL}(\mathcal L((\widetilde{y}_t)_{t\in [0,T]})\| \mathcal L((y_t)_{t\in [0,T]}))

&\leqslant 
\fc{L^2h^3}{6} \sum_{k=0}^{N-1} \mathop{{}\mathbb{E}}\ve{f(\widetilde{y}_{kh})}^2 + \fc{T L^2 n h}{2}\\
&\leqslant 
TL^2\pa{\fc{h^2M^2}{6}+ \fc{n h}{2}}
    \end{align*}
where the last inequality holds if $\left\Vert {f}\right\Vert_{\infty}\leqslant M$. If $h\leqslant \fc{\sqrt{3/2}\varepsilon}{\sqrt T LM}\wedge \fc{\varepsilon^2}{2nTL^2}$, then $\operatorname{TV}(\mathcal L((\widetilde{y}_t)_{t\in [0,T]}), \mathcal L((y_t)_{t\in [0,T]}))\leqslant \varepsilon$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:22:01.666359+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ab962a3e0a79220939b0506bfc91aa0bea14e57a2a9937912bb03e4d37dda3aa","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem of arXiv:2605.02226, 'Finitely Dependent Processes on Subshifts'] [Holroyd]
