{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:59:53.334531+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aba21d52fa2ff962a147d826e324170ccef46259e23483edbcbba26949a03048","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:operator of arXiv:2607.24705, 'Derangetropy Operators'] A \emph{kernel} is a probability density $w$ on $[0,1]$; the set of
		kernels is $\mathcal{W}$. The derangetropy operator with kernel $w$ is
