{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:30:28.825071+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_abb77b7bdfc0c9ea47e400504fb34d77d3fa15cc0fa40a39923351e1875b6ebf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2609.02104, 'Conformal Ricci Curvature and Spectral Estimates'] Let $\Omega\Subset M$ be a smooth bounded connected domain in an $n$-dimensional Riemannian manifold, $n\geq2$. Suppose that there exist
