}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:32:11.126206+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_abc2e78679d6132ceec49a2d12fdec568ef71c84645fe8bfa9d18a854fc046ee","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2510.01838, 'Shadow and percolation I: discrete landscapes with independence'] Let $X\in \mathbb{R}^{\mathbb{Z}^2}$ and $j\in \mathbb{Z}^2$. For $u\in \mathbb{Z}$ we denote by $\alpha_j(u)$ the quantity
