{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:01:56.345708+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_abf75c2c7cd49fd9dde7c78807f4c4a3005905913e93244504d07903a0d64df4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem contheights of arXiv:2609.01499, 'On the rigidity of sloped height functions in $d\ge 3$ \\ and non-crossing surfaces'] Let $a_1,a_2,\ldots,a_n,\ldots$ be a sequence of numbers such that $a_i \downarrow a \in \mathbb{R}$ and  all of the measures $\mu_{\mathfrak{s},a_i}$ have densely dominant heights. Furthermore, assume that there exists some $\tilde a< a$ such that $\mu_{\mathfrak{s},\tilde{a}}$ has densely dominant heights. Then, $\mu_{\mathfrak{s},a}$ has weak dominant heights and 
