{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:26.920958+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ac219f41aab1b7497433fac5a143982d140588a02e2cc6785d770cea2f2cc8b4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:4 of arXiv:2505.09604, 'Exceptional force, uncountably many solutions in the KPZ fixed point'] On the event $\Omega_1$, for all $\xi\in\mathbb{R}, (x_0,s)\in\mathbb{R}^2$, and ${\scaleobj{0.9}{\boxempty}} \in \{-,+\}$, if $\tau_t^{\scaleobj{0.8}{\boxempty}} = \tau_{(x_0,s)}^{\xi,{\scaleobj{0.8}{\boxempty}}}(t)$, then
