{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.415024+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ac2c43d0d4f1e5418c0b45a542c5c3638fb47c6cc86cab675304885d10fe003e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 88 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Consider a variational datum satisfying Assumptions~\ref{Assumption_A}, \ref{Assumption_B} and \ref{Assumption_C}. There exist \mbox{$\eps,C>0$} which depend only on the constants in the assumptions such that for any $h\in[H]$ and with the notation $\amsmathbb{B}_h^\eps$ for the complex $\eps$-neighborhood of the bands of $\mu_h$,
