{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:00:15.224180+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ac2d34755fef561c6d8a94532ce75a83f68000c5db249b75c3a4cb3d1813d32b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 58 (Thresholding with extra random leaves) of arXiv:2607.18201, 'Finding Adam in noisy trees'] Fix $k,\ell\in \N\cup\{0\}$, and $p\in (0,1)$. Given a \emph{finite} rooted tree $(\bt,o)\in \cT^*$, construct a random tree as follows.
\begin{itemize}
    \item [(i)]To each vertex $v\in \bt$, add $X_v$ extra leaves, where
    \begin{align*}
        X_v \stackrel{d}{=}\begin{cases}
            &{\rm Bin}((k-d_\bt(v))\vee 0,p),\textrm{ if }v\neq o,\\&
            {\rm Bin}((k-d_\bt(v)-1)\vee 0,p),\textrm{ if }v= o.
        \end{cases} 
    \end{align*}
    and these variables form an independent collection over $v$. Call the obtained random tree $\bt'$.
    \item [(ii)] Construct another random tree   $\bT=\psi^\ell_{\rm off}(\bt',o)$.
\end{itemize}
We view the above procedure as a map $\mu^\ell_{k,p}:\cT^* \to \cP(\cT^*)$, where $\mu^\ell_{k,p}(\bt,o)$ denotes the law of the random rooted tree $(\bT,o)$ thus constructed.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.830278+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ac30c72ee5a0f85c68fa0086b8ce6ffa3e9393fe625c09dc4455b76321e85727","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:ldp of arXiv:2606.28869, '\bfseries A General Theory of Paths:\\ \large Signatures, Jump Lifts, and Expected Signatu'] If a family of driving rough paths satisfies a large-deviation principle in $p$-variation with good rate function $I$, then their level-$N$ signatures satisfy a large-deviation principle with good rate function
