{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:41:29.041111+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ac3feaa4b674568bda2d2cdd6fb03bcf66175043710978609f32c5c7814491f3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 3 (cf.\ Section 2 of \cite{Chen2024}) of arXiv:2608.26598, 'Pinching cones for positive isotropic curvature in dimensions seven and eight'] If $S$ evolves by \eqref{eq:pullback-ode}, then
    \begin{equation}
        \begin{split}
            \dt\Ric(S)={}&2\bigl(S*\Ric(S)\bigr)-4b\,\Ric(S)^2
            +\frac4n\bigl(2b+(n-2)a\bigr)\Scal(S)\Ric(S)\\
            &+2\,\frac{n^2b^2-2(n-1)(a-b)(1-2b)}{n\bigl(1+2(n-1)a\bigr)}\,|\Rico(S)|^2\mathrm{id}
            +\frac4{n^2}(a-b)\Scal(S)^2\mathrm{id},
        \end{split}
    \end{equation}
    where $(S*\Ric)_{ik}=\sum_{p,q}S_{ipkq}\Ric_{pq}$, and $\dt\Scal(S)$ is given by
    \eqref{eq:scalar-evol}. In particular, $P+nQ=2+4(n-1)a$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:58:38.180479+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ac429a75b4b5db59bc31d20f0c481e9610281554b9a2cfb9b485bf494114ac6e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop unsommetvide of arXiv:2606.24793, '\LARGE Random sequential nearest-neighbor coloring on trees'] Let $\eta>0$. Then, there exist $H,C,N,n_0\ge 0$ such that, if $|T|\ge n_0$, then for any choice of vertices $w_1,\ldots,w_C$ of height greater than or equal to $|T|-2H$, starting from $B_0=\{o\}$ and $R_0=\partial T \cup\{w_1,\ldots,w_C\}$, we have
