 \mathbb{P}(\forall 1\le i\le N,\; \mathcal{A}_i^c)\le \eta.
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:07.265376+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ac44d38345f25907da852947d9ffe8f931363f5da86a65117038099e34580874","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2604.19924, 'Fluctuation theory for spectrally negative Lévy processes killed by additive functionals'] The function $Z^{(q)}_{\nu}$ defined in \eqref{sf_Z} is the unique solution to the integral equation
