	where $\mathds{P}_{\mu_\varepsilon}$ denotes the law of ${\rm DEP}$ when initialized according to $\mu_\varepsilon$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.279625+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ac587c9dfb53078c8039c99eb977a3993407cb44c01eb532f89b59804f1ca77f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2606.22611, 'Upper and Lower Bounds on Expected Soft Maxima\\of Gaussian Processes'] Let $X = (X_t)_{t \in T}$ be a centered Gaussian process on a finite index set $T$. Then
