{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:22:48.866646+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ac5cfb7715e54dfb3a75a316cea04a253277b1d71067bbd30a2b4990086d711b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2608.29143, 'Least Variability in a Polynomial-Square Class\\ of Rational Kernels'] Let \(\widetilde a(x)=a(x/\beta)\). Then \(a\mapsto\widetilde a\) is a bijection of \(\Pcal_m\), with inverse \(p(t)\mapsto p(\beta t)\), and
