{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-09-07T12:18:10.808157+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ac61f5db1768f03eb83bb9760d23bbba29637afd515a92c41de92612ba6495b1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2512.19517, 'Spiking and Resetting'] There exists a constant $C>0$ such that for any $\alpha \in (0,1/2)$ and $x\in (0,1)$, the following holds
