{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:26.258787+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ac6bb3a89d1a42540a73d82431c08880f361def4a31bedb1e20a36f0f580735f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 85 of arXiv:2605.23308, 'Convergence rate estimates for semigroups and heat kernels associated with resistance form'] Suppose that $\alpha$ and $\kappa\in (1/2,1]$ satisfy $\alpha>\frac{\kappa}{3\kappa+4}+5\kappa+\frac{7}{2}$.
  Then it holds for any $K\in (0,\infty)$ and $E<\frac{\kappa}{2(3\kappa+4)(\kappa+2)}$ that
