{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:25.281894+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_acaf231880566f7b12278b7c10076e22077085c34ac9a75d7bd930cd56ee71ea","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 1 of arXiv:2606.21778, 'Pontryagin Maximum Principle in Free Probability Theory'] Let $\hat{u} \in U$ and $\hat{x}$ the associated controlled diffusion. Suppose that there exists a solution $(\hat{y}, \hat{z})$ to the associated BSDE \eqref{eq:BSDE-classic}, such that

