{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.502196+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_acb6ac9c0deac0275cc3df3b813b53f6a6e2fcca89f31be2b39d7f740df54d47","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 46 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] Let $f \in C_b^{2 \alpha,3}([0,T] \times W,\bar{W})$ be arbitrary. Then there exists $g \in C_b^{2 \alpha,2}([0,T] \times (W \times W), L(W,\bar{W}))$ with $\| g \|_{C_b^{2 \alpha,2}} \leq \| f \|_{C_b^{2 \alpha,3}}$ such that
