{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:41:28.179569+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_acfb80632f79e0a9eb421c6e05a0606dcbcf3a2d8934366a6e82a05905e9ca64","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:Main of arXiv:2511.10630, 'Cutoff for generalised Bernoulli--Laplace urn models'] Let $d, m \in \mathbb{N}$ be fixed with $d, m \geqslant 2$. Consider a sequence $\{\mathbf{X}^{(n)}\}_{n \in \mathbb{N}}$ of generalised Bernoulli--Laplace chains where the $n^{\mathrm{th}}$ chain has parameters $(d, m, n, \mu_n)$. Suppose that the Cheeger constant of the single ball transition matrix satisfies $\Phi_{\ast}^{(n)} = \Omega(1)$. Then, for any $\varepsilon \in (0,1)$, we have
