{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:28:53.628359+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ad04f598cd8d9bfa650864a6c550d158e39dbf587cb646ead730975dcc09bb2c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 (Strong solution to Hamilton--Jacobi equation) of arXiv:2605.13512, '2605.13512'] Assume \ref{ass:pde-speed}. The limiting current $v(x,t)$, given by equation \eqref{eq:vdef}, is a solution to the Cauchy problem \eqref{eq:genHJ} with flux given by \eqref{eq:discoflux}, at all points $(x,t)$ that are differentiability points of $v(x,t)$ and continuity points of $\tilde c(x,-v(x,t))$. 

