\dif X_{j,t}=\mu_{j,t}\dif t + (\bm{\sigma}_t\dif B_t)_j,
\end{equation}
where $\mu_{j,t}\in\C$, $\bm{\sigma}_t\in\C^{p\times d}$ for some $d\in\N$, and $\dif B_t$ is the standard Brownian motion in $\R^d$. Assume that $X_{j,t}$ has all finite moments for all $j\in[p]$ and $t\in [0,T]$. Then it holds that
\begin{equation}
\frac{\dif}{\dif t}\kappa\left(\lbrace X_{j,t}\rbrace_{j\in[p]}\right) = \sum_{i=1}^p \kappa\left(\mu_{i,t},\lbrace X_{j,t}\rbrace_{j\in[p]\setminus\{i\}}\right) + \sum_{1\le i<h\le p}\kappa\left(\frac{\dif}{\dif t}[X_i,X_h]_t,\lbrace X_{j,t}\rbrace_{j\in[p]\setminus\{i,h\}}\right), 

\end{equation} 
for any $t\in [0,T]$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:03.902723+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ad06b90ff59d7532429dc94e3355e2d72ed16d9f248c725f73e636db7dfd8578","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 22 of arXiv:2606.20908, 'On It\^o-Stratonovich formula for rough sheets'] Let $f\in\cp_{1,1}$ and $g\in\cp_{2,2}$ (see~\eqref{c3}), let $\kappa_{1},\kappa_{2}>0$ and $p\geq 1$, and let $\eps>0$ be a small parameter. In all items below, $U^{2}_{\kappa_{1},\kappa_{2},p}$ is the functional introduced in Definition~\ref{def:U2}.
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textnormal{\textbf{(\roman*)}}]
    \item If $U^2_{\kappa_1,\kappa_2,p}(\delta f) < \infty$, then $f \in \cp^{\kappa_1,\kappa_2}_{1,1}$; more precisely
\begin{align}
\|\delta f\|_{\kappa_1,\kappa_2} \leq c_2  U^2_{\kappa_1,\kappa_2,p}(\delta f),
\end{align}
for a universal constant $c_2 > 0$.

   \item 
   Assume that \,$\doo g\in \cp_{3,2}^{\ka_1,\ka_2}$, $\dt g\in \cp_{2,3}^{\ka_1+\eps,\ka_2}$,  and $U^2_{\ka_1,\ka_2,p}(g)<\infty$.
   Then for all $p>\frac{1}{2\eps}$ we have
   \begin{align}
   \lVert g\rVert_{\kappa_1,\kappa_2}\le c_3 \Bigl(U^2_{\ka_1,\ka_2,p}(g)+\lVert \doo g \rVert_{\ka_1,\ka_2}+\lVert \dt g \rVert_{\ka_1+\eps,\ka_2}\Bigl),
   \end{align}
   for some constant $c_3$ depending on $\varepsilon$ and $p$.

    \item 
    Suppose that $\doo g\in \cp_{3,2}^{\ka_1,\ka_2+\eps}$, $\dt g\in \cp_{2,3}^{\ka_1,\ka_2}$, and $U^2_{\ka_1,\ka_2,p}(g)<\infty$. Then for all $p>\frac{1}{2\eps}$ we have
   \begin{align}
   \lVert g\rVert_{\kappa_1,\kappa_2}\le c_4 \Bigl(U^2_{\ka_1,\ka_2,p}(g)+\lVert \doo g \rVert_{\ka_1,\ka_2+\eps}+\lVert \dt g \rVert_{\ka_1,\ka_2}\Bigl),
   \end{align}
    for some constant $c_4$ depending on $\varepsilon$ and $p$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:11.412044+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ad0871428355c278b4d93651881b95165b2109a384993d9a302cd8018a82c839","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 26 (Sudakov-type comparison through supremum relaxation) of arXiv:2606.07931, 'Pointwise Complexity for Gaussian Fields:\\Upper Envelopes, Algorithmic Lower Bounds, and '] In the Gaussian location setup of Theorem~\ref{thm:nn-comparison}, take the ordinary nearest-neighbor decoder and the centered reference law.  If \(L_\pi(\Delta)\) is above a universal constant, then choosing
\[
\tau^2\asymp \frac{\mathsf V_\pi}{L_\pi(\Delta)}
\]
yields
\begin{equation}
\mathbb E\sup_{s,u\in T}(X_s-X_u)
\gtrsim
\Delta^2\sqrt{\frac{L_\pi(\Delta)}{\mathsf V_\pi}}.
