whenever the logarithm is above the universal threshold required by the information condition.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.369629+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ad09279c1e3593e4d882325542552d50c80bbb1c481346afd4fe6dbf025e54d6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Propo g of arXiv:2412.01673, 'Spatial SIR epidemic model with varying infectivity without movement of individuals'] For all $\varphi \in C_b(D)$, $\left\{ \overline{\mu}_t^{S,N},\overline{\mu}_t^{\mathfrak{F},N},\overline{\mu}_t^{I,N}, \overline{\mu}_t^{R,N},\ t\ge0\right\}$ satisfies
