{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:36:31.233851+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ad20a4a1628310b979de5630cce6582cc8e7737df25739522e43a41be35cfb6d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 ({\cite{bhatt2022Prismsa}*{Lemma 4.22}}) of arXiv:2609.00567, 'Hodge--Tate splitting and Akizuki--Nakano vanishing in positive characteristic'] Let \(A\to A'\) be a flat morphism of commutative rings, and let \(K^\bullet\) be a cosimplicial object of \(\mcalD(A)\). Assume that there exists an integer \(c\) such that \(K^n\in\mcalD^{\geq c}(A)\) for every integer \(n\geq0\). Then the canonical morphism
