{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:41:28.161788+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ad46f89984e39376716aaa8789c2984e2fd0ac61cdc31a6a5f0094ef6e7bc0b0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:d-East of arXiv:2510.20461, 'Long time behaviour of one facilitated kinetically constrained models: results and open pr'] Let $\mu$ be a stationary measure for the $d$-dimensional East model, and define $\mu_*$ as the law of the random variable $\bp{\eta}{}$ when $\eta\sim \mu$. Then
