{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:09:23.967571+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ad7883ef8c3fc2c94a7517c49e3203db61b3fb0d9bd60f44c540d12c0bb3dafa","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 10 (Symmetric Nash equilibrium) of arXiv:2607.22416, 'A multi-player optimal stopping game based on a spider Brownian bridge'] We say that $(\tau^{*},\sigma^{*})\in\mathcal{T}^{\mathbb{SQ}}\times \mathcal{T}^{\mathbb{SQ}}$ is a symmetric Nash equilibrium within the class of square-root threshold strategies if 
    \begin{align*}
