{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.586640+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ad7dddbbdb117972ab56d01b5c3c8e658679528b8612618537e9b05d8764268f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm intro-thm-3 of arXiv:2608.30518, 'Grow-up rates of inhomogeneous semilinear heat equations in the critical dimension'] Assume the hypotheses of Theorem (intro-thm-2 of the paper). Let $\Phi:=u^{*}-u$ and $\varphi_1>0$ be the principal eigenfunction of $\mathcal{L}$ with $\|\varphi_1 \|_{L^2(B_1)}=1$. 
Then, there exist $M,C,T>0$ depending only on $u_0$ and $f$ such that 
\begin{equation*}
\frac{1}{C}e^{-\mu_1 t}\Bigl(\zeta_2(t)\varphi_1+\nu |\zeta_2'(t)|r^{-4}\log r \Bigr)- Me^{-\mu_1 t}|\zeta_2'(t)| \varphi_1 \le \Phi \quad \text{in $B_1\times (T,\infty)$}
\end{equation*}
and
