{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:18:19.225772+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ad87cd83f6cf8dce24fcded7c332ba1b77d7f0b7e12831eb4e7eafe9d1bd5e68","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 18 of arXiv:2608.29086, '2608.29086'] [$A$ and $|A|$]
``$A$'' denotes a collection of non-overlapping loops of length $6$ on $M_0$ that fill $|M_0|$ (Figure \ref{figure2} (a) left), i.e.,
