    \end{split}
  \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:39:11.673736+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ada9838ade20a4a6f38473503d83ede204c3d35fe3c28eb843326276c092381b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2608.04853, 'Minimal-Norm Extensions of Stationary Kernels on Subgroups of Locally Compact Abelian Grou'] Let $H \subseteq G$ be a closed subgroup. Given a stationary kernel $k$ on $G$, the spectral density $\hat{k}_H:\hat{H} \to \R$ of the restricted kernel is given by 
\begin{align*}
    \hat{k}_H(\xi_H)= \int_{H^\perp} \hat{k}(\xi_H+\xi^\perp) \d \xi^\perp.
\end{align*}
If 
\begin{align}
    \sup_{\xi_H \in \hat{G}/H^\perp} \int_{H^\perp} \hat{k}(\xi_H + \xi^\perp) \d \xi^\perp < \infty,
\end{align}
additionally holds, then $\mathcal{N}(H) \subseteq L^2(H)$. 

If $G$ is compact, \eqref{eq:L2Condition} is satisfied.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:18:19.223627+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_adaaa849541c28fca5bd92b2153d792c52af7752c4bd920730e38f03ebfe0ee7","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 7 of arXiv:2608.29086, '2608.29086'] [Region] 
Given $M \subset M_0$ and $R \subset \mathbf{R}^2$. $R$ is called a \textit{region} on $M$ if it is a union of triangles in $Tri(M)$, i.e.,
\begin{equation*}
\exists U \subset Tri(M) \text{ such that } R=\bigcup_{abc \in U}  abc  \subset \mathbf{R}^2.
\end{equation*}
$REG(M)$ denotes the collection of all regions on $M$, i.e.,
\begin{equation*}
REG(M):=\{ \bigcup_{abc \in U}  abc  \subset \mathbf{R} \ |\  U \subset Tri(M) \}.
\end{equation*}
 A collection of regions is called a \textit{region complex}. 
 Given a region complex $R=\{r_1,\ r_2,\ \ldots,\ r_k\} \subset REG(M)$ ($k \in \mathbf{N}$). $|R|$ denotes the union of all regions in $R$, i.e., 
\begin{equation*}
|R|:=r_1 \cup r_2 \cup \cdots \cup r_k \quad \in REG(M).
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:38:58.687091+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_adabcf596335e86854dbdd985f2000a5834950b01584a403523a908307f69454","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem n_j-bound of arXiv:2510.18856, 'Evolution of recursive trees with limited memory'] We have \begin{enumeratei}
