{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.709063+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_adb8075fb88b15d2773f0ed657d784b2aaf7ab89c9212efaa6adafbac6e5baa0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:suplinpa of arXiv:2411.18749, 'A star is born: Explosive Crump--Mode--Jagers branching processes'] Let $(T_{i})_{i \in \mathbb{N}}$ be a preferential attachment tree with fitness function $f$ that satisfies Assumption~(equation eq:minfass of the paper). Let $(\lambda_n)_{n\in\mathbb{N}}\subset [0,\infty)$ be increasing and tend to infinity with $n$, such that there exists $N\in\mathbb{N}$ with $\lambda_n< f(i,w^*)$ for all $i\geq n\geq N$. If
