{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.916845+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ade54e390fa261b8c924a1e3661f979af74e4e1423c8fe9b460ab8e9420a088d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm|Beckner of arXiv:2504.08935, 'Higher-Order Derivatives of First-Passage Percolation with Respect to the Environment'] If $P_Lf$ is the projection of $f$ to the $\text{span} \left\{r_Q: |Q|\leq L\right\}$, then for each $q\geq 2$, there exists a constant $\alpha=\alpha(p,q)>0$ such that
