{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:58:09.905777+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae299cdfb1af8a4502578a99b61466a247484fb0df1715e286437c695e8835c0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:weighted-mgf of arXiv:2607.19583, 'Density-Dependent McKean--Vlasov Diffusions: Subgaussian Occupancy Bounds and Polynomial P'] Suppose the density admits the global Gaussian envelope $p(x)\le C_0e^{-c_0|x|^2}$. If $L_\Xi = 0$, the conclusion is trivial. Otherwise, there exist $\alpha_*,C_*\in(0,\infty)$, depending only on $d,C_0,c_0,R,L_\Xi$, such that 
