{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:43:43.390276+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae31412f350660246bdbea37d0ae3c41cc8d34dcfe70a19e05debe1a2506f109","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop p.axioms of arXiv:2507.16056, 'Conditional GMC within the stochastic heat flow'] Take $q\in(0,\infty),\theta'\in\mathbb{R}$, and any probability space that houses random $M'_{[s,t]}\in\mathcal{M}_+(\Gamma_{[s,t]})$ for $s<t\in q\mathbb{D}$. Write $Z'_{s,t}:=M'_{[s,t]}\circ\margin{\{s,t\}}^{-1}$ for the time-$\{s,t\}$ marginal.
If for all $t_0<\cdots<t_{\ell}\inq\mathbb{D}$ we have that
\begin{enumerate}
\setcounter{enumi}{1}
