{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:53.436679+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae3e2f87a1c1ef1918bd52d40f25d1a5a06af138378d0076948da159eedd82f3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 2 of arXiv:2606.15178, 'The distribution of the de Moivre experiment'] Let $ X $ be a random variable that follows an $s$-Bernoulli distribution with parameter $ p $, $ X \sim \mathcal {B}^{(s)} (p) $. Then the expectation and the variance of $ X $ are
