{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:02:17.908297+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae4a3226afa257dd25480ef279cbef11a2d277feccab79076f7b885c287e19e4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:aniso_inj_holder of arXiv:2602.08591, 'The Yang--Mills measure on compact surfaces as a \\ universal scaling limit of lattice gau'] For every $\alpha\in (0,1)$, any element $T\in \mathcal{C}^{\alpha,\alpha-1}_{x,y}(I\times J)$ for every $\chi\in C^\infty_c(J)$, the product $T1_I\chi$ which is well--defined
