  with $\nu$-high probability. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:22:21.882822+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae7a58a13cc3e20d237b58fec385a906d7eef8244274768d9fd28a2b035651b8","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:zeta as ellips of arXiv:2411.11345, 'Real Gaussian exponential sums via a real moment map'] Let $\mathcal{X}\randin \mathscr{F}\subset C^\infty(M)$ be an admissible centered Gaussian random field with covariance $\Sigma$. Endow $\mathscr{F}$ with the scalar product induced by $\Sigma$. Then, for all $x\in M$, we have
  \begin{equation}
    \zeta_\mathcal{X}(x)=\frac{1}{2\pi \sqrt{\mathrm{K}(x)}}(D_x\circ \pi_x)(B_{\Sigma}^\circ)
  \end{equation}
  where $\pi_x:\mathscr{F}\to \mathscr{F}_x$ is the orthogonal projection and where recall that $B_\Sigma^\circ$ denotes the dual of the unit ball of the quadratic form $\Sigma$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:22:08.539870+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae7bb7c6d64273168003f979188966deb625baa9759f96326b46aaa65160e849","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:CT-TASEP-multipoint of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] The dressed edge weights satisfy the mixed diamond
equation
