{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:19:00.856656+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae7da7bed918992150e709d87cc75587830ba37cd5bb00fffce7052ec60c34e3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 2 (Donsker--Varadhan / finite-measure Gibbs formula\cite{balsubramani2026information}) of arXiv:2608.20337, 'Information on trajectories:\\ martingales and random times'] Let $\mu$ be a finite positive measure on $(\cX,\cB)$ and let $g \colon \cX \to [0,\infty)$ be measurable with $0 < \int g\,\dd\mu < \infty$.
Let $Q^\star$ be the Gibbs measure $\dd Q^\star/\dd\mu = g / \int g\,\dd\mu$, a probability measure supported on $\{g > 0\}$.
Then for every probability measure $Q \ll \mu$ with $Q(\{g = 0\}) = 0$,
\begin{equation}
  \log \int g\,\dd\mu
  = \E_Q[\log g] - \KL(Q\|\mu) + \KL(Q\|Q^\star).
\end{equation}
Consequently,
\begin{equation}
  \log \int g\,\dd\mu
  = \sup_{Q \ll \mu}\bigl\{\E_Q[\log g] - \KL(Q\|\mu)\bigr\},
\end{equation}
with unique maximizer $Q = Q^\star$ (a $Q$ charging $\{g = 0\}$ has $\E_Q[\log g] = -\infty$ and is never optimal, so the supremum is unchanged by restricting to $Q \ll Q^\star$). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:52:51.757453+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae807cb82d6a6dd7bc56e676df18ce583fe05b4830f0ae7ac60574e25dcfad45","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor fmar of arXiv:2604.24061, 'A characterization of ruin-inducing probability measures in a renewal risk model'] Let \(u{\,\in\,}\mathbb R_+\) and \(r{\,\in\,}[0,r_{X_1})\), where \(r_{X_1}{\,>\,}0\). The following assertions hold:
\begin{enumerate}
