\[
Q_{X_1}^{(r)}(F):=\frac{\int_F e^{r\cdot x}\, P_{X_1}(dx)}{M_{X_1}(r)}\,\, \text{ and } \,\, Q_{W_1}^{(r)}(E):=\frac{\int_E e^{-y(r)\cdot w }\, P_{W_1}(dw)}{M_{W_1}\big(-y(r)\big)}
\]
for any $F,E{\,\in\,}\mathfrak B(0,\infty)$, there exists an essentially unique pair $(\gamma_r,\delta_r){\,\in\,}\hyperlink{fp}{\mathcal F_P}{\,\times\,}\hyperlink{gp}{\mathcal G_P}$ with  
