{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.251636+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae81d6744e1fa4938589ee966f5a5da19a35e5c8b7ffecfa5a5b0771384815ad","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2604.15226, '\bfseries Nonlinear Schrödinger equations with spatial white noise potential on full space'] Let $p_1,p_2,q_1,q_2\in[1,\infty]$ and $\mu,\mu'\in\R$ such that $p_1\le p_2,q_1\le q_2$ and $\mu_1\ge\mu_2$. For all $\alpha\in \R$, one has the Besov embeddings
\begin{equation*}
\mathcal{B}^\alpha_{p_1,q_1,\mu_1}(\R^d) \subset  \mathcal{B}^{\alpha-d\left(\frac{1}{p_1}-\frac{1}{p_2} \right)}_{p_2,q_2,\mu_2}(\R^d).
\end{equation*}
as well as the Sobolev embeddings
\begin{equation*}
\forall\alpha\ge \frac{d}{2}-\frac{d}{p},\quad \CH^\alpha_{\mu}(\R^d) \subset  L^p_{\mu}(\R^d)
