for $p\in[2,\infty]$. Finally, the embedding
\begin{equation*}
\CH_{\mu_1}^{\alpha_1}(\R^d)\hookrightarrow\CH_{\mu_2}^{\alpha_2}(\R^d)
\end{equation*}
is compact for $\alpha_1>\alpha_2$ and $\mu_1>\mu_2$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:04.963330+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae8440c6cd5c9ca890773d7be17cb041aada1a95d60844baa58b47672583f01b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2 of arXiv:2604.00742, 'Delayed Logistic equation as a limit\\ of long memory Markov chains'] For each $p \geq 1$ and $N \in \N$, there exists a constant $K_{N} \in (1, 1+1/N)$ such that 
	\begin{equation*}
		\E\left[\bigg(\sup_{t \in [0,T]} Y^{N}(t)\bigg)^p\right] \;\leq\; \mu^p \exp\left\{pK_{N}^{p-1}T\right\}.
