\end{equation*}
where $\mathfrak{m}_p^N(t):=\E[(Y^N(t))^p]$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:01:56.345072+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae851f5a0b32567e6b7eaed5ad92ad3fb8f81e0ce191d14fc421b92f38236fe3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem excitation-statistics-bound of arXiv:2609.01499, 'On the rigidity of sloped height functions in $d\ge 3$ \\ and non-crossing surfaces'] If $\mu_\infty^\nabla$ satisfies~(equation eq:exp-suppressed-gradients-condition of the paper) and $\beta_0$ is sufficiently large, for a universal constant $c'>0$ and for every $0 \le \ell \le \log_2 (\frac{1}{100 c \beta_0} \log L)$ (where $c$ is the constant from~(equation eq:exp-suppressed-gradients-condition of the paper)), 
    \begin{align*}
        \mu_{\infty}^\nabla\Big(\sum_{\boldsymbol{\zeta} \in A_\ell} W(\boldsymbol{\zeta}) \ge e^{ - c' \beta_0 2^{\ell}} L^2 \Big) \le e^{ - L^{0.9}}\,.
