{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:25:35.588557+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae8a0cce1cf1752c8831a3c025bfb7688297b9b9cef2464a221cd46f74b6596c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th:L2 of arXiv:2603.00705, '$L^2$-cutoff for the averaging process \\ on random regular graphs'] Let, for every integer $d\ge 3$,
			\begin{equation}
				\gamma=\gamma_d:= \begin{dcases}
