{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:43:55.657831+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae9fff6bae82d3d81534f14dbf7232a5d56dbc57508e9ae3c270c3553462204d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:increment-rademacher of arXiv:2604.05941, 'Banach spaces of continuous paths with finite $p$-th variation'] For $n\ge1$ and $k\in I_n$, set $\Delta_k^n x:=x(\frac{k+1}{2^n})-x(\frac{k+1}{2^n})$. Under Assumption~(assum: uniform mag of the paper), we define for any $p>1$
