{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:46:12.272575+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_af35c2d0ec7d0d833c4fe59bdeed59d772510b35d2056da53b1ff2d865e9cfd7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 19 (Compressed $S$-transform of $xP_sx^\ast$ (R-diagonal case)) of arXiv:2604.22114, 'Free compressions of R-diagonal random variables and the semigroup of Brown measures'] Let $x = u h \in \widetilde \AA$ be an $R$-diagonal random variable with $u$ Haar unitary and $h \geq 0$. Let $P_s$, $s \geq 1$ be a projection, $\ast$-free of $\{u, h\}$, with $\varphi(P_s) = 1/s$. Let $y_s =  [P_s s(x P_s x^\ast) P_s] \in \widetilde \AA_{P_s}$.  Then, 
