{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:49:25.050363+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_af36d2eeb2d85ef814457745dacb8172fcc289f6c2d17fb40ff3e795367262ca","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition p:fiber-prod-def-space of arXiv:2609.03731, 'Weightings and Lie groupoids'] Let $(M,N,\ensuremath{\mathcal{I}}_\bullet)$, $(M',N',\ensuremath{\mathcal{I}}'_\bullet)$, and $(M'',N'',\ensuremath{\mathcal{I}}''_\bullet)$ be weighted manifolds. Let $f\colon M\rightarrow M''$, $f'\colon M'\rightarrow M''$ be weighted morphisms that are weighted transverse. Then $\nu_w(f),\nu_w(f')$ (resp. $\ensuremath{\mathcal{D}}_w(f),\ensuremath{\mathcal{D}}_w(f')$) are transverse and the canonical morphisms are isomorphisms
\begin{align*} 
\nu_w(M\times_{M''}M',N\times_{N''}N')&\xrightarrow{\sim} \nu_w(M,N)\times_{\nu_w(M'',N'')}\nu_w(M',N'),\\
\ensuremath{\mathcal{D}}_w(M\times_{M''}M',N\times_{N''}N')&\xrightarrow{\sim} \ensuremath{\mathcal{D}}_w(M,N)\times_{\ensuremath{\mathcal{D}}_w(M'',N'')}\ensuremath{\mathcal{D}}_w(M',N'),
\end{align*} 
in the category of graded bundles, resp. the category of $\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^\times$-manifolds equipped with a $\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^\times$-equivariant submersion to $\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:40.046452+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_af38c4febf312bdb03d8fb3bd4acf0b47355a17b69f1e0df6468b86153baeb19","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 5 of arXiv:2510.24562, 'Hard wall repulsion for the discrete Gaussian free field in random environment on $\mathbb'] Recall $L \geq 1$, $K \geq 100$. Let $r=r(L)>0$ such that $r(L)\to \infty$ as $L \to \infty$, $b=b(L)>0$ bounded sequence, and $\beta \geq 0$. Then, for every $\Delta, \Theta > 0$ it holds that
    \begin{equation}
        \begin{aligned}

        & \varlimsup_{L \to \infty} \sup_{\omega\in\Omega_{\lambda,\Lambda}} \sup_{\cS} \sup_{x\in\bbZ^d} \Bigg\{ \bbP^\omega \Big[ \sup_{f \in \cF} Z^\omega_{f,\beta,b} \geq b \Delta -\beta \Theta \Big] \\
        & \quad - 2   \exp \Bigg[ -\frac{1}{2} \bigg( b \bigg( \Delta - \frac{c_7}{K^{c_8}}\sqrt{\frac{|\cS|}{\capa^\omega(S)}} \bigg) -\beta \Theta \bigg)_+^2 \frac{\capa^\omega(S)}{c_6\beta^2 r^{2-d}\capa^\omega(S)+\alpha^\omega_{K,L,\beta,b}} \Bigg] \Bigg\} \leq 0 \,,
        \end{aligned}
    \end{equation}
    where $\alpha^\omega_{K,L,\beta,b}$ is defined in Theorem~\ref{thm:ZfbetabBounds}. When $\beta = 0$, and $b = 1$ this bound simplifies to
      \begin{equation}

        \begin{aligned}
            & \varlimsup_{L \to \infty} \sup_{\omega\in\Omega_{\lambda,\Lambda}} \sup_{\cS} \sup_{x\in\bbZ^d} \Bigg\{ \bbP^\omega \Big[ \sup_{f \in \cF} Z^\omega_{f} \geq \Delta \Big] \\
            & \quad - 2 \exp \Bigg[ -\frac{1}{2} \bigg( \Delta - \frac{c_7}{K^{c_8}}\sqrt{\frac{|\cS|}{\capa^\omega(S)}} \bigg)_+^2 \frac{\capa^\omega(S)}{1+U(K,L)} \Bigg] \Bigg\} \leq 0\,,
        \end{aligned}
    \end{equation}
    with $U(K,L)$ as in Theorem~\ref{thm:ZfbetabBounds}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:32:28.996883+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_af38dc3277da08f0e8e9b054e959abffca51658909383830d18dc0a64c76d4d2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem CT UB of arXiv:2608.25471, 'Exact Hausdorff measures and fine geometry of collisions of independent Markov processes'] For all $t \in (0, 1 \wedge t_*)$ and $n \in \mathbb{N}$, 
