{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:37:08.321420+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_af3a7195b2d6a65a5693a82e426ef144ac71c13a0c3cf4dd14411df8b812d4d1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:geometry of arXiv:2608.31071, 'Global smooth solutions to the inhomogeneous Landau--Fermi--Dirac equation'] Fix $\Lambda > 0$ and $m > 0$ and define $b(v)$ as in (equation defn:barrier of the paper) using these values. Then, there is a $\delta\in (0,1)$, depending only on $m$, such that
