{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:02:34.836624+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_af3b1ae0655c95bddf1ae3b241fe8d86193a37b2402e112ddcaa00f4f126c424","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 6 of arXiv:2607.20646, 'The Independence-Preserving Property and Planar Web Geometry'] Under the assumptions of \cref{thm:characterization}, assume moreover that three linearly independent Abelian relations 
    \begin{align}
        \big(\Phi_i^X(x), \Phi_i^Y(y), -\Phi_i^U(u), -\Phi_i^V(v)\big) \in \A(\W_F) \quad (i = 1, 2, 3)
