{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:41:28.183538+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_af3dea32e3c732adc007c95cc0065878ca8fc16c5397f8c40e5d495df7cb6f6a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:RGrowth of arXiv:2511.10630, 'Cutoff for generalised Bernoulli--Laplace urn models'] There exist some constant $C_0 > 0$, depending only on $C$, $d$, and $m$, such that for all $\delta \in (0, 1]$ and $n$ sufficiently large, we have
