The implicit constant in $\mathcal{O}(\cdot)$ in the rhs. of (equation eq:determ_truncation of the paper) is uniform in $x_j\in [c_0,1]$, $j=1,2$, and may depend on $\|\Delta f_j\|_{L^2(\Omega)}$ and $|\Omega|$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.356639+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_af407e18934158f55291717f6206c012d72dde0479dcd28c6c15b5136fb810fb","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:uniqueness_lemma_weak_sol of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] Fix $R,\mu>0$ and $p,q\in (2,\infty)$ satisfying (equation eq:condition_pq_subcritical_scaling_cutoff of the paper). Then, for all $u_0\in \mathbb{B}^{1-2/p}_{q,p}(\mathbb{T}^3)$, weak solutions to (equation eq:navier_stokes_cutoff_det of the paper) are unique, and coincide with the $(p,q)$-solution provided by Lemma (l:global_cutoff of the paper). Moreover, if $(u_0^N)_N$ is a sequence of initial data weakly converging to $u_0$ in $B^{1-2/p}_{q,p}$, then 
