{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.577719+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_af4c02b3665216e9562a08f423935edbb3b8e33c58618b7807411fd903826230","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma d:DivergenceAdjoint:0 of arXiv:2411.14936, 'Massive Particle Systems,\\Wasserstein Brownian Motions,\\ and the Dean--Kawasaki Equation'] {HinRoeTep13}}]
 The operator~$\mathsf{div}$ has a unique bounded linear extension~$\mathsf{div}\colon \msH_{}\to \mbbA_1'$ with~$\norm{\mathsf{div} v}_{\mbbA_1'}\leq \sqrt{2}\left\lVertv\right\rVert_{\msH_{}}$ for~$v\in\msH_{}$ and satisfying the adjunction relation
