{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:44:17.358489+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_af5a7e26d04077f7f5601576b0561d2efd9020b8dfcddd7857c8fb623a35aa03","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:df of arXiv:2608.23860, 'Revelation Control'] The obstruction admits the exact decomposition
\begin{equation}
\boxed{
\mathcal O_t^{\rm DF}
=
L_t+\max_{a\in\mathcal A}\{\gamma\omega_t(a)-d_t(a)\}.
}

\end{equation}
Moreover,
\begin{equation}
\mathcal O_t^{\rm DF}=0
\iff
L_t=0
\quad\text{and}\quad
\gamma\omega_t(a)\le d_t(a)\ \forall a.
\end{equation}
In particular, if $\gamma>0$ and any current coarse-optimal action has $\omega_t(a)>0$, then the coarse representation is dynamically insufficient even when $L_t=0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:09:59.306575+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_af5bfa1e0ef7d96d6936a5599966d3eea2f05d5331ab4f1f68dfdcc32095c342","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:budget of arXiv:2608.07842, 'Resolution of a Conjecture on Shifted R\'enyi Divergence'] Let $D$ be a scalar $N(a,\tau^2)$ variable with $2\tau^2<w^2$. Then
$$\mathbb{E}\exp(D^2/w^2)=\Big(1-\frac{2\tau^2}{w^2}\Big)^{-1/2}\exp\Big(\frac{a^2}{w^2-2\tau^2}\Big),$$
so $\mathbb{E}\exp(D^2/w^2)=2$ iff
\begin{equation}
a^2=(w^2-2\tau^2)\Big(\log 2+{\tfrac12}\log\Big(1-\frac{2\tau^2}{w^2}\Big)\Big).
