{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.350119+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_afa3051296acf4aa3c59805b6ec22408d0af42d5fa1748bac5367db28b61d079","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem theorem_herrydensity of arXiv:2509.18045, 'Density convergence on Markov diffusion chaos via Stein's method'] Let $F\in \mathcal{A}$ and $\Gamma(F)^{-1}\in L^{4N+4}(E,\mu)$ for some $N\in \mathbb{N}$. Then $F$ admits a density that is N-time differentiable. Moreover for $0\leq k\leq N$, the k-th derivative of the density function has the representation
