    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:00.617902+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_afb798d895fbd009787255c59d8423fd93acf1817fd954f2190bfd1ffd9b138d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 69 of arXiv:2510.27589, 'Geodesic switches and exceptional times in dynamical Brownian last passage percolation'] Fix $k=1$. Let $\mathbf{a},t,s$ be such that $2\leq 2t<s$ and $[\mathbf{a},\mathbf{a}+t]\subseteq [-n^{1/10},n^{1/10}]$. Then for any $x\in \{\mathbf{a},\mathbf{a}+t\}$, we have
