{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.723944+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_afc0be848ce8aa713e52d741efd9175af31b29a0222ae8069828eb810247ad2b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition eq:FS-UB-top-exists of arXiv:2606.06612, 'The limit shape and emergence of the \\ Discrete Gaussian level lines'] Fix $m \geq 0$. For every sequence of $L \to \infty$ such that each $L$ satisfies $\pi^0_{\Lambda}(\mathfrak{L}_0 \neq \emptyset) > \delta_L$, then sampling $\mathfrak{L}_n$ under the measures $\pi^0_{\Lambda}(\cdot \mid \mathfrak{L}_0 \neq \emptyset)$, every weak limit point $({\ensuremath{\mathbf Y}}_n(t))_{0 \leq n\leq m}$ of the processes $(Y_n(t))_{0 \leq n\leq m}$ satisfies 
