{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:45:10.084044+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_afc4407a16be6e26b5cf2e8eac34504798bc4583882301c358d6dd5b855b6e23","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary HalfSharp of arXiv:2504.18739, 'discrete analogues of second-order Riesz transforms'] For all $j,k=1,2,\ldots,d$, with $j\ne k$, we have
