{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:58.445858+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_afd2f1df6f2355bdd94da51bcdb1adace787c7964f1be0ba6ce7184d9d5ee414","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:propA3 of arXiv:2604.24743, 'The impact of disorder and non-convex interactions on delocalisation of height functions'] For any integer $L \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{N}}$, any parameter $\lambda > 0$ and any collection of non-negative conductances $J:= \left( J_{xy,k} \right)_{\{x,y\} \in E(\Lambda_L), 1 \leq k \leq n}$, one has the identities:
\begin{itemize}
    \item For the partition functions:
    \begin{equation} 
        Z_{\Lambda_L, J, \lambda}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{XY}} = Z_{\Lambda_L,  J, \lambda}^{\mathrm{XY}}.
    \end{equation}
    \item For the variance of the height:
    \begin{equation*}
    \mathrm{Var}_{L  ,J , \lambda}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}- \mathrm{XY}} \left[ \varphi(0) \right] = \left\langle \lambda \cos \left( \theta_{0g} \right) + \frac{\lambda^2}{2} \cos \left( 2 \theta_{0g} \right)  - \frac{\lambda^2}{2}  \right\rangle_{L , J, \lambda}^{\mathrm{XY}}.
