{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:43:43.164872+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_afef96240c133f493d63ac409c1995831ae1c78291ef7168977530eed588ff4d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm: phi43 random bc of arXiv:2506.21466, 'The Markov property for $\varphi^4_3$ on the cylinder'] Let $\sigma \in \{\emptyset,+,-\}$ and let $(\varphi^{0,\sigma_-},\varphi^{0,\sigma}_+)$ be independent admissible boundary conditions. Then almost surely in the boundary conditions, the following statements hold.
