{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:22:48.878457+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b01be5650055414aad4ade102e94e7a86c49c31a4e171a54509f18ed5bc08c42","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 19 of arXiv:2608.29152, 'Uniform Statistical Convergence of Empirical Sinkhorn Potentials\\ with Exponential and Po'] For a model satisfying Definition~\ref{def:tight-graph-model}, there exist constants $\eps_0, \eta_0>0$ and $C_0<\infty$ (dependent only on the finite model) such that for $0<\eps\le\eps_0$ and any $\delta\in(0,1)$, if 
