{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:02:11.326418+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b02759507e705be9c11b7a3a471b7a27e3c932ad50d87c095c6b4adec6ecbcd1","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn KMSW-inv of arXiv:2510.26123, 'Directed distances in bipolar-oriented triangulations:\\ exact exponents and scaling limit'] Let $n\geq 1$ and $\mathfrak m$ be a bipolar-oriented triangulation with $n$ total edges, with $l$ edges on its left boundary and $r$ edges on its right boundary. We define the corresponding KMSW walk $\mathfrak  Z = (\mathfrak  L(j),\mathfrak  R(j))_{0\leq j\leq n-1}$ as follows: for $0\leq j\leq n-1$, 
\begin{itemize}
    \item $\mathfrak  L(j)$ is the height in the tree $T_{UL}(\mathfrak  m)$ of the initial vertex of $\lambda_{j+1}$ (i.e.\ its distance in $T_{UL}(\mathfrak  m)$ from the source);
    \item $\mathfrak  R(j)$ is the height in the tree $T_{LR}(\mathfrak m)$ of the terminal vertex of $\lambda_{j+1}$ (i.e.\ its distance in $T_{LR}(\mathfrak m)$ from the sink) minus $r-1$.
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.274622+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b02c0edc813984dffc1da2b2b6ab26ce03198b9eb64e9698d06679fc243b0273","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma_uniform_bound_infty_Omega of arXiv:2411.16452, 'Interface scaling limit for the critical planar Ising model perturbed by a magnetic field'] Let $\xi \in \{-,+\}$. There almost surely exists $m_0$ such that almost surely, for any $m \geq m_0$ and any $k \geq 1$,
\begin{equation*}
    \sum_{(x_1,\dots,x_k) \in \Omega_{m,j(\xi)}} \delta_m^{\frac{15k}{8}}{\mathbb{E}}_{m,j(\xi)}^{\xi}[\sigma_{x_1} \dots \sigma_{x_k}] \leq C_{k,\infty}^{(\xi)}
\end{equation*}
with $\sum_k\frac{h^k}{k!}C_{k,\infty}^{(\xi)} < \infty$ almost surely.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:38:23.613458+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b0347ac5ee5469bf171ba71d6abe5ebdebc652d33e0a2dfb687441ef63f3702d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2511.08956, '\textbf{Towards a characterization of elliptic Harnack inequality for jump processes}'] Let $X=(X_t)_{t \geq 0}$ be an isotropic unimodal L\'{e}vy jump process on $\mathbb{R}^d$, and let $X=X^{\left\langle r_0 \right\rangle}+\hat{X}^{\left\langle r_0 \right\rangle}$ be the small/flat decomposition of $X$ at $r_0$, as defined in Definition (EHI:d:smallflat of the paper). Let $\left(T^{\left\langle r_0 \right\rangle}_k \right)_{k=0}^\infty$ be the sequence of stopping times defined recursively by
    \begin{equation*}
        T_0 := 0, \qquad T_{k+1} = \inf \left\{ t>T_k : \hat{X}^{\left\langle r_0 \right\rangle}_t \neq \hat{X}^{\left\langle r_0 \right\rangle}_{t-} \right\}.
    \end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.743231+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b03587e9d9df6e7a22fbc6a949cc82e1f6c1bbd9d618c68bd8e5cf935f78f4c9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:p_bound of arXiv:2605.05193, 'Grokability in five inequalities'] Define the explicit Nazarov main term
\begin{equation}
L(n,\rho):=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}\frac{1}{\rho}\exp\!\Big(\frac{\rho^4}{4n}\Big)e^{-\rho^2/2}.
\end{equation}
Fix constants $a>0$ and $W>0$. Then there exist constants $C_{a,W}>0$ and
$n_0(a,W)$ such that for all $n\ge n_0(a,W)$, all $\rho=a n^{1/4}$, and all
$r=\sqrt{n-1}+w$ with $|w|\le W$, one has
\begin{equation}
p(r)\ \le\ L(n,\rho)\,\exp\!\Big(\frac{w\rho^2}{\sqrt{n}}\Big)\,
\exp\!\Big(\frac{C_{a,W}}{\sqrt{n}}\Big).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:43:00.038671+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b037f2f5805412417f2d75e889954869846d45ddecf0eeeaeccf9df768dc8f75","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 2 of arXiv:2609.00743, '$L_p$ Brunn-Minkowski inequality for the eigenvalue of generalized Monge-Ampère equation'] Let $u$ be a closed convex function on $\mathbb{R}^n$, and let $u^*$ denote its Legendre transform. Then
\begin{equation}
u(x)+u^{*}(\xi)\geq \xi\cdot x\quad \text{for all }x,\xi\in\mathbb{R}^n. 
\end{equation}
Moreover, the following three statements are equivalent:
\begin{itemize}
\item[(a)] $u(x)+u^{*}(\xi)=\xi\cdot x$;
\item[(b)] $\xi\in\partial u(x)$;
\item[(c)] $x\in\partial u^{*}(\xi)$.
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:09:43.670690+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b03bb328712a21c1444f70d94091f1c50dcc3c4b5bb963653dcd4b0e33f2c3f9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma_exponential_decay_with_gamma_n_upper of arXiv:2605.26804, '\Large Large Deviation Principle for the Empirical Measures of Simple Random Walks on $\ov'] Let $\gamma:\mathbb{R}_+^* \to \mathbb{R}_+^*$ be a function such that $\lim_{\varepsilon \to 0^+}\gamma(\varepsilon)=\overline{\gamma}$. Then, for all $\mu_0 \in \mathcal{P}(\mathbb{Z})$,
\begin{align}
\limsup_{\varepsilon \to 0^+} \limsup \limits_{n \to \infty} \frac{1}{n} \log \mathbb{P} \left( \ell_{2 \left \lceil \frac{\gamma(\varepsilon) n}{2} \right \rceil+1} \in B(\mu_0,\varepsilon) \right) & \leq -\overline{\gamma} I_{\textup{DV}}(\mu_0). 
\end{align}
In addition, for all $\varepsilon>0$, all $R \geq R_{\overline{\mathbb{Z}}}(\varepsilon)$ and all $\rho \in \{-,+\}$,
\begin{align}
\limsup \limits_{n \to \infty} \frac{1}{n} \log \mathbb{P}_{\rho R}\left(\Omega_{2 \left \lceil \frac{\gamma(\varepsilon) n}{2} \right \rceil+1,\textup{exc}}^{\rho} \right) & \leq -\gamma(\varepsilon) I_{\textup{Cr}}^{p_{\rho}}(0) + \gamma(\varepsilon) g(\varepsilon), \\
\limsup \limits_{n \to \infty} \frac{1}{n} \log \mathbb{P}_{\rho R}\left( \Omega_{2 \left \lceil \frac{\gamma(\varepsilon) n}{2} \right \rceil + 1,\textup{mea}}^{\rho} \right) & \leq - \gamma(\varepsilon) \inf_{\rho x \in [0,1]} I_{\textup{Cr}}^{p_{\rho}}(x) + \gamma(\varepsilon) g(\varepsilon), 
\end{align}
where $g$ is as in Proposition~(proposition_exponential_rate_of_decay_exc_and_end of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:44:39.752363+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b03e42ecf49cce97e561e46cc295a6a885c5813f6209b420bad660b509631531","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 35 (Anisotropic local law outside the spectrum) of arXiv:2608.29872, 'Local Laws and Outlier Eigenvalues for Spiked Separable Covariance Matrices'] Under the assumptions of Theorem \ref{local_law}, fix any constant $\epsilon>0$. Then, for any 
\begin{equation}
z\in S_{\mathrm{out}}(C_0,\epsilon):=\left\{z= E+ \ii\eta: \lambda_+ + n^{-2/3+\e} + n^{-1/3+\e}  q^2  \le E \le C_0 \lambda_+,  \eta\in [0,1]\right\},
\end{equation}
and any deterministic unit vectors $\uu, \vv \in \mathbb{C}^{p+n}$, the following anisotropic local law holds:
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
\left| \langle \mathbf u, G(X,z) \mathbf v\rangle - \langle \mathbf u, \Pi (z)\mathbf v\rangle \right| & \prec q + \sqrt{\frac{\Im m_{2c}(z)}{n \eta}}  \asymp q + n^{-1/2}(\kappa+\eta)^{-1/4} .
