{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:23.339771+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b075de4ad4fb3caff2eeafb4647df863262ede355bb84733994a9c3cfea6a1e3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2512.07156, 'Lorenz ordering of parasite loads across hosts in Isham's model of Host-Macroparasite Inte'] For each $j \in \mathbb{N}_0$, define $\beta_j = \sum_{i=j+1}^\infty \pi_C(i)$ and the function $\omega_j :[0,1] \to [0,1]$ such that 
