{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.896864+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b0aa60f279f675278732845ba2bd37e7381918415350312cc3a87b72b3a4405a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 54 of arXiv:2508.04938, 'Perfect t-embeddings of doubly periodic Aztec diamonds'] Let~$\cT$,~$\cO$ be given in Proposition~\ref{prop:ct_co_finite_2xell},~$\Omega$ in Proposition~\ref{prop:diffeomorphism_2xell}, and let~$\mathcal Z$,~$\vartheta$ be given in Definition~\ref{def:limit_surface_2xell}. Let~$(\xi,\eta)\in \mathcal F_R\subset(-1,1)^2$ and assume~$x$ and~$y$ are as in~\eqref{eq:global_coordinates_1xell}, and let~$i=0,1\dots,\ell-1$, $j = 0,1$, and~$\eps=0,1$. Then
