{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:05:52.442565+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b0ad4bf8a04ee04061cd8cad49b105f70c5fbb1e0a4ff6a18fc504d9cb0ec179","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm theorem:Lp of arXiv:2504.19942, 'The edge-averaging process on graphs \\ with random initial opinions'] For every $p\in[1,\infty)$, there exists $C_p>0$ (depending only on $p$), such that if the i.i.d.\ initial opinions $\{f_0(v)\}_{v \in V}$ are in $L^p$, then for every $t>0$ and every $o\in V$,
\begin{equation}
\|f_t(o)-\mu\|_p\leq C _p\|f_0(o)-\mu\|_p \cdot
\begin{cases}
    t_*^{\frac{1-p}{2p}}&p\in [1,2),\\
    t_*^{-1/4}&p\geq 2,
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
where  $t_*:=\min(t,|V|^2)$. 
Moreover, if $V$ is infinite and  $p \in [1,2)$, then
$\|f_t(o)-\mu\|_p =o\big(t^{\frac{1-p}{2p}}\big)$ as $t \to \infty$. \newline (In particular $f_t(o) \to \mu$ in $L^1$ if $f_0(o) \in L^1$.) (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:51:15.034814+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b0b47ac3648501543bebd5c89b8fd3031f74b3edb2eb28e5b0e7336d15abaed4","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition {{\cite[Definition~1.15 of arXiv:2609.03926, 'Overcolored Partition $k$-tuples Restricted by Parity of the Parts'] {wom}}}]
	Let $\chi$ be a Dirichlet character modulo $N$. Then a modular form $f\in M_k(\Gamma_1(N))$ has Nebentypus character $\chi$ if
	\begin{align*}
		f\left(\dfrac{az+b}{cz+d}\right)=\chi(d)(cz+d)^kf(z),
	\end{align*} 
	for all $z\in \mathbb{H}$ and all $\begin{bmatrix}
		a & b \\
		c & d
	\end{bmatrix}\in\Gamma_0(N)$. We denote the space of such modular forms by $M_k(\Gamma_0(N),\chi)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.237653+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b0b5a674ec5d8dd5b4f5bb4016051d7e9ac0c20c7e7a3edb20dd2bf58d074c5a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:brown_sig_def of arXiv:2604.22528, 'Malliavin calculus for signatures with applications to finance'] If $X$ is a time-augmented Brownian motion $X_t = \widehat{W}_t$, then $a^k_t \equiv {\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{k}}}$, so that $\mathbf{D}_s a^k_t \equiv 0$, and, for $\mathbb{P} \otimes ds \otimes dt\text{-almost every } (\omega, s, t) \in \Omega \times [0,T]^2$ with $s \leq t$,
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbf{D}_s^i \sig[t] = \sig[s] \otimes {\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{i}}} \otimes \sig[s, t].
    \end{equation}
    Moreover, $\sigW \in \mathbb{D}^{\infty, 2}$ for a.e. $t \in [0, T]$, and,  for $\mathbb{P} \otimes dt^{\otimes (n+1)}\text{-almost every } (\omega, s_1, \ldots, s_n, t) \in \Omega \times [0,T]^{n+1}$ with $s_1 \leq \ldots \leq s_n  \leq t$, we have
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbf{D}_{s_1}^{i_1} \cdots \mathbf{D}_{s_n}^{i_n} \sig[t]
        = \sig[s_1] \otimes {\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{i_1}}} \otimes \sig[s_1, s_2]
          \otimes {\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{i_2}}} \otimes \cdots \otimes {\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{i_n}}} \otimes \sig[s_n, t].
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.328424+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b0b7caa4e1384eb79e0d3dd17b70110c9654e476c9e4c23767a20cce7bf8460a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma equivensembles_bernoulli of arXiv:2606.01937, 'Stationary fluctuations for an exclusion process with mass and energy conservation'] Consider the Bernoulli product measure $\pi_\rho = \mathrm{Ber}(\rho )^{\otimes\mathbb{Z}}$ of parameter $\rho\in [0,1]$, and let $\xi$ be a random variable distributed according to $\pi_\rho$. Let $g:\{0,1\}^{\mathbb{Z}}\longrightarrow\mathbb{R}$ be a local function whose support is included in $\{0,\hdots ,\ell_0-1\}$ for some $\ell_0\ge 1$, and define the function $\varphi_g(\rho ) = \pi_\rho(g)$. Then, there exists a constant~$C_2=C_2(g)>0$ such that for any $\ell\ge\ell_0$, we have 
    \begin{equation*}
        \sup_{\xi\in\{0,1\}^{\mathbb{Z}}} \left| \pi_\rho [ g|\xi_0^\ell ] - \left(\varphi_g(\xi_0^\ell ) - \frac{1}{2\ell}\xi_0^\ell (1-\xi_0^\ell)\varphi_g''(\xi_0^\ell)\right)\right| \le \frac{C_2}{\ell^2}.
    \end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:45:05.500604+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b0b7ece3f3e4d96328284544a3396c9c4045449a8e69c2daaca09484efa844dd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 13 of arXiv:2608.05185, '\large\bf ON THE HEAT FLOW CONJECTURE FOR RANDOM MATRICES'] The eigenvalues of \(\mathbf{X}_{N,c}\) have joint density
\begin{equation}
 \frac{1}{\mathcal{Z}_{N,c}}
 \left|\Delta(\lambda_1,\ldots,\lambda_N)\right|^2
 \prod_{j=1}^{N}\dd\gamma_{N;1,c,0}(\lambda_j).
\end{equation}
Here \(\mathcal{Z}_{N,c}>0\) is the normalising constant.
Relative to \(\gamma_{N;1,c,0}\), they form a determinantal point process
with correlation kernel
\begin{equation}
 K_{N,c}(z,w)
 =\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}
 \frac{h_{k,c,N}(z)\overline{h_{k,c,N}(w)}}{\kappa_{k,N}},
 \qquad
 \kappa_{k,N}=\frac{k!}{N^k}.
\end{equation}
As an integral operator on
