{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.764281+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b0c3718c47acbac802b01fcee3b57146ee9b15f94e4b24875b4e1bd066c95b30","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l1 of arXiv:2411.19433, 'Singular mean-field backward stochastic Volterra integral equations in infinite dimensiona'] Assume that condition $(A_{2})$ holds. Then, for any \( \Psi(\cdot) \in L^2_{\mathcal{F}_T}(\delta, b; H) \), equation (equation f3.4 of the paper) has a unique adapted solution 

\[
