{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:16:18.691470+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b0db84b6aed18c56baed148ee36a10fda18ca3667416635f8deb1b53a2742a24","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 29 (Equivalent modified formulations) of arXiv:2607.26377, '\textbf{Entire Logarithmic Signatures\\ of Bounded-Variation Paths in Finite Dimensions}'] Let $V$ be a finite-dimensional real normed space, let $\gamma:[0,T]\to V$ be a continuous tree-reduced bounded-variation path, and put $v=\gamma_T-\gamma_0$. If $v\neq0$, then the following formulations are equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\roman*)}]
\item centred weak path conjugacy to a line in the sense of \cref{def:two-conjugacies};
\item conjugacy to $\e^v$ in the reduced bounded-variation path group;
\item a signature identity $S(\gamma)=a\e^v a^{-1}$ with $a\in\Sl(V)$.
\end{enumerate}
When $v=0$, the corresponding formulations all reduce to the constant reduced path. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.493009+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b0de96250ab3d49a13811e6149242592b59988db70648e5eae78818e92341ee6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2605.09459, 'Multipoint connectivity in the branching interlacement process'] For $d \geq 9$, and $k \geq 3$. Let
  \begin{equation}

    n(k,d) = \left\lceil\frac{d(k-1)}{4}\right\rceil - (k-2).
  \end{equation}
  Assume that the reproduction law is a mean $1$ distribution with finite $2\lceil d(k-1)/4\rceil$  moment, and that the jump law is centered, has finite range and its support does not generate any strict subgroup of $\mathbb{Z}^d$. Then almost surely, for every $k$ points of the interlacement, there exist $n(k,d)$ trajectories of the interlacement that connect them. Futhermore, almost surely, there exist $k$ points of the interlacement that are not connected using less than $n(k,d)$ trajectories. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:46:25.365387+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b0e0c6bd3dd631f76879b4df53c3650ce1ef0bfbf6f24259d6b2c0cdd9ad2a54","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem holder_bound_on_event of arXiv:2604.14122, 'The scaling limit of random walk and\\ the intrinsic metric on planar critical percolation'] Using the same parameters as before, for all $\nu<\frac{5}{8\cdot12}$, 
