    In other words, it is essentially induced by $\mathbf{w}_\Gamma$.
        \end{enumerate}
    \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:32:35.601230+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b1034d8b24ec96b4b154a7cc7bf6a5a3bf1a9531b04daf80ae617b7feb1c5270","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:dyadic of arXiv:2606.11248, 'Persistent Homology of the Planar Wiener Sausage: Brownian Scaling and a Logarithmic Expec'] There exist deterministic constants $c_{0}>0$, $c_{1}>0$, and an almost surely finite random integer $n_{0}$ such that, almost surely, for every integer $n\ge n_{0}$,
