{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.513475+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b10b4a81474f55c76feec091a2dd3b944ac3248c6f3a1ef05985433b4e48a2cf","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lemma: weight of all possible pinchings is 1 of arXiv:2411.11676, 'Surface sums for lattice Yang--Mills in the large-$N$ limit'] Fix a blue face $B$ with disjoint vertices. 
Then
\begin{equation}
	\sum_{B'\in \AF(B)}w_{\infty}(B')=1,
\end{equation}
where if $B'$ has multiple faces $\{B'_i\}_{i=1}^k$, we set $w_{\infty}(B'):= \prod_{i=1}^kw_{\deg(B'_i)/2}$.
As a consequence, if $M\in\mathcal{N}\mathcal{P}\mathcal{M}(s,K)$ is a non-separable planar embedded map and $B$ is one of its blue faces, then 
\begin{equation}
	\sum_{M'\in \AM(M,B)}w_{\infty}(M') = \prod_{f\in \BF(M)\setminus \{B\}}w_{\deg(f)/2},
\end{equation}
where we recall $\BF(M)$ is the set of blue faces of $M$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.537431+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b111875ba42bd0786a0c4d5f5e8ef303930d806bff51b8461382c42d3f9ecbf8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 16 of arXiv:2609.02610, 'The frame set of the first Hermite function'] Let $\beta>0$ and define $\varphi_\beta\colon\R\to\R$ by
\begin{equation}
  \varphi_\beta(t)=\e^{-\pi t^2/\beta}
  \quad\text{for all }t\in\R.
\end{equation}
Let $u=(u_k)_{k\in\Z}\in\ell^\infty(\Z)$, and let
$f\colon\R\to\C$ be the nonzero function defined by
\begin{equation}
  f(t)=\sum_{k\in\Z}u_k\varphi_\beta(t-k)
  \quad\text{for all }t\in\R.
\end{equation}
Let $\cZ(f)$ be the set of real zeros of the entire extension of $f$, and
define $\nu_f(\lambda):=\ord_\lambda f$ for $\lambda\in\cZ(f)$.  Then
\begin{equation}
  D^-(\cZ(f),\nu_f)\leq1.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:38:58.717643+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b112d3d045fc8254f52c09e7f955946aa8c367e5db82d44b9dec36f1953d752c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition defi:xyzspace of arXiv:2511.06321, 'Torus scaling limits and the plateau of the critical weakly coupled $|\varphi|^4$ model in'] We denote $\mathbb{A}$ for the sequence of $\underline{A} = (A_j)_{j\ge 0} = (x_j, y_j, z_j)_{j\ge 0} \in \prod_{j\ge 0} X_j \times Y_j \times Z_j$ such that
\begin{align}
	\norm{\underline{A}}_{\mathbb{A}} := \sup_{j \ge 0} \norm{A_j}_{X_j \times Y_j \times Z_j}  < \infty 
\end{align}
and $y_0 = z_0 = 0$. 
Let $\mathbb{A}_0 \subset \mathbb{A}$ be the subspace with $x_0 = y_0 = z_0 =0$.
Due to Lemma~(lemma:RcKisBanach of the paper),  $\mathbb{A}$ and $\mathbb{A}_0$ are Banach spaces.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:52.202776+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b116283e3e0062a4c2fc0054ad4f9f77708ae12667b1872bbc464dd4c97ba9c8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 1 of arXiv:2512.08745, 'Variance strikes back: sub-game--perfect Nash equilibria in time‑inconsistent $N$‑player g'] Let $M$ be an $(\F^i,\P)$-martingale $($respectively, an $(\F_N,\P)$-martingale$)$. There exists a unique process $Z \in \H^2_{\mathrm{loc}}(\F^i,\P,\R^d)$ $($respectively, $(Z^\ell)_{\ell \in \{1,\ldots,N\}}$ with each $Z^\ell \in \H^2_{\mathrm{loc}}(\F_N,\P,\R^d))$ such that
\begin{equation*}
M_{t} = M_0 + \int_0^t Z_s \cdot \d W^i_s \; \bigg(\text{\rm respectively,} \; M_{t} = M_0 + \int_0^t \sum_{\ell =1}^N Z^\ell_s \cdot \d W^\ell_s\bigg),\; t \in [0,T],\; \P \text{\rm --a.s.}
\end{equation*}
Moreover, this property is preserved under an equivalent change of measure, see for instance {\rm\cite[Theorem III.5.24]{jacod2003limit}}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:11:02.389583+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b1172ed248b829759ea69882bb6e2813bcc66f29f69dc172b308f8d6ee960cee","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:global_subgraph_clt of arXiv:2507.10531, 'Quantitative central limit theorems for exponential random graphs'] Assume that there are sequences $\sigma_n \gtrsim n$ and $\delta_n \to 0$ such that
