{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:01:48.582323+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b143cbeddd085731380f6e82ca3898788b09144d8b452864641e96f2b833462b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop precompact of arXiv:2606.30517, '\textsc{Convergence towards Ideal Poisson--Voronoi tessellations with a focus on Diestel--'] Assume that  there exists a real number $ r_0>0$‌ such that $p_1\coloneqq \liminf_r F(r+r_0)/F(r)>1$ and $p_2\coloneqq \limsup_r F(r+r_0)/F(r)<\infty$. Then: 



		\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
