{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.728017+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b14b4f99b4c6141f2e3dee79ad174e3b0e67e3be5bbd60064b9d2da47db126b1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary crl:nl_markov of arXiv:2604.25851, '{Non-uniqueness of nonlinear Markov processes in the sense of McKean associated with parab'] Let $\{u^z\}_{z\in\mathbb{R}^d}$ be such that each $u^z\coloneqq (u^z(t,\cdot))_{t>0}$ is a solution to the FPE (equation eq:Main_FPE_our_paper of the paper) in the sense of (def:FPE-sol of the paper) with initial condition $\delta_z$, satisfying the integrability condition (equation eq:integrability_our_paper of the paper) with $u^z$ replacing $u$. Assume further injectivity of $(t,z)\mapsto u^z(t,x)dx$ and that, for every $(s,z)\in (0,\infty) \times \mathbb{R}^d$, $u^z_{s+} \coloneqq (u^z({s+t},\cdot))_{t\geq 0} $ is the unique solution to the linearized FPE
    \begin{equation}
        \begin{dcases}
        \partial_t v(t,x) = \Delta\Big( a\big(x, u^z(s+t,\cdot)\big)\, v(t,x)\Big) - \nabla \cdot \Big( b\big(x, u^z(s+t,\cdot)\big) \, v(t,x)\Big), \\
        v(0,\cdot) = u^z(s,\cdot),
        \end{dcases}
    \end{equation}
    in 
     \begin{equation}
     \big\{v \geq 0: [t\mapsto v(t,x)dx] \in C(\mathbb{R}_+;\mathcal P),  v(t,x) \leq Cu^z(s+t,x)\,\text{ a.s. for some }C\geq 1 \big\}.
     \end{equation}
     Then there exists a nonlinear Markov core $\{P^z\}_{z\in \mathbb{R}^d}$ for $\{u^z\}_{z\in \mathbb{R}^d}$ in the sense of (def:NMC of the paper), consisting of the unique solution path laws to (equation eq:main_MV-SDE of the paper) with $P^z_t = u^z(t,x)dx$ and $P^z_0 = \delta_z$. In particular, the induced nonlinear Markov process $\{P^\zeta\}_{\zeta \in \mathcal P_0}$, $\mathcal P_0 := \{u^z(t,x)dx| z \in \mathbb{R}^d, t \geq 0\}$, is uniquely determined by $\{u^z\}_{z \in \mathbb{R}^d}$ and (equation eq:main_MV-SDE of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:21:45.350200+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b1514803d4509880fbe9079c4831f54f5b4b698442447b514403270be06d2ee5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 1 (Proposition 6.3 of \cite{niyogi_smale_weinberger}) of arXiv:2607.27535, 'Universal topological statistics on \\ triangulated singular spaces'] Let $M \subset \RR^D$ be a compact $C^2$ manifold. Suppose that $x, y\in M$ are connected by a geodesic $\gamma_{xy}$ of length $s$, and write $r = \|x-y\| $. Define $v$ as the initial velocity of $\gamma_{xy}$ at $x$. If $r \le (\sqrt 2 - 1) \reach_M$, the following are true:
    \begin{align*}
