{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:49:17.495179+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b1beb622bb2379405acfdcf58b2306faa6eb49ada4a3305446f87f6724f9c576","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 (Strict speed-up on $\Z_{\ge 0}$) of arXiv:2605.28766, 'Convex order and faster transmission in first contact percolation'] Let $\X,\X'$ be $\Z$-stationary random closed sets such that $\X$ dominates $\X'$ in terms of hitting probabilities. Additionally, assume that there exists an interval $[a,b]$,
