{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:55.641154+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b1fea4d50dd03a183fccaed0756184a63dbb37dac818461fe0b3cf51effd66fc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 26 (Vanishing local time of face detectors) of arXiv:2605.23529, 'Generalized Bessel-Dunkl diffusions'] Assume \ref{ass:k:dom}. Let $S\in\mathfrak S$, and let $T,r,\eta>0$. Let $\theta$ be a stopping time such that
