{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:53.170447+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b2137a84c474c24c98470db6436442d3a39bc32d9eb2e02825e126855a7505cd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 39 (Hölder Regularity of the Transitioned Source) of arXiv:2607.03318, 'Continuous Differentiability of the Value Function for Infinite-Dimensional Finite-Horizon'] Let Assumptions \ref{ass:coefficients} and \ref{ass:smoothing} hold, and let $\varphi \in \mathcal{B}_m(H)$. For any $0 \le t < s \le T$ and any Hölder exponent $\beta \in (0, 1)$, the Fréchet gradient of the mapping $x \mapsto P_{t,s}[\varphi](x)$ is locally equi-Hölder continuous. Specifically, there exists a constant $C_3 > 0$ such that for all $x, y \in H$:
\begin{equation}

