{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:01:22.645635+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b22478eaf61af2200dfb38d1bee524a577c12539fac687d4a8f1251c5a322c14","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:boundary-smoothing of arXiv:2607.03639, '\vspace{-0.6in}An AI-Assisted Solution to the Signed BAR Conjecture: Uniqueness in the Har'] For every $i\in J$ and every $x\in F_i$,
