{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.054058+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b22f28ccef764d8d502e341be9f0c5a0aa6ac42d81f4660cf1cddca54221d30b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 1 of arXiv:2607.01629, 'Quadratic fluctuations of speed-change Kawasaki dynamics'] \cite[Theorem~1]{fun96}
		The process $(\Y_t^N)_{t \in [0,T]}$ converges weakly as $N\to\infty$ in the space $D\left([0,T], \S' \left(\Td\right)\right)$. The limit is the Ornstein--Uhlenbeck process:
