{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:02:11.326160+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b2e1d268671149e59f554d9ecf1ca8864b8b2ce726428e2a875234aa0e3536a3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm thm-kmsw of arXiv:2510.26123, 'Directed distances in bipolar-oriented triangulations:\\ exact exponents and scaling limit'] Let $l ,r , n \in \mathbbm N$. The KMSW procedure restricts to a bijection between the following two sets.
