{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:45:05.441021+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b2e5d919842cb6eb649f236f32bad5117c51b010c17adea226fca04288ccd4a1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 153 (Quadratic restart rigidity) of arXiv:2608.04993, '2608.04993'] On the smooth finite-rank response skeleton, sequential concatenation obeys
\begin{equation}
 x(wv)=x(w)+x(v),\qquad
 V(wv)=V(w)+V(v)+x(w)\otimes x(v).
\end{equation}
Therefore joint signature-response equivalence is a restart congruence.  Under
the global decoder \eqref{eq:primitive-decoder}, the reconstructed product is
\begin{equation}
 (x,A,q)\star(y,B,r)
 =\bigl(x+y,A+B+\Anti(x\otimes y),q+r\bigr).
\end{equation}
The first and covariance coordinates are autonomous additive blocks, whereas
the area channel is triangularly coupled to the first level.  The product is
Cauchy-continuous on the finite-rank skeleton and has a unique jointly
continuous extension, given by the same formula, to the complete state and
coherent response targets.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.185959+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b2e67a28912dd23088a2ce2b610f73c2e6904e95b1f694857ead986e6f07367a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2510.20492, 'Heterochromatic two-arm probabilities for metric graph Gaussian free fields'] For $d\ge 3$, $n\ge 1$, $D\subset \widetilde{\mathbb{Z}}^d$, and $v,w\in \widetilde{\mathbb{Z}}^d$ with $\mathrm{dist}(D,\{v,w\})\ge n$, 
