{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:28:33.895463+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b2fb428213a5df9a1aff3c155df181cba19fd6bb0cf5d3204bdce9820e5b665b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:Hcont of arXiv:2505.01739, 'Stochastic dominance for linear combinations of infinite-mean risks'] If $F\in\mathcal{H}$, then  
\begin{equation*} 
\phi(x_1,x_2)= \overline{F} \left(\frac{1}{x_1}\right)+\overline{F} \left(\frac{1}{x_2}\right),~~(x_1,x_2)\in \mathbb{R}_{++}^2
