{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.706621+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b3173c75a7913a65edc7f7b90ba8f9bc49fdc7503e215fe8e4e6e4c67a517f49","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:generalized:sink:polynomial of arXiv:2412.09235, 'A semiconcavity approach to stability of entropic plans and exponential convergence of Sin'] Assume $c(x,\cdot)$ to be $\mathcal{C}^1(\mathcal{Y})$, that there exist $\Lambda\in(0,+\infty)$, a non-negative function $\omega\colon\mathcal{Y}\times\mathcal{Y}\to\mathbb{R}$ and $N\geq 2$ such that 
