{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.617563+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b34215bb0d2c834fa45bef35fe3849aac1dd68a20b76e684e8fd968119ae9fdc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 22 of arXiv:2609.01358, 'Regularized spectral expansion of a Rankin--Selberg period and moments'] Let $d\ge 2$ and for $\lambda:=(\lambda_1,\lambda_2)\in\a^\ast_{\Q_1,\C}$ let $\varphi_\lambda\in\1_1\cdot|\cdot|^{\lambda_1}\boxplus\1_{d-1}\cdot|\det|^{\lambda_2}$ be a normalized factorizable vector. If $\varphi_\lambda$ is holomorphic in a sufficiently small neighbourhood of the hyperplane $\lambda_1-\lambda_2=\tfrac{d}{2}$ then $\Eis(\varphi_\lambda)$ has at most a simple polar divisor along the same hyperplane where the residue is given by
