{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:58:09.907231+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b34f2eb23a809a3cc2203dc44cf9c1dc1cef6084c918ab6ceff2d76488a3e5d3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:uniform of arXiv:2607.19658, 'Hitting time mixing for random $k$-cycles'] For $t \geq t^*$, conditioned on the marked set $M_t$, $\rho_t$ is uniform on $\Omega_{t}(S_t)$. In particular, $\rho_{\tau_3}|\{\tau_3= t\}$ is uniform on $\Omega_t$. Consequently, if $k$ is odd, then
