{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:20.960623+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b363c6ce2f45c54b1f614088645433fc49be5c9189604f87af531cb4568e2a32","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 25 of arXiv:2604.20634, 'Distributional Statistical Models:\\ \large Weak Moments, Cumulants, and a Central Limit T'] Let $\beta \geq 1$.  A function $\varphi \in \mathcal{S}(\R)$ satisfies an \emph{exponential-type decay condition of order~$\beta$} if there exist $A > 0$ and, for each $m \geq 0$, a constant $C_m > 0$ such that
