{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:40:22.390288+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b3894313dddcd0e6e6959954423706dc85a1e18e9c3b4ef79ed01332583d3e43","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn def-metric of arXiv:2506.18827, 'Random walk reflected off of infinity, with applications to uniform spanning forests and s'] Let $S$ be a countable set with the discrete topology (we will eventually take $S = \mathcal V\mathcal G \cup \{\infty\}$). 
We define $L^1_{\operatorname{loc}}([0,\infty) ,S)$ to be the metric space of Lebesgue measurable functions $f : [0,\infty) \to S$, with functions identified if they agree Lebesgue a.e., with the metric
