				\limsup_{t \to \infty} \frac{1}{t} \log | y^{\xi, \epsilon}_t(\omega) | \leq \lambda^\epsilon.
			\end{equation}
			In particular, our stability result holds for every \(\xi \in C^{2\gamma}([-r, 0], \mathbb{R}^n)\), where \(\frac{1}{3} < \gamma < H\) and \(\gamma\) can be chosen arbitrarily close to \(\frac{1}{3}\).","status":"unverified"}

