{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:00:22.667126+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b3d2786441e95a42caf85a7bac4295eac45d6cbaa094ce75c3741399947aed96","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop thm:submatrices_suffice of arXiv:2411.01104, 'Gaussian universality of $p$-adic random matrix products via corners'] Let $1 \leq n \leq m$ be integers and $A \in \Mat_{n \times m}(\mathbb{Q}_p)$ with $\SN(A) = (\lambda_1,\ldots,\lambda_n)$. Then for any $1 \leq k \leq n$,
