{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.610800+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b3dad009d3803b1c5fa3540a1a96c47f804e0e32f9229c4bbb0bd18ab712eb5f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 18 (\cite{DvZ2001}) of arXiv:2607.08536, 'Soft edge limit of the Laguerre beta-ensemble at the lower edge'] Suppose that $\xi_k, k\ge 0$ are martingale differences with respect to a filtration $\FF_k,k\ge 0$, and let $M_k=\sum_{j=1}^k \xi_j$. 
Assume that we have the bounds $\ev[\xi_k^2|\FF_{k-1}]\le \sigma_k^2$ on the conditional second moments. For a fixed $\eta>0$ define
\begin{align}
