            \pi_R^\eta (\partial \lambda_1 =\{x,y\}\,,\,\partial \lambda_2 = \{u,v\}) \le \ell^{c_3} e^{ - c_4 \bar \alpha^2}\,.
        \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:15:09.113616+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b3f40601cf19ed52f05702142b8b94801934ac33f9fa5362d7650f48d2465431","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Corollary: Upper bound for cumulants of GUE of arXiv:2411.11341, 'Ultra high order cumulants and quantitative CLT for polynomials in Random Matrices'] Let $\mathcal{X}\sim GUE$. For any $r\geq 1$ and $m$ even,
