{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.524034+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b4041cb7e990b0279bee31703e0758e277f2cf59620a29e4d4cd4639e1c42027","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem e:heat_flow1 of arXiv:2411.03482, 'Ergodicity of 2D singular stochastic Navier--Stokes equations'] Let $\mathcal{A} = \{x\in \mathbf{R}^2: \frac{3}{4} \leq |x| \leq \frac{8}{3}\}$ be an annulus. Then there exist constants $c, C>0$ such that for any $p \in [1,\infty]$ and $t > 0$ and $\lambda \ge 1$, we have, for all $u$ with $\supp \hat{u} \subset \lambda \mathcal{A}$, the bounds
	\begin{equs}

		  \|e^{t\Delta} u\|_{L^p} &\leq Ce^{-ct\lambda^2}\|u\|_{L^p}\;;\\

		\|e^{t\Delta}u - u \|_{L^p} &\leq C t\lambda^{2} \|u\|_{L^p}\;.
