{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:29:08.635206+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b40c1ba416d9400015056c27f90e97a9e31f9864795a0c937e395436fce1f375","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem-decomp-qtf of arXiv:2411.19810, 'Radial conformal welding in Liouville quantum gravity'] There is a constant $C$ such that a sample from $M_W^f$ can be obtained by conformally welding a tuple $(\mathcal{D}_1, \mathcal{D}_2, \mathcal{D}_3, \mathcal T)$ sampled from 
