{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:49:17.483899+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b414082b069d352b6e9945faf2c82b60c041500538316d796ba4ebebf33f08a8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2605.28377, 'Geometric functionals of Brownian motion on Hermitian symmetric spaces of non-compact type'] Let $(e_1,\cdots,e_r)$ be a Jordan frame. Let $\phi$ be a linear map from $(V, (\cdot |\cdot))$ into itself satisfying, for every $x,y,z \in V$,
