\end{align*}
where  $\{a_n\}$ is an integer-valued sequence satisfying $na_n^{-\alpha}l(a_n)\to1$, and $T$ is a positive random variable with Laplace transform $\mathrm{e}^{-s^\alpha}$ ($s>0$). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:44:27.956666+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b4249cc64f608228a8e17992ac3c7733283cbdf5d42c41f7d98908d423742b79","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 26 (Continuous-time coalescence--meeting comparison) of arXiv:2607.13183, '2607.13183'] Let $(X_t)_{t\ge0}$ be a finite irreducible reversible continuous-time chain on
