where $\displaystyle D_{\theta} = \frac{1}{\log(m_{\theta}^{-1})}$. The same result holds if $x_n^1,x_n^2$ are chosen to be independent uniform vertices on $T_{n,g_n}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:38:37.416736+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b428b56940042eb2bd7a7394677dbed4f0ab2927e54aa9851055b2f4d9861871","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 14 of arXiv:2605.16072, 'Stochastic integration \\with respect to a L\'evy basis'] Let $\O$ be in $\Borel(\R^d)$. 
	An infinitely divisible random measure $\Theta\colon \Borel_b(\Rp\times \O) \to L_P^0(\Omega;\R)$ is called a L\'evy basis if: 
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item[{\rm (a)}] for every $A\in\Borel_b(\Rp\times \O)$ for which there exists $t\ge 0$ such that $A\subseteq [0,t]\times \O$, 
		the random variable $\Theta(A)$ is $\F_t$-measurable; 
		\item[{\rm (b)}] for every $A\in\Borel_b(\Rp\times \O)$ for which there exists $t\ge 0$ such that $A\subseteq (t,\infty)\times \O$,  
		the random variable $\Theta(A)$ is independent of $\F_t$;
		\item[{\rm (c)}] $\Theta(\{t\}\times [-n,n]^d\cap\O)=0$ $P$-a.s.\ for all $t\ge 0$ and $n\in\N$.
	\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:27:56.784462+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b4296e7c0a7228866d652cc84882fca20ef79fb04334a40bb9f5b869b8ceb088","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 32 (Control of the geometry-matter tensor) of arXiv:2608.31171, '\bf Finite-energy spacetimes with torus symmetry. \\ \Large Cauchy stability of Einstein--'] Given a Navier--Stokes potential~$\chi$ as in \autoref{def-pot-hyperbolic}, one has the following inequalities: for $a,b\in\{0,1\}$,
