{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:48:35.788057+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b45834f2d9a0a877e2ea149c3a590eb73f15f2db79d835bcccbd69dec66a9cbb","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lipschitz Bound of arXiv:2411.09260, 'The Hydrodynamic Limit of Hawkes Processes on Adaptive Stochastic Networks'] For any $c \in \Gamma_E$ any $\theta \in \mathcal{E}$, any $z , y \in \mathcal{D}([0,T] , \Gamma)$, there exists a unique $ \lbrace j_{\theta,\eta} \rbrace_{\theta,\eta \in \mathcal{E}}  \in   \mathcal{D}([0,T] , \mathcal{P}( \Gamma_E) ) $, written $ j_{\theta\eta} := (j_{\theta\eta,t})_{t\leq T}$ such that for all $t\leq T$, and all $a \in \Gamma_E$,
\begin{align}
j_{\theta\eta,t}(a) = v_{\theta\eta}(z_0, y_0,a)+ \sum_{b \in \Gamma_E : b \neq a} \int_0^t \bigg\lbrace j_{\theta\eta,s}(b) l_{b\mapsto a}(z_s , y_s)   - j_{\theta\eta,s}(a)    l_{a\mapsto b}(z_s , y_s)  \bigg\rbrace ds
\end{align}
We write
\begin{align}
\Psi_{\theta \eta , t} &:  \mathcal{D}([0,t] , \Gamma)^2 \mapsto \mathcal{D}\big([0,t] , \mathcal{P}( \Gamma_E) \big) \\
\Psi_{\theta \eta,t}(  z , y) &:=   j_{\theta\eta}.
\end{align}
Furthermore for each $T > 0$, there exists a constant $C_T$ such that for all $t\leq T$,
\begin{align}
\sup_{\theta,\eta\in \mathcal{E}} \norm{ \Psi_{\theta \eta,t}(  z , x) -  \Psi_{\theta \eta,t}(  \tilde{z} , \tilde{x}) } \leq C_T \big( \norm{z - \tilde{z}}_t + \norm{x - \tilde{x}}_t \big). 
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.461802+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b4590a14681c27c5c2b059e8f3a71a87c23ca5c1972afb0991fd1713a13e17ac","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 8 of arXiv:2609.02561, 'NON-NEF LOCI IN MIXED CHARACTERISTIC'] A real valuation $v$ of $K(X)$ is a map $v:K(X)\rightarrow\R\cup\{\infty\}$ such that for every $f,g\in K(X)$, the following hold:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $v(fg)=v(f)+v(g)$.
    \item $v(f+g)\geq \min\{v(f),v(g)\}$.
    \item $v(f)=\infty$ if and only if $f=0$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.758927+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b4634614844f0b3bbfb693e0c015c0344531a3bc07bcf3f0a5d3bfdd0c402197","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Satz thm:wavelet-characterization of arXiv:2411.18155, 'Besov regularity of random wavelet series'] Let $d\in \mathds{N}$, $p,q\in (0,\infty]$, $s \in\mathds{R}$.
Denote by $(\Psi_{j,t,m})_{(j,t,m)\in J}$ the orthonormal basis of $L_2(\mathds{R}^d)$ given in 
  \hyperref[{eq:wavelet-tensorization}]{\textup{\tagform@{\ref*{eq:wavelet-tensorization}}}}
.
Assume that $k>\max\setn{s,d\lr{\frac{1}{p}-1}-s}$ if $p\in (0,1)$ and $k>\left\lverts\right\rvert$ else.
Let $f\in\mathcal{S}^\prime(\mathds{R}^d)$.
Then $f\in B^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d,w)$ if and only if it can be represented as
\begin{equation}
f=\sum_{(j,t,m)\in J} a_{j,t,m}  \Psi_{j,t,m}
\end{equation}
with $a=(a_{j,t,m})_{(j,t,m)\in J}\in b^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d,w)$.
The convergence is unconditional in $\mathcal{S}^\prime(\mathds{R}^d)$.
Furthermore, the representation is unique, i.e., for given  $f\in B^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d,w)$, the unique element $(a_{j,t,m})_{(j,t,m)\in J}\in b^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d,w)$ such that 
  \hyperref[{eq:wavelet-characterization}]{\textup{\tagform@{\ref*{eq:wavelet-characterization}}}}
 holds is given by $a_{j,t,m}=\skpr{f}{\Psi_{j,t,m}}$, where the duality pairing is suitably defined.
The map
\begin{equation*}
I: f\mapsto (\skpr{f}{\Psi_{j,t,m}})_{(j,t,m)\in J}
\end{equation*}
defines an isomorphism of quasi-Banach spaces $B^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d,w)\to b^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d,w)$, and the map
\begin{equation*}
S:  (a_{j,t,m})_{(j,t,m)\in J}\mapsto \sum_{(j,t,m)\in J}a_{j,t,m}\Psi_{j,t,m}
\end{equation*}
defines an isomorphism of quasi-Banach spaces $b^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d,w)\to B^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d,w)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

