{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.626610+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b48c687d6fe57a34d4e32e225c3393197fcab50ff471d1785e61f4f1ca139ae0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:char. unique ergodic of arXiv:2411.03512, 'Ergodicity and Mixing of Sublinear Expectation System and Applications'] Let $(\Omega,f)$ be a topological dynamical system, which is point transitive. Then the following two statements are equivalent:
