{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:04.861840+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b4bb034cd5c235ff84ec7380483a2205517c88cd686f087b105bd563a5d3a15c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 1 of arXiv:2511.22156, ''] There is a Feller process $((X_t)_{t>0},(P^x)_{x\in F})$ on the Sierpi\'nski carpet $F$ with a transition density $q_t(x,y)$ satisfying the two-sided sub-Gaussian heat kernel estimate 
\begin{equation}
