{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:40.985153+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b4f3ca9b9342458f165311127ecf5933b7660964f241f5dc9aedecf195840835","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem_3 of arXiv:2412.03774, '{ Refining Concentration for \\Gaussian Quadratic Chaos with\\ Applications in Sonar and C'] Let $u,v,w, w'$ be positive numbers such that $w\geq w'$ and $x=\frac{\sqrt{v^2+3uw}-v}{3w}$. Then 
