{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:21:45.238564+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b52a2833eb21287d59051dfe1367283c36818977ab44837962f2953d8f2ee9c9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2607.26564, 'Stochastic Scalar Conservation Laws on Moving Hypersurfaces'] Assume that $u^\epsilon \in L^2(\Omega; C([0,T]; H^1(\Gamma_{\cdot}))) \cap L^2(\Omega; L^2([0,T]; H^2(\Gamma_{\cdot})))$ satisfies the following equation in $H^{-1}(\Gamma_{\cdot})$,
