{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.117261+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b55b919ce449da833d37f4918b6a9b8e4cf785e7a7d1c2678145ce6a10541041","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:specular of arXiv:2608.17022, 'Sharp hypocoercive convergence estimates for underdamped Langevin dynamics with specular r'] Let $\mathscr C$ denote the set of functions $f\in C^2(\overline\Omega\times\mathbb{R}^d)$ such that
\begin{equation}
|\partial^\alpha f(x,v)|\le C_\alpha(1+|v|)^{N}
\quad\text{for all }(x,v)\in\overline\Omega\times\mathbb{R}^d\text{ and all multi-indices }\alpha\text{ with }|\alpha|\le2,
\end{equation}
where $\partial^\alpha$ ranges over all mixed derivatives in $(x,v)$, for some $N\in(0,\infty)$ and constants $C_\alpha<\infty$ depending on $f$, and
\begin{equation}
f(x,v)=f(x,R_xv)\qquad\text{for all }x\in\partial\Omega,\ v\in\mathbb{R}^d.
\end{equation}
We write $\mathscr C_0:=\mathscr C\cap\Lmuz$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:52:47.249400+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b55be378888a79c7a49f31080061eabc6f33316ebfeb9a6485a95b79dd720f20","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 10 (Volume doubling) of arXiv:2609.01098, 'Gaussian upper bounds for averaged heat semigroups on graphs'] Let $x\in X$,   {$R_2\geq R_1\geq 4S$}, $n>2$ and $\phi\geq 1$. If for all $r\in[R_1,R_2]$ {and $u\in\cC_{c}(B_x(r))$}, we have
\begin{equation*}
\frac{m(B_x(r))^{\frac{2}{n}}}{\phi r^2}
\Vert u\Vert_{\frac{2n}{n-2}}^2
\leq \cE(u)+\frac{1}{r^2}\Vert u\Vert_2^2,
\end{equation*}
then we have
{\[
\frac{m(B_x(R))}{R^{n}}
\leq {A(n)} \Phi_x(n,r,R)\ \frac{m(B_x(r))}{r^{n}}, \quad R_1\leq r\leq R\leq R_2,
\]
}
where
{
\[
\Phi_x(n,r,R)=\left[1\vee  r^n
{\frac{m(B_x(R))}{m(B_x(R_1))R^n}}
\right]^{ 4\sqrt[n]{S/r}},\quad\mbox{and}\quad A(n)=2^{ 8n^2}\phi^{\frac{n}{2}}(1\vee S)^{4n}.
\]
}
In particular, if $R_2= 2R_1$, we obtain 
\begin{align*}
	m(B_x(R_2))
\leq {A'(n)} \Phi_x(n,R_2) m(B_x(R_2/2)),\qquad A'(n)=2^{ 9n^2}\phi^{\frac{n}{2}}(1\vee S)^{4n}
\end{align*}
where $\Phi_x(n,R_2)=\left[
{\frac{m(B_x(R_2))}{m(B_x(R_2/2))}}
\right]^{ 6\sqrt[n]{S/R_2}}\geq \Phi_x(n,R_2/2,R_2)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:55:37.885598+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b55f96a15ace983f0a5c386038b0612bf225b47ffdfb997b1f9841e065049d4f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lm:lclt_lemma of arXiv:2605.09377, 'A factorization formula for the partition function in the semi-discrete parabolic Anderson'] There is a constant $c > 0$, depending only on the dimension $d$, such that for any $r \in \mathbb{N}$,     
