{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.774795+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b59b1c39509c07c2bf24604ffe0a594f24db533975ae2ae67c6e4454e557763e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Thm:DPW_QD of arXiv:2609.02325, 'A Payne-Weinberger inequality\\for quantum dot Dirac operators'] Given $m\geqslant 0$ and  $\theta\in (-\frac{\pi}{2},\frac{\pi}{2})$, there exists a constant $C>0$ depending only on $m$ and $\theta$ such that
