{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.360391+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b5c230afe7ed47736fe981907a8a0aa9645e300e7e6d6fd3f8d1477bb98322ee","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:ordinary-BE-kernel of arXiv:2605.16244, 'Analysis of a twisted Bose--Einstein Markov chain with applications to sampling Catalan st'] Let $K_{\mathrm{BE}}$ and $\pi_{\mathrm{BE}}$ be the transition kernel and the stationary distribution of the Bose--Einstein Markov chain on $[k]^n$. Then for all $x,y \in [k]^n$,
\begin{equation}
 K_{\mathrm{BE}}(x,y)
 =\frac{1}{\prod_{a=1}^k i_a(x)!}
