	and its successive partial sums strictly bracket the left-hand side of \eqref{eq:nb-binet}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:20:55.705616+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b65dbadeda9ac15d284c990a9e7bc7631ed35ed5d0aa1ec130c3b825afd2711d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma LEM:bhperp of arXiv:2411.07840, 'Central limit theorem for the focusing $Φ^4$-measure in the infinite volume limit'] Under the condition $\textup{dist}(\supp g, x_0)=c_1>0$, where $g$ is smooth with compact support and $x_0 \in \mathbb{T}_L$, $b(h^{\perp })$ in (equation bhper of the paper) can be expressed in the coordinate $(h^{\perp \perp}, s)$ in (equation K1 of the paper)
