{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:14:57.636047+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b65e1fca2a1ea5d540d4cec8c0a705ef7dc64b675df95139c82f3d5e65ada4c5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:approximation lemma a bit more general prelim of arXiv:2605.28770, 'Cutoff profiles for conjugacy invariant random walks on symmetric groups'] Let $G$ be a finite group. Let $H$ be a subset of $G$, $A\subset B \subset \widehat{G}$, and let $(u_{\alpha})_{\alpha\in \widehat{G}}$ be a family of complex numbers. Then
