{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.769038+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b66b074f2440238f3fb1488faca14c9bb0f72da96b0fb916eb130527d0358085","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition NewProp of arXiv:2608.02897, 'Local limit theorem and Edgeworth expansions for inhomogeneous random walks on $GL(d,\bbR)'] Suppose that there are constants $C,\alpha,n_0>0$ such that for every $\epsilon\in(0,1)$,
