{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:50:44.876524+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b6b6180b6ade94702d2f60208f8e29ba00ca8cb47737c0481d212b0796c44f83","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 59 (All-order singular lattice profiles) of arXiv:2607.16724, 'Algebraic Transfer for Operator-Valued Gaussian Chaoses: Oriented Schatten Profiles and Si'] Let $\Gamma=\mathbb Z^D$, $m\ge2$, and
\[
 \frac{(m-1)D}{2m}<\sigma\le\frac D2,
 \qquad c_x=\langle x\rangle^{-\sigma}.
\]
Put
\[
 \beta_m=m\left(\frac D2-\sigma\right),\qquad
 \gamma_m=2m\sigma-(m-1)D,
\]
and
\begin{equation}

 \Omega_{m,\sigma}(R)=
 \begin{cases}
  R^{\beta_m},&\sigma<D/2,\\
  \log(e+R)^{m/2},&\sigma=D/2.
 \end{cases}
\end{equation}
For $R_+=\max\{L,Q\}$ and $R_-=\min\{L,Q\}$,
\begin{equation}

 \Prof_{m,r}(K_{m,N}^{L,Q}(c))
 \le C\Omega_{m,\sigma}(R_+)R_-^{D/r},
 \qquad2\le r\le\infty.
\end{equation}
If $N\ge M$ and $\sigma<D/2$, then
\begin{align}

 &\Prof_{m,r}(K_{m,N}^{L,Q}(c)-K_{m,M}^{L,Q}(c))\notag\\
 &\quad\le C\Omega_{m,\sigma}(R_+)R_-^{D/r}
 \min\{1,(R_+/M)^{\gamma_m/2}\}.
\end{align}
At $\sigma=D/2$, for every $0<\vartheta<D$ the right side is replaced by
\begin{equation}

 C_\vartheta\Omega_{m,D/2}(R_+)R_-^{D/r}
 \min\{1,(R_+/M)^{\vartheta/2}\}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:11:11.705419+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b6b61fa6474ec11e167624d6143ca4c96b1b09123bd022bbef602824cb6cbb53","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:sep of arXiv:2609.00672, 'Deciding superellipticity and computing the Weierstrass normal form'] Let $t: C\to\mathbb P^1$ be cyclic of degree $n$ with branch data $(l_1,\dots,l_r)$, the point at infinity included when it is a branch point. Then there is a birational map from $C$ to a curve $v^n=h(u)$ with $k(u)=k(t)$ and $h\in k[u]$ separable if and only if there is $c\in(\mathbb Z/n\mathbb Z)^\times$ such that

