{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:49.203025+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b6d3bd8602c2c0c86583823a71bc236ceaa057295759493730a583ef01ce5a66","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2604.26898, '\bf Stochastic Scaling Limits and Synchronization \\by Noise in Deep Transformer Models'] Under the previous assumptions, if $\dt \leq (2\mathsf c)^{-1}$:
\begin{align*}
X^i_{\ell+1} &= X^i_{\ell} + \dt P_{X^{i}_\ell}\attN{\ell}{X} + {\sqrt{\dt}} P_{X^i_{\ell}} G_{\ell+1}^m(X^i_\ell) \\
&\quad - \frac{{\dt}}{2}\left| P_{X^i_{\ell}} G_{\ell+1}^m(X^i_\ell) \right|^2 X^i_{\ell} - {\dt} ((X^i_{\ell})^\top G_{\ell+1}^m(X^i_\ell)) P_{X^i_{\ell}} G_{\ell+1}^m(X^i_\ell) + \mathcal{R}_\ell^i,
\end{align*}
where the total remainder $\mathcal{R}_\ell^i$ is bounded by:
\begin{align}

|\mathcal{R}^i_\ell| \leq   12\mathsf c\dt^2 + \mathsf c|\mathbf{w}|^3  + 2|\mathbf{w}| \mathsf c \dt + \frac{9}{2}|\mathbf{w}|^2 \mathsf c \dt +  (1 + 3|\mathbf{w}|)|\mathbf{w} - \mathbf{w}'| + \frac{3}{2}|\mathbf{w} - \mathbf{w}'|^2,
\end{align}
with the noise increments defined as $\mathbf{w} := \sqrt{\dt}G_{\ell+1}^m (Y^i_{\ell})$, $\mathbf{w}' := \sqrt{\dt}G_{\ell+1}^m (X^i_{\ell})$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.362573+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b6d45f0785fcb2701bb6bf956be8f618e6eb8d9b921d48e2f85917e054605538","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:omega-prime of arXiv:2509.23086, 'On Optimal Markovian Couplings of L\'evy Processes'] Let $\mathcal{A}, \mathcal{B} \in \mathcal{G}_2^\Lambda(\mathbb{R}^d)$ and $(x_0,y_0) \in \mathbb{R}^{2d}$. 
	We define the \emph{restricted dual transport derivative}
	\begin{align}
		\omega_2'(x_0, y_0; \mathcal{A}, \mathcal{B}) 
		:= \sup_{(\varphi,\psi)\in\mathcal{D}'(x_0,y_0)} 
		\Big[ \mathcal{A} \varphi(x_0) + \mathcal{B} \psi(y_0) \Big],
	\end{align}
	where $\mathcal{D}'(x_0,y_0)$ consists of all pairs 
	$(\varphi,\psi) \in [C^2_2(\mathbb{R}^d)]^2$ satisfying the \emph{touching condition}
	\begin{align}
		\varphi(x) + \psi(y) \,\le\, \tfrac{1}{2}|x-y|^2 
		\quad \text{for all $(x,y)$, with equality at } (x_0,y_0).
	\end{align}
	Equivalently, the definition in~(equation eq:omega-prime of the paper) is unchanged if condition~(equation eq:touch of the paper) is replaced by requiring that 
	\(
	c_2 - \varphi \oplus \psi
	\)
	attains a global minimum at $(x_0,y_0)$; see Remark~(rem:supdom of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:39:41.438749+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b6da2112db6bc717e8be2de1fd87e22e371fae2b7260e32dc91cc5e6547173b0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 12 of arXiv:2604.07370, 'Probabilistic Weyl law for twisted Toeplitz matrices with rough symbols'] For $\alpha_1$ and $\alpha_2$ such that $h\leq \alpha_1,\alpha_2\leq 1$, we denote $\Tilde{h}:=\frac{h}{\sqrt{\alpha_1\alpha_2}}$. We define $\mc{H}^d_{\Tilde{h},\alpha_1,\alpha_2}$ as the set of $u\in \mathscr{S}'(\R^d)$ such that for all $n\in \Z^d$, 
    \begin{equation*}
        u(x+\alpha_1^{-1/2}n)=u(x)\m\m\m\m\m\text{and} \m\m\m\m\m\mc{F}_{\Tilde{h}}(u)(\xi+\alpha_2^{-1/2}n)=\mc{F}_{\Tilde{h}}(u)(\xi) .
    \end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:38:57.117721+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b6da8a885bb19bad5315790d4e1236dcd4eb19c59c78643609521c59967c0f3f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 21 of arXiv:2604.04823, '2604.04823'] For any~$a\geq1$, there exist~$\hat\epsilon (a), \eta >0$ such that for any~$\epsilon$ and~$h$ with~$\epsilon < \hat\epsilon$ and~$h \leq \eta \epsilon^2$, the following holds. If~$x \in \Omega_h$ satisfies
