{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:23:27.789656+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b6ff0a993e5b3401b536efce42b78f9571a168e801e4f7ca208b9e860b62bbc4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Teo T: Survival of arXiv:2606.10165, 'The frog model with death and drift on free products of complete graphs'] Let $\beta = \frac{1-\alpha}{\Delta-1}$ and assume $m \geq 2$ and $d \geq 2$ are fixed integers. We define the functions

