{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:45:01.900238+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b7093e0b2b597206e28e47b6fd86c1e11b227d2f102acb5d20c22557910e40e2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma den1 of arXiv:2512.19897, 'On the convoy of the ASEP speed process'] Let $x\in \mathbb{R}$, $\gamma > 0$ and $n\in \mathbb{N}$. Let $q_n $ and $m_n\left(x\right)$ be as in our standard notation (equation standardnotation of the paper). Then, 
