{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:17:17.091158+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b723078e85e030b999a45fb7b10373931cc154b95467bd0b47bf1ba2094fba6b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 of arXiv:2608.19976, 'Random valuations'] Let $\Phi$ be a non-negative ID valuation.  Then there exists a
  unique (necessarily $\sigma$-finite) L\'evy measure $\Lambda$ on
  $\R_+^{\Kd}$ whose outer measure is concentrated on the family of valuations and a
  deterministic valuation $\phi$ such that, for any $m\ge1$, finite
  family $\sI=\{K_1,\dots,K_m\}\subset\Kd$, and $u\in\R_+^m$,
  \begin{displaymath}
    \E\exp\Big\{-\big\langle u,\Phi_{\sI}\big\rangle\Big\}
    =\exp\bigg\{-\langle u,\phi_{\sI}\rangle
    -\int_{\R_+^{\Kd}\setminus\{O_{\Kd}\}} \Big(1-e^{-\langle u,\psi_{\sI}\rangle}
    \Big)\Lambda(d\psi)\bigg\}.
  \end{displaymath}
  Furthermore, $\Phi$ is monotone if and only if $\phi$ is monotone
  and the $\Lambda$-outer measure is supported by monotone valuations.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:11.634221+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b724f43ea7906eb9f59fe0935245da399810fb547a1beba5043eb5d62c970133","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2605.31088, 'On couplings for kinetic Langevin diffusions'] Let $z,\tilde z\in\R^{2d}$ and $n\in\N_{>0}$, and assume
$U\colon\R^d\to\R$ is twice continuously differentiable with $\nabla U$
$L$-Lipschitz. Let $y$ be the trajectory defined by $y_0=\Delta z$
together with~\eqref{eq: def Ek}
and~\eqref{eq: y_k choices optimized trajectory}, and let
$\Psi^n_{z,\tilde z}$ be the coalescence map defined by $y$.  Then
\begin{equation}

    |\Psi^n_{z,\tilde z}(\xi)-\xi|^2 \leq 2\sum_{k=1}^n|E_k|^2+\frac{h^2L^2}{1-e^{-\gamma h}}\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}\l|u_{k}\r|^2,
\end{equation}
where $y_k=(u_k,w_k)$ and $E_k$ is given by~\eqref{eq: def Ek}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:01:25.659721+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b725ffce924dac92bf1405d98fb3298f99842f0fab40ba4e3f5704b5418298b1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem Lemma: Dimension reduction of arXiv:2605.16921, '${\ASL_n}(\mathbb Z)$ invariant random subsets of $\mathbb Z^n$'] With $f$ as fixed at the start of this section, there exist (up to an isomorphism of bundles of nilsystems) a subgroup $M \subseteq N_0$ such that:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $M$ stabilises $f$;
        \item $M \cap \Gamma$ is a lattice in $M$;
        \item $M$ is normal in $N_0$ and invariant under elements in the image of $\alpha$;
        \item the cocycle $\alpha_{N_0/M}$ is cohomologous to a cocycle taking values in a compact subgroup of $\Aut(N_0/M)$.
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:30.014107+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b7263d82e9d5a7677e44ead2c046fb87b31eecc5b3516ff97853588fdf24b0fd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2605.04684, 'Ergodicity of stochastic functional differential equation with jumps and finite delay'] Let $N(\d t,\d z)$ be a Poisson random measure on $\mathscr{B}\left(\mathbb{R}_{+}\right) \otimes \mathcal{Z}$ with compensator $\nu(\d z)\d t$  and fix $T>0$. Let $Y$ be the solution to the SDE
\begin{equation}
    \mathrm{d} Y(t)  =-\lambda Y(t) \mathrm{d} t+\int_{Z}h(t,z) \widetilde{N}(\d t,\d z) ,\quad Y(0)  =0,
\end{equation}
where $h$ is predictable with almost surely c\`agl\`ad sample paths.
\begin{enumerate}
\item If $\mathbb{E}\left(\int_{0}^{T} \int_{Z}|h(t, z)| \nu(\d z) \d t\right)<\infty$, then for any stopping time $\tau$, there exists a function $\varrho:[0, \infty) \rightarrow[0, \infty)$ with $\lim _{\lambda \rightarrow \infty} \varrho(\lambda)=0$ such that
\begin{equation}
    \begin{split}
        \mathbb{E}\left(\sup _{0 \leq t \leq \tau \wedge T}|Y(t)|^{p}\right)& \leq \varrho(\lambda) \bigg[\mathbb{E}\left(\sup _{0 \leq t \leq \tau \wedge T}\int_{Z}|h(t,z)|^{q}\nu(\d z)\right)^{p/q}\bigg].
    \end{split}
\end{equation}
holds for any $q \in[1,2]$ and $p \in(0, q]$.

\item If  $\mathbb{E}\left(\int_{0}^{T} \int_{Z}|h(t, z)|^{2} \nu(\d z) \d t\right)<\infty$ and $p \geq 2$, then for any stopping time $\tau$, there exists a function $\varrho:[0, \infty) \rightarrow[0, \infty)$ with $\lim _{\lambda \rightarrow \infty} \varrho(\lambda)=0$ such that
\begin{equation}
    \begin{split}
        \mathbb{E}\left(\sup _{0 \leq t \leq \tau \wedge T}|Y(t)|^{p}\right)& \leq \varrho(\lambda) \bigg[\mathbb{E}\left(\sup _{0 \leq t \leq \tau \wedge T}\int_{Z}|h(t,z)|^{2}\nu(\d z)\right)^{p/2}\\
        &\qquad\qquad +\mathbb{E}\left(\sup _{0 \leq t \leq \tau \wedge T}\int_{Z}|h(t,z)|^{p}\nu(\d z)\right)\bigg].
    \end{split}
\end{equation}
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:15:08.968221+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b728aac3f45006173f95a72ed72ac79570537d9f65bfe45f176a1908fe55d5cd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Theorem_corners_moments of arXiv:2411.10829, 'Airy$_\beta$ line ensemble and its Laplace transform'] Let $\{y^n_i\}_{1\leq i\leq k\leq N}\in \mathcal G_N$ be the G$\beta$E corners process of  variance $\tau$. Fix $m=1,2,\dots$ and take $2m$ positive integers $N_m\le N_{m-1}\le \dots \le N_1\le N$ and $k_1,k_2,\dots,k_m$. We have
 \begin{equation} 
  \mathbb E \left[ \prod_{\ell=1}^m \left(\sum_{i=1}^{N_\ell} \bigl(y^{N_\ell}_i\bigr)^{k_\ell}\right) \right]= \mathcal P_{k_m}^{N_m} \cdots \mathcal P_{k_2}^{N_2} \mathcal P_{k_1}^{N_1} \left[\exp\left(\frac{\tau}{2} \sum_{i=1}^N (x_i)^2\right)\right]_{x_1=\dots=x_N=0}.
 \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:59:24.049687+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b72c80179a98b3ad43baa59c2a37c987b66df3a574daf6d0f02aa8d33d6f91dc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:critical-shift of arXiv:2608.30831, 'Sharp discrete Hardy constants in dimensions three and four\\ and strict upper bounds from'] As $s\to\infty$,
\begin{equation}
 \mathcal R_{N,\beta}(s)
 =2N-\frac{(N-2)^2}{4s}
 +\frac{(N-2)(\beta_N^*-\beta)}{s^2}+O(s^{-3}),
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}
 \beta_N^*=\frac{N^3+18N^2+20N-24}{192}.
\end{equation}
If $\beta<\beta_N^*$, then $h_{N,\beta}$ cannot be a global supersolution for
the potential $A_N|n|^{-2}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:18:19.232640+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b72c878572f768cab9acc3a095f40280f0922e9e2934570b0cf023b8ebe57249","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 60 of arXiv:2608.29086, '2608.29086'] [Consistent vector fields]
Given $M \subset H_0$ and $\beta \in C^1(M)$. $\beta$ is called \textit{consistent} if 
\begin{equation*}
|\beta(ab)| \geq |\beta(bd)|,\   |\beta(da)| \quad \text{if } |\beta(ab)| \geq |\beta(bc)|,\  |\beta(ca)| 
\end{equation*}
for any pair $abc, abd \in Tri(S)$ sharing edge $ab$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:01:25.653172+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b72fbee58ef2f20cd52c3cfb19811c421b44eca419893a934bc56a6db3d50e26","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:loops-loop variables of arXiv:2605.16162, 'Deconfinement For $\mathrm{SO}(3)$ Lattice Yang--Mills at Strong Coupling'] We will represent loops $\ell$ in $\Lambda$ by the sequence of oriented edges $\ell = e_1 \cdots e_n$ that are traversed by $\ell$. We denote $|\ell| := n$. Let $Q : E_\Lambda^+ \ra G$ be a lattice gauge configuration. For  a loop $\ell=e_1e_2\dots e_n$, let $Q_{\ell}:=Q_{e_1}Q_{e_2}\dots Q_{e_n}$ denote the corresponding loop variable. We define
\begin{equs}
W_\ell(Q) := \tr(Q_\ell),
\end{equs}
where $\tr = \frac{1}{N} \Tr$ is the normalized trace.
We refer to $W_\ell$ as a Wilson loop observable.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:55:18.919940+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b7366d7fcb504cbc0051fd027fe42b12cfbb3bd63cec3a8af900eae0e7cbc5ba","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:URD of arXiv:2601.21762, 'Navier-Stokes with a fractional transport noise as a limit of multi-scale dynamics'] [URDog, EnergymethodRPDEs]
    Let $\alpha\in(\frac 13,\frac 12]$. An $\alpha$-continuous unbounded rough driver with respect to the scale $(H^{m})_{m>0}$ is a pair $(A^{1},A^{2})$ 
    of two index maps such that for any $s,t\in [0,T]$:
    \begin{align*}
        \norm{A^{1}_{s,t}}_{\mathcal{L}(H^{-m};H^{-(m+1)})} &\lesssim |t-s|^{\alpha}, \qquad m\in [0,2], \\
        \norm{A^{2}_{s,t}}_{\mathcal{L}(H^{-m};H^{-(m+2)})} &\lesssim |t-s|^{2\alpha}, \qquad
        m\in [0,1],
    \end{align*}
    and satisfies the Chen's relations: 
        $\delta A^{1}_{s,r,t}=0$ and $ \delta A^{2}_{s,r,t}=A^{1}_{r,t}A^{1}_{s,r}$  for all $ 0\leq s \leq r \leq t \leq T$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:57:30.994932+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b737820bdf5e57381c66b9677302a4f6b11d37754c37475993dbd510861dac52","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 46 (Scale-invariant reduced capture) of arXiv:2608.12492, 'Weak Limits of Wiener Chaos: Primitive--Fock Classification and Hilbert--Stein Extraction'] Assume $\mathfrak H:=\mathfrak H_Q(A,r)>0$.  Choose $q_*$ with maximal
$\lambda_*=\lambda_{\max}(E_{q_*})$, let $L_*$ be its full top eigenspace, and promote
