    p(t, x, y) = \frac{1}{\sqrt{2 \pi t}} \exp\left(-\frac{(y - x)^2}{2t}\right), \quad x, y \in \mathbb{R}. 
 \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:37:09.018637+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b7419ad1eceaf0fe273c55e942676ef6e3cd45d308d3b79d495f6a8d6d3545fb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:lln_lag of arXiv:2609.01697, 'Unique ergodicity of projective cocycles over the 2D stochastic Navier--Stokes equations'] Let $m \geqslant 1$ be an integer and let $(X_k)_{k \geqslant 0}$ be random variables such that
