{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.635429+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b74eac54d0a177f9119ea974a5d0601db7a7fa505f335987071f7fbb1a0a04c4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2609.01362, '{Double cluster swapping for spin models: \\Pfaffian relations and sharpness}'] Let $S$ be a reduction set for $G$ such that $S \subset \Vis$. 
    Then, there exists a classical spin model $ \widetilde{\vp}$ on the reduced graph $ \widetilde{G} = ( \widetilde{V}, \widetilde{E}) := R(G, S)$ such that 
