{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.680758+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b758912f698bc1044f82c8be8aebb38de09047195253f402486ca3ba7069f45e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:no-macro-contours of arXiv:2606.06612, 'The limit shape and emergence of the \\ Discrete Gaussian level lines'] For sufficiently large $\beta$, and $h$ such that ${\widehat\pi}_\infty(\phi_o\geq h) \leq (1/\log L)^2$, suppose $F \subset V \subset \mathbb Z^2$ and
