{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.350657+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b782363b64966fa841eaeebe20c839fe730c53bbd96fef50a6f9faf46cdfb476","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma_xinlandu_gendif of arXiv:2509.18045, 'Density convergence on Markov diffusion chaos via Stein's method'] Fix  $x\in (\ell, u)$ and $k\in \mathbb{N}$. Let the function $h$ in the ODE (equation equation_stein of the paper) be 
    \begin{align*}
        h(y):=\mathds{1}_{\{y>x\}}\frac{-2a(y)+b'(y)}{b(y)},\quad y\in \mathbb{R}\setminus \left\{y\in(x,\infty):b(y)=0 \right\}.
    \end{align*} 
Then a solution $g_x: \mathbb{R}\setminus \brac{\left\{y\in(\ell,u)^\complement:a(y)=0 \right\}\cup\left\{y\in(\ell,u):b(y)=0 \right\}}\to\mathbb{R}$ to (equation equation_stein of the paper) exists and satisfies for every $y$ in its domain, 

\begin{align*}
    & \left\vert g_x(y) \right\rvert\\
    &\leq \mathcal{V}_1(x,y):=\mathds{1}_{ \{y\geq u \} }\frac{\left\vert -2a(y)+b'(y) \right\rvert}{\left\vert b(y) \right\rvert2\left\vert a(y) \right\rvert }+\mathds{1}_{ \{y\notin (\ell,u) \} }\frac{p_\mathcal{Y}(x) }{2\left\vert a(y) \right\rvert}+\mathds{1}_{\{y\in(\ell,u) \}}C(x); 
\end{align*}
and 
\begin{align*}
    &\left\vert g_x'(y) \right\rvert\\
    &\leq \mathcal{V}_2(x,y):= \mathds{1}_{\{y\in(\ell,u) \}}\brac{C(x)\frac{\left\vert a(y) \right\rvert}{\left\vert b(y) \right\rvert}+\frac{\left\vert -2a(y)+b'(y) \right\rvert}{\left\vert b(y) \right\rvert^2}+\frac{p_\mathcal{Y}(x)}{\left\vert b(y) \right\rvert}}\\
    &+\mathds{1}_{ \{y\geq u\} } 2\abs{\frac{(-2a'(y)+b''(y))b(y)-(-2a(y)+b'(y))b'(y) }{b(y)^2a(y)}}\\
   &\qquad+\mathds{1}_{ \{y\geq u \} }
\abs{\frac{-2a(y)+b'(y)}{b(y)4a(y)^2} }+\mathds{1}_{ \{y\notin (\ell,u) \} }\frac{p_\mathcal{Y}(x) }{4a(y)^2}. 
\end{align*} 

Here $C(x)>0$ is a function that is well-defined on $(\ell,u)$ and does not depend on $y$.","status":"unverified"}

