{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.321913+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b7a4976bbc99a26d196af5eb1316f6d65ac8d0c51e36bc04badc2366545e4495","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary c:Gill of arXiv:2411.14936, 'Massive Particle Systems,\\Wasserstein Brownian Motions,\\ and the Dean--Kawasaki Equation'] In the setting of Theorem~(t:BendikovSaloffCoste of the paper) and under assumptions~(i:t:BendikovSaloffCoste:a of the paper)--(i:t:BendikovSaloffCoste:f of the paper) there,
\[
\boldsymbol\mssT_\bullet = \ev \circ (\widehat\otimes_k \mssH_{k,\bullet}) \circ \ev^{-1} \,\mathrm{.}
\]
\begin{proof}
Let~$(\boldsymbol\mssL^{\scriptscriptstyle\otimes },\dom{\boldsymbol\mssL^{\scriptscriptstyle\otimes }})$ be the generator of~$\widehat\otimes_k \mssH_{k,\bullet}$ on~$\widehat\otimes_k^{\car} L^2(\nu_k)$. By~[Gil74] we have $\otimes_k^{\car}\msD(\mssL_k)\subset \dom{\boldsymbol\mssL^{\scriptscriptstyle\otimes }}$ and
\[
\boldsymbol\mssL^{\scriptscriptstyle\otimes } (\otimes_k f_k) = \Sigma_k (\mssL_k f_k) \otimes_{i\neq k} f_i\,\mathrm{,}\;\, \qquad \otimes_k f_k\in \otimes_k^{\car}\msD(\mssL_k) \,\mathrm{.}
\]
As a consequence,~$\ev^{-1}\circ \boldsymbol\mssL^{\scriptscriptstyle\otimes } \circ \ev =\tilde\boldsymbol\mssL$ on~$\ev\tparen{ \otimes_k^{\car} \msD(\mssL_k)} \supset \Cyl{}{}$.
Since, as shown in the proof of Theorem~(t:BendikovSaloffCoste of the paper)(i:t:BendikovSaloffCoste:2 of the paper), the operator~$(\tilde\boldsymbol\mssL,\Cyl{}{})$ is essentially self-adjoint on~$L^2(\boldsymbol\nu)$, the operator~$\tparen{\boldsymbol\mssL^{\scriptscriptstyle\otimes },\otimes_k^{\car}\msD(\mssL_k)}$ is essentially self-adjoint on~$\widehat\otimes_k^{\car} L^2(\nu_k)$, and~$(\tilde\boldsymbol\mssL,\msD(\tilde\boldsymbol\mssL))\circ\ev = \ev \circ (\boldsymbol\mssL^{\scriptscriptstyle\otimes },\dom{\boldsymbol\mssL^{\scriptscriptstyle\otimes }})$.
It follows that the corresponding semigroups too are intertwined by~$\ev$, i.e.~$\boldsymbol\mssH_\bullet \circ \ev= \ev \circ (\widehat\otimes_k \mssH_{k,\bullet})$, and the conclusion follows by the identification~$\boldsymbol\mssH_\bullet=\boldsymbol\mssT_\bullet$ in Theorem~(t:BendikovSaloffCoste of the paper)(i:t:BendikovSaloffCoste:3 of the paper).
\end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

