{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:37:08.316329+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b7ee669bb540ff62845af3d4efc50311fa0476086ad4248446749e9e20df9695","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Perfect fits of arXiv:2608.30973, 'Pseudo-Anosov flow and dynamics on guts'] Two leaves \(F\in \mathcal{F}^{s}\) and \(G\in \mathcal{F}^{u}\), form a \emph{perfect fit} if \(F\) has a half ray \(F'\) and \(G\) has a half ray \(G'\), such that
