{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:29:35.077485+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b7f56c46cc44cad986470eafb28a146c415371cd0b8f57ff522cda6d1ef382b2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2609.03793, 'Typical martingale diverges on a co-$\sigma$-porous set'] Let $(X,\psi)$ be a metric space and let $x\in X$, $A\subset X$ and $\alpha>0$. Then $A$ is $2\alpha$-porous at $x$ if and only if
