{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.770419+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b809c1e95b37c59e47742cc2609398c9835b1e7bfa3e19578d017f536f9c539d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem thm:UniformLLN-new of arXiv:2411.18155, 'Besov regularity of random wavelet series'] Let $(X_{j,\tau})_{j \in \mathds{N}_0, \tau \in \mathds{N}}$ be a family of non-negative i.i.d.\ random variables.
Suppose that
\begin{equation}
\mathds{E}[X_{j,\tau} \cdot \log_2^+ (X_{j,\tau})] < \infty.
\end{equation}
Fix $d\in\mathds{N}$ and let
\begin{align*}
M_j&\mathrel{\mathop:}= \#\setcond{m\in\mathds{Z}^d}{\left\lVertm\right\rVert_{\infty}\leq 2^j}=(2^{j+1}+1)^d,\\
N_j&\mathrel{\mathop:}=\#\setcond{m\in\mathds{Z}^d}{2^j<\left\lVertm\right\rVert_\infty\leq 2^{j+1}}=M_{j+1}-M_j
\end{align*}
for $j\in\mathds{N}_0$.
Then the (random) quantity 
\begin{equation*}
\Xi\mathrel{\mathop:}= \sup_{j \in \mathds{N}_0} \lr{\frac{1}{M_j} \sum_{\tau=1}^{M_j} X_{j,\tau}+\sup_{\ell\geq j} \frac{1}{N_\ell} \sum_{\tau=M_\ell + 1}^{M_{\ell+1}} X_{j,\tau}}
\end{equation*} 
is almost surely finite.","status":"unverified"}

