{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:26.250772+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b8182a85e99a0e09a48901ab629b1d870f6985dd6598c941d587d1cb417e2330","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 5 of arXiv:2605.22760, 'Extremes of Gaussian fields with a product term in the variance'] Assume \ref{ass:variance}--\ref{ass:nondegenerate}.  Fix \(M>0\), \(\lambda>0\), and \(\varepsilon>0\).  There exists \(\delta>0\) such that, as \(u\to\infty\),
\begin{align}
&\PP\left\{\sup_{\bft\in S_{1,u}(\lambda)\cup S_{2,u}(\lambda)}X(\bft)>u\right\}
\notag\\
&\quad\le
(1+\varepsilon)\Psi(u)
\biggl[
2\calH_\alpha(\lambda)^2
+\frac{\calH_\alpha(M)\calH_\alpha(\lambda)}{M}u^{2/\alpha}
      \sum_{i=1}^2\int_0^\delta e^{-(1-\varepsilon)u^2x^\beta}\dd x
\biggr].
\end{align}
In addition, if \(R_u\to\infty\) and \(R_uq_u=o(u^{-2/\beta})\), then for some function \(\eta_1(M)\downarrow0\) as \(M\to\infty\),
\begin{align}
&\PP\left\{\sup_{t\in[0,\delta]}X(t,0)>u\ \text{or}\ \sup_{t\in[0,\delta]}X(0,t)>u\right\}
\notag\\
&\quad\ge
(1-\varepsilon)\frac{\calH_\alpha(M)}{M}u^{2/\alpha}
\Psi(u)
\sum_{i=1}^2\int_{R_uq_u}^\delta e^{-(1+\varepsilon)u^2x^\beta}\dd x
\notag\\
&\hspace{2.5em}
-\eta_1(M)\Psi(u)u^{2/\alpha}\int_0^\delta e^{-(1-\varepsilon)u^2x^\beta}\dd x+o\left(\Psi(u)u^{2/\alpha-2/\beta}\right).
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.888656+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b819bd46b6fcec3d415f91857ea785dfaadc1208c46c4998725750377aa1cbd8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 31 (Long-range order threshold) of arXiv:2504.02435, 'Poisson-Voronoi percolation in higher rank'] Let $G$ be a lcsc group acting continuously and transitively by isometries on a proper geodesic metric space $(M,d)$ and fix some $o\in M$. Suppose that $G$ has property (T). Then for every $R>0$, there exists $p^*<1$ such that every $G$-invariant normal random closed subset $\mathcal Z$ of $M$ with $\mathbb P(o \in \partial \mathcal Z)=0$ satisfies
