{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:33:12.363464+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b865a510653794a93265a8de301c95eb9048fdbcb7f6a7ce55f0134453d83c05","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 (Consistency and rate for \textup{($iii$)}) of arXiv:2608.29465, 'Deciding When to Decide:\\Testing Operational Suboptimality Under Distributional Shift'] Suppose the assumptions of Lemma~\ref{lem:termI_consistency} hold, specifically the square-integrability of the envelope and Lipschitz modulus under $\mathbb{P}_1$. Let $\varepsilon_{m''}$ denote the uniform convergence rate of the empirical OCE risk over the evaluation sample. It holds that:
