{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:10.965935+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b89b08774d18944f6e7b0720a4a8f5c1854ed6168b297bed0a6b3d90fe83d9b1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 22 of arXiv:2606.12720, 'On McDiarmid's Inequality under Dependence \\ via Approximate Tensorization of Entropy'] {Gaussian Hamming-Lipschitz Concentration}


    Let $X \sim \mathcal N(\mu, \Sigma)$ on $\R^n$ with $\Sigma \in \R^{n \times n}$. Assume $f : \R^n \to \R$ fulfills the bounded differences property with constants $c = (c_1,...,c_n)\T$. Then, with $\kappa^\star(\Sigma) := \eigmax{D^{1/2} \Sigma D^{1/2}}$ where $D := \diagonal{\Sigma\inv}$, 
    \begin{align*}
