{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.677233+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b8addebfa436eaca2f4753cb78d765e64b5ad65814604fff3acf6e9d065423b1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm main of arXiv:2411.12149, 'Airy limit for $\beta$-additions through Dunkl operators'] Let $\lambda_{i}(N)\ (i=1,2,\ldots,N)$ denote the eigenvalues of our $N\times N$ addition in Eqn.~((eq_betaaddition of the paper)). Assume that ((eq_gamma of the paper)), ((eq_alpha of the paper)) and ((eq_positivekappa of the paper)) hold,  then there exists a positive constant $\tilde{C}$ and a sequence of positive real numbers $\mu_{+}(N)$, such that
