the $\mathrm{Airy}(\beta)$ process. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:43:19.187800+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b8aef32600d64bf7e617030bb3965f0ad9bfab7b482c7a6acdf65e56af6a5b0e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma4.1 of arXiv:2609.02607, 'Spatial inhomogeneity for a three-dimensional doubly degenerate nutrient system with indir'] Let $\Omega \subset \mathbb R^3$  be a smoothly bounded domain and $K>0$ with the property that (equation 1.6 of the paper) holds. Then there exist  $\sigma>0$ and $C=C(K)>0$ such that for all $\varepsilon\in(0,1)$ we have
