{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.460515+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b8afd76871f768c35ccf58b1b66858383ee474b98fb6f03ee009814746071da4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Pro 10 (Evolution of one-sided supports) of arXiv:2609.02523, '\bf Strong Ill-Posedness in critical and subcritical regimes for the Hunter--Saxton equati'] Let $u_0 \in C^\infty(\R)\cap L^\infty(\mathbb R)\cap\dot H^1(\mathbb R)$, and let $u$ be the associated global
dissipative solution.
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\roman*)}]
\item If $\supp u_0\subset[a,\infty)$, then
\begin{equation*}
	 \supp u(t,\cdot)\subset[a,\infty),  \qquad \text{for every } t \geqslant 0.
\end{equation*}
\item If $\supp u_0\subset(-\infty,b]$, then
\begin{equation}
  \supp \partial_x u(t,\cdot)  \subset \left(-\infty,b+\frac{t^2}{4}\|u_0'\|_{L^2}^2\right],  \qquad\text{for every } t \geqslant 0.
\end{equation}
Moreover, $u(t,\cdot)$ is constant on the right of the endpoint in
\eqref{right-q-support}.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:56:14.353652+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b8b2c7c7ef78392c9b2994a27de53330c0e44fb51fed49b113ebe18365ca8e1b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Them fd_to_wiener of arXiv:2412.10001, 'On the Markov transformation of Gaussian processes'] Let us consider a continuous positive semi-definite  kernel $K : \mathbb{R} \times \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}$ such that $K(t,t) = 1$ for every $t \in \mathbb{R}.$ We denote by $P$ a centered Gaussian measure with covariance function $K.$ 
		\begin{enumerate}
			\item Assume, for every $s<t \in \mathbb{R}^2$,
			\begin{equation*}
				\sup_{v \in [s,t]} \left|L^K_v(h) - \alpha^K(v)\right| \xrightarrow[h \to 0^+]{} 0.
			\end{equation*}  
				 Then  \[ \forall (R_n)_{n \geq 1} \in \mathcal{A},  \forall a<b \in \mathbb{R}^2, \textnormal{proj}^{[a,b]}_\# P_{[R_n]} \xrightarrow[n \to + \infty]{w} \textnormal{proj}^{[a,b]}_\# P_{\alpha^K}.\]
			\item Assume  $K : (s,t) \mapsto \tilde{K}(t-s)$ is a stationary positive semi-definite kernel, $ \alpha \in \mathbb{R}_+$ is a cluster point of $L : h \in \mathbb{R}_+^* \mapsto h^{-1}(1- \tilde{K}(h)) $ and $L$ is bounded. Fix $(s_n)_{n \geq 1}$ a positive sequence converging to zero such that $\lim_{n \to + \infty} L^K(s_n) = \alpha$ and set $(R_n)_{n \geq 1} := \left( \left( s_n \cdot \mathbb{Z} \right) \cap [-n,n] \right)_{n \geq 1} \in \mathcal{A}$. Then \[\forall a<b \in \mathbb{R}^2, \textnormal{proj}^{[a,b]}_\# P_{[R_n]} \xrightarrow[n \to + \infty]{w} \textnormal{proj}^{[a,b]}_\# P_\alpha.\]
		\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:44:27.958233+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b8b2ffbfbe832bd4776df0754e9bfe2f14879d89e05cac13c18c716e7f5be937","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 (Hitting before killing and forest connectivity) of arXiv:2607.13210, 'Punctured Wilson--Evolving Sets and Root Identities for Massive Kirchhoff Forests'] Let $U\subset V$ and $x\notin U$. Then
