{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.972297+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b8bff718df5b37457580d688ee0c6c5f893a15025cb419b9df5827d1d1c7f390","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2411.07157, 'Rough differential equations in the flow approach'] Let $\mu \in[0,1]$, $\tau_i \in \mathfrak{T}$, and $\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_i} \in {\mcb{C}}[\tau_i]\,$ for $i = 1,2$. 
We can then write 
\[
\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_2}
\graft^\mu\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_1}=\prod_{\tau\in\mathfrak{T}} \big(\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_2}\graft^\mu\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_1}\big)^\tau\,,
\]
where one has $\big(\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_2}\graft^\mu\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_1}\big)^\tau \in {\mcb{C}}[\tau]$. Moreover, for any $\underline{\tau} \in \tau$, $\underline{\tau}_1 \in \tau_1$ and $\underline{\tau}_2 \in \tau$, again writing for $n \in N(\underline{\tau}_1)$ $\underline{\tau}_{1,2,n} = \underline{\tau}_{2} \graft_{n} \underline{\tau}_{1}$, we have
\begin{equ}  
\big(\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_2}\graft^\mu\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_1}\big)^{\underline{\tau}}
\eqdef
\iota_{\underline{\tau}}
\big(\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_2}\graft^\mu\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_1}\big)^{\tau}
=
\sum_{\substack{n\in N(\underline{\tau}_1)\\
\underline{\tau}_{1,2,n}\in\tau}}\
\frac{1}{|\mathrm{Aut}(\tau)|} 
\sum_{ f \in \mathrm{Iso}(\underline{\tau}_{1,2,n},\underline{\tau})}
\mathbf{f} \big( \text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\underline{\tau}_2} \graft^{\mu}_{n} \text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\underline{\tau}_1} \big)\;.
\end{equ}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.240377+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b8c2ac8589ba3bdaa89f0bd688d28ba6a4cbc64e80d2a97965055bafea581e81","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2604.14752, 'Strong and weak rates of convergence in the Smoluchowski--Kramers approximation for stocha'] For all $\alpha\in[0,1]$ and all $\delta\in[0,\frac{\alpha}{2}]$, there exists $C_{\alpha,\delta}\in(0,\infty)$ such that, for all $\epsilon\in(0,1)$ and all $t>0$ one has
\begin{equation}
\underset{n\in\N}\sup~\Bigl(\lambda_n^{2\delta-\alpha}\big|f_n^{\epsilon,1,0}(t)-e^{-t\lambda_n}\big|^2\Bigr)\le Ct^{-2\delta}\epsilon^{2\alpha}.
\end{equation}

Moreover, for all $\alpha\in[0,1]$ and all $\delta\in[\frac{\alpha}{2},\frac12]$, there exists $C_{\alpha,\delta}\in(0,\infty)$ such that, for all $\epsilon\in(0,1)$ and all $t>0$ one has
