{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:32:11.131337+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b8e9f99833242a9845aa397eb798711eecedf26248c23835a0ac5bcd96be1810","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm th3 of arXiv:2510.10898, 'A central limit theorem for unbalanced step-reinforced random walks'] Assume that
\begin{eqnarray*}
\sum_{k=1}^n \xi_k  /{a_n}\stackrel{d}{\rightarrow} S,
\end{eqnarray*}
where $S$ is a stable random variable 
with characteristic function $\mathbb{E}(e^{it S})=e^{-|t|^{\alpha}}$ and $\alpha\in (0,2)$.
Suppose further that
\begin{enumerate}
\item[$(A5).$]
$
\frac{1}{n}\sum_{k=1}^n |W_{nk}|^{\alpha} \stackrel{d}{\rightarrow} F,
$ where $F$ is some distribution function;
 \item[$(A6).$]   There exists $\beta\ge 1$ satisfying $\beta>\alpha$ and  $
\lim\limits_{c\rightarrow \infty} \sup\limits_n \frac{1}{n}\sum_{k=1}^n \mathbb{E} (|W_{nk}|^{\beta} I(|W_{nk}|>c))=0.
$
\end{enumerate}
Then we have
\begin{eqnarray*}
\frac{1}{a_n}\sum_{k=1}^n W_{nk} \xi_k \stackrel{d}{\longrightarrow} W^{1/\alpha}  S,
\end{eqnarray*}
where $W$ is a non-negative random variable with distribution function $F$, independent of $S$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

