{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.063294+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b93b08e6a4fa5a1a219db82638cac2c0f50afceb91d2f2ae0dae4081535e3260","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 8 of arXiv:2606.17452, 'Optional Stopping for Superhedging Supermartingales'] (Stopping Time \cite[Definition 5.3]{bender3})  
Given a Trajectory Space $\Se$, a \emph{trajectory based stopping time} (or \emph{stopping time} for short) is a function $\tau:\Se\rightarrow \mathbb{N}\cup\{\infty\}$ such that:
\begin{equation*}
    \text{for any}\quad S,S'\in\Se\quad\text{if}\quad S_k=S'_k\quad\text{for}\quad 0\leq k\leq \tau(S),\quad\text{then}\quad \tau(S)=\tau(S').
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

