{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:04.860762+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b9408e6ecbcdd45d770104de92dc5ea7f69bd51535e3474c855f96891c55a805","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 29 of arXiv:2511.21496, 'Optimal local central limit theorems on Wiener chaos'] Let $F \in \bD^{k+1, p}$ and $\Delta_F^{-1} \in L^q(\Omega)$ for some $k \in \N$ and $p, q\in (1, \infty)$. 
If $s_j = s_j[p,q] > 1$ for some $j \in \{1, \ldots, k\}$, then for any $i \in \{1, \ldots, j\}$, the linear operator
\begin{equation}
    \sC_F^{(-i, s_i)} \colon \cS_{-i} \to \bW^{-i,s_i}, \qquad \Dom \left(\sC_F^{(-i, s_i)}\right) = \cS(\R),  \qquad \varphi \mapsto \varphi(F) 
\end{equation}
is continuous and can be uniquely extended to the continuous linear operator 
\begin{equation}
    \wt{\sC_F^{(-i, s_i)}} \colon \cS_{-i} \to \bW^{-i,s_i}, \qquad  \Dom \left(\wt{\sC_F^{(-i, s_i)}}\right) = \cS_{-i}. 
\end{equation}
Moreover, for any $i_1, i_2 \in \{1, \ldots, j\}$ with $i_1 \leq i_2$ and any $T \in \cS_{-i_1}$, we have
\begin{equation}
    \wt{\sC_F^{(-i_2, s_{i_2})}}(T) = \wt{\sC_F^{(-i_1, s_{i_1})}}(T) \quad \text{in $\bW^{-i_1, s_1}$}. 
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:33.747002+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b941c6e4bcb4d208fa4f893fb2052571c32e082ca866af4375f1f06e9e257bdf","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 24 of arXiv:2606.11994, 'Sample Path Properties of the\\ Fractional Wiener--Weierstrass Bridge II'] Let $1\le q<\infty$.  If $a_n\to a$ and $c_n\to c$ in $[0,1]$, then
