{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:07.263867+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b9678233d17f09510e028df162dfec21b527165dfb7f4b0dbcd84356efc42bbb","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 36 (Locally uniformly bounded family) of arXiv:2604.19738, 'Phase Transitions in the Fluctuations of Functionals of Random Neural Networks \\'] A family $\mathcal{F}$ of functions $F : D \to \mathbb{C}$ is said to be \emph{locally uniformly bounded}
