{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:05:52.396915+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b988683e3ae1148906d0502ccec355649bb9370c750ef38bddf6fc9f63b9a7da","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma c4.1 of arXiv:2504.15992, 'Repeated singular values of a random symmetric matrix and decoupled singular value estimat'] Fix $B>0,\zeta\in\Gamma_B$ and $A_n\sim\operatorname{Sym}_n(\zeta)$. Then for any $x\in\mathbb{S}^{n-1}$, one has
