{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:35:05.805686+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b988d7d7afa7238890ae81f7d537b24d0b3905582ca09243861a6797fb8091f7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma L:Int-8 of arXiv:2606.23865, 'Uniform-in-time Gaussian fluctuations for multiscale nonlinear stochastic systems via Mall'] For $0 \le u \le s \le w \le r \le t$, let the term $\mathcal{J}_8(t;\varepsilon,\eta)$ be defined as follows:
\begin{multline*}
\mathcal{J}_8(t;\varepsilon,\eta)  \triangleq K  \int_{u=0}^t \int_{s=u}^t \int_{w=s}^t \int_{r=w}^t  (\varepsilon+ \eta + \sqrt{\varepsilon \eta}) e^{-\alpha (t-u)} e^{-\alpha(t-s)} e^{- \alpha(t-w)}  e^{-\frac{\lambda}{\eta} (r-w)} e^{-\frac{\lambda}{\eta} (s-u)} \\
\times  e^{-\frac{\lambda}{\eta} (w-s)} dr \thinspace dw \thinspace ds \thinspace du. 
\end{multline*}
Then, there exists a time-independent positive constant $K$ such that
$$ \mathcal{J}_8(t;\varepsilon,\eta) \le K  \thinspace \eta^2 \thinspace (\varepsilon+ \eta + \sqrt{\varepsilon \eta}).$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:24:45.912155+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b98952f904fc948da2f30418d100c8f47d787d155c507a6ab112b052365baecd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem theo:normald=1 of arXiv:2509.07372, 'On the edge eigenvalues of sparse random geometric graphs'] Fix some small constant $0<\varepsilon<\frac{1}{2(d+4)}$ and assume 
