{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:40.983389+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b9ea74a3976ecb53d8f7bec325988ddfc61cd4b6545b7b080f727f0eceaa1de8","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop_9 of arXiv:2412.03774, '{ Refining Concentration for \\Gaussian Quadratic Chaos with\\ Applications in Sonar and C'] Let $r(A)\geq 3$, $\lambda_{\max}(A)>0$, $\lambda_1,\cdots, \lambda_k$ be as in ((poloi_1 of the paper)) and $r(A)-k$ be even. If
