{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:33:17.741271+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ba00bc116cfbdeee159053bdfe47b9a710e372a586a55a44c7eb6e88e078fe86","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 112 (Rough and oscillatory kernel bounds) of arXiv:2607.10813, '2607.10813'] Uniformly for $0\le r_1,r_2\le t\le T$ and $\nu=0,1$,
\begin{equation}
  |\mathcal K_{a,\nu}
  (\xi,\eta;t,r_1,r_2)|
  \lesssim_T
  \frac{N_0^\nu}{N_0N_1N_2}.
\end{equation}
If
\[
  |\xi|\ge1,
  \qquad |\eta|\ge1,
  \qquad |\xi-\eta|\ge1,
\]
then
\begin{equation}
  |\mathcal K_{a,\nu}|
  \lesssim_T
  \frac{N_0^\nu}{N_0N_1N_2}
  \sum_{\bm\eps\in\{\pm1\}^3}
  \mathfrak m(\Phi_a^{\bm\eps}(\xi,\eta)).
\end{equation}
Moreover, if $0<\theta\le1/2$ and
$0\le r_1,r_2\le t\wedge t'$, then the corresponding time difference satisfies
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
  &|\mathcal K_{a,\nu}
  (\xi,\eta;t,r_1,r_2)
  -\mathcal K_{a,\nu}
  (\xi,\eta;t',r_1,r_2)|\\
  &\quad\lesssim_{T,\theta}
  |t-t'|^\theta
  \frac{N_0^\nu N_{\max}^\theta}{N_0N_1N_2}
  \sum_{\bm\eps\in\{\pm1\}^3}
  \mathfrak m(\Phi_a^{\bm\eps}(\xi,\eta))
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
whenever the three displayed frequencies are at least one.  Without that high-frequency condition, the same estimate holds with the sign sum on the right replaced by $1$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:42:08.458583+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ba0284c53233cffd459d8b71b728315e19e974aaabaa960430b5cb3b2ca3aa48","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem MH2p1 of arXiv:2511.15893, 'On a Class of Dynamical Poisson-Voronoi Tessellations'] Suppose there are two types of stations with intensities $\lambda_1, \lambda_2$ and speeds $v_1> v_2$. Let $\lambda_1+\lambda_2=\lambda$. Then we have:

