with constants that depend only on $d, M, K_{\mathrm{IR}}, s_0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:33:12.000191+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ba66946e3e14d42720d4bf96c04a813456ae7719d6d43a67481be95ba8f9e3b3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:discrepancy of arXiv:2609.02820, 'Sharpness and critical scaling of parking'] Under the assumptions of Theorem~(thm:master of the paper), suppose $d\leq3$. For
	$n\geq1$, let $r=2\vee\lceil\log(n+1)\rceil$. Then
