{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:53.178080+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ba670d1c9bafd0e71e070847a77d8f3a439c1e36c175ef022b5e968736a812c1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 2 (Exact Poissonized identity) of arXiv:2606.29635, 'Extremality and Limit Laws for the Siblings of the Coupon Collector'] For every $N\ge1$, every probability vector $p$, and every $j\ge2$,
