{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.304580+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_babd4ac0bc37acf05c08c470fb586e5cef4ec5ca3525d5b696ecacafeb873bfd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:asymptotical_optimality of arXiv:2607.13748, 'Load Balancing with Individually Heterogeneous Servers'] Suppose that the assumptions of Theorem~(thm:stationary_bounds of the paper) hold. Then, for any tie-breaking policy $\pi$ where the stationary  $(X_1^{\pi,n}(\infty), \boldsymbol{\xi}^{\pi,n}(\infty))$ exists for all $n\in \mathbb{N}$, and for all $y>0$, we have 
