{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:12:19.474060+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bac6de1c5f5603cd8ca5bcc666f1796fc0d2f36fc6407d4dc3fa37c72c2daeec","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2608.17562, '2608.17562'] Let $b \in (0, \alpha)$ and $h_{b}(x) = x^{b}$. The derivative of
  the Stein solution $g_{b}$ associated with $h_{b}$
   is infinitely differentiable on $(0,\infty)$ and satisfies:
\begin{align}
g'_{b}(x) = -\int_0^\infty \frac{bx^{b-1}}{(u+1)^{1+{b}/{\alpha}}}e^{-{u}{x^{-\alpha}}}\dif u,\quad x \in \Rp, 
\end{align}
 and we have 
\begin{align}
  x\vert g'_{b}(x) \vert \leq bx^{b}\min
  ( \alpha / b , x^{\alpha}
  ),\quad x \in \Rp.  
\end{align}
Moreover, the second derivative of $g_{b}$ satisfies: 
\begin{align}

    x\vert g''_{b}(x) \vert &\leq bx^{b-1}
    \big(
    \vert b-1 \vert\min(\alpha / b , x^{\alpha}) + \alpha \min(x^{-\alpha}, x^{\alpha})
    \big),\quad x \in \Rp.
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.038842+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bace5515b827bf76879c2fed34c1293aaa90377eb6cf46cf779a642f9fdf7179","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 18 ({\cite{mingoFreeProbabilityRandom2017}}) of arXiv:2606.31528, 'Well-posedness and stationary distribution of free stochastic differential equations'] If $\{\mu_n\}_{n\in\mathbb N}$ is a sequence of probability measures on $\mathbb R$ such that
