{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:51:15.029001+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_baed613e33033ac3923abd0a098ab6ea962de804b8d6d678f1a69cf04c8bb279","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma untied-truncation-stability of arXiv:2609.03858, 'High-Dimensional Learning Dynamics of \\ Attention-Indexed Models'] Let \(\bar\mu\) be the admissible slow trajectory in
Lemma (lemma:untied-global-slow-dynamics of the paper), and fix \(T>0\). Let \(C_*\) be the spectral constant in Lemma (lemma:spectral_bounds_untied of the paper) and set
$R:=C_*^2$. Then there exist constants
$R<s_-<s_+<\infty$, $\varepsilon_T>0$ and 
$C_T<\infty$ such that the following holds.

If \(\nu_0\in X_{s_-}^0\) satisfies
\begin{equation}
\|\nu_0-\bar\mu(0)\|_{s_-}\le\varepsilon_T,

\end{equation}
then the extended ODE
\begin{equation}
\frac{d\nu}{d\tau}=V_{\rm ext}(\nu),
\qquad
