  \mathbb P_{\beta,r} (x \leftrightarrow y \leftrightarrow w),\\
   \mathbb P_{\beta,r} (x \leftrightarrow y \leftrightarrow z)\mathbb P_{\beta,r} (y \leftrightarrow w)
  \mathbb P_{\beta,r} (x \leftrightarrow z \leftrightarrow w)
  \}
\end{multline*}
holds for all $x,y,z,w\in \mathbb Z^d$ and $\beta,r\geq 0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:12:20.554513+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bb0d742dfbc399a6104c214d243b129e39417c58e532349adb829889e5058486","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma prob-nontree-small of arXiv:2603.28936, 'Composition of random functions and word reconstruction'] Let $F$ be an induced event and let $R$ be chosen independently and uniformly at random from $[n]$. We have	
