{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:33:17.712839+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bb1f6660c032b474cad9618185bedbd58bf530eea10bfc908b5c2247ba0aa83b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 36 (Dyadic Volterra estimate) of arXiv:2607.10813, '2607.10813'] Let $a,b\in\mathfrak C$ with $a\ne b$, $Q\le c_{\mathrm{ap}}N$, and $0<s<1-2\beta_b$.
\begin{align}
  \norm{\cD^{a;b}_{N,Q}P_Qw}_{C_TH^{s-1}}
  \lesssim{}&N^{-1+2\beta_b}\norm{P_Qw}_{L_T^\infty L^2}\notag\\
  &+N^{-1+2\beta_b}Q^s
    \norm{\partial_tw}_{C_TH^{-1}},
\end{align}
and
\begin{equation}
  \norm{\cD^{a;b}_{N,Q}P_Qw}_{L_T^\infty B_{2,\infty}^{\sigma-1}}
  \lesssim_T
  N^{-1+2\beta_b}
  \paren{Q^{-1}\norm{w}_{L_T^\infty B_{2,\infty}^{\sigma}}
  +\norm{\partial_tw}_{L_T^\infty B_{2,\infty}^{\sigma-1}}}.
\end{equation}
The constants are uniform in $N,Q$ and in the spectral cutoff.  If
$[\mathfrak h_b]_{\beta_b,0}\le H$ and $\parvec$ ranges over a separated
parameter class, the implicit constants are bounded by a constant depending
on $H$ and the parameter class.  The phase-gap constants themselves are
independent of the forcing profiles.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:48:24.615250+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bb23888ea9b9526f18061851b103357b5c221f9efe33b3d4d9f8d3b644c963d0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:tv-ber-lb of arXiv:2601.04079, 'TV homogenization inequalities'] For $\textup{{\bf p}},\textup{{\bf q}}\in[0,1]^n$,
let $I=\left\{ i\in[n]:p_i\ge q_i \right\}$ and $J=[n]\setminus I$,
with
$\textup{{\bf p}}_I,\textup{{\bf p}}_J,\textup{{\bf q}}_I,\textup{{\bf q}}_J$ the corresponding subsequences of $\textup{{\bf p}},\textup{{\bf q}}$.
Then
\begin{eqnarray*}
\TV(\Ber(\textup{{\bf p}}),\Ber(\textup{{\bf q}}))
&\ge&
\max\paren{
\TV(\Ber(\textup{{\bf p}}_I),\Ber(\textup{{\bf q}}_I))
,
\TV(\Ber(\textup{{\bf p}}_J),\Ber(\textup{{\bf q}}_J))
}\\
&\ge&
\frac{1}{9}
\max(
\Phi(\textup{{\bf p}}_I,\textup{{\bf q}}_I)
,
\Phi(\textup{{\bf q}}_J,\textup{{\bf p}}_J)
).
\end{eqnarray*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:07.309625+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bb2509cf187c0d55c195a19d5f9fb197aff4dd1f3f8cc4ffd1ed9152d7aa3de3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 10 of arXiv:2606.24485, 'On the convex hull of a planar Brownian bridge with a random Gaussian endpoint'] For $0 \le \si \le 1$,
