{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:34:45.754390+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bb399638eec358feb61ba724ed001a7a70162711649defb1de115c0e0e16ee83","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary eq:orbint of arXiv:2609.01990, 'Jacquet-Zagier treatment of the beyond endoscopy trace formula for \(\GL_2\)'] For $\Phi$ given by
    \[
        \Phi_{\infty} (x,y) = e^{-(x^2+y^2)}, \qquad \Phi_q(x,y) = \mathbf{1}_{\mathbb{Z}_q} \times \mathbf{1}_{\mathbb{Z}_q}
    \]
    the orbital integral for any non-central conjugacy class \(C\) is given by 
