{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:15.339630+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bb7061711013cca1d04963d19cea3a744dd670f08d05de1f0a0cf1d6c0d3d5ec","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 18 of arXiv:2506.15044, '2506.15044'] Let $H\in \mathcal{P}^\mathbb{C}$ and $A\in \mathcal{V}^\mathbb{C}$.
\begin{itemize}
  \item [$(1)$] $H\in\mathcal{L}^\mathbb{C}_s(A)$ if and only if
      there exist an FS $(\tau_n)$ for $\mathbb{C}$ such that for each $n\in \mathbf{N}^+$, $H^{\tau_n}\in \mathcal{L}_s(A^{\tau_n})$.
  \item [$(2)$] Suppose that $H\in\mathcal{L}^\mathbb{C}_s(A)$ and $(\tau_n)$ is an FS for $\mathbb{C}$. Then $(\tau_n,H^{\tau_n}.A^{\tau_n})$ is an FCS for $H_{\bullet}A\in\mathcal{V}^\mathbb{C}$, and $H_{\bullet}A$ can be expressed as
      \begin{equation}
      H_{\bullet}A=\left((H_0A_0)I_{\llbracket{0}\rrbracket}+\sum\limits_{n=1}^{{+\infty}}
      (H^{\tau_n}.A^{\tau_n})I_{\rrbracket{\tau_{n-1},\tau_n}
