{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:37:20.369344+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bb71f9147017fe732c23b2450826581023db0f740492386454c889bd21f6e503","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition thm3 of arXiv:2411.13430, 'Optimal subelliptic super-Poincar\'e and isoperimetric inequalities on stratified Lie grou'] Assume as in Theorem (thm1 of the paper) except that $n_1 = 1$. If $p = \alpha + 1$ then $I_\mu \gtrsim \mathcal{U}_1$, and otherwise if $p > \alpha + 1$ then $I_\mu$ satisfies 
