where $ \mathbf P_{\mathsf y}$ (resp. $ \mathbf P^0_{\mathsf y}$)  is the law of  $(Y_t(\mathsf y),t\ge 0)$ (resp. of $(Y_t^0(\mathsf y),t\ge 0)$, see (equation eq.Lcin0 of the paper)), and $(\mathbf m_t^0,t\ge 0)$ is the   Doléans-Dade exponential (true) martingale defined by $\mathbf m_t^0=\exp\big[  - \int_0^t   \big(\gamma v_s^0+\nabla \mathbf V_{\mathbf c}(x_s^0)\big)dB_s -\frac 12 \int_0^t  \big\vert   \gamma v_s^0+\!\nabla \mathbf V_{\mathbf c}(x_s^0)\big\vert^2 ds   \big]$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:01:25.654242+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bbe48d615fde33f7606ef152748e7f973bb1b757a9af5c1865ace5541d66d6ef","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Coordinate reflections of arXiv:2605.16162, 'Deconfinement For $\mathrm{SO}(3)$ Lattice Yang--Mills at Strong Coupling'] For any coordinate hyperplane in $\Z^d$ of the form $P=\{(x_1,\dots,x_d) \in \R^d:x_i=a\}$ for $i \in [d]$ and $a \in \Z \cup \frac{1}{2}\Z$, we let $\Theta_P:E_{\Lambda} \to E_{\Lambda}$ denote the map which reflects edges over $P$ (keeping track of orientation so that edges parallel to the hyperplane reverse orientation after reflection). Moreover for any configuration $Q=(Q_e)_{e \in E_{\Lambda}^+} \in G^{E_{\Lambda}^+}$
