{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:04:55.812283+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bc084a4711a808e04f607baa8d1c0756722a0493ae367da3e2e7267d345d7658","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop p:dov-holder-general of arXiv:2607.18194, 'Temperature chaos in directed polymers'] {dov}}]
    For all $L\geqslant 1$ and $\epsilon\in(0,1)$,
    there exists a random constant $\mathfrak{C}_{(p:dov-holder-general of the paper)}>0$ such that the following holds.
    First, we have
    \begin{align*}
        \mathbb{P}(\mathfrak{C}_{(p:dov-holder-general of the paper)} > m) \leqslant CL^{10} \epsilon^{-6} e^{-cm^{3/2}}
        \qquad\text{for all $m\geqslant 0$},
    \end{align*}
    where $C,c>0$ are universal constants.
    Second, for all $x,x',y,y'\in [-2L,2L]$ and all $-2L<s<t<2L$ with $t-s \geqslant \epsilon$, we have
    \begin{multline*}
        \left|
            \mathcal{L}(s,x;t,y) - \mathcal{L}(s,x';t,y')
            + \frac{(y-x)^2 - (y'-x')^2}{t-s}
        \right|\\
        \leqslant \mathfrak{C}_{(p:dov-holder-general of the paper)} \left\lVert(x,y)-(x',y')\right\rVert_2^{1/2} \log^{1/2}\left(\frac{8L}{\left\lVert(x,y)-(x',y')\right\rVert_2}\right).
    \end{multline*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:05:52.398030+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bc0a6abceb686853c3008f6e9f0aecd2ae719ff251935642aab26d5b1b62d121","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma3.23 of arXiv:2504.15992, 'Repeated singular values of a random symmetric matrix and decoupled singular value estimat'] For any given disjoint subsets $D_1,D_2,D_3\subset[n]$ of cardinality $c_0^2n/12$ each and $D_1\cup D_2\cup D_3=[c_0^2n/4]$,  the subset $\Lambda_{\epsilon,\epsilon_1}(c)$ can be covered by a family $\mathcal{F}_{\epsilon,\epsilon_1}(c)$ of $(N,N_1,\kappa,\kappa',D_1,D_2,D_3)$ box pairs $(\mathcal{B}_1,\mathcal{B}_2)_i,i\in\mathcal{F}_{\epsilon,\epsilon_1}(c)$ , where we take $N={\kappa_0}/4\epsilon$, $N_1=\kappa_0\epsilon_1/4\epsilon$, $\kappa=\max({\kappa_1}/{\kappa_0},2^8{\kappa_0}^{-4})$ and $\kappa'=\sqrt{\frac{100}{c_0^2}}/\kappa_0$: 
    \begin{equation}
\Lambda_{\epsilon,\epsilon_1}(c)\subset\cup_{i\in\mathcal{F}_{\epsilon,\epsilon_1}(c)}4\epsilon n^{-1/2}\cdot (\mathcal{B}_1\times(c\mathcal{B}_1+\mathcal{B}_2))_i,
    \end{equation} 
    in the sense that for any $(v,w)\in \Lambda_{\epsilon,\epsilon_1}(c)$ with $w=cv+\epsilon_1 r$ then we have $(v,r)\in (4\epsilon n^{-1/2})\mathcal{B}_1\times (4\epsilon n^{-1/2}/\epsilon_1)\mathcal{B}_2$ for one such box $(\mathcal{B}_1\times\mathcal{B}_2)_i$ in the family $i\in \mathcal{F}_{\epsilon,
    \epsilon_1}(c)$.

  The index set has cardinality $|\mathcal{F}_{\epsilon,\epsilon_1}(c)|\leq \kappa^{2n}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:21:45.350739+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bc109f4d3a8ae8a47524d80419b8effb2c864302ca9817a9f7ecea4798f7a611","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 5 (Universality of general functionals over triangulable spaces) of arXiv:2607.27535, 'Universal topological statistics on \\ triangulated singular spaces'] Let $M \subset \RR^D$ be an admissibly triangulable space and let $f: M \rightarrow \RR_{\ge 0}$ be a good density. Let $\func_n$ be a functional that satisfies the conditions (1)--(7). Then there exists a real number $\overline{\func}^*$ so that the  following holds independently of $M$ and $f$:
