{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.240041+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bc5cfc724f22f1663bad46e0eb95dac272661d65f986b133f0cb4d3a460647e4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 5 of arXiv:2604.14752, 'Strong and weak rates of convergence in the Smoluchowski--Kramers approximation for stocha'] For all $\delta\in[0,\frac12]$ and $\rho\in[2\delta,1]$, there exists $C_{\delta,\rho}\in(0,\infty)$ such that, for all $\alpha\in\R$, all $\epsilon\in(0,1)$, all $t>0$ and all $u\in H^{\alpha+\rho-2\delta-1}$, 
