{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:53:51.337605+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bc63fe5490493f6e128bf2faef0c6a74d1cd86bfbb86872052cb23722e141237","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:arc_chain_identity of arXiv:2605.03896, 'Dimer models on astroidal zig-zag graphs'] Let $\mathsf b \in B(\mathsf G_{c, \mathsf f_0})$ and $\mathsf w \in W(\mathsf G_{c, \mathsf f_0})$. Let $J=[a,b]$ and $K=[c,d]$ be any two nontrivial closed intervals in $\partial N$ with endpoints in $V(N)$. Then
