{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:00:30.488837+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bc877ae88ecc633c88ff2f128915823c99c51c706a51249a999c6f4fd5cf5f89","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 9 of arXiv:2607.03924, 'Tree Coordinates and Range Martingales for Positive Operator-Valued Measures'] The triple $\left(K_{E},P,V\right)$ is a minimal
Naimark dilation of $E$. That is, 
\begin{equation}
E\left(B\right)=V^{*}P\left(B\right)V,\qquad B\in\mathcal{B}\left(\Omega_{m}\right),
\end{equation}
and 
