{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:34:20.704346+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bc9f08d2354719e38c5e5ab6ec868e420ced19ca4e36ddcb67f26dcf90494789","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 28 of arXiv:2609.02193, 'State-law dynamics of McKean-Vlasov stochastic reaction-diffusion equations on $\mathbb R^'] Assume \textnormal{(A1)-(A4)}. Let $T>0$, $R>0$ and $\omega\in\Omega_0$. There exists $C_{T,\omega,R}>0$ such that, for every $\epsilon\in(0,\epsilon_0]$, $x_\epsilon,x_0\in H$ and $\mu_\epsilon,\mu_0\in P$ satisfying
