{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:34:45.635461+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bd3496f9a97fb78fb8aa6974123d335cf7635aea64567b0fd5ef7df4100452fe","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem maintheorem_with_simplices of arXiv:2609.01825, 'On everywhere locally soluble varieties \\ in families over toric bases'] Let $f\colon \mathbb N^s \to \mathbb C$ satisfy (mainassumption of the paper) and be real and non-negative or satisfy (upperboundassp of the paper) as well. Assume that the polytope $\cal P$ is bounded, that $\cal F$ is not contained in any coordinate hyperplane, and that $\vec \ell$ is of convergent type for $\cal F$. 
    Dissect the polytope $\cal P$ into simplices and let $S_1,\ldots, S_h$ be those simplices that have exactly $d+1$ vertices in the maximal face $\cal F$, where $d = \dim \cal F$. Let the constants $C_{S_j}$ be as in (lem:simplex_computation of the paper) and $\cal F_{S_j} = \cal F \cap S_j$ for $1\leq j\leq h$.

	Then there exists $\varepsilon > 0$ such that 
    \begin{align*}
\Upsilon(B; \vec 1)
		= c_{\cal P} c_f \Bigl( \prod_{i=1}^s \alpha_i^{-\ell_i} \Bigr) B^a (\log B)^{d+\ell}  +  O_{\vec \varpi, \vec \alpha, \vec \ell}(C_f B^a (\log B)^{d + \ell - \varepsilon}),
\end{align*}
where
\begin{align}
c_{\cal P} = \sum_{j=1}^h C_{S_j} \int_{\cal F_{S_j}} \prod_{i=1}^s t_i^{\ell_i} \,\mathrm d\mu.
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:04.997228+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bd35ef9077df5d1988f35b5cc67270b533c421b9c847e10dd623456e8cad4d04","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 52 of arXiv:2604.01685, 'Probability with Measure\footnote{Lecture notes. University of Ljubljana.}'] Let $(\mu_n)_{n\in \mathbb{N}}$ be a sequence of measures on a measurable space $(\Omega,\FF)$. Then $\sum_{n\in \mathbb{N}}\mu_n$ is a measure on $(\Omega,\FF)$. Furthermore, for all $f\in \FF/\mathcal{B}_{[-\infty,\infty]}$, $\int f\dd(\sum_{n\in \mathbb{N}}\mu_n)$ is well-defined iff  $(\sum_{n\in \mathbb{N}} \int f^+\dd\mu_n)\land \left(\sum_{n\in \mathbb{N}} \int f^-\dd\mu_n\right)<\infty$, and then
	\begin{equation}
	\left(\sum_{n\in \mathbb{N}}\mu_n\right)[f]=\sum_{n\in \mathbb{N}} \int f\dd\mu_n. 
	\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:44.947781+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bd397611ce03fd223d0d92bd4a5e0ad2598061a56c749dc436f7a353a7b3ae49","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 22 of arXiv:2606.24599, '\bf Perron--Frobenius theorem for a general tree-valued growth-fragmentation-isolation pro'] Assume $\lambda>0$. There exist two positive functions $V$ and $V^*$ on $\TT$ such that $h\in\mathcal{B}(V)\subset \mathcal{B}(V^*)$ and $\langle\pi,V^*\rangle<+\infty$. Moreover, there exist $C>0$ and $\omega>0$ such that for all $s\ge 0$, we have
    \begin{equation}

        \sup_{|f|\leq V^*}|e^{-\lambda s}M_s f(\tt)-h(\tt)\langle\pi,f\rangle|\leq CV^*(\tt)e^{-\omega s},\forall\tt\in\TT.
    \end{equation}
    For any $s\in(0,1]$ we have
    \begin{equation}

        \sup_{\tt\in\TT}\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\delta_{\tt}}\Ll[\langle X_s,V\rangle\log^*\langle X_s,V\rangle\Rr]}{V^*(\tt)}<+\infty,
    \end{equation}
    where
    \[
    \log^*{x}=
    \begin{cases}
    \frac{x}{e},&0\leq x\leq e\\
    \log(x),&x>e
    \end{cases}
    \]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:02.098490+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bd3c6721d88259d9ca38c375a831298907bbd381104d2494e103990a95ed5eec","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 1 of arXiv:2604.26396, '\LARGE Limiting spectral distributions of large consistent rank correlation matrices'] Under \eqref{eq:assumption} and \eqref{eq:asymptotics}, we have almost surely,
