{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:59:45.009700+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bd600e0d76f3a99ca7bb72206703ce324254f7f2cd03eb5f5659cc698767c1ca","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem LUE left soft of arXiv:2605.12777, 'Mesoscopic Rates of Convergence for Complex Wishart Matrices at the Leftmost Spectrum Edge'] (left soft edge) Consider an LUE $L_{a,N}$ such that $\lim\limits_{N\rightarrow\infty}\frac{N}{n}=\gamma\in(0,1)$ where $n:=N+a$. Let $I\subset[s,+\infty)$ for $s>-\infty$. Define parameters:
    \begin{equation*}
      \begin{array}{ll}
      \mu^L_{k,m}:=\left(\sqrt{k+\frac{1}{2}}-\sqrt{m+\frac{1}{2}}\right)^2,\\
      \sigma^L_{k,m}:=\left(\sqrt{k+\frac{1}{2}}-\sqrt{m+\frac{1}{2}}\right)\left(\left(m+\frac{1}{2}\right)^{-\frac{1}{2}}-\left(k+\frac{1}{2}\right)^{-\frac{1}{2}}\right)^{\frac{1}{3}},
      \end{array}
    \end{equation*}
\begin{equation*}
    \mu_L=\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{\sigma_{n-1,N}^{L}}}+\frac{1}{\sqrt{\sigma_{n,N-1}^{L}}}\right)\left(\frac{1}{\mu^L_{n-1,N}\sqrt{\sigma_{n-1,N}^L}}+\frac{1}{\mu^L_{n,N-1}\sqrt{\sigma_{n,N-1}^{L}}}\right)^{-1}
\end{equation*}
and
\begin{equation*}
    \sigma_L=\left(\frac{\sqrt{\sigma_{n-1,N}^{L}}}{\mu^L_{n-1,N}}+\frac{\sqrt{\sigma_{n,N-1}^{L}}}{\mu^L_{n,N-1}}\right)\left(\frac{1}{\mu^L_{n-1,N}\sqrt{\sigma_{n-1,N}^{L}}}+\frac{1}{\mu^L_{n,N-1}\sqrt{\sigma_{n,N-1}^{L}}}\right)^{-1}.
\end{equation*}
Let $\mathcal{X}_{L_{a,N}}^{LS}$ denote the left-soft-edge-scaled point process for $L_{a,N}$ with the kernel $K_{L_{a,N}}^{LS}(x,y):=\sigma_{L}K_{L_{a,N}}(t_{L_{N}}(x),t_{L_{N}}(y))$ where $t_{L_N}(x):=\mu_{L}-\sigma_{L}x$ for any $x\in I$. Then on $A\subset I$, there exists $n(s,\gamma)\in\mathbb{N}$ such that for any $N>n(s,\gamma)$,
\begin{equation}
W_1(\mathcal{N}_{L_{a,N}}^{LS},\mathcal{N}_{Ai})\le\frac{g(s,\gamma)e^{-s}}{N^{\frac{2}{3}}}
\end{equation}
where $g(s,\gamma)$ is continuous and non-increasing with respect to $s$ for any fixed $\gamma$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:38:17.787221+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bd6238fd3b54a7f487a02506dc94c1bbbabad414bb1f05b3a43cc806e0943428","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:theta_hjb_mkv of arXiv:2507.22577, 'A Mean-Field Theory of $\Theta$-Expectations'] Let $(\mu_t)_{t\in[0,T]}$ be a given flow of probability measures in $\mathcal{P}_2(\mathbb{R})$. The \textbf{$\Theta$-HJB-McKean-Vlasov (HJB-MKV) equation} is the terminal-value problem for a function $v: [0,T]\times\mathbb{R}^k \to \mathbb{R}$:
\begin{equation}
\begin{cases}
    -\partial_t v - \sup_{a \in \mathcal{U}_{g(\mu_t)}} \Big\{ \mathcal{L}^{t,x,a,\mu_t} v(t,x) + F(t, x, v, (\nabla_x v)\sigma(t,x,a,\mu_t), a, \mu_t) \Big\} = 0, \\
    v(T,x) = \Phi(x),
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
for $(t,x) \in [0,T) \times \mathbb{R}^k$, where the second-order operator is given by
\[ (\mathcal{L}^{t,x,a,\mu} \phi)(x) \coloneqq \scpr{b(t,x,a,\mu)}{\nabla_x \phi(x)} + \frac{1}{2} \mathrm{Tr}\big(\sigma\sigma^T(t,x,a,\mu) \nabla_x^2 \phi(x)\big). \]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:01:39.495960+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bd653c38ae0bd9b33e9d032ed4e6bdb9c40955b0690a8243c19879dad397f239","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:pnqn of arXiv:2607.22291, 'Rare subtree patterns in size-conditioned Bienaymé trees: Poisson approximation and declum'] Assume (hyp:M of the paper) holds for $(G_k)$ along $(k_{n})$ with respect to $(M_{n})$. Set $p_n = \P(I_1^{(M_n)}=1)$ and $r_n = \sqrt{a_{M_n} a_n}$. Then:
