{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.580709+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bda32a2c08d9e55d4afc84ca077ed40d1e67f50166238aae176994651e554e0d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem bound_on_bm of arXiv:2509.06730, 'Hyperbolic branching Brownian motion: \\ the empirical limit measure'] For any $x\in \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}$, $y\in (0,\infty)$ and any interval $I\subseteq \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}$ we have that
